COLLDATA("sh12520","en",[[1,"I used to, when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ, benefit from it as much as God willed. But if someone else narrated to me, I would not believe him unless he swore an oath. So when he swore, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr spoke truthfully—saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'There is no Muslim who commits a sin, then performs wudu, prays two rak'ahs, and seeks God's forgiveness, except that He forgives him.'"],[2,": 'I am the heir of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then you came—meaning al-Abbas and Ali—you seeking your inheritance from your nephew, and he seeking his wife's inheritance from her father.' Abu Bakr said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said: We are not inherited from; what we leave behind is charity.'"],[3,"We are not inherited from; what we leave behind is charity."],[4,"Umar sent for me after the day had advanced, and he granted me permission. I entered upon him while he was on a bed of palm fibers, leaning his back against its ropes, reclining on a leather cushion. He said to me: 'O Malik, a group of your people has arrived, and I have ordered some wealth for them. Take it and distribute it among them.' I said to him: 'O Commander of the Believers, I have no strength for that. If only you would order someone else.' He said: 'Take it and distribute it among them.' He said: Then Yarfa' came to him and said: 'O Commander of the Believers, will you receive Uthman b. Affan, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, al-Zubayr, and Sa'd?' He said: 'Yes.' So he granted them permission and they entered. Then he came to him again and said: 'O Commander of the Believers, will you receive Ali and al-Abbas?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: Then they entered, and al-Abbas was saying: 'O Commander of the Believers, judge between me and this man.' Sufyan said: And he mentioned some harsh words. The people said: 'O Commander of the Believers, judge between them, and give each of them relief from the other.' Umar said to them: 'I adjure you by God, by whose permission the heavens and the earth stand: do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: We are not inherited from; what we leave behind is charity?' They said: 'Yes.' Umar said: 'God singled out His Messenger ﷺ with a special privilege that He did not single out for anyone else.' Then he recited the verse: 'And what God restored to His Messenger from them—you did not spur any horse or camel for it' (Quran 59:6). Sufyan said: I do not know whether he recited the verse after it or not. He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed among you the wealth of Banu al-Nadir. By God, he did not prefer himself over you, nor did he keep it from you. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to take from it his own yearly expenditure and that of his family, and he would make what remained into horses and weapons as equipment in the way of God.' Then he said to them: 'I adjure you by the One by whose permission the heaven and the earth stand: do you know that?' They said: 'Yes.' Then he adjured Ali and al-Abbas by what he had adjured the people: 'Do you two know that?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'When the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away, Abu Bakr was the heir of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then you, O Abbas, came seeking your inheritance from your nephew, and Ali came seeking the inheritance of his wife from her father. Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: We are not inherited from; what we leave behind is charity. Yet you considered me—and God knows that he was dutiful and rightly guided—a withholder of the truth. When Abu Bakr passed away, I said: I am the heir of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the heir of Abu Bakr. Yet you considered me—and God knows that I am truthful, dutiful, rightly guided, and a follower of the truth. Then you two came to me with your case being one, and you asked me to hand it over to you. I said: If you wish, I will hand it over to you on condition that you have a covenant with God to do with it what the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do with it. So you took it on that basis.' Then he said to them: 'Is that so?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then you two came to me for me to judge between you. By God, I will not judge between you other than that until the Hour comes. If you are unable, then return it to me.'"],[5,"Umar looked in on Abu Bakr while he was sticking out his tongue. He said: 'What are you doing, O successor of the Messenger of God?' He said: 'This has brought me to ruin. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: There is no part of the body except that it complains of the sharpness of the tongue.'"],[6,"When Hafsa became a widow after Ibn Hudhafa. Umar said: 'I met Uthman and offered him Hafsa. He said: I will consider my matter. I waited for some nights, then he met me and said: It has become clear to me that I should not marry on this day of mine.' Umar said: 'Then I met Abu Bakr and said: I will marry you to Hafsa. He did not return anything to me, and I was more upset with him than with Uthman. I waited for some nights, then the Messenger of God ﷺ proposed to her, and I married her to him. Then Abu Bakr met me and said: Perhaps you were upset with me when you offered Hafsa?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Nothing prevented me from returning to you except that I already knew that the Messenger of God ﷺ had mentioned her, and I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ. If he had left her, I would have accepted her.' Umar said: 'Then I complained about Uthman to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Hafsa will marry someone better than Uthman, and Uthman will marry someone better than Hafsa. Then the Prophet ﷺ married his daughter to him.'"],[7,"When Hafsa bt. Umar became a widow after Khunays b. Hudhafa al-Sahmi, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Umar said: 'I went to Uthman b. Affan and offered him Hafsa bt. Umar.' He said: 'I said: If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsa.' He said: 'I will consider my matter.' I waited for some nights, then he met me and said: 'It has become clear to me that I should not marry on this day of mine.' Umar said: 'Then I met Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and said to him: If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsa bt. Umar. Abu Bakr remained silent and did not return anything to me, and I was more upset with him than with Uthman. I waited for some days, then the Messenger of God ﷺ proposed to her, and I married her to him. Then Abu Bakr met me and said: Perhaps you were upset with me when you offered me Hafsa and I did not return anything to you?' He said: 'I said: Yes.' He said: 'Nothing prevented me from returning to you regarding what you offered me except that I had already known that the Messenger of God ﷺ had mentioned her, and I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ. If the Messenger of God ﷺ had left her, I would have accepted her.'"],[8,"Abu Bakr stood up as a preacher and said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us in the first year and said: Nothing has been distributed among people better than well-being after certainty. Indeed, truthfulness and righteousness are in Paradise, and indeed lying and wickedness are in the Fire.'"],[9,"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken, some of his companions became disturbed, and I was among those who became disturbed. He said: Then Umar passed by me and greeted me, but I did not return his greeting. He complained about me to Abu Bakr. He said: Then he came to us and said to me: 'Your brother greeted you, but you did not return his greeting.' He said: I said: 'I did not notice his greeting, and I was preoccupied with that.' He said: 'And why?' I said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ has been taken, and I did not ask him about the salvation of this matter.' He said: 'I did ask him.' He said: Then I stood up to him and embraced him. He said: I said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, you are more entitled to that.' He said: 'I did ask him, and he said: Whoever accepts the word that I offered to my uncle—it is salvation for him.'"],[10,"Some men among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ grieved for him when the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away, until some of them almost became disturbed. Uthman said: 'I was one of them. While I was sitting in the shade of a fortress tower, Umar b. al-Khattab passed by me and greeted me, but I did not sense that he passed or greeted. Umar went until he entered upon Abu Bakr and said: Should I not amaze you? I passed by Uthman and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting to me. Then Abu Bakr and Umar came—during Abu Bakr's caliphate—until they reached me and both greeted. Then Abu Bakr said: Your brother Umar came to me and claimed that he passed by you and greeted, but you did not return the greeting to him. What led you to that?' I said: 'I did not do that.' Umar said: 'Yes, but it is your pride, O Banu Umayya.' Uthman said: I said: 'By God, I did not sense that you passed or greeted.' He said: Abu Bakr said: 'Uthman has spoken truthfully. Has some matter distracted you from that?' He said: I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is it?' Uthman said: I said: 'God took His Prophet ﷺ before I could ask him about the salvation of this matter.' Abu Bakr said: 'I did ask him about that.' Uthman said: I said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom, you are more entitled to it.' Abu Bakr said: 'I said: O Messenger of God, what is the salvation of this matter?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever accepts from me the word that I offered to my uncle and he rejected it—it is salvation for him.'"],[11,"I was a man who, when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ, God benefited me with it as much as He willed. But if one of his companions narrated to me, I would make him swear an oath, and if he swore to me, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr spoke truthfully—that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Any servant who commits a sin, then performs wudu and perfects the wudu, then stands and prays, then seeks God's forgiveness, except that He forgives him.' Then he recited: 'And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves...' (Quran 3:135)."],[12,"I used to, when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ, benefit from it as much as God willed. But if someone else narrated it to me, I would make him swear an oath, and if he swore to me, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr spoke truthfully—that he ﷺ said: 'There is no one who commits a sin, then performs wudu and perfects the wudu'—Mis'ar said: then prays, Sufyan said: prays two rak'ahs—then seeks forgiveness, except that He forgives him.'"],[13,"I used to, when I heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ, benefit by it as much as God willed me to benefit. Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr spoke the truth—from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: There is no servant—Shuʿba said: I think he said: Muslim—who commits a sin, then performs ablution, then prays two rakʿahs, then asks God's forgiveness for that sin, but that He forgives him. Shuʿba said: And he recited one of these two verses: “Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it” and “Those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves…”"],[14,"I heard Ali b. Rabiʿa—a man from Banu Asad—narrating from Asma (or Ibn Asma) of Banu Fazarah, from Ali, who said: I used to, when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ, benefit by it as much as God willed me to benefit. And Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr spoke the truth—that the Messenger of God ﷺ… then he mentioned something similar."],[15,"I used to, when I was told a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ, make the one who told it swear an oath; and if he swore to me, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me—and Abu Bakr spoke the truth—that he ﷺ said: There is no servant who commits a sin, then performs ablution, and prays two rakʿahs, and asks God's forgiveness, but that He forgives him."],[16,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed between Abu Bakr and ʿUmar while Abdullah was praying. He had begun Surah al-Nisa and was reciting it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever would love to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it as Ibn Umm ʿAbd recites it. Then he asked, and the Messenger of God ﷺ kept saying: Ask and you will be given, ask and you will be given. Among what he asked was: O God, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, and bliss that does not run out, and the companionship of our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in the highest garden of eternity. Then ʿUmar went to Abdullah to give him the good news, but found Abu Bakr already outside, having beaten him to it, and he said: If you did that, you are indeed foremost in good."],[17,"I was in the mosque praying when the Messenger of God ﷺ entered with Abu Bakr and ʿUmar. I was reciting Surah al-Nisa, and I read it. When I finished I sat down, and began praising God and invoking blessings on the Prophet ﷺ, then I supplicated for myself. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Ask and you will be given. Then he said: Whoever would love to recite the Quran fresh, let him recite it as Ibn Umm ʿAbd recites it. He said: Then I returned home, and Abu Bakr came to me and said: Do you remember anything of what you were supplicating? I said: Yes—O God, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, and bliss that does not run out, and the companionship of our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in the highest garden of eternity. Then ʿUmar went to Abdullah to give him the good news, but found Abu Bakr already outside, having beaten him to it, and he said: If you did that, you are indeed foremost in good."],[18,"Ibn ʿUmar said to his servant: Do not pass me by Ibn al-Zubayr. But the servant was heedless and passed by him, and he raised his head and saw him, and said: May God have mercy on you. I have known you only as one who fasts much, prays much, and maintains family ties. By God, I hope that despite the evils and sins you have committed, He will not punish you. Mujahid said: Then he turned to me and said…"],[19,"I said: O Messenger of God, what is the salvation of this matter in which we are? He said: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, that is salvation for him."],[20,"When Hafsa became a widow—she had been married to Khunays b. Hudhafa—ʿUmar went to Abu Bakr and offered her to him, but he remained silent. Then he went to ʿUthman and offered her to him, and ʿUthman said: I have no need of women. But then the Messenger of God ﷺ proposed to her, and she was married to him. ʿUmar met Abu Bakr and said: I offered Hafsa to you and you remained silent, and I was more angry with you than with ʿUthman, who refused me. Abu Bakr said: There had been mention of her matter, but it was a secret, and I disliked disclosing the secret."],[21,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when this verse was revealed: “Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it and will not find for himself besides God any protector or helper.” The Prophet ﷺ said: O Abu Bakr, shall I recite to you a verse that was revealed to me? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: So he recited it to me. He said: I do not know except that I felt a cracking in my back, so much so that I stretched for it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: As for you, O Abu Bakr, and your believing companions, you will be recompensed for that in this world until you meet God with no sins. As for the others, it will be gathered for them until they are recompensed for it on the Day of Resurrection."],[22,"When they wanted to dig a grave for the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu ʿUbayda b. al-Jarrah used to dig in the Makkan style—a trench—for the people of Makkah, while Abu Talha Zayd b. Sahl was the one who used to dig for the people of Madinah in the lahd style. Al-ʿAbbas called two men and said to one of them: Go to Abu ʿUbayda; and to the other: Go to Abu Talha. O God, choose for Your Messenger. The one sent to Abu Talha found him and brought him, and he dug a lahd for the Messenger of God. When the preparation of the Messenger of God ﷺ was finished on Tuesday, he was placed on his bier. The Muslims had differed about where to bury him. One said: We bury him in his mosque. Another said: Rather he should be buried with his companions. Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: No prophet is taken but he is buried where he was taken. So the bed of the Messenger of God ﷺ on which he died was lifted, and a grave was dug for him beneath it. Then the people were called to pray over the Messenger of God ﷺ in groups: the men, until when they finished, the women were admitted, until when the women finished, the children were admitted. No one led the people in prayer over the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ was buried in the middle of the night on Wednesday night."],[23,"No prophet is taken but he is buried where he was taken."],[24,"The Prophet ﷺ bit into a shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."],[25,"When “Perish the hands of Abu Lahab” was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came to the Prophet ﷺ, and Abu Bakr was with him. When Abu Bakr saw her, he said: “O Messenger of God, she is an abusive woman, and I fear that she may harm you, so would you get up?” He said: “She will not see me.” She came and said: “O Abu Bakr, your companion has satirized me.” He said: “He does not recite poetry.” She said: “You are believed by me,” and turned away. I said: “O Messenger of God, she did not see you!” He said: “An angel kept shielding me from her with his wings.”"],[26,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away and Abu Bakr was appointed as successor, al-Abbas disputed with Ali concerning things the Messenger of God ﷺ had left, bringing the case to Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said: “A thing the Messenger of God ﷺ left and did not move, I will not move it.”"],[27,"Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet ﷺ while he was dead."],[28,"Ibn al-Zubayr was mentioned, and he said: “How long he has been eager for command.” I said: “And what is that?” He said: “A thief was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered him to be killed. It was said: ‘He stole.’ He said: ‘Cut off his hand.’ Then he was brought after that to Abu Bakr having stolen, and his limbs had been cut off. Abu Bakr said: ‘I find nothing for you except what the Messenger of God ﷺ decreed for you on the day he ordered your killing, for he knew you better.’ So he ordered him to be killed by young boys from the sons of the Muhajirun, I among them. Ibn al-Zubayr said: ‘Put me in command over you.’ So we put him in command over us, and we went with him to al-Baqi and killed him.”"],[29,"Ghassan b. al-Rabi narrated to us, from Layth b. Saʿd, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah b. Amr b. al-As, from Abu Bakr."],[30,"Yazid b. Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah b. Amr, from Abu Bakr, who said:"],[31,"He said to the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Teach me a supplication I can use in my prayer.” He said: “O God, I have wronged myself greatly—and in the hadith of al-Qawariri alone from Asim: much—and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me with forgiveness from You and have mercy on me. You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"],[32,"O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication I can use in my prayer and in my house. He said: “Say: O God, I have wronged myself greatly, and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me with forgiveness from You and have mercy on me. You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"],[33,"The Dajjal will emerge from a land toward the east called Khurasan, followed by peoples whose faces are like hammered shields."],[34,"Abu Musa Harun b. Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, al-Fazari—meaning Abu Ishaq—narrated to me, from Abd Allah b. Shawdhab. 35—And al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyya, the son-in-law of Abu Ishaq, narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira b. Subay, from Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr, who said:"],[35,"Fatima sent to Abu Bakr, saying: “What is the matter with you, O successor of the Messenger of God ﷺ? Did you inherit the Messenger of God, or his family?” He said: “No, rather his family.” She said: “Then what about the share of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “I heard him say: ‘When God feeds a prophet a morsel and then takes him to Himself, He assigns it to the one who comes after him.’ So I considered—I, after him—that I should return it to the Muslims.” She said: “You and what you heard from the Messenger of God.”"],[36,"I went out with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq after the ʿAsr prayer, nights after the death of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and ʿAli was walking at his side. He passed by al-Hasan b. ʿAli while he was playing with the boys, so Abu Bakr lifted him onto his shoulder and began saying: 'May my father be ransomed for the one who resembles the Prophet, not one who resembles ʿAli!' He said: And ʿAli was laughing."],[37,"I saw Abu Bakr carrying al-Hasan b. ʿAli and saying: 'May my father be ransomed for the one who resembles the Prophet, not one who resembles ʿAli,' while ʿAli was with him, smiling."],[38,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Maʿiz b. Malik came to him and confessed to fornication. He sent him back. Then he came a second time and he sent him back. Then he came a third time and he sent him back. I said: 'If you come a fourth time, he will stone you.' So he came a fourth time, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be detained. Then he sent someone to ask about him, and they said: 'We know nothing but good of him.' So he ordered that he be stoned."],[39,"That the Prophet ﷺ sent Maʿiz b. Malik back four times."],[40,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out at the time of al-Hudaybiyah with some ten and some hundred of his companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfah, the Prophet ﷺ garlanded the sacrificial animal, marked it, and entered ihram for ʿumrah. Then ʿUrwah b. Masʿud al-Thaqafi came and said: 'I see faces that are likely to flee and abandon you.' Abu Bakr said: 'Suck the clitoris of al-Lat! Would we flee and abandon him?'"],[41,"That Fatimah bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ asked Abu Bakr after the death of the Messenger of God to divide for her her inheritance from what the Messenger of God ﷺ left, from what God had granted him as spoils. Abu Bakr said to her: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity.\"'"],[42,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to do something, he would say: 'O God, choose for me and select for me.'"],[43,"They differed about the burial of the Prophet ﷺ when he passed away. Abu Bakr said: 'I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"A prophet is not taken except in the place most beloved to him.\"' So he said: 'Bury him where he was taken.'"],[44,"A man from the polytheists came and faced the Messenger of God ﷺ with his private parts while urinating. I said: 'O Messenger of God, does not the man see us?' He said: 'If he saw us, he would not face us with his private parts,' meaning while they were in the cave."],[45,"That when ʿAbd Allah b. Abu Bakr died, he was wept over. Abu Bakr went out to the men and said: 'I apologize to you concerning these women; they are new to the covenant from the time of ignorance. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The deceased is scalded with boiling water because of the weeping of the living.\"'"],[46,"That Abu Bakr entered upon the Prophet ﷺ after his death, placed his mouth between his eyes, placed his hands on his temples, and said: 'O my Prophet, O my close friend, O my chosen one.'"],[47,"That Abu Bakr stood in the place of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the following year, the year in which the Messenger of God ﷺ died, and said: 'I heard your Prophet ﷺ in the summer the previous year, in a place like this place of mine,' then his eyes overflowed, then he said: 'I heard your Prophet ﷺ in the summer the previous year, in a place like my place,' then his eyes overflowed, then he said: 'I heard your Prophet ﷺ in the summer the previous year, in a place like this place of mine,' then his eyes overflowed, then he said: 'I heard your Prophet ﷺ , in a place like this place of mine, saying: \"Ask God for pardon, well-being, and protection in this world and the Hereafter.\"'"],[48,"Abu Bakr entered upon her while two slave girls were with her beating two duffs, so Abu Bakr scolded them. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Leave them, for every people has a festival.'"],[49,"I saw my father praying in a single garment, so I said: 'O father! You pray in a single garment while your clothes are set aside?' He said: 'O my daughter, the last prayer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed behind me was in a single garment.'"],[50,"They said to her: 'What is the harshest thing you saw the polytheists do to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' She said: 'The polytheists sat in the mosque, discussing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and what he said about their gods. While they were doing so, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached, so they all rose against him. The cry came to Abu Bakr, and it was said: \"Help your companion.\" He went out from us, having four braids, saying: \"Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah, when he has brought you clear proofs from your Lord?\" They left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and turned to Abu Bakr.' She said: 'Abu Bakr returned to us, and he did not touch any of his braids without it coming off with it, saying: \"Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.\"'"],[51,"When 'Perish the hands of Abu Lahab' was revealed, the one-eyed Umm Jamil came with a wail and a stone in her hand, saying: 'Mudhammam we have rejected – or: we have come, the doubt is from Abu Musa – and his religion we have despised, and his command we have disobeyed.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and Abu Bakr was beside him – or he said: with him. Abu Bakr said: 'This one has approached, and I fear she may see you.' He said: 'She will not see me,' and he recited a Qur'an with which he sought protection: 'And when you recite the Qur'an, We put between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter a hidden barrier.' He said: 'She came and stood over Abu Bakr and did not see the Prophet ﷺ. She said: \"O Abu Bakr, I have heard that your companion has satirized me.\" Abu Bakr said: \"No, by the Lord of this House, he has not satirized you.\" She left saying: \"Quraysh know that I am the daughter of their chief.\"'"],[52,"She gave birth at Dhu al-Hulayfah, so Abu Bakr asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Order her to bathe and enter ihram.'"],[53,"I went out with two anklets to sell them, and our family had become in need of provisions. I saw Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and he said: 'Where do you intend?' I said: 'Our family has become in need of provisions, so I wanted to sell these two anklets.' He said: 'I have come out with some dirhams wanting better silver than them.' He placed the anklets in one pan and the dirhams in the other, and the anklets outweighed the dirhams somewhat. He called for a pair of scissors. I said: 'Glory be to Allah! It is yours, it is yours.' He said: 'If you leave it, Allah will not leave it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like. The one who gives more and the one who takes more are in the Fire.\"'"],[54,"What will happen of the affairs of this world and the Hereafter was shown to me. The first and the last were gathered on one plain, and the people were terrified. They went to Adam, while sweat almost bridled them, and said: 'O Adam, you are the father of mankind, and Allah chose you; intercede for us with your Lord.' He said: 'I have faced the like of what you faced. Go to your father after your father, to Noah, for Allah chose Noah and the family of Abraham and the family of Imran over all worlds.' So they went to Noah and said: 'Intercede for us with your Lord. Allah chose you and answered your supplication, and you did not leave on earth any of the disbelievers.' He said: 'That is not with me. Go to Moses, for Allah spoke to him directly.' Moses said: 'That is not with me, but go to Jesus, for he used to heal the blind and the leper and raise the dead.' Jesus said: 'That is not with me, but go to the master of the children of Adam, for he is the first from whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection. Go to Muhammad, and he will intercede for you with your Lord.' So he goes, and Gabriel is called. Gabriel comes to his Lord, and Allah says: 'Give him permission and give him the good news of Paradise.' Gabriel takes him, and he falls prostrate for a week. Then Allah says: 'O Muhammad, raise your head; speak and you will be heard, intercede and you will be granted intercession.' He raises his head, and when he looks at his Lord he falls prostrate for another week. Allah says: 'O Muhammad, raise your head; speak and you will be heard, intercede and you will be granted intercession.' He falls prostrate again, and Gabriel takes him by his upper arms. Allah opens for him from supplication something He never opened for any human. He says: 'O Lord, You made me master of the children of Adam, and no boast; and the first from whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast, until the cistern will come to me, larger than the distance between San'a and Eilat.' Then it is said: 'Call the truthful ones,' and they intercede. Then it is said: 'Call the prophets.' A prophet ﷺ comes with a band, a prophet with five or six, and a prophet with no one. Then it is said: 'Call the martyrs,' and they intercede for whom they wish. When the martyrs finish, the Blessed and Exalted says: 'I am the Most Merciful of the merciful. Admit into My Paradise whoever did not associate anything with Me.' They enter Paradise. Then Allah says: 'Look into the Fire: is there anyone who ever did any good?' They find a man in the Fire, and he is asked: 'Did you ever do any good?' He says: 'No, except that I used to be lenient in selling.' Allah says: 'Be lenient to My servant as he was lenient to My servants.' He is brought out of the Fire. And another man, and Allah says: 'Did you ever do any good?' He says: 'No, except that I commanded my children: when I die, burn me, then grind me until I become like kohl, then take me to the sea and scatter me in the wind.' Allah says: 'Why did you do that?' He says: 'From fear of You.' He says: 'Look at the kingdom of the greatest king, for you will have its like and ten times its like.' He says: 'Do You mock me while You are the King?' That is the one at whom I laughed in the forenoon."],[55,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke one day"],[56,"Shirk among you is more hidden than the crawling of an ant. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is shirk anything but what is worshiped besides Allah – or: called upon with Allah, the doubt is from Abd al-Malik.' He said: 'May your mother lose you, O Siddiq! Shirk among you is more hidden than the crawling of an ant. Shall I not tell you of a saying that removes its small and its great – or: its small and its great?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Say every day three times: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating anything with You while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\" Shirk is for a person to say: \"Allah and so-and-so gave me,\" and the rival is for a person to say: \"Were it not for so-and-so, so-and-so would have killed me.\"'"],[57,"Amr b. al-Husayn narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Muslim narrated to us, from Layth b. Abi Sulaym, from Abu Muhammad, from Ma'qil b. Yasar. Abu Bakr narrated to me from the Prophet ﷺ that he said:"],[58,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ with Abu Bakr, or he said: Abu Bakr narrated to me from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: 'Shirk is more hidden among you than the crawling of an ant.' Then he said: 'Shall I not guide you to what removes from you its small and its great? Say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating anything with You while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\"'"],[59,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ with Abu Bakr, or he said: Abu Bakr narrated to me from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: 'Shirk is more hidden among you than the crawling of an ant.' Abu Bakr said: 'Is shirk anything but one who calls upon another god with Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shirk is more hidden among you than the crawling of an ant.' Then he said: 'Shall I not guide you to what removes from you its small and its great? Say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating anything with You while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\"'"],[60,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the cave, and he said: O Allah, (grant us) a stabbing and a plague. I said: O Messenger of God, I know that you have asked for the modes of death of your community; this stabbing we know, so what is the plague? He said: An abscess like boils; if you live long you will see it."],[61,"Abu Bakr sent for me after the killing of the people of al-Yamama, and I came, and there was Umar with him. Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of al-Umari, and added in it after the statement of Zayd b. Thabit: \"so I attached it,\" he said: Ibn Shihab said: On that day they differed regarding \"al-tabut,\" so Zayd said: \"al-tabuh,\" and the Qurayshi group said: \"al-tabut,\" so they referred their difference to Uthman, and he said: Write it as \"al-tabut,\" in the dialect of Quraysh. Ibn Shihab said: And Ibn Mas'ud had disliked that Zayd was appointed to copy the codices. Ibn Shihab said: And Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah narrated to me that Abd Allah said: O assembly of Muslims, am I to be removed from the Book of God and a man appointed to it, by God, I became Muslim while he was in the loins of a disbelieving man? meaning Zayd b. Thabit. He said: For that reason Abd Allah said: O people of Iraq - or: O people of Kufa - hide the codices that you have and conceal them, for God says: And whoever withholds [something], will come with what he withheld on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn Shihab said: It reached me that men among the virtuous companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ disliked this statement of his."],[62,"Abu Bakr sent for me after the killing of the people of al-Yamama, and there was Umar b. al-Khattab with him. He said: Umar came to me and said: The killing has intensified among the reciters of the Qur'an on the day of al-Yamama, and I fear that killing will intensify among the reciters in all the battlefields, and much of the Qur'an will be lost. I think you should command that it be collected. Abu Bakr said: I said to Umar: How can I do something the Messenger of God ﷺ did not do? Umar said: It is, by God, good. Umar kept coming back to me until God expanded my chest for what He had expanded Umar's chest for, and I saw in it what he saw. Zayd said: Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not suspect you; you used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of God ﷺ, so pursue the Qur'an and collect it. He said: By God, if they had tasked me with moving a mountain among the mountains, it would not have been heavier upon me than that. He said: I said: How can you do something the Messenger of God ﷺ did not do? Abu Bakr said: It is, by God, good. Abu Bakr and Umar kept coming back to me until God expanded my chest for what He had expanded the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar for. So I pursued the Qur'an, collecting it from parchments, palm stalks, stones, and thin stones, and from the hearts of men, and I found at the end of Surat al-Tawbah (Bara'ah) with Khuzaymah b. Thabit: There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves, to the end of the verse."],[63,"Zayd b. Thabit narrated to him that Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not suspect you; you used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of God ﷺ, so pursue the Qur'an and collect it."],[64,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ while we were in the cave: If one of them looked at the bottom of his feet, he would see us beneath his feet. He said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two when God is the third of them?"],[65,"I looked at the feet of the polytheists above our heads while we were in the cave, and I said: O Messenger of God, if one of them looked at his feet, he would see us beneath his feet. He said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two when God is the third of them?"],[66,"Umar said to Abu Bakr, regarding the apostasy: Didn't the Messenger of God ﷺ say: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but God, and when they say it, they have protected from me their blood and their property except by its right, and their reckoning is upon God? Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: - and in the hadith of Ibn Abi Sumaynah: Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God ﷺ only said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but God, and establish prayer, and give zakah. By God, if they withheld from me a rope, I would fight them over it until my soul meets God. Umar said: When I saw that Abu Bakr was determined on that, I knew that it was the truth."],[67,"Abu Bakr said to Umar after the death of the Messenger of God ﷺ: Come with us to Umm Ayman to visit her as the Messenger of God ﷺ used to visit her. When we reached her, she wept, and they said to her: What makes you weep? What is with God is better for His Messenger. She said: I do not weep because I do not know that what is with God is better for His Messenger, but I weep because the revelation has ceased from heaven. He said: She stirred them to weep, and they both wept with her."],[68,"Abu Bakr entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was gloomy, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: Why do I see you gloomy? He said: O Messenger of God, I was with a cousin of mine last night, so-and-so, and he was struggling with death. He said: Why didn't you prompt him to say: There is no god but God? He said: I did, O Messenger of God. He said: Did he say it? He said: Yes. He said: Paradise is guaranteed for him. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, how is it for the living? He said: It is more destructive of their sins, it is more destructive of their sins."],[69,"Abu Bakr sent for him after the killing of the people of al-Yamama. He said: I came to him, and there was Umar with him. Abu Bakr said: Umar came to me and said: The killing has intensified among the people of al-Yamama from the reciters of the Qur'an - or: the people, Abu Yala was uncertain - so I fear that killing will intensify in all the battlefields, and much of the Qur'an will be lost without being retained. I think you should command the collection of the Qur'an. I said to Umar: How can I do something the Messenger of God ﷺ did not do? Umar said: It is, by God, good. He kept coming back to me in that matter until God expanded my chest, and I saw in it what Umar saw. Zayd said: And Umar was sitting with him, not speaking. Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not suspect you; you used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of God ﷺ, so pursue the Qur'an and collect it. Zayd said: By God, if they had tasked me with moving a mountain among the mountains, it would not have been heavier upon me than what he commanded me regarding the collection of the Qur'an. I said: How can you do something the Messenger of God ﷺ did not do? He said: It is, by God, good. He kept coming back to me until God expanded my chest for what He expanded the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar for. So I collected the Qur'an, pursuing it from parchments, shoulder blades, and the hearts of men, until I found the last part of Surat al-Tawbah with Khuzaymah al-Ansari; I did not find it with anyone else: There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves, to the end of the verse. The codices in which we collected the Qur'an were with Abu Bakr during his lifetime until God took him, then with Umar until God took him, then with Hafsah."],[70,"Uqbah b. Amir came to Mu'awiyah while he was in Ilya, and he did not stay long before he left, so he was sought and not found - or he said: we sought him and did not find him - so we followed him, and there he was praying in an open area of land. He said: What brought you? They said: We came to renew our covenant with you, or to fulfill your right. He said: I have your gift. We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and each man among us had the task of tending the camels for a day, and it was my day to tend them. He said: I brought the camels back in the evening and came to the Prophet ﷺ, and his companions had gathered around him while he was speaking. He said: I let the camels go and headed toward him, and I reached him while he was saying: Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two units seeking thereby the face of God, God will forgive him what was before them. I said: God is greatest. He said: A man struck my shoulder, so I turned, and there was Abu Bakr. He said: O Ibn Amir, what was before it is better. I said: What was before it? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, his heart confirming his tongue, will enter from any of the gates of Paradise he wishes."],[71,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, or rejects something I commanded, let him take his seat in a house in Hell."],[72,"Abu Bakr stood on the pulpit and said: You know what the Messenger of God ﷺ stood for last year. Then he wept, then he repeated it, then he wept, then he repeated it, then he wept, and said: People have not been given anything in this world better than pardon and well-being, so ask God for both."],[73,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood on the pulpit and delivered a sermon. He praised God and extolled Him, then said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us last year on this pulpit, on a day like this, in a month like this. Then he wept, and said: Ask God for pardon and well-being."],[74,"Abu Bakr was sent on the pilgrimage over which the Messenger of God ﷺ appointed him before the Farewell Pilgrimage, on the Day of Sacrifice, in a group to proclaim among the people that no polytheist should perform Hajj after this year, and no one should circumambulate the House naked."],[75,"Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, teach me words to say when I enter upon morning and when I enter upon evening. He said: Say: O God, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, You are the Lord of everything and its Sovereign; there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, the evil of Satan, and his enticement. Say it when you enter upon morning and when you enter upon evening, and when you retire to your bed."],[76,"Beware of the milking animal—or: beware of those with milk. He took a sheep, slaughtered it and skinned it, and told his wife to cook and bake. He kept cutting meat into the pot and lit a fire under it until the meat and bread were done and he made tharid. Then he ladled broth and meat over it and brought it to us and placed it before us, and we ate until we were full. Then he went to the water skin, which the wind had cooled, and it became cold. He poured into the vessel, then handed it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he drank. Then he handed it to Abu Bakr, and he drank. Then he handed it to Umar, and he drank. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Praise be to God. We went out, and nothing drove us out except hunger, and we returned having obtained this. You will surely be asked about this on the Day of Resurrection; this is part of bliss. Then he said to the Waqifi: Do you not have a servant to give you water? He said: No, O Messenger of God. He said: When captives come to us, come to us so that we may order a servant for you. It was only a short while before captives came to him. The Waqifi came to him and he said: What brings you? He said: O Messenger of God, your promise that you made to me. He said: Here are captives, so stand and choose from among them. He said: You be the one to choose for me. He said: Take this boy and treat him well. He took him and went with him to his wife. She said: What is this? He related the story to her. She said: What did you say to him? He said: I said to him: You be the one to choose for me. She said: You did well. He told you to treat him well, so treat him well. He said: What is treating him well? She said: That you free him. He said: He is free for the sake of God."],[77,"While Abu Bakr was engaged in his work, he became angry with a man among the Muslims, and his anger against him became very intense. When I saw that, I said: O successor of the Messenger of God, shall I strike his neck? When I mentioned killing, he turned away from that whole matter to something else of that sort. When we dispersed, Abu Bakr sent for me afterwards and said: O Abu Barza, what did you say? He said: I had forgotten what I said. He said: I said: And what did I say? Remind me. He said: Do you not remember what you said? I said: No, by God. He said: Do you recall when you saw me angry with the man and you said: Shall I strike his neck, O successor of the Messenger of God? Do you not remember that? Would you have done it? He said: Yes, by God, and even now if you command me, I will do it. He said: Woe to you—or: may your mother be bereaved of you—by God, that is not for anyone after the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[78,"Abu Bakr became angry with a man with such intense anger that none more intense than his anger was seen that day. Abu Barza said to him: O successor of the Messenger of God, command me and I will strike his neck. He said: It was as if a fire was extinguished. He said: Abu Barza went out, then he sent for him and said: May your mother be bereaved of you, what did you say? He said: I said: By God, if you command me to kill him, I will surely kill him. He said: May your mother be bereaved of you, Abu Barza, that was not for anyone after the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[79,"A man was rude to Abu Bakr. He said: I almost killed him. He said: Abu Bakr rebuked me and said: It is not for anyone except the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[80,"A man insulted Abu Bakr. I said: Shall I not strike his neck, O successor of the Messenger of God? He said: No, it is not for anyone after the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[81,"No body nourished with what is unlawful will enter Paradise."],[82,"No body nourished with what is unlawful will enter Paradise."],[83,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ on the wooden pulpit saying: Guard against the Fire, even with half a date. It straightens what is crooked, wards off an evil death, and takes from the hungry the place it takes from the full."],[84,"I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq saying on the pulpit: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he recovered, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he recovered, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this intense heat last year, saying: Ask Allah for pardon, well-being, and certainty in the Hereafter and in this world."],[85,"I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, and Abu Bakr wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he recovered, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying in heat like this last year: Ask Allah for pardon, well-being, and certainty in the Hereafter and in this world."],[86,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited striking those who pray."],[87,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited striking those who pray."],[88,"In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there was a man whose devotion and striving impressed us. We mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by name, but he did not recognize him. We described him by his appearance, but he did not recognize him. While we were mentioning him, the man appeared. We said: Here he is. He said: You are telling me about a man on whose face there is a mark from Satan. He came forward and stood by them without greeting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: I adjure you by Allah, did you say when you stood by the gathering: There is no one among the people better or more virtuous than I? He said: O Allah, yes. Then he entered to pray. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Who will kill the man? Abu Bakr said: I will. He entered upon him and found him standing in prayer. He said: Glory be to Allah, should I kill a man who is praying when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has prohibited killing those who pray? He came out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What did you do? He said: I disliked killing him while he was praying, and you have prohibited killing those who pray. Umar said: I will. He entered and found him prostrating with his face on the ground. Umar said: Abu Bakr is better than me. He came out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What happened? He said: I found him prostrating, and I disliked killing him. He said: Who will kill the man? Ali said: I will. He said: You, if you catch him. Ali entered and found that he had left. He returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: What happened? He said: I found that he had left. He said: If he had been killed, no two men in my community would have differed. He was the first and the last of them. Musa said: I heard Muhammad b. Ka'b saying: He is the one whom Ali killed, Dhu al-Thudayya."],[89,"Abu Bakr sent for me after the killing of the people of al-Yamama, and Umar b. al-Khattab was with him. Abu Bakr said: Umar came to me and said: The killing was intense on the day of al-Yamama among the reciters of the Quran, and I fear that killing will intensify among the reciters of the Quran in other places, and much of the Quran will be lost. I think you should order that it be collected. I said: How can I do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do? Umar said: By Allah, it is good. He kept arguing with me about it until Allah opened my chest to it, and I saw in it what Umar saw. Zayd b. Thabit said: Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not suspect you. You used to write down the revelation for the Prophet ﷺ. So track down the Quran and collect it. Zayd said: By Allah, if he had tasked me with moving a mountain, it would not have been heavier on me than what he ordered me to do in collecting the Quran. I said: How can you do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do? He said: By Allah, it is good. He kept arguing with me until Allah opened my chest to what He had opened the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar to, and I saw in it what they saw. So I tracked down the Quran, collecting it from parchments, flat stones, palm stalks, and the hearts of men, until I missed the end of Surat al-Tawba. I found it with Khuzayma b. Thabit al-Ansari: 'There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves. Grievous to him is what you suffer; he is concerned over you and to the believers is kind and merciful' up to the end of Bara'a. The sheets remained with Abu Bakr during his life until Allah took him, then with Umar until Allah took him, then with Hafsa."],[90,"Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman came to Uthman b. Affan. He had been campaigning with the people of Syria in the conquest of Armenia and Azerbaijan alongside the people of Iraq. Their differences in recitation alarmed Hudhayfa. Hudhayfa said to Uthman: O Commander of the Faithful, catch this community before they differ about the Book as the Jews and Christians differed. Uthman sent to Hafsa: Send us the sheets so we can copy them into the codices and then return them to you. Hafsa sent them to Uthman. Uthman ordered Zayd b. Thabit, Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, Sa'id b. al-As, and Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith b. Hisham to copy them into the codices. He said to the three Qurayshi men: If you and Zayd b. Thabit differ about anything in the Quran, write it in the language of Quraysh, for it was revealed in their language. They did so. When the sheets had been copied, Uthman returned the sheets to Hafsa and sent to every region a codex of what they had copied, and ordered that everything else containing the Quran, whether a page or a codex, be erased or burned."],[91,"No deceiver or one who mistreats his slaves will enter Paradise. The first to knock on the gate of Paradise will be a male slave or a female slave when they worship their Lord well and are sincere to their master."],[92,"No one who mistreats his slaves will enter Paradise. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not tell us that this community has the most slaves and orphans among nations? He said: So honor them as you honor your children, feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear. He said: What benefit does this world give us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A horse you keep for the sake of Allah, and a slave who suffices you; when he prays, he is your brother, when he prays, he is your brother."],[93,"No deceiver, no miser, no one who reminds others of his favors, and no one who mistreats his slaves will enter Paradise. The first to enter Paradise will be a slave when he obeys Allah and obeys his master."],[94,"No one who mistreats his slaves will enter Paradise. Cursed is one who harms a Muslim or deceives him."],[95,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in a place like where I am standing, then he wept and said: Ask Allah for well-being; for no one has been given anything better than well-being, except certainty. Abu Mu'awiya said: except certainty."],[96,"I said: O Messenger of God, how can there be well-being after this verse: “Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it”? Are we to be recompensed for everything that occurs from us? He said: May God have mercy on you, Abu Bakr. Do you not grieve? Do you not toil? Do you not suffer hardship? I said: Yes. He said: That is what you are recompensed for."],[97,"I said: O Messenger of God, how can there be well-being after this verse: “Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it”? He said: May God have mercy on you, Abu Bakr. Do you not toil? Do you not suffer hardship? That is what you are recompensed for."],[98,"O Messenger of God, how can there be well-being after this verse: “Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it”? Is every evil we do requited? He said: May God have mercy on you, Abu Bakr. Do you not fall ill? Do you not toil? Do you not suffer hardship? That is what you are recompensed for."],[99,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: How can there be well-being after this verse: “Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it”? Is every evil we do requited? The Prophet ﷺ said to him: May God forgive you—or: May God have mercy on you—do you not fall ill? Do you not grieve? Do you not suffer hardship?"],[100,"Abu Bakr met Talha and said: Why do I see you looking distressed? He said: A word I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, which he claimed is efficacious, and I did not ask him about it. Abu Bakr said: I know what it is. He said: What is it? He said: There is no god but God."],[101,"The Prophet stopped at a place, and a woman sent him a sheep with her son. He milked it, then said: Take it to your mother. She drank until satisfied. Then he came with another sheep, milked it, and gave Abu Bakr to drink. Then he came with another sheep, milked it, and drank."],[102,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him with Bara’ah to the people of Makkah: No polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year, and no one shall circumambulate the House naked, and none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul. Whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of God ﷺ, its term is until its duration. God and His Messenger are free from the polytheists. He said: He traveled with it for three days, then he said to Ali: Catch up with him, and send Abu Bakr back to me, and deliver it yourself. He said: He did so. When Abu Bakr came to the Prophet ﷺ, he wept and said: O Messenger of God, has something happened concerning me? He said: Nothing has happened concerning you except good, but I was commanded that no one should deliver it except myself or a man from my family."],[103,"Go out and call among the people: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, Paradise is assured for him. He said: I went out, and Umar b. al-Khattab met me and said: What is the matter with you, Abu Bakr? I said: The Messenger of God ﷺ told me: Go out and call among the people that whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, Paradise is assured for him. Umar said: Return to the Messenger of God ﷺ, for I fear that they will rely on it. So I returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: What brought you back? I informed him of Umar’s words. He said: He is right."],[104,"A man from the captives, from Tahiyah, called Bayrah b. Asad, came out as an emigrant to Madinah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had died shortly before that. He said: Umar b. al-Khattab saw Bayrah walking in the streets of Madinah and did not recognize him, so he said: Who are you? He said: I am a man from the people of Oman. He took his hand and went with him to Abu Bakr, and said: O Abu Bakr, this is from the land whose people I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ mention, from the people of Oman. Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: I know a land whose side the sea splashes, with a tribe of Arabs. If my messenger came to them, they would not shoot him with an arrow or stone."],[105,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: What has made you gray? He said: Hud, al-Waqi‘ah, ‘Amma Yatasa’alun, and Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat have made me gray."],[106,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: What has made you gray?"],[107,"The siwak is a means of purification for the mouth and a source of pleasure for the Lord."],[108,"The siwak is a purification for the mouth, pleasing to the Lord."],[109,"The people of Paradise do not engage in trade, and if they were to trade, they would trade only in fine cloth."],[110,"Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise without reckoning, their faces like the moon on the night of the full moon, their hearts like the heart of one man. I asked my Lord for more, so He increased me, with every man, seventy thousand. Abu Bakr said: We used to think that this encompassed the people of the villages and included those who increased from the desert dwellers."],[111,"When we set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Makkah to Madinah, we passed by a shepherd. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was thirsty, so I milked a small amount of milk for him and brought it to him, and he drank until I was satisfied."],[112,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from Makkah to Madinah, Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum pursued him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against him, and his horse sank with him into the ground. He said: Supplicate to Allah, and I will not harm you. He said: So he supplicated to Allah for him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became thirsty, and they passed by a shepherd of sheep. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I took a bowl and milked a small amount of milk for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, brought it to him, and he drank until I was satisfied."],[113,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from Makkah to Madinah, Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum pursued him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against him, and his horse sank with him into the ground. He said: Supplicate to Allah for me, and I will not harm you. So he supplicated for him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became thirsty, and they passed by a shepherd. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I took a bowl and milked into it a small amount of milk, brought it to him, and he drank, then he drank until I was satisfied."],[114,"Abu Bakr bought a mount from Abu for thirteen dirhams. He said: Tell al-Bara' to carry it to my mount. He said: No, not until you tell me how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah for Madinah. He said: We set out and we were delayed our day and our night until it became noon - or he said: the midday stood - then I cast my eyes and saw a rock that had a remnant of shade, so I sprinkled it and spread a fur for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in it. I said: Sleep, O Messenger of Allah. Then I went about inspecting what was around me, to see if I could see anyone from the pursuit. Then I saw a shepherd of sheep wanting from the rock the same as I wanted. I said: Who are you, O boy? He said: For a man of Quraysh. I recognized him. I said: Is there any milk in your sheep? He said: Yes. I said: Will you milk for us? He said: Yes. So I ordered him, and he restrained a ewe from the sheep, then I ordered him, and he shook its udder, then I ordered him, and he shook his hands from the dust, then he milked a small amount of milk for me. I had a water skin with a cloth over its mouth, so I poured water over the milk. Then I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I found him awake. I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah. Then we set out, and no one from the pursuit caught up with us except Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum on a horse of his. I said: This is the pursuit catching us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not grieve; indeed, Allah is with us. When he drew near, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against him, and his horse sank into the ground up to its belly. He jumped off it and said: O Muhammad, I know that this is your doing. Supplicate to Allah to deliver me from what I am in, and I will conceal your whereabouts from those behind me. This is my quiver, so take an arrow from it. You will pass by my camels and my servants at such-and-such a place, so take from them what you need. He said: I have no need of your camels. Then we arrived in Madinah at night. They disputed as to which of them the Messenger of Allah would stay with. He said: I will stay with the Banu al-Najjar, the maternal uncles of Abd al-Muttalib, honoring them by that. Then the men and women climbed above the houses, and the boys and servants spread out in the roads calling: O Muhammad, O Messenger of Allah, O Muhammad, O Messenger of Allah."],[115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Which deed is best? He said: The raising of the voice in talbiyah and the shedding of blood of sacrificial animals."],[116,"Between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is over a canal from the canals of Paradise."],[117,"The grandmother came to Abu Bakr asking him about her inheritance. He said: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and you have nothing in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so return until I ask the people."],[118,"The grandmother came to Abu Bakr after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I have been told that I have a right. Abu Bakr said: I do not find for you in the Book any right, nor have I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give you anything. He said: Then al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah testified. He said: Who will testify with you? Muhammad b. Maslamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her one sixth. Al-Zuhri said: She is the mother of the father's mother or the father. When Umar came, the one who differed from her came. Umar said: Whichever of you is alone in it, it is hers, and if you both are together, it is between you."],[119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us in the first year. Then Abu Bakr wept and said: Ask Allah for well-being, for people have not been given in this world, after certainty, anything better than well-being. Indeed, adhere to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and they are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and they are in Hell. Do not sever ties, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers as Allah commanded you."],[120,"Adhere to truthfulness, for it accompanies righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it accompanies wickedness, and both are in the Fire. Do not sever ties with one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers as Allah has commanded you."],[121,"I heard Abu Bakr address us when he was appointed caliph. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in this place of mine last year, then wept, then said: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being."],[122,"He said when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us last year in this place of mine, then said: Ask Allah for well-being, for no one has been given anything better after certainty than well-being."],[123,"He read the letter of Umar b. al-Khattab: that nothing is due on fewer than five camels; when they reach five, one ewe is due up to nine; when they are ten, two ewes up to fourteen; when they reach fifteen, three ewes up to nineteen; when they reach twenty, four ewes up to twenty-four; when they reach twenty-five, a one-year-old she-camel is due up to thirty-five; when they exceed that, a two-year-old she-camel is due up to forty-five; when they exceed that, a three-year-old she-camel is due up to sixty; when they exceed that, two two-year-old she-camels are due up to ninety; when they exceed that, two three-year-old she-camels are due up to one hundred and twenty; when they exceed that, for every fifty a three-year-old she-camel is due, and for every forty a two-year-old she-camel. And nothing is due on sheep fewer than forty; when they reach forty, one ewe is due up to one hundred and twenty; when they exceed that, two ewes up to two hundred; if they exceed two hundred, three ewes up to three hundred; when they exceed three hundred, for every hundred one ewe."],[124,"We saw with Thumama b. Abd Allah b. Anas a letter that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq wrote for Anas b. Malik when he sent him to collect the zakat of al-Bahrayn, bearing the seal of the Prophet ﷺ, containing a statement like this."],[125,"These are the obligatory alms that Allah enjoined upon His Messenger. Whoever among the Muslims is asked for them in their proper manner should give them, and whoever is asked for more should not give it: For fewer than twenty-five camels, for every five a ewe; when they reach twenty-five, a one-year-old she-camel is due up to thirty-five; if there is no one-year-old she-camel, then a male two-year-old camel; when they reach thirty-six, a two-year-old she-camel is due up to forty-five; when they reach forty-six, a three-year-old she-camel that has been covered by the stallion is due up to sixty; when they reach sixty-one, a four-year-old she-camel is due up to seventy-five; when they reach seventy-six, two two-year-old she-camels are due up to ninety; when they reach ninety-one, two three-year-old she-camels that have been covered by the stallion are due up to one hundred and twenty; when they exceed one hundred and twenty, for every forty a two-year-old she-camel, and for every fifty a three-year-old she-camel. If the ages of camels differ in the obligatory alms, then whoever owes a four-year-old she-camel but does not have one and has a three-year-old she-camel, it may be accepted from him, and he adds two ewes if they are easy for him, or twenty dirhams. Whoever owes a three-year-old she-camel but has only a four-year-old she-camel, it may be accepted from him, and the collector gives him twenty dirhams or two ewes. Whoever owes a three-year-old she-camel but does not have one and has a two-year-old she-camel, it may be accepted from him, and he adds two ewes if they are easy for him, or twenty dirhams. Whoever owes a two-year-old she-camel but has only a three-year-old she-camel, it may be accepted from him, and the collector gives him twenty dirhams or two ewes. Whoever owes a two-year-old she-camel but does not have one and has a one-year-old she-camel, it may be accepted from him, and he adds two ewes if they are easy for him, or twenty dirhams. Whoever owes a one-year-old she-camel but has only a male two-year-old camel, it may be accepted from him without anything added. Whoever has only four camels, nothing is due unless their owner wishes. On zakat of sheep in their grazing herds, when they are forty, one ewe is due up to one hundred and twenty; when they exceed that, two ewes up to two hundred; when they exceed that, three ewes up to three hundred; when they exceed that by one, for every hundred one ewe. In zakat, no old ewe, no defective animal, and no male goat is to be taken unless the collector wishes. Herds should not be combined, and combined herds should not be separated out of fear of zakat. Whatever belongs to two partners, they settle between themselves equally. If a man's grazing herd is one ewe short of forty, nothing is due unless its owner wishes. On silver, one quarter of one tenth is due; if the wealth is only one hundred and ninety dirhams, nothing is due unless its owner wishes."],[126,"O people, you recite this verse and apply it other than as Allah applied it: O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided. When people see wrongdoing and do not change it, Allah is about to encompass them all with punishment."],[127,"Ubayd Allah b. Muadh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us; from al-Hakam, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the like of that, without mentioning the Prophet ﷺ."],[128,"When people see wrongdoing and do not change it, Allah is about to encompass them all with punishment."],[129,"O people, you recite this verse and apply it other than its proper places: O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided. We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When people see wrongdoing and do not change it, Allah is about to encompass them all with His punishment."],[130,"Abu Bakr recited this verse: O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided. Then he said: People apply this verse other than its proper place. Verily, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When a people see an oppressor and do not seize his hands, and see wrongdoing and do not change it, Allah encompasses them all with His punishment."],[131,"Umar b. al-Khattab passed by Uthman while he was sitting in the mosque and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting. He entered upon Abu Bakr and complained about that to him, saying: I passed by Uthman and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. He said: Where is he? He said: He is sitting in the mosque. He said: So we went to him, and Abu Bakr said to him: What prevented you from returning your brother's greeting when he greeted you? He said: By Allah, I did not realize that he greeted me. He passed by me while I was talking to myself, and I did not notice his greeting. Abu Bakr said: What were you talking to yourself about? He said: Satan withdrew with me and began casting into my mind things that I would not love to have spoken even if I had all that is on earth. When Satan cast that into my mind, I said to myself: Would that I had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what saves us from this whispering that Satan casts into our minds. Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him: What saves us from this whispering that Satan casts into our minds? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It saves you to say the like of what I commanded my uncle at death, but he did not do it."],[132,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood up after the death of the Prophet ﷺ and said: You know what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said among you last year. He said: Ask Allah for well-being, for no servant has been given anything better than well-being except certainty of faith. I ask Allah for certainty of faith and well-being."],[133,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said while on the pulpit, and he wept: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the summer of last year, while the covenant was recent, saying: Ask Allah for certainty of faith and well-being."],[134,"Hold to 'There is no god but Allah' and seeking forgiveness, and do them abundantly, for Iblis said: I destroy people through sins, but they destroy me through 'There is no god but Allah' and seeking forgiveness. When I saw that, I destroyed them through whims and desires while they think they are guided."],[135,"One who seeks forgiveness is not persistent in sin, even if he returns to it seventy times in a day."],[136,"Ishaq b. Abi Isra'il and others narrated to us: Abu Yahya Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from Uthman b. Waqid, from Abu Nusayra, from a freed slave of Abu Bakr, from Abu Bakr, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, something similar."],[137,"Whoever seeks forgiveness is not persistent in sin, even if he returns to it seventy times in a day."],[138,"We were with Umar b. al-Khattab in Madinah. We sighted the new moon. I was a man of sharp sight, and I saw it while no one else claimed to have seen it. I kept saying to Umar: 'Do you not see it?' but he could not see it. Umar said: 'I will see it while lying on my bed.' Then he began to tell us about the people of Badr, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed us the places where the people of Badr would fall the day before, saying: 'This is where so-and-so will fall tomorrow, if Allah wills.' Umar said: By the One who sent him with the truth, they did not miss the spots that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had marked. They were thrown into a well, one on top of another. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went until he reached them and said: 'O so-and-so son of so-and-so, and O so-and-so son of so-and-so, have you found what Allah and His Messenger promised you to be true? For I have found what Allah promised me to be true.' Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to bodies without souls?' He said: 'You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, except that they cannot reply to me.'"],[139,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed us at al-Jabiya and said: O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I stand among you today. He said: Be good to my Companions, then to those who follow them, then lying will spread until a man testifies without being asked to testify and swears an oath without being asked to swear. Whoever desires the spaciousness of Paradise, let him adhere to the community, for Satan is with the solitary individual and is farther from two. Let none of you be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Whoever is pleased by his good deeds and grieved by his evil deeds is a believer."],[140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in my place among you today and said: Indeed, be good to my Companions, then to those who follow them. Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Shayban."],[141,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed the people at al-Jabiya and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in a place like this one of mine and said: Be good to my Companions, then to those who follow them, then to those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man swears an oath before being asked to swear and testifies before being asked to testify. Whoever among you loves to attain the spaciousness of Paradise, let him adhere to the community, for Satan is with the solitary individual and is farther from two. Indeed, let no man be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Indeed, whoever among you is grieved by his evil deeds and pleased by his good deeds is a believer."],[142,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he came upon a man, and it was said: He has not broken his fast for such and such a time. He said: He neither fasted nor broke his fast—or: He did not fast and did not break his fast, Ghaylan was unsure. When Umar saw the Prophet's ﷺ anger, he said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting two days and breaking fast one day? He said: Can anyone endure that? I said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting one day and breaking fast one day? He said: That is the fast of my brother Dawud. He said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting one day and breaking fast two days? He said: Who can endure that? He said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting on Mondays? He said: That is the day I was born and the day prophethood was sent down to me. He said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting the day of Arafah and the day of Ashura. He said: One of them expiates and the other said: what is before it, or what is after it, Abu Hilal was unsure."],[143,"I came to Madinah when a disease had struck it, and people were dying rapidly. I sat with Umar b. al-Khattab. A funeral procession passed by and its deceased was praised with good, so Umar said: It has become obligatory. Then another passed by and its deceased was spoken of with evil, so Umar said: It has become obligatory. Abu al-Aswad said: I asked: What has become obligatory, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I said as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Any Muslim for whom four people testify to good, Allah will admit him to Paradise. We said: And three? He said: And three. We said: And two? He said: And two. Then we did not ask him about one."],[144,"O people, be not deceived concerning stoning. Be not deceived concerning stoning, for the Messenger of God ﷺ stoned, and Abu Bakr stoned, and I have stoned. There will come people who deny stoning, intercession, the Dajjal, and people who will come out of the Fire after it has scorched them — or: after they have been scorched."],[145,"He forbade prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."],[146,"Umar b. al-Khattab was riding alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ on one of his journeys, and he asked him about something, but he did not answer him. Then he asked him again, but he did not answer him. Then he asked him again, but he did not answer him. Umar said: I said to myself: 'May your mother lose you, Umar! You asked the Messenger of God ﷺ three times, and every time he did not answer you.' So I spurred my camel and went ahead of the people. No sooner had I done so than I heard a caller crying out, so I went back. I said: 'I feared that something of the Qur'an had been revealed concerning me.' I greeted him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A surah was revealed to me tonight that is dearer to me than all that the sun rises upon.' Then he recited: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that God may forgive you your past and future sins.'"],[147,"Gold for silver is usury, except hand to hand. Barley for barley is usury, except hand to hand. And in Ishaq's version: dates for dates is usury, except hand to hand."],[148,"I attended the Eid prayer with Umar b. al-Khattab. He began with the prayer before the sermon and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade fasting on these two days. As for the day of Fitr, it is your breaking of fast after your fasting; as for the day of Adha, eat from the meat of your sacrifices. He did not mention more than this."],[149,"When the sun declined, Umar ascended the pulpit and the muezzins called the adhan. He delivered a sermon, praised God and extolled Him, and said in his sermon: Stoning is a true punishment for the married person when there is clear evidence, pregnancy, or confession. The Messenger of God ﷺ stoned, and we stoned with him and after him."],[150,"I attended the Eid prayer with Umar. He began with the prayer before the sermon, then said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade fasting on these two days. As for the day of Adha, you eat from your sacrifices; as for the day of Fitr, it is your breaking of fast after your fasting. He said: I also attended it with Uthman. He began with the prayer before the sermon, and it coincided with a Friday. He said: This is a day on which two Eids have come together. Whoever is here from the people of al-Awali, we have given him permission: if he wishes, he may return, and if he wishes to stay, he may stay. Then I attended it with Ali. He began with the prayer before the sermon and said: None of you should eat from his sacrifice beyond three days."],[151,"Do not praise me excessively as the Christians praised Jesus son of Mary. Say: Servant of God and His Messenger."],[152,"Do not prevent the female servants of God from the mosques of God."],[153,"The deceased is punished by the weeping of his family over him."],[154,"The deceased is punished in his grave as long as wailing is done over him."],[155,"The deceased is punished in his grave as long as wailing is done over him — or: as long as weeping is done over him."],[156,"The deceased is tormented by his family's weeping over him."],[157,"He forbade prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and after 'asr until the sun sets."],[158,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'Tell me who among the people of faith is most excellent in faith.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, the angels.' He said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs. What prevents them, when God has placed them in the station He placed them in? Rather, others.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, the prophets whom God honored with His message and prophethood.' He said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs. What prevents them, when God has placed them in the station He placed them in? Rather, others.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, the martyrs who were martyred with the enemies.' He said: 'They are so, and that is rightfully theirs. What prevents them, when God has honored them with martyrdom along with the prophets? Rather, others.' They said: 'Then who, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'Peoples in the loins of men who will come after me, who believe in me though they have not seen me, and attest to me though they have not seen me. They find the suspended leaf and act according to what is in it. These are the most excellent of the people of faith in faith.'"],[159,"Shall I not inform you of the best of your leaders from the worst of them? They are those whom you love and who love you, and you supplicate for them and they supplicate for you. The worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and you curse them and they curse you."],[160,"Umar allotted Usama more than he allotted me. I said: 'My emigration and Usama's emigration are the same.' He said: 'His father was dearer to the Messenger of God ﷺ than your father, and he was dearer to the Messenger of God ﷺ than you. Your parents brought you on the emigration.'"],[161,"The Prophet ﷺ swore an oath to keep away from his wives for a month. When twenty-nine days had passed, he came down to them."],[162,"O son of al-Khattab, are you not content that for us is the Hereafter and for them is this world? I said: 'Yes.' He said: And I entered upon him when I entered, and I saw anger in his face. I said: 'O Messenger of God, what distresses you concerning the matter of the women? If you have divorced them, then God is with you, and His angels, and Jibril and Mika'il, and I and Abu Bakr and the believers are with you.' And rarely have I spoken—and praise be to God—any words except that I hoped God would confirm the saying I uttered. He said: And this verse was revealed, the verse of choice: 'It may be that his Lord, if he divorces you, will give him in exchange wives better than you, and if you two support one another against him, then indeed God is his protector, and Jibril, and the righteous of the believers, and the angels after that are his supporters.' And 'A'isha daughter of Abu Bakr and Hafsa were supporting one another against the rest of the Prophet's ﷺ wives. I said: 'O Messenger of God, have you divorced them?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, I entered the mosque and the Muslims were scratching with pebbles, saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ has divorced his wives. So come down and inform them that you have not divorced them.' He said: 'Yes, if you wish.' And I kept speaking to him until the anger left his face and until he smiled and laughed, and he had the finest front teeth of anyone. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ came down, and I came down clinging to the palm trunk. The Messenger of God ﷺ descended as if walking on the ground without touching it with his hand. I said to him: 'O Messenger of God, you were in the upper room only twenty-nine days?' He said: 'The month may be twenty-nine.' Then I stood at the door of the mosque and called out at the top of my voice: 'He has not divorced his wives.' He said: And this verse was revealed: 'And when there comes to them a matter of security or fear, they spread it abroad. But if they had referred it to the Messenger and to those in authority among them, those who can derive it from them would know it.' And I was the one who derived that matter, and God revealed the verse of choice."],[163,"Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights of Ramadan."],[164,"He found a horse which he had ridden in the way of God, and he wanted to buy it. He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he forbade him from it."],[165,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, did you not say to me: It is better for you not to ask anyone of the people for anything?' He said: 'That is only if you ask. But what God gives you without asking, it is only provision God has provided for you.'"],[166,"You have known that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights.'"],[167,"I met Umar when he was at the pilgrimage season, and I called to him from behind the tent: 'Indeed I am so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Jarmi, and a nephew of ours has a brother who is a captive among the tribe of so-and-so. We offered him the obligatory share of the Messenger of God ﷺ, but he refused.' He said: Umar raised the side of the tent and said: 'Do you know your companion?' I said: 'Yes, that is he.' He said: 'Take him away so that he may carry out for you two the ruling of the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: We used to say that the ruling was four camels."],[168,"Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas asked Umar about wiping, and Umar said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ command wiping on the back of the leather socks when he has put them on while both are pure."],[169,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ command us to wipe on the leather socks: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."],[170,"Umar entered upon Hafsa while she was weeping, so he said to her: What makes you weep? Perhaps the Messenger of God ﷺ divorced you? He had already divorced you once, then took you back because of me. By God, if he divorced you another time, I would never speak to you again."],[171,"The Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsa, then took her back."],[172,"Abd al-Rahman b. Salih and others narrated to us with his chain something similar."],[173,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was mentioning the people of a cemetery one day. He said: He prayed over it and prayed much over it. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about it, and he said: The people of the cemetery of the martyrs of Ascalon, they are escorted to Paradise as a bride is escorted to her husband."],[174,"There was a man nicknamed Himar, and he used to give the Messenger of God ﷺ a leather container of clarified butter and a leather container of honey. When their owner came demanding payment, he brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, give this man the price of his goods. The Messenger of God ﷺ would do no more than smile and order that it be given. One day he was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ after drinking wine, and a man said: O God, curse him; how often he is brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ! The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not curse him, for he loves God and His Messenger."],[175,"Abdullah b. Amir b. Barrad narrated to us, Muhammad b. Bishr narrated to us, Hisham b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, and he mentioned something similar."],[176,"I said to Umar b. al-Khattab: O Commander of the Faithful, who are the two women who backed each other against the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Aisha and Hafsa."],[177,"The deceased is punished in his grave as long as wailing is done over him, or: as long as weeping is done over him."],[178,"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then raises his gaze to the sky and says: I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him and he may enter through whichever he wishes."],[179,"I said to Umar: Why do people today shorten the prayer? He only said, \"If you fear that those who disbelieve may harm you\" [Quran 4:101], and that day has passed. He said: I wondered at what you wondered at, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: It is a charity God has given you, so accept His charity."],[180,"I performed tawaf with Umar b. al-Khattab. When we were at the third corner, the one next to the Black Stone or the chambers next to the gate, I took his hand to touch it, so he said: 'Did you not perform tawaf with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did you see him touching it?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Then leave it, for you have an excellent example in the Messenger of Allah.'"],[181,"I heard al-Nu'man b. Bashir delivering a sermon. He said: Umar b. al-Khattab mentioned what the people had acquired of worldly things and said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spend the day doubled over, unable to find even low-quality dates with which to fill his belly.'"],[182,"Umar b. al-Khattab delivered a Friday sermon. He mentioned the Prophet of Allah and mentioned Abu Bakr, then said: 'I saw as if a rooster pecked me once or twice, and I see that only as portending the approach of my appointed time. Some people are telling me to appoint a successor, but Allah would not neglect His religion, His caliphate, or that with which He sent His Prophet ﷺ. I know that some people will criticize this matter; I struck them with this hand of mine for the sake of Islam. If they do so, they are the enemies of Allah, the disbelievers, the misguided. If death comes to me soon, the caliphate is a matter of consultation among these individuals with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased when he passed away. I will not leave behind anything more important to me than kalala. I never went back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about anything as much as I did about kalala, and he never spoke harshly to me about anything as he did about it, until he poked his finger into my chest and said to me: \"O Umar, is the verse of summer at the end of Surah al-Nisa' not enough for you?\" If I live, I will issue a ruling on it by which those who recite the Qur'an and those who do not recite the Qur'an will judge.' Then he said: 'O Allah, I call You to witness over the governors of the garrison cities, for I sent them only to teach the people their religion and the Sunnah of their Prophet, to be just with them, to distribute their booty among them, and to refer to me whatever of their affairs is unclear to them. Then you, O people, eat of two plants that I consider only impure: this onion and garlic. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he detected their odor on a man in the mosque, order him to be taken out to al-Baqi'. So whoever eats them should kill their odor by cooking.'"],[183,"Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'Who witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the Bedouin came to him with a rabbit?' A man from the group said: 'I did. The Bedouin brought it cleaned and prepared, presenting it as a gift to the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Eat.' A man from the group said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw it bleeding.' So the people ate, but the Bedouin did not eat. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Will you not eat?' He said: 'I am fasting.' He said: 'Why not [use] the white [eggs]?'"],[184,"There is no emigration after the passing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[185,"Whoever humbles himself for Me like this—and Yazid tilted his hand toward the ground—I will raise him like this, and Yazid gestured with the palm of his hand toward the sky."],[186,"Why the ramal and the uncovering of shoulders, when Allah has made Islam prevail and removed polytheism? He said: Then he said: 'And why not? Shall we abandon something we used to do in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'"],[187,"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab kiss the Stone and say: 'Indeed I kiss you, and I know that you are a stone that cannot harm or benefit, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ treat you with great respect.'"],[188,"Umar used to perfume the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ every Friday."],[189,"Ibn Umar told him that he had divorced his wife once while she was menstruating. Umar consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Tell Abdullah b. Umar to take her back, then keep her until she becomes pure from this menstruation. Then when she menstruates another time and becomes pure, if he wishes he may divorce her before having intercourse with her, and if he wishes he may keep her. That is the waiting period in which Allah commanded women to be divorced.'"],[190,"I was in Madinah in a gathering in which Umar b. al-Khattab was present. He said to one of those sitting with him: 'How did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ describe Islam?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Islam began as a jadha', then a thaniyy, then a raba'i, then a sadis, then a bazil.\"' Umar said: 'After the bazil there is only decrease.'"],[191,"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."],[192,"A man came to Umar while he was at Arafah and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, I have come from Kufah and I left a man there dictating the masahif from his memory.' He said, 'Umar became angry and swelled up until he almost filled the space between the two sides of the saddle. He said, 'Woe to you! Who is he?' He said, 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud.' Umar kept calming down and concealing his anger until he returned to his previous state. Then he said, 'Woe to you! By Allah, I do not know of anyone among the people more deserving of that than him. I will tell you about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would often spend the night conversing with Abu Bakr regarding some affair of the Muslims. One night he conversed with him while I was with him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left walking, and we walked with him. There was a man standing and praying in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood listening to his recitation. When we were about to recognize the man, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever would like to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd.' He said, 'Then the man sat down supplicating, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began saying, 'Ask and you shall be given.' Umar said, 'I said to myself, By Allah, I will go to him in the morning and give him the glad tidings.' He said, 'I went to him in the morning to give him the glad tidings, but I found that Abu Bakr had preceded me to him and given him the glad tidings. By Allah, I never raced him to any good but that he preceded me to it.'"],[193,"A man came to Umar while he was standing at Arafah, and he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Abu Khaythamah, but they did not mention Khaythamah or Qays b. Marwan in it."],[194,"I witnessed Umar b. al-Khattab while he was addressing the people. He said, 'O people, a time has come upon me when I thought that whoever recited the Quran desired Allah and what is with Him. Now it seems to me that some people recite it desiring thereby people and desiring thereby the world. Verily, desire Allah with your deeds. We only knew you when the revelation was descending, and when the Prophet ﷺ was among us, and when Allah informed us of your news. Now the revelation has stopped and the Prophet of Allah has gone. We only know you by what we say to you. Whoever we see good from, we think good of him and love him for it. Whoever we see evil from, we think evil of him and hate him for it. Your secrets are between you and your Lord. I only send my governors to teach you your religion and to teach you your Sunnah. I do not send them to beat your backs or to take your wealth. Whoever is troubled by any of that, let him bring it to me. By the One in Whose hand is Umar's soul, I will surely give you retribution from him.' He said, 'Amr b. al-As stood up and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, what do you think if you send one of your governors and he disciplines a man from his subjects and beats him, will you give retribution from him?' He said, 'Yes, by the One in Whose hand is Umar's soul, I will surely give retribution from him. Should I not give retribution when I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give retribution from himself? Do not beat the Muslims and humiliate them, do not withhold their rights and make them disbelieve, do not send them to the frontiers and tempt them, and do not station them in the forests and waste them.'"],[195,"I wanted to ask Umar for nearly a year about the two women who supported one another against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but I did not dare to ask him. We were at Marr Zahran when he went to perform ablution and said, 'Bring me a water skin.' I brought it to him and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, who were the two women?' Before I could finish my words, he said, 'Aishah and Hafsah.'"],[196,"Perform Hajj and Umrah consecutively, for performing them consecutively removes poverty and sins just as the bellows removes the impurities of iron."],[197,"The child belongs to the bed."],[198,"Samurah sold wine. Umar said, 'May Allah fight Samurah! Did he not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: May Allah curse the Jews. Animal fat was forbidden to them, but they sold it and consumed its price.'"],[199,"Whoever is grieved by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is the believer."],[200,"He is a believer."],[201,"He ruled that for a hyena killed by a pilgrim in ihram, a sheep is due; for a rabbit, a kid; for a jerboa, a young goat; and for a gazelle, a ram."],[202,"Whomever you find stealing from the war booty, beat him and burn his belongings. He said, 'I entered upon Maslamah b. Abd al-Malik when he had seized a man who had stolen from the booty. He called Salim and narrated the hadith to him. He said, 'So he burned his belongings, and he found a mushaf among his belongings. He assessed the mushaf and gave its value as charity.'"],[203,"When he was struck, Abd Allah b. Umar said to him, 'Will you not appoint a successor, O Commander of the Faithful?' He said, 'I do not find anyone more deserving of this matter than those with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased when he passed away.' He named Ali, Uthman, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas. He said, 'Let Abd Allah b. Umar witness them, but he has no share in the matter. Whomever they appoint as successor is the caliph after me. If it falls to Sa'd, then good; otherwise, let the caliph after me seek his assistance, for I did not remove him due to weakness or treachery.'"],[204,"I was present with my father when he was struck. He said: They praised him with good. He said: A monk and one who desires. They said: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: Should I bear your affair alive and dead? I would love that my share from you be sufficiency, neither against me nor for me. Then he said: If I appoint a successor, then one better than me appointed a successor, and if I leave you, then one better than me left you—the Messenger of God ﷺ. Abdullah b. Umar said: I knew that when he mentioned the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would not appoint a successor."],[205,"Let none of you eat with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand."],[206,"Talha b. Ubayd Allah exchanged silver for gold with me and said: Give us respite until our produce comes from al-Ghaba. Umar b. al-Khattab heard him saying that. He said: No, by God, you shall not part from him until you pay him, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Gold for silver is usury unless it is hand to hand, wheat for wheat is usury unless it is hand to hand, barley for barley is usury unless it is hand to hand, and dates for dates is usury unless it is hand to hand."],[207,"Umar b. al-Khattab sold to Talha b. Ubayd Allah one hundred dinars for silver. Umar said: Its like is not in his hand. I said: I have no money until the keeper of my estate comes from al-Ghaba. He said: No, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Gold for silver is usury unless it is hand to hand."],[208,"Umar b. al-Khattab appointed Ibn Abd al-Harith over the people of Makkah. Umar arrived and Nafi b. Abd al-Harith met him, having appointed Abd al-Rahman b. Abza as his successor over the people of Makkah. Umar became angry until he stood up in the stirrup and said: Do you appoint Abd al-Rahman b. Abza over the people of God? He said: I found him the most versed of them in the Book of God and the most knowledgeable of them in the religion of God. Umar then humbled himself for it until he settled back on his saddle and said: If you say that, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God will raise peoples by this religion and abase others by it."],[209,"I went out with Umar b. al-Khattab to Makkah. The governor of Makkah, Nafi b. Alqama—named after a paternal uncle of his called Nafi—met us. He said: Whom did you appoint as successor over Makkah? He said: I appointed Abd al-Rahman b. Abza over it. He said: You deliberately chose a man from the freedmen and appointed him over the Quraysh and the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ who are there? He said: Yes, I found him the most versed of them in the Book of God, and Makkah is a land that is frequented, so I wished that they would hear the Book of God from a man of good recitation. He said: What a good thing you have seen. God raises peoples by the Quran and abases peoples by the Quran, and Abd al-Rahman b. Abza is among those whom God raised by the Quran."],[210,"He said that there will be among the successors a man from Qaran called Uways b. Amir. He will have a white patch of leprosy, and he will supplicate God to remove it from him, and He will remove it. Then he will say: O God, leave for me in my body something by which I remember Your favor upon me. He said: So He leaves for him some of it by which he remembers His favors upon him. Whoever of you meets him and is able to ask him to seek forgiveness for him, let him do so. So seek forgiveness for me, O Uways b. Amir. He said to him: May God forgive you, O Commander of the Believers. He said: And you, may God forgive you, O Uways b. Amir. He said: When they heard Umar say: On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, one man said: Seek forgiveness for me, O Uways, and another said: Seek forgiveness for me, O Uways. When they became many upon him, he slipped away and departed, and he was not seen until this hour."],[211,"Umar b. al-Khattab wrote to Utba b. Farqad: Peace be upon you. To proceed: Wear cloaks and wrappers, discard trousers, put on sandals and cast off boots, shoot at targets and cut the knees, leap upon horses vigorously. Keep to the Jarmi and Maaddi style, and beware of affectation and the dress of the Persians, for the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade silk except something like this—three fingers—or like this—four fingers."],[212,"Beware of wearing silk, for the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade wearing silk except like this—and he raised his index and middle fingers."],[213,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was at al-Hajun, sorrowful and sad. He said: O God, show me today a sign after which I will not care who among my people denies me. Then he called a tree from the direction of Aqabat Ahl al-Madina. He called it and it came cleaving the earth until it reached him. It greeted him, then he commanded it and it went back. He said: I do not care who among my people denies me after this."],[214,"I said to Umar b. al-Khattab: How did the Messenger of God ﷺ do when he entered Makkah? He said: He prayed two rak'ahs."],[215,"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab touch the Black Stone and kiss it, and say: I kiss you, and I know that you are a stone that can neither harm nor benefit, but I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kiss you."],[216,"Umar kissed it — meaning the Stone — and embraced it, and said: I saw Abu al-Qasim ﷺ being gracious to you."],[217,"I saw Muhammad b. Abbad b. Jafar kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, and he said: I saw Umar b. al-Khattab kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do it."],[218,"I saw Umar b. al-Khattab kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, then he returned and kissed it and prostrated upon it, then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do."],[219,"He saw Umar b. al-Khattab kissing the Stone and saying: I testify that you are a stone, but I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing you."],[220,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and there he was reclining on a sand mat that had left marks on his side. I raised my head in the house, and by God, I saw nothing in it that would catch the eye except three hides."],[221,"Umar b. al-Khattab mentioned what the people had acquired of worldly goods, and said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ spend the day doubled over, unable to find even low-quality dates to fill his stomach."],[222,"By God, were it not that we would leave the last of time as destitute with nothing, no town that God opened to the people of Islam would I have divided it except as the Messenger of God ﷺ divided Khaybar."],[223,"The likeness of one who takes back his charity is like the likeness of a dog that returns to its vomit."],[224,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, he gathered the women of the Ansar in a house. Then he sent Umar to us. He stood and greeted, and we returned the greeting. He said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of God to you. We said: Welcome to the Messenger of God and to the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: He said: Will you pledge allegiance to me that you will not commit adultery, nor steal, nor kill your children, nor bring a slander you fabricate between your hands and feet, and not disobey in what is right? We said: Yes. She said: So we extended our hands from inside the house, and he extended his hand from outside. And he commanded us to bring out the menstruating women and the adolescent girls on the two Eids, and he forbade us from following funerals, and there is no Friday prayer upon us. He said: I said: What is the right that you were forbidden from? She said: Wailing."],[225,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying to another man: Come, let me gamble with you. So he ordered him to give charity as alms."],[226,"Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah."],[227,"Bad luck is in three things: in the mount, the dwelling, and the woman."],[228,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition, and we said: O Messenger of God, the enemy has arrived and they are well-fed while the people are hungry. The Ansar said: Shall we not slaughter our water-carrying camels and feed the people? The Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever has surplus food, let him bring it. So he began to bring a mudd, a sa', and more and less, and the total in the army was twenty-some sa's. The Prophet ﷺ sat beside it and invoked blessing, then said: Take, but do not plunder. A man would take in his provision bag and in his large sack, and they took in their vessels, until a man would tie the sleeve of his shirt and fill it. They finished and the food was as it was. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: I bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God; no sincere servant comes with them but God protects him from the heat of the Fire."],[229,"I saw Ali drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw it for him, but he said: Stop, O Abu al-Janub, for I saw Umar drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw it for him, but he said: Stop, O Abu al-Hasan, for I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw it for him, but he said: Stop, O Umar, for I dislike that anyone share in my purification."],[230,"These two days the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade you to fast: the day of your breaking fast from your fasting, and the day when you eat from the meat of your sacrifices."],[231,"When Umar was stabbed, Hafsa wailed over him, and he said: O Hafsa, did you not hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The one wailed over is punished."],[232,"He informed him that he sought to exchange one hundred dinars. He said: Talha b. Ubayd Allah called me, and we mutually agreed on the exchange until he exchanged with me and took the gold, turning it over in his hand. He said: until my treasurer comes from al-Ghaba, while Umar b. al-Khattab was listening. Umar said: No, by God, you will not part from him until you take it from him. Then he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Gold for gold is usury unless hand to hand, dates for dates is usury unless hand to hand, barley for barley is usury unless hand to hand."],[233,"Whoever sleeps past his portion of Quran or part of it, then recites it between the dawn prayer and the noon prayer, it is written for him as if he recited it at night."],[234,"Were it not that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God defends the religion with Christians from Rabi'a on the bank of the Euphrates, I would not have left any Arab but that I killed him or he submitted."],[235,"Some people say: If only you would appoint a successor? I find no one more entitled to this matter than these individuals with whom the Prophet ﷺ died while pleased with them; whichever of them they appoint as successor, he is the caliph after me."],[236,"I attended the Eid prayer with Umar b. al-Khattab, and he began with the prayer before the sermon and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade fasting on these two days: as for the day of breaking fast, it is your breaking fast from your fasting, and as for the day of sacrifice, eat from the meat of your sacrifices."],[237,"Umar saw on a man of al-Utarid a cloak of brocade or silk, and said: O Messenger of God, would you buy it? He said: Only one who has no share wears this. He said: Then a striped silk suit was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he sent it to me. He said: I said: You sent it to me while I heard you say about it what you said? He said: I sent it to you only to enjoy it."],[238,"When the night advances from here and the day departs, the faster has broken his fast."],[239,"The travel prayer is two rak'ahs, the Eid al-Fitr prayer is two rak'ahs, the Eid al-Adha prayer is two rak'ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak'ahs, complete without shortening, on the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ."],[240,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: What is faith? He said: To believe in God, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, and predestination, its good and its evil. Gabriel said: You have spoken truthfully. We were astonished at him, asking him and affirming him. The Prophet ﷺ said: That is Gabriel, who came to you to teach you your religion."],[241,"Moses said: O Lord, our father Adam expelled us and himself from Paradise. So God showed him Adam. He said: Are you Adam? Adam said to him: Yes. He said: Are you the one into whom God breathed of His spirit, and to whom He caused His angels to prostrate, and whom He taught all the names? He said: Yes. He said: Then what led you to expel us and yourself from Paradise? Adam said to him: Who are you? He said: I am Moses. He said: Are you Moses of the Children of Israel, to whom God spoke from behind a veil and did not make between you and Him any messenger from His creation? He said: Yes. He said: Then do you blame me for a matter concerning which God's decree preceded before me? The Messenger of God ﷺ said at that: Adam defeated Moses, Adam defeated Moses."],[242,"Adam and Moses met. Moses said to Adam: You are the father of humanity; God settled you in His Garden and caused His angels to prostrate to you. Adam said to Moses: Do you not find it written? He said: Adam defeated Moses, Adam defeated Moses."],[243,"Do not sit with the people of qadar, and do not engage them in conversation."],[244,"Al-Qawariri narrated to us; Abdullah b. Yazid narrated to us with his chain something similar."],[245,"If you were to rely on God as He truly deserves to be relied upon, He would provide for you just as He provides for the birds; they go out in the morning hungry and return in the evening full."],[246,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[247,"He went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition to Tabuk. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ sat talking with his companions and said: Whoever rises when the sun begins to decline, performs ablution and perfects it, then stands and prays two units, his sins will be forgiven—or he said: he will be as on the day his mother bore him. Uqbah said: I said: Praise be to God who blessed me to hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ. Umar b. al-Khattab, who was sitting facing me, said: Do you marvel at this? The Messenger of God ﷺ said something more marvelous than this before you came. I said: What did he say, may my father be your ransom? Umar b. al-Khattab said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever performs ablution and perfects it, then raises his eyes to the sky and says: I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger, eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him; he may enter through whichever he wishes."],[248,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out at midday and found Abu Bakr in the mosque. He said: What brought you out at this hour? He said: The One who brought you out, O Messenger of God. Then Umar b. al-Khattab came, and he said: O Ibn al-Khattab, what brought you out? He said: The One who brought you both out, O Messenger of God. Umar sat down, and the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to talk with them. Then he said: Do you have strength to go to this palm grove and get food, drink, and shade? We said: Yes. He said: Take us to Ibn al-Tayyihan, Abu al-Haytham al-Ansari. The Messenger of God ﷺ went ahead of us and greeted, and asked permission three times. Umm al-Haytham was behind the door listening to the speech and wished the Messenger of God ﷺ would give her more. When the Messenger of God ﷺ was about to leave, Umm al-Haytham came out running after them and said: O Messenger of God, by God I heard your greeting, but I wished that you would increase us in your greetings. The Messenger of God ﷺ said something good to her and said: Where is Abu al-Haytham? I do not see him. She said: He is nearby; he has gone to fetch fresh water for us. Come in; he will come this hour, God willing. She spread a mat for them under a tree. Abu al-Haytham came and was delighted with them, and his eye was cooled by them. He climbed a palm tree and cut a bunch of dates for them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Enough for you, O Abu al-Haytham. He said: O Messenger of God, you may eat from its unripe dates, its ripe dates, and its hanging clusters. Then he brought them water, and they drank. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: This is part of the delight about which you will be asked. Abu al-Haytham got up to slaughter a sheep for them, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Beware of milch animals. Umm al-Haytham got up to knead dough for them and bake. The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar laid their heads down for the midday nap. They woke up and their food was ready. The food was placed before them, and they ate and were satisfied and praised God, Mighty and Majestic. Umm al-Haytham returned to them the remainder of the date clusters, and they ate from its ripe dates and hanging clusters. The Messenger of God ﷺ greeted them and supplicated for them."],[249,"O people, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not sit at a table around which wine is passed. He said: And he mentioned the hadith."],[250,"The martyrs are four: A believing man of excellent faith who met the enemy and was true to God until he was killed—that is the one to whom people will raise their eyes on the Day of Resurrection, like this, and he raised his head until his cap fell; I do not know whether it was Umar's cap or the Prophet's ﷺ. And a believing man of excellent faith, such that when he met the enemy it was as if his skin was being struck with the thorns of the talh tree out of cowardice; a stray arrow came to him and killed him, and he is in the second rank. And a believing man who mixed a good deed with an evil one, met the enemy and was true to God until he was killed—that one is in the third rank. And a believing man who was immoderate against himself, met the enemy and was true to God until he was killed—that one is in the fourth rank."],[251,"Whoever shades the head of a warrior, God will shade him on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God with his equipment will have his reward. Whoever builds a mosque in which the name of God is remembered, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[252,"I said: O Messenger of God, I made a vow in the time of ignorance; then God brought Islam. He said: Fulfill your vow."],[253,"He gave a horse as charity in the way of God. When we gave charity in the way of God, we brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and handed it to him, and he placed it where God showed him. I brought the horse and handed it to him, and he mounted a man from his companions on it. I then found it being sold in the market, and I wanted to buy it. I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: Do not buy it, and do not take back anything of your charity."],[254,"Umar b. al-Khattab delivered a sermon and said: I saw in a dream as if a red rooster pecked me once or twice, and I see that only as the approach of my term. If my affair hastens, then the caliphate is a consultation among these six persons with whom the Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased when he passed away. I know that people will criticize this matter; I fought them with this hand of mine for Islam. If they do so, they are the enemies of God, the disbelievers, the misguided. I bear witness concerning the governors of the regions: I sent them only to teach the people their religion and the Sunnah of their Prophet ﷺ and to distribute their spoils. The Messenger of God ﷺ did not speak harshly to me about anything, or: I did not dispute with the Messenger of God ﷺ about anything regarding the verse of al-kalala, until he struck my chest and said: The verse of summer, which was sent down at the end of Surah al-Nisa, suffices you: 'They ask you for a ruling. Say: God gives you a ruling concerning al-kalala.' No ruling was decided in it that is known to those who read and those who do not read; it is what excludes the father — so I think. Indeed, O people, you eat from two plants that I consider nothing but foul: onion and garlic. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to order that a man from whom their smell is detected be taken out to al-Baqi'. Whoever must eat them should kill their odor by cooking."],[255,"When night comes and day departs and the sun sets, the fasting person has broken his fast."],[256,"While Umar b. al-Khattab was delivering the Friday sermon to the people, Uthman b. Affan entered the mosque. Umar alluded to him and said: What is the matter with men who come late after the call? Uthman said: O Commander of the Faithful, I did not delay after hearing the call except to perform ablution and then come. Umar said: And ablution too! Did you not hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When one of you comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform a full bath?"],[257,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[258,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[259,"When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ, falling from the sky would be dearer to me than lying about him. When I narrate to you from other than him, I am but a warrior, and war is deception. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: At the end of time, a people will emerge, young in age, foolish in intellect, who say the best words of creation, but their faith does not pass beyond their throats. Wherever you find them, kill them, for killing them is a reward on the Day of Resurrection for the one who kills them."],[260,"Abu Musa came to al-Hasan b. Ali to visit him. Ali said to him: Have you come as a visitor or a gloater? He said: No, rather as a visitor. He said: If you have come as a visitor, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When a man visits his Muslim brother, he walks in the gardens of Paradise until he sits. When he sits, mercy envelops him. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening. If it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning."],[261,"Whoever claims that we have anything to read except the Book of God and this sahifa — a sahifa containing the ages of camels and matters of wounds — has lied. In it is: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Madinah is sacred between Ayr and Thawr. Whoever introduces an innovation in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. On the Day of Resurrection, God will accept from him neither justice nor ransom. The protection of Muslims is one; the lowest of them may grant it."],[262,"I asked A'isha about wiping over the leather socks. She said: Go to Ali and ask him, for he is more knowledgeable about that than me. I went to Ali and asked him about wiping. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us that the resident wipe for a day and a night, and the traveler for three days."],[263,"I said: O Messenger of God, why do you choose women from Quraysh and leave us? He said: Do you have anyone? We said: Yes, the daughter of Hamza. He said: She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding."],[264,"A funeral procession passed by Ali, so his companions went to stand up. Ali said to them: \"What makes you do this?\" They said: \"Abu Musa told us that when a funeral procession passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would stand until it passed him.\" He said: \"Abu Musa does not say anything [of his own accord]. Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that once. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like to imitate the People of the Book in matters about which nothing had been revealed to him, but when something was revealed to him, he abandoned it.\""],[265,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me a month to fast after Ramadan.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you are going to fast, then fast al-Muharram, for it is the month of Allah, and in it there is a day on which Allah accepted the repentance of a people, and on which He will accept the repentance of others.\""],[266,"In Paradise there is a market in which there is no buying or selling, only forms of men and women. When a man desires a form, he enters it. He said: \"And in it there is a gathering of the houris with wide eyes.\" He said: \"They raise their voices in a way the creatures have never heard the like of.\" He said: \"They say: 'We are the eternal ones and we never perish; we are the ones living in comfort and we never suffer; we are the content ones and we never become discontent. Blessed is the one who is for us and we are for him.'\""],[267,"When the Prophet ﷺ slaughtered the sacrificial camels, he ordered me to give their meat, hides, and saddle blankets in charity."],[268,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade [sacrificing] an animal with a broken horn or a slit ear."],[269,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sacrificing an animal with a broken horn or a slit ear."],[270,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with gold in one hand and silk in the other, and said: \"These two are forbidden for the males of my community.\""],[271,"I went out for a funeral and stood waiting for it to be placed down so that I could sit, while Nafi' b. Jubayr was near me. When it was placed down, I sat next to him. He said: \"It seems you were waiting for this funeral to be placed down so that you could sit?\" I said: \"Yes, because of a hadith I heard from Abu Sa'id.\" Then he said:"],[272,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us until he placed his foot between me and Fatimah, and he taught us what to say when we went to bed: thirty-three glorifications (tasbihat), thirty-three praises (tahmidat), and thirty-four declarations of greatness (takbirat). Ali said: \"I have never left them since.\" A man said to him: \"Not even on the night of Siffin?\" Ali said: \"Not even on the night of Siffin.\""],[273,"He used to say in his witr: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot enumerate praise of You; You are as You have praised Yourself.\""],[274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me—and I do not say he forbade you—from wearing gold rings, wearing qassi garments, and reciting while bowing."],[275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me to keep the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days."],[276,"He forbade visiting graves, and [forbade] certain vessels, and [forbade] that we keep the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three [days]. He said: I had forbidden you to visit graves, but visit them, for they remind you of the Hereafter. I had forbidden you [to use certain] vessels, but drink from them and avoid whatever intoxicates. I had forbidden you to keep the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, but keep it as long as seems [proper] to you."],[277,"There is no obedience to any human being in disobedience to God."],[278,"There was no horseman among us on the day of Badr except al-Miqdad. And I saw us when no one was standing except the Messenger of God ﷺ, praying under a tree and weeping until morning."],[279,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me to place the ring on this one or on this one: the index finger and the middle finger."],[280,"He used to wake his family during the last ten [nights] of Ramadan."],[281,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution [washing] three [times] three [times]."],[282,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was ill, and I was saying: O God, if my appointed time has come, then give me rest; and if it is delayed, then raise me [from illness]; and if it is a trial, then give me patience. He struck my chest with his hand and said: O God, grant him well-being and heal him. I never complained of that pain again."],[283,"When he began the prayer, he said the takbir, then said: I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a true believer, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for God, Lord of the worlds. He has no partner, and with that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims."],[284,"Ali entered al-Rahaba after praying the dawn prayer and sat down in al-Rahaba. Then he said to a servant of his: Bring me water for purification. The servant brought a vessel containing water and a basin. Abd Khayr said: We were sitting watching him. He took the vessel with his right hand and poured it over his left hand and washed his palms three times. Abd Khayr said: All of that without putting his hand into the vessel until he had washed it three times. Then he put his right hand into the vessel and took a mouthful of water, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose and expelled it with his left hand three times. Then he washed his face three times. Then he washed his right hand three times up to the elbow. Then he washed his left hand three times. Then he put his right hand into the vessel until the water covered it, then lifted it with what it carried of water, then wiped it with his left hand. Then he wiped his head with both hands together. Then he put his right hand into the vessel, then poured water over his right foot and washed it three times with his left hand. Then he put his right hand into the vessel and filled it, then poured with his right hand over his left foot and washed it three times with his left hand. Then he put his right hand into the vessel and filled it with water and drank from it. Then he said: This is the purification of the Prophet of God ﷺ. Whoever would like to see the purification of the Messenger of God ﷺ, let him look at this."],[285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would come out of the privy and recite the Quran, and eat meat with us, and nothing prevented him—or held him back—from the Quran except major ritual impurity."],[286,"We saw the Messenger of God ﷺ stand, so we stood, and he sat, so we sat—meaning at the funeral."],[287,"Amr b. Hurayth visited al-Hasan b. Ali. Ali said to him: Do you visit Hasan while there is in the heart what is in it? He said: O Ali, you are not the lord of my heart to turn it wherever you wish. He said: Indeed, that does not prevent me from giving you sincere advice. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: No Muslim visits a sick person except that seventy thousand angels send blessings upon him during whatever hours of the day he visits until evening, and during whatever hours of the night he visits until morning."],[288,"He was brought a married man who had committed adultery. He said: He flogged him on Thursday. He said: Then he stoned him on Friday. He said: He was asked: You combined two punishments on him? He said: He said: I flogged him according to the Book of God, and I stoned him according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[289,"By the One who split the grain and created the breath, it is indeed the covenant of the Messenger of God ﷺ to me that no one loves you except a believer, and no one hates you except a hypocrite."],[290,"I set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ at night until we came to the Kaaba. He said to me: Sit. So I sat, and the Messenger of God ﷺ climbed onto my shoulders, then I stood up with him. When he saw my weakness beneath him, he said: Sit. So I sat, and the Messenger of God ﷺ came down and sat for me, and said: Climb onto my shoulders. So I climbed onto him, then he stood up with me until it seemed to me that if I wished I could touch the horizon of the sky. I climbed onto the House and came to the idol of Quraysh, which was a statue of a man made of brass or copper. I kept working at it from the right and the left, and in front of it and behind it, until I got a firm hold of it. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ was saying: Hit! Hit! while I was working at it. Then he said to me: Throw it down. So I threw it, and it shattered as glass shatters. Then I came down, and we went off running until we hid among the houses, fearing that someone would see us. It was never raised up after that."],[291,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said: O Messenger of God, you are sending me to a people who are elders, advanced in age, and I fear that I may not judge correctly? He said: God will make your tongue firm and guide your heart."],[292,"The wife of al-Walid b. Uqba came to the Messenger of God ﷺ complaining that al-Walid was beating her. He said to her: Go back and say to him: The Messenger of God ﷺ has granted me protection. He said: She went and stayed for a while, then came and said: O Messenger of God, he did not stop beating me. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ cut a fringe from his garment and gave it to her, and said: Say: The Messenger of God ﷺ has granted me protection; this is a fringe from his garment. She stayed for a while, then returned and said: O Messenger of God, he only increased me in beating. So the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands and said: O God, take al-Walid to account, twice or three times."],[293,"I was with Ali, and we came to the big market. He recognized an old man among them and said: O old man, give me a good sale on a shirt for three dirhams. He said: Yes, O Commander of the Faithful. When the old man recognized him, Ali did not buy anything from him. He went to a young boy and bought a shirt from him for three dirhams. He put it on, and it reached from his wrists to his ankles, and he said about his garment: Praise be to God who has provided me with clothing with which I beautify myself among people and cover my private parts. The Muslims said: Is this something you say of yourself or from the Prophet ﷺ? He said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say that when he put on a garment."],[294,"We have nothing except the Book of God and this sheet from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Madinah is sacred between Air and Thawr. Whoever innovates in it or gives refuge to an innovator, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. Neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him. And he said: The protection of the Muslims is one, and the lowest of them may extend it. Whoever violates the protection of a Muslim, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. Neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him. And whoever allies himself with a people without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. God will not accept from him an obligatory or a supererogatory act."],[295,"He forbade a man from reciting the Quran while bowing. He said: When you bow, glorify God, and when you prostrate, supplicate to God, for it is fitting that you be answered."],[296,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to oversee his sacrificial camels, to distribute their hides and their coverings, and he commanded me not to give the butcher anything of them. We give him from our own."],[297,"I have pardoned you regarding the zakat of horses and slaves."],[298,"He judged that the debt comes before the bequest. He said: And you recite the bequest before the debt."],[299,"The Magians had a book they read and knowledge they studied. Their leader committed adultery, and they wanted to carry out the prescribed punishment on him. He said to them: Did not Adam marry his sons to his daughters? So they did not carry out the punishment on him. Then the book was taken away. The Messenger of God ﷺ took the jizya from the Magians, as did Abu Bakr, and I."],[300,"We, when the battle grew fierce and the people met, would seek protection by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and none of us was closer to the enemy than he."],[301,"He asked permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether, if a child were born to him after his death, he might name him with his name and give him his kunya? He said: So it was a concession from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: His name was Muhammad and his kunya was Abu al-Qasim."],[302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing a gold ring, from reciting while bowing, and from wearing qassi and muʿaṣfar."],[303,"There was no horseman among us on the day of Badr except al-Miqdad."],[304,"When one of you sneezes, let him say: Al-hamdu lillahi rabbi al-ʿalamin ʿala kulli hal, and let it be said to him: Yarhamukum Allah, and let him say: Yahdikum Allah wa yuslihu balakum."],[305,"He said concerning the suckling infant: The urine of a boy is sprinkled, and the urine of a girl is washed."],[306,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood then sat."],[307,"Water was brought to Ali and he drank while standing, then said: Some people dislike drinking while standing, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drink while standing. Then water was brought to him and he wiped himself with it, then said: This is the ablution of one who has not invalidated it."],[308,"Ali said to al-Abbas: Ask the Prophet ﷺ to give you the treasury. So al-Abbas asked him, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: I give you what is better for you than that: what you are provided with and what you do not provide yourselves; so he gave them the water supply."],[309,"Al-Mughira had a spear. When we set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a raid, he would plant it, and people would pass by it and carry it. He said: I said: I will inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, but he said: Then lost property will not be picked up; so I left it."],[310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at Arafa and said: This is Arafa and this is the standing place, and all of Arafa is a standing place. Then he departed when the sun set, and he mounted Usama behind him while the people were striking to his right and left. He turned to them and said: O people, be calm. When he came to Muzdalifa, he prayed the two prayers together. When morning came, he came to Quzah and stood upon it and said: This is Quzah, and all of Muzdalifa is a standing place. Then he departed. When he came to Muhassir, he struck his she-camel until he crossed the valley, then stopped, then mounted al-Fadl behind him, then came to the Jamra, then came to the place of sacrifice and said: This is the place of sacrifice, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice. He said: A young woman from Khathʿam asked him for a ruling and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who has become senile, and the obligation of Hajj has overtaken him. Is it sufficient for me to perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father. He turned the neck of al-Fadl, so al-Abbas said to him: O Messenger of Allah, why did you turn the neck of your cousin? He said: I saw a young man and a young woman and did not feel safe for them from Satan. He said: A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I threw before I shaved. He said: Shave or shorten, and no harm. He said: Another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed before I threw. He said: Throw, and no harm. He said: Then he came to the House and circumambulated it, then came to Zamzam and said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, your water supply, were it not that the people would overpower you, I would draw it."],[311,"Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, nor one ritually impure, nor a dog."],[312,"I was a man who emitted madhy frequently, so I commanded al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about madhy. He said: \"From it is wudu, and from mani is ghusl.\""],[313,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from reciting while I was bowing. He said: \"O Ali, the likeness of the one who does not straighten his back in his prayer is like the likeness of a pregnant woman who carries, and when her delivery draws near she miscarries, so she is neither one with a pregnancy nor one with a child.\""],[314,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen, I said: \"You send me while I am a young man, and I have no knowledge of much of judiciary?\" He said: \"Then he struck my chest and said: 'Go, for God will make firm your tongue and guide your heart.'\""],[315,"Witr is not obligatory like the prescribed prayer, but it is a sunnah, so do not abandon it. Shu'bah said: \"Then I found it written with me: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ performed witr.'\""],[316,"We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ during the day. He said: \"You would not be able to do that.\" We said: \"Who among us could do that?\" He said: \"When the sun was here, like its position here at the time of Asr, he would pray two rak'ahs, and when the sun was here, like its position here at the time of Zuhr, he would pray four, separating between every two rak'ahs with the salam upon the angels brought near, and the prophets, and those who followed them from the prophets and messengers.\""],[317,"The Prophet ﷺ was gifted a silk garment. He said: \"He clothed me with it.\" Ali said: \"I went out wearing it, and the Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself.' He said: 'And he commanded me, so I tore it into pieces among my women as head covers: Fatimah and his paternal aunt.'\""],[318,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to a slave girl who had committed fornication. He said: \"Establish the prescribed punishment on her.\" I found her in her blood, not yet recovered from her postpartum bleeding, so I came to him and mentioned that to him. He said: \"When she has recovered from her postpartum bleeding and become pure, then establish the prescribed punishment on her.\" He said: \"Then he said: 'Establish the prescribed punishment on those whom your right hands possess.'\""],[319,"I was lifted up with al-Husayn b. Ali from Muzdalifah, and I kept hearing him say: \"Labbayk, labbayk,\" until he reached the Jamrah. I said to him: \"What is this talbiyah, O Abu Abd Allah?\" He said: \"I heard my father Ali b. Abi Talib making talbiyah until he reached the Jamrah, and he told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ made talbiyah until he reached it.\" He said: \"Then I returned to Ibn Abbas and informed him of Husayn's statement. He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'And my brother al-Fadl b. Abbas told me, and he was the riding companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ: he made talbiyah until he reached the Jamrah.'\""],[320,"From all parts of the night the Messenger of God ﷺ performed witr: from its beginning, its middle, and its end, and his witr ended at the last part of the night."],[321,"The Prophet ﷺ made a treaty with the Banu Taghlib on the condition that they remain upon their religion and not Christianize their children. Indeed they have broken it, and if the matter is completed for me, I will kill the fighters and take the offspring captive."],[322,"At the end of time there will come forth a people young in age, foolish in intellect, who say from the best of the speech of creation, who recite the Quran but it does not pass beyond their throats. So when you meet them, kill them, for in killing them there is a reward for the one who kills them with God on the Day of Resurrection."],[323,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took gold in his right hand and silk in his left, and said: \"These two are forbidden for the males of my nation.\""],[324,"Ali gave a sermon and said: \"O people, carry out the prescribed punishment on your slaves—those who are married and those who are not—for a slave woman belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ committed adultery. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to flog her. I came to her and found she had recently given birth. I feared that if I flogged her she would die, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said: 'You have done well.'\""],[325,"Ali came to the cloth sellers and said to a man: \"Sell me a shirt for three dirhams.\" He gave him a garment, and he wore it, reaching from his ankle to his wrist. When he wore it, he said: \"Praise be to Allah who has clothed me with fine clothing with which I cover my private parts and adorn myself among the people.\" Then he said: \"When the Prophet ﷺ wore a garment, he said this.\""],[326,"I saw Ali brought a man, and they said: \"He has stolen a camel.\" He said: \"I do not think you stole.\" He said: \"Yes, I did.\" He said: \"Perhaps it was made to appear so to you?\" He said: \"Yes, I did steal.\" He said: \"Take him, O Qanbar, bind his finger, light the fire, call the butcher to cut it, then wait until I come.\" When he came, he said to him: \"Did you steal?\" He said: \"No.\" So he released him. They said: \"O Commander of the Believers, why did you release him when he had confessed to you?\" He said: \"I took him by his statement, and I release him by his statement.\" Then Ali said: \"A man who had stolen was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered his hand to be cut off, then he wept. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why do you weep?' He said: 'How can I not weep when a member of my ummah is being cut off before you?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, could you not have pardoned him?' He said: 'That is an evil authority that pardons the prescribed punishments, but you should pardon among yourselves.'\""],[327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing a gold ring, from wearing qassi and safflower-dyed garments, and from reciting the Quran while bowing. He clothed me with a striped silk garment. I went out wearing it, or I set out wearing it. When he saw it on me, he said: \"I did not clothe you with it so that you could wear it.\" He said: So I returned and gave Fatimah one side of it, as if she was folding it with me. He said: So I split it into two. He said: She said: \"May your hands be rubbed in dust, what have you done?\" I said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing it, so wear it and clothe your women.\""],[328,"I found a document tied to the pommel of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"The people most hostile to Allah are the one who kills someone other than his killer, the one who strikes someone other than his striker, and whoever denies the favor of his patrons has disowned what Allah revealed to Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[329,"Do not expose your thigh, and do not look at the thigh of a living person or a dead person."],[330,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ make a treaty with the Christians of Banu Taghlib that they would not make their children Christians, and if they did, the protection would be withdrawn from them. Ali said: \"By Allah, they have done it. By Allah, if the matter is accomplished for me, I will kill their fighting men and take their offspring captive.\""],[331,"I asked Ali about the cow (as a sacrifice). He said: \"It is for seven people.\" He said: \"What about one with a broken horn?\" He said: \"There is no harm in it.\" He said: \"What about a lame one?\" He said: \"If it reaches the place of sacrifice. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to examine the eyes and ears.\""],[332,"He used to pray the Duha prayer."],[333,"I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists. I said to him (about it), and he said: \"Did not Ibrahim seek forgiveness for his father?\" He said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and Allah revealed: \"And Ibrahim's seeking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him.\""],[334,"I would not carry out a prescribed punishment on anyone and have him die and then find anything in my heart, except for the wine drinker. For if he died, I would pay his blood money, because the Prophet ﷺ did not establish it as a fixed punishment."],[335,"Ali mentioned the people of Nahrawan and said: \"Among them is a man with a defective hand, or a deformed hand. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would inform you of what Allah promised those who kill them on the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ.\" He said: I said: \"Did you hear it from him?\" He said: \"Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba.\""],[336,"I set out to 'Ali, myself and a man. He said: I said to him: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ entrust to you anything he did not entrust to anyone? He said: No, except what is in this scabbard of mine. He said: He took out a document, and in that document of his was: 'The believers' blood is equal; the lowest of them may grant protection on their behalf; and they are one hand against those besides them. A believer is not killed for an unbeliever, nor one with a covenant while his covenant stands. Whoever introduces an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of God and the angels and all people.'"],[337,"A funeral was brought past 'Ali and some people stood up. He said: What is this? They said: Abu Musa. 'Ali said: The Messenger of God ﷺ only stood once, then he did not stand again."],[338,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me on the day of Badr, and to Abu Bakr: With one of you is Gabriel, and with the other is Michael; and Israfil, a mighty angel, witnesses the fighting, or is present in the fighting."],[339,"It was said to 'Ali: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: No, but I leave you as the Messenger of God ﷺ left you."],[340,"'Ali and 'Uthman met, and 'Uthman was forbidding mut'a or 'umra. 'Ali said: What do you intend regarding a matter the Messenger of God ﷺ did, that you forbid it? 'Uthman said: Leave us alone. He said: I cannot leave you. He said: When 'Ali saw that, he entered ihram for both together."],[341,"I am sending you upon what the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me upon: Leave no grave but that you level it, and no image but that you efface it."],[342,"The Messenger of God ﷺ left 'Ali b. Abi Talib behind during the expedition to Tabuk. He said: O Messenger of God, are you leaving me behind with the women and children? He said: Are you not pleased that you are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us and even placed his foot between me and Fatimah, and taught us what to say when we took to our beds: thirty-three glorifications, thirty-three praises, and thirty-four magnifications. He said: 'Ali said: I have never abandoned it since. A man said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? He said: Not even the night of Siffin."],[344,"I used to think that the bottoms of the feet were more entitled to wiping than their tops, until I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe their tops."],[345,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not pray any prayer but that he prayed two rak'ahs after it."],[346,"Nothing prevented him from reciting the Qur'an except that he be junub."],[347,"We were travelling with 'Uthman b. 'Affan and he heard a man pronouncing the talbiyah for both together. He said: Who is this? He said: 'Ali. So he came to him and said: Did you not know that I forbade this? He said: Yes, but I will not abandon the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ for your saying."],[348,"Ali said to Abu al-Hayyaj: I send you with what the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me: Leave no raised grave but you level it, and no image but you efface it."],[349,"The wife of al-Walid b. Uqba came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Al-Walid beats me.\" He said, \"Tell him: The Messenger of God ﷺ has granted me protection.\" Ali said: She did not remain but a little while before she returned and said, \"He only increased me in beating.\" So he took a fringe from his garment and gave it to her and said, \"Tell him: The Messenger of God ﷺ has granted me protection.\" She did not remain but a little while before she returned to him and said, \"He only increased me in beating.\" He raised his hands and said, \"O God, take al-Walid to task.\""],[350,"A servant does not believe until he believes in four things: in the resurrection after death, and believes in the divine decree."],[351,"I proposed to the Prophet ﷺ for his daughter Fatimah. Ali sold a coat of mail of his and some of what he sold of his belongings, and it reached four hundred and eighty dirhams. He said: The Prophet ﷺ commanded that two thirds of it be spent on perfume and one third on clothing. He spat into a jar of water and ordered them to wash with it. He said: He commanded her not to precede him in nursing her child. Ali said: She preceded him in nursing al-Husayn. As for al-Hasan, the Prophet ﷺ put something in his mouth that we do not know, and he became the more learned of the two men."],[352,"\"I will give the banner tomorrow to a man through whose hands God will grant victory.\" He said: The people went early to the Messenger of God ﷺ, each hoping that he would give him the banner. He said, \"Where is Ali b. Abi Talib?\" They said, \"He has an eye complaint, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Call him.\" He was brought, and he spat in his eye and prayed for him, and he was cured. Then he gave him the banner and said, \"Call Ali.\" He came, and he said, \"O Ali, do not turn aside until you descend upon the people and call them.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, shall we fight them until they say 'There is no god but God'?\" He said, \"Proceed gently. When you come to them, call them to God. By God, if one man becomes Muslim at your hands, it is better for you than having red camels.\""],[353,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military detachment and put Ali b. Abi Talib in command. He said to him, \"O Ali, [take charge of] the detachment.\" Imran said: When the Muslims returned from a campaign, they would come to the Messenger of God ﷺ before going to their own lodgings and tell him of their journey. He said: Ali obtained a slave girl. Four men made a pact and told him of their journey. One of the four stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, Ali obtained a slave girl.\" He turned away from him. Then the second stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, Ali did such and such.\" He turned away from him. Then the third stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, Ali did such and such.\" He turned away from him. Then the fourth stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, Ali did such and such.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to him angrily, anger visible on his face, and said, \"What do you want from Ali? Ali is from me and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me.\""],[354,"His father prepared a meal for Uthman b. Affan at Qudayd. Tharid was brought with partridge on it. He said to the people, \"Eat, for it was only hunted for my sake.\" The people said, \"This Ali forbade us to eat it.\" So he sent for Ali. He came while wiping leaves from his hands. Uthman said to him, \"Eat it.\" He, meaning Ali, said, \"I adjure by God any man who witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ when a bedouin came with the leg of a wild ass and the Messenger of God ﷺ returned it and said, 'Go to the people outside the sanctuary, for we are in a state of ihram,' or something like that.\" Some people stood up and testified. Then he said, \"I adjure by God—or he said, I remind by God—any man who witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ when a bedouin came to him with ostrich eggs and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Take them to the people outside the sanctuary, for we are a people in a state of ihram.'\" Some people stood up and testified. Uthman turned on his side and entered his house, and the people left the food. Then the people outside the sanctuary came and ate it."],[355,"He forbade eating every beast of prey with fangs, and every bird with talons, and the price of carrion, and wine and domestic donkeys, and the earnings of a prostitute, and the stud fee of every male animal."],[356,"A people will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game. They recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their collarbones. Blessed is the one who kills them and whom they kill. Their mark is a man with a defective hand."],[357,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said something when I returned from a funeral that I would not love to have the whole world in exchange for it."],[358,"He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt, or in addition to her maternal aunt."],[359,"A man inherits from his full brother to the exclusion of his half-brothers on the father's side."],[360,"I was a young man who emitted a lot of prosternal fluid; when the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that the fluid troubled me, he said: \"The ritual bath is only required for the gushing fluid.\""],[361,"He traveled with Ali and was in charge of his ablution vessel. When he drew near Nineveh, while heading toward Siffin, Ali called out: \"Have patience, Abu Abd Allah; have patience, Abu Abd Allah, at the bank of the Euphrates.\" I said: \"And what, O Abu Abd Allah?\" He said: \"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ one day and his eyes were overflowing. I said: 'O Prophet of God, has someone angered you? What is the matter that your eyes are overflowing?' He said: 'Rather, Gabriel had just left me and told me that al-Husayn will be killed at the bank of the Euphrates.' He said: 'And he said: Would you like me to let you smell some of its soil?' I said: 'Yes.' He stretched out his hand, grasped a handful of earth, and gave it to me, and I could not control my eyes from overflowing.\""],[362,"I, Fatimah, al-Abbas, and Zayd b. Harithah gathered together. Al-Abbas said: \"O Messenger of God, I have grown old, my bones have become thin, and my expenses have increased. If you see fit, O Messenger of God, to order for me such-and-such measures of food, then do so.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I have done so.\" Fatimah said: \"O Messenger of God, if you see fit to order for me what you ordered, then do so.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have done that.\" Zayd b. Harithah said: \"O Messenger of God, you had given me some land from which I made my living, then you took it back from me. If you see fit to return it to me, then do so.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I have done that.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, if you see fit to entrust to me this right that God has assigned to us in His Book regarding this fifth, so that I may distribute it during your lifetime and no one will dispute it with me after you, then do so.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I have done that.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ entrusted it to me, and I distributed it during his lifetime. Then Abu Bakr entrusted it to me, and I distributed it during his lifetime. Then Umar entrusted it to me, and I distributed it during his lifetime, until the last year of Umar's caliphate, when a large amount of wealth came to him and he set aside a fifth. He then sent for me and said: \"O Ali, this is your due, so take it.\" I said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, we have no need of it this year, and the Muslims have need of it, so return it to them.\" Umar returned it that year. Then no one called me to it after Umar, until I stood in this position of mine. Al-Abbas met me and said: \"O Ali, today you have taken away from us something that will never be returned to us.\""],[363,"Ali was brought water for ablution. He rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, then washed his face three times, and washed his hands and forearms three times each, then wiped his head, and washed his feet. Then he said: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution.\" Then he recited something from the Quran, and said: \"This is for one who is not in a state of major ritual impurity; as for the one in major ritual impurity, then no, by God.\""],[364,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came in upon me and Fatimah one night and roused us for prayer. He then went back to his house and prayed for a quiet portion of the night, and we did not hear any sound from him. Then he came back to us and roused us, saying: \"Get up and pray.\" I sat up, rubbing my eyes, saying: \"By God, we do not pray except what God has decreed for us; our souls are in God's hand, and if He wills to raise us, He raises us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned away, saying and striking his thigh: \"We do not pray except what was decreed for us; we do not pray except what God decreed for us,\" saying it twice. And man is the most argumentative of all things."],[365,"Gabriel came to me and said: \"O Muhammad, your community will differ after you.\" I said: \"Where is the way out, O Gabriel?\" He said: \"The Book of God; through it God breaks every tyrant. Whoever clings to it is saved, and whoever abandons it is ruined. It is a decisive word and not jest; tongues cannot distort it, and it does not wear out from repeated refutation, and its wonders do not cease. In it is the news of those before you and the report of what will happen after you.\""],[366,"I prayed the noon prayer with Ali, then he went to a gathering he used to hold in Madinah and sat down, and we sat around him until the afternoon prayer was due. A vessel with water was brought to him, and he took a handful from it and rinsed his mouth, then sniffed water into his nose, wiped his face and forearms, wiped his head, and wiped his feet. Then he stood and drank the remaining water in the vessel, and said: \"I have been told that some men dislike one of them drinking while standing, but I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do that. And this is the ablution of one who has not broken his state of purity.\""],[367,"He described the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"He was large-headed, fair-complexioned with a reddish tinge, thick-bearded, big-boned, and coarse in the palms and soles. I never saw the like of him before or after, ﷺ with much peace.\""],[368,"He was asked about the description of the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"He was neither short nor tall, with beautiful, well-combed hair, a reddish tinge in his face, big-boned, coarse in the palms and soles, large-headed, and with a long line of hair from the chest to the navel. I never saw the like of him before or after him. When he walked, he leaned forward as if descending a slope.\""],[369,"The Messenger of God sent me to people of mature age, while I was young in years. He said: \"When the two disputants come to you, do not listen to one of them until you have heard from the other, for that will clarify the judgment for you.\" He said: \"So I learned, and I have remained a judge ever since.\""],[370,"He used to wake his family during the last ten nights of Ramadan."],[371,"He used to wake his family during the last ten nights of Ramadan."],[372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake his family during the last ten nights and raise the curtains."],[373,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a funeral procession. When we reached Baqi' al-Gharqad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and we sat with him. He took a stick and began to scratch the ground with it, then raised his head and said: 'There is none among you, no soul that is breathed, but Allah has known its place in Paradise and its place in Hell, and whether it is wretched or blessed.' A man from the group stood up and said: 'Should we then abandon deeds and rely upon our book? For whoever among us is of the people of happiness will be facilitated to its deeds, and whoever is of the people of wretchedness will go to wretchedness.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Rather, act, for everyone is facilitated. Whoever is of the people of happiness will be facilitated to its deeds, and whoever is of the people of wretchedness will be facilitated to its deeds.'"],[374,"Four things: no man will find the taste of faith until he believes in them: that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with the truth, and that he will die and be resurrected after death, and he believes in the divine decree, all of it."],[375,"There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah."],[376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition and appointed over them a man from the Ansar, and commanded them to listen and obey. They angered him about something, and he said: 'Gather firewood for me.' Then he said: 'Light it,' and they lit it. Then he said: 'Did not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command you to listen and obey?' He said: 'Enter it.' They looked at one another and said: 'We fled to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Fire.' They remained like that, and his anger subsided and the fire was extinguished. When they returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Had they entered it, they would never have come out of it. Obedience is only in what is right.'"],[377,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why do you choose among Quraysh and leave us?' He said: 'Do you have anyone?' I said: 'Yes, the daughter of Hamzah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding.'"],[378,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why do you choose among the women of Quraysh and leave us?' He said: 'Do you have anyone?' I said: 'Yes, the daughter of Hamzah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'She is only the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding.'"],[379,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I not point you to the most beautiful young woman in Quraysh?' He said: 'Where is she?' I said: 'The daughter of Hamzah.' He said: 'Do you not know that she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding? Allah has forbidden through breastfeeding what He has forbidden through lineage.'"],[380,"Ali said from the pulpit, and Ibn al-Kawwa' asked him about the daughter of a brother through breastfeeding. Ali said: 'I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Do you not know that she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding?'"],[381,"Ali came out and said: 'Ask me.' Ibn al-Kawwa' asked him about the daughter of a brother through breastfeeding. Ali said: 'I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding.'"],[382,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was detained by the polytheists on the Day of the Confederates from the afternoon prayer until the sun was about to set. He said: 'O Allah, fill their graves and their homes with fire as they distracted us from the middle prayer, until the sun was about to set.'"],[383,"On the Day of the Trench he said: 'They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their homes and their graves with fire.'"],[384,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Trench: May God fill their houses and their graves with fire just as they distracted us from the middle prayer."],[385,"May God fill their graves and their hearts with fire, just as they distracted us from the middle prayer."],[386,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting on the Day of the Confederates at one of the breaches of the Trench, and he said: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May God fill their houses and their graves—or: May God fill their bellies and their graves—with fire."],[387,"The polytheists distracted us on the Day of the Confederates from the middle prayer—the middle prayer is the afternoon prayer. May God fill their graves, their houses, and their insides with fire."],[388,"We ordered Abida to ask Ali about the middle prayer, so he asked him and he said: I used to think that it was the dawn prayer, until I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ on the Day of the Confederates saying: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the afternoon prayer. May God fill their graves and their insides with fire."],[389,"The polytheists distracted the Prophet ﷺ from the afternoon prayer until he prayed it after the two evening prayers, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: May God fill their houses and their graves with fire, just as they distracted us from the middle prayer."],[390,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Confederates: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the afternoon prayer. May God fill their graves, their houses, and their insides with fire. Then he prayed it between the two evening prayers, between sunset and evening."],[391,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Trench: May God fill their graves and their bellies with fire, just as they distracted us from the middle prayer, the afternoon prayer, until the sun set."],[392,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me, along with al-Zubayr and al-Miqdad, and he said: Go until you reach the meadow of Khakh, for there is a woman there, and with her is a letter that you will find with her. So we went racing, until we came to the meadow, and there was the woman. We said: Bring out the letter. She said: I have no letter with me. We said: You will bring out the letter or we will search your clothes. So she brought it out from her hair braids. Then we came to the Prophet ﷺ, and in it was: From Hatib b. Abi Balta'a to the people of Makkah, informing them of some of the affairs of the Messenger of God ﷺ. So the Messenger of God ﷺ called Hatib and said: What is this? He said: Do not be hasty with me. I was an ally attached to Quraysh, not one of their own, and there is no one among your companions but has in Makkah someone to protect him and look after his family, except me. So I wanted to have a favor with them. I did not do it out of disbelief or apostasy from my religion, nor out of approval of disbelief after Islam. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: He has told you the truth. Umar said: Let me strike the neck of this hypocrite, O Messenger of God. He said to him: He was present at Badr. And what do you know? Perhaps God has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you."],[393,"The Messenger of God sent me, along with al-Zubayr and al-Miqdad. Sufyan said: These are the knights of the believers. He said: Go until you reach the meadow of Khakh."],[394,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me, along with al-Zubayr and Abu Marthad al-Sulami, and we were all horsemen. He said: Go until you reach the meadow of Khakh, for there is a woman there with a letter from Hatib b. Abi Balta'a to the polytheists. Bring her to me. We caught up with her while she was leaning on her camel where the Messenger of God ﷺ had told us. I said: Where is the letter that is with you? She said: I have no letter with me. So we made her camel kneel and searched her saddle. My two companions said: We do not see anything with her. I said: We know that the Messenger of God ﷺ did not lie to us. By the One by whom we swear, you will bring it out or I will cut you—meaning with the sword. When she saw seriousness, she reached for her waistband, and she was wearing a woolen garment, and she brought out the letter. We brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: O Hatib, what made you do what you did? He said: O Messenger of God, I am nothing but a believer in God and His Messenger, but I wanted to have among the people a favor by which God might protect my family and property. Every one of your companions has among his people there someone through whom God protects his family and property. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: He has spoken the truth, so say nothing to him but good. Umar said: O Messenger of God, he has betrayed God, His Messenger, and the believers. Let me strike his neck. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Is he not one of the people of Badr? What do you know, O Umar? Perhaps God has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish, for Paradise is assured for you."],[395,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ intended to go to Makkah, he sent word to some of his companions that he intended Makkah, among them Hatib b. Abi Balta'a, and it spread among the people that he intended Hunayn. He said: Hatib wrote to the people of Makkah that the Messenger of God ﷺ intends you. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was informed of it. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me and Abu Marthad, and there was no man with us but had a horse. He said: Go to the meadow of Khakh, for you will meet a woman there with a letter. Take it from her. He said: We went until we saw her at the place the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned. We said to her: Hand over the letter. She said: I have no letter with me. He said: We put down her baggage and searched her, and we did not find it in her baggage. Abu Marthad said: Perhaps she does not have a letter with her. We said: The Messenger of God ﷺ did not lie, nor did we. We said to her: You will bring it out or we will strip you. She said: Do you not fear God? Are you not Muslims? We said: You will bring it out or we will strip you. Amr b. Murra said: She brought it out from her waistband—and Habib b. Abi Thabit said: She brought it out from her front. We came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the letter was from Hatib b. Abi Balta'a. Umar stood up and said: O Messenger of God, he has betrayed God and betrayed His Messenger. Give me permission to strike his neck. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Did he not witness Badr? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. Umar said: Yes, but he has broken his oath and aided your enemies against you. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Perhaps God has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish. Umar's eyes overflowed, and he said: God and His Messenger know best. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for Hatib and said: What made you do what you did? He said: O Messenger of God, I was a man attached to Quraysh, and my family and property were there. There is no one among your companions but has in Makkah someone to protect his family and property. So I wrote to them about that. By God, O Messenger of God, I am a believer in God and His Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Hatib has spoken the truth, so say nothing to Hatib but good. Habib said: Then God revealed: O you who believe, do not take My enemy and your enemy as allies, offering them affection."],[396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me, al-Miqdad, and al-Zubayr to the meadow of Khakh, and he said: “There is a woman there who has a letter with her.” He said: We went out, our horses racing with us, and we came upon the woman. We said: “You will bring out the letter or we will search your clothes.” He said: She brought out a letter from the plaits of her hair, and in it was a message from Hatib b. Abi Balta‘ah to the people of Makkah, informing them of some of the affairs of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What is this, O Hatib?” He said: “O Messenger of God, I did not write it as an apostasy from my religion,” and he made an excuse by something—its meaning was that he was a stranger there or something like this. ‘Umar said: “O Messenger of God, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite.” He said: “And what will make you know, O ‘Umar? Perhaps God has looked upon the people of Badr and said: ‘Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.’”"],[397,"He ascended the pulpit on Friday and delivered a sermon. Then al-Ash‘ath stood up to him and said: “This fair-skinned woman has prevailed over us in regard to you.” He said: “Who will excuse me from these sluggish men? One of them stays behind, tossing on his cushions, while these others hasten to the remembrance of God. If I were to drive them away, I would indeed be among the wrongdoers. By God, I heard him say: ‘They will certainly strike you back onto the religion, just as you struck them onto it at first.’”"],[398,"When it was revealed: “O you who believe, when you converse privately with the Messenger, present a charity before your private conversation,” the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “What do you think? A dinar?” He said: I said: “They cannot bear it.” He said: “Then how much?” I said: “A barley grain.” He said: “You are indeed frugal.” He said: Then it was revealed: “Do you fear to present charities before your private conversation?” He said: By this God lightened the burden for this community."],[399,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen while I was young in age and had no knowledge of judging. He said: So he struck my chest and said: “God will guide your heart and make firm your tongue.” He said: After that, I never doubted in any judgment between two people."],[400,"Muhammad ﷺ cursed the one who consumes usury, the one who pays it, its two witnesses, its scribe, the woman who tattoos, the woman who has herself tattooed, the one who makes a marriage lawful, and the one for whom it is made lawful, and the one who withholds charity. And he forbade wailing, and he did not say: He cursed."],[401,"‘Ammar came asking permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Grant him permission. Welcome to the good one, the purified one.”"],[402,"We were sitting with ‘Ali when ‘Ammar entered, and he said: “Welcome to the good one, the purified one. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Ammar was filled with faith up to his very bones.’”"],[403,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that the daughter of Hamzah belong to her maternal aunt, and he said: “The maternal aunt is in the position of the mother.” ‘Ali, Ja‘far, and Zayd had disputed over her."],[404,"I entered upon ‘Ali b. Abi Talib, I and two men: a man from my people and a man from Banu Asad, I think. He sent us on a mission and said: “You two are sturdy fellows, so strive for your religion.” Then he entered the privy, relieved himself, then came out, took a handful of water, and wiped himself with it. Then he began to recite the Quran. He said: It was as if he saw that we disapproved of that, so he said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ used to relieve himself, then come out and recite the Quran, and eat meat with us, and nothing prevented him from reciting the Quran except major ritual impurity.”"],[405,"Ali b. al-Ja‘d narrated to us, Shu‘bah narrated to us, something similar to it. I memorized it and did not find it after that."],[406,"I entered upon ‘Ali, I and two men: a man from among us and a man from Banu Asad, I think. He sent the two of them on a mission and said: “You two are sturdy fellows, so strive for your religion.” Then he entered the privy and then came out, took a handful of water and wiped himself with it, then came reciting the Quran. He saw that we disapproved of that, so ‘Ali said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ used to go to the privy and relieve himself, then come out and eat bread and meat with us. Nothing prevented him—or perhaps he said: nothing withheld him—from the Quran except major ritual impurity or a funeral.”"],[407,"I was ill, and the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was saying: “O God, if my appointed time has come, then give me rest; and if it is delayed, then raise me; and if it is a trial, then give me patience.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What did you say?” He repeated it to him, and he struck him with his foot and said: “O God, grant him well-being; O God, heal him.” He said: I never complained of that pain after that."],[408,"I was unwell, and the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was saying."],[409,"Do not pray after the afternoon prayer, unless you pray while the sun is still high."],[410,"When the fighting became intense on the day of Badr, we sought protection by the Messenger of God ﷺ. He was among the bravest of the people; no one was [braver]. He said: And no one was closer to the polytheists than he was."],[411,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from reciting while bowing, from wearing qassī garments, and from gold rings."],[412,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me—and I do not say he forbade you—from wearing qassī and saffron-dyed garments, from wearing gold rings, and from reciting the Qur’an while bowing."],[413,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from wearing gold rings, from qassī garments, from reciting while bowing and prostrating, and from wearing saffron-dyed garments."],[414,"We were with Ali when a man asked him: Should I recite while bowing or prostrating? He said: Ali said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: I was forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating. When you bow, glorify God; and when you prostrate, strive in supplication, for it is worthy of being answered for you."],[415,"Masrūq narrated to us: Ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Sulaymān b. Suḥaym, from Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Maʿbad, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, with something similar."],[416,"O Ali, say: O God, guide me and direct me aright; and remember, by guidance, Your guiding to the path, and remember, by directing aright, Your directing of the arrow. He said: And he forbade me from placing the ring on the index finger or the middle finger, and he forbade me from qassī garments and the mīthara. Abū Burda said: We said to Ali: What is qassī? He said: Garments from Syria and Egypt, ribbed, having designs like citrons. He said: And the mīthara is something women used to make for their husbands, like qatāʾif (a kind of cushion or cloth)."],[417,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from placing the ring on this one or on this one."],[418,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from gold rings, from reciting while bowing and prostrating, and from wearing saffron-dyed garments."],[419,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man from reciting the Qur’an while bowing, and he said: When you bow, glorify God; and when you prostrate, supplicate to God, for it is worthy of being answered for you."],[420,"I never heard the Prophet ﷺ combine his parents for anyone except Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas. Indeed, I heard him say on the day of Uhud: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[421,"When Abu Talib died, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Your errant, elderly uncle has died.' He said, 'Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I did as he ordered me, then came to him. He said to me, 'Perform a ritual bath,' and he taught me supplications that are dearer to me than red camels."],[422,"When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet and said, 'Your elderly uncle has died.' He said, 'Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I buried him, then came to him. He said, 'Go and perform a ritual bath, and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I performed the ritual bath, then came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications that I would not trade for red or black camels."],[423,"O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning."],[424,"A man came to Ali and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, tell me of a month I should fast after Ramadan.' He said, 'You have asked me about something I have not heard anyone ask about after a man I heard ask the Prophet ﷺ. He said to him: If you are to fast a month after Ramadan, then fast Muharram, for it is Allah's month. In it is a day on which Allah accepted the repentance of a people, and on it repentance will be accepted for others.'"],[425,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a month I should fast after Ramadan.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If you are to fast a month after Ramadan, then fast Muharram, for it is Allah's month. In it is a day on which Allah accepted the repentance of a people, and on it repentance will be accepted for others.'"],[426,"Indeed, in Paradise there are chambers whose insides are seen from their outsides and whose outsides are seen from their insides. A Bedouin said, 'For whom are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'For one who speaks good words, feeds food, spreads peace, and prays at night while people sleep.'"],[427,"Indeed, in Paradise there is a market in which there is no buying or selling except forms of men and women. When a man desires a form, he enters it. He said: And in it there is a gathering of houris. He said: They raise voices the like of which creatures have never heard. He said: They say, 'We are the eternal ones and do not perish; we are the blissful ones and do not suffer; we are the content ones and do not become angry. Blessed is the one who is for us and we are for him.'"],[428,"There is no Safar, no Hama, and no sick person infects a healthy one. He said: I asked, 'Did you hear it?' He said, 'Yes, my ears heard it and my eyes saw it.'"],[429,"There is no Safar, no Hama, and no sick person infects a healthy one."],[430,"His father was in charge of Uthman's food. My father said: It is as if I can see the partridges around the large bowls. A man came and said to Uthman, 'Ali dislikes this.' So he sent for Ali, who came with his forearms smeared with leaves. He said, 'You are very often opposing us.' Ali said, 'I adjure by Allah any man who witnessed that a haunch of a wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"We are in a state of ihram; feed it to those not in ihram.\" Men stood and testified. Ali said, 'I adjure by Allah any man who witnessed that five ostrich eggs were gifted to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"We are in a state of ihram; feed it to those not in ihram.\" Men stood and testified. Uthman stood, entered his tent, and the people departed, leaving the food for the people of the water."],[431,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought game meat while he was in ihram, and he did not eat it."],[432,"I witnessed Ali and Uthman between Makkah and Madinah, while Uthman was prohibiting temporary marriage for Hajj and did not combine them. When Ali saw that, he entered into ihram for both, saying: 'Labbayk with Umrah and Hajj together.' Uthman said: 'Do you see me prohibiting people while you do it?' Ali said: 'I would not abandon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ for the saying of any person.'"],[433,"A Muslim owes another Muslim six duties of courtesy: to greet him when he meets him, to answer him when he invites him, to say 'Yarhamuk Allah' when he sneezes, to visit him when he is sick, to follow his funeral procession when he dies, and to love for him what he loves for himself."],[434,"He prepared some food and invited the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came and saw a curtain with images in the house, so he went back. He said: 'I said: O Messenger of God, what made you go back, may my father and mother be your ransom?' He said: 'There is a curtain with images in the house, and the angels do not enter a house containing images.'"],[435,"Ukaydir of Dumat al-Jandal gifted the Messenger of God ﷺ a silk garment, and he gave it to Ali, saying: 'Tear it into head covers and distribute them among the Fatimahs.'"],[436,"Indeed, in Paradise there are chambers whose outsides can be seen from their insides, and their insides from their outsides. A Bedouin said: 'For whom are they, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'For those who feed others, spread peace, and pray at night while people are sleeping.'"],[437,"Supplication is the weapon of the believer, the pillar of the religion, and the light of the heavens and the earth."],[438,"Would one of you not stand and pray four rak'ahs before Asr, and say in them what the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'Your light is complete, so You guided, and to You belongs praise. Your forbearance is great, so You pardoned, and to You belongs praise. You spread out Your hand and gave, and to You belongs praise. Our Lord, Your face is the noblest of faces, Your honor is the greatest honor, and Your gift is the best and most pleasant gift. You are obeyed, our Lord, and You thank; You are disobeyed, our Lord, and You forgive. You answer the distressed, remove harm, heal the sick, forgive sin, accept repentance, and no one can repay Your favors, nor can any speaker's words reach the extent of Your praise.'"],[439,"It suffices for a group, when they pass by, that one of them greets; and it suffices for those seated that one of them responds."],[440,"Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month is fasting for a lifetime, and it removes what is in the heart."],[441,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was gifted a silk robe. He said: 'He clothed me with it.' Ali said: 'I went out wearing it, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself.\" Then he ordered me, and I tore it up and divided it among my women: Fatimah and her aunt.'"],[442,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took the jizyah from the Magians, as did Abu Bakr and I."],[443,"I saw Ali come and ascend the pulpit; he praised God and extolled Him, then said: 'It is a decree that God decreed upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ, the unlettered Prophet: that no one loves me except a believer, and no one hates me except a hypocrite. He who has fabricated has failed.' Al-Nadr said: 'Ali also said: I am the brother of the Messenger of God ﷺ and his cousin; no one after me can say this.'"],[444,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sent on Monday, and I embraced Islam on Tuesday."],[445,"I do not know anyone of this nation, after its Prophet, who worshipped God before me. I worshipped Him five years, or seven years, before anyone of them worshipped Him."],[446,"We have nothing except the Book of God and this—meaning the scroll—from the Prophet ﷺ."],[447,"I heard Ali say to Abd Allah al-Sabaʾi: Woe to you! By God, he did not confide to me anything that he concealed from anyone of the people. And I heard him say: Before the Hour there will be thirty liars, and you are one of them."],[448,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shayba narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Hasan narrated to us with its chain of transmission, the like of it."],[449,"I said to Ali: Do you have anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ besides the Book of God? He said: No, by the One who splits the grain and creates the soul. We have nothing besides the Book of God, except that God grants a man understanding in this Quran, and what is in this scroll. He said: The blood-money, the ransom of the captive, and that a Muslim is not killed for a disbeliever."],[450,"We asked Ali: With what were you sent? He said: I was sent with four things: that no one should circumambulate the House naked, that no polytheist should enter the Sanctuary, that whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of God ﷺ, it is until its term, and whoever has no treaty has a period of four months, and none shall enter Paradise except a believing soul."],[451,"Shall I not inform you of the best verse in the Book of God, which the Messenger of God ﷺ related to me? He said: 'And whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: I will explain it to you, O Ali. Whatever affliction or illness or punishment befalls you in this world, God is too generous to repeat the punishment for you in the Hereafter. And whatever He pardons in this world, God is too forbearing to return to it after His pardon."],[452,"We entered with the Prophet ﷺ upon a man of the Ansar who had become swollen. The Prophet ﷺ said: Will you not relieve him of it? He said: So he was lanced while the Messenger of God ﷺ was present."],[453,"Honor your paternal aunt, the palm tree, for it was created from the clay from which Adam was created, and no other tree is pollinated besides it. And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Feed your childbearing women ripe dates, and if there are no ripe dates, then dried dates. And there is no tree more honored by God than the tree under which Maryam bt. Imran descended."],[454,"I said to Ammar: Ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for me about pre-seminal fluid, for his daughter is married to me, and I am ashamed to ask him. So he asked him, and he said: When he finds that, he should perform ablution."],[455,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about pre-seminal fluid, and he said: In it is ablution, and he should wash it. And in semen is the full bath."],[456,"He was a man who emitted madhy frequently, and he was too shy to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about madhy. He said: So he said to al-Miqdad, “Ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about madhy.” He said: So he asked him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “For it, ablution is required.”"],[457,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to sacrifice two rams on his behalf, and I love to do it."],[458,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform witr with nine surahs: in the first rakʿah: “Competition in more increase diverts you” (al-Takathur), “Indeed, We sent it down in the Night of Decree” (al-Qadr), and “When the earth is shaken” (al-Zalzalah); and in the second: “By time” (al-ʿAsr), “When the victory of God and the conquest comes” (al-Nasr), and “Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar” (al-Kawthar); and in the third: “Say, O disbelievers” (al-Kafirun), “May the hands of Abu Lahab perish” (al-Masad), and “Say, He is God, the One” (al-Ikhlas)."],[459,"It is as if I am looking at ʿAli on the gray mule of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mountain pass of the Ansar, and he was saying: “O people, indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ said: These are not days of fasting; they are days of eating and drinking, the days of Mina.”"],[460,"I departed from Muzdalifah with Husayn b. ʿAli, and I kept hearing him say: “Labbayka, Labbayk” until he reached the Jamrah. I said to him: “What is this talbiyah, O Abu ʿAbd Allah?” He said: “I heard my father, ʿAli b. Abi Talib, reciting the talbiyah until he reached the Jamrah, and he told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ recited the talbiyah until he reached it.”"],[461,"The camels of zakah passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he took a hair from the back of a camel and said: “I have no more right to this hair than any man among the Muslims.”"],[462,"ʿAli used to travel until when the sun set and it became dark, he would dismount and pray Maghrib, then eat supper, then pray ʿIsha immediately after it. Then he would say: “This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.”"],[463,"The Mahdi is from among you, the people of the house; God will set him aright in one night."],[464,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ while he was sleeping, and we mentioned the Dajjal. He woke up with his face red and said: “Other than the Dajjal is more fearful to me for you than the Dajjal: misleading leaders.”"],[465,"I was sitting with ʿAli when Abu Masʿud came to him, and ʿAli said: “Furrukh has come.” He sat down, and ʿAli said: “Do you give legal opinions to people?” He said: “Yes, and I tell them that the Hereafter is better.” He said: “Tell me, have you heard anything from him?” He said: “Yes, I heard him say: ‘There will not come upon people the year one hundred while on earth there is an eye that blinks.’” ʿAli said: “Your buttocks missed the hole; you erred in your first legal opinion. He only said that to those who were present with him that day. Is there prosperity except after the hundred?”"],[466,"Indeed, a miscarried fetus will intercede with its Lord if He admits its parents to the Fire, until it is said to it: ‘O miscarried fetus interceding with its Lord, go back, for I have admitted your parents to Paradise.’ He said: Then it will drag them by its umbilical cord until it enters them into Paradise."],[467,"He saw a man coming to a gap that was near the grave of the Prophet ﷺ, entering it and supplicating. He forbade him and said: “Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from my father, from my grandfather, from the Messenger of God ﷺ who said: Do not take my grave as a festival, nor your houses as graves, for your greetings reach me wherever you are.”"],[468,"When I married Fatimah, I said: O Messenger of God, what should I sell—my horse or my armor? He said: Sell your armor. So I sold it for twelve uqiyyahs, and that was Fatimah's dowry."],[469,"On the night Fatimah was brought to me as a bride, we had nothing to sleep on except a ram's skin."],[470,"I was sitting with Ali while he was engaged in some matter concerning the people, when a man came to him wearing travel clothes and said: O Commander of the Faithful. Ali was occupied with his affair, so the man said: I am... I said: What is your concern? He said: I was on Hajj or Umrah—he said: I do not know which of them he said—and I passed by Aishah, and she said: Who are those people who went out before you, called the Haruriyyah? He said: I said: In a place called Harura'. He said: They are therefore called the Haruriyyah. He said: She said: Blessed is the one who witnesses their destruction. She said: By God, if you asked Ibn Abi Talib, he would tell you their story. So from there I came to ask him about that. He said: Ali finished his matter and said: Where is the one seeking permission? The man stood before him and related the same story as he had told me. He said: Ali raised his voice three times, then said: I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and no one was with him except Aishah. He said: He said to me: O Ali, how will you be with a people who will go out at such-and-such a place—and he gestured with his hand toward the east—reciting the Quran but it does not pass their throats, or their collarbones? They pass through Islam as an arrow passes through the game. Among them is a man with a deformed hand, as if his hand were the breast of an Abyssinian woman. Then he said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god, did I tell you that he is among them? They said: Yes, so you went and sought him, then you brought him dragging him, as I described to you. He said: Then he said: God and His Messenger spoke the truth, three times."],[471,"O Ibn al-Khattab, I am the Messenger of God, and God will never cause me to be lost. So Umar went away, not enduring his anger, until he came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, are we not upon truth while they are upon falsehood? He said: Yes. He said: Are not our dead in Paradise and their dead in the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why should we give the diniyyah (concession) in our religion and return without God judging between us and them? He said: O Ibn al-Khattab, he is the Messenger of God, and God will never cause him to be lost. Then the Quran was revealed to Muhammad with victory, so he sent for Umar and recited it to him. Umar said: O Messenger of God, is it a victory? He said: Yes. So his soul was at ease and he returned, and the people returned. Then they went out to Harura'—that band of Kharijites, more than ten thousand—and Ali sent to them adjuring them by God, but they refused. Sa'sa'ah b. Suhan came to them and adjured them, saying: On what basis will you fight your own caliph? They said: Out of fear of fitnah. He said: Do not hasten into the misguidance of this year out of fear of the fitnah of next year. So they returned and said: We will proceed as we came. If Ali accepts the arbitration, we will fight as we fought on the day of Siffin, and if he rejects it, we will fight with him. They marched until they reached Nahrawan. A faction split off from them and began terrorizing people at night. Their companions said: Woe to you! This is not why we parted with Ali. Their affair reached Ali, so he stood and addressed the people, saying: What do you think? Should we march against the people of Syria or return to those who remained behind among your families? They said: Rather, return to them. He mentioned their affair and told them what the Messenger of God ﷺ said about them: A faction will emerge at a time of dissension among the people, and the nearest of the two parties to the truth will kill them. Their sign is a man among them whose hand is like a woman's breast. They marched until they met at Nahrawan and fought a severe battle. Ali's cavalry could not withstand them, so Ali stood and said: O people, if you fight for my sake, by God I have nothing with which to reward you, and if you fight for God's sake, then let not this be your conduct. The people made one united charge, and the enemy was cleared away, face down. Ali said: Seek the man among them. The people searched for the man but did not find him, until some of them said: Ibn Abi Talib deceived us regarding our brothers until we killed them. He said: Ali's eyes filled with tears, and he called for his mount, rode it, and went until he came to a hollow in which the dead were piled one upon another. He began pulling them by their feet until he found the man beneath them. They informed him, and Ali said: God is great, and he rejoiced, and the people rejoiced and returned. Ali said: I will not conduct a military expedition this year, and he returned to Kufa. He was killed, may God have mercy on him, and Hasan was made caliph and followed the way of his father, then he sent the pledge of allegiance to Muawiyah."],[472,"O mushaf, narrate to the people. The people called out to him: O Commander of the Faithful, do not ask it; it is only ink on paper, and we speak of what we have seen from it, so what do you want? He said: These companions of yours who went out—between me and them is the Book of God. God says in His Book concerning a woman and a man: 'If you fear a breach between the two, appoint an arbiter from his family and an arbiter from her family; if they both desire reconciliation, God will bring about accord between them.' The community of Muhammad ﷺ is greater in sanctity—or protection—than a woman and a man. They criticized me for making a written agreement with Muawiyah. I wrote 'Ali b. Abi Talib,' but Suhayl b. Amr came to us, and the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote: 'In the name of God, the Merciful, the Compassionate.' Suhayl said: Do not write 'In the name of God, the Merciful, the Compassionate.' He said: How then should we write? Suhayl said: Write 'In Your name, O God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Then write: 'Muhammad is the Messenger of God.' Suhayl said: If I knew you were the Messenger of God, I would not have opposed you. So he wrote: 'This is what Muhammad b. Abdullah has agreed upon with Quraysh.' God says in His Book: 'You have in the Messenger of God a good example for whoever hopes in God and the Last Day.' So Ali sent Abdullah b. Abbas to them, and I went out with him until, when we were in the middle of their camp, Ibn al-Kawwa' stood and addressed the people, saying: O bearers of the Quran, this is Abdullah b. Abbas. Let whoever does not know him know him, for I introduce him from the Book of God. This is one of those about whom and about his people it was revealed: '...a contentious people.' So send him back to his companion and do not debate the Book of God with him. He said: Their orators stood and said: By God, we will debate the Book with him. If he brings us a truth we recognize, we will follow it, and if he brings falsehood, we will refute him and return him to his companion. So they debated the Book with Abdullah b. Abbas for three days, and four thousand of them returned, all repentant, including Ibn al-Kawwa', until Ali brought them into Kufa. Then Ali sent to the rest of them, saying: You have seen what has happened in our affair and that of the people. So remain where you wish, but between us and you: do not shed sacred blood, do not cut off a road, and do not wrong a protected person. If you do, we will declare war on you openly. God does not love the treacherous. He said: Aishah said to him: O Ibn Shaddad, so he killed them? He said: By God, he did not send against them until they cut off roads, shed blood, and violated protected persons. She said: By God? He said: By God besides whom there is no god, it was so. She said: What is this thing I have heard from the people of Iraq, that they call him 'Dhu al-Thudayya'? twice. He said: I saw him and stood with Ali over him among the slain. He called the people and said: Do you know this man? Many came saying: I saw him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so praying, but they did not bring any proof other than that. She said: What did Ali say when he stood over him, as the people of Iraq claim? He said: I heard him say: God and His Messenger spoke the truth. She said: Did you hear him say anything else? He said: By God, no. She said: Yes, God and His Messenger spoke the truth. May God have mercy on Ali. It was part of his speech that whenever he saw something that pleased him, he would say: God and His Messenger spoke the truth. The people of Iraq then lie about him and add to the narration."],[473,"When the people of Nahrawan were struck down, Ali said to us: Search among them, for if they are the people the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned, among them is a man with a deformed hand, or a stunted hand. He said: We searched and found him, and we called him to Ali. He stood over him and said: God is great. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would tell you what God decreed on the tongue of His Messenger ﷺ for those who killed these people. He said: I said: You heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba. He said: This reached one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, as if she envied him for that."],[474,"I witnessed Ali on the day of killing the people of Nahrawan. He said: Ali said when they were killed: Bring me Dhu al-Thudayya—or the maimed one—he mentioned something of that which I do not remember. He said: They searched for him, and there was an Abyssinian like a camel, on his shoulder something like a woman's breast, with—Abdu al-Rahman said: I think he said—hair on it. If a soul could leave from joy, Ali's soul would have left that day. He said: God and His Messenger spoke the truth. Who..."],[475,"Ali mentioned the people of Nahrawan and said: Among them is a man with a deformed hand, or a stunted hand, or a maimed hand. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would inform you of what God promised through the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ for those who kill them. He said: I said: You heard it from him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba."],[476,"I was with my master Ali b. Abi Talib when the people of Nahrawan were killed. He said: The people felt something within themselves about killing them. Ali said: O people, the Prophet of God ﷺ told us of people who pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game, and they do not return to it until the arrow returns to its bowstring. The sign of that is that among them is a man with a deformed hand, one of his hands like a woman's breast, with a nipple like a woman's nipple, and with seven coarse hairs on it. Seek him, for I think he is among them. They searched and found him on the bank of the river beneath the dead. They brought him out, and Ali said: God is great, God and His Messenger spoke the truth. And the sign of that was a man wearing a bow with an Arab (bowstring). He took it in his hand and began thrusting with it into his deformed limb, saying: God is great, God and His Messenger spoke the truth, God and His Messenger spoke the truth. The people said God is great when they saw him and rejoiced, and what they had felt left them."],[477,"Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would inform you of what God promised through the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ to those who kill them. He said: I said: You heard it from Muhammad ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, three times. Among them is a man with a deformed hand, or a stunted hand—I think he said: or a maimed hand. He said: They sought that man and found here and there something like a woman's breast with small hairs on it. Muhammad said: Ubaydah swore to me three times that he heard it from Ali, and Ali swore three times that he heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[478,"I witnessed Ali when he killed the people of Nahrawan. He said: Seek the maimed one. He said: They searched among the dead and said: We do not find him. He said: Go back and search for him, for by God I have not lied, nor have I been lied to. They went back and searched, then he repeated the same several times: I have not lied, nor have I been lied to. They went and found him beneath the dead in the mud, and they extracted him and brought him. Abu al-Wadi' said: It is as if I am looking at him, an Abyssinian wearing a short tunic, one of his hands like a woman's breast, with hairs on it like the hairs on a jerboa's tail."],[479,"He mentioned the Kharijites and said: Among them is a man with a deformed hand, or a maimed hand, or a stunted hand. Were it not that you would become arrogant, I would tell you of what God promised to those who kill them through the tongue of Muhammad. He said: I said: You heard it from Muhammad? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba."],[480,"I was sitting with Ali when a man in travel clothes came and said, “O Commander of the Faithful, will you permit me to speak?” Ali was speaking to the people and they were speaking to him, and he paid no attention to the man. Then I asked the man about his news, and he said, “I was performing umrah and met Aisha. She asked, ‘Who are these people who have gone out in your land called the Haruriyya?’ I said, ‘They went out from a place called Harura, and they were named after that.’ She said, ‘Did you witness their destruction? I do not know’ – he said, ‘Yes,’ or, ‘No.’ Then she said, ‘Blessed is the one who witnesses their destruction. By Allah, if Ali b. Abi Talib wished, he would tell you their story.’ So I came to ask him about them.” Ali finished, and said, “Where is the one who sought permission?” The man told him what he had told us. Ali said, “There is no god but Allah,” and said “Allahu akbar” twice, then said, “I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when no one was with him except Aisha, the Mother of the Believers. He said, ‘O Ali, how will you be with a people who are such and such?’ I said, ‘Allah and His Messenger know best.’ He gestured with his hand and said, ‘A people who will come out of the east, reciting the Quran but it will not pass beyond their collarbones. They will pass through the religion as an arrow passes through its target. Among them is a man with a defective limb, whose hand is like the breast of an Abyssinian woman. I adjure you by Allah, did I tell you about them?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘I adjure you by Allah, did I tell you that he is one of them?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then you told me that he is not one of them, so I swore to you that he is one of them.’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then you came to me dragging him just as I described to you?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.’”"],[481,"Allah loves the believing servant who is tested and frequently repentant."],[482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “O Ali, perform ablution thoroughly even if it is difficult for you, do not consume charity, do not breed donkeys with horses, and do not sit with astrologers.”"],[483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Who is the most wretched of the former peoples?” I said, “The one who hamstrung the she-camel.” He said, “You have spoken the truth. So who is the most wretched of the latter peoples?” I said, “I have no knowledge, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “The one who strikes you on this,” and he gestured with his hand to the top of his head. He used to say, “I wish that the most wretched of you would rise up and dye this from this,” meaning his beard from the blood of his head."],[484,"When he entered the mosque, he would say, “O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy,” and when he left, he would say, “O Allah, open for me the doors of Your bounty.”"],[485,"All blessings are either oppressive or unjust."],[486,"Performing ablution thoroughly in difficult circumstances, walking to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous prayer wash away sins completely."],[487,"On the day of Badr, I was at a well drawing water from it, when a strong wind came. Then another strong wind, stronger than the first, came, and I had never seen a wind stronger than it except the one before it. Then a third strong wind came. The first was Michael with a thousand angels on the right of the Prophet ﷺ, the second was Israfil with a thousand angels on the left of the Prophet ﷺ, and the third was Gabriel with a thousand angels. Abu Bakr was on his right and I was on his left. When Allah defeated the disbelievers, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted me on a horse, and when I settled on it, it bolted with me and I was on its neck. I called upon Allah, and He made me firm on it. Then I thrust with my spear until the blood reached my armpit."],[488,"Allah is gentle and loves gentleness, and He gives for it what He does not give for harshness."],[489,"Abd Allah b. Salam came to me when I had placed my foot in the stirrup and said to me, “Do not go to Iraq, for I fear that the edge of a sword will strike you there.” Ali said, “By Allah, indeed…”"],[490,"Ammar sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Welcome to the good one, made good.”"],[491,"Doubt is from Sharik."],[492,"Indeed, Allah named war a deception on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ."],[493,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray at night eight voluntary rak'ahs, and during the day twelve rak'ahs."],[494,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[495,"He forbade a man from raising his voice with the Quran before the 'atamah and after it, confusing his companions while the people were praying."],[496,"He named his eldest son Hamzah, and he named Husayn after his paternal uncle Ja'far. He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called 'Ali, and when he came, he said: \"You changed the names of these two sons of mine?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" So he named them Hasan and Husayn."],[497,"I saw 'Ali performing ablution. He washed his palms until he cleaned them, then rinsed his mouth three times, and sniffed water into his nose three times, and washed his face three times, and his forearms three times, and wiped his head, and washed his feet up to the ankles. Then he took some of the leftover water of his purification and drank it while standing. Then he said: \"I wanted to show you how the purification of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was.\""],[498,"When he finished his purification, he would take a handful of the leftover water of his purification and drink it."],[499,"When blood stirs in one of you, let him shed it, even with a broad arrowhead."],[500,"I went out on a cold morning, hungry, and the cold had exhausted me. I took a woolen garment that we had, then I put it around my neck and tied it on my chest to keep warm with it. By Allah, there was nothing in my house for me to eat, and if there had been anything in the house of the Prophet ﷺ it would have reached me. So I went out to one of the areas of Madinah and went to a Jew in his garden. I looked at him from a gap in his wall. He said: \"What is the matter with you, O Bedouin? Would you like a bucket for a date?\" I said: \"Yes, open the garden for me.\" So he opened it for me, and I entered. I began drawing the bucket and he would give me a date, until I filled my palm. I said: \"That is enough from you now.\" Then I ate them, then drank some water. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat with him in the mosque, while he was with a group of his companions. Mus'ab b. 'Umayr appeared before us in a cloak of his patched with fur. He had been the most pampered youth in Makkah and the most comfortable in his living. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he remembered the luxury he had been in, and saw the condition he was in now, so his eyes shed tears and he wept. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Are you better today, or when a tray of bread and meat is brought to one of you in the morning, and another in the evening, and he goes out in one fine garment and returns in another, and you cover your houses as the Ka'bah is covered?\" We said: \"Rather we are better then, free for worship.\" He said: \"Rather you are better today.\""],[501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me to Fatimah for an iron coat of mail of the Hutami type, and he had given it to me as armor. He said: \"Send it to her, so it may make her lawful to you by it.\" So I sent it to her. By Allah, its price was not such and such and four hundred dirhams."],[502,"I witnessed 'Uthman b. 'Affan when al-Walid b. 'Uqbah was brought to him, who had led the people of Kufah in the morning prayer with four rak'ahs, then said: \"Shall I give you more?\" He said: Humran and another man testified against him. One of them testified that he saw him drinking it - meaning wine - and the other testified that he saw him vomiting it. 'Uthman said: \"He would not have vomited it unless he drank it.\" So he said to 'Ali b. Abi Talib: \"Carry out the prescribed punishment on him.\" 'Ali said to his son al-Hasan: \"Carry out the prescribed punishment on him.\" Al-Hasan said: \"Appoint someone to handle its heat who has assumed its cold.\" So he said to 'Abdullah b. Ja'far, his nephew: \"Carry out the prescribed punishment on him.\" He took a whip and flogged him, while 'Ali counted. When it reached forty, he said: \"Stop. The Prophet ﷺ flogged forty, Abu Bakr forty, and 'Umar eighty. Each is a Sunnah, and this is dearer to me.\""],[503,"The watchword of the Prophet ﷺ was 'O all good.'"],[504,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out in a funeral procession and said: 'Is there not a man who will go to Madinah and leave no grave but that he levels it, no image but that he smears it over, and no idol but that he breaks it?' A man stood up, but he was fearful of the people of Madinah, so Ali stood up and said: 'I, O Messenger of God.' He said: So he went, then he came back and said: 'O Messenger of God, I did not come back to you until I had left no grave among them but that I leveled it, no image but that I smeared it over, and no idol but that I broke it.' He said: 'Whoever returns to making any of that has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ. Do not be a tempter, nor arrogant, nor a trader—except a trader of good, for those are the ones who race ahead in deeds.'"],[505,"He summoned the chief of his guards and said: 'Go out and leave no grave but that you level it, and no adornment but that you remove it.' Then he said: 'Do you know for what I have sent you? I have sent you for what the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me.'"],[506,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to slaughter the camels and to give their meat in charity. I returned to him to ask him about their saddle blankets and hides, and he commanded me to give them in charity."],[507,"The right of a Muslim over a Muslim is six: to greet him with peace when he meets him, to answer him when he invites him, to advise him in his absence, to invoke God's mercy on him when he sneezes, to visit him when he falls ill, and to attend his funeral when he dies."],[508,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Fatimah: 'I, you, this one—meaning me—and these two, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, will be on the Day of Resurrection in one place.'"],[509,"Whoever would like to look at a man some of whose limbs have preceded him to Paradise, let him look at Zayd b. Suhan."],[510,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would eat tharid, drink milk, and pray without performing ablution."],[511,"Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire."],[512,"I would not pay blood money for someone on whom I carried out a prescribed punishment, except the wine drinker, for the Messenger of God ﷺ did not establish any ruling regarding it; it is just something we said ourselves."],[513,"I heard Ali on the Day of the Camel say: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me saying: Talhah and al-Zubayr are my two neighbors in Paradise.'"],[514,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed ten: the one who consumes usury, the one who gives it, its scribe, its two witnesses, the woman who tattoos, the woman who asks to be tattooed, the one who withholds charity, the one who makes lawful, and the one for whom it is made lawful."],[515,"When it was revealed: 'And [due] to God from the people is a pilgrimage to the House—for whoever is able to find thereto a way' [Quran 3:97], the believers said: 'O Messenger of God, is it every year? Twice?' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent. They said: 'O Messenger of God, is it every year? Twice?' He said: 'No, and if I had said yes, it would have become obligatory.' Then God sent down: 'O you who have believed, do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you' [Quran 5:101]."],[516,"I heard Ali on the pulpit, and a man came to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, why do I see you treating people the way a man treats his camels? Is it by a covenant from the Messenger of God ﷺ or something you have seen? He said: By God, I have not lied, nor have I been lied to; I have not strayed, nor have I been led astray. Rather, it is a covenant from the Messenger of God ﷺ which he entrusted to me. And he who fabricates has failed."],[517,"I heard Ali say from this pulpit of yours: The Prophet ﷺ entrusted to me that I should fight the oath-breakers, the deviators, and the renegades."],[518,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in my dream, and I complained to him of the crookedness and stubbornness I had encountered from his community, and I wept. He said to me: Do not weep, O Ali; and he turned, so I turned, and behold, two men were climbing up, and there were boulders with which their heads were being crushed until they split open; then it would return — or he said: it would go back. He said: Then I went to Ali in the morning as I used to go to him every day, until when I was among the leather-workers I met the people, and they said: The Commander of the Faithful has been killed."],[519,"He prepared food and invited the Messenger of God ﷺ; he saw in the house something in which there were images, and he went back. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, what made you go back, may my father and mother be your ransom? He said: In the house there is a curtain with images on it, and the angels do not enter a house in which there are images."],[520,"The best of its women is Maryam bt. Imran; she is the best of its women in that time, and the best of its women is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid."],[521,"Islam is eight shares: Islam is a share, prayer is a share, zakāt is a share, hajj is a share, jihad is a share, fasting Ramadan is a share, enjoining good is a share, and forbidding evil is a share. And he has failed who has no share."],[522,"Nothing would prevent him from reciting the Quran except being in a state of major ritual impurity."],[523,"I saw the moon on the Night of Decree as if it were half a bowl."],[524,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Zayd b. Harithah when they disputed over the daughter of Hamzah: As for you, O Zayd, you are our brother and our client."],[525,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade singing-girls and wailing-women, and buying them, selling them, and trading in them, and said: Their earnings are unlawful."],[526,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came looking for me and found me asleep in a stream bed, so he said: Get up; I do not blame people for calling you Abu Turab. He said: He saw that I felt something in myself because of that, so he said: Get up, for by God, I will surely please you. You are my brother and the father of my children; you fight for my Sunnah and free my responsibility. Whoever dies under my protection is a treasure of God, and whoever dies under your protection has fulfilled his vow. Whoever dies loving you after your death, God will seal for him with security and faith as long as the sun rises or sets. And whoever dies hating you dies a death of ignorance and will be held to account for what he did in Islam."],[527,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen and ordered me to forbid gourds, green jars, pitch-covered vessels, tarred vessels, and hollowed stumps."],[528,"I fought on the day of Badr, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and found him prostrating, saying: O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting. Then I went and fought, then I came and found the Prophet ﷺ prostrating, saying: O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting. He said: Then Allah granted him victory."],[529,"A man killed his slave deliberately, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged him one hundred lashes, exiled him for a year, erased his share from the Muslims, and did not retaliate against him."],[530,"The adornment of prayer is wearing shoes."],[531,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Bakr and Umar approached. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: These two are the masters of the elderly men of Paradise from the first and the last, except for the prophets and messengers. O Ali, do not inform them."],[532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: In you there is a likeness of Jesus son of Mary. The Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they placed him in a station that was not his. He said: Then Ali said: Two men will perish concerning me: a loving exaggerator who goes to excess for me with what is not in me, and a hating slanderer whose hatred of me leads him to slander me."],[533,"I saw Ali rinse his mouth three times with the sniffing of water, using one handful of water, then he said: Whoever wants to look at the purification of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this is the purification of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[534,"I said to a man: Recite to me thirty verses from al-Ahqaf. He recited to me differently from what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had recited to me. I said to another: Recite to me thirty verses from al-Ahqaf. He recited to me differently from what the first had recited to me. So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Ali was sitting with him. Ali said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Recite as you have been taught."],[535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing a gold ring, from reciting while bowing, and from wearing qassi and garments dyed with safflower."],[536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds and pitch-coated vessels."],[537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Ibn Mas'ud to climb a tree and bring him something from it. His companions looked at the thinness of his legs and laughed at them. The Prophet ﷺ said: Why do you laugh? The leg of Abdullah on the Day of Resurrection will be heavier than Uhud."],[538,"I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say on this pulpit: Shall I not inform you of the best of this nation after its Prophet? He said: Then he mentioned Abu Bakr. He said: Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the second? He said: Then he mentioned Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: Then he said: If I wished, I would inform you of the third. He said: Then he was silent. He said: Then we thought that he meant himself."],[539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade bargaining before sunrise and slaughtering milk-producing animals."],[540,"When this verse was revealed: 'And [due] to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House – for whoever is able to find thereto a way' [Qur'an 3:97], they said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is it every year?' He remained silent. Then they said, 'Every year?' He said, 'No; and if I had said yes, it would have become obligatory.' Then Allah revealed: 'O you who have believed, do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you' [Qur'an 5:101], to the end of the verse."],[541,"Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba had a spear. When we went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, he would plant it in the ground, and people would pass by it and carry it off. I said to him, 'If I go to the Prophet ﷺ, I will certainly inform him.' He said, 'If you do that, you will never have a lost item returned.'"],[542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at ʿArafah and said, 'This is ʿArafah, and this is the standing place; all of ʿArafah is a standing place.' Then he departed when the sun had set, placing Usama behind him on his mount, and he proceeded at his own unhurried pace while the people were striking right and left, not turning toward them, and he was saying, 'O people, you must be calm.' Then he came to Muzdalifah and prayed the two prayers with them together. When morning came, he came to Quzah and stood upon it, saying, 'This is Quzah, and this is the standing place; all of Muzdalifah is a standing place.' Then he departed, and when he reached the valley of Muhassir, he urged his she-camel on, and she quickened her pace until he crossed the valley. He stopped and placed al-Fadl behind him, then came to the Jamrah and threw the pebbles. Then he came to the place of sacrifice and said, 'This is the place of sacrifice, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice.' A young woman from Khathʿam asked him for a ruling, saying, 'My father is an old man who has become senile, and the obligation of Allah in the Hajj has overtaken him; will it suffice for me to perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said, 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.' He turned al-Fadl's neck away, and al-ʿAbbas said to him, 'Why did you turn the neck of your cousin?' He said, 'I saw a young man and a young woman, and I did not feel safe from Satan concerning them.' A man came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I departed from ʿArafah before shaving my head.' He said, 'Shave or shorten, and there is no harm.' Another man came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before throwing the pebbles.' He said, 'Throw, and there is no harm.' Then he came to the House and circumambulated it, then came to Zamzam and said, 'O Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib, your water-giving; were it not that the people would overcome you, I would draw water with you.'"],[543,"ʿUmar b. al-Khattab said, 'What do you think about the surplus of this wealth that remains with us?' The people said, 'O Commander of the Believers, we have kept you away from your family, your estate, and your trade, so it is yours.' He said to me, 'What do you say?' I said, 'They advised you.' He said, 'Speak.' I said, 'Why do you make your certainty into assumption and your knowledge into ignorance?' He said, 'You will come out of what you said, or I will punish you.' I said, 'Yes, I will come out of it. Do you remember when the Prophet of Allah ﷺ sent you as a tax collector, and you came to al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, and he withheld his alms from you? You said to me, \"Come with me to the Prophet ﷺ, and we will inform him of what al-ʿAbbas did.\" So we went to the Prophet ﷺ and found him dejected, so we returned. Then we came back to him the next day and found him in good spirits, and you informed him of what al-ʿAbbas did. He said, \"Do you not know that a man's uncle is the equal of his father?\" And we mentioned to him the dejection we had seen on the first day and the good spirits we had seen on the second day. He said, \"You came to me on the first day while one dinar from the alms remained with me, and what you saw was because of that; and you came to me today after I had distributed it, and that good spirits you saw was because of that.\"' ʿUmar said, 'You have spoken the truth. By Allah, I will thank you for the first and the last.' I said, 'O Commander of the Believers, why do you hasten the punishment and delay the thanks?'"],[544,"When the people withdrew from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, I looked among the slain but did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, 'By Allah, he would not flee, and I do not see him among the slain, but I think Allah became angry with us for what we did and raised up His Prophet ﷺ. There is no good in me unless I fight until I am killed.' So I broke the sheath of my sword, then charged at the people, and they parted for me, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among them."],[545,"I obtained an old she-camel among the spoils of Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me another old she-camel. I made both of them kneel at the door of a man from the Ansar, intending to load on them sweet rush to sell, and with me was a goldsmith from Banu Qaynuqaʿ. ʿAli said, 'I was seeking his help for the wedding feast of Fatima.' Hamza b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib was in the house drinking, and with him was a singing girl who was singing to him: 'O Hamza, for the noble old she-camels.' He rushed at them with his sword, cut off their humps, ripped open their flanks, and took some of their livers. I said to Ibn Shihab, 'And from the hump?' He said, 'He cut off their humps.' He said: I looked at something that horrified me, and I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was Zayd b. Haritha. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, and with him was Zayd b. Haritha, and I went out with him until he stood over Hamza. He said: He became angry with him. He said: Hamza raised his eyes and said, 'Are you not but slaves of my fathers?' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ backed away from him."],[546,"When ʿAli traveled, he would journey after the sun had set until it was almost dark, then he would dismount and pray the Maghrib prayer, then he would call for his dinner and eat, then he would pray the ʿIsha prayer, then he would resume his journey, and he would say, 'Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do.'"],[547,"He forbade that any of the meat of your sacrificial animals remain with you after three days."],[548,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr. He gave me his daughter in marriage, carried me to the abode of emigration, and freed Bilal from his own wealth. May Allah have mercy on ʿUmar. He speaks the truth even if it is bitter; the truth has left him with no friend. May Allah have mercy on ʿUthman. The angels are shy of him. May Allah have mercy on ʿAli. O Allah, make the truth turn with him however it turns.'"],[549,"I said to Fatima, 'If only you would go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him for a servant, for the work has exhausted you.' She went to him but did not find him, and he said, 'Shall I not direct you both to something better than what you asked for? When you retire to your beds, glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times. That is one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the scale.'"],[550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us until he placed his foot between me and Fatima and taught us what to say when we took to our beds: thirty-three glorifications, thirty-three praises, and thirty-four magnifications. ʿAli said, 'I have never abandoned them since.' A man said to him, 'Not even on the night of Siffin?' He said, 'Not even on the night of Siffin.'"],[551,"The one who speaks an obscenity and the one who listens to it are equal in sin."],[552,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Zayd b. Harithah when they disputed over the daughter of Hamzah: “As for you, Zayd, you are our brother and our mawla.”"],[553,"We were with Ali when the people of al-Nahrawan were killed. He said: “Seek out for me the mukhaddaj (the one with the deformed limb).” The people went but did not find him. He said: “Return and seek him.” They went but did not find him. He said: “Return and seek him, for by God, I have not been lied to, nor have I lied.” He said: They went and extracted him from beneath the slain, in mud, and brought him. It is as if I am looking at him: an Abyssinian, upon him a short garment, one of his hands like the nipple of a woman, upon it hairs like the hairs on the tail of a jerboa."],[554,"Ali prepared food, and the Prophet ﷺ came. When he looked at the house, he turned back. Ali said: “What made you turn back, O Prophet of God, may my father and mother be your ransom?” He said: “I saw in your house a curtain with images upon it, and indeed the angels do not enter a house in which there are images.”"],[555,"Maternal brothers do not inherit the blood-money of their brother for their mother when he is killed."],[556,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to destroy its wells."],[557,"When I narrate to you from the Messenger of God ﷺ, then for me to fall from the sky is more beloved to me than to say about the Messenger of God ﷺ what he did not say. However, war is deception."],[558,"I came to Ali and asked him about wiping over the leather socks. He said: “We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and we wiped for three days and their nights, and for the resident, one day.”"],[559,"You have been exempted from the zakat of horses and slaves, but come forward with the zakat of silver: from every forty dirhams, one dirham. And nothing is taken from you until it reaches two hundred dirhams; when it is two hundred dirhams, in it is five dirhams."],[560,"The believers' blood is equal, and they are one hand against others; the lowest of them may grant protection on their behalf. Verily, a believer is not to be killed for a disbeliever, nor one with a covenant while his covenant is in effect."],[561,"He sent the commander of his police and said to him: “Do you know upon what I am sending you? I am sending you upon what the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me: to obliterate every image, meaning every picture, and to level every grave.”"],[562,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed the people one day and said: “Verily, the commanders are from Quraysh; verily, the commanders are from Quraysh; verily, the commanders are from Quraysh, as long as they uphold three things: when they judge, they are just; when they make a treaty, they fulfill it; and when mercy is asked of them, they show mercy. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people.”"],[563,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was holding my hand and we were walking in some lanes of Madinah, we came upon a garden. I said: “O Messenger of God, how beautiful a garden it is!” He said: “For you in Paradise is what is more beautiful than it.” Then we passed by another, and I said: “O Messenger of God, how beautiful a garden it is.” He said: “For you in Paradise is what is more beautiful than it.” Until we passed by seven gardens, each time I said: “How beautiful it is!” and he said: “For you in Paradise is what is more beautiful than it.” When the road became empty for him, he embraced me and then burst into tears. He said: I said: “O Messenger of God, what makes you weep?” He said: “Grudges in the chests of people; they will not show them to you except after me.” He said: I said: “O Messenger of God, will my religion be safe?” He said: “Your religion will be safe.”"],[564,"The first of creation to be clothed will be Ibrahim, in two Egyptian garments, and Muhammad will be clothed in a striped Yemeni cloak. He said: And he will be on the right of the Throne."],[565,"I witnessed Ali in al-Rahaba adjuring the people: I adjure by God anyone who heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: 'Whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla,' to stand and testify. Abd al-Rahman said: So twelve Badris stood, as if I were looking at one of them with trousers on, and they said: We testify that we heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: 'Am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves, and are my wives not their mothers?' We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: 'So whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be an enemy to whoever is an enemy to him.'\""],[566,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to the butcher who was slaughtering his camels, and he commanded me to give their meat, hides, and saddle cloths as charity, and not to give anything of that to the butcher. He said: 'We will give him from something else.'\""],[567,"Ali b. Abi Talib fell severely ill, so much so that he became exhausted and we feared for him. Then he recovered and regained strength. We said: Good news to you, Abu al-Hasan. Praise be to God who has healed you. We were afraid for you. He said: But I was not afraid for myself."],[568,"We saw the Messenger of God ﷺ stand, so we stood, and sit, so we sat."],[569,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution three times three times."],[570,"I saw Ali perform ablution three times three times, and he said: This is how the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution."],[571,"He used to pray after every obligatory prayer two rak'ahs, except after Asr and Fajr."],[572,"When he began the prayer, he said the takbir, then said: 'I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for God, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He, and with this I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O God, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself, and I have acknowledged my sin, so forgive all my sins, for none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character, for none guides to its best but You. Turn away from me its evil, for none turns away its evil from me but You. At Your service and Your aid. All good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. We are from You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You.' When he bowed, he said: 'O God, to You I have bowed, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed. My hearing, my sight, my bones, my marrow, and my sinews have humbled themselves to You.' When he raised his head from bowing, he said: 'God hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after that.' When he prostrated, he said: 'O God, to You I have prostrated, to You I have submitted, and in You I have believed. My face has prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it, and made its form excellent, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.' When he said the salam, he said: 'O God, forgive me what I have done before, what I have delayed, what I have kept secret, and what I have declared, and what You know better than I. You are the One who brings forward, and You are the One who holds back. There is no god but You.'\""],[573,"You are the One who brings forward, and You are the One who holds back."],[574,"He prohibited mut'ah marriage on the day of Khaybar, and the meat of domestic donkeys."],[575,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to take charge of his camels and to distribute their hides and saddle cloths, and he commanded me not to give the butcher anything from them, and he said: 'We will give him from our own resources.'"],[576,"Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him for a servant, and he said: Shall I direct you—or: teach you—what is better for you than that? When you go to your bed, glorify Allah thirty-three times, and say Allah is greater, and praise Allah, one of them thirty-three times and the other thirty-four times. Ali said: I have not left it since I heard it. It was said to him: Not even on the night of Siffin? He said: Not even on the night of Siffin."],[577,"Nothing prevented him from reciting the Quran except major ritual impurity."],[578,"We have exempted you from the zakat of horses and slaves."],[579,"Do not pray after 'Asr unless the sun is white and high."],[580,"We were at a funeral in Baqi' al-Gharqad, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and sat down, and we sat around him. He had a small staff, and he lowered his head and began scratching the ground with his staff. Then he said: There is not one of you, there is no soul that is breathed in, except that Allah has written its place in Paradise and its place in the Fire, and except that it has been written as wretched or blessed. He said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not rely on our book and abandon action? For whoever is among the people of blessedness will end up doing the deeds of the people of blessedness, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will end up doing the deeds of the people of wretchedness. He said: Act, for everyone is facilitated. As for the people of blessedness, they are facilitated for the deeds of the people of blessedness, and as for the people of wretchedness, they are facilitated for the deeds of the people of wretchedness. Then he recited: As for him who gives and fears Allah, and believes in the best, We will ease him toward ease. But as for him who is stingy and considers himself self-sufficient, and denies the best, We will ease him toward hardship."],[581,"A servant does not believe until he believes in four things: that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with the truth, and he believes in the resurrection after death, and he believes in divine decree."],[582,"I was with Ali when Abu Mas'ud entered upon him, and Ali said to him: O Farrukh, are you the one who said: A hundred years will not pass upon the people while there is on the earth an eye that blinks? Your anus missed the hole! He only said: A hundred years will not pass upon the people while there is on the earth an eye that blinks among those who are alive today. And the ease and joy of this ummah is only after the hundred years."],[583,"Indeed Allah is odd and loves the odd, so perform witr, O people of the Quran."],[584,"I saw Ali when a mount was brought to him, and he placed his foot in the stirrup and said: In the name of Allah. When he settled on it, he said: Praise be to Allah. Then he said: Glory be to the One who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we will return. Then he said Allah is greater three times. Then he said: Glory be to You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. Then he laughed. I said: Why did you laugh? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day the like of what I said, then he laughed. I said: Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Our Lord wondered at the saying of His servant: Glory be to You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. He said: My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives sins."],[585,"A woman who had committed fornication was brought to Umar, and he ordered that she be stoned. She was passed by Ali, and he recognized her, so he let her go. Umar was told: Ali took her from our hands and released her. He said: Call him to me. He came, and Umar said: Why did you release her? He said: By Allah, you know, O Commander of the Faithful, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the child until he reaches puberty, and from the insane until he recovers. And this is an insane woman of Banu so-and-so, and perhaps the one who fornicated with her came to her while she was in her affliction."],[586,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I bear witness that among what he pointed to me: This will certainly be dyed from the blood of this."],[587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade soaking in gourds and pitch-coated vessels."],[588,"Ali b. Abi Talib addressed us and said: By the One who split the grain and created the soul, this will surely be dyed from this – meaning his beard from the blood of his head. He said: A man said: By Allah, no one says that except that we will destroy his family. He said: I adjure you by Allah – or: I implore Allah – that you do not kill anyone on account of me except my killer. A man said: Will you not appoint a successor, O Commander of the Believers? He said: No, but I leave you as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left you. They said: What will you say to Allah when you meet Him? He said: I will say: O Allah, You left me among them for as long as You willed, then You took me, and I left You among them. If You will, You set them right, and if You will, You corrupt them."],[589,"When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, think of it in the way that is most fitting, most guided, and most God-fearing."],[590,"I had a time before dawn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I would come to him. When I came, I would ask permission. If I found him praying, he would say subhan Allah, and I would enter. If I found him free, he would give me permission. I came to him one night and he gave me permission, and said: The angel came to me – or he said: Jibril – and I said: Enter. He said: In the house there is something I cannot enter because of. He said: I looked and said: I do not find anything. He said: Look. So I looked, and there was a puppy belonging to al-Husayn b. Ali, tied to the leg of the bed in the house of Umm Salama. He said: The angels – or: we, the company of angels – do not enter a house in which there is an image, or a dog, or a person in a state of major ritual impurity."],[591,"I have not had sore eyes or a headache since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped my face and spat into my eye on the day of Khaybar, when he gave me the banner."],[592,"The killer of al-Zubayr asked permission to enter upon Ali, and he said: Let him enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Every prophet has a close disciple, and my close disciple is al-Zubayr."],[593,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud was mentioned in the presence of Ali, and he spoke of his virtue, then said: He once climbed a tree intending to pick fruit for his companions, and his companions laughed at the thinness of his shins. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Why do you laugh? His leg is heavier in the Balance on the Day of Resurrection than Mount Uhud."],[594,"The last words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were: The prayer, the prayer; fear Allah concerning those whom your right hands possess."],[595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform witr in the first part of the night, in its middle, and in its last part; then he settled on performing witr in its last part."],[596,"Some people from the people of al-Kufa rode to Uthman b. Affan and informed him about the matter of al-Walid – that he drank wine. Ali spoke to him about that, and Uthman said to him: Take charge of your cousin and carry out the prescribed punishment on him. He said: Get up, Hasan, and flog him. He said: What are you in this? Appoint someone other than me. He said: Rather, you have become weak and feeble. Get up, Abdullah b. Ja'far, and flog him. He began flogging him while Ali counted until it reached forty. Then he said: Stop – or: let him go. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged forty, Abu Bakr forty, and Umar completed it to eighty, and all are sunnah."],[597,"Ali flogged a man from Quraysh with the prescribed punishment for wine, forty lashes, with a whip that had two ends."],[598,"I entered upon Ali in his house, and he had urinated. He called for water for ablution, and we brought him a large cup that held a mudd or close to it, until it was placed before him. He said: Shall I perform ablution for you as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom. He said: The vessel was placed for him, and he washed his hands, then rinsed his mouth and inhaled water into his nose. Then he took water with his hands and splashed it onto his face, and his thumbs caught what was before his ears. Then he repeated the like of that three times. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and poured it over his forelock, then let it run down over his face. Then he washed his right hand to the elbow three times, and his other hand likewise. Then he wiped his head and his ears from their backs. Then he took water with both palms and splashed it onto his feet while he had on his sandals, then turned them over, and then did the same to the other foot. I said: In the sandals? He said: In the sandals, three times."],[599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from wearing garments dyed with safflower, from qassi silk, from a gold ring, and from reciting while bowing. Ayyub said: Or he said: and from reciting while I am bowing."],[600,"I was with Ali b. Abi Talib when a man came to him and said: 'What did the Prophet ﷺ confide to you?' He became angry and said: 'The Prophet ﷺ did not confide to me anything that he concealed from the people, except that he did'"],[601,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me three things—I do not say he forbade the people: wearing gold rings, wearing qassi and mu'asfar mufaddam, and reciting while bowing or prostrating."],[602,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade me three things—I do not say he forbade the people: wearing gold rings, wearing qassi and mu'asfar mufaddam, and reciting while bowing or prostrating."],[603,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade gold rings, qassi, and red mayathir."],[604,"I was sitting with my father when Ali b. Abi Talib came to us on some matter concerning the people. Then he said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: Say: O God, guide me and direct me aright; and remember with guidance Your guiding to the path, and remember with right direction the directing of the arrow by the forefinger. And he forbade me to place my ring on this one.' Abu Burda pointed with his thumb to the forefinger or the middle finger—Asim said: I was confused as to which one it was. He said: Ali said: 'And the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the mithara and the qassiyya.' He said: 'As for the mithara, it is something that women used to make for their husbands which they placed on their saddles. As for the qassiyya, they are garments of Syria—it was said: Syria or Egypt—ribbed, containing silk, and having patterns like citrons.'"],[605,"Zakariyya narrated to us, Salih narrated to us with his chain something similar."],[606,"Shall I not inform you of the best verse in the Book of God, which the Messenger of God ﷺ narrated to us: 'Whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your own hands have earned, and He pardons much.' And he ﷺ said: 'I will explain it to you, O Ali: whatever befalls you of illness, punishment, or trial in this world is because of what your hands have earned. God is too generous to repeat the punishment for you in the Hereafter. Whatever God pardons in this world, God is too majestic to return to it after His pardon.'"],[607,"We were traveling with Uthman when he heard a man reciting the talbiya for both (Hajj and Umra). He said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Ali.' He said: 'Did you not know that I have forbidden this?' He said: 'Yes, but I would not abandon the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ for your saying.'"],[608,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he said: 'There is none of you but has his seat written in Paradise and his seat in the Fire.' We said: 'O Messenger of God, should we not then rely?' He said: 'No, act, for everyone is facilitated.' Then he recited: 'As for him who gives and fears and believes in the best, We will facilitate for him the easy way. But as for him who is stingy and considers himself self-sufficient and denies the best, We will facilitate for him the difficult way.'"],[609,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed a man from the Ansar over an expedition he sent, and ordered them to listen to him and obey. They angered him over something, and he said: 'Gather firewood for me.' They gathered it. He said: 'Light a fire.' They lit it. Then he said: 'Did the Messenger of God ﷺ not command you to listen to me and obey?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then enter it.' They looked at one another and said: 'We fled to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the Fire.' He said: Then his anger subsided, and the fire was extinguished. When they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him, he said: 'If they had entered it, they would not have come out of it. Obedience is only in what is right.'"],[610,"The best of its women is Khadija, and the best of its women is Maryam."],[611,"I used to think that the bottom of the feet was more deserving of wiping than their top, until I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wiping their top."],[612,"I send you on what the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me: to not leave any image but that I efface it, nor any grave but that I level it."],[613,"A man came to Ali and said: ‘I bought a cow.’ He said: ‘Slaughter it on behalf of seven.’ He said: ‘It is broken-horned.’ He said: ‘It will not harm you.’ He said: ‘It is lame.’ He said: ‘When it reaches the place of sacrifice, then slaughter. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear.’"],[614,"The key of prayer is purification, its sanctification is the takbir, and its release is the taslim."],[615,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray after every prescribed prayer two rakʿahs, except Fajr and ʿAsr."],[616,"The witr is not an obligation like the prescribed prayer, but it is a practice established by the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[617,"I saw a man seeking forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists. I said: ‘You seek forgiveness for your parents while they are polytheists?’ He said: ‘Did not Abraham seek forgiveness for his father while he was a polytheist?’ He said: I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and it was revealed: ‘It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists,’ to the end of the two verses."],[618,"On the day of the Trench, the Prophet ﷺ was at one of the openings of the trench and said: ‘They diverted us from the middle prayer, the ʿAsr prayer, until the sun set. May God fill their cavities—or their houses—their bellies, and their graves with fire.’"],[619,"Zuhayr narrated to us: Wakiʿ narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from ʿAsim, from Zirr, that ʿAbidah al-Salmani asked Ali about this, and he mentioned from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to the hadith of Shuʿbah."],[620,"We asked Ali about the voluntary prayers of the Prophet ﷺ during the day. He said: ‘You will not be able to do them.’ We said: ‘Tell us, and we will take from them what we can.’ He said: ‘When the Prophet ﷺ prayed Fajr, he would wait until the sun was here—meaning from the east—at the same height as it is at the time of ʿAsr from here—meaning from the west—then he would stand and pray two rakʿahs. Then he would wait until the sun was here—meaning from the east—at the same height as it is at the time of Zuhr from here—meaning from the west—then he would stand and pray four rakʿahs, and four before Zuhr when the sun declines, and two after it, and four before ʿAsr, separating between each two rakʿahs with the taslim upon the angels brought near, the prophets, and those with them of the believers and Muslims.’ Ali said: ‘These are sixteen rakʿahs of the voluntary prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ during the day, and few persist in them.’"],[621,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would recite the Qurʾan to us in every state as long as he was not in a state of major ritual impurity."],[622,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Abu Bakr and Umar approached. He said: ‘These two are the masters of the elders of the people of Paradise, from the first and the last, except for the prophets and messengers.’"],[623,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that the debt is before the bequest, and you recite: ‘after any bequest that is made or debt.’ And that the full brothers of the same mother inherit to the exclusion of half-brothers from the father."],[624,"No angel enters a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[625,"Do not tell lies about me, for whoever tells a lie about me will enter the Fire."],[626,"Al-Ashtar and I entered upon ʿAli and he said: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ entrust to you something he did not entrust to the people generally? He said: No, except what is in this document of mine. He said: Then he brought out a document from the scabbard of his sword, and in it was: The believers' blood is equal, and they are one hand against those besides them, and the lowest of them may give protection on their behalf. A believer is not to be killed for a disbeliever, nor one with a covenant while his covenant stands. Whoever introduces an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people."],[627,"Let one of you place in front of him something like the back of a saddle, then pray."],[628,"We used to pray while animals passed in front of us, so we mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Something like the back of a saddle should be in front of one of you, then what passes in front of him will not harm him."],[629,"Whoever deliberately tells a lie about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[630,"The Prophet of God ﷺ used to perform ablution after eating camel meat and drinking its milk, and he did not pray in their resting places, and he did not perform ablution after eating sheep meat and drinking its milk, and he prayed in their enclosures."],[631,"ʿUthman b. ʿAffan called for water for ablution while al-Zubayr, Talhah, ʿAli, and Saʿd were with him. Then he performed ablution while they watched. He washed his face three times, then poured water over his right arm three times, washed his left arm three times, wiped his head, sprinkled water on his right foot, then washed it three times, then sprinkled water on his left foot, then washed it three times. Then he said to those present: I adjure you by God, do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform ablution as I have just performed ablution? They said: Yes. That was because of something that had reached him about the ablution of some people."],[632,"Three men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Who will suffice me against these? So I sufficed him against them. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent out an expedition, and one of those men went out and was killed. Then the other two stayed with me. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent out another expedition, and the second man went out and was killed. Then the last one stayed with me, fell ill, and died on his bed. Talhah said: I saw them in a dream as if the one who died on his bed was the first of them to enter Paradise, and the last of them to enter was the one who was killed first. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: What do you find strange about this? Indeed, the believer has such and such glorifications."],[633,"We were with Talhah b. ʿUbayd Allah while we were in a state of ihram, and a bird was gifted to him while Talhah was asleep. Some of us ate from it and some of us abstained out of scrupulousness. When Talhah woke up, he approved of those who ate and said: We ate it with the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[634,"I was with Talhah b. ʿUbayd Allah when a man entered and said: O Abu Muhammad, we do not know whether this Yamani is more knowledgeable about the Messenger of God than you, or whether he says about the Messenger of God ﷺ what he did not say. He said: By God, we do not doubt that he heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ what we did not hear and knew what we did not know. We were wealthy people with houses and families, and we used to come to the Prophet of God ﷺ at the two ends of the day and then return. He was poor, with no wealth and no family; his hand was with the hand of the Prophet of God ﷺ, and he went around with him wherever he went. So we do not doubt that he came to know what we did not know and heard what we did not hear, and we do not find anyone with any good in him saying about the Messenger of God ﷺ what he did not say."],[635,"A man came to Talhah b. ʿUbayd Allah and said: O Abu Muhammad, what do you think of this Yamani — or he said: al-Khidr said — the Yamani is more knowledgeable of the hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ than you — meaning Abu Hurayrah — we hear from him things we do not hear from you? He said: As for his having heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ what we did not hear, I do not doubt it, and I will tell you about that. We were people of households, and we used to come to the Messenger of God ﷺ in the morning and the evening, while he was poor with no wealth, just at the door of the Messenger of God ﷺ. So I do not doubt that he heard what we did not hear. And do you find anyone with any good in him saying about the Messenger of God ﷺ what he did not say?"],[636,"He used to pay the sadaqah of al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib two years in advance."],[637,"I passed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by a people on the tops of the palm trees, and he said: \"What are these people doing?\" They said: \"They are pollinating them, putting the male into the female so it becomes pollinated.\" He said: \"I do not think that avails anything.\" So they took that and abandoned it. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, and he said: \"If it benefits them, let them do it. I only thought a thought, so do not take me to task for conjecture. But when I tell you something from Allah, take it, for I will never tell a lie against Allah.\""],[638,"I heard Umar saying to Talhah b. Ubayd Allah: \"Why do I see you disheveled and dusty since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died? Perhaps it is the rule of your cousin that bothers you?\" He said: \"I seek refuge with Allah. I heard him say: 'I know a word which no man says when death is present to him except that his soul finds relief through it until it leaves his body, and it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.' So I did not ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he did not tell it to me. That is what has entered me.\" Umar said: \"I know it.\" He said: \"Praise be to Allah. What is it?\" He said: \"The word he said to his uncle.\" He said: \"You have spoken truth.\""],[639,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a word I did not ask him about until he died, or was taken. He said: \"I know a word which no man says at his death except that it will be light for him in his record, and his soul and body will find comfort through it at death.\" Umar said: \"I know it. It is the word he wanted from his uncle. I do not think it is anything but that.\""],[640,"Umar passed by Talhah after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Why do I see you dejected? Does the rule of your cousin displease you?\" He said: \"No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I know a word which no one says at his death except that it will be light for his record, and his body and soul will find relief through it at death.'\" He said: \"I know it. It is the one he wanted from his uncle. If he had known that anything would save him more than it, he would have commanded him with it.\""],[641,"I came to Madinah with a milch camel of mine, and I stayed with Talhah b. Ubayd Allah. I said: \"I have no knowledge of the people of the market, so if you would sell for me.\" He said: \"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a settled person from selling for a Bedouin. But go to the market and see who will do business with you, then consult me so I may command you or forbid you.\""],[642,"He sat with me while I was in the mosque of Basra in the time of al-Hajjaj b. Yusuf, with his staff in his hand and a document he was carrying in his hand. He said: \"O Abdullah, do you think this document will benefit me with this ruler of yours?\" I said: \"What is this document?\" He said: \"A document the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for us.\" I said: \"How did he write it?\" He said: \"I came to Madinah with my father when I was a young boy, with camels we brought to Madinah to sell. Talhah b. Ubayd Allah was a friend of my father, so we stayed with him. My father said: 'Abu Muhammad, come out with us and sell our riding camels for us, for we have no knowledge of this market.' He said: 'As for selling for you, no. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a settled person from selling for a Bedouin. But I will go out with you to the market, and when I approve of a man for you among those who trade with you, I will command you to sell to him.' So we went out, and he went out with us. He sat in a corner of the market, and men bargained with us for our camels, until when a man offered us what satisfied us, we came to him and sought his advice about selling to him. He said: 'Yes, then do business with him, for I approve of his faithfulness and his fullness for you.' So we traded with him and took what was ours. Then my father said to him: 'Get a document for us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that we will not be wronged in our sadaqahs.' He said: 'That is for every Muslim.' We said: 'Even so.' He said: 'He walked with us and said: O Messenger of Allah, these two would like you to write for them that they will not be wronged in their sadaqahs.' He said: 'That is for every Muslim.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, they would like to have a document from you.' So he wrote this document for them. Do you think it will benefit me with this ruler of yours? By Allah, we have been wronged in our sadaqahs.' I said: 'I do not think so, by Allah.'\""],[643,"I will not tell you anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that I heard him say: \"Amr b. al-As is among the righteous of Quraysh, and what an excellent household: Abu Abdullah, Umm Abdullah, and Abdullah.\""],[644,"\"Amr b. al-As is among the righteous of Quraysh, and what an excellent household: Abdullah, Abu Abdullah, and Umm Abdullah.\""],[645,"\"Amr b. al-As is among the righteous of Quraysh, and what an excellent household: Abdullah, Abu Abdullah, and Umm Abdullah.\""],[646,"Two men from Bali accepted Islam. One of them was killed in the way of Allah, and the other was delayed after the killed one for a year, then died. Talhah said: \"I saw Paradise in a dream, and I saw the latter of the two men admitted to Paradise before the first. In the morning I told the people about that, and it reached the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Did he not fast Ramadan after him, and pray six thousand rak'ahs after him, and such and such rak'ahs?'\""],[647,"\"No one remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in those days in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought except Talhah and Sa'd, according to their report.\""],[648,"And a number of people narrated to us, from Mu'tamir, with his chain of narration, something similar."],[649,"A camel that had been branded on its face was brought past the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"If only the owners of this camel had kept the fire away from this animal?\" He said: So I said: \"I will certainly brand it in the farthest place from its face.\" He said: So I branded it on the root of the tail."],[650,"We said: \"O Messenger of God, we have learned how to greet you with peace, so how should we invoke blessings upon you?\" He said: \"Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And grant barakah to Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You granted barakah to Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.\""],[651,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, how should we invoke blessings upon you?\" He said: \"Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim; indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And grant barakah to Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You granted barakah to Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.\""],[652,"Abu Musa Harun b. Abd Allah al-Bazzaz and others narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Bishr, with his chain of narration, something similar."],[653,"Umar saw Talhah b. Ubayd Allah looking sad, and said: \"What is the matter with you?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'I know some words which no servant says at the time of death except that relief is granted to him, his complexion brightens, and he sees what pleases him.'\" What prevented me from asking him about them was only my ability to bear them. Umar said: \"I know what they are.\" Talhah said: \"What are they?\" He said: \"Do you know any word that is better than the word to which the Messenger of God ﷺ called his uncle at the time of death?\" Talhah said: \"By God, it is that.\" Umar said: \"There is no god but God.\""],[654,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a non-muhrim who hunted game: may a muhrim eat it? He said: \"Yes.\""],[655,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a non-muhrim who hunted game: may a muhrim eat it? He said: \"Yes.\""],[656,"We set out as pilgrims with Talhah b. Ubayd Allah, and game was brought to us. Some of us ate and some refrained. He woke from his sleep—he had been sleeping—and we told him. He said: \"The one who ate did well. We ate it with the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[657,"The Prophet ﷺ wore two coats of mail on the day of Uhud, one over the other."],[658,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wore two coats of mail on the day of Uhud, one over the other."],[659,"When he saw the new moon, he would say: \"O God, let it appear over us with blessing and faith, safety and Islam. My Lord and your Lord is God.\""],[660,"When the Prophet ﷺ sighted the new moon, he would say: \"O Allah, let it appear upon us with blessing and faith, and with safety and Islam. My Lord and your Lord is Allah.\""],[661,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a Bedouin who came asking him about the one who had fulfilled his vow: Who is he? They would not venture to ask him, as they held him in awe and reverence. He said: The Bedouin asked him, but he turned away from him. Then he asked him again, but he turned away from him. Then I looked in from the door of the mosque wearing green garments, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me, he said: \"Where is the one asking about the one who has fulfilled his vow?\" The Bedouin said: I am he, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"This is one of those who has fulfilled his vow.\""],[662,"\"When one of you prays, let him place something like the rear part of a saddle in front of him, then pray and not care who passes beyond that.\""],[663,"\"Every Prophet has a companion in Paradise, and my companion is Uthman.\""],[664,"I witnessed Ali and al-Zubayr when they faced each other. Ali said to him: \"O Zubayr, I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'You will fight me while you are in the wrong'?\" He said: \"Yes, but I did not remember it until this very moment.\" Then he turned away."],[665,"I said to Abu al-Zubayr: \"Why do you not narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as so-and-so and so-and-so narrate from him?\" He said: \"I never separated from him since I embraced Islam, but I heard a word from him. I heard him say: 'Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[666,"When this verse was revealed: 'Indeed, you are to die, and indeed, they are to die' (Q 39:30), al-Zubayr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will the wrongs that occur among us in this world be brought back upon us, along with the specific sins?\" He said: \"Yes, they will surely be brought back upon you, until every right-holder is given his due.\""],[667,"\"The disease of the nations before you has crept upon you: envy and hatred. It is the shaver; I do not mean the shaver of hair, but the shaver of religion. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I tell you what will make that firm for you? Spread peace among yourselves.\""],[668,"\"Talhah made it obligatory when he did what he did for the Messenger of Allah.\""],[669,"By Allah, it is as if we are looking at al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam when he came to us on a white mule of his and said: \"O Umm Ata, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden the Muslims to eat the meat of their sacrificial animals after three days, so do not eat it.\" She said: I said: \"O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, what should we do with what is gifted to us?\" He said: \"What is gifted to you, that is your concern.\""],[670,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ joined his parents for me on the day of Uhud.\""],[671,"Ibn al-Zubayr said to him: \"O father, I saw you charging on your chestnut horse on the day of the Trench.\" He said: \"You saw me, my son?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"On that day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was joining his parents for your father, saying: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'\""],[672,"I said to Abu al-Zubayr: What prevents you from narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as his companions narrate from him? He said: I had a status and position with him, but I heard him say: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[673,"That one of you should take his ropes, then go to the mountain and bring a bundle of firewood on his back, then sell it and become self-sufficient with its price, is better for him than asking people, whether they give him or refuse him."],[674,"When it was revealed: 'You will surely be asked that Day about pleasure,' al-Zubayr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what pleasure are we in? There are only the two black things. He said: 'It will come to pass.'"],[675,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to address us and remind us of the days of Allah, until that could be seen in his face, as if he were warning of an army, saying: The matter will come upon you in the morning. He said: And when he had recently received revelation from Jibril, he would not smile broadly until it was lifted from him."],[676,"A morning or an afternoon spent in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that is in it."],[677,"When it was revealed: 'And warn your nearest kindred,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cried out on Abu Qubays: O Banu Abd Manaf, I am a warner. Quraysh came to him, and he warned them and alarmed them. They said: You claim that you are a prophet to whom revelation is sent, and that Sulayman had the wind and the mountains subjected to him, and that Musa had the sea subjected to him, and that Isa used to revive the dead? So call upon Allah to move these mountains away from us and to make the earth burst forth with rivers for us, so that we can make them into cultivated fields and plant and eat. Otherwise, call upon Allah to revive our dead for us so that we can speak to them and they speak to us. Otherwise, call upon Allah to turn this rock beneath you into gold so that we can carve from it and it can spare us the winter and summer journeys. For you claim that you are like them. While we were around him, revelation descended upon him. When it was lifted from him, he said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, He has given me what you asked. If I willed, it would be. But He gave me the choice between your entering through the gate of mercy, so that your believers would believe, and between leaving you to what you chose for yourselves, so that you would stray from the gate of mercy and no believer among you would believe. I chose the gate of mercy, so that your believers would believe. And He informed me: If He gave you that and then you disbelieved, He would punish you with a punishment with which He has punished no one in the worlds.' Then it was revealed: 'And nothing prevented Us from sending signs except that the former peoples denied them' until he recited three verses. And it was revealed: 'If there were a Quran by which mountains were moved, or by which the earth was split, or by which the dead were made to speak...' the verse."],[678,"We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would hurry to the thickets, and we would find only the places of our feet."],[679,"Change grey hair, and do not imitate the Jews."],[680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me, and for my children, and for my children's children. He said: I heard my father say to a sister of mine, who was older than me: O my little daughter. Meaning: you are among those reached by the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[681,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left his women in Madinah, he left them in Fari', and among them was Safiyyah bt. Abd al-Muttalib, and he left with them Hassan b. Thabit. A man from the polytheists approached to enter upon them. Safiyyah said to Hassan: The man is at your side! Hassan showed cowardice and refused. Safiyyah took the sword and struck the polytheist with it until she killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed of that, and he allotted a share to Safiyyah as he used to allot for men."],[682,"That on the day of the conquest of Makkah, he gave him the banner of Sa'd b. Ubadah. So al-Zubayr entered Makkah with two banners."],[683,"There is no morning upon which the servants wake except that a crier cries out: O creatures, glorify the Holy One."],[684,"On the day of Uhud, a woman came hurrying until she was about to overlook the slain. He said: The Prophet ﷺ disliked that she should see them, so he said: 'The woman, the woman.' Al-Zubayr said: I sensed that she was my mother Safiyyah. He said: So I went out hurrying to her and caught up with her before she reached the slain. He said: She struck me on the chest, and she was a hardy woman, and said: 'Away with you, may you have no mother!' He said: I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has firmly resolved concerning you.' He said: So she stopped and brought out two garments she had with her, and said: 'These are two garments I brought for my brother Hamzah. But there beside him was a man of the Ansar who had been killed, and had been done to as was done to Hamzah. We felt shame and shyness that Hamzah should be shrouded in two garments while the Ansari had no shroud. So we said: For Hamzah one garment, and for the Ansari one garment. We measured them, and one of them was larger than the other, so we cast lots between them, and each of them was placed in the garment that fell to him.'"],[685,"When it was revealed: 'Then, on the Day of Resurrection, you will dispute before your Lord,' al-Zubayr said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will our disputes in this world be repeated for us?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: I said: 'Then the matter is indeed severe.'"],[686,"'A single suckling or two sucklings do not make (marriage) unlawful, nor does a single suckling or two sucklings.'"],[687,"Sa'd b. Malik came to us after he had lost his sight, so I went to him to greet him and identified myself to him. He said: Welcome, son of my brother. I have heard that you have a good voice for the Quran. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'This Quran was sent down with sorrow. So when you recite it, weep; and if you do not weep, then make yourselves weep, and chant it. For whoever does not chant it is not one of us.'"],[688,"About the plague: 'If it occurs and you are in it, do not flee from it.'"],[689,"'If the plague is in a land, do not go down into it. And if it occurs in a land and you are in it, do not depart from it.'"],[690,"Umar said to Sa'd: 'They have complained about you in everything, even in prayer.' He said: 'As for me, I prolong the first two (rak'ahs) and shorten the last two, and I do not fall short of following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'That is what is expected of you,' or: 'Such is my expectation of you.'"],[691,"The people of Kufa complained about Sa'd to Umar, saying: 'He does not pray well.' Sa'd said: 'As for me, I used to lead them in the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the two evening prayers, without omitting anything from them. I would be deliberate in the first two and shorten the last two.' Umar said: 'That is what is expected of you, O Abu Ishaq.' He sent men to inquire about him in Kufa. They did not come to any mosque among the mosques of the people of Kufa but that the people spoke well of him and praised him, until they came to a mosque among the mosques of Banu Abs. There a man called Abu Sa'dah said: 'Since you have adjured us by Allah, he did not act justly in judgment, nor divide equally, nor conduct expeditions properly.' Sa'd said: 'O Allah, if he is lying, then blind his sight, prolong his life, and expose him to trials.' Abd al-Malik said: I later saw him accosting slave women in the streets. When he was asked, 'How are you?' he would say: 'Old, poor, and afflicted. The supplication of Sa'd has overtaken me.'"],[692,"'I forbid you from a small amount of that which intoxicates in large amounts.'"],[693,"'I forbid you from a small amount of that which intoxicates in large amounts.'"],[694,"My father took a sword from the fifth (of the spoils) and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'Grant me this.' He refused, so Allah sent down: 'They ask you about the spoils of war. Say: The spoils of war belong to Allah and the Messenger.'"],[695,"A man came to the prayer while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying, and when he reached the row he said: 'O Allah, grant me the best of what You grant Your righteous servants.' He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: 'Who spoke just now?' The man said: 'I, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Then your horse will be hamstrung, and you will be martyred in the path of Allah.'"],[696,"I said to Sa'd b. Malik: I want to ask you about a hadith, and I am in awe of you to ask you about it. He said: Do not do that, O son of my brother. If you know that I have knowledge, then ask me about it and do not hold me in awe. He said: I said: The saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ to Ali when he left him behind in Madinah during the expedition of Tabuk. He said: O Messenger of God, you are leaving me behind among the women and children? He said: Are you not pleased that you are to me in the position of Aaron to Moses? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Then Ali turned away hurrying, and it is as if I can see the dust of his feet rising. And Hammad said: Ali returned hurrying."],[697,"\"I declare inviolable what lies between the two lava tracts of Madinah, just as Abraham declared his sanctuary inviolable. Its thorn trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be killed, and no one shall depart from it out of aversion to it except that God will replace it for him with something better. And Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. No one intends them harm except that God Almighty will melt him as lead is melted in the fire, and as salt is melted in water.\""],[698,"\"Whoever claims descent from other than his father in Islam, while he knows that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him.\" He said: And my two ears heard it and my heart retained it from Muhammad ﷺ."],[699,"\"It is part of a person's happiness that he seeks the best from his Lord and is content with what He decrees, and it is part of the servant's wretchedness that he abandons seeking the best and is discontent with what He decrees.\""],[700,"\"The servant has been commanded to prostrate on seven parts of his body: his face, his two palms, his two knees, and his two feet. Whichever of them he does not place down, then he has fallen short.\""],[701,"The Messenger of God ﷺ closed the doors of the people in the mosque and opened the door of Ali. The people spoke about that, so he said: I did not open it; rather God opened it."],[702,"I said to my father: O my dear father, what do you think of His saying: \"Those who are heedless of their prayer\" — which of us does not become heedless? Which of us does not talk to himself? He said: It is not that. It is only the wasting of the time: he amuses himself until the time is wasted."],[703,"I asked my father Sa'd, and I said: O my father, \"Those who are heedless of their prayer\" — is it the heedlessness of one of us in his prayer, the talking of his self? Sa'd said: Do not all of us do that? But the one heedless of his prayer is the one who prays it at other than its time. That is the one heedless of it. Mus'ab said on another occasion: \"His abandoning the prayer in its times.\""],[704,"\"Whoever claims descent from other than his father in Islam, while he knows that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him.\" He said: And my two ears heard it and my heart retained it from Muhammad."],[705,"\"Whoever supplicates with the supplication of Jonah will be answered.\""],[706,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas said to a man: There is no Friday prayer for you. The Prophet ﷺ said: Why, O Sa'd? He said: Because he was talking while you were delivering the sermon. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Sa'd has spoken the truth.\""],[707,"The Prophet ﷺ left Ali behind, and he said: Are you leaving me behind? He said: Are you not pleased that you are to me in the position of Aaron to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me? He said: I am pleased, I am pleased."],[708,"He entered with the Messenger of God ﷺ upon a woman, and before her were date stones and pebbles with which she was glorifying God. He said: Shall I inform you of what is easier for you than this, or better? Saying: Glory be to God by the number of what He created in the heaven, and glory be to God by the number of what He created in the earth, and glory be to God by the number of what is between that, and glory be to God by the number of what He is yet to create, and God is greatest, the like of that, and praise be to God, the like of that, and there is no god but God, the like of that, and there is no power except with God, the like of that."],[709,"Every trait is imprinted – or he said: folded – upon the believer, except treachery and lying."],[710,"He asked Sa'd about white barley – meaning sult –, and Sa'd said: Which of the two is better? He said: White. So he forbade him from that, and Sa'd said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ being asked about buying dried dates with fresh dates, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do fresh dates decrease when they dry? They said: Yes, so he forbade that."],[711,"Abd Allah b. Awn narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Yazid, from Abu Ayyash, from Sa'd, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[712,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave to a group of people while Sa'd was sitting among them. Sa'd said: The Messenger of God ﷺ left out one who was not given, and he was the most admirable of them to me. I said: O Messenger of God, what about so-and-so? By God, I regard him as a believer. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Or a Muslim. He said: I fell silent for a while. Then what I knew of him overcame me, and I said: O Messenger of God, what about so-and-so? By God, I regard him as a believer. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Or a Muslim. He said: I fell silent for a while. Then what I knew of him overcame me, and I said: O Messenger of God, what about so-and-so? By God, I regard him as a believer. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Or a Muslim. Indeed, I give to a man while another is dearer to me than him, for fear that he be thrown into the Fire on his face."],[713,"Sa'd saw a son of his praying and supplicating, saying: I ask You for Paradise, and for its fruits, its delights, and its spouses, and the like of that, and he went on at length, and I seek refuge with You from the Fire, and from its chains, its shackles, and its blaze, and the like of that, while Sa'd was listening. When he finished his prayer, Sa'd said to him: You have asked for prolonged bliss and sought refuge from prolonged evil. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: There will be people who transgress in supplication. And Sa'd recited: Call upon your Lord humbly and secretly; indeed, He does not like the transgressors. He said: I do not know whether he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ or whether it is Sa'd's own statement: It is sufficient for you to say: I ask You for Paradise and whatever word or deed brings one near to it, and I seek refuge with You from the Fire and whatever word or deed brings one near to it."],[714,"Sa'd used to teach us five things, mentioning them from the Prophet ﷺ: O God, I seek refuge with You from miserliness, and I seek refuge with You from cowardice, and I seek refuge with You from being returned to the most abject age, and I seek refuge with You from the trial of this world, and I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave."],[715,"Whoever takes seven ajwa dates in the morning, neither poison nor magic will harm him that day."],[716,"Are you not pleased that you are to me of the standing of Aaron from Moses?"],[717,"I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza, and my companions said to me: You have uttered something abominable. So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I am new to the faith, and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. He said: Say: There is no god but God, three times, and blow to your left three times, and seek refuge from Satan, and do not do it again."],[718,"It is not lawful for anyone to abandon his brother beyond three days."],[719,"I was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he had a leftover portion of food. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A man from the people of Paradise will come upon you from this mountain pass and eat this leftover. He said: I passed by Umayr b. Malik while he was performing ablution, and I said to myself: He is the one. Then we began looking out for the figures of those who would come upon us, and Abd Allah b. Salam came upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he called him over for the leftover and he ate it."],[720,"Whoever says when he hears the muezzin: 'And I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Muhammad as Messenger, and with Islam as religion,' his sins will be forgiven."],[721,"Is one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day? A man among those sitting with him asked: How can one of us earn a thousand good deeds? He said: He glorifies Allah one hundred times, and thus earns a thousand good deeds and a thousand bad deeds are erased from him."],[722,"Sa'd b. Malik heard a man saying: Labbayka dha al-ma'arij (Here I am, O Possessor of the ascending ways). He said: Indeed Allah is Dhu al-ma'arij, but we did not say that with our Prophet ﷺ."],[723,"There was no prophet but described the Dajjal to his nation, and I will describe him with a description no one before me has described: he is one-eyed, and Allah is not one-eyed."],[724,"He used to perform ablution with a water-skin of water. He came out of the privy, performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. We were amazed at that and asked him, and he said..."],[725,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'One third, and one third is large—or much—for a bequest.'"],[726,"The plague is a punishment and a remnant of torment with which people before you were afflicted. If it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it. If you hear of it in a land, do not enter it."],[727,"I obtained a sword on the day of Badr and it pleased me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, grant it to me. Then it was revealed: 'They ask you about the spoils of war. Say: The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger.'"],[728,"Whatever you spend on your family, you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth."],[729,"The best provision is what suffices, and the best remembrance is the hidden one."],[730,"I was the first Arab man to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah. We saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when we had no food except samur leaves and the leaves of the hubla plant, until one of us would defecate like a goat defecates, with no mixture."],[731,"A group of people came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he gave them, except one man among them. Sa'd said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave them and left so-and-so. By Allah, I consider him a believer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Or a Muslim.' Sa'd said that he said that three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I give a man a gift while someone else is more beloved to me, and I do that only out of fear that Allah may cast him face-first into the fire of Hell."],[732,"He was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he passed by the mosque of Banu Mu'awiya, entered it, and prayed two rak'as in it. Then he stood and conversed privately with his Lord, then departed, and said: I asked my Lord for three things, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy my community by drowning nor by the year—meaning by famine—and He granted me those two. And I asked Him not to make their might turn against themselves, and He withheld that from me."],[733,"On the day of Badr, I brought a sword and said: O Messenger of God, this sword has healed my breast, so give it to me. He said: This sword is neither yours nor mine. I went out saying: Perhaps he will give it to someone whose trial is not like my trial. Then the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to me and said: Respond. I thought something had come down concerning me because of my words. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You asked me for it while it was not mine, and God has made it mine, so it is yours."],[734,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: I swore by al-Lat and al-'Uzza—and the covenant was recent. The Prophet ﷺ said: You have said an indecency. Say: There is no god but God, three times, and spit to your left three times, and seek refuge from Satan, and do not repeat it."],[735,"His father Sa'd was among his camels and sheep when his son 'Umar came to him. When he saw him, he said: I seek refuge in God from the evil of this rider. When he reached him, he said: Are you content to be a bedouin among your camels and sheep while the people in Madinah are contending for kingship? He struck his chest with his hand and said: My son, be quiet. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God loves the servant who is pious, self-sufficient, and hidden."],[736,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ went on the expedition to Tabuk, he left 'Ali behind in Madinah. People said: He has grown weary of him and dislikes his company. This reached 'Ali, so he set out until he caught up with the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, you left me in Madinah with the women, children, and dependents, until people said: He has grown weary of him and dislikes his company? He said: O 'Ali, I left you only over my family. Are you not content to be to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[737,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to 'Ali: You are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet with me."],[738,"Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an that you may understand. We relate to you the best of stories—the verse. He said: The Qur'an was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he recited it to them for a time. They said: O Messenger of God, if only you would relate stories to us. Then God revealed to us: Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an—the verse. He recited it to them for a time. They said: O Messenger of God, if only you would tell us. Then God revealed: God has sent down the best of speech, a Book consistent—the verse. All of that they were commanded with the Qur'an."],[739,"The people of Kufa complained about you in everything, even in prayer. He said: I lengthen in the first two and shorten in the last two, and I do not fall short of what I follow from the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: That is the thought about you, or: My thought about you."],[740,"Ali b. al-Madini narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us something like the hadith of Yahya, except that he said in his hadith: That is the thought about you, and he did not doubt."],[741,"The people of Kufa complained about you until they said: He does not pray well. He said: Me? He said: Yes. He said: By God, I do not fall short with them from the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. I prolong in the first two and shorten in the last two. I heard 'Umar say to him: That is the thought about you, that is the thought about you."],[742,"Whoever takes any part of the earth without its right will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths. Neither an exchange nor an equivalent will be accepted from him. And whoever claims descent from other than his father, or allegiance to other than his patron, has disbelieved."],[743,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about this verse: Say: He is the One able to send upon you punishment from above you or from beneath your feet. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Indeed, it will occur, but its interpretation has not yet come."],[744,"Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said regarding the third being made sunnah for me: I fell ill, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me. He said, \"Have you made a bequest?\" I said, \"I have bequeathed all my wealth.\" He said, \"Then what have you left for your heirs?\" I said, \"They are wealthy.\" He said, \"Bequeath a tenth, and leave the rest to your heirs.\""],[745,"\"I fell ill in the year of the conquest with an illness from which I feared death. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me during it. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have abundant wealth, and none will inherit from me except my daughter. Should I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth?' He said, 'No.' I said, 'Then half?' He said, 'No.' I said, 'Then a third?' He said, 'A third, and a third is large—or: much. Indeed, if you leave your heirs wealthy, it is better than leaving them poor, begging from people. You will not spend any expenditure but that you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my emigration?' He said, 'You will not be left behind after me such that you do a deed desiring the Face of Allah by it except that you will increase in elevation and degree. Perhaps you will be left behind until some people benefit through you and others are harmed through you. O Allah, complete the emigration of my companions, and do not turn them back on their heels. But the unfortunate one is Sa'd ibn Khawlah.' He expressed sorrow that he died in Makkah.\""],[746,"\"He is not from us who does not chant the Quran.\""],[747,"That his father, when he saw the disagreement of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and their division, bought livestock for him, then left and withdrew with his family in it at a water called Qalahhi. He said: And Sa'd was among the sharpest-sighted of people. One day he saw something moving, and he said to those with him, \"Do you see anything?\" They said, \"We see something like a bird.\" He said, \"I see a rider on a camel.\" Then after a little while 'Umar ibn Sa'd came on a Bactrian camel—or a female Bactrian camel. Then he said, \"O Allah, we seek refuge in You from the evil of what he has brought.\" 'Umar greeted, then said to his father, \"Are you content to follow the tails of these livestock among these mountains while your companions dispute over the affair of the ummah?\" Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There will be trials after me—or he said: matters—in which the best of people is the wealthy, hidden, God-fearing one. If you are able, my son, to be like that, then be so.'\" 'Umar said to him, \"Do you have anything other than this?\" Sa'd said to him, \"No, my son.\" 'Umar jumped up to mount, and he had not unloaded his camel. Sa'd said to him, \"Wait until we give you lunch.\" He said, \"I have no need of your lunch.\" Sa'd said, \"Then we will milk for you and give you drink.\" He said, \"I have no need of your drink.\" Then he mounted and departed from his place."],[748,"That Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said during the fitnah of 'Uthman: I testify that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There will be a fitnah in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one running.' He said: 'Do you see if he enters my house upon me and extends his hand to kill me?' He said: 'Be like the son of Adam.'"],[749,"\"Concerning me the prohibition of wine was revealed. I drank with a group of the Ansar before it was prohibited, and one of them struck me on the nose with the jawbone of a camel. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the prohibition of wine was revealed.\""],[750,"Indeed I am the first man to shoot an arrow at the idolaters, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never combined his parents for anyone before me. I heard him say: 'Shoot, O Sa'd, may my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[751,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned—meaning Dhu al-Thudayyah, the one found with the people of the Nahrawan—and said: 'A devil of a hollow, driven out by a man from Bajilah called al-Ashhab, or Ibn al-Ashhab, a sign among a people he wronged.'"],[752,"That a bowl was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ate from it, and some food remained. He said: 'A man from this mountain pass will come, one of the people of Paradise, and he will eat this leftover.' Sa'd said: I had left my brother 'Umayr performing ablution, so I said, 'It is 'Umayr.' He said: Then 'Abdullah ibn Salam came and ate it."],[753,"He said to 'Ali: 'You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.' Sa'id said: I wished to hear that directly from Sa'd, so I met him and mentioned to him what 'Amir had told me. He said, 'Yes, I heard it.' I said, 'You heard it?' He inserted his two fingers into his ears and said, 'Yes, and if not, may they be deaf!'"],[754,"\"Indeed faith began as something strange and will return as it began, so blessed are the strangers on that day when people become corrupt. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, Islam will surely withdraw between these two mosques as a snake withdraws into its hole.\""],[755,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted safety to the people except four men and two women, and he said: 'Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah: 'Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, 'Abdullah ibn Khatal, Miqyas ibn Subabah, and 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh.' As for 'Abdullah ibn Khatal, he was caught while clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah, and Sa'id ibn Hurayth and 'Ammar ibn Yasir raced to him; Sa'id beat 'Ammar—and he was the younger of the two men—and killed him. As for Miqyas ibn Subabah, the people caught him in the market. As for 'Ikrimah, he rode the sea, and a storm struck them. The people of the ship said to those on the ship, 'Be sincere, for your gods will avail you nothing here.' 'Ikrimah said, 'If nothing saves me in the sea except sincerity, then nothing else will save me on land. O Allah, I make a covenant to You: if You heal me from what I am in, I will come to Muhammad until I place my hand in his hand, and I will surely find him forgiving and generous.' He said: Then he came and accepted Islam. As for 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh, he hid with 'Uthman ibn 'Affan. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the people to pledge allegiance, he brought him and stood him before the Prophet ﷺ, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, accept the pledge of 'Abdullah.' He raised his head and looked at him three times, each time refusing, then he accepted his pledge after the third. Then he turned to his companions and said, 'Was there not among you a strong man who would stand up to this one—when he saw me withhold my hand from his pledge—and kill him?' They said, 'How could we know, O Messenger of Allah, what was in your soul? [Why did you not gesture to us with your eye?]' He said, 'It is not befitting for a prophet to have a treacherous eye.'"],[756,"He proposed to a woman in Makkah while he was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he said: \"If only I had someone who could see her, and tell me about her.\" A man called Hit said: \"I will describe her for you: when she approaches, you would say she walks on six; when she turns away, you would say she walks on four.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"I consider this objectionable; I think he knows about women's affairs.\" He used to visit Sawdah, so he forbade him from visiting her. When he came to Madinah, he banished him. This remained so until the caliphate of Umar. He struggled, so he allowed him to enter Madinah on Fridays, and he would give him charity."],[757,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas led us in prayer, and he rose in the two rak'ahs, so we glorified God to alert him, but he remained standing. He said: He continued in his standing until he finished. Then he said: \"Did you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.\""],[758,"Amr narrated to us, Waki' b. al-Jarrah narrated to us, Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, who said: Sa'd b. Malik led us in prayer, and he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah, but he did not mention the Prophet."],[759,"\"The Muslim with the greatest offense against Muslims is one who asks about a matter that was not forbidden to the people, and it becomes forbidden to the people because of his asking.\""],[760,"\"The Muslim with the greatest offense is one who asks about a matter that was not forbidden to the people, and it becomes forbidden because of his asking.\""],[761,"Ishaq b. Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir b. Sa'd, from his father, reaching it back to the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[762,"\"The Muslim with the greatest offense against Muslims is one who asks about a matter that was not forbidden to the people, and it becomes forbidden because of his asking.\""],[763,"When Ziyad made his claim, I met Abu Bakrah. He said: I said: \"What is this that you have done?\" He said: \"I heard Sa'd narrate, saying: My ears heard and my heart retained the Prophet ﷺ saying: 'Whoever claims a father in Islam while knowing that he is not his father, God has forbidden Paradise to him.'\" Abu Bakrah said: \"And I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[764,"\"There is no hamah, no contagion, no evil omen. If there is anything in birds, it is in the woman, the horse, and the house.\""],[765,"\"I never heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to anyone that he was among the people of Paradise, except to Abdullah b. Salam.\""],[766,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Prophet of God, teach me words to say.\" He said: \"Say: There is no god but God alone, with no partner. God is most great, greatly. Praise belongs to God, abundantly. Glory be to God, Lord of the worlds. There is no power nor strength except with God, the Mighty, the Wise.\" He said: \"These are for my Lord; what is for me?\" He said: \"Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, provide for me, and grant me well-being.\""],[767,"A man came while the Prophet ﷺ was leading us in prayer, and he said: \"O God, give me the best of what You give the righteous.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: \"Who spoke just now?\" The man said: \"I did.\" He said: \"Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be killed in the path of God.\""],[768,"I was sitting in the mosque, I and two men with me, and we disparaged Ali. The Messenger of God ﷺ came angry, anger recognizable in his face. I sought refuge in God from his anger, and he said, \"What is it between you and me? Whoever harms Ali has harmed me.\""],[769,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us these words: \"O God, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the worst of life, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of this world and the punishment of the grave.\""],[770,"I passed by Uthman b. Affan in the mosque and greeted him. He looked me up and down, then did not return my greeting. I went to the Commander of the Believers, Umar b. al-Khattab, and said, \"O Commander of the Believers, has something new happened in Islam?\" He said, \"Why do you say that?\" I said, \"Nothing, except that I passed by Uthman a short while ago in the mosque and greeted him, and he looked me up and down and then did not return my greeting.\" So Umar sent for Uthman and called him, and said, \"What prevented you from returning your brother's greeting?\" Uthman said, \"I did not do that.\" Sa'd said, \"I said, 'Yes, you did.'\" He said, \"Until he swore and I swore.\" Then Uthman remembered and said, \"Yes. I seek God's forgiveness and turn to Him. You passed by me a short while ago while I was reminding myself of a word I had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. By God, I never remembered it but my sight and heart were covered with a veil.\" Sa'd said, \"I will inform you of it: The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned to us the first supplication, then a Bedouin came and distracted him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and I followed him. When I feared he would reach his house before me, I struck the ground with my foot. The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to me and said, 'Who is this, Abu Ishaq?' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'What then?' I said, 'No, by God, except that you mentioned to us the first supplication, then this Bedouin came.' He said, 'Yes, the supplication of Dhu al-Nun: \"There is no god but You; glory be to You; I have been of the wrongdoers.\" No Muslim ever supplicates his Lord with it for anything but He answers him.'\""],[771,"Two prayers after which there is no prayer: the morning prayer until the sun rises, and the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."],[772,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other, except the Sacred Mosque."],[773,"Whoever wishes humiliation for Quraysh, God, Mighty and Majestic, will humiliate him."],[774,"I never heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say of any living person walking that he was among the people of Paradise except for Abdullah b. Salam."],[775,"He came to Sa'd b. Malik and said, \"It has reached me that you are exposed to the reviling of Ali in Kufa. Have you reviled him?\" He said, \"God forbid. By the One in whose hand is Sa'd's soul, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say about Ali something such that if a saw were placed on my head to make me revile him, I would never revile him.\""],[776,"I give to a man while another is dearer to me than him, fearing that he might fall on his face in the Fire."],[777,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited me while I was ill and said, \"Have you made a will?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"For how much?\" I said, \"For all my wealth in the path of God.\" He said, \"What have you left for your children?\" I said, \"They are wealthy with good.\" He said, \"Will a tenth.\" I kept reducing and he kept reducing until he said, \"Will a third, and a third is a lot.\""],[778,"I fear for you the trial of prosperity more than the trial of adversity. You were tested with the trial of adversity and were patient, and the world is green and sweet."],[779,"Sa'd fell ill in Makkah, and the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him. He said, \"O Messenger of God, I fear dying in this land as Sa'd b. Khawla died, so supplicate God to heal me.\" He said, \"O God, heal Sa'd,\" three times. He said, \"O Messenger of God, I have much wealth and no heir except distant kin. Should I bequeath half my wealth?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Should I bequeath a third of my wealth?\" He said, \"A third is a lot—or much. Your charity from your wealth is charity for you, and your wife's eating from your food is charity, and your spending on your family is charity. That you leave your family after you with a livelihood—or he said with sufficiency—is better than them begging.\""],[780,"Verses of the Qur'an were revealed concerning him. He said: The mother of Sa'd swore that she would never speak to him again until he disbelieved in his religion, and that she would not eat or drink. She said: You claim that Allah has enjoined upon you to honor your parents, and I am your mother, and I command you to do this. He said: She remained for three days until she fainted from exhaustion. Then a son of hers called 'Umara got up and gave her water, and she began to pray against Sa'd. Then Allah revealed this verse: 'And We have enjoined upon man goodness toward his parents. But if they endeavor to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them. To Me is your return, and I will inform you of what you used to do.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ obtained a great amount of booty, and in it was a sword. I took it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Give me this sword as a gift, for I am one whom you know. He said: 'Return it to where you took it from.' I went back with it, then I returned after that and spoke to him again, and he said: 'Return it to where you took it from.' I went away until, when I wanted to throw it into the pile of spoils, my soul reproached me, so I returned to him and said: Give it to me. He said: He raised his voice at me and said: 'Return it to where you took it from.' Then Allah revealed: 'They ask you about the spoils of war.' I sent for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he came to me. I said: Allow me to divide my wealth wherever I wish. He refused. I said: Then half. He refused. I said: Then a third. He remained silent. So a third was considered permissible. He said: I came upon a group of the Ansar and the Muhajirun, and they said: Come, we will feed you and give you wine to drink - and that was before wine was forbidden. I went to them in a hush - and hush means a garden - and there was a roasted camel's head with them, and a skin of wine. He said: I ate and drank with them. He said: Then I mentioned the Ansar and the Muhajirun and said: The Muhajirun are better than the Ansar. He said: A man took the jawbone of the head and struck me with it, wounding my nose. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. Then Allah revealed concerning me - meaning himself - the matter of wine: 'Intoxicants, gambling, idolatrous sacrifices, and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan.'"],[781,"The people of the West will continue to prevail upon the truth until the Hour is established."],[782,"He mentioned Dhu al-Thudayya and said: A devil of a hollow, whom a man from Bajila called al-Ashhab - or Ibn al-Ashhab - leads. A sign among an unjust people."],[783,"He stood up after two rak'ahs and they said subhan Allah to him. He said: He remained standing. He said: And he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness when he finished. Then he said: Do you think I should sit? I did only as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do."],[784,"No man has a morning drink of seven dates from between its two lava fields, but poison will not harm him that day."],[785,"Whoever has a morning meal of seven 'ajwa dates will not be harmed that day by poison or magic."],[786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rejected celibacy for 'Uthman b. Maz'un. Had he permitted it, we would have castrated ourselves."],[787,"There will be a trial in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one striving, and the one striving is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one galloping."],[788,"Allah is good and loves the good, clean and loves cleanliness, generous and loves generosity, munificent and loves munificence. So clean your houses, and do not imitate the Jews who gather refuse in their homes."],[789,"Allah is good and loves the good, clean and loves cleanliness, generous and loves generosity, munificent and loves munificence. So clean your courtyards and open spaces, and do not imitate the Jews who gather refuse in their homes."],[790,"Deliberateness in everything is better, except in the work of the Hereafter."],[791,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by while I was supplicating with two fingers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'One, one,' and he pointed with the index finger."],[792,"Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas stood up after two rak'ahs, so they glorified Allah to alert him, and he completed it, then said: \"Did you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\""],[793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ joined both his parents for me on the day of Uhud. Yahya said: I think he said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom.\" Sa'd was an excellent archer."],[794,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Teach me some words to say.\" He said: \"Say: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; Allah is most great, greatly; and much praise be to Allah; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; there is no power and no strength except with Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.\" The man said: \"This is for my Lord; what is for me?\" He said: \"Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me.\""],[795,"\"That one of you's belly be filled with pus until it ruins him is better for him than being filled with poetry.\""],[796,"I asked Sa'd about bad omens, and he scolded me and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no contagion and no bad omen. If there is a bad omen in anything, it is in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling."],[797,"\"The hand is cut off for the price of a shield.\""],[798,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"It is a punishment with which those before you were afflicted. If it breaks out in a land while you are in it, do not leave it, and if it is in a land, do not enter it.\""],[799,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give the greeting of peace to his right until his cheek appeared, and to his left until his cheek appeared.\""],[800,"\"Uthman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to remain celibate, and had he permitted him, we would have castrated ourselves.\""],[801,"The Prophet ﷺ came to visit him while he was in Makkah, and he disliked dying in the land from which he had emigrated. The Prophet ﷺ said: May Allah have mercy on Sa'd ibn 'Afra'. He had only one daughter, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, should I bequeath all my wealth? He said: \"No.\" He said: Then half? He said: \"No.\" He said: Then a third? He said: \"A third, and a third is much. That you leave your heirs wealthy is better than leaving them poor, begging from people. Whatever you spend, it is charity, even a morsel you raise to your wife's mouth. Perhaps Allah will grant you provision and some people will benefit through you, and others will be harmed through you.\""],[802,"\"O Allah, bless the people of Madinah in their city, bless them in their sa', bless them in their mudd. O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and friend, and I am Your servant and messenger. Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah, and I ask You for the people of Madinah the like of what Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah, and the like of it along with it. Madinah is meshed, with two angels guarding every opening; neither the plague nor the Dajjal will enter it. Whoever intends it with evil, Allah will melt him as salt melts in water.\""],[803,"He heard Sa'd ibn Malik and al-Dahhak ibn Qays during the year Mu'awiya performed Hajj, while they were mentioning tamattu' (combining 'umrah with Hajj). Al-Dahhak said: \"None does that except one ignorant of Allah's command.\" Sa'd said: \"What a bad thing you have said, O son of my brother.\" Al-Dahhak said: \"Umar forbade it.\" Sa'd said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it, and we did it with him.\""],[804,"I witnessed Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas. A group of people came to him concerning a slave of theirs whose spoils Sa'd had seized. He had seen him hunting in the sanctuary of Madinah, which the Messenger of God ﷺ had declared sacred, so he seized his spoils. They spoke to him about returning the spoils to them, but he refused and said, 'Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said when he set the boundaries of the sanctuary of Madinah: \"Whoever you find hunting within these boundaries, whoever seizes him, the spoils are his.\" So I shall not return to you a gift that the Messenger of God ﷺ has granted me. However, if you wish, I will pay you the value of his spoils.'"],[805,"\"The month is like this, and like this, and like this: ten and ten, and nine once.\""],[806,"\"When one of you spits while he is in the mosque, let him bury his spittle so that it does not touch the skin of a believer or his clothing and harm him.\""],[807,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say this statement to 'Ali: 'Are you not pleased, O 'Ali, that you are to me of the station of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?'"],[808,"'Umar sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he had women of Quraysh with him, speaking to him and asking him for more, their voices raised. When he sought permission, they rushed to the screen. The Messenger of God ﷺ gave him permission, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was laughing. 'Umar said, 'May God make you laugh, O Messenger of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I was amazed at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice, they rushed to the screen.' 'Umar said, 'You, O Messenger of God, were more deserving that they should be in awe.' Then 'Umar said, 'O enemies of your own selves, do you fear me and not fear the Messenger of God ﷺ?' They said, 'Yes, you are harsher and rougher than the Messenger of God ﷺ.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, Satan never meets you walking on a path except that he takes a path other than yours.'"],[809,"The owners of farms during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ used to lease their farms for the portion of crops that grew on the irrigation channels and what was watered by the water around the well. They came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and disputed about some of that, so the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade them from leasing for that, and said to them: 'Lease for gold and silver.'"],[810,"\"I prayed and placed my hands together, and my father forbade me and said: 'We were commanded to place our hands on the knees.'\""],[811,"He used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil, and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[812,"\"The best of you is the one who learns the Qur'an and teaches it.\" He said: And he took my hand and seated me in this seat of mine where I teach."],[813,"\"I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he found a date receptacle containing dates. He took one date and gave me one date.\""],[814,"\"For one of you to fill his belly with pus is better than to fill it with poetry.\""],[815,"\"For one of you to fill his belly with pus is better for him than to fill it with poetry.\""],[816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he took the road of al-Fur', would enter ihram when his mount stood up with him; and when he took the other road, he would enter ihram when he ascended Sharaf al-Bayda'."],[817,"Several people narrated it to us: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. 'Ar'arah and others. They said: Wahb b. Jarir narrated to us with his chain of transmission, the like of it. : : :"],[818,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at Baqi' al-Khayl when al-'Abbas approached. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most maintaining of ties.'"],[819,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would hand me the arrow on the day of Uhud and say: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[820,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about those who are heedless of their prayer. He said: 'They are those who delay the prayer beyond its time.'"],[821,"\"The month is thus, thus, and thus,\" then he decreased in the third by one finger."],[822,"\"When one of you spits in the mosque, let him bury it, so that it does not touch the skin of a believer or his garment and harm him.\""],[823,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being asked about fresh dates for dry dates. He said: 'Do fresh dates decrease when they dry?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then no.'"],[824,"And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening. He said: It was revealed concerning six: I was among them, and Ibn Mas'ud was among them. The polytheists had said to him: 'Do you admit these?'"],[825,"He heard al-Dahhak b. Qays, during the Hajj of Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan, saying: 'No one gives a ruling permitting tamattu' with 'umrah to Hajj except one who is ignorant of the command of Allah.' Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas said to him: 'What an evil thing you have said, O son of my brother! By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that, and we did it with him.'"],[826,"\"Whoever withholds surplus water, Allah will withhold His surplus from him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[827,"\"Is any of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day?\" A man among those sitting with him said: 'How can a thousand good deeds be written for him?' He said: 'He glorifies Allah with a thousand glorifications, so a thousand good deeds are written for him and a thousand sins are erased from him.'"],[828,"I said: O Messenger of God, which people face the severest trial? He said: \"The prophets, then the next best and the next best. A servant is tested according to his religion.\" He said: \"Trial does not cease to afflict the servant until he walks on the earth with no sin upon him.\""],[829,"\"Kill the little transgressor.\""],[830,"Wahb b. Baqiyya narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Amir b. Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[831,"He said to him on the day of Uhud while he was shooting: \"Go on, may my father and mother be your ransom.\""],[832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to visit me during the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage due to an illness that had become severe upon me. I said: O Messenger of God, the illness has reached me as you see, and I am a man of wealth, and none will inherit from me except a daughter of mine. Should I give two-thirds of my wealth as charity? He said: \"No.\" I said: Then half of it? He said: \"No.\" Then he said: \"A third, and a third is large—or much. Indeed, that you leave your heirs wealthy is better for you than leaving them needy, begging from people. And you will never spend any expenditure seeking thereby the face of God except that you will be rewarded for it, even what you place in your wife's mouth.\" He said: O Messenger of God, will I be left behind after my companions? He said: \"You will not be left behind and then do a righteous deed seeking thereby the face of God except that you will increase thereby in rank and elevation. And perhaps you will be left behind until some people benefit through you and others are harmed through you. O God, complete for my companions their emigration and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Sa'd b. Khawla.\""],[833,"\"Ten are in Paradise: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talha is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf is in Paradise, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas is in Paradise, Sa'id b. Zayd b. Amr is in Paradise, and Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah is in Paradise.\""],[834,"I said to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf: O uncle, tell me about your story on the day of Badr. He said: Recite after the hundred and twentieth verse of Al Imran and you will find our story: 'And [remember] when you, [O Muhammad], left your family in the morning to post the believers at their stations for the battle' up to His saying: 'When two parties among you were about to lose heart.' He said: They are the ones who sought protection from the polytheists. Up to His saying: 'And you had certainly wished for death before you met it, so you have seen it while you were looking on.' He said: That is the longing of the believers for the encounter. Up to His saying: 'When you were slaying them by His permission.'"],[835,"Umar b. al-Khattab went out to Syria until when he was at Sargh, the commanders of the armies met him: Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah and his companions. They informed him that the plague had occurred in Syria. Umar said: Summon for me the earliest Muhajirun. They were summoned for him, and he consulted them. Some of them said: You have gone out for a matter, and we do not think that you should return. Others said: With you are the remainder of the people and the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we do not think that you should advance them upon this plague. He said to them: Leave me. Then he said: Summon for me the Ansar. They were summoned for him, and he consulted them. They followed the path of the Muhajirun and differed as they differed. He said: Rise from me. Then he said: Summon for me whoever is here from the elders of Quraysh, from the Muhajirun of the conquest. They were summoned for him, and he consulted them. No two men differed upon him; they said: We think that you should return with the people and not advance them upon this plague. So Umar called out: I am departing in the morning upon a mount. They gathered before him, and Abu Ubayda said: Fleeing from the decree of God? He said: If someone other than you had said it, O Abu Ubayda. Yes, we flee from the decree of God to the decree of God. Do you see if you had camels and they descended into a valley with two sides, one fertile and the other barren—if you grazed the fertile one, you grazed it by the decree of God, and if you grazed the barren one, you grazed it by the decree of God? Then Abd al-Rahman came, having been absent on some errand of his, and he said: I have knowledge about this. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"If you hear of it in a land, do not go forward to it; and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it.\" Then Umar praised God and turned back."],[836,"Umar b. al-Khattab adjured a group, among them Abd al-Rahman b. Awf: I adjure you by God, by whose permission the heaven and the earth stand, do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity\"? They said: Yes."],[837,"I sat with Umar b. al-Khattab, and he said to me: O Ibn Abbas, have you heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ about what the Muslim man is commanded to do when he forgets in his prayer, how he should act? I said: No, by God. Or have you, O Commander of the Faithful, heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ about that? He said: No, by God. While we were in that state, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf came and said: What are you two discussing? Umar said to him: I asked him, and he informed him of what he had asked. Abd al-Rahman said to him: But I have heard the Messenger of God ﷺ command regarding that. Umar said to him: You are among us a just witness. What did you hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ? Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"If one of you forgets in his prayer until he does not know whether he added or subtracted, then if he doubts between one and two, let him make it one; and if he doubts between two and three, let him make it two; and if he doubts between three and four, let him make it three, so that the doubt is in the addition. Then he should prostrate twice while sitting before he gives the salutation, then give the salutation.\""],[838,"Abu al-Raddad fell ill, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf visited him. He said: The best and most dutiful of them is Abu Muhammad. Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God said: \"I am God, and I am the Merciful. It is the womb. I created the womb and derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him; and whoever severs it, I sever him.\" Or: \"I cut him off.\""],[839,"He entered upon Abd al-Rahman b. Awf to visit him, and Abd al-Rahman said to him: A womb has connected you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God said: \"I am the Merciful, and it is the womb. I derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him; and whoever severs it, I sever him.\" Or he said: \"He severs it, I cut him off.\""],[840,"I saw 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf circumambulating the House while he was chanting, wearing two leather socks. 'Umar said to him: \"I do not know which of the two is more astonishing: your chanting around the House, or your circumambulation in your two leather socks?\" He said: \"I did this during the time of one who is better than you: the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not find fault with me for that.\""],[841,"That 'Umar b. al-Khattab passed by 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf while he was circumambulating the House, chanting and wearing two leather socks. He said: \"By God, I do not know whether your circumambulation in your two leather socks is more astonishing, or your chanting around the House?\" He said: \"I did that during the time of one who is better than you: the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[842,"\"I witnessed as a boy, along with my paternal uncles, the pact of al-Mutayyabin, and I would not love to have red camels and then break it.\""],[843,"\"I witnessed as a boy, along with my paternal uncles, the pact of al-Mutayyabin, and I would not love to have red camels and then break it.\""],[844,"Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Isma'il b. Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I witnessed with my paternal uncles...\" and he mentioned something similar."],[845,"I was standing in the courtyard of the mosque, and I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ coming out of the door that is adjacent to the cemetery. I waited a little, then I went out following him, and I found that he had entered a garden belonging to al-Aswaf. The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs, and he prostrated with a prostration in which he prolonged the prostration. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the tashahhud, I hastened to him and said: May my father and mother be your ransom, you prostrated with a prostration whose length made me fear that God had taken your soul. He said: \"Gabriel gave me good news that whoever sends blessings upon me, God sends blessings upon him, and whoever greets me, God greets him.\""],[846,"That when 'Umar b. al-Khattab went out to Syria and heard about the plague, he turned back from that. 'Abd al-Rahman said to him: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"When you hear that it has broken out in a land, do not enter it, and when it breaks out while you are in a land, do not leave it fleeing from it.\""],[847,"Duplicate - Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us: Hisham b. 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Umar b. Abi Salamah, from his father, from the judge of the people of Palestine, from 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said... and he mentioned something similar."],[848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ placed a turban on me and let it hang down in front of me and behind me."],[849,"\"The adornment of the world will be lifted in the year one hundred and twenty-five.\""],[850,"That he witnessed that when 'Uthman b. 'Affan gave the Messenger of God ﷺ what he used to equip the army of hardship, and he brought seven hundred uqiyahs of gold."],[851,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf while he was leading the people in prayer, Abd al-Rahman wanted to move back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him: \"Stay in your place.\" So he prayed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed following the prayer of Abd al-Rahman."],[852,"I saw him prostrate in \"When the sky is split open\" ten times."],[853,"He and Umar were discussing prayer. He said: Abd al-Rahman b. Awf passed by us and said: Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I bear witness by the testimony of God that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When one of you prays and is uncertain about deficiency in his prayer, let him pray until he becomes uncertain about addition."],[854,"The scholar is preferred over the worshipper by seventy degrees, between each two degrees is like what is between the heaven and the earth."],[855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out to look for a man from the Ansar and called him. The Ansari came out of his house to the Messenger of God ﷺ with his head dripping water. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What is wrong with your head?\" He said: You called me while I was with my wife, and I feared I would be delayed for you, so I hurried and got up and poured water over myself, then came out. He said: Had you ejaculated? He said: No. He said: If you do that, do not wash; wash what of you touched the woman and perform your ablution for prayer, for water is from water."],[856,"Five or four of us from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ would not part from the Messenger of God ﷺ for what befell him of his needs by night and day. He said: I came to him and he had gone out, so I followed him. He entered a garden from the gardens of al-Aswaf and prayed, then prostrated and lengthened the prostration. I said: God has taken his soul. He said: He raised his head and called me, saying: What is the matter with you? I said: O Messenger of God, you lengthened the prostration; I said: God has taken the soul of His Messenger, and I will never see him again. He said: I prostrated in thanks to my Lord for what He has granted me concerning my community: whoever from my community sends one blessing upon me, ten good deeds are written for him and ten bad deeds are erased from him."],[857,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Makkah, he turned to al-Taif and besieged it for nineteen or eighteen days but did not conquer it. Then he set out in the evening or morning, then stopped, then announced: O people, I am a predecessor for you, and I enjoin you to treat my family well. Your appointment is the Basin. By the One in whose hand is my soul, they must establish prayer and give zakah, or I will send to them a man from me—or like myself—and he will strike the necks of their fighters and take their descendants captive. He said: The people thought it was Abu Bakr or Umar, but he took Ali by the hand and said: \"This is he.\""],[858,"I was a scribe for Jazʾ b. Muawiya, the uncle of al-Ahnaf. Umar's letter came to us a year before his death, saying: Kill every sorcerer, separate every Mahram among the Magians, and forbid them from zamzama. So we killed three sorceresses, and we began separating a man and his female relative in the Book of God. He made much food and invited the Magians, and laid the sword on his thigh, and they threw down a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver, and they ate without zamzama. Umar had not taken jizya from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman b. Awf informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ had taken it from the Magians of Hajar."],[859,"I heard Bajala telling Abu al-Shatha and Amr b. Aws, in the year Musab b. al-Zubayr performed Hajj, while he was beside the steps of Zamzam: I was a scribe for Jazʾ b. Muawiya, the uncle of al-Ahnaf. Umar came to him a year before his death: Kill every sorcerer, separate every Mahram among the Magians, and forbid them from zamzama. He said: So we killed three sorceresses, and we began separating a woman and her female relative in the Book of God. He made much food and invited the Magians, and laid the sword on his thigh, and they threw down a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver, and they ate without zamzama. He said: Umar had not taken jizya from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman b. Awf informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ had taken it from the Magians of Hajar."],[860,"Umar b. al-Khattab said: How should I deal with the Magians? He said: Abd al-Rahman b. Awf stood up and said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ when he was asked about them, and he said: Their way is the way of the People of the Book."],[861,"Whoever fasts Ramadan in faith and seeking reward, he will come out of his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him."],[862,"God has made the fasting of Ramadan obligatory, and I have instituted its standing in prayer."],[863,"Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned Ramadan, and said: \"Indeed, Ramadan is a month whose fasting God has made obligatory, and I have instituted for the Muslims its night prayer. Whoever fasts it and prays it, comes out of sin like the day his mother bore him.\""],[864,"I was standing on the day of Badr in the row. I looked to my right and left, and found myself between two young boys of the Ansar, whose teeth were newly grown. I wished I were between sturdier ones than them. One of them nudged me and said: \"O uncle, do you know Abu Jahl?\" I said: \"Yes, and what do you need with him, O son of my brother?\" He said: \"I have been told that he insults the Messenger of God ﷺ. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if I see him, my body will not part from his body until the sooner of us dies.\" He said: I was amazed at that. Then the other nudged me and said the like to me. It was not long before I saw Abu Jahl moving among the people. I said to them: \"Do you not see? This is your companion whom you were asking about.\" They rushed at him and struck him with their swords until they killed him. Then they went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him. He said: \"Which of you killed him?\" Each one of them said: \"I killed him.\" He said: \"Did you wipe your swords?\" They said: \"No.\" He looked at the two swords and said: \"Both of you killed him.\" He ruled his belongings as spoils to Mu'adh b. 'Amr b. al-Jamuh, and the name of the other was Mu'adh b. 'Afra'."],[865,"\"Quraysh, the Ansar, Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, Ghifar, Ashja', and Sulaym are my allies; they have no ally besides God and His Messenger.\""],[866,"\"Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you regarding the name of your prayer, for God said: 'And after the night prayer there are three times of privacy for you,' and the Bedouins call it al-'atamah. Indeed, al-'atamah is the milking of camels.\""],[867,"I entered the mosque and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ coming out of the mosque. I followed him, walking behind him while he did not notice me, until he entered a palm grove. He faced the qiblah and prostrated, lengthening the prostration while I was behind him, until I thought that God had taken his soul. I came walking until I reached him. I lowered my head to look at his face. He raised his head and said: \"What is the matter with you, O 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf?\" I said: \"When you lengthened the prostration, I thought that God had taken your soul, so I came to look.\" He said: \"When you saw me enter the palm grove, I met Gabriel, and he said: I bring you good news: God says, 'Whoever greets you, I greet him, and whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him.'\""],[868,"\"This matter will continue to stand with justice until a man from Banu Umayyah breaches it.\""],[869,"\"The affair of my nation will continue to stand with justice until the first to breach it is a man from Banu Umayyah called Yazid.\""],[870,"The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ spoke, he said: \"Expel the Jews of the Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula, and know that the worst of people are those who took the graves of their prophets as mosques.\""],[871,"Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah and Mu'adh b. Jabal were conversing privately with each other about a matter. I said to them: \"Have you not kept the injunction of the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning me?\" He said: And he had enjoined them concerning me. They said: \"We did not intend to converse privately about anything without you; we only mentioned a matter.\""],[872,"Muhammad b. al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj, al-Anmati, narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad narrated to us, from Layth, with his chain, and he mentioned something similar."],[873,"\"There was no prophet after Noah but he warned his people of the Dajjal, and I warn you of him.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ described him to us and said: \"Perhaps some of those who saw me or heard my words will live to see him.\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, how will our hearts be that day? Like they are today?\" He said: \"Or better.\""],[874,"A man from the Muslims granted protection to a man from the polytheists. Khalid b. al-Walid and 'Amr said: \"You shall not grant protection.\" Abu 'Ubaydah said: \"You shall grant him protection. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Protection granted by some of the Muslims is valid for all of them.'\""],[875,"A man granted protection to a people while he was with Khalid b. al-Walid, Abu 'Ubaydah, and 'Amr b. al-'As. Khalid and 'Amr said: We do not grant protection to the one who granted protection. Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Some of the Muslims grant protection on behalf of the others."],[876,"I entered upon Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah during his illness, and his wife Tuhayfah was sitting at his head, and he was facing the wall. I said: How did Abu 'Ubaydah spend the night? She said: He spent the night with reward. He said: By God, I did not spend the night with reward. He said: It was as if the people were upset, so he said: Will you not ask me about what I said? They said: We did not like what you said, so how could we ask you? He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever spends a surplus expenditure in the path of God, it is multiplied by seven hundred; and whoever spends on his family, or visits a sick person, or removes something harmful, the good deed is multiplied by ten; and fasting is a shield as long as one does not tear it; and whoever God tests with an affliction in his body, it is an expiation for him."],[877,"We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he ordered for us twelve young she-camels, and we were in the process of extracting them, but his death came, so the people prevented us from them until they gathered. He said: I said to Abu Juhaifah..."],[878,"They said: O Messenger of God, you have grown gray? He said: Hud and its sisters have made me grow gray."],[879,"Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me while awake; indeed, Satan cannot take my form."],[880,"Bounty was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ while he was in prayer. A man said: The bounty of so-and-so is in horses; another said: The bounty of so-and-so is in camels; another said: The bounty of so-and-so is in sheep; another said: The bounty of so-and-so is in slaves. He said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he raised his head from the last rak'ah and said: O God, our Lord, to You be praise, filling the heavens, and filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after that, until he reached: Nor does bounty avail the possessor of bounty against You. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ prolonged his voice on 'bounty' so that they would know that it is not as they say."],[881,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Describe him to me. He said: He was fair-skinned with some gray hair."],[882,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and he said to a man with him: I do not eat while reclining."],[883,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ; the person who resembled him most among the people was al-Hasan b. 'Ali."],[884,"Al-Hajjaj delayed the prayer on Friday. An old man said to him: By God, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying, and I never saw him do what you do. He said: When I heard him mention the Messenger of God ﷺ, I said: How did you see the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I saw him come out when the sun had declined, and the old man was Abu Juhaifah."],[885,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ in Makkah while he was at al-Abtah in a red leather tent of his. He said: Bilal came out with his ablution water, and some were getting it and some were sprinkling it. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out in a red garment, as if I am looking at the whiteness of his shins. He said: He performed ablution, and Bilal gave the call to prayer. He said: I started following this way and that, he says: right and left, saying: Come to prayer, come to success. Then a short spear was fixed for him, and he stood and prayed the afternoon prayer as two rak'ahs. Then a donkey and a dog would pass in front of him without being prevented. He said: Then he continued to pray two rak'ahs until he returned to Madinah."],[886,"I do not eat while reclining."],[887,"I do not eat reclining."],[888,"He bought a slave who was a cupper, and he ordered that his cupping instruments be broken. I said to him, \"Will you break them?\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a prostitute, and he cursed the woman who tattoos and the woman who gets tattooed, the one who consumes riba and the one who pays it, and he cursed the image-maker.\""],[889,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ perform wudu in the midday heat, and the people began taking from the leftover water of his wudu. Then he prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs and Asr as two rak'ahs, with a short spear in front of him."],[890,"A donkey and a woman would pass behind him."],[891,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed toward a short spear."],[892,"We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ in a group from Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah at al-Abtah. He said, \"Welcome; you are of me.\" When the prayer time arrived, Bilal went out and gave the call to prayer, placing his fingers in his ears and turning around during his call. When he gave the iqamah, the Prophet ﷺ planted a short spear and prayed toward it."],[893,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on the journey during which they slept until the sun rose. He said, \"You were dead, and God returned your souls to you. Whoever sleeps through a prayer should pray it when he wakes, and whoever forgets a prayer should pray it when he remembers.\""],[894,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of a dog, the price of blood, and the dowry of a prostitute."],[895,"A man slaughtered before the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed on the Day of Sacrifice. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"It is not sufficient for you.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of God, I have a jadha'ah.\" He said, \"It is sufficient for you, but it will not be sufficient for anyone after you.\""],[896,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda'. Salman came to visit Abu al-Darda' and saw Umm al-Darda' in disheveled clothing. He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" She said, \"Your brother has no need for this world.\" When Abu al-Darda' came, Salman welcomed him and brought him food. Salman said to him, \"Eat.\" He said, \"I am fasting.\" Then he said, \"I adjure you to eat, for I will not eat until you eat.\" So he ate with him and spent the night at his place. When night came, Abu al-Darda' got up, but Salman made him sit down. Then he said, \"O Abu al-Darda', your Lord has a right over you, your family has a right over you, and your body has a right over you. Give each possessor of a right his right: fast and break your fast, pray and sleep, and go to your family.\" When it was near dawn, he said, \"Now get up.\" They got up and prayed, then went out to the prayer. When the Prophet ﷺ had prayed, Abu al-Darda' went to him and told him what Salman had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him the same as Salman had said."],[897,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, and this part of him was white—meaning his lower lip. It was said to him, \"What were you like then?\" He said, \"I would cut arrows and feather them.\""],[898,"The Prophet ﷺ was at al-Ji'ranah distributing meat, and I was then a boy carrying the limb of a camel. A Bedouin woman approached, and when she drew near to the Prophet ﷺ, he spread his cloak for her, and she sat on it. I asked, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"His mother who nursed him.\""],[899,"The Prophet ﷺ walked briskly (ramal) from the Black Stone to the Black Stone."],[900,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, he sent Khalid b. al-Walid to Nakhlah, where al-Uzza was. It was upon three acacia trees, so Khalid b. al-Walid came to it, cut down the acacia trees, and demolished the house that was over it. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: 'Go back, for you have not done anything.' So Khalid returned. When the custodians, its keepers, saw him, they fled into the mountain, saying: 'O Uzza, confound him! O Uzza, blind him! Or else die in spite.' He said: Khalid came to it, and there was a naked woman with disheveled hair throwing dust on her head. He struck her with the sword until he killed her. Then he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: 'That was al-Uzza.'"],[901,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulating the House on his she-camel, touching the Black Stone with a hooked staff he had with him."],[902,"While I was drawing water that night, some black sheep and some light-colored sheep came to me. Abu Bakr came and drew one or two buckets, and there was weakness in them, and Allah forgives him. Then Umar came and it became a large bucket, and he filled the troughs and satisfied the thirsty. I did not see any genius among men better at drawing than him. I interpreted that the black sheep were the Arabs and the light-colored sheep were the non-Arabs."],[903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: 'It has reached me that Ibn Sufyan b. Nubayh al-Hudhali has gathered people against me to raid me, and he is at Nakhlah or Uranah. Go to him.' He said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me so I may recognize him.' He said: 'The sign between you and him is that when you see him, you will feel a shuddering.' He said: I went out with my sword slung over my shoulder until I came upon him among women in howdahs, seeking a place for them, at the time of Asr. When I saw him, I felt what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had described to me of shuddering. I approached him, but I feared that there might be an encounter between me and him that would distract me from prayer. So I prayed while walking toward him, gesturing with my head. When I reached him, he said: 'Who is the man?' I said: 'A man from the Arabs who heard of you and your gathering against this man, and he came for that.' He said: 'Yes, I am indeed in that.' He said: I walked with him a little until I could, then I attacked him with the sword and killed him. Then I left, leaving his women bowed over him. When I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he saw me and said: 'The face has succeeded.' He said: I said: 'I killed him, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.' He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood with me, took me into his house, and gave me a staff, saying: 'Keep this staff with you, O Abdullah b. Unays.' He said: I went out with it to the people. They said: 'What is this staff?' I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave it to me and ordered me to keep it.' They said: 'Will you not go back and ask him why?' He said: I went back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you give me this staff?' He said: 'It is a sign between me and you on the Day of Resurrection. The fewest people on that day will be those who carry staffs'—or: 'who lean on staffs.' So Abdullah tied it to his sword, and it remained with him until he died. Then he ordered that it be placed with him in his shroud, and they were buried together."],[904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on an expedition alone."],[905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, Abu Qatadah, an ally of theirs from the Ansar, and Abdullah b. Atik to Ibn Abi al-Huqayq to kill him. We went out and came to Khaybar at night. We tracked their doors and locked them from outside. Then we gathered the keys and threw them up. The people climbed into the palm trees, and I and Abdullah b. Atik entered the stairway of Abu al-Huqayq. Abdullah b. Atik spoke, and Ibn Abi al-Huqayq said: 'May your mother lose you, Abdullah, how did you get to this town? Get up and open, for a noble man does not turn away from his door at this hour.' She got up, and I said to Abdullah b. Atik: 'You take care of it.' He drew his sword upon them. His wife went to cry out, and I drew upon her, but I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he forbade killing women and children, so I held back. Abdullah b. Unays said: I entered upon him in an upper room of his. I stood looking at the intense whiteness of his body in the darkness of the room. When he saw me, he took a pillow and covered himself with it. I went to raise my sword to strike him but could not because of the shortness of the room. So I stabbed him, then I went out. My companion said: 'Did you do it?' I said: 'Yes.' He entered and stood over him. Then we went out and descended the stairway. Abdullah b. Atik fell on the stairs and said: 'Oh my leg, it is broken.' I said to him: 'Your leg is fine.' I put down my bow and carried him. Abdullah was short and slight. I brought him down, and his leg was fine. We went on until we caught up with our companions. The woman cried out: 'A night attack!' The people of Khaybar stirred. Then I remembered the place of my bow in the stairway, and I said: 'By Allah, I will go back and get my bow.' My companions said: 'The people of Khaybar have stirred; you will be killed.' I said: 'I will not go back until I get my bow.' So I went back, and the people of Khaybar had stirred, and they had nothing to say except: 'Who killed Ibn Abi al-Huqayq?' I made sure not to look at any person's face, nor anyone look at my face, except that I said as they said: 'Who killed Ibn Abi al-Huqayq?' Until I came to the stairway, climbed up with the people, took my bow, then caught up with my companions. We traveled by night and hid by day. When we hid by day, we appointed a watchman to look out for us. When we approached Madinah and were at al-Bayda, I was their watchman. Then I signaled to them with my garment, and they came down and went out at a fast pace. I came down after them and caught up with them until we reached Madinah. My companions said to me: 'Did you see anything?' I said: 'No, but I saw the exhaustion that had overtaken you, and I wanted the alarm to carry you.' Then we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was addressing the people. He said ﷺ: 'The faces have succeeded.' We said: 'May your face succeed, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Did you kill him?' We said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the sword with which he was killed and said: 'This is his food in the edge of the sword.'"],[906,"I prayed in the mosque of Banu Ghifar. When I sat down, I started supplicating and pointing with one finger. Khufaf b. Ayma' al-Ghifari entered upon me while I was doing that, and he said: 'What do you intend by pointing with one finger?' He said: I said: 'I am supplicating to Allah and asking Him.' He said: 'How well you have done. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that.' The polytheists said: 'He only uses it for magic.' The polytheists have lied. Indeed, that is sincerity."],[907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed, then raised his head and said: 'Ghifar, may Allah forgive it; Aslam, may Allah keep it safe; and Usayyah have disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. O Allah, curse Banu Lihyan, and curse Ri'l and Dhakwan.' Then he fell into prostration."],[908,"I witnessed Uhud with my master. I struck a man from the polytheists, and when I killed him, I said: 'Take it from me, and I am the Persian man.' This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Why did he not say: Take it from me, and I am the Ansari man? For the freed slave of a people is from themselves.'"],[909,"O Yazid b. Asad, love for people what you love for yourself."],[910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Qays b. Malik al-Arhabi: 'In Your name, O Allah. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Qays b. Malik. Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, His blessings, and His forgiveness. To proceed: I have appointed you over your people—their Arabs and their non-Arabs, their clients and their retinue—and I have granted you from the corn of Yasar two hundred saa's, and from the raisins of Khaywan two hundred saa's, effective for you and your descendants after you, forever and ever.' Qays said: 'And the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"forever and ever,\" is more beloved to me. I hope that my descendants will remain forever.'"],[911,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting among his companions, he said: “May God bless the people of that graveyard,” three times. He said: We did not know which graveyard, and he did not name anything for them. He said: Then some of the companions of the Messenger of God went in to one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Attaf said: I was told that it was 'A'ishah, and he said to her: “The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the people of a graveyard and blessed them, but he did not tell us which graveyard it is.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ went in to her and she asked him about it, and he said to her: “The people of a graveyard in 'Asqalan.”"],[912,"The prayer was called, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by a man praying two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer. He spoke to him something we do not know what it was. When we finished, we surrounded him asking him: “What did the Prophet ﷺ say?” He said: “He said to me: 'One of you is about to pray the dawn prayer as four.'”"],[913,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out for the dawn prayer while a man was praying, and the Messenger of God ﷺ struck his shoulder and said: “Do you want to pray four? Or: twice?”"],[914,"“The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.”"],[915,"Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[916,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and I said to him: “On the condition that if I leave my religion and enter your religion, God will not punish me in the Hereafter?” He said: “Yes.”"],[917,"“The lost property of a Muslim is the fire of hell.”"],[918,"“Your brothers—be good to them,” or he said: “be upright to them—seek their help in what overcomes you, and help them in what overcomes them.”"],[919,"“Whoever fasts a day seeking the Face of God, God will distance him from Hell as far as a crow flies while it is a fledgling until it dies of old age.”"],[920,"“We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, four persons, and we had a horse with us. He gave each person among us one share, and he gave the horse two shares.”"],[921,"He went out to visit one of his brothers, and he had not reached him until news came to him that he was ill. When he entered upon him, he said: “I came to you as a visitor, or I came to you as one visiting the sick, or as one bringing good news.” He said: “How did you combine all this?” He said: “I went out intending to visit you, and I did not reach you until your illness reached me, so it became a sick visit, and I bring you good news of something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'When a station from God for a servant is preceded but he has not reached it by his deeds, He tries him in his body, or in his wealth, or in his child, then He gives him patience until he attains the station that was preceded for him from God, Mighty and Majestic.'”"],[922,"“After me there will be trials, in which the one sleeping is better than the one awake, and the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking. Whoever comes upon it, let him take his sword, then walk to a rock and strike it until it breaks, then lie down for it until it clears as it clears.”"],[923,"Whoever receives a kindness from his brother without asking for it or coveting it, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is only a provision that Allah has brought to him."],[924,"Whoever takes in an orphan among Muslims, sharing his food and drink until he becomes self-sufficient, Paradise is definitely guaranteed for him. And whoever finds his parents or one of them alive, then does not treat them kindly, and then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him. And any Muslim who frees a Muslim slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire."],[925,"When Allah wants to take a servant's soul in a certain land, He creates a need for him there."],[926,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his she-camel touching the Black Stone with his staff."],[927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and we went out with him. He passed by a man from Banu 'Adi who had uncovered his thigh, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Cover your thigh, O Ma'mar, for the thigh is part of the 'awrah.'"],[928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sheep, giving one ewe for every ten of his companions."],[929,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and camped in a land with many lizards. We caught some, and the cooking pots were boiling with them. The Prophet ﷺ asked: 'What is this?' We said: 'Lizards we caught.' He said: 'A nation from the Children of Israel was transformed, and I fear these may be they.' So he ordered us, and we overturned the pots even though we were hungry."],[930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us holding something like a leather shield. He put it down, then urinated toward it. Some of the people said: 'Look at him urinating as a woman does.' The Prophet ﷺ heard that and said: 'Woe to you! Do you not know what happened to the companion of the Children of Israel? They used to cut off whatever urine touched with scissors, and he forbade them, but he was punished in his grave.'"],[931,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a grain seller selling his grain. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O grain seller, is the bottom of the grain like the top?' He said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever cheats the Muslims is not one of them.'"],[932,"A fire is about to emerge from Habas, moving at the pace of slow camels. It travels by day and lies hidden by night. It goes forth in the morning and returns in the evening. It will be said: 'The fire has set out, O people, so set out.' The fire will say: 'O people, take a midday rest.' And it will be said: 'The fire has returned, O people, so return.' Whomever it catches, it consumes."],[933,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ on a festival day standing in the market, watching the people as they passed by."],[934,"I am riding tomorrow to the Jews, so do not initiate greeting them with salam. And if they greet you, then say: 'And upon you.'"],[935,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to al-Baqi', and he saw a fresh grave and said, \"What is this grave?\" They said, \"So-and-so, the freedwoman of so-and-so, died at noon while you were taking a midday nap, and we disliked waking you.\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and lined us up behind him, and he said the takbir over her four times. Then he said, 'No one should die while I am among you without informing me.'\" He said, \"And I think he said, 'For my prayer over him is a mercy.'\""],[936,"He forbade mut'ah marriage."],[937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Enjoy these women.\" He said, \"And enjoyment among us means marriage.\" He said, \"So we presented that to the women, but they refused unless they set a term between us and them. We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Do it.' So I and a cousin of mine went out, each of us with a cloak. He said, 'We passed by a woman, and she was pleased with my youth and my cousin's cloak, and she said, \"A cloak like a cloak.\" So I married her and spent that night with her. Then in the morning I went and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between the door and the corner, saying, \"I had permitted mut'ah for you, so whoever has any of these women should separate from her, for Allah has forbidden it until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[938,"He forbade praying in the resting places of camels and allowed praying in the sheepfolds."],[939,"\"An arrow is sufficient as a screen for a man in prayer, and when one of you prays, let him use a screen, even if only with an arrow.\""],[940,"\"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah until his tongue expresses it; then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian.\""],[941,"\"Whoever considers lawful with a dirham in marriage, he has indeed considered lawful.\""],[942,"Malik b. 'Abd Allah al-Khath'ami passed by while he was in command of the people on a summer expedition in the land of the Romans, and a man was leading his mount. He said to him, \"Ride, for I see your mount is strong-backed.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The feet of a servant do not become dusty in the path of Allah except that Allah forbids the Fire to them.'\" He said, \"So Malik dismounted and the people dismounted and walked, and no day was seen with more people walking than that.\""],[943,"Usayd b. Hudayr invited me, and I cauterized his sciatic nerve, and he narrated two hadiths to me. He said, \"Two households of my people came to me: a household from Banu Zafar and a household from Banu Mu'awiya, and they said, 'Speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he apportion for us—or give us—or something like that.' So I spoke to him, and he said, 'Yes, I will apportion for each household among them a share, and if Allah restores to us, we will restore to them.'\" He said, \"I said, 'May Allah reward you well, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'And you too, may Allah reward you well, for you are—as far as I know—chaste and patient.'\""],[944,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have exhausted my mount.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever reaches Jam' and stands with the imam until he departs, he has caught the Hajj, and whoever does not reach Jam', there is no Hajj for him.\""],[945,"When Marwan fought al-Dahhak b. Qays, he sent to Ayman b. Khuraym al-Asadi and said, \"We would like you to fight with us.\" He said, \"My father and my uncle witnessed Badr and instructed me not to fight anyone who testifies that there is no god but Allah. If you bring me a clearance from the Fire, I will fight with you.\" He said, \"Go,\" and he reviled and insulted him. So Ayman began to recite: \"I am not one to fight a man who prays, on behalf of another authority from Quraysh; his is his authority, and upon me is my sin. God forbid ignorance and recklessness! Should I fight a Muslim for nothing? It will not benefit me as long as I live.\""],[946,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned a tribulation and magnified it. He said, \"So we said, or they said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if we live to see this, we will surely be destroyed?'\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No, for killing will be enough for you.'\" Sa'id said, \"I saw my brothers killed afterwards.\""],[947,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr, and whoever wrongfully seizes anything of the earth will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[948,"Arwa bt. Aws came to us in a group of Quraysh, among them 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl, and said: I would like you to go to Sa'id b. Zayd and speak with him and remind him, for he has taken away from my land into his land. So we went to Sa'id until we came to him on his land at al-'Aqiq. He came out to us and said: I know what brings you. Arwa bt. Aws came to you and said that I am taking from her land into my land what is not mine. I will tell you what I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever takes from the earth what is not his will be made to wear it as a collar down to the seventh earth."],[949,"Arwa disputed with him concerning a piece of land, so he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever takes a handspan of land without his right will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths on the Day of Resurrection. Then he said: O God, if she is lying, then blind her sight and make her grave in her own house. He said: I saw her blind, feeling for the walls, saying: The supplication of Sa'id b. Zayd has struck me. Then while she was walking in the house, she fell into a well in the house and fell into it, and it became her grave."],[950,"Whoever wrongfully seizes a handspan of land without his right, he will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[951,"Whoever wrongfully seizes a handspan of land will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths, and whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[952,"Whoever takes a handspan of land without his right will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths on the Day of Resurrection."],[953,"Go and reconcile between these two: Sa'id and Arwa. So we came to Sa'id b. Zayd and he said: Do you think I have taken anything from her right? I testify that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever takes a handspan of land without his right will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths, and whoever allies himself with a people without their permission, upon him is the curse of God, and whoever cuts off the property of his brother with his oath, may God not bless it for him."],[954,"Whoever wrongfully seizes anything of the earth will be made to wear it as a collar from seven earths."],[955,"Whoever revives dead land, it is his, and there is no right for a wrongful root."],[956,"I asked Sa'd b. Ibrahim about the Banu Najiya and he said: They are from us. Sa'd said: They narrate from Sa'id b. Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: They are a tribe from me. Shu'ba said: And I think he said: And I am from them."],[957,"Whoever seizes a handspan of land wrongfully, God will make him wear it as a collar on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."],[958,"The Prophet ﷺ took the hand of al-Hasan b. 'Ali and said: 'O God, I love him, so love him.'"],[959,"\"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.\""],[960,"That Arwa bt. Aws claimed against Sa'id b. Zayd that he had taken something from her land, and she brought a dispute against him to Marwan b. al-Hakam. Sa'id said: Would I take anything from her land after what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: And what did you hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever takes a span of land will be made to wear it as a collar down to seven earths. Marwan said to him: I will not ask you for proof after this. He said: O God, if she is lying, blind her sight and kill her in her land. He said: She did not die until her sight went, and while she was walking in her land she fell into a pit and died."],[961,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus.\""],[962,"\"O assembly of Arabs, praise your Lord who has lifted the tithes from you.\""],[963,"\"Truffles are from the manna that was sent down upon the Children of Israel, and their water is a cure for the eye.\""],[964,"We were with al-Mughira b. Shu'ba while he was in the mosque and with him were the people of Kufa. Sa'id b. Zayd came, and al-Mughira made room for him, and said: Here, sit. So he seated him with him on the bed. Sa'id b. Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Lying about me is not like lying about anyone else. Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[965,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about truffles, and he said: They are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."],[966,"\"Truffles are from the manna that was sent down upon the Children of Israel, and their water is a cure for the eye.\""],[967,"I bear witness for the nine that they are in Paradise, and if I were to bear witness for the tenth, I would not be sinning. He said: It was said: How is that? He said: We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on Hira, and he said: Be still, Hira, for there is upon you only a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. He said: It was said: Who are they? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Ali, and Uthman, and Talha, and al-Zubayr, and Sa'd, and Ibn Awf. He said: It was said: Who is the tenth? He said: I am. Meaning himself."],[968,"We hid with the Messenger of God ﷺ on top of Hira, and when we settled, it shook with us. The Messenger of God ﷺ struck it with his palm, then said: Be still, Hira, for there is upon you only a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. And upon it were the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman, and Ali, and Talha, and al-Zubayr, and Sa'd, and Abd al-Rahman, and Sa'id b. Zayd."],[969,"Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba addressed us and disparaged Ali. Sa'id b. Zayd stood up and said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The Prophet is in Paradise, and Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Talha is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf is in Paradise, and Sa'd is in Paradise, and if I wished, I would name the tenth.\""],[970,"\"I have not left after me among the people a trial more harmful to men than women.\""],[971,"I and Umar b. al-Khattab asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Zayd b. Amr, and he said: He will come on the Day of Resurrection as a nation by himself."],[972,"A time will come upon the people when groups of people will go on military expeditions, and it will be said to them: Is there anyone among you who saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They will say: Yes, so victory will be granted to them. Then groups of people will go on military expeditions, and it will be said: Is there anyone among you who saw someone who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They will say: Yes, so victory will be granted to them. Then groups of people will go on military expeditions, and it will be said to them: Is there anyone among you who saw someone who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They will say: Yes, so victory will be granted to them."],[973,"The Prophet ﷺ saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it with a pebble, then he forbade a man from spitting in front of him or to his right, and said: He should spit to his left or under his left foot."],[974,"He forbade two types of transactions and two ways of wearing garments: the two ways of wearing garments are al-shamma' wrapping, and a man wrapping himself in a single garment with nothing of it covering his private part, and he forbade mulamasah and munabadhah."],[975,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and after asr until the sun sets."],[976,"Bathing on Friday is obligatory for every adult male."],[977,"There is no zakat on less than five awaq, and there is no zakat on less than five awsuq, and there is no zakat on less than five camels."],[978,"I asked Abu Sa'id: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the lower garment? He said: Yes. I said."],[979,"When one of you asks permission three times and is not given permission, let him return."],[980,"My son, when you are in the wilderness, raise your voice with the call to prayer, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Its voice is not heard by any jinn, human, stone, or tree except that it testifies for him."],[981,"It is near that the best wealth of a man will be sheep that he follows through mountain peaks and places where rain falls, fleeing with his religion from trials."],[982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Hudaybiyah: Let no fire be lit at night. Then afterwards he said: Light fires and make preparations, for no one after you will attain your mudd or your sa'."],[983,"A man from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf and a man from Banu Khudrah disputed about the mosque founded upon piety. Al-Khudri said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Al-'Umari said: It is the mosque of Quba'. He said: They went out until they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about that. He said: It is this mosque, the mosque of the Messenger of God, and in that there is much good."],[984,"When a fly falls into the food of one of you, immerse it fully, for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other a cure."],[985,"The Hour will not come until the earth is filled with wrongdoing and aggression. Then a man from my household—or he said: from my descendants—will come forth and fill it with equity and justice as it was filled with wrongdoing and aggression."],[986,"He forbade drinking while standing, or something like that."],[987,"He forbade drinking while standing."],[988,"Whoever has little wealth, many dependents, performs his prayer well, and does not backbite the Muslims, will come on the Day of Resurrection with me like these two."],[989,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was more modest than a virgin in her chamber. And he said: The Hour will not come until the House is no longer performed pilgrimage to."],[990,"We asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the fetus of a camel and a cow. He said: If you wish, eat it, for its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother."],[991,"He liked clusters of dates, holding them in his hand. One day he entered the mosque with one in his hand and saw sputum in the direction of the qiblah of the mosque. He scraped them off with it until he cleaned them. Then he turned to the people angry and said: Would any of you like a man to face him and spit in his face? When one of you stands for prayer, he is facing his Lord, and the angel is on his right, so let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but to his left or under his left foot. If he is overtaken by sudden spittle, let him spit like this."],[992,"A man entered the mosque on Friday while the Messenger of God ﷺ was on the pulpit. He called him and ordered him to pray two rak'ahs. Then he entered the mosque a second time while the Messenger of God ﷺ was on the pulpit. He called him and ordered him to pray two rak'ahs. Then he said: Give charity. They gave charity, and he gave him two garments from what they gave. Then he said: Give charity. He threw one of his two garments, and the Messenger of God ﷺ disliked what he did and said: Look at this man. He entered the mosque in shabby appearance, and I hoped you would notice him and give him charity or clothe him, but you did not. I said: Give charity, and they gave him two garments. Then I said: Give charity, and he threw one of his two garments. Take your garment. And he rebuked him."],[993,"A man among the Muslims said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of these illnesses that afflict us? What do we get from them? He said: They are expiations. He said: O Messenger of God, even if they are small? He said: Even a thorn and what is above it. He said: Then he supplicated against himself that fever would not leave him until he died, and that it would not distract him from Hajj, 'Umrah, jihad in the path of God, or the prescribed prayer in congregation. No person touched his body except that he found its heat until he died."],[994,"He forbade the inverting of water-skins."],[995,"He prohibited the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, then he gave permission for us to eat and store it. He said: Qatada b. al-Nu'man, the brother of Abu Sa'id, arrived, and they served him some of the dried sacrificial meat. He said: 'Is this from the dried meat of the sacrifice?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Did not the Messenger of God ﷺ prohibit it?' Abu Sa'id said: 'Indeed, but a matter occurred concerning it. He had prohibited us from keeping it beyond three days, and he gave us permission to eat and store it.'"],[996,"The Messenger of God ﷺ declared sacred what lies between the two lava fields of Madinah: that its trees not be cut or beaten for leaves."],[997,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed mixed food of dates, and we bartered among ourselves with an increase, so the Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited us from selling it except measure for measure."],[998,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, advise me.' He said: 'You must have taqwa of God, for it is the sum of all good. You must engage in jihad, for it is the monasticism of the Muslims. You must remember God and recite His Book, for it is a light for you on earth and a remembrance for you in heaven. And guard your tongue except from good, for by that you will overcome Satan.'"],[999,"A servant entered Paradise who had never done any good. When death came to him, he said to his family: 'When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter half of me in the sea and half of me on land.' Then God commanded the sea and the land, and they gathered him. He said: 'What made you do what you did?' He said: 'Fear of You,' and He forgave him for that."],[1000,"And the man was a grave robber, and He forgave him for his fear."],[1001,"The highest of people in rank on the Day of Resurrection is the just ruler, and the lowest of people in rank on the Day of Resurrection is the ruler who is not just."],[1002,"Three whom God laughs to on the Day of Resurrection: a man when he rises from the night to pray, a group when they line up for prayer, and a group when they line up to fight the enemy."],[1003,"God says: 'Fasting is for Me, and I reward for it.' The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast he rejoices, and when he meets God he rejoices. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the breath of a fasting person is more fragrant to God than the smell of musk."],[1004,"We said: 'O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord?' He said: 'Do you harm one another in seeing the sun at midday without clouds?' We said: 'No.' He said: 'Do you harm one another in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon without clouds?' We said: 'No.' He said: 'Then you will not harm one another in seeing Him, just as you do not harm one another in seeing them.'"],[1005,"No man who believes in God and the Last Day hates the Ansar."],[1006,"The killers of the renegades are the more beloved of the two factions to God and the nearer of the two factions to God."],[1007,"Marwan brought out the minbar and began with the sermon before the prayer. A man stood up and said: O Marwan, you have opposed the Sunnah: you brought out the minbar when it used not to be brought out, and you began with the sermon before the prayer. Abu Sa'id said: Who is this? They said: So-and-so. He said: As for this one, he has fulfilled what was upon him. Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever sees a wrong, let him change it with his hand; if he cannot, then with his tongue; if he cannot, then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith."],[1008,"\"I have made inviolable what is between the two lava fields of Madinah, just as Ibrahim made Makkah inviolable.\" He said: Then Abu Sa'id would find one of us with a bird in his hand that he had caught, and he would loosen it from his hand and set it free."],[1009,"\"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees. And if he prays it in a desolate land, and completes its ablution, bowing, and prostration, his prayer reaches fifty degrees.\""],[1010,"\"A woman is married for one of three qualities: for her wealth, for her beauty, or for her religion. Choose the one of religion and character, may your right hand be dusty.\""],[1011,"\"Among my nation are those who will intercede for a man and his household, and they will enter Paradise through his intercession.\""],[1012,"\"Every prophet was given a gift and hastened to use it, but I have saved my gift as intercession for my nation.\""],[1013,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a sheep whose tail a wolf had cut off: may it be offered as a sacrifice? He said: Yes, sacrifice it."],[1014,"\"Gold for gold, silver for silver, like for like, hand to hand, weight for weight. Whoever adds or asks for more has engaged in riba.\""],[1015,"\"Say: He is Allah, the One (Qur'an 112) is equal to a third of the Qur'an.\""],[1016,"\"Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an?\" He said: That was difficult for them, and they said: Who can do that? He said: He recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One,' and it equals a third of the Qur'an."],[1017,"\"There is no Muslim who supplicates to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, with a supplication that contains no sin or severing of kinship, but Allah grants him one of three things: either He hastens his supplication, or He stores it for him in the Hereafter, or He averts from him evil equivalent to it.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, then we will increase. He said: \"Allah is more.\""],[1018,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade building over graves, sitting on them, and praying over them.\""],[1019,"\"I am about to be called and to answer. I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah, a rope extended between heaven and earth, and my progeny, my household. Indeed, the Kind and Aware.\""],[1020,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn while he was distributing a share among the people. A man from Banu Umayyah stood up and said to him: \"Act justly, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Then I would have failed and lost if I were not just. Who will act justly? Woe to you!\" Umar b. al-Khattab asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to kill him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am not one who kills my companions. People will emerge saying the like of his saying; they recite the Quran but it does not pass their collarbones. They exit the religion as the arrow exits the target.\" He took an arrow and looked at its binding but saw nothing on it; then he looked at its head—meaning the shaft—but saw nothing on it; then he looked at its feathers but saw nothing on it. It outran the dung and blood. Their mark is a man whose hand is like a woman's breast, like a piece of flesh quivering, on which there are hairs like the forelock of a beast of prey.\" Abu Sa'id said: \"I was present at this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and I was present with Ali on the day he killed them at Nahrawan.\" He said: \"Ali searched for him but did not find him.\" He said: \"Then he found him later under a wall with this description.\" Ali said: \"Which of you knows this man?\" A man from the people said: \"We know him. This is Hurqus, and his mother is here.\" He said: \"Ali sent for his mother and said to her: 'Who is this?' She said: 'I do not know, O Commander of the Faithful, except that I used to graze sheep of mine in the Jahiliyyah at al-Rabadhah, and something like a shade covered me, and I conceived from it and gave birth to this.'\""],[1021,"A young man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication by which I may attain good.\" He said to him: \"Come closer.\" He came closer until his knee almost touched the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he said: \"Say: O Allah, pardon me, for You are Pardoning, You love pardon, and You are Pardoning, Generous.\""],[1022,"He forbade the stud fee of a horse and the miller's measure."],[1023,"\"Indeed, my intimate ones to whom I resort are my household, and my close supporters are the Ansar. So overlook their wrongdoers and accept from their doers of good.\""],[1024,"\"Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.\""],[1025,"\"I am leaving among you the two weighty things, one of which is greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended between heaven and earth, and my progeny, my household. They will never separate until they return to me at the Pond.\""],[1026,"\"I have a Pond whose length is from the Ka'bah to the Sacred House, whiter than milk, its vessels as numerous as the stars. I will have the most followers of the prophets on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1027,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the mosque founded on piety. He took a handful of pebbles and threw them on the ground, then said: \"This.\""],[1028,"\"This House will surely be pilgrimaged to, and umrah will be performed after the emergence of Gog and Magog.\""],[1029,"\"Indeed, a servant for whom I have made his body healthy and expanded his livelihood, yet five years pass without him coming to Me, is deprived.\""],[1030,"\"A child is the fruit of the heart, and indeed he is a cause of cowardice, stinginess, and grief.\""],[1031,"A man killed ninety-nine people. He came asking: Is there any repentance for him? He came to a monk and asked him, and he said, “You have no repentance.” So he killed the monk. Then he began asking. Then he set out from a village to a village in which there were righteous people. He said: When he was on part of the way, death overtook him, so he pushed himself away with his chest, then he died. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment gathered. He was closer to the righteous village by a span, so he was made from its people."],[1032,"There is no zakat on less than five uqiyas, nor on less than five camels, nor on less than five wasqs. A wasq is sixty sa's."],[1033,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after sixteen days of Ramadan had passed. Some of us fasted and some of us broke the fast, but the one fasting did not criticize the one breaking the fast, nor did the one breaking the fast criticize the one fasting."],[1034,"There will be two factions of my ummah from which an extremist group will emerge; the one closer to the truth of the two will carry out their killing."],[1035,"The wife of Safwan b. al-Mu'attal came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “Safwan beats me when I recite, and he forbids me to fast, and he does not pray until the sun rises.” Safwan stood up and said: “As for her statement, 'he beats me,' she recites my surahs. As for her statement, 'he forbids me to fast,' I am a young man. As for her statement, 'he does not pray until the sun rises,' we are a household known for that; we do not wake up until the sun rises.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Do not fast except with his permission, and do not recite his surahs.” And to you, O Safwan, “When you wake up, then pray.”"],[1036,"No one has been given anything better than patience."],[1037,"The nocturnal emission, vomiting, and cupping do not break the fast of the fasting person."],[1038,"People will come to Ibrahim and say to him: “Intercede for us with your Lord.” He will say: “I lied three lies.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is none of them except that he defended the religion of Allah with it: his saying, 'Then he cast a glance at the stars and said, \"Indeed, I am ill\"'; his saying, 'Rather, this, the largest of them, did it'; and his saying to Sarah, 'She is my sister.'\""],[1039,"Someone who had drunk was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “What did you drink?” He said: “I did not drink wine; it is only raisins and dates that I put in my gourd.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mixing raisins and dates."],[1040,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: “It is not lawful for anyone to be in a state of major ritual impurity in this mosque except you and me.”"],[1041,"Whoever's fasting coincides with Friday, and he visits a sick person, attends a funeral, gives charity, and frees a slave, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[1042,"Five things: whoever does them in a day, Allah will record him as one of the people of Paradise: whoever fasts on Friday, goes to the Friday prayer, attends a funeral, and frees a slave."],[1043,"He entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was feverish, with a velvet cloak over him. He placed his hand on him and found its heat above the velvet cloak. Abu Sa'id said: How severe is the heat of your fever, O Messenger of God! The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Thus indeed is affliction intensified for us, and our reward is multiplied. We said: O Messenger of God, who among people is most severely tried? He said: \"The prophets and then the righteous. One of them would be tried with poverty until he found nothing but a cloak, which he would gather up and wear; and he would be tried with lice until they killed him. One of them would be more joyful at affliction than you are at a gift.\""],[1044,"\"On the Day of Resurrection the Lord will say: Today the people of the gathering will know who are the people of nobility. It was said: Who are the people of nobility, O Messenger of God? He said: The gatherings of remembrance in the mosques.\""],[1045,"\"There was a man among those before you who had never stored up any good with God at all—Qatadah explained it: he had never saved any good with God at all. At the time of death he said to his sons: O my sons, what kind of father was I to you? They said: The best father. He said: When I die, burn me—or he said: crush me, or he said: dismember me—then on a day of strong wind scatter me. He died and that was done to him. God said: Be, and he was as quick as the blink of an eye. God said: O My servant, what made you do what you did? He said: Fear of You, O Lord. He said: So the first thing that reached him was that He forgave him.\""],[1047,"\"A man will take his father by the hand on the Day of Resurrection and will cut him off with fire, wanting to bring him into Paradise. It will be called out: Paradise is not entered by a polytheist; God has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist. He will say: O Lord, my father. Then he will be changed into an ugly form and a foul smell, and he will leave him. The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ thought that it was Abraham, and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not tell them more than that.\""],[1048,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about coitus interruptus. He said: Do you do that? You are not at fault if you do not do it. There is no soul that God has decreed will exist but that it will come to be. He said: Umar and Ibn Umar disliked coitus interruptus, while Zayd and Ibn Mas'ud practiced it."],[1049,"\"When a believer desires a child in Paradise, its age, its position, and its youth will be as he desires, or something like that.\""],[1050,"We were at the house of the Prophet ﷺ among a group of the Muhajirun and Ansar. He came out to us and said: \"Shall I tell you about the best of you?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"The best of you are those who fulfill their promises and are good and pure. God loves the hidden, pious one.\" He said: Then Ali b. Abi Talib passed by, and he said: \"Truth is with this one, truth is with this one.\""],[1051,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was on the pulpit saying: A little that suffices is better than much that distracts."],[1052,"\"When three go out on a journey, let one of them lead the prayer.\""],[1053,"\"God is beautiful and loves beauty; He loves to see His blessing upon His servant.\""],[1054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a sermon and said: God is allowing—meaning with regard to wine—so whoever has any of it, let him sell it and benefit from it. Only a short while later the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God has forbidden wine, so whoever this verse reaches, let him neither sell nor drink.\" He said: The people then took what they had of it and poured it out in the streets of Madinah."],[1055,"The Prophet of God ﷺ prayed with his companions. A man came, and the Prophet of God ﷺ said: Who will do business with this man and pray with him? He said: A man prayed with him."],[1056,"Whoever fasts Ramadan, and knows its limits and guards what he should guard of it, it expiates what preceded it."],[1057,"Whoever shows off, Allah will show off concerning him, and whoever seeks to be heard, Allah will make his name heard."],[1058,"There is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it."],[1059,"Winter is the believer's spring."],[1060,"Gatherings are of three kinds: sound, profitable, and blameworthy."],[1061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: O people, I had been shown the Night of Qadr, but it was taken away from me, and perhaps that is better. And I saw as if on my arm were two gold bracelets, and I disliked them, so I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as these two liars: the one of Yemen, whose name is al-Aswad b. Ka'b al-'Ansi, and the one of al-Yamamah. Al-Aswad had spoken during the time of the Prophet ﷺ."],[1062,"While we were on a journey with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came on his mount and began striking right and left. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever has an extra mount should give it to one who has no mount, and whoever has extra provisions should give to one who has no provisions.' He mentioned of the types of wealth what he mentioned, until we saw that none of us had any right to surplus."],[1063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw among his companions some lingering behind, so he said to them: 'Come forward and follow me, and let those behind you follow you. A people will continue to lag behind until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, puts them behind.'"],[1064,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Muhammad, are you in pain?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you, from every ailment that harms you, from every soul or envious eye, may Allah heal you. In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you.'"],[1065,"The Prophet ﷺ used to stand by a wooden stump, leaning on it, delivering the sermon every Friday, until a man from the people came to him and said: 'If you wish, I will make something for you that when you sit on it, it will be as if you are standing.' He said: 'Yes.' So he made the pulpit for him. When he sat on it, the stump yearned like a she-camel yearning for her young, until the Prophet ﷺ descended and placed his hand on it. Then the next day, I saw it had been moved. We said: 'What is this?' They said: 'The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar came last night and moved it.'"],[1066,"The stump yearned like a milch she-camel."],[1067,"I saw in what a sleeper sees as if I were under a tree, and as if the tree were reciting Sad. When it reached the prostration, it prostrated, and said in its prostration: 'O Allah, forgive me by it; O Allah, remove from me by it a burden, and grant me by it gratitude, and accept it from me as You accepted from Your servant Dawud his prostration.' I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him, and he said: 'You prostrated, O Abu Sa'id?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'You are more entitled to the prostration than the tree.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Surah Sad, then he came to the prostration, and said in his prostration what the tree said in its prostration."],[1068,"When one of you strikes his servant and he mentions Allah, then raise your hands."],[1069,"There is no zakah on less than five awaq, nor on less than five awsuq, nor on less than five camels."],[1070,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the mosque of Banu Amr b. Awf, and he passed by the village of Banu Salim and called out to a man."],[1071,"Ali brought him a dinar he had found in the market. He said: \"Announce it for three days.\" He did not find anyone who recognized it, so he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: \"Eat it, or: do as you wish with it.\" So he bought with three dirhams barley, and with three dirhams dates, and bought with a dirham meat, and with a dirham oil, and he had a dirham left over—the exchange rate was eleven to a dinar—until after that its owner came and recognized it. Ali said to him: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to eat it.\" Then its owner went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned all of that to him. He said to Ali: \"Return it to the man.\" He said: \"I have eaten it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If anything comes to us, we will give it to you.\""],[1072,"There was no prophet except that he warned his people about the Dajjal, and I warn you about him. He is one-eyed, with a protruding eyeball, and he is not hidden, as if it were a piece of flesh on the side of a wall. His left eye is like a brilliant star. With him is something like Paradise and Hell. His Paradise is a haze with smoke, and his Hell is a green garden. In front of him are two men who warn the people of the villages. Whenever they leave a village, its first people enter, and he is given power over a man whom he is not given power over anyone else. He slaughters him, then strikes him with his staff, then says: 'Arise.' Then he says to his companions: 'What do you think? Am I not your Lord?' They testify to him with polytheism. The slaughtered man says: 'O people, this is the false Messiah about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us.' Then he returns and slaughters him again, then strikes him with his staff, and says to him: 'Arise.' Then he says to his companions: 'What do you think? Am I not your Lord?' They testify to him with polytheism. The slaughtered man says: 'O people, indeed this is the false Messiah about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us. This has only increased me in insight about you.' Then he returns and slaughters him a third time, then strikes him with his staff, and says: 'Arise.' Then he says to his companions: 'What do you think? Am I not your Lord?' They testify to him with polytheism. He says: 'O people, indeed this is the false Messiah about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us. This has only increased me in insight about you.' Then he returns and slaughters him a fourth time, and Allah places a plate of copper on his throat, so he cannot slaughter him.\" Abu Sa'id said: \"By Allah, I did not see copper except on that day.\" He said: \"Then the people plant and cultivate after that.\" Abu Sa'id said: \"We used to think that man was Umar b. al-Khattab because of what we knew of his strength and endurance.\""],[1073,"When this verse was revealed: 'And give the relative his due' (Q 17:26), the Prophet ﷺ called Fatimah and gave her Fadak."],[1074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed i'tikaf during the middle ten days of Ramadan, seeking Laylat al-Qadr. Then he ordered the structure to be dismantled, so it was taken down. Then it was made clear to him that it was in the last ten days, so he ordered it to be rebuilt. He came out to us and said: \"Laylat al-Qadr was shown to me, and I came out to inform you of it, but two men quarreled and I was made to forget it. So seek it in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.\" I said: \"O Abu Sa'id, you know the numbers better than us. Which night is the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth?\" He said: \"Yes, and we are more entitled to that. When it is the twenty-first night, then leave one night, then the one after it is the third, then leave one night, and the one after it is the fifth.\""],[1075,"The key to prayer is wudu, its sanctification is the takbir, its release is the taslim, and in every two rak'ahs there is a taslim. No prayer is valid without reciting in it the Opening of the Book and something with it."],[1076,"O people of Madinah, do not eat the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days. They complained to him that they had families and servants, so he said: \"Eat, feed others, and store.\""],[1077,"When he put on a garment, he would name it by its type: turban, shirt, or cloak, and say: \"O Allah, praise be to You. You have clothed me. I ask You for its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was made for.\""],[1078,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a river of water while riding a mule, and the people were fasting, with many on foot. He said: \"Drink.\" They kept looking at him, so he said: \"Drink, for I am lighter than you.\" They kept looking at him, so he turned his hip and drank, and the people drank."],[1079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and noticed phlegm in the direction of the qiblah. He removed it with a stick he had with him, or a reed, then turned to the people, who recognized anger in his face, and said: \"Who did this?\" The people remained silent. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Would any of you like, when he stands in his prayer place, a man to face him and spit in his face?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we would not like that.\" He said: \"Indeed Allah is before you, so let none of you face anything harmful in front of him, but rather to his left or under his foot.\""],[1080,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ acquired a new garment, he would name it by its type. He would say: O God, You have clothed me with this shirt, or cloak, or turban. We ask You for its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was made for."],[1081,"The wealthy are destroyed, the wealthy are destroyed, except... They said: O Messenger of God, except whom? He said: Except the one who gives like this and like this, to his right and to his left."],[1082,"How can I be at ease when the bearer of the trumpet has put it to his mouth and inclined his forehead, waiting for when he is commanded to blow? It was said: We said: O Messenger of God, what should we say on that day? He said: Say: God is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs. Upon God we rely."],[1083,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom God has given the Quran, and he recites it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, so he says: If only I had been given the like of what this man has been given, I would do as he does; and a man to whom God has given wealth, and he spends it in its due right, so he says: If only I had been given the like of what this man has been given, I would do as he does."],[1084,"Among you there is one who will fight for the interpretation of the Quran as I fought for its revelation. Abu Bakr said: Is it I, O Messenger of God? He said: No. Umar said: Is it I, O Messenger of God? He said: No, but it is the mender of the sandal. He had given Ali his sandal to mend."],[1085,"Do not revile my companions, for if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud in gold, you would not attain the measure of one of them, nor even half of it."],[1086,"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection is a tyrannical leader."],[1087,"The servant will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked: What prevented you, when you saw wrongdoing, from denouncing it? When God inspires a servant with his proof, he will say: O Lord, I hoped in You and feared the people."],[1088,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was in the house of Umm Salama, and he was praying in a single garment, wrapping himself with it."],[1089,"A community is not sanctified if the weak among them is not given his right without hesitation."],[1090,"The Ansar are the inner garment and the people are the outer garment. Were it not for the emigration, I would have been a man of the Ansar."],[1091,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the purchase of what is in the wombs of livestock until they give birth, and of what is in their udders except by measure, and the purchase of a runaway slave, and the purchase of spoils until they are distributed, and the purchase of charity until it is received, and the diver's catch."],[1092,"It will be said to the companion of the Quran when he enters Paradise: Recite and ascend. So he recites and ascends with each verse a degree."],[1093,"We used to give him an inheritance in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, meaning the grandfather."],[1094,"Instruct your dying ones to say: There is no god but Allah."],[1095,"The people of the Fire who are its people will neither die nor live, but some people – or as he said – the Fire will afflict them for their sins – or he said: for their errors – he said: this is how Abu Nadrah said it – so He will cause them to die until when they become charcoal, permission will be given for intercession. They will be brought in bundles and scattered over the rivers of Paradise, and it will be said to the people of Paradise: Pour water over them. So they will grow as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood. A man from the people said: It is as if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were in the desert."],[1096,"The mercy of Allah is one hundred parts. He divided one part among creation, and through it they show mercy to one another: humans, wild beasts, and birds."],[1097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Abbas: O boy, O little boy – or: O little boy, O boy – preserve from me some words..."],[1098,"The Friday bath is obligatory upon every Muslim, and touching perfume if he has it."],[1099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us after the afternoon prayer until the sun was nearly setting. Those who memorized it memorized it, and those who forgot it forgot it. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed: indeed, the world is sweet and green, and Allah is making you successors in it and is watching how you act. So beware of the world and beware of women. Indeed, every betrayer will have a banner in proportion to his betrayal, and there is no betrayal greater than the betrayal of a leader of a group. Indeed, the best of men is one who is slow to anger and quick to calm down, and the worst of men is one who is quick to anger and slow to calm down. If he is quick to anger and quick to calm down, then it is as it is. If he is slow to anger and slow to calm down, then it is as it is. Indeed, the best of merchants is one who is good in repayment and good in seeking, and the worst of merchants is one who is bad in repayment and bad in seeking. If a man is bad in repayment and good in seeking, then it is as it is. If a man is good in repayment and bad in seeking, then it is as it is. Indeed, anger is a live coal kindled in the heart of the son of Adam. Do you not see his eyes and the swelling of his veins? So whoever senses any of that, let him cling to the ground. And let not any of you be prevented by awe of people from speaking the truth when he knows it. Indeed, the most excellent jihad is a word of truth in the presence of a tyrannical ruler. Then when the sun was nearly setting, he said: Indeed, the amount of the world that has passed compared to what remains of it is like the amount of this day of ours that has passed compared to what remains."],[1100,"The best rows for men are the front ones and the worst are the back ones, and the best rows for women are the back ones and the worst are the front ones."],[1101,"A man had anal intercourse with his wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they said: So-and-so had anal intercourse with his wife. Then Allah revealed: Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you will."],[1102,"The likeness of one who plays backgammon and then stands to pray is the likeness of one who performs ablution with pus and the blood of a pig; he said: his prayer is not accepted."],[1103,"In the end of time, when life spans are prolonged and time is cut short, there will be an imam who will be the most generous of people. A man will come to him and he will pour into his lap, and it will concern him who will accept the charity of that wealth from him, between him and his family, because of the good that befalls the people."],[1104,"The example of the believer and of faith is like a horse at its tethering post: it roams about, then returns to its tethering post. Indeed, the believer is heedless, then returns to faith. So feed your food to the God-fearing, and direct your kindness to the believers."],[1105,"Is any one of you unable to recite one-third of the Qur’an in a night? They said: Who can do that? He said: He recites “Say: He is Allah, the One,” and that is one-third of the Qur’an."],[1106,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the night prayer, he began his prayer by saying the takbir, then he said: “Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god besides You,” three times. “There is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great, greatly,” three times. “I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his blowing, and his spitting,” then he recited."],[1107,"Whoever humbles himself before Allah by one degree, Allah raises him one degree until He places him in the highest of the high. And whoever is arrogant toward Allah by one degree, Allah lowers him one degree until He places him in the lowest of the low."],[1108,"A people will surely remember Allah in this world upon spread couches, and Allah will admit them to the highest degrees."],[1109,"There is no Muslim who feeds a Muslim in hunger except that Allah feeds him from the fruits of Paradise. And there is no Muslim who clothes his brother in nakedness except that Allah clothes him from the green garments of Paradise. And whoever gives a Muslim water to drink in thirst, Allah will give him to drink from the pure nectar."],[1110,"When a man wakes up during the night and prays two rak’ahs, it is recorded for him among those men and women who remember Allah much."],[1111,"Give good news to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."],[1112,"Whoever sleeps through the Witr prayer or forgets it, let him pray Witr when he wakes up or when he remembers."],[1113,"There will indeed come upon the people a time when you will have foolish rulers who put forward the worst of people, show off their best, and delay the prayer beyond its appointed times. Whoever among you reaches that time, let him not be a tribal leader, nor a policeman, nor a tax collector, nor a treasurer."],[1114,"He forbade two types of sales and two types of dress. As for the two sales, they are mulamasah and munabadhah. As for the two types of dress, one is wrapping oneself in a single garment with no opening for the arms. And he forbade sitting with the legs drawn up wrapped in a single garment, with nothing between him and the sky over his private parts."],[1115,"Instruct your dying ones to say: There is no god but Allah."],[1116,"Did you memorize anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he used to say after he said the taslim? He said: Yes, he used to say: “Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they describe, and peace be upon the messengers, and praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.”"],[1117,"\"Visit the sick and follow funerals; they will remind you of the Hereafter.\""],[1118,"Regarding “When the matter is decided while they are heedless,” he said: “In this world.”"],[1119,"He forbade prayer after ʿAsr and after Fajr."],[1120,"\"Whoever does not thank people does not thank God.\""],[1121,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping it around himself.\""],[1122,"He forbade the tilting of waterskins (to drink from their mouths)."],[1123,"\"The key to prayer is purification; its sanctification is the takbir; its desanctification is the taslim.\""],[1124,"\"We used to estimate the standing of the Messenger of God ﷺ in Zuhr and ʿAsr. We estimated his standing in the first two rakʿahs of Zuhr as the length of thirty verses, each rakʿah the length of reciting al-Sajdah (Qur'an 32). We estimated his standing in the first two rakʿahs of ʿAsr as the length of the last two of Zuhr, and we estimated his standing in the last two as half of that.\""],[1125,"\"Bathing on Friday is obligatory for every adult.\""],[1126,"\"A man from my family will surely rise over my community, aquiline-nosed, with a clear forehead, filling the earth with justice just as it was filled with injustice and oppression; he will rule for seven years.\""],[1127,"\"We became extremely poor, and my family told me to go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and ask him for something. So I went, and the first thing I heard the Prophet of God ﷺ say was: 'Whoever seeks to be self-sufficient, God will make him self-sufficient; whoever seeks to abstain, God will make him abstain; and whoever asks us, we will not withhold anything from him if we find it' — or as he said. I said to myself: I will seek self-sufficiency and God will make me self-sufficient, and I will seek abstinence and God will make me abstain. So I did not ask the Prophet ﷺ for anything.\""],[1128,"\"Indeed, the people of the highest ranks will see those below them as you see the shining star rising in the horizon of the sky, and indeed Abu Bakr and Umar are among those, and how excellent they are.\""],[1129,"I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri about the saying of Allah: 'Indeed, He who imposed the Quran upon you will surely return you to a place of return.' He said: 'His place of return is the Hereafter.'"],[1130,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the fast of Ashura, and he would not fast it.\""],[1131,"He forbade wisal (continuous fasting)."],[1132,"He forbade fasting on the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice, and forbade prayer after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."],[1133,"Coitus interruptus was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Do you practice it?\" - and he did not say: do not do it - \"There is no soul that Allah creates except that Allah is its Creator.\""],[1134,"\"A man should not look at the nakedness of a man, and a woman should not look at the nakedness of a woman, and a man should not lie with a man under one cloth, and a woman should not lie with a woman under one cloth.\""],[1135,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say after rising from bowing: 'O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and the earths, and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter. There is no one to withhold what You give, and no benefit does the one of high rank derive from You, for high rank is Yours. The best of what the servant has said, and all of us are servants to You: there is no one to withhold what You give, and no benefit does the one of high rank derive from You, for high rank is Yours.'\""],[1136,"\"A neck will emerge from Hell on the Day of Resurrection, saying: 'I have been assigned to three: every tyrannical and stubborn one, and whoever set up another god besides Allah, and whoever killed a soul without a soul.'\""],[1137,"\"Do not mix unripe dates and ripe dates.\""],[1138,"\"O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray after me: the two weighty things, one of which is greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended from the sky to the earth, and my family, the people of my house. They will never separate until they return to me at the Pond.\""],[1139,"I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and said: 'One of us prays and does not know how much he has prayed.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: When one of you prays and does not know how much he has prayed, let him perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting. And when Satan comes to one of you and says, \"You have invalidated your ablution,\" let him say, \"You have lied,\" unless he finds an odor or hears a sound with his ear.'"],[1140,"\"I forbid you from fasting on two days: the day of Fitr and the day of Adha.\""],[1141,"Uqbah b. Mukram narrated to us; Yunus narrated to us; Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, from Ya'qub b. Utbah, from Sulayman b. Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the like of it."],[1142,"\"Yajuj and Majuj will emerge, and they will come forth as Allah said: 'From every elevation they will descend.' He said: They will cover the earth, and the Muslims will withdraw from them until the remainder of the Muslims are in their cities and fortresses, and they will gather their livestock to them. The first of them will pass by the river and drink it until they leave nothing in it. Then the last of them will pass by after them, and one of them will say: 'There was water here once.' Then they will prevail over the earth, and one of them will say: 'These are the people of the earth; we have finished with them. Let us fight the people of heaven.' One of them will shake his spear and hurl it toward heaven, and it will return stained with blood. They will say: 'We have killed the people of heaven.' While they are in that state, Allah will send against them creatures like the worms of locusts, which will seize their necks and they will die like locusts, one falling upon another. The Muslims will wake up and hear no sound from them. They will say: 'Who will offer himself to see what they have done?' A man among them will say, having resolved that they will kill him, and he will find them dead, then call to them: 'Rejoice! Allah has destroyed your enemy.' The people will come out and release their livestock, and they will find no pasture except their flesh, and they will become fat from it as they never did from any vegetation they had ever eaten.\""],[1143,"\"When Allah gathers the people on one plain on the Day of Resurrection, the Fire will come riding, one part upon another, with its keepers restraining it, while it says: 'By the might of my Lord, let me be free with my mates, or I will sweep over the people as one neck.' They will say: 'Who are your mates?' It will say: 'Every arrogant tyrant.' It will then thrust out its tongue and pick them out from among the people, casting them into its interior. Then it will retreat, then come again riding, one part upon another, with its keepers restraining it, while it says: 'By the might of my Lord, let me be free with my mates, or I will sweep over the people as one neck.' They will say: 'Who are your mates?' It will say: 'Every ungrateful tyrant.' It will then pick them out with its tongue from among the people and cast them into its interior. Then it will retreat, then come again riding, one part upon another, with its keepers restraining it, while it says: 'By the might of my Lord, let me be free with my mates, or I will sweep over the people as one neck.' They will say: 'Who are your mates?' It will say: 'Every conceited boaster.' It will then pick them out with its tongue from among the people and cast them into its interior. Then it will retreat, and Allah will judge between the servants.\""],[1144,"\"On the Day of Resurrection a neck will come out from the Fire, having a tongue that speaks. It will say: 'I have been entrusted today with three: whoever set up another god with Allah, and every stubborn tyrant'—and he did not name the third—'so it will fold over them and cast them into the depths of Jahannam.'\""],[1145,"\"Paradise was displayed to me, and I went to take a bunch from it to show you, but something came between me and it. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is it like the berry of a grape?' He said: 'Like the largest bucket your mother ever made.'\""],[1146,"\"We captured female captives on the day of Awtas who had husbands, and we disliked to have intercourse with them, so we asked the Prophet ﷺ, and the verse was revealed: 'And married women, except what your right hands possess.' So we considered them lawful.\""],[1147,"\"That he prayed in his sandals.\""],[1148,"\"The example of one who plays with dice.\""],[1149,"I was among a band of weak emigrants, and some of them would screen themselves with one another due to nakedness. There was a reciter among us reciting to us, and we were listening to the Book of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and stood over us. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over us, the reciter fell silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What were you doing?' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a reciter was reciting and we were listening to the Book of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Praise be to Allah who has placed in my Ummah those with whom I have been commanded to be patient.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in our midst to make himself equal among us. Then he gestured with his hand: 'Form a circle.' So the circle turned and their faces became visible to him. I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recognize any of them except me. He said: 'Rejoice, O company of poor emigrants, with the everlasting light on the Day of Resurrection. You will enter Paradise before the rich believers by half a day, and that is five hundred years.'"],[1150,"\"When the Banu al-Hakam reach thirty, they will take Allah's religion as a deception, Allah's servants as slaves, and Allah's wealth as booty to be passed around.\""],[1151,"We captured women on the day of Hunayn, and we were practicing withdrawal (coitus interruptus) with them. Some of us said to others: 'You do this while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among you?' So we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Not every water produces a child. When Allah wills to create something, nothing can prevent it.'"],[1152,"\"There is no harm upon you if you do not do it, for it is only the decree.\""],[1153,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us in his illness in which he died, and his head was bandaged. I followed him until he stood on the pulpit, and he said: \"Indeed, at this hour I am standing at the Hawd.\" Then he said: \"Indeed, a servant was offered the world and its adornment, and he chose the Hereafter.\" He said: \"No one among the people understood this except Abu Bakr, who said: May my father and mother be your ransom. Rather, we will ransom you with our wealth, our selves, and our children.\" Then he descended from the pulpit, and thereafter he was not seen upon it until this hour."],[1154,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ was more shy than a virgin in her private chamber, and when he disliked something, we would recognize it in his face.\""],[1155,"\"When you see the funeral procession, stand up, and whoever follows it should not sit until it is placed down.\""],[1156,"We discussed the Night of Qadr among a group of Quraysh. I went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who was a friend of mine, and said: \"Will you not come out with us to the palm groves?\" He came out wearing a striped cloak. I said to him: \"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ mention the Night of Qadr?\" He said: \"Yes. We performed i'tikaf with the Messenger of God ﷺ during the middle ten days of Ramadan. We came out on the morning of the twentieth, and the Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon to us, saying: 'I was shown the Night of Qadr, but I was made to forget it—or: I forgot it—so seek it in the last ten nights on the odd nights. And I saw that I was prostrating in water and mud. Whoever performed i'tikaf with the Messenger of God ﷺ should return.' So we returned, and we did not see any cloud in the sky. Then a cloud came and rain fell upon us until the mosque flowed with water—and it was made of palm branches. The prayer was called, and I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrating in water and mud, until I saw the trace of mud on his forehead.\""],[1157,"\"When you follow a funeral procession, do not sit until it is placed down.\" Suhayl said: \"I saw Abu Salih not sitting until it was placed down from the shoulders of the men.\""],[1158,"I heard something from him that pleased me, and I said to him: \"Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"Would I say about the Messenger of God ﷺ what I did not hear?\" He said: \"I heard him say: 'Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and the Aqsa Mosque.'\""],[1159,"The statement of A'ishah was mentioned to Abu Sa'id: that the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs after Asr. He said: \"As for me, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and none after Fajr until the sun rises.'\""],[1160,"\"When one of you yawns, let him put his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters.\""],[1161,"Ali sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ from Yemen a piece of gold in tanned leather that had not been purified. He divided it among four men: Zayd al-Khayl, al-Aqra' b. Habis, Uyaynah b. Hisn, and Alqamah b. Ulathah. Some people from the Muhajirun and the Ansar said: \"We are more entitled to this.\" This reached him and distressed him, and he said: \"Do you not trust me, while I am the trustee of the One in heaven? The news of heaven comes to me morning and evening.\" Then a man with protruding eyes, prominent cheeks, a receding forehead, a thick beard, a shaved head, and a raised lower garment stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of God, fear God.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Woe to you! Am I not the most entitled of the people of the earth to fear God?\" Then he turned away. Khalid, the sword of God, stood up and said: \"O Messenger of God, shall I strike his neck?\" He said: \"No, for perhaps he may pray.\" He said: \"If he prays, he says with his tongue what is not in his heart.\" He said: \"I have not been commanded to split open people's hearts or split open their bellies.\" The Prophet ﷺ looked at him as he was departing and said: \"From the stock of this one there will come a people who recite the Book of God, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game.\" Umarah said: \"I think he said: 'If I catch them, I will kill them as Thamud was killed.'\""],[1162,"Concerning the one who has intercourse and then wishes to repeat it, let him perform wudu."],[1163,"The Messenger of God ﷺ bade farewell to a man and said to him: \"Where do you intend to go?\" He said: \"I intend to go to Jerusalem.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a hundred prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque.\""],[1164,"\"No fasting on the day of Eid, and a woman should not travel for three days except with a mahram.\""],[1165,"\"The saddles should not be fastened (i.e., journeys should not be undertaken) except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of Madinah, and the Aqsa Mosque.\""],[1166,"\"The child of zina will not enter Paradise, nor the one addicted to wine, nor the one who is disobedient to parents, nor the one who reminds others of his favors.\""],[1167,"\"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise. And Fatimah is the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise, except for what was the case with Maryam bt. 'Imran.\""],[1168,"\"The muhrim may kill the black snake, the scorpion, the kite, the vicious dog, and the fuwaysiqah.\" He said: I said: \"What is the fuwaysiqah?\" He said: \"The mouse.\" I said: \"And what is the matter with the mouse?\" He said: \"The Prophet ﷺ woke up and the mouse had taken the wick and climbed with it to the ceiling.\""],[1169,"There was something between Khalid b. al-Walid and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, and Khalid insulted him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not insult any of my companions, for if one of you were to spend the like of Uhud, he would not reach the mudd of one of them, nor half of it.\""],[1170,"\"Paradise and the Fire argued. The Fire said: 'In me are the tyrants and the arrogant.' Paradise said: 'In me are the weak people and their poor.' He said: So He judged between them: 'You are Paradise, My mercy; I have mercy through you on whom I will. And you are the Fire, My punishment; I punish through you whom I will. And for both of you, it is incumbent upon Me to fill you.'\""],[1171,"Noah will be called on the Day of Resurrection, and he will say: 'At Your service and obedience, O Lord.' He will say: 'Did you convey?' He will say: 'My Lord, yes.' So He will say to his ummah: 'Did he convey to you?' They will say: 'No warner came to us.' It will be said: 'Who will testify for you?' He will say: 'Muhammad ﷺ and his ummah.' He said: So they will testify that he conveyed, and the Messenger will be a witness over you. That is His saying: 'We have made you a middle ummah that you may be witnesses over the people.' He said: And the middle means the just."],[1172,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, my husband Safwan b. al-Mu'attal beats me when I pray, makes me break my fast when I fast, and does not pray the dawn prayer until the sun rises.' Safwan was with him, so he asked him about what she said. He said: 'O Messenger of God, as for her saying that he beats me when I pray, she recites with my two surahs and I have forbidden her from that.' He said: 'If it were a single surah it would suffice the people.' He said: 'As for her saying that he makes me break my fast when I fast, she goes off and fasts while I am a young man, and I cannot restrain myself.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said that day: 'A woman should not fast except with her husband's permission.' 'As for her saying that I do not pray until the sun rises, we are a household known for that; we hardly wake up until the sun rises.' He said: 'So when you wake up, pray.'"],[1173,"When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, it will be said: 'O people of Paradise,' and they will crane their necks and look. Death will be brought as if it were a speckled ram, and it will be said to them: 'Do you recognize this Death?' They will say: 'It is this,' and all of them will have recognized it. It will be brought forward and slaughtered. Then it will be said to them: 'O people of Paradise, eternity without death. O people of the Fire, eternity without death.' He said: That is His saying: 'And warn them of the Day of Regret, when the matter will be decided, while they are in heedlessness and do not believe.'"],[1174,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mixing raisins and dried dates, and unripe dates and dried dates.\""],[1175,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mixing raisins and dried dates."],[1176,"The people of the highest degrees will be seen by those below them as you see the rising star in the horizon of the sky, and indeed Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and excellent they are."],[1177,"\"When one of you fights, let him avoid the face.\""],[1178,"\"He grants respite until, when the first third of the night has passed, the Blessed and Exalted descends to the lowest heaven and says: Is there anyone seeking forgiveness? Is there anyone asking? Is there anyone supplicating? Until dawn breaks.\""],[1179,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ notice some of his companions lagging behind, so he said: \"Come forward and follow me, and let those behind you follow you. A people will keep lagging behind me until Allah puts them behind.\""],[1180,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered the sermon on the day of Eid while on his mount.\""],[1181,"We captured some donkeys on the day of Khaybar, and the pots were boiling with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is this?\" We said: \"Donkeys we captured.\" He said: \"Wild or domestic?\" We said: \"No, rather domestic.\" He said: \"Then overturn them.\" He said: So we overturned them."],[1182,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land abounding with lizards, so what do you command us?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It has reached me that a nation from the Children of Israel was transformed into animals, and I do not know which of the animals. He neither commanded us nor forbade us.\""],[1183,"The limbs wake up in the morning rebuking the tongue, saying: 'Fear Allah concerning us, for if you are upright we are upright, and if you deviate we deviate.'"],[1184,"\"When the believers are saved from the Fire, they will be detained on a bridge between Paradise and the Fire, where they will settle the wrongs that were between them in the world. Then when they are purified and refined, they will be permitted to enter Paradise. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, one of them will be more acquainted with his dwelling in Paradise than you are with your dwelling that you inhabited in the world.\""],[1185,"\"There will be rulers over you who are surrounded by crowds of people. Whoever believes their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing, I am innocent of him and he is innocent of me. And whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is from me and I am from him.\""],[1186,"The Banu Qurayza surrendered to the judgment of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, so a message was sent to Sa'd, and he came on a donkey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Stand up for your best one—or: for your chief.\" He said: \"These people have surrendered to your judgment.\" He said: \"Then I judge that their fighters be killed and their offspring be taken captive.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You have judged by the judgment of Allah,\" and once he said: \"You have judged by the judgment of the King.\""],[1187,"\"When you hear the call, then say the like of what the muezzin says.\""],[1188,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning the one who forgets a prayer, he said: “He should pray it when he remembers it.”"],[1189,"He forbade muzābanah and muḥāqalah. Muzābanah is buying dates on the tops of date palms, and muḥāqalah is the leasing of land."],[1190,"“There are in Madinah a number of jinn who have accepted Islam. Whoever sees any of these creatures (al-ʿawāmir) should give it a warning three times. If it appears to him after that, let him kill it, for it is a devil.”"],[1191,"“People will emerge from the direction of the east who recite the Qurʾān, but it will not pass beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes through the game, and they will not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. Their mark is shaving the head and cutting the hair close (al-taḥlīq wa-l-tasbīt).”"],[1192,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took off his sandals during the prayer and placed them on his left. So the people took off their sandals. He said: “What is the matter with you?” They said: “We saw you take them off, so we took ours off.” He said: “Gabriel came to me and informed me that there was some filth on them. So when any of you comes, let him look. If he sees filth or harm on them, let him wipe them, then pray in them.”"],[1193,"We had hardly returned when Khaybar was conquered, and we fell upon that herb—garlic and onions—and ate of them ravenously. He said: And the people were hungry. We returned to the mosque, and the Messenger of God ﷺ noticed the smell. He said: “Whoever has eaten anything of this foul herb should not come near us in the mosque.” The people said: “It has been made forbidden, it has been made forbidden.” That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “O people, I have no power to forbid what God has made lawful. But it is a plant whose smell I dislike.”"],[1194,"“O people of Madinah, do not eat the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days.” He said: The people of Madinah complained to him that they had dependents. He said: “Then eat, feed others, and store it.” Al-Jurayrī said: I do not know whether it was in this hadith or another that he said: “And preserve it.”"],[1195,"“It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to undertake a journey of three days or more unless she has with her her father, her son, her husband, or a maḥram of hers.”"],[1196,"“Do not revile my Companions. For if one of you were to spend the like of Uḥud in gold, he would not attain the measure of a mudd of one of them, nor half of it.”"],[1197,"When the expedition to Tabūk took place, the people suffered from hunger. They said: “O Messenger of God, if you would permit us, we could slaughter our water-carrying camels and eat and use the fat.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: “Do so.” Then ʿUmar came and said: “O Messenger of God, if they do that, the riding animals will become scarce. But call them to bring the surplus of their provisions, then pray for blessing over them, perhaps God will place blessing in that.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ called for a leather mat and spread it out, then called for the surplus of their provisions. He said: A man would come with a handful of corn, another with a handful of dates, another with a piece of bread, until something of that gathered on the mat. He said: He prayed for blessing over it, then said: “Take into your vessels.” He said: They took into their vessels until they left no vessel in the army but they filled it. He said: They ate until they were full. He said: And a surplus remained. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God. No servant meets God with this, without doubting, but he will be veiled from Paradise.”"],[1198,"“There is no ṣadaqah on less than five awsuq.”"],[1199,"There is no ṣadaqah on less than five awsuq of dates or grain."],[1200,"Charity is not lawful for a rich person except for three: a fighter in the path of God, a wayfarer, or a man who has a neighbor to whom charity was given, and he gifted it to him."],[1201,"Whoever sees a wrong and is able to change it with his hand, let him do so; if he cannot with his hand, then with his tongue; if he cannot with his tongue, then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith."],[1202,"Adam and Moses argued. Moses said: O Adam, God created you with His hand, breathed into you of His spirit, commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, and lodged you in His Paradise, yet you led people astray and brought them out of Paradise? Adam said: O Moses, God chose you with His word and sent down the Torah upon you and did with you and did. Do you blame me for a matter that God decreed upon me before He created me? He said: Thus Adam defeated Moses, peace be upon them both."],[1203,"A man was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ - he said: I think it was for drinking - and the Prophet ﷺ struck him with two sandals forty times."],[1204,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[1205,"Regarding His saying: 'And thus We made you a middle nation,' he said: 'Just.'"],[1206,"The witr is at night."],[1207,"Relate from me and there is no harm. Relate from me and do not lie about me. Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And relate from the Children of Israel and there is no harm."],[1208,"Our Prophet ﷺ commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book and whatever was easy."],[1209,"He forbade the nabidh of the jar."],[1210,"Let not fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it and knows it, or sees it and hears it."],[1211,"Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection raised for him according to his treachery. Indeed, there is no traitor greater in treachery than a ruler of the common people."],[1212,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood at a river of rainwater while the people were fasting on a hot day, and they were on foot while the Messenger of God ﷺ was on his mule. He said: “Drink, O people.” They said: “Should we drink, O Messenger of God?” He said: “I am not like you; I am more comfortable than you; I am riding.” He said: They refused. He said: The Prophet of God ﷺ bent his thigh and dismounted, then drank, and the people drank, though he had not intended to drink it.”"],[1213,"Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I have incurred a prescribed punishment, so carry it out on me.” He said: The Prophet ﷺ turned him away three times, or perhaps four times. Then he asked about him: “Is there anything wrong with him?” They said: “No, O Messenger of God, except that he has incurred a prescribed punishment and does not think anything can release him from it but the punishment.” He said: The Prophet ﷺ gave the order, and we took him to Baqi' al-Gharqad. We did not dig a grave for him nor tie him up. We threw at him pieces of pottery and bones. That distressed him, so he ran to the harrah, and we followed him and threw at him the hard stones of the harrah until he fell silent. Then the Prophet ﷺ stood as a preacher and said: “When we go out in the path of God, one of them stays behind and has a bleating like the bleating of a he-goat. Indeed, if anyone of those is brought to me, I will make an example of him.” He said: He claimed, but he did not curse him or ask forgiveness for him."],[1214,"“There will be in the last of time a caliph who distributes wealth and does not count it.”"],[1215,"“Silver for silver, gold for gold, equal for equal, like for like. Whoever adds or asks for addition has committed usury, and the taker and the giver are the same.”"],[1216,"The Messenger of God ﷺ asked Ibn Sayyad about the soil of Paradise. He said: “White fine flour, pure musk.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He has spoken the truth.”"],[1217,"“When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise and the people of the Fire have entered the Fire, God, Blessed and Exalted, will say: ‘Whoever has in his heart the weight of a grain of good, bring him out of the Fire.’ He said: They will come out having been scorched and become charcoal, and they will be cast into a river called the River of Life, and they will grow as a seed grows in the silt of a flood.” Or he said: “in the silt of wormwood” — Abu 'Amr was uncertain. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do you not see how it grows yellow and twisted?”"],[1218,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Ibn Sayyad: “What do you see?” He said: “I see a throne on the water of the sea, and around it are snakes.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He has seen the throne of Iblis.”"],[1219,"“There is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of God over it.”"],[1220,"“Visit the sick and follow funerals; they will remind you of the Hereafter.”"],[1221,"He forbade the jar, the gourd, and the pitch-smeared vessel, and he forbade unripe dates with ripe dates."],[1222,"\"while they are in heedlessness\" — he said: “in this world.”"],[1223,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Which of the people is best?” He said: “A man who strives with his life and wealth in the path of God, and a man — meaning in one of the mountain passes — who worships his Lord and keeps people safe from his evil.”"],[1224,"A man brought the Prophet ﷺ some dates, and he disapproved of them. He said, \"Where did you get this?\" He replied, \"I took it in exchange for two sāʿs of dates.\" He said, \"You have doubled and engaged in ribā.\" Or: \"You have engaged in ribā and doubled.\""],[1225,"I will never give less than a sāʿ. During the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, we used to give a sāʿ of dates, barley, aqit, or raisins."],[1226,"There was no prophet sent nor any caliph appointed but that he had two close confidants: one that commands him to good and urges him to it, and one that commands him to evil and urges him to it. The protected one is he whom God protects."],[1227,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1228,"A man from the Ansar asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about coitus interruptus. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There is no blame on you if you do not do it, for there is no soul that God has decreed to come forth but that it will come forth.\""],[1229,"On the day of Awtas, we captured female captives who had husbands among their people. They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"So it was revealed: 'And [also forbidden to you are] married women, except what your right hands possess.'\""],[1230,"The Prophet of God ﷺ mentioned a woman from the Children of Israel who filled her ring with musk, and musk is the most fragrant of perfumes."],[1231,"When the Haruriyya came out, we went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said, \"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ mention the Haruriyya?\" He said, \"No, but I heard him say, 'A people will soon come whose prayer you will despise compared to their prayer, and your deeds compared to their deeds. They will pass out of Islam as an arrow passes through its target, until its owner takes it and looks at its arrowhead and sees nothing, then looks at its shaft and sees nothing, then looks at its notch and sees nothing in it, then looks at its fletching, whether he sees anything in it or not.'\""],[1232,"Abu Hurayra fell ill and was overcome. Abu Sa'id al-Khudri led the prayer, and he said the takbir aloud when he began, when he bowed, after saying, 'God hears the one who praises Him,' when he raised his head from prostration, when he prostrated, when he rose, and when he stood up from the two rak'as, until he completed his prayer in that manner. When he finished, it was said to him, 'People have differed about your prayer.' He stood up until he was by the pulpit and said, 'O people, by God, I do not care whether your prayer differs or not. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying like this.'"],[1233,"Eat the meat of sacrificial animals and store it."],[1234,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ on Monday to Quba. He passed by us among the Banu Salim, and the Messenger of God ﷺ stopped at the door of Ibn 'Itban and called out to him while he was on top of his wife. He came out dragging his lower garment. When he saw him, he said, 'We have rushed the man.' Ibn 'Itban said, 'O Messenger of God, what do you think about a man who is rushed away from his wife before he ejaculates; what is upon him?' He said, 'Water is only from water.'"],[1235,"No fatigue, illness, worry, sorrow, grief, or harm befalls a believing person, even a thorn that pricks him, but that God expiates some of his sins by it."],[1236,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on this pulpit: What is the matter with men who say that the kinship of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will not benefit his people? Indeed, by Allah, my kinship is connected in this world and the Hereafter, and indeed I, O people, am a forerunner for you at the Cistern. When you come, one man will say: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, and another will say: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. Then I will say: As for the lineage, I have recognized it, but you introduced innovations after me and you turned back on your heels."],[1237,"Instruct your dying ones (to say): There is no god but Allah."],[1238,"While Abu Sa'id al-Khudri was praying on Friday toward something that screened him from the people, a young man from Banu Mu'ayt came and wanted to pass in front of him. He said: Abu Sa'id pushed him in his chest, and he found no way except what was in front of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, so he returned, and Abu Sa'id pushed him in his chest harder than the first push. He said: He stood still, then he reviled Abu Sa'id. He said: Abu Sa'id entered upon Marwan, who said: What is the matter between you and your nephew? He came complaining about you. Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When one of you prays and someone wants to pass in front of him, let him push him in his chest; if he refuses, let him fight him, for he is only a devil."],[1239,"I said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: One of us prays and does not know how much he has prayed. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When one of you prays and does not know how much he has prayed, let him prostrate twice while sitting. And when Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and says: You have broken your ablution, let him say: You have lied, unless he finds its odor with his nose or hears a sound with his ear."],[1240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: Indeed, the thing I fear most for you is what Allah brings out for you of the adornment and splendor of this world. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, can good bring evil? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was silent, and we saw that revelation was coming down upon him. It was said to him: What is the matter with you? You speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he does not speak to you? Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was relieved, and he began wiping the sweat from his face. He said: Where is the questioner? We saw that he praised him. He said: Indeed, good does not bring evil. And indeed, among what the spring causes to grow is that which kills, or nearly kills, by bloating. Have you not seen the eater of green vegetation? It ate until its flanks were full, then it faced the sun and dropped dung and urinated, then it grazed again. Indeed, wealth is sweet and green, and an excellent companion to a Muslim is it if he maintains kinship ties and spends in the way of Allah. The example of the one who takes it without right is like the one who eats and does not become full, and it will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection."],[1241,"A servant of the Prophet ﷺ brought moist dates, while the dates of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were dry dates with some dryness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Where did you get these dates? He said: This is a sa' that I bought for two sa's of our dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is not correct. But if you want that, sell your dates, then buy whatever dates you wish."],[1242,"When one of you comes upon a shepherd, let him call out: O camel herder, three times. If he answers him, then (leave him); otherwise let him milk and drink, but let him not carry any away. And when one of you comes upon the wall of a garden, let him call out three times: O owner of the garden. If he answers him, then (leave him); otherwise let him eat but not carry any away."],[1243,"Every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection at his anus."],[1244,"A group of dissenters will break away at a point of division among the Muslims; the party that is closer to the truth will kill them."],[1245,"Beware of sitting in the roads. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot avoid our gatherings; we talk in them. He said: If you insist on sitting, then give the road its right. They said: What is the right of the road? He said: Lowering the gaze, refraining from harm, returning the greeting, enjoining good, and forbidding evil."],[1246,"When one of you is praying, let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him. If the person refuses, let him fight him, for he is only a devil."],[1247,"Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and stretches a hair in his anus, so he thinks that he has broken his ablution. He should not leave until he hears a sound or finds an odor."],[1248,"A man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about coitus interruptus, and he said: \"Do you do that? There is no harm if you do not do that; there is no harm if you do not do it, for there is no soul that God has decreed to come into existence but that it will come to be.\""],[1249,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and saw him praying in a single garment, wrapping it around himself."],[1250,"\"No people sit remembering God but that mercy envelops them, the angels surround them, tranquility descends upon them, and God mentions them among those with Him.\""],[1251,"\"People will pass over the bridge of Hell, upon which are thorns, hooks, and grapnels that snatch people right and left, and on its two sides are angels saying: 'O God, grant safety, grant safety.' Among the people are those who pass like lightning, some who pass like the wind, some who pass like a horse, some who run, some who walk, some who crawl on hands and knees, and some who drag themselves along. As for the people of the Fire, those who are its inhabitants, they will neither die nor live. As for some people, they will be seized for sins and errors, and they will burn and become charcoal. Then permission will be given for intercession, and they will be taken out in groups and thrown onto a river from the rivers of Paradise, and they will grow as a seed grows in the silt carried by a torrent.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Have you not seen the ṣabghā'? (A tree that grows in the flood debris?) Among the last to be brought out of the Fire will be a man on its edge, and he will say: 'O Lord, turn my face away from it.' He will say: 'Your covenant and your protection, that you will not ask Me for anything else?' He said: And on the path there are three trees. He will say: 'O Lord, transfer me to this tree so I may eat from its fruit and be in its shade.' He will say: 'Your covenant and your protection, that you will not ask Me for anything else?' He said: Then he will see another tree better than it, and he will say: 'O Lord, transfer me to this one so I may eat from its fruit and be in its shade.' He said: He will say: 'Your covenant and your protection, that you will not ask Me for anything else?' He said: Then he will see another tree, and he will say: 'O Lord, transfer me to this one so I may eat from its fruit and drink in its shade.' Then he will see the black mass of people and hear their speech, and he will say: 'O Lord, admit me to Paradise.'\" Abu Naḍrah said: Abu Sa'id and a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ differed. One of them said: \"He will admit him to Paradise and give him the world and the like of it.\" The other said: \"He will enter Paradise and be given the world and ten times the like of it.\""],[1252,"\"People will come out of the Fire having been burned and become like charcoal, and the people of Paradise will keep sprinkling water on them until they grow as flood debris grows in a torrent.\""],[1253,"\"A group will come out of the Fire, having been charcoal, and it will be said: 'Settle them in Paradise and sprinkle water on them.' He said: They will grow as a seed grows in the silt carried by a torrent. A man from the people said: 'It is as if you were from the desert people, O Messenger of God.'\""],[1254,"\"No fatigue, illness, grief, or harm befalls a believer, not even worry that concerns him, but that God expiates some of his sins thereby.\""],[1255,"\"No servant fasts a day in the path of God but that God distances his face from the Fire by that day seventy autumns.\""],[1256,"\"When the servant says: 'There is no god but God, and God is greater,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, and I am greater.' When he says: 'There is no god but God alone,' his Lord confirms him: 'There is no god but Me alone.' When he says: 'There is no god but God, with no partner,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'There is no god but Me, with no partner.' When he says: 'There is no god but God; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me; to Me belongs dominion and to Me belongs praise.' When he says: 'There is no god but God, and there is no might and no power except with God,' his Lord confirms him, saying: 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, and there is no might and no power except with Me.'\""],[1257,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade unripe dates mixed with ripe dates, and raisins mixed with dates. I said: 'That they be soaked together?' He said: 'Yes.'\""],[1258,"\"The Throne shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh.\""],[1259,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, my brother has diarrhea.\" He said: \"Give him honey to drink.\" He said: He gave it to him. Then he came to him and said: \"I gave him honey to drink, but it only increased his diarrhea.\" He said: \"Give him honey to drink.\" Then he came to him and said: \"I gave him honey to drink, but it only increased his diarrhea.\" He said: \"Give him honey to drink.\" He said: Then on the third or fourth time, I think he said, he was cured. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God has spoken the truth, and your brother's belly has lied.\""],[1260,"O Allah, I take with You a covenant that You will fulfill for me on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You do not break the promise. I am only a human, so whichever of the Muslims I have harmed or insulted – or he said: struck or insulted – make it for him a prayer, and make it for him a zakat and a means of nearness by which You bring him near to You on the Day of Resurrection."],[1261,"The Prophet ﷺ shaved his head on the day of al-Hudaybiyah along with his Companions except Abu Qatadah and Uthman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on those who shave.\" They said: \"And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"May Allah have mercy on those who shave.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And those who shorten\" on the third time."],[1262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and addressed the people, saying: \"By Allah, I do not fear for you, O people, except what comes to you from the splendor of this world.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, does good bring evil?\" The Messenger of Allah remained silent."],[1263,"\"When the bier is placed and men carry it upon their shoulders, if it was righteous it says: 'Send me forward, send me forward.' And if it was not righteous, it says: 'Woe to it, where are they taking it?' Every thing hears its voice except humans, and if a human heard it, he would fall unconscious.\""],[1264,"He came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri during the nights of al-Harrah and consulted him about leaving Madinah, complaining of its high prices and his many dependents, and told him he had no patience for the hardship of Madinah. He said to him: \"Woe to you! I do not command you to do that. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No one endures the hardship and distress of Madinah and then dies, except that I will be an intercessor – or a witness – for him on the Day of Resurrection, if he was a Muslim.'\""],[1265,"Once severe hardship befell him, and some of my family said to me: \"Would you ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for us?\" He said: So I went in anger to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The first thing with which he confronted me was his saying: \"Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient. And whoever asks us, we will not withhold from him anything we find.\" He said: So I returned to myself and presented to it the choice: \"Should I not seek chastity, so that Allah makes me chaste? Should I not seek sufficiency, so that Allah makes me self-sufficient?\" He said: After that I never walked to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him for anything out of need, until the world came to us and overwhelmed us, except what Allah protected."],[1266,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two prayers, two marriages, and two fasts: a prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, and a prayer after Fajr until the sun rises; and fasting on the day of Fitr and the day of sacrifice; and that a woman be married along with her maternal aunt or her paternal aunt.\""],[1267,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah.\""],[1268,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the Duha prayer until we would say, 'He will not leave it,' and he would leave it until we would say, 'He will not pray it.'\""],[1269,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have camels and I want to emigrate, so what do you command me?\" He said: \"Do you give them as a gift for milk?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"And do you pay their zakat?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"And do you milk them on their watering day?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then go and work beyond the seas, for Allah will not withhold any of your deeds from you, and the matter of emigration is difficult.\""],[1270,"\"There is no servant who fasts a day in the path of Allah, except that Allah distances his face from the Fire by that day seventy autumns.\""],[1271,"\"Indeed Iblis said to his Lord: 'By Your might and Your majesty, I will not cease to mislead the son of Adam as long as their souls remain in them.' His Lord said to him: 'Then by My might and My majesty, I will not cease to forgive them as long as they seek My forgiveness.'\""],[1272,"In a hadith in which he mentioned a group that would come out against a faction of the people, differing, and the closest of the two groups to the truth would kill them."],[1273,"The distance between two gate-panels in Paradise is a forty-year journey."],[1274,"Whoever seeks to be self-sufficient, Allah will enrich him, and whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste."],[1275,"We had wine belonging to an orphan. When the verse in Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed, we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, saying, \"It belongs to an orphan.\" He said, \"Pour it out.\""],[1276,"The people of 'Illiyyin are seen by those below them as you see the shining star on the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them, and what excellent ones they are."],[1277,"The women said, \"The men have overwhelmed us with your company, O Messenger of Allah, so set aside a day for us.\" He promised them a day. They came, and he preached to them and said among other things: \"There is no woman among you who sends ahead three of her children except that they will be a barrier for her from the Fire.\" A woman said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and two?\" for she had lost two. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And two.\""],[1278,"We discussed the Night of Decree among ourselves, so we went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. I said to him, \"O Abu Sa'id, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the Night of Decree?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed i'tikaf during the middle ten days of Ramadan, and we observed i'tikaf with him. On the morning of the twentieth he returned, and we returned with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept and saw the Night of Decree in a dream, but then he was made to forget it. He came out in the evening and addressed us, saying, 'I saw the Night of Decree in a dream, but then I was made to forget it, and I saw myself prostrating that night in water and mud. Whoever observed i'tikaf with us should return to his place of i'tikaf. Seek it in the last ten nights, in the odd nights among them, for Allah is odd and loves the odd.'\" He said, \"So we returned, and the sky poured rain upon us that evening. The roof of the mosque was an arbor of palm branches. He observed i'tikaf, and by the One who honored him and sent down upon him the Book, I saw him on the night of the twenty-first, with his forehead and the tip of his nose in water and mud.\""],[1279,"We said to Abu Sa'id, \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the Haruriyyah?\" He said, \"I heard him say,\" and he mentioned the hadith."],[1280,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Banu Lihyan. He said, \"Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is between them.\" Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, bless our sa' and our mudd, and place with the blessing two blessings.\""],[1281,"No people sit remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, without the angels surrounding them, mercy covering them, tranquility descending upon them, and Allah mentioning them among those with Him."],[1282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Banu Lihyan of Hudhayl. He said, \"Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is between them.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, bless us in our sa' and our mudd, and place with the blessing two blessings.\""],[1283,"They were forbidden from exchanging money, and two men among them trace that prohibition back to the Messenger of Allah."],[1284,"\"There will be rulers whom multitudes of people—or he said: crowds—will surround. Shu'ba said: I think he said: They will oppress and lie. Whoever confirms them in their lies and helps them in their oppression is not from me, nor am I from him. And whoever does not confirm them in their lies and does not help them in their oppression, he is from me and I am from him.\""],[1285,"\"When one of you comes upon a camel herder, let him call out: 'O camel herder!' three times. If he answers him, then (it is) otherwise let him milk and drink, but he must not carry any away. And when one of you comes upon a garden wall, let him call out three times: 'O owner of the wall!' If he answers him, then (it is) otherwise let him eat, but he must not carry any away.\""],[1286,"\"Do not write anything from me except the Qur'an. Whoever has written anything from me other than the Qur'an, let him erase it.\""],[1287,"\"Whoever sleeps through the Witr or forgets it, let him pray Witr when he remembers or wakes up.\""],[1288,"\"While I was sleeping, I saw people being shown to me, and they were wearing shirts. Among them were shirts that reached the chest, and among them were shirts that reached less than that. And 'Umar b. al-Khattab passed by wearing a shirt that he was dragging.\" They said: \"How did you interpret that, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"The religion.\""],[1289,"\"When there are three people, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled to lead them is the one who recites the Qur'an best.\""],[1290,"We used to estimate the standing of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the Zuhr and 'Asr prayers. We estimated his standing in the Zuhr in the first two rak'ahs as the length of reciting thirty verses—the length of reciting Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah. And in the last two rak'ahs, half of that. And we estimated his standing in the first two rak'ahs of 'Asr as the length of the last two of Zuhr, and the last two of 'Asr as half of that."],[1291,"\"Indeed the world is green and sweet, so fear God and fear women.\" He said: Then he mentioned three women among the Children of Israel: one short and two tall. She made a leg of wood so that she caught up with them, and she took a ring and made a lock for it, and she stuffed it with the best perfume: musk. Whenever she passed by a gathering, she opened the lock and the fragrance of musk spread."],[1292,"\"There will be a caliph who will scatter wealth without counting it.\""],[1293,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for a man among his companions. He said: The man went out to him and went to the upper room and performed ghusl in it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Did I rush you?\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, I was between the legs of the woman, and I did not ejaculate.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Then you do not need a ghusl.\""],[1294,"We were detained on the day of the Trench from the Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, and 'Isha' prayers until we were relieved, and that is the saying of God: 'And God sufficed the believers in battle, and God is Strong, Mighty.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood and ordered Bilal, and he called the iqamah. Then he prayed Zuhr as he used to pray it before that. Then he called the iqamah and prayed 'Asr as he used to pray it before that. Then he called the iqamah for Maghrib and prayed it as he used to pray it before that. Then he called the iqamah for 'Isha' and prayed it as he used to pray it before that. And that was before the revelation of: 'And if you fear, then pray on foot or riding.'"],[1295,"\"Let not fear of a man—or fear of a human—prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or knows it.\""],[1296,"A man from those who came before was granted wealth and children by God. When death came to him, he called his sons and said, 'What kind of father was I to you?' They said, 'The best father.' He said, 'By God, he never did any good for God. So when I die, burn me until I am charcoal, then crush me, then scatter me on a windy day.' He said: And the Prophet of God ﷺ said, 'He took their covenant on that, by my Lord, and they did it, by my Lord: when he died they burned him until he was charcoal, crushed him, then scattered him on a windy day.' He said: Then his Lord said to him, 'Be,' and he was a man standing. His Lord said to him, 'What made you do what you did?' He said, 'Lord, I feared Your punishment.' He said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, He did not overlook him at that point but forgave him."],[1297,"The people of the highest degrees are seen by those below them as you see the star rising in the horizon of the sky, and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them and have been favored."],[1298,"There will be rulers over you to whom hearts feel at ease and skins soften. Then there will be rulers over you from whom skins shudder and hearts recoil. A man said, 'O Messenger of God, should we not fight them?' He said, 'No, as long as they establish the prayer.'"],[1299,"I was with Marwan b. al-Hakam when Abu Sa'id al-Khudri came, and Marwan said to him, 'Did you hear the Prophet ﷺ forbidding blowing into drink?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[1300,"God is more delighted with the repentance of His servant than a man who lost his mount in a desert, searched for it and could not find it, then lay down to die. While he was like that, he heard the thud of the mount as it knelt, uncovered his face, and there was his mount."],[1301,"I and Abd Allah b. Abi Talha entered upon Abu Sa'id al-Khudri to visit him. Abu Sa'id said to us, \""],[1302,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was performing ablution from the well of Buda'a. I said, 'O Messenger of God, do you perform ablution from it when foul things are thrown into it?' He said, 'Water is not made impure by anything.'"],[1303,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the bearer of the trumpet and said, 'On his right is Jibril and on his left is Mika'il.'"],[1304,"We asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, 'Did you hear anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ about coitus interruptus?' He said, 'We asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about coitus interruptus. He said, \"What is coitus interruptus?\" We said, \"A man has a wife who is nursing, he has intercourse with her but dislikes that she becomes pregnant, so he withdraws from her; or he has a slave girl, he has intercourse with her but dislikes that she becomes pregnant, so he withdraws from her.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"It does not matter if you do not do that, for it is only decree.\"'"],[1305,"We asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri about nabidh in earthenware jars. He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade nabidh in earthenware jars.' We said, 'What about leather containers?' He said, 'That is worse.'"],[1306,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying on a mat and prostrating on it."],[1307,"Delay the noon prayer in the heat, for the intensity of heat is from the scorching breath of Hell."],[1308,"I was walking with Ibn Umar in the Balat when he passed by a man dragging his lower garment. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever drags his clothes out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.' He said: I said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrate this hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah.'"],[1309,"The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal from it? He said: 'He does not complete its bowing or its prostration.'"],[1310,"If Allah withheld rain from my nation for ten years, then sent it down, a group of my nation would become disbelievers because of it, saying: 'It is due to the rising of al-Mijdah.'"],[1311,"Paradise and Hell boasted. Hell said: 'O Lord, tyrants, kings, the great, and nobles will enter me.' Paradise said: 'O Lord, the poor, the weak, and the destitute will enter me.' Allah said to Hell: 'You are My punishment, with which I afflict whomever I will.' And He said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy, which encompasses all things. Each of you will be filled.' As for Hell, its people will be thrown into it, and it will say: 'Is there any more?' until the Blessed and Exalted comes to it and it is constricted, and it says: 'Enough! Enough!' As for Paradise, whatever Allah wills will remain in it, then Allah will create for it a new creation from whatever He wills."],[1312,"There is a tablet before the Most Merciful containing three hundred and fifteen laws. The Most Merciful says: 'By My might and majesty, no servant of Mine who does not associate anything with Me, and has one of them, will enter Paradise.'"],[1313,"Do not accompany anyone but a believer, and let no one eat your food except a pious person."],[1314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Sayyad: 'What do you see?' He said: 'I see a throne on the water with snakes around it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is the throne of Iblis.'"],[1315,"They were sitting reciting and supplicating. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us. He said: When we saw him, we fell silent. He said: 'Were you not doing such and such?' We said: Yes. He said: 'Then do as you were doing.' And he sat with us. Then he said: 'Rejoice, O poor emigrants, for the triumph on the Day of Resurrection over the rich by five hundred years, until the rich will wish that they had been poor or destitute in the world.'"],[1316,"On the day they conquered Awtas, they captured women who had husbands, and some of their men disliked that, so Allah revealed this verse: 'And married women are forbidden to you, except those your right hands possess.'"],[1317,"When three people gather, let one of them lead the prayer, and the most entitled to lead them is the one who recites the most."],[1318,"Visit the sick and follow funerals; they will remind you of the Hereafter."],[1319,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking while standing."],[1320,"I and a companion of mine differed regarding the hantam (jar). We came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said to him: 'Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding the hantam?' He said: 'If you say that, then indeed sometimes during the era of the Messenger of God ﷺ some of us would be present with him and hear from him, while some of us would be occupied with property and would come after the Messenger of God ﷺ had risen, and he would say: \"What did he say?\" So we would inform him of what the Messenger of God ﷺ said. And indeed one day a drinker was brought, and he was struck with hands and beaten with sandals. He said: \"O Messenger of God, by God, I did not drink wine.\" He said: \"Then what did you drink?\" He said: \"I only took some dates and raisins and put them in a gourd of mine.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mixing dates and raisins in the gourd and the pitched vessel.'"],[1321,"\"Whoever of you drinks nabidh, let him drink it as raisins alone, or dates alone, or unripe dates alone.\""],[1322,"The Messenger of God ﷺ observed i'tikaf during the middle ten days of Ramadan, seeking the Night of Decree before it was made clear to him. When it ended, he ordered his tent to be taken down, and it was dismantled. Then it was made clear to him that it was in the last ten days, so he ordered the tent to be rebuilt and it was restored, and he observed i'tikaf during the last ten days. Then he came out to the people and said: 'O people, the Night of Decree was made clear to me, and I came out to inform you of it, but I saw two men disputing with Satan alongside them, and I was made to forget it. So seek it in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.' I said: 'O Abu Sa'id, you know the counting better than us.' He said: 'We are more entitled to that than you. As for the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.' He said: 'You leave what you call the twenty-first, and the one that follows it is the ninth; and you leave what you call the twenty-third, and the one that follows it is the seventh; and you leave what you call the twenty-fifth, and the one that follows it is the fifth.'"],[1323,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri came to a man and said to him: 'Have you read what we have not read, and accompanied what we have not accompanied?' He said: 'I have not read except what you have read, and you have accompanied.' He said: 'Then on what basis do you give fatwas to the people: two dirhams for three, and a dirham for two dirhams?' Abu Sa'id said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Gold for gold, like for like; whatever is more is riba. Silver for silver, like for like; whatever is more is riba.\" He said: 'I heard him later say: \"O God, I repent to You from what I used to give fatwas to the people regarding exchange.\"'"],[1324,"I set out with some men from an 'umrah, and we passed by Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and entered upon him. He said: 'Where do you intend to go?' I said: 'We intend to go to the Mount (al-Tur).' He said: 'And what is the Mount? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The saddles of mounts are not fastened to any mosque in which God is mentioned, except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of Madinah, and the Aqsa Mosque. And prayer is not valid in two hours of the day: after dawn until the sun rises, and after 'asr until the sun sets. And fasting is not valid on two days of the year: the day of breaking the fast of Ramadan, and the day of sacrifice in Dhu al-Hijjah. And no woman travels a journey in Islam except with a husband or a mahram.\""],[1325,"Two men entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about the price of a camel, and he helped them with two dinars. They went out from his presence, and 'Umar met them. They spoke well and thanked what the Messenger of God ﷺ had done for them. 'Umar entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of what they had said. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'But so-and-so, I gave him between ten and a hundred, and he did not say that. Indeed, one of them asks me and goes away with his request, carrying it under his arm, and it is nothing but fire.' 'Umar said: 'You give us what is fire?' He said: 'They refuse except to ask me, and God refuses stinginess for me.'"],[1326,"\"Two traits do not combine in a believer: bad character and miserliness.\""],[1327,"\"Ninety nine serpents are set upon the disbeliever in his grave, biting and stinging him until the Hour rises. If one of them were to breathe upon the earth, no vegetation would grow.\""],[1328,"\"I seek refuge in God from disbelief and debt.\" A man said: 'O Messenger of God, do you equate debt with disbelief?' He said: \"Yes.\""],[1329,"\"When God is pleased with a servant, He praises him with nine kinds of good that he has not done; and when He is angry with a servant, He attributes to him nine kinds of evil that he has not done.\""],[1330,"\"The likeness of the believer and the likeness of faith is like the likeness of a horse at its tethering post: it roams and then returns to its post. Indeed, the believer forgets, then returns to faith. So feed your food to the pious, and bestow your kindness upon the believers.\""],[1331,"\"Charity is not lawful for a rich person, except if he has a poor neighbor and he invites him and he eats with him, or a traveler, or one in the way of God.\""],[1332,"This fire of yours is one part of seventy parts of the Fire of Jahannam; for each part of it is its heat."],[1333,"The dream of the righteous Muslim is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."],[1334,"The mujahid in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah: either He will take him to His forgiveness and mercy, or He will return him with reward and spoils. And the likeness of the mujahid in the path of Allah is like the one who fasts and stands in prayer without slackening until he returns."],[1335,"Avoid the supplications of the wronged. And 'Atiyya said: A man from the people of Khurasan said: Abu Hurayra said: Between it and Allah there is no veil."],[1336,"It will be said to the companion of the Qur'an when he enters Paradise: 'Recite and ascend.' So he recites and ascends by each verse a degree, until he recites the last thing with him."],[1337,"Whoever says when he retires to his bed: 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no god, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining' - three times - 'and I turn to Him in repentance', Allah will expiate his sins even if they were like the foam of the sea."],[1338,"He forbade that nabidh be made in the hantam, the dubba', and the naqir, and that unripe dates be mixed with dried dates, and raisins with dried dates."],[1339,"What is between my grave and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."],[1340,"When one of you intends a matter, let him say: 'O Allah, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek Your power by Your might, and I ask You of Your bounty. For You have power and I have no power; You know and I do not know; and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter - the matter he intends - is good for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair, then decree it for me and make it easy for me, then bless me in it. And if this matter is evil for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, then decree for me the good wherever it may be, then make me pleased with it.' There is no power and no strength except with Allah."],[1341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out on the day of the Eid - the day of Fitr - and pray with the people those two rak'ahs, then give the salam and stand up facing the people while they were seated, and say: 'Give charity, give charity' three times. And the ones who gave charity most were women, with earrings, rings, and things. If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a need, or if he was dispatching an expedition, he would mention it to them; otherwise he would depart."],[1342,"Allah will question the servant on the Day of Resurrection until He says: 'What prevented you, when you saw the wrong, from denouncing it?' Then when Allah has taught the servant his argument, he says: 'My Lord, I trusted in You and feared the people.'"],[1343,"My community will split into two factions, and between them a renegade group will emerge; the one of the two factions that is closer to the truth will kill it."],[1344,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took the banner and shook it, then said: 'Who will take it with its due right?' Then al-Zubayr came and said: 'I will.' He said: 'Step aside.' Then another man stood and said: 'I will.' He said: 'Step aside.' Then another stood and said: 'I will.' He said: 'Step aside.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'By the One who honored the face of Muhammad, I will give it to a man who will not flee with it. Here, take it, O 'Ali.' So he grasped it, then went off until God granted the conquest of Fadak and Khaybar, and he brought back its pressed dates and dried meat."],[1345,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to eat on the day of Fitr before going out, and he would not pray before the prayer, but when he finished he prayed two rak'ahs."],[1346,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us with some truffles in his hand, and said: 'These are from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.'"],[1347,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent 'Alqamah b. Mujazziz on an expedition in which I was among them. We set out until we were at the start of our campaign or on part of the road. A group sought his permission to leave, and he permitted them, and appointed 'Abdullah b. Hudhafah over them. He was one of the companions of Badr, and he had a sense of humor. I was among those who returned with him. While we were on part of the road, we halted at our camp, and the people lit a fire to warm themselves or to prepare something for themselves. Then 'Abdullah said to them: 'Do I not have the right of hearing and obedience over you?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Whatever I command you, will you not do it?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then I adjure you by my right and your obedience to me: throw yourselves into this fire.' He said: Some people stood up and girded themselves, until when he thought they were about to leap into it, he said: 'Restrain yourselves; I was only joking with you.' When they came to the Prophet of God ﷺ, they mentioned that to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever among them commands you to disobedience, do not obey him.'"],[1348,"The entire earth is a place of prostration except the graveyard and the bathhouse."],[1349,"Yajuj and Majuj will be let loose upon the people, as God said: 'And they descend from every elevation.' They will overwhelm the people, and the Muslims will withdraw from them to their cities and fortresses, and gather their livestock to themselves, and drink the waters of the earth until one of them passes by a river and they drink what is in it until they leave it dry, so that those after them pass by that river and say: 'There was once water here.' Until when none of the people remain except one in a fortress or city, one of them says: 'These are the people of the earth; we have finished with them. The people of heaven remain.' Then one of them shakes his spear and hurls it toward the sky, and it returns to him stained with blood, as a trial and tribulation. While they are in that state, God sends worms in their necks like the larvae of locusts that emerge in their necks, and they become dead, no sound heard from them. The Muslims say: 'Is there a man who will risk his life for us to see what has happened to these enemies?' A man among them volunteers for that, expecting to be killed, and finds them dead, one upon another. He calls out: 'O assembly of Muslims, rejoice, for God has sufficed you against your enemy.' So they come out of their cities and fortresses and send their livestock to graze, but there is no pasture for them except their flesh, and they fatten as well as they ever fattened on any vegetation they had eaten."],[1350,"Some people of the Ansar asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and no one asked him but he gave him, until what he had was exhausted. When he had spent all that he had, he said: 'Whatever good I have, I will never withhold it from you. Whoever seeks chastity, God will make him chaste; whoever seeks self-sufficiency, God will enrich him; whoever seeks patience, God will grant him patience. You have not been given a gift better or more ample than patience.'"],[1351,"Regarding His saying: 'On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith' - he said: 'The rising of the sun from its west.'"],[1352,"A Nabataean from Syria arrived with thirty loads of barley and dates in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he set a price, meaning a mudd for a dirham, using the mudd of the Prophet ﷺ, and there was no other food among the people that day. The people complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the high price, so the Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon and said: 'Indeed, I will meet God, Blessed and Exalted, before I give anyone anything from another's wealth without his willing consent.'"],[1353,"Shall I not guide you to something by which God expiates sins and increases good deeds?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Performing ablution thoroughly in difficult circumstances, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer. There is no man among you who leaves his house in a state of purity and prays the congregational prayer with the Muslims, then sits in the mosque waiting for the next prayer, but the angel says: 'O God, forgive him; O God, have mercy on him.' When you stand for prayer, straighten your rows, stand upright, and close the gaps, for I see you from behind my back. When your imam says: 'God is greatest,' say: 'God is greatest.' When he bows, bow, and when he says: 'God hears those who praise Him,' say: 'O God, our Lord, to You be praise.' The best of the rows is the front one, and the worst is the back one; the best of the rows of women is the back one, and the worst is the front one. O assembly of women, when the men prostrate, lower your eyes so that you do not see the private parts of the men, because of the tightness of their waist-wrappers.'"],[1354,"A man killed ninety-nine people, then asked about the most knowledgeable person on earth and was directed to a man. He came to him and said: 'He has killed ninety-nine people; is there any repentance for him?' He said: 'After killing ninety-nine, there is no repentance for you.' So he drew his sword and killed him, completing a hundred with him. Then he remained as long as God willed, then asked about the most knowledgeable person on earth and was directed to a man. He said: 'He has killed a hundred people; is there any repentance for him?' He said: 'Who can stand between you and repentance? Leave this wicked village you are in and go to such-and-such village, and worship your Lord there.' He set out, and his appointed time came on the road. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed. Iblis said: 'He never disobeyed me for even an hour.' The angels of mercy said: 'He came out as a penitent.' Humayd al-Tawil claimed that Bakr narrated to him from Abu Rafi' that God sent an angel, and they gathered to him - the hadith returns to the hadith of Qatadah - he said: 'Look to which of the two towns he was closer, and attach him to its people.' Qatadah said: 'God, Mighty and Majestic, brought the righteous town near, and made the wicked town far from him, and they attached him to its people.'"],[1355,"The most truthful of dreams are in the early morning hours."],[1356,"A man from the Ansar said to his companions: Indeed, by Allah, I used to tell you that once matters became settled for him he would favor others over you. He said: They replied to him harshly. He said: That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He came to them and said things to them that I do not remember. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Were you not those who did not ride horses? He said: Each time he said something to them, they said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. When he saw that they would not answer him back with anything, he said: Will you not say: Your people fought you and we supported you, and your people expelled you and we sheltered you? They said: We will not say that, O Messenger of Allah; you say it. He said: Then he said: O assembly of Ansar, are you not pleased that the people go with the world while you go with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: O assembly of Ansar, are you not pleased that if the people were to take a valley and you were to take a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner circle and my family, my trusted confidants to whom I turn. Pardon their wrongdoers and accept from their doers of good. Abu Sa'id said: Ibn Marjanah, the enemy of Allah, did not know that. Abu Sa'id said: I said to Mu'awiyah: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had..."],[1357,"\"When three people go out on a journey, let one of them lead them in prayer.\""],[1358,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Talib was mentioned in his presence, and he said: Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will be placed in a shallow part of the Fire reaching to his ankles, from which his brain will boil."],[1359,"\"Congregational prayer is superior to the prayer of an individual by twenty-five degrees.\""],[1360,"\"A righteous dream is one of forty-five parts of prophethood.\""],[1361,"\"When one of you sees a dream that he likes, it is from Allah, so let him praise Allah for it and narrate it. And when he sees other than that, something he dislikes, it is from Satan, so let him seek refuge from its evil and not mention it to anyone, for it will not harm him.\""],[1362,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the greeting of peace upon you, so how should we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim."],[1363,"\"He would be affected by janabah at night and want to sleep, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to perform wudu and then sleep.\""],[1364,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to speak about the Dajjal. He said: He will be given power over one soul, he will kill it and then bring it back to life, then he will say: Am I not your Lord? He will say: You have never been more false to me than at this hour. He said: We did not think it was anyone other than Umar b. al-Khattab until he died.\""],[1365,"\"And they therein are grim-faced. He said: The Fire will disfigure them, so his lip will shrink until it reaches the middle of his head, and the other will hang loose until it strikes his navel.\""],[1366,"\"Do not give preference among the prophets.\""],[1367,"A man narrated this hadith to Ibn Umar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he went to him until he entered upon Abu Sa'id while I was with him, and he said: Indeed this..."],[1368,"\"As for the people of the Fire who are its inhabitants, they will neither die in it nor live. But there are people—or as he said—whom their sins—or he said: their faults—strike, so He will cause them to die utterly, until when they become charcoal, permission is granted for intercession, and they are brought in groups, groups, and spread upon the rivers of Paradise. Then it is said: 'O people of Paradise, pour water upon them.' So they sprout just as a seed sprouts in the silt carried by a torrent.'\" A man from the people said at that moment: \"It is as though the Messenger of God ﷺ was in the desert.\""],[1369,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas about money exchange. He said: \"Hand to hand.\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"No harm.\" He said: Then I met Abu Sa'id and told him that I asked Ibn 'Abbas about money exchange, and he said: \"No harm in it.\" He said: \"Did he say that? Indeed, we shall write to him so he will not give you that ruling.\" He said: \"By God, one of the young servants of the Messenger of God ﷺ brought some dates, and he found them strange. He said: 'It is as though this is not from the dates of our land?' He said: 'In this year's dates there was something, so I took this and added some increase.' He said: 'You have doubled, you have dealt in usury. Do not approach this. If you have any doubt about your dates, sell them, then buy the dates you want.'\""],[1370,"\"We used to raid with the Messenger of God ﷺ during Ramadan. Among us were those fasting and among us those breaking the fast. The fasting one did not find fault with the one breaking the fast, nor did the one breaking the fast find fault with the fasting one. They held that whoever found strength and fasted, that was good, and they held that whoever found weakness and broke the fast, that was also good.\""],[1371,"\"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying wearing a cloth draped over one shoulder.\""],[1372,"A man said: \"O Messenger of God, blessed is the one who saw you and believed in you.\" He said: \"Blessed is the one who saw me and believed in me. Then blessed, then blessed, then blessed is the one who believed in me and did not see me.\" A man said to him: \"And what is Tuba?\" He said: \"A tree in Paradise, a journey of a hundred years, from the sleeves of which the garments of the people of Paradise come out.\""],[1373,"A man said: \"What is like molten brass?\" He said: \"Like the dregs of oil, and when it is brought near him, the skin of his face falls into it.\""],[1374,"\"Remember God with much remembrance, until they say: 'He is mad.'\""],[1375,"\"If a mountain were struck with an iron rod, it would crumble, then return as it was.\""],[1376,"\"If one of you were to work upon a solid rock that has no door or window, his deed would surely come out to the people, whatever it may be.\""],[1377,"\"Every letter in the Qur'an in which qunut is mentioned is obedience.\""],[1378,"\"Gabriel came to me and said: 'My Lord and your Lord says: How did I exalt your mention?' He said: 'God knows best.' He said: 'When I am mentioned, you are mentioned with Me.'\""],[1379,"\"If a bucket of ghasq were poured into this world, it would make the people of this world stink.\""],[1380,"\"The dust consumes everything of the human being except the coccyx.\" It was said: \"And what is it like, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Like a mustard seed; from it they will grow.\""],[1381,"Wayl: a valley in Hell into which the disbeliever falls for forty autumns before reaching its bottom. And he said: al-Sa'ud: a mountain of fire which he climbs for seventy autumns, then falls down with it like that, in it forever."],[1382,"\"Increase in the everlasting righteous deeds.\" It was said: \"And what are they, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"The milla.\" It was said: \"And what is it, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"The tahlil, the takbir, the tasbih, and praise be to God, and there is no might nor power except with God.\""],[1383,"\"It will be appointed for the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection a duration of fifty thousand years, as he did not work for God in this world. And indeed the disbeliever will see Hell and think that its encounter is from a distance of forty years.\""],[1384,"\"Indeed a man will recline in Paradise for a distance of seventy years before turning over. Then a woman will come to him and strike him on his shoulders, and he will look at his face in her cheek, clearer than a mirror. And indeed the least pearl upon her will illuminate what is between the east and the west. She will greet them, and he will return the greeting and ask her: 'Who are you?' She will say: 'I am the increase.' And indeed upon her will be seventy garments, the least of which is like the anemone of Tuba, and his sight will penetrate them until he sees the marrow of her shin from behind that. And indeed upon them will be crowns; the least pearl in them will illuminate what is between the east and the west.\""],[1385,"\"Winter is the believer's spring.\""],[1386,"\"The disbeliever's seat in the Fire is three days, each of his molars is like Uhud, his thigh is like Warqan, and his skin apart from his flesh and bones is forty cubits.\""],[1387,"\"If an iron hook were placed on the earth and the two heavy ones [humans and jinn] gathered upon it, they could not lift it from the earth.\""],[1388,"\"The pavilion of the Fire has four walls; between each wall is the like of forty years.\""],[1389,"It was said: \"O Messenger of God, a day whose measure is fifty thousand years—how long this is!\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it will certainly be lightened for the believer until it becomes lighter for him than an obligatory prayer that he performs in this world.\""],[1390,"\"A people will certainly remember God in this world upon spread-out beds; He will admit them to the highest gardens.\""],[1391,"\"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the disbeliever will be made to recognize his deed, but he will deny and dispute. It will be said: 'These are your neighbors who testify against you.' He will say: 'They lie.' He will say: 'Your family, your clan?' He will say: 'They lie.' He will say: 'Swear.' They will swear. Then God will silence them and their tongues will testify. Then He will admit them to the Fire.\""],[1392,"Moses said: \"O Lord, teach me something by which I remember You and call upon You.\" He said: \"Say, O Moses: 'There is no god but Allah.'\" He said: \"All Your servants say this.\" He said: \"Say: 'There is no god but Allah.'\" He said: \"There is no god but You; I want something that You single me out with.\" He said: \"O Moses, if the seven heavens and their inhabitants other than Me, and the seven earths, were on one side of a scale, and 'There is no god but Allah' were on the other side, the latter would outweigh them.\""],[1393,"Gatherings are of three types: sound, profitable, and ruinous."],[1394,"He said: \"And on raised couches\" (Qur'an 56:34). He said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, its elevation is as the distance between the heaven and the earth, and the distance between the heaven and the earth is a journey of five hundred years.\""],[1395,"Calling out goods for sale is forbidden."],[1396,"Perhaps a man earns wealth from lawful means and feeds himself, and a man who has wealth on which charity is due. He said: \"O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, and send prayers upon the believing men and women and the Muslim men and women, for that is a purification for him.\""],[1397,"Paradise has one hundred levels; if all creatures were to gather in one of them, it would accommodate them."],[1398,"Satan said: \"By Your might, O Lord, I will never cease leading Your servants astray as long as their souls are in their bodies.\" The Lord said: \"By My might and majesty, I will never cease forgiving them as long as they seek My forgiveness.\""],[1399,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, even two sheep will contend with each other over what they butted heads for."],[1400,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which act of worship is highest in degree with Allah on the Day of Resurrection?\" He said: \"Those who remember Allah much.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about the one who fights in the cause of Allah?\" He said: \"Even if he strikes the disbelievers and polytheists with his sword until it breaks and is dyed with blood, the one who remembers Allah is superior to him.\""],[1401,"A man migrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Yemen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"You have abandoned polytheism, but it is jihad. Are your parents in Yemen?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Did they permit you?\" He said: \"No.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Return to your parents and ask their permission. If they do, then fight; otherwise, be dutiful to them.\""],[1402,"The Lord will say on the Day of Resurrection: \"Today the people of the gathering will know who the people of honor are.\" It was asked: \"Who are the people of honor?\" He said: \"Those who remember Allah in the mosques.\""],[1403,"The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank will have eighty thousand servants and seventy-two wives, and a dome of pearl, ruby, and chrysolite will be erected for him, as wide as the distance between al-Jabiyah and San'a'."],[1404,"Whoever dies from the people of this world, young or old, will be returned to sixty years of age in Paradise; they will never exceed it. And likewise the people of the Fire."],[1405,"A man will certainly take his father by the hand on the Day of Resurrection, and the Fire will certainly cut him off (i.e., prevent him), wanting to enter him into Paradise. It will be called out: \"Paradise is not entered by a polytheist. Indeed, Allah has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist.\" He will say: \"My Lord, my father; my Lord, my father; my Lord, my father.\" He (the Prophet) said: \"Then he will be transformed into an ugly form and a stinking odor, and he will leave him.\""],[1406,"He forbade continuous fasting (wisal). It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, why do you do it?\" He said: \"I am not like any of you. I am fed and given drink.\""],[1407,"When one of you finishes his prayer and then returns to his house, let him pray (there) and let him assign a portion of his prayer to his house, for Allah will make good from his prayer in his house."],[1408,"When this verse was revealed: 'And give the relative his due' (17:26), the Prophet ﷺ called Fatimah and gave her Fadak."],[1409,"The Dajjal will emerge, and a man from the Muslims will head toward him. The outposts—the outposts of the Dajjal—will meet him. They will say to him: 'Where are you heading?' He will say: 'I am heading to this one who has emerged.' They will say to him: 'Do you not believe in our lord?' He said: He will say: 'I do not think—I believe—it is true (i.e., I do not think he is truly God).' He said: They will say: 'Kill him.' He said: Then some of them will say to others: 'Has not your lord forbidden you to kill anyone without his permission?' He said: So they will take him to the Dajjal. He said: When the believer sees him, he will say: 'O people, this is the Dajjal whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned.' He said: The Dajjal will order that he be stretched out. He said: He will say: 'Take him and stretch him out.' He said: So he will be stretched out. He said: His back and belly will be struck with blows. He said: He will say to him: 'Will you not believe in me?' He said: He will say: 'You are the lying Messiah.' He said: So he will order that he be sawn with a saw from the top of his head until he is split between his legs. He said: Then the Dajjal will walk between the two pieces. He said: Then he will say: 'Arise,' and he will stand upright. He said: He will say to him: 'Will you not believe in me?' He said: He will say to him: 'I have only increased in insight concerning you.' He said: Then he will say: 'O people, he will not do to anyone else what he has done to me.' He said: Then the Dajjal will take him to slaughter him, and what is between his chin and his collarbone will be made copper, so he will not be able to find a way to him. He said: So he will take him by his hands and feet and throw him, and the people will think that he threw him into the Fire, but he was only thrown into Paradise. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is the greatest of people in martyrdom before the Lord of the worlds.'"],[1410,"It is not for the believer to humiliate himself. It was said: 'And what is his humiliating himself?' He said: 'He exposes himself to trials that he cannot bear.' It was said: 'O Abu Sa'id, what about Yazid al-Dabbi and his speaking in prayer?' He said: 'Indeed, he did not leave prison until he regretted.' Al-Mu'alla said: So I got up from the gathering of al-Hasan and came to Yazid and said: 'O Abu Mawdud, while al-Hasan and I were discussing, I brought up your matter.' He said: 'Wait, O Abu al-Hasan.' He said: I said: 'I have done so.' He said: 'What did al-Hasan say?' I said: 'He said: Indeed, he did not leave prison until he regretted his statement.' Yazid said: 'I did not regret my statement. By Allah, I stood in a position in which I risked my own life.' Yazid said: So I came to al-Hasan and said: 'O Abu Sa'id, we have been overcome in everything; will we be overcome in our prayer?' He said: 'O servant of Allah, you have done nothing; you are exposing yourself to them.' Then I came to him, and he said to me the like of his statement. He said: So I stood on Friday in the mosque while al-Hakam b. Ayyub was giving the khutbah, and I said: 'May Allah have mercy on you, (the) prayer.' He said: When I said that, men surrounded me, passing me from one to another. They took hold of my beard and the collar of my garment, and they began striking my belly with the scabbards of their swords. He said: They took me toward the maqsurah, and I had not reached it when I thought they would kill me before it. He said: The door of the maqsurah was opened for me. He said: I entered and stood before al-Hakam while he was silent. He said: 'Are you insane?' He said: And we were not in prayer. I said: 'May Allah set the amir right, is there any speech better than the Book of Allah?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'May Allah set the amir right. Do you think that if a man opened a mushaf and read it from morning until night, would that suffice him from his prayer?' He said: 'By Allah, I think you are insane.' He said: And Anas b. Malik was sitting under his pulpit, silent. I said: 'O Anas, O Abu Hamzah, I adjure you by Allah, for you served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and accompanied him. Did I say what is right or what is wrong? Did I say truth or falsehood?' He said: By Allah, he did not answer me with a single word. Al-Hakam b. Ayyub said to him: 'O Anas.' He said: He said: 'At your service, may Allah set you right.' He said: And the time of prayer had passed. He said: A portion of the sun remained. He said: 'Detain him.' Yazid said: I swear to you, O Abu al-Hasan—meaning to al-Mu'alla—what I met from my companions was harder on me than my standing. Some of them said: 'A show-off.' Others said: 'Insane.' He said: Al-Hakam wrote to al-Hajjaj: 'A man from Banu Dabba stood on Friday and said: \"(The) prayer,\" while I was giving the khutbah, and just witnesses have testified before me that he is insane.' Al-Hajjaj wrote to him: 'If the just witnesses have testified that he is insane, then let him go; otherwise, cut off his hands and feet, put out his eyes, and crucify him.' He said: So they testified before al-Hakam that I was insane, and he released me. Al-Mu'alla said: From Yazid al-Dabbi: A brother of ours died, and we followed his funeral and prayed over him. When he was buried, I withdrew with a group, and we remembered Allah and remembered our return. While we were doing that, we saw the forelocks of horses and spears. When my companions saw that, they got up and left me alone. Al-Hakam came and stood over me and said: 'What were you doing?' I said: 'May Allah set the amir right, a companion of ours died, and we prayed over him and he was buried. We sat remembering our Lord and remembering our return and what he has come to.' He said: 'What prevented you from fleeing as they fled?' I said: 'May Allah set the amir right, I am far removed from that and safer for the amir than to flee.' He said: Al-Hakam was silent. Then Abd al-Malik b. al-Muhallab, who was in charge of his police, said: 'Do you know who this is?' He said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'The one who spoke on Friday.' He said: Al-Hakam became angry and said: 'Indeed you are bold. Seize him.' He said: So I was seized, and he beat me with four hundred lashes. I did not know when he left me because of the severity of the beating. He said: He sent me to Wasit, and I was in the dungeon of al-Hajjaj until al-Hajjaj died. Here ends the musnad of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."],[1411,"I met in Makkah a man from the people of Ascalon called Abu al-Hasan. He narrated to me from Abu Ja'far b. Muhammad b. Rukanah, from his father, that he wrestled with the Prophet ﷺ. Rukanah said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'The difference between us and the polytheists is the turbans over the caps.'"],[1412,"When he sent out a raiding party or an army, he would enjoin its commander to fear Allah regarding himself and enjoin him to treat the Muslims with him well. Then he would say: 'Fight in the name of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. When you meet your enemy from the polytheists, call them to Islam. If they accept Islam, accept from them and refrain from them. Then call them to move from their land to the land of the Muslims. If they do so, accept from them; otherwise, inform them that they are like the Bedouin Muslims: the judgment of Allah that applies to the Muslims applies to them, and they have no share in the fay' or the spoils. If they refuse that, call them to pay the jizyah. If they do so, accept from them and refrain from them. If you besiege a fortress or a city, and they ask you to grant them the judgment of Allah, do not grant them that, for you do not know what the judgment of Allah is. Instead, grant them your own judgment, then judge among them as you see fit. If you besiege a castle, do not grant them the protection of Allah or the protection of His Messenger; rather, grant them your own protection and the protection of your fathers, for it is less serious for you to violate your own protection and the protection of your fathers.'"],[1413,"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[1414,"When the Prophet ﷺ overcame a people, he liked to stay in their open area for three (days)."],[1415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and Umrah."],[1416,"The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams, and at the first slaughter he said: 'On behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,' and at the second slaughter he said: 'On behalf of those of my community who believed in me and affirmed me.'"],[1417,"The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams, and at the first slaughter he said: 'On behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,' and at the second slaughter he said: 'On behalf of those of my community who believed in me and affirmed me.'"],[1418,"The Prophet ﷺ combined the Hajj and the Umrah."],[1419,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ during the illness in which he died, and he said: 'Convey peace to your people, for, as far as I know, they are chaste and patient.'"],[1420,"We were sitting in open areas talking, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and stood over us and said: 'What is it with you and sitting in elevated places? Avoid sitting in elevated places.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we sat for no harmful purpose; we sat to remind each other and talk.' He said: 'If you must, then give them their due.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is their due?' He said: 'Lowering the gaze, returning the greeting, and good speech.'"],[1421,"I raised my head on the day of Uhud and began to look, and there was not one among them except that he was swaying from drowsiness beneath his shield."],[1422,"From al-Zubayr, the like of it, and he recited: 'Then after the distress, He sent down upon you security, a slumber overcoming a party.'"],[1423,"The sky rained hail, and Abu Talhah said to us while we were boys: 'Hand me some of that hail, O Anas.' He began eating it while fasting. I said: 'Are you not fasting?' He said: 'Indeed I am; this is neither food nor drink. It is only a blessing from the sky with which we purify our stomachs.' Anas said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: 'Take from your uncle.'"],[1424,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while his face was radiant, rejoicing, and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you are indeed in a state unlike any I have seen you in before.' He said: 'What would prevent me? Jibril came to me and said: Give your community glad tidings: whoever sends one prayer upon you, Allah records for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, raises him ten degrees, and Allah returns to him the like of what he said, and it will be presented to him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1425,"I entered the mosque and recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I went out until I came to Umm Sulaym, who was the mother of Anas b. Malik; she had been married to Malik, the father of Anas b. Malik. I said: 'O Umm Sulaym, I recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; do you have anything?' She said: 'I have something,' and she gestured with her hand. I said: 'Prepare it well.' She sent Anas to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I said: 'Whisper to him in his ear and invite him.' When Anas came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Here is a man who has come with good.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Did your father send you to invite us, O my son?' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: 'Go in the name of Allah.' Anas hurried back until he came to Abu Talhah and said: 'Here is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming to you with the people.' So I went out until I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the door, at the top of the step, and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what have you done to us? I only recognized hunger in your face, so we prepared something for you to eat.' He said: 'Enter and rejoice.' He took it and gathered it in the bowl with his hand, then arranged it, and said: 'Is there any?' as if he meant condiment. They brought him a small skin containing something, or containing nothing, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ worked it with his hand, and ghee poured from it. Then he said: 'Let ten enter upon me at a time.' They all ate and were satisfied, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning what remained: 'Eat, you and your families.' So they ate and were satisfied."],[1426,"O youth of Quraysh, do not commit fornication. Whoever preserves his youth will have Paradise."],[1427,"The sword fell from my hand on the day of Badr because of the drowsiness that overcame us. Allah says: 'When He was covering you with drowsiness as a security from Him.'"],[1428,"Perform ablution from what the fire has altered."],[1429,"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[1430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered on the day of Badr that twenty-four men from the leaders of Quraysh be thrown into a foul, stinking pit of the pits of Badr. When he was victorious over a people, he liked to stay in their courtyard for three nights. When it was the third day at Badr, he ordered his riding camel to be brought, and its saddle was fastened on it. Then he walked, and his companions followed him. They said: We do not think he is going except to relieve himself. Until he stood at the edge of the well, and he began calling them by their names and their fathers' names: O so-and-so son of so-and-so, O so-and-so son of so-and-so, would it please you that you had obeyed Allah and His Messenger? We have found what our Lord promised us to be true. Have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? He said: Umar b. al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you speak to bodies that have no souls? The Prophet ﷺ said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, you are not more able to hear what I say than they are. Qatadah said: Allah brought them to life so that He could make them hear rebuke, belittlement, vengeance, regret, and remorse."],[1431,"The angels do not enter a house in which there are images or a dog. Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani said to Abu Talhah: Let us go to A'ishah and ask her about this. So they came to A'ishah and asked her. She said: As for this, I do not remember it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a military expedition of his, and I waited for his return. I covered the canopy of the house with a patterned cloth. When he entered, I met him and took his hand, and I said: Praise be to Allah who granted you victory, honored you, and ennobled you. He looked at it, and I saw displeasure in his face."],[1432,"If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, people from the people of Persia would attain it."],[1433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to give the Zakat al-Fitr before the zakat was revealed. When the zakat was revealed, he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and we still do it."],[1434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, so we prepared water for him and he bathed. Then we brought him a wars-dyed wrap, and he wrapped himself in it. It is as if I am looking at the trace of the wars on the folds of his stomach."],[1435,"Whoever deliberately tells a lie about me, let him take his place in a house in Hell, or a resting place in Hell. Indeed, whoever drinks wine will come on the Day of Resurrection thirsty, and every intoxicant is wine, and beware of the ghubayra'."],[1436,"Sahl b. Hunayf and Qays b. Sa'd were sitting at al-Qadisiyyah when a funeral procession passed by them, and they stood up. It was said to them: It is only one of the people of the land. They said: A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ and he stood up. It was said: It is the funeral of a disbeliever. He said: Is it not a soul?"],[1437,"If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from the sons of Persia would attain it."],[1438,"Whoever traces his lineage to nine disbelieving forefathers, seeking through them honor and might, he is their tenth in the Fire."],[1439,"I went out with Uthman b. Hunayf to visit Abu Talhah during an illness of his. He said: We entered upon him, and underneath him on his bed was a patterned cloth with images of figures. He said: Remove this from under me. Uthman said to him: Did you not hear, O Abu Talhah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say when he prohibited images: 'Except a design in a garment, or a garment with a design'? He said: Yes, but it is more pleasant for my soul that it not be placed under me."],[1440,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Khaybar, he passed by a tree on which the polytheists used to hang their weapons, called Dhat Anwat. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat.\" He said, \"Allah is greatest! This is as the people of Musa said to Musa: 'Make for us a god as they have gods.' You will surely follow the ways of those who came before you.\""],[1441,"He heard Abu Waqid al-Laythi, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while prayer was mentioned in his presence, say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer upon the people and the most constant of it upon himself.\""],[1442,"Umar went out on the day of Eid and asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi: \"With what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite on this day?\" He said: \"With Qaf and Iqtarabat.\""],[1443,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to his wives in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"This, then the appearance of the mats.\""],[1444,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, three persons passed by. One of them came and found a gap in the circle and sat down. Another sat behind them, and the third went away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you about these persons?\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"As for the one who came and sat, he sought refuge, so Allah sheltered him. As for the one who sat behind you, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him. As for the one who went away, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him.\""],[1445,"Umar went out on the day of Eid and asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi: \"With what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite on this day?\" He said: \"With Qaf and Iqtarabat.\""],[1446,"Umar asked me: \"With what did the Prophet of Allah ﷺ recite on the two Eids?\" I said: \"With Iqtarabat al-Sa'ah wa inshaqqa al-Qamar, and Qaf wa al-Qur'an al-Majid.\""],[1447,"He was the lightest of people in prayer and the most constant of it upon himself."],[1448,"I entered upon Abu Waqid al-Laythi in Makkah during the illness in which he died, and I heard him say, or he said to me: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer and the most constant of it upon himself.\""],[1449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while the people were cutting the humps of camels and cutting the fat tails of sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is dead meat.\""],[1450,"The sun rises with a horn of Satan, and when it rises high, he leaves it; when it is at its zenith, he joins it; when it declines, he leaves it; when it approaches setting, he joins it; when it sets, he leaves it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade prayer during those times."],[1451,"I am competing with you for the nations, so do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks."],[1452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a fine she-camel among the camels of zakat, and he said: May Allah fight the owner of this she-camel. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I took it back with two camels from the outskirts of the camels. He said: Then yes, indeed."],[1453,"I will precede you to the Hawd, and I will vie in numbers with you against the nations, so do not fight one another after me."],[1454,"Abu Bakr narrated to us; Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama narrated to us; they said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[1455,"My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he wiped my head and supplicated for provision for me."],[1456,"I prayed Fajr behind the Prophet ﷺ, and I heard him reciting: 'Nay, I swear by the retreating stars, the runners, the sinkers.' He said: And none of us would bend his back until he was upright in prostration."],[1457,"I sold a house of mine and land in Madinah. My brother Sa'id b. Hurayth said to me: Withhold from it as much as you can, and do not spend any of it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever sells a house or real estate, it is likely that he will not be blessed in it unless he puts it into the like of it. 'Amr said: So I bought with part of its price this house of mine, meaning the house of 'Amr b. Hurayth."],[1458,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a black turban."],[1459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us wearing a black turban."],[1460,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting in Fajr: 'By the night when it darkens.'"],[1461,"The Prophet ﷺ would sometimes touch his beard in prayer."],[1462,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and he recited, and it was as if I could hear his voice saying: 'Nay, I swear by the retreating stars, the runners, the sinkers.' Muhammad b. Yazid said in his hadith: And my mother or my father took me to him, and he supplicated for provision for me."],[1463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marked out for me a house in Madinah with a bow, and said: Shall I give you more?"],[1464,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in two patched sandals."],[1465,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in two patched sandals."],[1466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Abd Allah b. Ja'far while he was selling with the boys or the children, and he said: 'O Allah, bless him in his sale,' or he said: 'in his transaction.'"],[1467,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the morning prayer: 'By the night when it darkens' or he said: 'When the sun is folded up.'"],[1468,"I prayed the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ and he recited: 'When the sun is folded up.' It is as if I hear his voice saying: 'So I swear by the retreating stars, the runners, the hidden ones.' And he said: 'My mother and father took me to him and he supplicated for me for provision.'"],[1469,"Truffles are of the manna, and their water is a healing for the eye."],[1470,"I came to Amr b. Hurayth to rent a house in his dwelling from him, and he said: 'Rent it, for it is blessed for whoever owns it, blessed for whoever lives in it.' I said: 'From what is that?' He said: 'I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after a camel had been slaughtered and he had ordered its distribution. He said to the one distributing it: \"Give Amr a portion of it.\" But he did not give me anything and neglected me. The next day, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and before him were dirhams. He said: \"Did you take the portion I ordered for you?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, he did not give me anything.\" He said: So he took a handful of dirhams and gave them to me. I brought them to my mother and said: \"Take these dirhams; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took them with his hand and gave them to me. Keep them until we see in what to put them.\" Then time passed until I bought this house. My mother said: \"When you want to pay its price, do not pay until you call me so that I may supplicate for you for blessing.\" So I called her when I had prepared it, and she said to me: \"Take these dirhams.\" So I scattered them among it, then mixed them with it, and she said: \"Take it.\""],[1471,"Whatever you lighten for your servant of his work, its reward is in your scales."],[1472,"You will come upon a people with curly hair, so treat them well, for they are strength for you and a means to reach your enemy by Allah's permission, meaning the Copts of Egypt."],[1473,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs, when the people were most secure and most numerous."],[1474,"Give charity, for it is near that a man will go out with his charity and not find anyone to accept it."],[1475,"The arrogant boaster and the one who is coarse and self-important will not enter Paradise."],[1476,"Shall I not guide you to the people of Paradise? Every weak, humble person who, if he were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill it for him; and the people of the Fire are every arrogant, coarse person."],[1477,"I performed Hajj in the pre-Islamic period, and there was a man circumambulating the House while reciting rajaz: 'Return to me my rider Muhammad; return him to me and do me a favor.' I said: 'Who is this, meaning?' They said: 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim. Some camels of his went astray, so he sent his son's son in search of them. He was detained from him, and he never sent him on an errand except that he came back with it fulfilled.' He said: 'It was not long before the Prophet ﷺ came with the camels. He said: \"O my son, I have grieved for you this time with a grief that will never leave me.\""],[1478,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication of seeking refuge that I may use.' He took my hand and said: 'Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, from the evil of my hearing, from the evil of my sight, from the evil of my heart, from the evil of my tongue, and from the evil of my private part.'"],[1479,"I was sitting with Yazid b. Abi Muslim during the days of al-Hajjaj while he was torturing people. He mentioned a man in prison, and he sent for him with rage and anger. So the man was brought, and when he stood before him, I saw the man move his lips with something I could not hear. Then he raised his head to him and said: 'Release him,' or he said: 'Return him.' He said: 'I went to the man and said: \"I witnessed this when he sent for you with rage and anger, and I had no doubt that he would harm you. When you stood before him, I saw you move your lips with something I could not hear, and he ordered concerning you what you see. What did you say?\" He said: \"I said: O Allah, I ask You by Your power with which You hold the seven heavens, that some of them fall upon others, to suffice me against him.\""],[1480,"Is any of you unable to recite in a night: 'Say: He is Allah, the One'? For it is equal to the entire Quran."],[1481,"I was a boy throwing stones at the date-palms of the Ansar. It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Here is a boy throwing stones at our date-palms,' or he said: 'throwing stones at the date-palms.' He said: 'I was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O boy, do not throw stones at the date-palms.\" I said: \"I eat [from them].\" He said: \"Do not throw stones at the date-palms; eat what falls.\" He said: 'And he wiped his head and said: \"O Allah, fill his belly.\""],[1482,"I went on the summer expedition with my father during the time of Abd al-Malik b. Marwan, and Abdullah b. Abd al-Malik was over us. We encamped at the fortress of Sinan, and the people cramped the campsites and cut off the roads. My father stood among the people and said: 'O people, I went on such-and-such expedition with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, and the people cramped the campsites and cut off the roads. So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ sent a caller who announced among the people: \"Whoever cramps a campsite or cuts off a road, there is no jihad for him.\""],[1483,"Whoever gives up wearing fine clothing while able to do so out of humility before Allah, Allah will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all creatures and let him choose whichever of the garments of faith he wishes to wear."],[1484,"Whoever gives for Allah, withholds for Allah, loves for Allah, hates for Allah, and marries for Allah, has completed his faith."],[1485,"Whoever fasts a day voluntarily in the path of Allah, outside Ramadan, will be distanced from the Fire by a hundred years' journey of a well-trained, swift horse."],[1486,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer and then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[1487,"Whoever eats food and says: 'Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided it for me without any strength or power from me,' his previous sins will be forgiven. And whoever wears a garment and says: 'Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided it for me without any strength or power from me,' his previous sins will be forgiven."],[1488,"Whoever recites a thousand verses in the way of Allah, will be written on the Day of Resurrection with the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and excellent are those as companions, if Allah wills."],[1489,"Whoever guards behind the Muslims in the way of Allah voluntarily, not compelled by a ruler, will not see the Fire with his own eye except for the fulfillment of the oath; for indeed Allah, glory be to Him, no partner has He, says: 'And there is none of you but will pass over it.'"],[1490,"Whoever steps over people on Friday has taken a bridge to Hell."],[1491,"He forbade sitting with knees drawn up on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon."],[1492,"Whoever recites the Qur'an and acts upon what is in it, his parents will be clothed with a crown on the Day of Resurrection, whose light is better than the light of the sun in the houses of the people of this world if it were among them. So what do you think of the one who acts upon it himself?"],[1493,"Whoever is dutiful to his parents, glad tidings to him; Allah increases his lifespan."],[1494,"Whoever prays the dawn prayer, then remains sitting remembering Allah until the sun rises, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[1495,"He forbade sitting with knees drawn up on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon."],[1496,"Whoever suppresses anger while he is able to vent it, Allah will call him on the heads of witnesses on the Day of Resurrection and let him choose whichever of the houris he wishes."],[1497,"Whoever eats food and then says, 'Praise be to Allah who fed me this food and provided it to me without any power or strength from me,' his past sins will be forgiven. And whoever wears a garment and says, 'Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided it to me without any power or strength from me,' his past sins will be forgiven."],[1498,"Whoever gives up clothing while he is able to afford it out of humility to Allah, Allah will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all creatures and let him choose from the garments of faith, wearing whichever he wishes."],[1499,"Whoever gives for Allah, withholds for Allah, loves for Allah, hates for Allah, and marries for Allah, has perfected his faith."],[1500,"That his grandfather 'Arfajah had his nose injured in the Jahiliyyah on the day of al-Kulab, so he acquired a nose made of silver, but it became foul for him. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he ordered him to acquire a nose made of gold."],[1501,"The nose of 'Arfajah was injured on the day of al-Kulab, so he acquired a nose made of silver, but it became foul for him. The Prophet ﷺ ordered him to acquire a nose made of gold."],[1502,"\"O Messenger of God, is the slaughter only from the throat or the upper chest?\" He said: \"If you had stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed for you.\" 2 - (1504) - Hawtharah added: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed for you.\""],[1503,"\"O Messenger of God, is the slaughter only from the throat or the upper chest?\" He said: \"If you had stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed for you.\" 2 - (1504) - Hawtharah added: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed for you.\""],[1504,"I arrived in Madinah and met 'Itban b. Malik. I said: \"A hadith reached me from you.\" He said: \"Something affected my eyesight, so I sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'I would love for you to come to me and pray in my house, so that I may take it as a place of prayer.'\" He said: \"The Prophet ﷺ came to me with whomever God willed of his companions. He entered upon me and prayed in my house while his companions conversed among themselves. Then they attributed the bulk and gravity of that to Malik b. Dukhshum.\" He said: \"They wished that he would supplicate against him and he would perish; they wished that some illness would afflict him. The Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer and said: 'Does he not testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?' They said: 'He says that, but what is in his heart?' He said: 'No one testifies that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God and then enters the Fire, or the Fire consumes him.'\" He said: \"This hadith pleased me, so I said to my son: 'Write it down,' and he wrote it.\""],[1505,"And his companions conversed among themselves and mentioned what they encountered from the hypocrites. Then they attributed the bulk of that to Malik b. Dukhshum. He said: \"They wished that he would supplicate against him, urging him to do so. The Messenger of God finished.\""],[1506,"I met 'Itban after that, and he narrated to me a hadith that pleased me. I said to my son: \"Write it down,\" and he wrote it. He said: \"His eyesight had gone.\" He said: \"I said: 'O Prophet of God, would you come to me and pray with me in a place I would take as a mosque?'\" He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ came and began to pray, and his companions began to converse.\" He said: \"They mentioned what they encountered from the hypocrites in the way of harm, and they placed the bulk of that upon Malik b. al-Dukhshum. It pleased them to urge the Prophet ﷺ to supplicate against him so that he would perish. They said: 'O Prophet of God, of his affair is such and such.'\" He said: \"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: 'Does he not testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God?' They said: 'He only says that with his tongue, and there is no reality to it in his heart.'\" He said: \"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: 'No one testifies that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, and then God will enter him into the Fire'—or he said: 'and then the Fire will consume him—ever.'\""],[1507,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon while he was on a she-camel, and I was beneath its neck, and it was chewing its cud, and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders. He said: \"O people, God has given every possessor of a right his right. So there is no bequest for an heir; the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or affiliates himself with other than his patrons out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all the people. God will not accept from him any turning away or any just compensation.\""],[1508,"And he had prayed toward both qiblahs together. He said: \"I was in my house when a caller called at the door: 'The Prophet ﷺ has changed the qiblah.' I bear witness to our imam, the men, the women, and the boys that they prayed toward this direction—meaning Jerusalem—and toward this direction, meaning the Ka'bah.\""],[1509,"That a man died and left three hundred dirhams and dependents. He said: \"I wanted to spend it on his dependents, but the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Your brother is detained by his debt, so pay it off on his behalf.' So he paid it off on his behalf. Then he said: 'O Messenger of God, I have paid it off on his behalf except for a woman who claimed two dinars, and she has no proof.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Give it to her, for she is truthful.'\""],[1510,"'Abd Allah b. Sa'd used to go out to his companions in Tustar to visit them. He would stay on the day of his arrival and the second day, and leave on the third. They would say to him: \"If only you would stay.\" He would say: \"I heard my father say: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me,' or 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid residency in the land of the enemy. Whoever resides in the land of the kharaj has become a resident there, so I dislike to stay.'\""],[1511,"That his father died and left three hundred dirhams, dependents, and a debt. I wanted to spend it on his dependents, but the Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'Your father is detained by his debt, so pay it off on his behalf.' I said: 'May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of God. I have paid off everything on his behalf except for a woman who claimed two dinars, and she has no proof.' He said: 'Give it to her, for she is truthful.' So I gave it to her."],[1512,"Ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us: 'Abbad b. Musa narrated to me, from Hammad b. Salamah, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, with its like."],[1513,"Do not sit on graves, and do not pray towards them."],[1514,"The firmly-rooted in mud, the feeders in times of famine. Whoever sells them, its price is like ashes on a high place, upon which a wind blew and scattered it."],[1515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: O 'Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership."],[1516,"O Miqdad, take this and milk it, then divide it into four parts: a part for me, a part for you, and a part for your two companions. I used to do that. Then one night, I drank my part, and my two companions drank their parts, and I placed the Prophet's ﷺ part in the wooden cup and covered it. The Prophet ﷺ was delayed, and my self said to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been invited by a household in Madinah, and he had dinner with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ does not need this milk. My self kept turning me until I went to the cup and drank what was in it. When it settled in my stomach, I was seized by what was old and what was new. My self said to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ will come hungry and thirsty, and he will lift the cup and find nothing in it, and he will supplicate against you. So I covered myself as if I were asleep, and I had no sleep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and greeted with a greeting that the awake could hear and which did not wake the sleeping. When he did not see anything in the cup, he raised his head to the sky and said: O Allah, feed the one who fed us and give drink to the one who gave us drink. I seized the opportunity of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I took the knife, intending to slaughter one of those goats and feed him. I struck with my hand and it fell upon her udder, and behold she was full of milk. Then I looked at all of them, and behold they were all full of milk. I milked into the cup until it was full, then I came to him smiling. He said: Ah, some of your misdeeds, O Miqdad. I said: O Messenger of Allah, drink, then I will tell you. He drank, then I drank what remained, then I informed him. He said: O Miqdad, this is a blessing; you should have informed me so we could wake our two companions and give them to drink from this blessing. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you drink the blessing and I do, I do not care whom it misses."],[1517,"Recite the Quran, and do not go to extremes in it, nor neglect it, nor eat by means of it, nor seek increase through it."],[1518,"Recite the Quran as long as your hearts are united upon it, but when you differ about it, then stop. He said: I was a young boy during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1519,"Whoever speaks about the Quran based on his own opinion, even if he is correct, he has erred."],[1520,"Adam and Musa argued. Musa said: You are Adam, whom Allah created with His hand, and to whom He prostrated His angels, and whom He settled in His Garden, yet you expelled people from the Garden? Adam said: You are Musa, to whom Allah spoke intimately and gave the Torah. Do you blame me for a matter that was decreed for me before He created me? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: So Adam defeated Musa, so Adam defeated Musa."],[1521,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a bearer of good news came to him from a military expedition he had sent, informing him of the victory Allah granted his expedition and the conquest Allah opened for them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, while we were pursuing the enemy and Allah had defeated them, I caught up with a man with my sword. When he sensed that the sword had reached him, he turned while running and said: I am a Muslim, I am a Muslim. But I killed him, and he was only seeking protection, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Why did you not split open his heart to see whether he was truthful or lying? He said: If I had split open his heart, the heart would not have informed me; is his heart anything but a lump of flesh? He said: You killed him; you did not know what was in his heart, nor did you believe his tongue. He said: O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me. He said: I will not ask forgiveness for you. They buried him, but he appeared on the surface of the earth three times. When his people saw that, they were ashamed and humiliated by what had happened to him, so they carried him and threw him into a ravine among those ravines."],[1522,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a bearer of good news came to him from a military expedition he had sent, informing him of the victory Allah granted his expedition and the conquest Allah opened for them. He mentioned something similar and added to it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said at that point: After me there will be trials like pieces of dark night, striking like the striking of snakes and strong bulls. A man will become a Muslim in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and become a Muslim in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. A man among the Muslims said: What should we do at that time, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Enter your houses and conceal your mention. A man among the Muslims said: What if one of us is entered upon in his house? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Let him restrain himself with his hand, and let him be the servant of Allah who is killed, not the servant of Allah who kills. For a man may be within the dome of Islam, yet he consumes his brother's wealth, sheds his blood, disobeys his Lord, disbelieves in his Creator, and Hellfire becomes obligatory for him."],[1523,"Whoever lets others hear of his deeds, Allah will expose him; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose him."],[1524,"I am your predecessor at the pond."],[1525,"Whoever prays the Subh prayer is under the protection of Allah, so beware that Allah should seek anything from you from His protection."],[1526,"A man from those before you had an abscess, and he became impatient with it, so he took a knife and cut his hand with it, and the blood did not stop until he died. Allah, the Exalted, said: 'My servant hastened his own death; I have forbidden Paradise to him.'"],[1527,"Abu Musa narrated to us: al-Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar b. Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah."],[1528,"A man said: 'By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so.' Allah said: 'Who is this who swears by Me that I will not forgive so-and-so? I have indeed forgiven so-and-so, and I have made your deeds worthless.'"],[1529,"Whoever greets you from Allah's creation, return the greeting to him even if he is a Magian, for Allah says: 'And when you are greeted with a greeting, greet with better than it or return it.'"],[1530,"\"And when you are greeted with a greeting, greet with better than it\" for the people of Islam or \"return it\" to the people of polytheism."],[1531,"We prayed with the Prophet ﷺ one day, and some people slaughtered their sacrificial animals before the prayer. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished and saw that they had slaughtered before the prayer, he said: 'Whoever slaughtered his sacrifice before the prayer, let him slaughter another in its place. And whoever has not slaughtered until we prayed, let him slaughter in the name of Allah.'"],[1532,"The finger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bled during one of the battles, and he said: 'Are you anything but a finger that has bled, and in the cause of Allah what you have met?'"],[1533,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a group and appointed Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah over them. When he was about to set out, he wept out of longing for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he sent a man in his place named Abdullah b. Jahsh, and wrote him a letter, and commanded him not to compel anyone of his companions to proceed with him. When he read the letter, he said: 'We belong to Allah and to Him we return,' and said: 'Hearing and obedience, meaning to Allah and His Messenger.' He informed them of the news and read the letter to them. Two men went back, and the rest went on. They met Ibn al-Hadrami and killed him, and they did not know whether that day was from Rajab or Jumada. The polytheists said to the Muslims: 'You did such and such in the sacred month.' They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the story. Allah revealed: 'They ask you about fighting in the sacred month. Say: Fighting therein is great' up to His saying: 'and fitnah is greater than killing.' He said: 'Polytheism.' One of those who were in the expedition said: 'By Allah, only one killed him. If it is good, you have done it; if it is a sin, you have committed it.' Some Muslims said: 'If they did not incur sin in their month, they have no reward in it.' Allah revealed: 'Indeed, those who have believed and those who emigrated and fought in the cause of Allah - those expect the mercy of Allah, and Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.'"],[1534,"Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely, he is as he said. No man is bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess."],[1535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on an expedition and put him in command, and said: 'If you seize so-and-so, burn him with fire.' When I turned away, they called me back, so I came, and he said: 'If you seize so-and-so, kill him, but do not burn him with fire, for none punishes with fire except the Lord of fire.'"],[1536,"that he divorced his wife with an irrevocable divorce, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"What did you intend by it?\" He said: \"One (divorce).\" He said: \"By Allah?\" He said: \"By Allah.\" He said: \"It is according to what you intended.\""],[1537,"that he divorced his wife with an irrevocable divorce during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: \"What did you intend by that?\" He said: \"One (divorce).\" He said: \"By Allah?\" He said: \"By Allah.\" He said: \"It is according to what you intended.\""],[1538,"The lost property of a Muslim is a flame of the Fire."],[1539,"that he and a companion of his passed by Umm Ayman, and some youths of Quraysh had untied their lower garments and made them into ropes with which they were striking one another while they were naked. Abdullah said: When we passed by them, they said: \"These are priests, so leave them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out upon them, and when they saw him, they dispersed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned angry until he entered. I was behind the chamber, and I heard him saying: \"Glory be to Allah! They did not feel ashamed before Allah, nor did they cover themselves from His Messenger.\" And Umm Ayman was with him, saying: \"Seek forgiveness for them, O Messenger of Allah.\" Abdullah said: By my father, he did not seek forgiveness for them."],[1540,"We ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day some roasted meat while we were in the mosque, and the prayer was called. We did no more than wipe our hands on the pebbles."],[1541,"that he saw Muhammad ibn Ulbah al-Qurashi dragging his lower garment, and Hubayb ibn Mughaffal looked at him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever treads upon it out of pride, he will tread upon it in the Fire.\""],[1542,"A slave-girl passed by me on one of the roads of Madinah, and I reached with my hand to her waist. The next day, the people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and I came and held out my hand to pledge allegiance to him, but he withdrew his hands and said: \"Are you not the one with the little pinch yesterday?\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, accept my pledge; I will never return.\" He said: \"Then yes.\""],[1543,"Good management of property is growth, and bad character is misfortune."],[1544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity and fast without breaking the fast."],[1545,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and at the forefront of the people was Khalid ibn al-Walid. Suddenly there was a woman killed on the road, and they were marveling at her form; the vanguard had struck her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and stood over her and said: \"Indeed, this woman was not fighting.\" Then he said to a man: \"Catch up with Khalid, and let him not kill any child or hired servant.\""],[1546,"I came in the pre-Islamic era to Makkah, wanting to buy for my family some of its garments and perfume. I went to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who was a merchant, and I was sitting with him where I could see the Kaaba. The sun had risen high in the sky, and I went away when a young man came, raised his gaze to the sky, then stood facing the qiblah. I did not wait long before a boy came and stood on his right, and in a little while a woman came and stood behind them. The young man bowed, and the boy and the woman bowed; the young man raised, and the boy and the woman raised. I said: \"O Abbas, a great matter!\" Al-Abbas said: \"A great matter. Do you know who this young man is?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"This is Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the son of my brother. Do you know who this boy is? This is Ali, the son of my brother. Do you know who this woman is? This is Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, his wife. This son of my brother\""],[1547,"A man stood up during the time of the Prophet ﷺ reciting at dawn: 'Say: He is Allah, the One,' repeating it and not adding to it. When morning came, a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so stood up last night and recited at dawn: \"Say: He is Allah, the One, Allah, the Eternal Refuge. He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent,\" repeating it and not adding to it,' as if the man considered it too little. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is indeed equal to a third of the Quran.'"],[1548,"He was wounded in his eye on the day of Badr, and his eyeball slid down onto his cheek. They wanted to cut it off, so he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: No. Then he called for him and pressed his eyeball back with the palm of his hand, and thereafter one could not tell which of his eyes had been injured."],[1549,"Abu Dharr's eye was injured on the day of Uhud, and the Prophet ﷺ spat into it, and it became the healthier of his two eyes."],[1550,"I, my father, and my grandfather gave allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ. I brought a dispute before him and he ruled in my favor, and he sought a wife on my behalf and married me. Ma'n also said: Booty is not lawful until it is distributed to the people all at once in a single share; when it has been distributed, then it is lawful for me to give you some."],[1551,"We used to take shelter with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because he kept his elbows away from his sides when he prostrated."],[1552,"The Ansar came on the day of Uhud and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have wounds and exhaustion, so what do you command us? He said: Dig, widen, and place two or three men in one grave. They said: Whom should we put forward? He said: Put forward the one among you who knows the most Quran. He said: So my father was placed in front of two of the Ansar, or he said: one of the Ansar."],[1553,"People used to buy gold with silver on credit. Isma'il said: I think until the next stipend. Hisham b. Amir came upon them and forbade them, and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from selling gold on credit, and he informed us, or he said."],[1554,"You are passing over me to go to men who were not closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or more retentive of his hadith than I. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Between the creation of Adam and the coming of the Hour there is no creature greater than the Dajjal."],[1555,"We used to pass by Hisham to go to Imran b. Husayn. One day he said: You are bypassing me to go to men who were not closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than I or more knowledgeable of his hadith than I. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Between the creation of Adam and the coming of the Hour there is no creature greater than the Dajjal."],[1556,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to shun another Muslim for more than three days. They both deviate from the truth as long as they are shunning each other. The first of them to return to reconciliation will have his precedence in returning serve as an expiation for him. If one greets the other and he does not accept his greeting, the angels return the greeting to him, and Satan returns it to the other. If they both die while still shunning each other, they will not enter Paradise, or they will not be gathered together in Paradise."],[1557,"They complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about their wounds. He said: Dig, make it good, and widen, and bury two or three in one grave, and put forward the one among them who knows the most Quran. He said: Then my father died, and he was placed before two men."],[1558,"I ate lunch with the Prophet ﷺ, and Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah was with us. Abu Ubayda said to him: O Messenger of Allah, is there anyone better than us? We embraced Islam with you and fought alongside you. He said: Yes, a people who will come after me, who believe in me without having seen me."],[1559,"I fought against the Prophet ﷺ at the beginning of the day as an unbeliever, and I fought with him at the end of the day as a Muslim. We were three men and seven women, and concerning us was revealed: 'And if not for the believing men and the believing women...' the verse."],[1560,"I met an old man in Syria and said: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Yes, I heard him say: O God, forgive us and have mercy on us."],[1561,"I said to 'Abd Khayr: How old are you? He said: One hundred and twenty years. I said: Do you remember anything from the time of ignorance? He said: Yes, we were in the lands of Yemen, and the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us calling people to abundant good. My father was among those who went out while I was a boy. When my father returned, he said to my mother: Order this pot to be poured out for the dogs, for we have become Muslims, so accept Islam too."],[1562,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ and ate with him bread and meat — or he said: tharid. I said: May God forgive you, O Messenger of God. He said: And you. I said to 'Abdullah b. Sarjis: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ ask forgiveness for you? He said: Yes, and for you. And he recited this verse: \"And ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women\" (Q 47:19). He said: Then I went around until I was behind him, and I saw the seal of prophethood near the cartilage of his left shoulder, like a clenched fist with moles on it."],[1563,"He forbade that a man bathe with the leftover water of a woman, and that a woman bathe with the leftover water of a man, but rather they should both scoop from it together."],[1564,"There is no ruler who closes his door against those in need and poverty but that God closes the gates of heaven against his need and destitution."],[1565,"There is no commander or ruler who closes his door against those in need, poverty, and destitution but that God closes the gates of heaven against his need and destitution. He said: So Mu'awiya appointed a man to attend to people's needs."],[1566,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he said: Let whoever here is from Ma'add stand up. He said: So I took hold of my garment to stand, but he said: Sit down. Then he said it a second time. I said: From whom am I, O Messenger of God? He said: From Himyar."],[1567,"I set up my snares at al-Abwa', and a gazelle fell into one of them but escaped. I went out after it and found a man who had taken it. We disputed over it and raced to the Messenger of God ﷺ. We found him encamped at al-Abwa' under a tree shading himself with a leather cloth. We brought our dispute to him, and he ruled that it be divided between us in two halves. I said: O Messenger of God, we come upon camels that have milk and are restrained, while we are in need. He said: Call out to the owner of the camels three times. If he comes, then leave it; otherwise, untie their udder straps, then drink, then tie them again, and leave some milk for the suckling. I said: O Messenger of God, stray animals come to us; is there reward for us if we water them? He said: Yes, in every living being with a thirsty liver there is reward. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ began to tell us, saying: A time will come upon people when the best wealth will be sheep between the two mosques, eating trees and coming to water. Their owner will eat from their produce, drink from their milk, and wear from their wool — or he said: their hair — while tribulations will churn among the masses of the Arabs. By God, you will not care, the Messenger of God ﷺ said it three times. I said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: Establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, perform 'umrah, be dutiful to your parents, maintain family ties, honor the guest, enjoin good, forbid evil, and move with the truth wherever it moves."],[1568,"I was holding the halter of the Messenger of God's ﷺ she-camel in the middle of the days of tashriq during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said among what he said: O people, indeed every usury is abolished, and the first usury to be abolished is the usury of al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. You have your principal amounts; you do not wrong and you are not wronged."],[1569,"The wealth of a Muslim man is not lawful except with his own willing consent."],[1570,"And I command you with five things that God has commanded me: the congregation, hearing, obedience, emigration, and jihad in the path of God. Whoever separates from the congregation by a handspan has Islam removed from his head, unless he returns. And whoever calls with the call of ignorance, he is of the fuel of Hell. It was said: Even if he fasts and prays? He said: Even if he prays and fasts. So call with the call of God who named you Muslims, believers, servants of God."],[1571,"Abu Hubayra al-Ansari, a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, saw me praying the forenoon prayer when the sun had risen, and he criticized me for that and forbade me. Then he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not pray until the sun has risen high, for it rises between the horns of a devil."],[1572,"He said to Abu Bakr, and Sa'd was his slave, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with his service. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Free Sa'd. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, we have no one here besides him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Free Sa'd, men will come to you, men will come to you."],[1573,"I placed dates before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they began pairing them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade pairing."],[1574,"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-five years old."],[1575,"Two women were fasting, and they were backbiting people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and said to them: Vomit. They vomited pus, blood, and fresh flesh. Then he said: These two fasted from what is lawful, and broke their fast on what is forbidden."],[1576,"Four things in my community from the affairs of the pre-Islamic era that they will not abandon: boasting about ancestors, slandering lineages, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing. And he said: The wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will be made to stand on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of tar and a coat of scabies."],[1577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated on the evening of 'Arafah for his community for forgiveness and mercy, and he increased in supplication. Allah answered him: I have done so and forgiven your community except the wrongdoing of some against others. He repeated, saying: O Lord, You are able to forgive the wrongdoer and reward the wronged with better than his grievance. That evening was nothing but that. The next day, he supplicated in the morning of Muzdalifah, and he repeated supplicating for his community. The Prophet ﷺ did not wait long before smiling. Some of his companions said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, you smiled at a time when you would not laugh. What made you laugh, may Allah make you smile? He said: I smiled at the enemy of Allah, Iblis, when he knew that Allah had answered me regarding my community and forgiven the wrongdoer. He fell down calling for destruction and woe, throwing dust on his head. And he said once: I laughed at his distress."],[1578,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Umar: Gather for me the Quraysh who are here. He gathered them, then said: O Messenger of Allah, shall you go out to them or shall they enter? He said: Rather, I will go out to them. He went out and said: O assembly of Quraysh, is there anyone among you other than you? They said: No, except the sons of our sisters. He said: The son of a people's sister is from them. Then he said: O assembly of Quraysh, know that the people most deserving of the Prophet are the righteous. So look, do not let people come with deeds on the Day of Resurrection while you come with the world, carrying it, lest I turn away from you with my face. Then he recited: Indeed, the people most deserving of Ibrahim are those who followed him and this Prophet and those who believe, and Allah is the guardian of the believers."],[1579,"We came to 'Umayr b. Sa'd among a group from the people of Palestine. He was called 'unique in his kind.' We sat on a large bench of his in his house. He said to his servant: O boy, bring the horses to water. In the house there was a stone trough. He brought them to water. He said: Where is so-and-so? He said: She is mangy, dripping blood, or he said dripping water; Abu Ishaq was uncertain. He said: Bring her to water. One of the people said: Then all the horses will become mangy. He said: Bring her to water, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no hama. Have you not seen the camel among the camels, how it is in the desert, then in its chest or its tender parts appears a spot that was not there before? Who infected the first one?"],[1580,"There are no two Muslims between whom four children die except Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and three? He said: And three. He said: And two? He said: And two. He said: Indeed, among my community is one for whose intercession more will enter than Mudar."],[1581,"There is nothing in the hama, the evil eye is true, and the truest of omens is the fa'l."],[1582,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when revelation came down upon him. When revelation came down upon him, his gaze remained fixed, his eyes open, and his hearing and heart were devoted to what came to him from Allah. He said: We recognized that from him. He said to the scribe: Write: 'Not equal are those believers who sit and those who strive in the cause of Allah.' Then a blind man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is our sin? Then Allah sent down revelation. We said to the blind man: Revelation is coming down upon the Prophet ﷺ. He feared that something concerning his matter was being revealed, so he remained standing, saying: I seek refuge from the anger of the Messenger of Allah. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ said to the scribe: Write: 'Other than the disabled.'"],[1583,"Nadla met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Murrin, and he had some milch camels with him. He milked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ into a vessel, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank, then he drank from the same vessel. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I used to drink seven and not be satisfied or filled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The believer drinks in one intestine, and the disbeliever drinks in seven intestines."],[1584,"Abu Yala informed us, Ibn al-Madini narrated it to us with his chain of transmission in a similar manner."],[1585,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, intending not to leave anything of righteousness or sin without asking him about it. I came to him while a band of people were around him seeking his legal opinions, so I began to step over them. They said: 'Stay back, O Wabisa, from the Messenger of God ﷺ.' I said: 'Let me draw near to the Messenger of God ﷺ, for he is the most beloved of people to me that I should draw near to him.' He said: 'Leave Wabisa; draw near, O Wabisa. Consult your heart, and consult your soul. Consult your heart, and consult your soul. Righteousness is that to which the soul feels tranquility and to which the heart feels tranquility, while sin is that which agitates in the soul and wavers in the breast, even if people give you a legal opinion, and give you a legal opinion'—three times."],[1586,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, intending not to leave anything of righteousness or sin without asking him about it. I came to him while a band of Muslims were around him seeking his legal opinions, so I began to step over them toward him. They said: 'Stay back, O Wabisa.' I said to them: 'Let me draw near to him, for he is the most beloved of people to me that I should draw near to him.' He said: 'Leave Wabisa; draw near, O Wabisa. Draw near, O Wabisa.' So I drew near and sat before him. He said to me: 'O Wabisa, are you asking me, or shall I inform you?' I said: 'Rather [inform me].'"],[1587,"The Messenger of God ﷺ departed while a man was praying behind the group, so he said: 'O you who pray alone, will you not join the row and enter with them, or pull a man to yourself if the place is too crowded for you? Repeat your prayer, for you have no prayer.'"],[1588,"He would stand among the people on the day of the sacrifice, or on the day of the breaking of the fast, and say: 'I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he was saying: Which day is this?' The people said: 'The day of sacrifice.' He said: 'Which month is this?' Then he said: 'Which land is this?' They said: 'This sacred land.' He said: 'Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet Him.' Then he said: 'O God, have I conveyed? Let the one present convey to the one absent.' Wabisa said: 'We call upon you as witnesses, just as he called upon us as witnesses.'"],[1589,"We call upon you as witnesses, just as he called upon us as witnesses; so you have taken it in, and we are conveying it to you."],[1590,"On the day of Qurayza, a man of the Ansar called Khallad was killed. His mother was told: 'O Umm Khallad, Khallad has been killed.' She came wearing a face veil, and it was said to her: 'Khallad has been killed, and you come to us wearing a face veil?' She said: 'If I am bereaved of Khallad, I will not be bereaved of my modesty.' They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Indeed he has the reward of two martyrs.' It was said: 'O Messenger of God, why is that?' He said: 'Because the People of the Book killed him.'"],[1591,"I entered with al-Hakam al-A'raj upon Bakr b. Abdullah, and they discussed the matter of a deceased person being punished by the weeping of the living. Bakr narrated to us, saying: A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated to us, and Abu Hurayrah differed with him on that, saying: Abu Hurayrah said: 'By God, if a man goes out fighting in the path of God, then is killed in one of the regions of the earth as a martyr, and a woman out of foolishness or ignorance then weeps over him, this martyr will surely be punished by the weeping of this foolish woman over him.' A man said: 'The Messenger of God spoke the truth and Abu Hurayrah lied. The Messenger of God spoke the truth and Abu Hurayrah lied.'"],[1592,"O Messenger of God, teach me a deed that will admit me to Paradise, and do not make it burdensome for me. He said: 'Do not become angry.'"],[1593,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My brother is ill.' He said: 'What is your brother's illness?' He said: 'He has a touch of madness.' He said: 'Send him to me.' So he came to him and sat before him. He said: 'The Prophet ﷺ recited over him the Opening of the Book, and four verses from the beginning of Surat al-Baqarah, and two verses from its middle: \"And your God is one God; there is no god but He, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth...\" until he finished the verse, and the Throne Verse, and three verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah, and a verse from the beginning of Surat Al Imran: \"God bears witness that there is no god but He, and the angels, and those possessed of knowledge, standing firm in justice\" to the end of the verse, and a verse from Surat al-A'raf: \"Indeed, your Lord is God who created the heavens and the earth,\" and a verse from Surat al-Mu'minun: \"Exalted be God, the True King; there is no god but He, Lord of the Noble Throne,\" and a verse from Surat al-Jinn: \"And exalted is the majesty of our Lord; He has taken neither a wife nor a son,\" and ten verses from the beginning of Surat al-Saff, and three verses from the end of Surat al-Hashr, and \"Say: He is God, the One,\" and the two protective surahs.'"],[1594,"He forbade on the day of Khaybar having intercourse with pregnant women, and said: 'Would you water the crop of another?'"],[1595,"I came to Madinah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'What has brought you?' He said: I said: 'That you teach me words [to say] when I take to my bed.' He said: 'Recite: Say, O disbelievers, for it is a declaration of freedom from polytheism.'"],[1596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Dihya al-Kalbi to Caesar, and wrote with him a letter giving him the choice of one of three things: either to submit and keep the kingship in his hands, or to pay the tribute, or to give permission for war. He said: Caesar gathered his patricians and priests in his palace, locked the door upon them, and said: Muhammad has written to me giving me the choice of one of three things: either to submit and keep the kingship in my hands, or to pay the tribute, or to give permission for war. You will find in what you read of your scriptures that he will possess what is under my feet of my kingdom. They snorted a snort until some of them came out of their cowls, and said: Will you send to a man of the Arabs, who has come in his two cloaks and his two sandals, regarding the tribute? He said: Be quiet. I only wanted to know your adherence to your religion and your desire for it. Then he said: Seek for me a man of the Arabs. They brought me, and he wrote with me a letter to the Prophet ﷺ, and said to me: Look at what escapes you of his speech, so let nothing escape you at the mention of the night and the day. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was with his companions, and they were sitting with their sword belts wrapped around them at the well of Tabuk. I said: Which of you is Muhammad? He pointed with his hand to himself. I handed him the letter, and he gave it to a man beside him. I said: Who is this? They said: Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan. He read it, and in it was: You have written calling me to a Paradise whose width is the heavens and the earth; so where is the Fire then? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Glory be to Allah! When night comes, where is the day? I wrote it down with me. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You are the messenger of a people, and you have a right, but you have come to us while we are destitute. 'Uthman said: I will clothe him with a Saffuri robe. A man of the Ansar said: I will host him. And Caesar said to me in what he said: Look at his back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that I wanted to look at his back, so he cast his garment off his back. I looked at the seal in the cartilage of the shoulder, and I came to him and kissed it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I wrote to the Negus, and he burned my letter; Allah will burn him. I wrote to Chosroes, the great one of Persia, and he tore my letter; Allah will tear him. I wrote to Caesar, and he raised my letter, so people will not cease – he mentioned a word – as long as there is good in life."],[1597,"That 'Urwa b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi said to his people at the time of al-Hudaybiya: O my people, I have seen kings and spoken with them. Send me to Muhammad and I will speak with him. He came to him at al-Hudaybiya, and 'Urwa began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ and to take hold of the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while al-Mughira b. Shu'ba was armed, standing at the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Mughira said to him: Withdraw your hand before it does not reach you. 'Urwa raised his head and said: Is it you? By Allah, you are still in your treachery from which you have not yet emerged. 'Urwa returned to his people and said: O my people, I have seen kings and spoken with them. I have never seen the like of Muhammad. He is not a king. I have seen the sacrificial animals restrained, their wool being eaten, and I think a calamity will befall you. So he departed with those of his people who were with him, climbed the wall of al-Ta'if, bore witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and a man of his people shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: Praise be to Allah who has placed in my community one like the companion of Yasin."],[1598,"I entered the mosque upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing, and his chest had a humming like the humming of a cauldron."],[1599,"Whoever abandons the Friday prayer three times out of negligence for it, Allah will set a seal upon his heart."],[1600,"That a man in Kufa testified that 'Uthman ؓ was killed as a martyr, so the guards seized him and raised him to 'Ali ؓ, and said: Were it not that you forbade us, or that you had forbidden us, from killing anyone, we would have killed him. This one claims that he testifies that 'Uthman ؓ was killed as a martyr. The man said to 'Ali ؓ: And you testify. Do you remember that I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he gave me; and I came to Abu Bakr ؓ and asked him, and he gave me; and I came to 'Umar ؓ and asked him, and he gave me; and I came to 'Uthman ؓ and asked him, and he gave me? He said: Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to bless me. The Prophet ﷺ said: How can you not be blessed when a Prophet gave you, and a Siddiq and two martyrs; and a Prophet gave you, and a Siddiq and two martyrs; and a Prophet gave you, and a Siddiq and two martyrs?"],[1601,"He said to 'Ali: O 'Ali, blessed is the one who loves you and is truthful about you, and woe to the one who hates you and lies about you."],[1602,"O 'Ammar, Gabriel came to me just now, and I said: O Gabriel, tell me of the virtues of 'Umar b. al-Khattab in heaven. He said: O Muhammad, if I were to tell you of the virtues of 'Umar for as long as Noah remained among his people, a thousand years less fifty, the virtues of 'Umar would not be exhausted. Indeed 'Umar is one good deed among the good deeds of Abu Bakr."],[1603,"That he saw 'Ammar b. Yasir perform ablution and that he ran his fingers through his beard. It was said to him: Do you do this? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it."],[1604,"That 'Ammar said to 'Umar: Do you remember when you and I were with the camels, and I became ritually impure, so I rolled in the dust as an animal rolls? I met the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: It would have sufficed you to perform tayammum."],[1605,"We were with 'Umar when a man came to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, we remain for a month or two without finding water. 'Umar said: As for me, I would not pray until I found water. 'Ammar said: O Commander of the Faithful, do you remember when we were at such-and-such a place and we were pasturing the camels, and we recalled that we had become ritually impure? He said: He said: Yes. I rolled in the dust, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, and he laughed and said: Clean earth would have sufficed you, and he struck the ground with his two palms, then blew into them, then wiped his face and part of his forearms. He said: Fear Allah, O 'Ammar. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you wish, I will never mention it as long as I live. He said: No, but we will entrust you with as much of it as you have undertaken."],[1606,"A man asked 'Umar, saying: I became ritually impure and did not find water. He said: Do not pray. 'Ammar said: Do you not remember that you and I were in a military expedition in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we became ritually impure? As for you, you did not pray, and as for me, I rolled in the dust and prayed. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: It would have sufficed you, and he struck the ground once with his hand, then blew into his palms and wiped his face and his two palms."],[1607,"That the Prophet ﷺ commanded him regarding tayammum with the two palms and the face."],[1608,"We performed tayammum with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we wiped our faces and our hands up to the shoulders with dust."],[1609,"I saw 'Ammar b. Yasir on the day of Siffin, an old man, tall, dark-skinned, holding the spear in his hand while his hand trembled. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I fought with this banner alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ three times, and this is the fourth. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they were to strike us until they drove us to the peaks of Hajar, we would know that our righteous ones are upon the truth and that they are upon misguidance."],[1610,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was watering a she-camel of mine. I spat, and my spittle fell on my garment. I began washing my garment from the water-skin that was in front of me. The Prophet ﷺ said: O 'Ammar, your spittle and the tears of your eyes are only like the water in your water-skin. You only wash your garment from urine, feces, semen, from major water, blood, and vomit."],[1611,"A man asked him about eating hare. He said: Call 'Ammar for me. 'Ammar came, and he said: Tell us the hadith of the hare on the day when we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in such-and-such a place. 'Ammar said: A bedouin gave a hare as a gift to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered the people to eat. A bedouin said: I saw blood. He said: It is nothing. Then he said: Come closer and eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: Fasting what? He said: I fast three days every month. He said: Why did you not make them the white days?"],[1612,"A drink of milk was brought to 'Ammar, and he laughed. It was said to him: What makes you laugh? He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: The last drink you will drink is milk when you die."],[1613,"'Ammar fell ill with an illness that became severe, and he lost consciousness. He regained consciousness while we were weeping around him. He said: What makes you weep? Do you fear that I will die on my bed?"],[1614,"'Ammar b. Yasir prayed two rak'ahs, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, I see you have made them light. He said: I hurried through them to avoid distraction. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A man may pray a prayer and perhaps he gets only a tenth of it, or a ninth, or an eighth, or a seventh, or a sixth, or a fifth—until he reached the end of the count."],[1615,"I said to 'Ammar b. Yasir: Do you consider your fighting a matter of opinion that you yourselves held—for opinion can err and be right—or a covenant that the Messenger of God ﷺ entrusted to you? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ did not entrust to us anything that he did not entrust to all the people. And he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ—Shu'bah said: I think he said—"],[1616,"The righteous have not adorned themselves in this world with anything like renunciation of this world."],[1617,"'Ammar spoke and was concise. He was told: You made a statement—if only you had given us more. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to shorten the sermons."],[1618,"'Ammar and 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud began discussing tayammum. 'Abd Allah said: If I remained for a month without finding water, I would not pray. 'Ammar said to him: Do you not remember when you and I were with the camels, and I became ritually impure, and you rolled in the dust like an animal rolls? When I returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him what I had done, he said: Tayammum would have sufficed you."],[1619,"Whoever has two faces in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[1620,"'Ammar b. Yasir delivered a sermon to us and was brief in the sermon. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to prolong the sermon.'"],[1621,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and said: 'Which day is this?' We said: 'The Day of Sacrifice.' He said: 'Which month is this?' We said: 'Dhu al-Hijjah, a sacred month.' He said: 'Which land is this?' We said: 'The Sacred Land.' He said: 'Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Indeed, let the one present convey to the one absent.'"],[1622,"'I have been commanded to fight the oath-breakers, the deviators, and the apostates.'"],[1623,"I was with 'Ammar, and he was making a supplication in his prayer. A man came to him, and 'Ammar said to him: 'Say: O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive as long as You know life is better for me, and take my soul when You know death is better for me. O Allah, I ask You for fear of You in secret and in public, the word of truth in pleasure and anger, moderation in wealth and poverty, and I ask You for contentment after Your decree, and a pleasant life after death. I ask You for longing to meet You without harmful adversity or misleading trial. O Allah, adorn me with the adornment of faith, and make me one of the guides who are rightly guided.' 24 - (1625) - Then he said: 'Shall I not teach you words that are better than those?' As if he was raising them to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'When you go to your bed at night, say: O Allah, I have submitted my soul to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, believed in Your revealed Book and Your sent Prophet. My soul is a soul You created; to You belongs its life and its death. If You take it, have mercy on it, and if You delay it, protect it with the protection of faith.'"],[1624,"I was with 'Ammar, and he was making a supplication in his prayer. A man came to him, and 'Ammar said to him: 'Say: O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive as long as You know life is better for me, and take my soul when You know death is better for me. O Allah, I ask You for fear of You in secret and in public, the word of truth in pleasure and anger, moderation in wealth and poverty, and I ask You for contentment after Your decree, and a pleasant life after death. I ask You for longing to meet You without harmful adversity or misleading trial. O Allah, adorn me with the adornment of faith, and make me one of the guides who are rightly guided.' 24 - (1625) - Then he said: 'Shall I not teach you words that are better than those?' As if he was raising them to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'When you go to your bed at night, say: O Allah, I have submitted my soul to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, believed in Your revealed Book and Your sent Prophet. My soul is a soul You created; to You belongs its life and its death. If You take it, have mercy on it, and if You delay it, protect it with the protection of faith.'"],[1625,"On the day of Siffin, 'Ammar fought but was not killed. He would come to 'Ali and say: 'O Commander of the Faithful, is this not such-and-such a day?' He would say: 'Go away from me.' He said that several times. Then milk was brought and he drank it. 'Ammar said: 'This is the last drink I will drink from this world.' Then he advanced and fought until he was killed."],[1626,"Part of the fitrah is rinsing the mouth, sniffing water into the nose, trimming the mustache, using the siwak, washing the knuckles, plucking the armpit hair, shaving the pubic hair, circumcision, and washing the private parts with water."],[1627,"'Ammar prayed, and a man said to him: 'You have made the prayer light, O Abu al-Yaqzan.' He said: 'Did you see me omit anything from its limits? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man prays and then leaves, and only half of it is recorded for him, or a third, a quarter, a fifth, a sixth, a seventh, an eighth, a ninth, a tenth.'"],[1628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped for the night at Dhat al-Jaysh, and with him was his wife 'A'ishah. A necklace of hers made of Dhafar onyx broke, and the people were detained seeking that necklace until dawn broke, and the people had no water. Abu Bakr became angry with her and said: 'You have detained the people and they have no water.' Then Allah, exalted is He, sent down upon His Messenger the concession of purification with clean earth. The Muslims stood with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, struck their hands on the ground, raised their hands without taking any dust, and wiped their faces and hands up to the shoulders, and from the palms of their hands to the armpits."],[1629,"I was among the people when the concession was revealed for wiping with clean earth if we could not find water. He said: 'We struck one blow with the hands on the earth for the face and wiped it once. Then we struck another blow for the hands and wiped them up to the shoulders, back and front.'"],[1630,"We wiped ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with dust, and we wiped our faces and hands up to the shoulders."],[1631,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and with him was 'A'ishah. Her necklace was lost, and the people were delayed or detained seeking it, and they had no water. Then Allah, exalted is He, sent down the verse of tayammum. 'Ammar said: 'They struck their hands and wiped their faces with them, then they struck their hands again and wiped their hands up to the armpits,' or he said: 'to the shoulders.'"],[1632,"We were with the Messenger of Allah on a journey. A necklace of 'A'ishah was lost, and they searched for it until morning, and the people had no water. Then the concession was revealed. The Muslims stood and struck their hands on the ground and wiped their faces with them, and the outer and inner parts of their hands up to the armpits."],[1633,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he responded to me."],[1634,"I arrived at my family at night from a journey, and my hands had become chapped, so they smeared me with saffron. Then I went in the morning to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I greeted him, but he did not respond to me, nor did he welcome me. He said: 'Go and wash this off yourself.' So I went and washed it off, then I came and greeted him, and he responded to me and welcomed me. He said: 'The angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever with good, nor that of one smeared with saffron, nor of a ritually impure person.' And he gave a concession for the ritually impure person, if he wants to sleep, or eat, or drink, to perform ablution."],[1635,"\"O Abu Musa, I adjure you by God: did you not hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire'? I am asking you about a hadith, and if you tell the truth, good, otherwise I will send against you some of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ to press you. Then I adjure you by God: was it not that the Messenger of God ﷺ meant you specifically by himself? He said: 'There will be a tribulation in my community, in which you, O Abu Musa, asleep will be better than you sitting, and one sitting will be better than you standing, and one standing will be better than you walking.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ singled you out and did not generalize the people?\" So Abu Musa went out and did not answer him anything."],[1636,"Whoever had two faces in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[1637,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about dry ablution (tayammum). He said: \"He commanded me to do the face and the palms with one strike.\""],[1638,"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed in a single garment, wrapping himself with it."],[1639,"I became ritually impure while I was among the camels, and I did not find water, so I rolled around as an animal rolls. Then I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him of that. He said: \"It would have sufficed you to do dry ablution (tayammum).\""],[1640,"I met Ammar b. Yasir on the Day of the Camel while he was urinating in a horn. I said to him: \"Should I fight with you and be with you?\" He said: \"Fight under the banner of your people, for the Messenger of God ﷺ used to like a man to fight under the banner of his people.\""],[1641,"Ammar b. Yasir delivered a sermon to us, and he was brief and eloquent. When he came down, we said: \"O Abu al-Yaqzan, you have been eloquent and brief; would that you had paused for breath?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Indeed, the length of a man's prayer and the shortness of his sermon is an indication of his understanding, so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermons, and indeed there is magic in eloquence.'\""],[1642,"That he greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he returned the greeting."],[1643,"We were with Ammar on the day about which there is doubt concerning Ramadan, and a sheep was brought. Some of the people withdrew. Ammar said: \"Whoever fasts this day has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.\""],[1644,"I have not forgotten the Day of the Trench when he was passing milk to them, and his hair had become dusty—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—and he was saying: 'Indeed, the best good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun.' Then Ammar came, and he [the Prophet] said: 'Woe to you, or woe upon you'—Khalid was uncertain—'O Ibn Sumayya, the transgressing group will kill you.'"],[1645,"When Ali sent Ammar and al-Hasan to Kufa to raise troops, Ammar delivered a speech and said: Indeed, I know that she is his wife in this world and the Hereafter, meaning Aishah."],[1646,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in a single garment."],[1647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon."],[1648,"Ammar b. Yasir entered the mosque and prayed two light rak'ahs. A man said: You made them light, O Abu al-Yaqzan. He replied: Did you see me omit anything from their limits? I hastened them to ward off whispering, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A man prays, yet perhaps he has from his prayer only a tenth, or a ninth, or an eighth, or a seventh, or a sixth, or a fifth, or a quarter, or a third, or half."],[1649,"We were sitting in the mosque when Ammar passed by us, and we said to him: Tell us the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the trial. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: After me there will be rulers who fight one another for dominion, killing one another over it. We said: If anyone other than you had narrated it, we would have rejected it. Indeed, it will happen."],[1650,"The table was sent down from heaven as bread and meat. They were commanded not to betray or store for tomorrow, but they betrayed, stored, and lifted, and were transformed into apes and pigs."],[1651,"We performed tayammum with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and wiped our faces and hands up to the shoulders with dust."],[1652,"Indeed, the lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever guards against them safeguards his religion, and whoever falls into them is likely to fall into major sins, like a shepherd grazing around a sanctuary who is likely to graze in it. Every king has a sanctuary."],[1653,"Whoever lives in the desert becomes coarse."],[1654,"We camped with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Hudaybiyyah and found that its water had been consumed by the first arrivals. The Prophet ﷺ sat by the well and called for a bucket, took a mouthful from it, then spat into the well and supplicated to Allah, the Exalted, and its water increased until the people drank their fill."],[1655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about kalalah, and he said: The summer verse suffices you."],[1656,"He was asked: Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate? He said: He prostrated between his two palms."],[1657,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he began the prayer raise his hands until they were level with his thumbs, or level with his ears."],[1658,"It is a duty upon the Muslims that each of them should perform a full bath on Friday, and touch some perfume if he has any with his family; if they have none, then water is perfume."],[1659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah before the hajj. He said: And 'A'ishah said: He knew that he had performed 'umrah four times, his 'umrah being in the Farewell Hajj."],[1660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice and said: 'Indeed, no one should sacrifice until he has prayed.' A man stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is a day on which meat is desired, and I hastened my sacrifice to feed my family and the people of my house, or my family and my neighbors.' He said: 'You have already done so, so repeat another sacrifice.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a young she-goat that is better than two meat sheep. Should I sacrifice it?' He said: 'Yes, and it is better than your sacrifice, but a jadha'ah will not suffice for anyone after you.'"],[1661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on the day of Eid al-Adha after the prayer and said: 'Whoever prays our prayer and performs our sacrifice has fulfilled the sacrifice. Whoever sacrifices before the prayer, his sheep is only a sheep of meat, and he has no sacrifice.' Abu Burdah b. Niyar, the maternal uncle of al-Bara', said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed my sheep before the prayer because I knew that today is a day of eating and drinking, and I wanted my sheep to be the first thing slaughtered in my house. So I slaughtered my sheep and ate lunch before coming to the prayer.' He said: 'Your sheep is a sheep of meat.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have a young she-goat, a jadha'ah, which is dearer to me than two sheep. Will it suffice for me?' He said: 'Yes, and it will never suffice for anyone after you.'"],[1662,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on a journey, he would say: 'O Allah, grant us a provision that brings good, forgiveness from You and Your pleasure. In Your hand is all good. You have power over all things. O Allah, You are the companion in travel and the guardian of the family. O Allah, make the journey easy for us and fold the earth for us. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel and from a sorrowful return.'"],[1663,"When he returned from a journey, he would say: 'Returning, repentant, worshiping, praising our Lord.'"],[1664,"He was on a journey and recited in the last 'isha' prayer in one of the two rak'ahs: 'By the fig and the olive.'"],[1665,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent my uncle to a man who had married his father's wife, and he ordered him to strike his neck."],[1666,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a man to a man who had married his father's wife, and he ordered him to strike his neck and bring his head."],[1667,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded a man, when he took to his bed, to say: 'O Allah, I submit myself to You, I turn my face to You, I entrust my back to You, I commit my affairs to You, in hope and fear of You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down and in Your Messenger whom You sent.' For if he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."],[1668,"He would place his face between his palms when he prostrated."],[1669,"The Prophet ﷺ heard Abu Musa reciting, and said: \"The voice of this one is like one of the flutes of the family of Dawud.\""],[1670,"We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the noon prayer, and we thought that he recited \"Tanzil\" (the prostration)."],[1671,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out with his companions, and we entered ihram for Hajj. When we arrived in Makkah, he said: \"Make your Hajj an 'Umrah.\" Some people said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we have already entered ihram for Hajj, so how can we make it an 'Umrah?\" He said: \"Look at what I have commanded you and do it.\" They repeated their words back to him, so he became angry. Then he went off until he entered upon 'A'ishah angry. She saw the anger in his face and said: \"Whoever has angered you, may Allah Almighty anger him.\" He said: \"Why should I not be angry when I command something and it is not followed?\""],[1672,"When two Muslims meet and shake hands, and praise Allah and seek His forgiveness, they are forgiven."],[1673,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunut in the sunset and dawn prayers."],[1674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us until he made the secluded maidens in their houses hear him, or he said: in their private chambers. He said: \"O assembly of those who believe with their tongues, do not backbite the Muslims and do not pursue their faults. For whoever pursues the fault of his brother, Allah will pursue his fault, and whoever Allah pursues his fault, He will expose him in the interior of his house.\""],[1675,"They used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he bowed, they bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing and said: \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" we remained standing until we saw that he had placed (his forehead on the ground)."],[1676,"When we prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and raised our heads from bowing, we stood in rows until the Prophet ﷺ prostrated. When he prostrated, we followed him."],[1677,"When the Prophet ﷺ met the polytheists on the day of Hunayn, he dismounted from his mule and walked."],[1678,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him about the times of prayer. He commanded Bilal, and he advanced (the call) and delayed (it), and said: \"The time is what is between them.\""],[1679,"The bowing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and between the two prostrations, were close to equal."],[1680,"The prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and when he raised his head from the two prostrations, were close to equal."],[1681,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down to sleep, he placed his right hand under his right cheek and said: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You gather Your servants."],[1682,"On the day You resurrect Your servants."],[1683,"It is an obligation upon the Muslims to perform ritual bathing on Friday."],[1684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the digging of the trench. He said: A boulder appeared before us that the pickaxes could not break. They complained about that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: So he took the pickaxe. He said: I think he said: He placed down his garment and struck a blow, saying: In the name of Allah. He broke one third of the boulder. Then he said: Allah is greatest! I have been given the keys of Syria. Indeed, I can see its red palaces from this place of mine. Then he said: In the name of Allah, and struck another blow, breaking one third of it. He said: Allah is greatest! I have been given the keys of Persia. By Allah, indeed I can see al-Mada'in and its white palace from this place of mine. Then he said: In the name of Allah, and struck another blow, breaking the rest of the rock. He said: Allah is greatest! I have been given the keys of Yemen. By Allah, indeed I can see the gates of San'a' from this place of mine."],[1685,"Adorn the Quran with your voices."],[1686,"Spread the greeting of salam and you will be safe, and pride is evil."],[1687,"Whoever calls Madinah Yathrib, let him seek Allah's forgiveness."],[1688,"When he began the prayer, he raised his hands, then he did not raise them again until he finished."],[1689,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the prayer, he raised his hands near his head, then he did not repeat it."],[1690,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he began the prayer: he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were almost level with his ears, then he did not repeat it."],[1691,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raise his hands when he faced the prayer, until I saw his thumbs close to his ears, then he did not raise them again."],[1692,"I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in fifteen military expeditions."],[1693,"I went on campaign with the Messenger of God ﷺ fifteen or so expeditions."],[1694,"On the day of Badr I was presented to the Messenger of God ﷺ, I and Ibn 'Umar, and he deemed us too young. We were present on the day of Uhud."],[1695,"Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, died when he was sixteen months old, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Bury him in al-Baqi', for he has a wet nurse who will complete his suckling in Paradise."],[1696,"We used to pray behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when he said: 'God hears the one who praises Him', none of us would bend his back until the Prophet ﷺ placed his forehead on the ground, and when he placed his forehead on the ground we would fall down in prostration."],[1697,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by us while our cooking pots were boiling with the meat of donkeys, and he ordered us to tip them over, so we tipped them over."],[1698,"We never saw anyone in a red hulla, with combed hair, more handsome than the Messenger of God ﷺ. His hair came close to his shoulders."],[1699,"I never saw one with a limma in a hulla more handsome than the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[1700,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ began the prayer, he would raise his hands until they were level with his ears."],[1701,"Muhammad b. al-Qasim sent me to al-Bara' b. 'Azib to ask him about the banner of the Messenger of God ﷺ, what it was. He said: It was black, square, made of namira."],[1702,"Among the conditions they imposed on the Prophet ﷺ was that they would not enter Makkah except with the scabbards of weapons. He said: And what are the scabbards of weapons? He said: The sheath and what is in it."],[1703,"What do you say about the joy of a man whose riding camel escaped from him, dragging its halter in a barren land in which there is no food or drink, and on it is his food and drink, and he sought it until it became hard for him, then it passed by the trunk of a tree and its halter got caught, and he found it hanging on it? We said: Very great, O Messenger of God. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: By God, God is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than the man at his riding camel."],[1704,"I never saw anyone in a red hulla more handsome than the Messenger of God ﷺ, with combed hair. His hair was close to his ears, or he said: his shoulders."],[1705,"Beautify the Quran with your voices."],[1706,"When you prostrate, place your palms and raise your elbows."],[1707,"I saw on al-Bara' a ring of gold, and it was said to him it was because of it. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ divided and this ring remained over. He said: Who do you think is more entitled to this? Then he said: Come near, O Bara', and he put it on my finger, and said: Wear what God and His Messenger have clothed you."],[1708,"Sheep are a blessing."],[1709,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ approached from Makkah to Madinah, Suraqah b. Ju'shum followed him, so the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated against him, and his horse sank with him. He said: Supplicate to God for me and I will not harm you, so he supplicated for him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ became thirsty, and they passed by a shepherd. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I took a bowl and milked into it a small amount of milk, and I brought it to him, and he drank, then I drank until I was satisfied."],[1710,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to sleep, he would place his right hand under his cheek and say: O God, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You gather Your servants."],[1712,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ made peace with the people of Makkah, Ali wrote a document between them and wrote: Muhammad is the Messenger of God. The polytheists said: Do not write Muhammad is the Messenger of God, for if you were the Messenger of God, we would not fight you. He said to Ali: Erase it. Ali said: I am not one to erase it. So the Messenger of God ﷺ erased it with his hand. He made peace with them on condition that he and his companions enter it for three days, and that they not enter except with the sheaths of weapons. They asked him: What are the sheaths of weapons? He said: The scabbard and what is in it."],[1713,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was a man of medium height, broad-shouldered, with thick hair reaching his earlobes. He was wearing a red robe, and I never saw anything more beautiful than him."],[1714,"The first to come from the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ were Mus'ab b. 'Umayr and Ibn Umm Maktum, and they used to teach the people the Quran. He said: Then Bilal, Sa'id, and 'Ammar b. Yasir came. He said: Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab came with twenty of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then the Messenger of God ﷺ came, and I never saw the people of Madinah rejoice at anything as they rejoiced at the Messenger of God ﷺ, so much so that even the slave girls were saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ has come. He said: He did not come until I had recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and other surahs from the Mufassal."],[1715,"The Prophet ﷺ was carrying dust, and the dust covered his belly while he was saying: O God, if not for You we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. So send down tranquility upon us and make our feet firm if we meet. The first ones have transgressed against us, and perhaps he said: The assembly has refused against us; if they want a trial, we refuse, raising his voice with it."],[1716,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by people sitting in the road and said: If you must do so, then guide the way, return the greeting, and help the oppressed."],[1717,"Muhammad b. Bashshar narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara' from the Prophet ﷺ with the like of it. Shu'bah said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Did you hear it from al-Bara'? He said: No."],[1718,"Some people among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ died while they were drinking wine. When its prohibition came down, some people among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: 'But what about our companions who died while they were drinking it?' Then came down: 'There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they consumed, if they fear [God], believe, and do righteous deeds.'"],[1719,"Muhammad b. Bashshar narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara' b. 'Azib similarly. Shu'ba said: I said: 'Did you hear it from al-Bara'?' He said: 'No.'"],[1720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded a man, when he took to his bed, to say: 'O God, I have submitted my soul to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, leaned my back upon You, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and in Your Prophet whom You sent.' If he dies, he dies upon the fitrah."],[1721,"A man recited al-Kahf while in the house there was an animal, and it began to shy. He said salam, and there was a mist or a cloud that had covered him. He mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Recite, so-and-so, for it is the sakina that descended with the Qur'an, or it descended for the Qur'an.'"],[1722,"The last verse revealed was al-kalala, and the last surah revealed was Bara'a."],[1723,"I was considered too young on the day of Badr, I and Ibn 'Umar. The Emigrants were over sixty, and the Helpers over two hundred and forty."],[1724,"'Not equal are those among the believers who remain seated, other than those with a disability, and those who strive in the path of God.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered Zayd, and he brought a shoulder blade. He said: Ibn Umm Maktum complained of his disability, so it came down: 'Not equal are those among the believers who remain seated, other than those with a disability.'"],[1725,"Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us from Sa'd b. Ibrahim from his father from a man from Zayd b. Thabit regarding this verse 'Not equal are those who remain seated,' similar to the hadith of al-Bara'."],[1726,"A man from Qays asked him: 'Did you flee from the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Hunayn?' Al-Bara' said: 'But the Messenger of God did not flee. Hawazin were archers. When we charged at them, we fell upon the spoils, and they met us with arrows. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on his white mule, and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith was holding its bridle, and he was saying: \"I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib.\"'"],[1727,"On the day of Khaybar we captured donkeys. The caller of the Messenger of God ﷺ announced: 'Overturn the pots.'"],[1728,"When he returned from a journey, he said: 'Returning, repenting, worshipping our Lord, praising.'"],[1729,"A silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ. His companions began to touch it, marveling at its softness. He said: 'You marvel at the softness of this? The handkerchiefs of Sa'd in Paradise are better than it and softer.'"],[1730,"A silk garment was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ. His companions began touching it, so he said: \"Are you amazed at the softness of this? The handkerchiefs of Sa'd in Paradise are softer than this.\""],[1731,"When the Ansar performed the Hajj, they would not enter their houses except from the back. A man from the Ansar came and entered through his door, and he was told about that. Then it was revealed: \"It is not righteousness that you enter houses from the back...\" the verse."],[1732,"He heard Abu Musa reciting the Qur'an: \"It is as if this voice is from the voices of the family of Dawud.\""],[1733,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about the two protective surahs? 'Uqbah said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer reciting them, then called me.\" So he mentioned his hadith about them."],[1734,"Recite these two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah; I was given them from beneath the Throne."],[1735,"While I was leading the Messenger of God ﷺ by the reins through a mountain pass, he said: \"O 'Uqbah, will you not ride?\" I held back from riding the mount of the Messenger of God ﷺ out of reverence. Then he said: \"O 'Uqbah, will you not ride?\" I feared it would be disobedience. So the Messenger of God ﷺ dismounted, and I rode for a little while, then he mounted. Then he said: \"O 'Uqbah, shall I not teach you two surahs that are among the best surahs that people recite?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Then he recited to me: 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,' and 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.' Then the prayer was called, and the Messenger of God ﷺ went forward and recited them. Then he passed by me and said: \"How did you find it, O 'Uqbah? Recite them whenever you sleep and whenever you rise.\""],[1736,"The one who recites the Qur'an quietly is like the one who gives charity secretly, and the one who recites the Qur'an aloud is like the one who gives charity openly."],[1737,"When it was revealed: \"So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great,\" the Messenger of God ﷺ said to us: \"Place it in your bowing.\" When it was revealed: \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,\" he said: \"Place it in your prostration.\""],[1738,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ saying to his companions: \"Do not frighten your selves,\" or he said: \"the selves.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, with what do we frighten our selves?\" He said: \"With debt.\""],[1739,"We were sitting in the mosque reciting the Qur'an, when the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us and said: \"Learn the Book of God and spread it.\" Qabath said: I think he also said: \"and chant it. For by the One in whose hand is my soul, it slips away faster than untethered camels.\""],[1740,"Do not force your sick to eat and drink, for God feeds them and gives them drink."],[1741,"Lands will be opened to you and God will suffice you, so let none of you fail to amuse himself with his arrows."],[1742,"And prepare against them whatever you are able of power. Verily, power is archery; verily, power is archery; verily, power is archery."],[1743,"A vow is an oath, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."],[1744,"If the Qur'an were placed in a hide and then thrown into the fire, it would not burn."],[1745,"The ruin of my nation is in the Book and milk. They said: What is the Book and milk? He said: They learn the Qur'an and interpret it other than its interpretation, and they love milk and abandon the congregations and Friday prayers and go into the desert."],[1746,"Whoever goes out from his house to the mosque, ten good deeds are written for him for every step he takes, and the one sitting in the mosque waiting for the prayer is like the devout worshipper, and is written among those who pray until he returns to his house."],[1747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over the slain of Uhud after eight years, like one bidding farewell to the living and the dead. He said: Verily before you are forerunners; I am a witness over you. Your appointed meeting is the Hawd, and I see it from this place of mine. Its width is as between Ayla and al-Juhfa. Verily I have been given the keys of the treasures of the earth while I am in this station of mine. Verily I do not fear for you that you associate partners, but I fear for you the world, that you compete for it. 'Uqbah said: It was the last look I looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1748,"Our Lord wonders at a young man who has no youthful passion."],[1749,"May Allah have mercy on the guard of the guard post."],[1750,"I heard Maslama b. Mukhallad while he was standing on the pulpit giving a sermon, saying: O people, do you not have in coarse cloth and linen what suffices you from silk? Here is a man among you who reports from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Stand, O 'Uqbah. So 'Uqbah b. 'Amir stood while I was listening, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I bear witness that I heard him say: Whoever wears silk in this world will be deprived of wearing it in the Hereafter."],[1751,"Whoever is thrown from his mount in the path of Allah and dies is a martyr."],[1752,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about his sister who vowed to walk veiled. So he commanded her to veil, ride, and fast three days."],[1753,"The most deserving conditions to be fulfilled are those by which the private parts are made lawful."],[1754,"Three hours in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid us to pray and to bury our dead: when the sun rises until it has risen high, when the sun stands at its zenith until it declines, and when it inclines toward setting until it sets."],[1755,"The collector of maks will not enter Paradise—meaning the customs tax collector."],[1756,"O son of Adam, are you unable to pray four rak'as at the beginning of the day, and I will suffice you for the rest of it?"],[1757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided sacrificial animals, and I received a jadha'. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a jadha' fell to my lot.' He said, 'Sacrifice it.'"],[1758,"Whoever hangs a tamima, may Allah not complete it for him, and whoever hangs a wada'a, may Allah not grant him peace."],[1759,"Whoever frees a believing slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire."],[1760,"We went out on a journey, and with us was 'Uqba b. 'Amir. We said to him, 'Lead us in prayer, may Allah have mercy on you.' He said, 'I will not do it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever leads the people in prayer and gets the time right and completes the prayer, the reward is for him and for them. And whoever falls short in any of that, it is against him and not against them.\"'"],[1761,"It is not lawful for a Muslim man to propose to a woman when his brother has proposed, until he gives up, nor to buy when his brother has bought, until he gives up."],[1762,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition to Tabuk. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat talking to his companions and said: \"Whoever rises when the sun meets him, performs ablution and does it well, then stands and prays two rak'as, his sins will be forgiven, and he will be as his mother bore him.\""],[1763,"Whoever has three daughters and is patient with them, feeds them, gives them drink, and clothes them from his wealth, they will be a screen for him from the Fire."],[1764,"If there is healing in anything, it is in the cut of a cupper, a drink of honey, or a cauterization that hits the disease. But I dislike cauterization and do not love it."],[1765,"A man will be in the shade of his charity until judgment is passed among people—or he said: until retribution is taken among people."],[1766,"Whoever fasts one day in the path of God, God will distance Hell from him a distance of one hundred years."],[1767,"He forbade mixing raisins and dates, and unripe dates and dates."],[1768,"Nabidh used to be made for him in a stone vessel."],[1769,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when I slept, then woke, then slept, then woke. A man from the Muslims stood up and said: 'The prayer, the prayer.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us with his head dripping, and he prayed. Then he said: 'Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community—and I do not love to make things difficult for my community—I would have loved for you to pray this prayer at this hour.'"],[1770,"Restrain your livestock until the fright of the evening passes, for it is an hour in which the devils spread."],[1771,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to close the doors, cover the vessels, tie the water-skins, extinguish the lamps, and restrain our livestock until the darkness of the evening passes. He forbade any of us from eating with his left hand, walking in a single sandal, and from al-samma' and wrapping oneself in a single garment."],[1772,"He prayed over the Negus. He said: I was in the second or third row."],[1773,"A man called Abu Humayd brought the Prophet ﷺ a vessel containing milk from al-Naqi' during the day, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Why did you not cover it, even by placing a stick across it?'"],[1774,"Adhere to moderation and seek closeness, and none of you will be saved by his deeds. We said: 'Not even you, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'Not even me, unless God envelops me in His mercy.'"],[1775,"Shame and disgrace will afflict the son of Adam on the Day of Resurrection in the standing before God to the extent that the servant will wish to be ordered into the Fire."],[1776,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called Abu Tayba and had him cup him, then asked him about his tax. He said: 'Three sa's.' He said: So he reduced one sa' for him."],[1777,"The Prophet ﷺ fought Muharib Khasafa at Nakhl. They saw an opportunity from the Muslims, so a man from among them called Ghawrath b. al-Harith came and stood over the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ with a sword, saying: 'Who will protect you from me?' He said: 'God.' He said: The sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took the sword and said to him: 'Who will protect you from me?' He said: 'Be the best taker.' He said: 'Will you testify that there is no god but God?' He said: 'No, but I promise you that I will not fight you, nor be with a people who fight you.' He said: So he let him go. He came to his companions and said: 'I have come to you from the best of people.' When it was noon or afternoon—Abu 'Awana was uncertain—the Prophet ﷺ ordered the prayer of fear. He said: The people were in two groups: one group facing their enemy, and one group praying with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He prayed two rak'as with the group that was with him, then they left and took the place of those others, and those others came and prayed two rak'as with the Prophet ﷺ. Thus the Messenger of God ﷺ had four rak'as and the people had two."],[1778,"A man slaughtered a young goat (a jadha') before the Prophet ﷺ prayed. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is not sufficient for anyone after you to slaughter until he prays.\""],[1779,"The Prophet ﷺ traveled during Ramadan, and fasting became severe for a man among his companions. His she-camel began wandering with him under the shade of trees. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, so he ordered him to break his fast. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called for a vessel with water in it and placed it on his hand. When the people saw him drink, they drank."],[1780,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted the sale of 'araya (unpicked dates) for one wasq, two wasqs, three, or four. He said: \"For every jadd (portion), ten wasqs; and what remains is a branch placed in the mosque for the poor.\""],[1781,"Whoever swears a false oath on this pulpit of mine has taken his seat in the Fire."],[1782,"Between a servant and disbelief is abandoning the prayer."],[1783,"What is between my pulpit and my chamber is a garden from the gardens of Paradise. And indeed my pulpit is upon a canal from the canals of Paradise."],[1784,"The Messenger of God ﷺ asked a man who had apostatized from Islam to repent four times."],[1785,"They were on a military expedition of theirs and were struck by severe hunger. The sea cast up a great creature, and they ate from it fresh meat for twenty-five days. Abu al-Zubayr said: Jabir b. 'Abd Allah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Have you brought us any of it?\""],[1786,"On the day of Khaybar they slaughtered horses, mules, and domestic donkeys. The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade mules and donkeys, and he did not forbid horses."],[1787,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade (making nabidh in) the dubba' (gourd), the muzaffat (vessel smeared with pitch), and the naqir (hollowed-out wood). Abu al-Zubayr said: Jabir, when he could not find a waterskin, would make nabidh for him in a stone trough."],[1788,"There is no 'adwa (contagion), no tiyara (evil omen), no safar (month considered ill-omened), and no ghul (desert demon)."],[1789,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar came to us, and we fed them fresh dates and gave them water to drink. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"This is part of the blessings about which you will be asked.\""],[1790,"When a man goes to his bed, an angel and a devil race to him. The angel says: 'Seal with good,' and the devil says: 'Seal with evil.' If he remembers Allah then sleeps, the angel spends the night guarding him. When he wakes, the angel says: 'Begin with good,' and the devil says: 'Begin with evil.' If he says: 'Praise be to Allah who restored my soul to me and did not cause it to die in its sleep; praise be to Allah who holds the heavens and the earth lest they cease'—to the end of the verse—'praise be to Allah who holds the heaven lest it fall upon the earth except by His permission,' then if he falls from his bed and dies, he enters Paradise."],[1791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought two large, horned, white-flecked rams. He laid one down and said: 'In the name of Allah, Allah is greatest. O Allah, on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.' Then he laid down the other and said: 'In the name of Allah, Allah is greatest, on behalf of Muhammad and his nation: whoever bears witness to Your oneness and bears witness to my conveyance.'"],[1792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him during the expedition of Tabuk, while he was on a red camel: the camel lagged behind. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you, Jabir?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my camel lagged behind.' He came to it from its rear, supplicated for it, and urged it on. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said: 'What did the camel do, Jabir?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it has been leading us since last night.' He said: 'For how much did you buy it?' I said: 'For thirteen dinars.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Sell it to me for the price you paid, and you may ride it to Madinah.' I did so. When we reached Madinah, I put a nose-rein on it and brought it to him, and he gave me the camel and the thirteen dinars."],[1793,"Three things: whoever brings them along with faith enters from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes and is married to houris wherever he wishes: one who pardons his killer, one who repays a hidden debt, and one who recites after every prescribed prayer ten times: 'Say: He is Allah, the One.' Abu Bakr said: 'Or one of them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Or one of them.'"],[1794,"Ubayy led the people in prayer in Quba. A boy from the Ansar entered his prayer while he had a water channel. When he heard Ubayy reciting a long surah, he left his prayer. When Ubayy finished, he was informed of that. Ubayy knew that the boy would complain to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the boy came to complain about Ubayy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Among you are those who drive people away. When you pray, be brief'—or he said: 'make it light'—Abu Yahya doubted, or as he said—'for behind you are the elderly, the sick, and those with needs.'"],[1795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in Makkah and passed by a man standing praying on a rock. He went to a side of Makkah and stayed for a while, then returned and found the man still praying in the same state. He clasped his hands and said three times: 'O people, keep to moderation, keep to moderation, keep to moderation, for Allah will not tire until you tire.'"],[1796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by in Makkah a man praying on a rock. He went to a side and stayed for a while, then left and found the man still praying in the same state. He stood and clasped his hands, then said: 'O people, keep to moderation, keep to moderation, for Allah does not tire until you tire.'"],[1797,"Ubayy was leading the people of Quba in prayer. He began a long surah, and a boy from the Ansar joined him in prayer. When he heard him begin a long surah, the boy left his prayer, intending to attend to a camel of his that he used for watering. When Ubayy b. Ka'b finished, the people said to him: 'So-and-so left the prayer.' Ubayy became angry and went to the Prophet ﷺ to complain about the boy. The boy also came to complain about him. The Prophet ﷺ became angry until anger was seen on his face, then said: 'Among you are those who drive people away. When you pray, be brief, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, the sick, and those with needs.'"],[1798,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was giving a sermon. He sat next to Ubayy b. Ka'b and asked him about something—or spoke to him about something—but Ubayy did not reply. Ibn Mas'ud thought it was due to resentment. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, Ibn Mas'ud said: 'O Ubayy, what prevented you from replying to me?' He said: 'You did not attend the Friday prayer with us.' He said: 'Why?' He said: 'You spoke while the Prophet ﷺ was giving a sermon.' Ibn Mas'ud stood up, went to the Prophet ﷺ, and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ubayy is right. Obey Ubayy.'"],[1799,"Ibn Mas'ud entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was giving a sermon, and he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Abd al-A'la."],[1800,"Ubayy b. Ka'b came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, something happened from me last night'—meaning in Ramadan. He said: 'And what is that, O Ubayy?' He said: 'Women in my house said: We do not recite the Quran, so we pray with your prayer.' He said: 'So I led them in eight rak'ahs, then performed witr.' He said: 'It was as if he approved, and he did not say anything.'"],[1801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in eight rak'ahs in the month of Ramadan and performed witr. The next night we gathered in the mosque and hoped he would come out to us, but we remained there until morning. Then we entered and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we gathered in the mosque and hoped you would lead us in prayer.' He said: 'I feared or disliked that it would be made obligatory upon you.'"],[1802,"Ibn Umm Maktūm came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I am blind and my dwelling is far away.” He spoke to him about the prayer, asking that he be allowed to pray in his home. He said: “Do you hear the call to prayer?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Come to it, even if crawling.”"],[1803,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the killing of dogs. Ibn Umm Maktūm came and said: “O Messenger of God, my dwelling is far and I have a dog.” He granted him a concession for some days, then ordered that it be killed."],[1804,"Whoever revives dead land has a reward in it, and what the grazing animals eat—meaning birds and beasts of prey—is charity for him."],[1805,"He forbade muḥāqalah, muzābanah, mukhābarah, muʿāwamah, and thunyā."],[1806,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade entering the water except with a waist-wrapper."],[1807,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother, when it has hair."],[1808,"Do not give permission to one who does not begin with the greeting of peace."],[1809,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ walk briskly from the Black Stone until he reached the Black Stone, three circuits."],[1810,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited a sick person while I was with him, and saw him praying and prostrating on a cushion. He forbade him and said: “If you are able to prostrate on the ground, then prostrate; otherwise, gesture, and make the prostration lower than the bowing.”"],[1811,"Shall I not guide you to what will save you from your enemy and increase your provisions? Call upon God in your night and day, for supplication is the weapon of the believer."],[1812,"It may be that a man will call me a liar while reclining on his couch, when a hadith from me reaches him and he says: “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not say this. Leave this and bring what is in the Qur’an.”"],[1814,"Ride the sacrificial animals with courtesy until you find another mount."],[1815,"He forbade the stud's covering."],[1816,"He forbade withholding surplus water to prevent thereby the pasture."],[1817,"Quraysh gathered to the Prophet ﷺ one day and said, \"Look for the most knowledgeable among you in sorcery, divination, and poetry, and let him go to this man who has divided our assembly, scattered our affairs, and defamed our religion. Let him speak to him and see how he responds.\" They said, \"We know no one but Utbah b. Rabiah.\" They said, \"You, Abu al-Walid.\" So Utbah went to him and said, \"O Muhammad, are you better or Abdullah?\" The Messenger of God remained silent. Then he said, \"Are you better or Abd al-Muttalib?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent. He said, \"If you claim that these are better than you, then they worshipped the deities you have defamed. If you claim that you are better than them, then speak so that we may hear your words. By God, we have never seen a young lamb more ill-omened upon your people than you. You have divided our assembly, scattered our affairs, and defamed our religion, and you have disgraced us among the Arabs, until it has spread among them that there is a sorcerer in Quraysh and a diviner in Quraysh. By God, we are only waiting for a cry like that of a pregnant woman before some of us rise against others with swords until we perish. O man, if it is need that drives you, we will gather for you until you become the richest man of Quraysh. If it is marriage, then choose any of the women of Quraysh you wish, and we will marry you to ten.\" The Messenger of God said to him, \"Have you finished?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Ha Mim. A revelation from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,\" until he reached: \"But if they turn away, then say: I have warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud.\" Utbah said, \"Enough, enough! Do you have anything other than this?\" He said, \"No.\" He returned to Quraysh, and they said, \"What is behind you?\" He said, \"I left nothing that I thought you would speak to him about except that I spoke to him about it.\" They said, \"Did he answer you?\" He said, \"Yes. By the One who erected it as a building, I understood nothing of what he said except that he said, 'I have warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud.'\" They said, \"Woe to you! A man speaks to you in Arabic and you do not know what he said?\" He said, \"No, by God, I understood nothing of what he said except the mention of the thunderbolt.\""],[1818,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Makkah, Abu Quhafah was brought to him with his head and beard white as the thaghamah plant. He said, \"Change the gray hair, and avoid black.\""],[1819,"Call out, O Umar, among the people: that whoever dies worshipping God sincerely from his heart, God will admit him to Paradise and forbid him from the Fire. He said: Umar said, \"O Messenger of God, shall I not give the people glad tidings?\" He said, \"No, lest they rely on it.\""],[1820,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, \"When do you perform witr?\" He said, \"From the beginning of the night after the evening prayer.\" Then he said to Umar, \"When do you perform witr?\" He said, \"From the end of the night.\" He said to Abu Bakr, \"You have taken the cautious approach,\" and he said to Umar, \"You have taken the strong approach.\""],[1821,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took the hand of a leper and placed it with him in the bowl, then said, \"Eat in the name of God, with trust in God and reliance upon Him.\""],[1822,"Two women of Hudhayl, one killed the other, and each of them had a husband and a child. The Messenger of God ﷺ made the blood money of the slain woman the responsibility of the killer's agnates, and he absolved her husband and child. He said: The agnates of the slain woman said, \"Her inheritance belongs to us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No, her inheritance belongs to her husband and her child.\" He said: She was pregnant, so the agnates of the slain woman said, \"She was pregnant and she cast a fetus.\" He said: The agnates of the killer feared that they would be held liable. He said: They said, \"O Messenger of God, it did not drink, nor eat, nor cry out, so did it utter a sound?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Is it the rhymed prose of the pre-Islamic era?\" So he ruled for the fetus a ghurrah: a male slave or a female slave."],[1823,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition when a man from the Muhajirun struck a man from the Ansar on the back of his neck. The Ansari said, \"O Ansar!\" and the Muhajir said, \"O Muhajirun!\" The Messenger of God ﷺ heard that and said, \"What is this call of the pre-Islamic era?\" It was said, \"O Messenger of God, a man from the Muhajirun struck a man from the Ansar.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Leave it, for it is foul.\""],[1824,"The Prophet ﷺ sold a mudabbar slave."],[1825,"War is deception."],[1826,"Muadh used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, then return and lead his people in prayer. One night the Prophet ﷺ delayed the prayer, then he came and recited Surah al-Baqarah. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Are you a troublemaker, O Muadh?\""],[1827,"The Prophet ﷺ came to him—meaning Abd Allah b. Ubayy—after he had been placed in his grave. He ordered that he be taken out, then he blew some of his saliva on him and clothed him in his shirt. And Allah knows best."],[1828,"When it was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: “Say: He is the One able to send upon you a punishment from above you,” he said: “I seek refuge in Your Face.” “Or from beneath your feet,” he said: “I seek refuge in Your Face.” “Or to confound you into factions and make you taste the might of one another,” he said: “These two are lighter or easier.”"],[1829,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He said: “Have you prayed?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then pray two rak‘ahs.”"],[1830,"Some people will come out of the Fire and enter the Garden."],[1831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fed us the meat of horses, and he forbade us the meat of domesticated donkeys."],[1832,"A man passed by some arrows in the mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ instructed him to hold them by their arrowheads. He said: “Yes.”"],[1833,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade sharecropping (mukhabarah)."],[1834,"Tariq ruled that a life grant goes to the heir, based on the statement of Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1835,"Whoever among you has land or palm trees should not sell them until he offers them to his partner."],[1836,"He commanded licking the dish and licking the fingers, for one does not know in which of that the blessing lies."],[1837,"Extinguish the lamps."],[1838,"We did not pledge allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ upon death. We pledged allegiance to him only upon not fleeing."],[1839,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a settled person from selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[1840,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'I saw as if my neck was struck, or my head was cut off.' He said: 'Why does one of you relate the playing of Satan?'"],[1841,"He forbade the sale of fruit until its ripeness appears."],[1842,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that the slain of Uhud be returned to their places of martyrdom, and some of them had already been carried to Madinah, or as Allah willed of them."],[1843,"He forbade that you come to women at night. Jabir said: Then we came to them afterwards."],[1844,"He forbade the sale of produce for years [in advance]."],[1845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, mukhabarah, and the sale of fruit until its ripeness appears, and that it not be sold except for dinars and dirhams, except for 'araya."],[1846,"He used to pour water over his head three times, meaning in the bath."],[1847,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1848,"Indeed, no man should spend the night with a woman in a house unless he is married to her or is a close relative (mahram)."],[1849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who pays it, the one who writes it, and its two witnesses, and he said: 'They are all equal.'"],[1850,"We went out on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: When we returned, I hurried ahead on a slow camel of mine. He said: A rider caught up with me from behind and prodded my camel with a staff that he had, so my camel went off as the best camel you could see. I turned, and it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'What is making you hurry?' I said: 'I am newly married.' He said: 'Did you marry a virgin or a previously married woman?' I said: 'A previously married woman.' He said: 'Why not a young girl so that you could play with her and she could play with you?' He said: When they returned, he said: 'Slow down until we enter at night, so that the disheveled woman may comb her hair and the one whose husband has been absent may shave.'"],[1851,"The lifetime gift is permissible for its recipients."],[1852,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said when he departed from Arafat: O people, upon you is tranquility and dignity, and let not one of you kill another."],[1853,"Shall I not inform you of those for whom the Fire is forbidden tomorrow? Upon every gentle, lenient, near, and easy person."],[1854,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about faith. He said: Patience and generosity."],[1855,"Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I will guarantee for him Paradise."],[1856,"O people, repent to God before you die, and hasten to righteous deeds, and connect what is between you and your Lord through abundant remembrance of Him and abundant charity in secret and in public. You will be rewarded, helped, and provided for. And know that God has made the Friday prayer an obligatory obligation upon you on this day of mine, in this place of mine, in this month of mine, in this year of mine, until the Day of Resurrection. So whoever abandons it during my life or after my death, denying it or belittling it, may God not unite his affairs, nor bless him in his matter. Indeed, there is no prayer for him, nor zakat for him, nor hajj for him, nor fasting for him, nor righteousness for him. Whoever repents, God will accept his repentance. A woman should not lead a man in prayer, nor should a Bedouin lead an emigrant, nor should a wicked person lead a righteous one, except a ruler who fears his sword and his whip."],[1857,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, do you think that if I fight in the path of God patiently, seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, until I am killed, will I enter Paradise? He said: Yes, unless you have a debt for which you have no means to repay."],[1858,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: I saw in a dream as if my head was cut off, or my neck was struck. He said: Why would one of you report the playing of Satan?"],[1859,"A man should not spend the night with a woman in a house unless he is married to her or is a close relative."],[1860,"We bought a cow in the time of the Prophet ﷺ to share in it, but it escaped from us and resisted us. A freed slave of ours named Dhakwan confronted it with a sword in his hand while it was roaming in the rocky highlands. It climbed a hill, and when it passed by him, he struck it with the sword at the base of its neck, or on its neck, and cut through it with the sword, and it fell. Its slaughter was not completed. I went out with Abdullah b. Thabit b. al-Jidh, and we met the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned its situation to him. He said: Eat, if any of these animals eludes you, then restrain it as you would restrain a wild animal."],[1861,"Marhab b. al-Harith the Jew came out saying: Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, armed with weapons, a tested hero. Sometimes I thrust, and sometimes I strike, when lions advance, they blaze. The tested one is protected from attack; my protection is the sanctuary that is not approached. Is there any challenger? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Who will face this? Muhammad b. Maslama said: I, O Messenger of God, by God, I am the one bereaved and seeking revenge; they killed my brother yesterday. He said: Arise to him, O God, help him. When one of them approached the other, a tree appeared between them, and one of them began to take refuge behind it from the other. Whenever he took refuge behind it, he cut with his sword what was before him until I saw it like a standing man, until each of them reached the other. Marhab charged at him and struck him, but he defended with his shield, and his sword fell into it and stuck, and the shield held it fast. Then Muhammad b. Maslama struck him and killed him."],[1862,"We advanced with the Messenger of God ﷺ, unaware of the ambush that the people had prepared for us. We entered the valley of Hunayn in the darkness of dawn, and it is a deep valley among the valleys of Tihama, sloping downward, where they descend steeply. He said: By God, the people were following one another without knowing anything, when suddenly the battalions surprised them from every direction. The people did not wait to turn back in retreat. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ moved to the right. He said: Where are you, O people? I am the Messenger of God, I am Muhammad b. Abdullah."],[1863,"Before the Hawazin there was a large man on a red camel, in his hand a black banner; whenever he caught up, he thrust with it, and whenever something escaped him in front, he pushed it from behind and ran it through. Ali b. Abi Talib and a man from the Ansar both made for him, each wanting him. He said: Ali struck the camel's two hocks and it fell on its rear. He said: The Ansari struck its leg. He said: It flung the man's foot with half his lower leg and he fell, and the people fought. And when the defeat occurred, Kalada — who was the brother of Safwan b. Umayya and was on that day a polytheist during the term that the Messenger of God ﷺ had set for him — came out saying: Indeed magic is void today! Safwan said to him: Be quiet, may God break your mouth! For by God, that a man of Quraysh should lord over me is dearer to me than that a man of Hawazin should lord over me."],[1864,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus, and I was in the second row."],[1865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: O people, God has detachments of angels that alight and stand over the gatherings of remembrance on earth, so graze in the meadows of Paradise. They said: And where are the meadows of Paradise, O Messenger of God? He said: The gatherings of remembrance. So go forth morning and evening in the remembrance of God, and remind yourselves of Him. Whoever loves to know his station with God, let him look at how God's station is with him, for God brings the servant down with Him where he has brought Him down with himself."],[1866,"Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Bishr b. al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Umar the client of Ghufra, from Ayyub b. Khalid, from Jabir, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[1867,"God Most High is modest and generous; He is ashamed of His servant when he raises his hands to Him, to return them empty with nothing in them."],[1868,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the market, a woman took hold of his mount's rein while he was on a donkey, and she said: O Messenger of God, my husband does not come near me, so separate me from him. Her husband passed by, and the Prophet ﷺ called him and said: What is the matter with you and her? She came complaining of your harshness, complaining that you do not come near her. He said: O Messenger of God, by the One who honored you, my last time with her was this very night. The woman wept and said: He lies; separate me from him, for he is among the most hateful of God's creation to me. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled, then took hold of his head and her head and joined them together, and said: O God, bring each one of them close to his companion. Jabir said: We remained as long as God willed us to remain, then the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by the market, and there was a woman carrying leather hides. When she saw him, she threw down the hides and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, God has not created any human more beloved to me than him, except you."],[1869,"The Prophet ﷺ called for a sheet at the time of his death to write in it a document for his community. He said: They will not go astray nor lead astray. There was clamor in the house, and Umar b. al-Khattab spoke, so the Prophet ﷺ discarded it."],[1870,"Whoever ascends the pass, the pass of al-Murar, will have removed from him what was removed from the Children of Israel. The first to ascend it were our horsemen, the horsemen of the Banu al-Khazraj. He said: Then the people followed one after another, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: All of you are forgiven except the owner of the red camel. We said: Come, let the Messenger of God ﷺ seek forgiveness for you. He said: By God, that I find my stray camel is dearer to me than that your companion should seek forgiveness for me. And he was a man seeking a stray."],[1871,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called for a sheet at the time of his death to write in it a document so that they would not go astray after him nor lead astray. There was clamor in the house, and Umar b. al-Khattab spoke, so the Messenger of God ﷺ discarded it."],[1872,"He forbade mixing dates and raisins together."],[1873,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: God and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of wine, the sale of pigs, the sale of carrion, and the sale of idols. A man said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of the fat of carrion, for we grease ships with it, grease skins with it, and use it for lamps? He said: May God curse the Jews; God forbade them their fats, so they took them, melted them down, then sold them and ate their prices."],[1874,"Whoever would like to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at al-Husayn b. Ali, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say it."],[1875,"Greeting with one finger, pointing with it, is the practice of the Jews."],[1876,"When Ja'far came from Abyssinia, the Prophet ﷺ embraced him."],[1877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to attend the gatherings of the polytheists. He said: He heard two angels behind him, one of them saying to his companion: Come with us so that we may stand behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He said: How can we stand behind him when his only recent contact was with the touching of the idols before? He said: After that, he never again attended the gatherings of the polytheists."],[1878,"Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah b. Ziyad b. Hudayr, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it. In the text there is a scribal error where the word [b.] was corrupted to [from], so the chain became..."],[1879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling palm trees for two or three years in advance, and he forbade buying what is on the tops of palm trees for a measure of dates, and he forbade selling fruit until its ripeness appears."],[1880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out in the year of the conquest to Makkah in Ramadan, and he fasted until he reached Kura' al-Ghamim. He said: The people fasted, both those on foot and those mounted. It was said to him: The people are finding the fast difficult; they are only watching what you do. He called for a cup and raised it up so that the people could see it, then he drank. Some of the people broke their fast and some fasted. It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: Some of them fasted. He said: Those are the disobedient ones. The walkers among his companions gathered to him and lined up before him, and they said: We seek the supplications of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for the journey has become hard and the distance long. He said to them: Seek help by moving quickly (al-nasl), for it consumes the ground for you and you become light for it. He said: We did so, and we became light for it."],[1881,"When the Arabs are humiliated, Islam is humiliated."],[1882,"The Prophet ﷺ performed raml (brisk walking) from the Black Stone to the Black Stone."],[1883,"We were on a journey, and a man fasted and then fainted. His companions stopped for him, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by. They said: He is fasting. The Prophet ﷺ said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[1884,"A man used to carry wine from Khaybar to Madinah and sell it to the Muslims. He carried some of it with wealth, and brought it to Madinah. A Muslim man met him and said: O so-and-so, wine has been forbidden. So he set it down where he ended up on a hill and covered it with cloaks. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have heard that wine has been forbidden. He said: Yes. He said: May I return it to the one I bought it from? He said: It is not lawful to return it. He said: May I give it as a gift to someone who will compensate me for it? He said: No. He said: There is wealth in it belonging to orphans under my care. He said: When the wealth of Bahrain comes to us, come to us and we will compensate your orphans from their wealth. Then he called out in Madinah. He said: The man said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the vessels; can we benefit from them? He said: Then untie their covers, and it poured out until it settled in the bottom of the valley."],[1885,"Respond even if crawling or creeping."],[1886,"Ja'far narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, from Isa, from Jabir, similar to the hadith of Ibn Umm Maktum regarding dogs."],[1887,"When the Prophet ﷺ met the naqibs from the Ansar, he said to them: 'You will shelter me and protect me.' They said: 'And what will we get?' He said: 'You will have Paradise.'"],[1888,"He used to deliver the sermon standing on Friday. A caravan from Syria arrived, and the people dispersed until only twelve men remained. Then this verse in Surat al-Jumu'ah was revealed: 'And when they saw a transaction or a diversion, they rushed to it and left you standing.'"],[1889,"Whoever eats of this garlic, onion, or leek, let him not come near us."],[1890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or in addition to her maternal aunt."],[1891,"When one of you is absent for a long time, let him not come to his family at night."],[1892,"The fever came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked permission to enter. He said: 'Who are you?' It said: 'I am Umm Mildam.' He said: 'Will you go to the people of Quba?' It said: 'Yes.' So it came to them, and they developed a fever and met severe hardship from it. They complained to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what we have suffered from the fever!' He said: 'If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah and He will remove it from you, and if you wish, it will be a purification.' They said: 'No, rather it will be for us a purification' or (he said) 'a benefit.'"],[1893,"Harshness and coarseness of hearts are in the direction of the east, among Rabi'ah and Mudar, and faith is among the people of the Hijaz."],[1894,"People are followers of Quraysh in good and evil."],[1895,"When Satan hears the call to prayer, he goes away until he reaches the place of al-Rawha'."],[1896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a horse in Madinah, and it threw him onto a palm stump, so his foot was dislocated. We came to visit him and found him in an upper room of Aisha's, glorifying Allah while sitting. We stood behind him, and he remained silent toward us. Then we came another time and found him praying the obligatory prayer, so we stood behind him. He gestured to us, and we sat down. When he finished the prayer, he said: 'When the imam prays sitting, pray sitting, and when the imam prays standing, pray standing. And do not do as the people of Persia do with their great ones.'"],[1897,"We arrived with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, circumambulated the House, and exited ihram. When we came to al-Batha', he commanded us to enter ihram for Hajj. He said: Some of the people said: 'Should we enter ihram for Hajj when our last contact with women was only yesterday?' He said: There was some discussion among them about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If I had known they would do this, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal.' He said: And he said to us: 'Let a group share in the sacrificial animal.'"],[1898,"We set out from Makkah to Madinah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: My camel became exhausted, so I lagged behind driving it. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had remained behind for a need, and he caught up with me and said to me: 'Why are you lagging behind?' He said: I said: 'No, O Messenger of Allah, except that my camel has gone lame, so I wanted to catch up with the people.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of its tail and struck it, then urged it on, and said: 'Mount.' And I saw myself afterward holding it back from the people. He said: We stopped at a place short of Madinah, and I wanted to hasten to my family. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Do not come to your family at night.' He said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I am newly married.' He said: 'What did you marry?' I said: 'A previously married woman.' He said: 'Why not a virgin, so you could play with her and she could play with you?' He said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah died or was martyred, and left young daughters, and I disliked to bring to them someone like them.' He said: He remained silent and did not say to me, 'You did well' or 'You did badly.' He said: Then he said to me: 'Sell me this camel of yours.' He said: I said: 'No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'No, sell it to me.' He said: I said: 'No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'No, sell it to me.' He said: I said: 'A man is owed by me an uqiyah of gold, so it is yours for that.' He said: 'I have taken it, and ride it to Madinah.' He said: When I arrived in Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Bilal: 'Give him an uqiyah of gold and add more.' He said: So he gave me an uqiyah of gold and added a qirat. He said: I said: 'The addition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will never leave me.' He said: It was in a purse of mine, and the people of Syria took it on the day of al-Harrah."],[1899,"If the son of Adam had a palm grove, he would wish for another like it, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."],[1900,"A slave belonging to Hatib came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, Hatib has entered the Fire.” He said, “You have lied. Did he not witness Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah?”"],[1901,"Every servant will be resurrected upon that upon which he died."],[1902,"The food of one man suffices two men, and the food of two men suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."],[1903,"When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for you do not know in which of them the blessing descends."],[1904,"Indeed, Satan attends one of you at every thing, until he attends him at his food and drink. So if a morsel of one of you falls, let him pick it up, and let him remove whatever harm has befallen it, then let him eat it and not leave it for Satan."],[1905,"Whoever fears that he will not wake up at the end of the night, let him perform witr at the beginning of the night and then sleep. And whoever hopes to wake up at the end of the night, let him perform witr at the end of the night, for the Qur’anic recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."],[1906,"Indeed, the people of Paradise will eat and drink therein, and they will not spit, nor urinate, nor blow their noses, nor defecate. He [the narrator] said, “Then what happens to the food?” He said, “It becomes belching and sweat like the sweat of musk. They will be inspired with glorification and praise just as you are inspired with breath.”"],[1907,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say three [days] before his death: “Let none of you die except while he has good thoughts of God, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[1908,"We did not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah upon death, but rather we pledged allegiance to him upon not fleeing—except Jadd b. Qays, who hid under the armpit of his camel."],[1909,"Indeed, the throne of Iblis is upon the sea, and he sends out his detachments to tempt people. The greatest of them in his sight is the one who creates the greatest temptation."],[1910,"A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have a slave girl, and I practice coitus interruptus with her.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “What has been decreed for her will come to her.” Then he came to him after that and said, “O Messenger of God, the slave girl has become pregnant.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whatever soul God has decreed to come forth will inevitably come into being.”"],[1911,"Indeed, in the night there is an hour in which no Muslim man coincides while asking Allah for good of this world and the Hereafter except that He grants it to him."],[1912,"There was with the Mother of the Believers ʿĀʾishah a woman who had a boy with his nostrils dripping blood. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said: \"What is the matter with this boy?\" She said: \"He has the ʿudhrah (tonsillitis/quinsy).\" He said: \"Woe to you, O womenfolk! Do not kill your children. Any woman whose child has ʿudhrah or a pain in his head should take Indian costus, grind it, then administer it through the nose.\" Then he instructed ʿĀʾishah, and she did that to the boy, and he recovered."],[1913,"I had a maternal uncle from the Anṣār who used to perform ruqyah for snakebite. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade ruqyah, so my uncle came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you forbade ruqyah, but I perform ruqyah for snakebite.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Present it to me.\" He said: So he presented it to him. He said: \"There is no harm in this. This is from the covenants.\""],[1914,"A man from the Anṣār used to perform ruqyah for scorpion stings. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade ruqyah. He said: So he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you forbade ruqyah, but I used to perform ruqyah for scorpion stings.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever of you can benefit his brother, let him do so.\""],[1915,"A boy was born to a man among us, and he named him Muḥammad. His people said to him: \"We will not let you name him with the name of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So he set off carrying his son on his back and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a boy was born to me and I named him Muḥammad. My people said to me: 'We will not let you name him with the name of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\" He said: \"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah, for I am only Qāsim, distributing among you.\""],[1916,"I used to pray the noon prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would take a handful of pebbles and place them in my palm, then transfer them to the other palm until they cooled, then place them for my forehead so that I could prostrate, due to the intense heat."],[1917,"We did not kill the merchants of the polytheists during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1918,"He forbade the thunyā (exception in a sale) unless it is made known."],[1919,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the price of a dog and a cat, except the trained one."],[1920,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us, six hundred men, with Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ, and we had with us only a sack of dates. He said: So we divided it, and each man among us received five dates or seven dates. We ate them until hunger overtook us. He said: We started sucking the date stones. When hunger overtook us, we went to the seashore, and there was a huge creature like a large sand dune from which the water had receded. Some of us said: \"Shall we eat this when it is dead meat?\" Abū ʿUbaydah said: \"You are warriors in the path of Allah, eat, for there is no harm.\" So we ate from it, salted some of it, and took provisions. When we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we mentioned that to him, and he said: \"There is no harm in it. Does any of you have any of it to feed me?\" He said: Some of us said to others: \"Yes.\" So we sent some of it to him."],[1921,"ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAmr b. Ḥarām died or was martyred while owing a debt. I sought the help of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against his creditors to reduce his debt. I asked them but they did not agree. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Go and sort your dates into categories: the ʿajwah separately, and ʿadhq Zayd separately, into categories, then send for me.\" He said: So I did that, then sent for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came and sat at its top or in its middle, then said: \"Measure out for the people.\" He said: So I measured for them until I paid them what they were owed. Then my dates remained as if nothing had been taken from them."],[1922,"There is no soul on earth that lives to be a hundred years old."],[1923,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya, for I have been made a distributor (Qasim) to divide among you."],[1924,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya, for I have been made a distributor (Qasim) to divide among you."],[1925,"We used to pray Jumu'ah with the Prophet ﷺ, then we would return and give rest to our camels."],[1926,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse without a waist-wrapper, whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not let his wife enter the bathhouse, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not eat at a table upon which wine is drunk."],[1927,"The Arabs used to be led away by a man called Abu Sayyarah on a donkey, but when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj, Quraysh stood at their stations, and they used to say: 'We are the Hums.' He went out until he stood at 'Arafat, and that is His saying: 'Then depart from where the people depart.'"],[1928,"Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge in Allah from knowledge that does not benefit."],[1929,"He stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."],[1930,"Abu Bakr used to pray following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people used to pray following the prayer of Abu Bakr."],[1931,"Whoever intends to fast should eat the pre-dawn meal, even if only a little."],[1932,"The Throne shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh."],[1933,"The Prophet ﷺ sold a mudabbar (a slave freed after the owner's death)."],[1934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[1935,"When any of you finishes his food, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies."],[1936,"Faith is among the people of the Hijaz, while harshness and hardness of hearts are toward the east, among Rabi'a and Mudar."],[1937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ equipped an army until midnight or nearly so, then came out to us and said: 'The people have prayed and slept, while you are still waiting for this prayer. Indeed, you will continue to be in prayer as long as you wait for it.'"],[1938,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how are you this morning?' He said: 'Better than one who has not begun the morning fasting, and has not visited a sick person.'"],[1939,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said:"],[1940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to his companions one night while they were waiting for the 'Isha' prayer, and said: 'The people have prayed and slept, while you are waiting for it. Indeed, you are in prayer as long as you wait for it.' Then he said: 'Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the old age of the elderly, I would have delayed this prayer until the middle of the night.'"],[1941,"Al-Nu'man b. Qawqal came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if I make lawful what is lawful, make unlawful what is unlawful, and pray the prescribed prayers, will I enter Paradise?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[1942,"The likeness of the five prayers is that of a flowing, abundant river at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times every day."],[1943,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say three days before his death: 'Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah.'"],[1944,"When any of you has finished praying in his mosque, let him make for his house a share of his prayer, for Allah will place in his house good from his prayer."],[1945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram for Hajj only."],[1946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man performing ablution while washing his leather socks, so he poked him with his hand and said: 'We were not commanded to do this.' He said: 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed him with his hand from the front of the leather socks to the shin, and spread his fingers apart, one time only.'"],[1947,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon. He said to him: “Did you pray before you came?” He said: “No.” He said: “Pray two rak'ahs, and keep them brief.”"],[1948,"When a great event occurs, or a dark wind blows, then you should say takbir, for it disperses the black dust."],[1949,"I asked Abu Salamah b. 'Abd al-Rahman: “Which part of the Qur'an was revealed first?” He said: “O you wrapped in garments.” I said: “Or 'Read in the name of your Lord who created'.” He said: “I asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah: 'Which part of the Qur'an was revealed first?' He said: 'O you wrapped in garments.' I said: 'Or Read in the name of your Lord who created.' Jabir said: 'I will not tell you except what...'”"],[1950,"I asked Abu Salamah: “Which part of the Qur'an was revealed first?” He said: “O you wrapped in garments.” He said: I said: “I was informed that the first surah to be revealed from the Qur'an was: 'Read in the name of your Lord who created'.” Abu Salamah said: “I asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah: 'Which part of the Qur'an was revealed first?' He said: 'O you wrapped in garments.' I said to him: 'I was informed that the first surah to be revealed from the Qur'an was: Read in the name of your Lord who created.' Jabir said: 'I will not tell you except what...'”"],[1951,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a funeral procession passed by us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for it. When we went to carry it, it turned out to be the funeral of a Jewish woman. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is the funeral of a Jewish woman.” He said: “Death is a terror, so when you see a funeral procession, stand up.”"],[1952,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ looked over the martyrs who had been killed that day and said: “Wrap them in their blood, for I have witnessed for these.” So two or three men would be buried in a single grave, and he would ask: “Which of them knew more of the Qur'an?” and he would place him forward. Jabir said: “My father and my paternal uncle were buried that day in one grave.”"],[1953,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[1954,"There is nothing between a servant and abandoning faith except abandoning prayer."],[1955,"We were with Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah on a military expedition or an army, and our provisions ran out. We spotted a fish cast up by the sea and wanted to eat from it, but Abu 'Ubaydah forbade us. Then he said: “We are messengers of the Messenger of Allah and in the path of Allah, so eat.” We ate from it. When we returned, we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “If you have any of it with you, send it to us.”"],[1956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us out as three hundred riders, with Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah as our commander, to lie in wait for a Quraysh caravan. We stayed on the coast for half a month and were struck by severe hunger until we ate khubat leaves. He said: So that army was called the Army of Khubat. Then the sea cast up for us a creature called al-'Anbar, and we ate from it for half a month until our bodies recovered, and we anointed ourselves with its fat. Abu 'Ubaydah took one of its ribs and looked for the tallest camel in the army, placed it on him, and it passed beneath it."],[1957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a leather bag containing dates. When it was exhausted, we missed it, and a man would bring something. He said: We extracted from its eyes such-and-such a jar of fat. He said: When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, he asked us: “Do you have any of it with you?”"],[1958,"A man from the Muhajirun kicked a man from the Ansar. The Ansari said: 'O Ansar!' and the Muhajir said: 'O Muhajirun!' When the Prophet ﷺ heard that, he said: 'What is this call of Jahiliyyah?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a man from the Muhajirun kicked a man from the Ansar.' He said: 'Leave it, for it is stinking.' Then 'Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul said: 'Have they done it? If we return to Madinah, the more honorable will surely expel from it the meaner.' 'Umar said: 'Let me, O Messenger of Allah, strike the neck of this hypocrite.' He said: 'Leave him, lest people say that Muhammad kills his companions.'"],[1959,"The Prophet ﷺ came to 'Abdullah b. Ubayy after he had been placed in his grave. He ordered that he be brought out, and he was taken out and placed on his knees. He blew on him from his saliva and clothed him with his shirt. And Allah knows best."],[1960,"A man from the Muhajirun kicked a man from the Ansar. He said: The people of this one came and the people of that one came. These said: 'O Muhajirun!' and those said: 'O Ansar!' That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Leave it, for it is stinking.' Then he said: 'Indeed, what is this call of Jahiliyyah? Indeed, what is this call of Jahiliyyah?'"],[1961,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who pays it, its two witnesses, and its scribe, and said: 'They are equal.'"],[1962,"Abu Bakr said: 'Whoever has a promise from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him stand.' He said: I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ promised to give me such and such,' and he scooped with his hand three scoops. He said: Abu Bakr said: 'When wealth comes to us, come to us.' He said: Wealth came to him, so I went to him. He said: I scooped it with my two hands, and he said: 'Count it,' and it was five hundred. He said: He gave me another thousand. He said: And he said: 'Do you have any wealth besides it?' He said: I said: 'No.' He said: 'When a year passes over it, pay its zakah.'"],[1963,"Whoever has a promise, let him stand."],[1964,"I ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman bread and meat, and they prayed without performing wudu'."],[1965,"What is between my minbar and my room is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and indeed my minbar is upon a canal from the canals of Paradise."],[1966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought from me a camel that I owned while we were on a journey. He said: He granted me its use until we arrived. When we arrived, I brought him the camel and handed it over to him. He ordered for me its price: two uqiyyahs. I left, and there was his messenger following me. He said: 'Come, the Prophet ﷺ is calling you.' I thought that he had changed his mind. When I came to him, he said to me: 'Take your camel, for it is yours.' He said: I left and met a man from the Jews, and I told him what had happened. He began to marvel and said: 'He gave you the price and returned the camel to you?'"],[1967,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'When the wealth of Bahrain comes, we will give you like this and like this.'"],[1968,"When it was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Say: He is the Able to send upon you punishment from above you,' he said: 'I seek refuge in Your Face.' 'Or from beneath your feet,' he said: 'I seek refuge in Your Face.' 'Or to confuse you in factions and make you taste the might of one another,' he said: 'These two are lighter, or these two are easier.'"],[1969,"War is deception."],[1970,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon. He said: 'Have you prayed?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then pray two rak'ahs.'"],[1971,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon. He said: 'Have you prayed?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then pray two rak'ahs.'"],[1972,"I said to 'Amr: 'Did you hear Jabir b. 'Abd Allah say: A man passed by carrying arrows in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Hold them by their heads?'"],[1973,"A man said on the day of Uhud: 'O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed, where will I be?' He said: 'In Paradise.' So he threw away some dates that were in his hand and fought until he was killed."],[1974,"That some people will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise."],[1975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O Jabir, have you married?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'A virgin or a previously married woman?' He said: I said: 'No, rather a previously married woman.' He said: 'Why not a young girl, so that you could play with her and she could play with you?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my father was killed on the day of Uhud and left nine daughters, and they are nine sisters to me, so I did not like to bring to them a young girl like them, but rather a woman who could comb their hair and take care of them.' He said: 'You have done well.'"],[1976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fed us the meat of horses, and he forbade us the meat of donkeys."],[1977,"I entered Paradise and saw in it a house, and I heard in it a commotion. I said: 'Who is this for?' They said: 'For a man from Quraysh.' I said: 'Who is he?' They said: ''Umar b. al-Khattab.' I wanted to enter it, but then I remembered your jealousy, O Abu Hafs. So he wept and said: 'Would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?'"],[1978,"A man made a slave of his a mudabbar (one to be freed after his death), and he had no property other than him. So the Prophet ﷺ sold him, and Ibn al-Nahham bought him from him."],[1979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me when I married: 'Have you acquired any anmat (embroidered mats or carpets)?' I said: 'How could we have anmat?' He said: 'Indeed, they will come.'"],[1980,"While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon, a caravan arrived in Madinah, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rushed to it until only twelve men remained with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, if you had all followed one another until none of you remained, the valley would have swept you into the Fire.' Then this verse was revealed: 'And when they saw a transaction or a diversion, they rushed to it and left you standing.' He said: 'Among the twelve who remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were Abu Bakr and 'Umar.'"],[1981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the pulpit: 'Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge with Allah from knowledge that does not benefit.'"],[1982,"Vinegar is an excellent condiment, and it is enough evil for a man to despise what is brought near to him."],[1983,"When it was revealed: “Say: He is the One able to send upon you punishment from above you or from beneath your feet,” the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I seek refuge in Your countenance.” “Or to confound you into factions and make you taste the violence of one another,” he said: “This is lighter” or “this is easier.”"],[1984,"When it was revealed: “He is the One able to send upon you punishment from above you,” he said: “I seek refuge in Your countenance,” “or from beneath your feet,” he said: “I seek refuge in Your countenance,” “or to confound you into factions,” he said: “This is lighter.”"],[1985,"A man from the Ansar freed a slave of his, and he had no property other than him. He said: That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “Who will buy him from me?” So Nu'aym b. 'Abd Allah bought him for eight hundred, and he handed it over to him. He said: I heard Jabir say: A Coptic slave who died last year."],[1986,"Ishaq related to us, Hammad related to us with his chain, the like of it."],[1987,"A man from the Muhajirun struck a man from the Ansar on the back of his neck. The people of this one and the people of that one gathered, and this one said: “O Muhajirun!” and that one said: “O Ansar!” That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “Leave it, for it is stinking.” Then he said: “Indeed, what is the matter with the call of Jahiliyyah? Indeed, what is the matter with the call of Jahiliyyah?”"],[1988,"Ishaq related to us, Hammad related to us with his chain, something similar."],[1989,"A man entered while the Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering the sermon on Friday. He said: “Have you prayed, O so-and-so?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then stand and pray two rak'ahs.”"],[1990,"Ishaq related to us, Hammad b. Zayd related to us from 'Amr b. Dinar from Jabir, who said: While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon to the people on Friday—and he mentioned something similar."],[1991,"My father died and left seven daughters or nine daughters—Hammad said: And I only think he said nine—so I married a previously married woman. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Have you married, O Jabir?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “A virgin or a previously married woman?” I said: “A previously married woman.” He said: “Why not a young girl so that you could play with her and she could play with you?” or he said: “so that you could laugh with her and she could laugh with you?” He said: I said: “'Abd Allah died and left nine daughters, and I disliked bringing them someone like them, so I wanted a woman who could take care of them.” He said to me: “May God bless you,” or he said something good."],[1992,"My father died and left nine—or seven—and he mentioned something similar, except that he said: He said to me: “May God bless you,” and he supplicated for me."],[1993,"O Abu Muhammad, did you hear Jabir b. 'Abd Allah narrate from the Prophet ﷺ that God will bring out people from the Fire by intercession? He said: Yes."],[1994,"Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with his chain of narration the like of it:"],[1995,"A man passed by some arrows in the mosque whose tips were exposed, so he was ordered to take them by their tips so that he would not scratch a Muslim."],[1996,"Did you hear Jabir narrate that a man entered the mosque with arrows, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Take them by their tips? He said: Yes."],[1997,"He forbade leasing land."],[1998,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade leasing land."],[1999,"On the day of Khaybar he forbade the meat of domesticated donkeys and permitted the meat of horses."],[2000,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to Ka'b b. Ujra: O Ka'b b. Ujra, prayer is a means of nearness, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire. O Ka'b b. Ujra, people go forth in two ways: one who sells himself and so destroys his own neck, and one who buys himself and so frees his own neck."],[2001,"When a slave marries without the permission of his master, he is an adulterer."],[2002,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was never asked for anything and said: No."],[2003,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: O Jabir, I know that God revived your father and said to him: Wish upon God. He said: I wish to return to the world and be killed once more. He said: I have decreed that they shall not return."],[2004,"When the emigrants who had crossed the sea returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: Will you not tell of the wonders you saw in the land of Abyssinia? Some youths among them said: O Messenger of God, while we were sitting, an old woman from among their old women passed by carrying a water jar on her head. She passed by a young man of theirs, and he placed one of his hands between her shoulders and pushed her, so she fell on her knees and her jar broke. When she rose, she turned to him and said: You will know, O treacherous one, when God sets up the Footstool and gathers the first and the last, and the hands and feet speak of what they used to earn, then you will know how your affair and my affair will be before Him tomorrow. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: She spoke the truth, indeed she spoke the truth. How can God sanctify a people whose weak are not protected from their strong?"],[2005,"When it was the (battle of) the Trench, I looked at the Messenger of God ﷺ and found that he had placed a stone between himself and his waist-wrapper to straighten his back from hunger."],[2006,"A man called Abu Humayd came with a bowl of milk from al-Naqīʿ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Will you not cover it, even with a stick that you lay across it?”"],[2007,"A man used to perform ruqya for scorpion stings, and the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade ruqya. He said: “O Messenger of God, you have forbidden ruqya, but I used to perform ruqya for scorpion stings.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever of you is able to benefit his brother, let him do it.”"],[2008,"My maternal uncle, one of the Ansar, used to perform ruqya for venomous stings. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Present it to me.” So he presented it to him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no harm in this; this belongs to the covenants.”"],[2009,"When one of you prostrates, let him keep his posture balanced, and not spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."],[2010,"A woman was with ʿAʾishah — Abu Yala said: pouring water on a boy whose nostrils were dripping blood. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered and said: “What is the matter with this boy?” They said: “He has al-ʿudhra.” He said: “Woe to you, O assembly of women! Do not kill your children. Any woman whose child has al-ʿudhra or a pain in his head should take Indian costus root, grind it, then apply it as a nasal drop.” Then he ordered ʿAʾishah, and she did that to the boy, and he recovered."],[2011,"When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, he kept his arms apart until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[2012,"The delegation of Thaqif asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “Our land is a cold land, so what about the ritual bath?” He said: “As for me, I pour three handfuls over my head.”"],[2013,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions did not walk between al-Safa and al-Marwa except a single walking: his first walking."],[2014,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ looked over the martyrs who had been killed that day and said: “Wrap them in their blood, for I have testified on behalf of these.” Two or three men would be buried in a single grave, and he would ask which of them knew more of the Quran and put him first. Jabir said: “My father and my paternal uncle were buried that day in a single grave.”"],[2015,"I entered Paradise and saw in it a house, or a palace, and heard in it a sound, or clamor. I said: “For whom is this?” It was said: “It is for Ibn al-Khattab.” Sufyan said: Ibn al-Munkadir added: “I wanted to enter it, but I remembered your jealousy.” Umar wept and said: “O Prophet of God, would I be jealous of you?”"],[2016,"O Jabir, have you taken carpets (anmat)? I said: “O Messenger of God, how could we have carpets?” He said: “Indeed, they will come to be.”"],[2017,"A boy was born to a man among us, so he named him al-Qasim. We said, “We will not give you the kunya Abu al-Qasim, nor will we grant you comfort.” He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, “Name him Abd al-Rahman.”"],[2018,"That the Prophet ﷺ ate meat then prayed without performing ablution, and that Abu Bakr ate meat then prayed without performing ablution, and that Umar b. al-Khattab ate meat then prayed without performing ablution."],[2019,"I fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr came to me, walking. They found me unconscious, so the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution and poured his ablution water over me, and I regained consciousness. I asked him, “O Messenger of God, what should I do with my wealth?” He did not answer me until the verse of inheritance was revealed—meaning His saying: “God instructs you concerning your children.”"],[2020,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, “If the wealth of Bahrain comes, I will give you this much and this much and this much.” Sufyan gestured with his hand, showing us three scoops toward his head. The wealth of Bahrain did not arrive until the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away. When the wealth of Bahrain arrived, Abu Bakr stood and said, “Whoever has a promise or a debt owed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, let him come.” Jabir said, “I went to him and said, ‘The Prophet ﷺ promised me.’” He said, “So he gave me. Then I came to him afterward asking him, but he did not give me. Then I came to him a third time and said, ‘I asked you and you did not give me, and I asked again and you did not give me. Either give me, or be stingy with me.’ He said, ‘What disease is worse than stinginess! I did not withhold from you any time except while I intended to give you.’”"],[2021,"He scooped for me a scoop, so I counted it and found it to be five hundred. He said, “Then he said, ‘Take twice its like.’”"],[2022,"My father was killed on the day of Uhud. He was brought, having been mutilated, and placed before the Messenger of God ﷺ. I wanted to uncover him but my people forbade me twice. Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be lifted. Sufyan said, “It was as if they had been returned to their battlefields.” He heard the sound of a woman wailing, and said, “Who is this?” They said, “The daughter of Amr, or the sister of Amr.” He said, “Why does she weep? Or let her not weep, for the angels kept shading him with their wings until he was lifted.”"],[2023,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called upon the people on the day of the Trench, and al-Zubayr responded. Then he called upon the people again, and al-Zubayr responded. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr.”"],[2024,"Madinah is like a bellows: it expels its impurities and its goodness shines forth."],[2025,"The Jews used to say, “Whoever has intercourse with his wife from her rear but in her vagina, the child will be cross-eyed.” Then it was revealed: “Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish.”"],[2026,"There is no harm in animals, two for one, hand to hand, but there is no good in it on credit."],[2027,"That the Prophet ﷺ saw a man with filthy clothes and said, “Could this man not find something to clean his clothes?” And he saw a man with disheveled hair and said, “Could this man not find something to settle his hair?”"],[2028,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed nine [years] in Madinah without performing Hajj. Then he announced to the people to set out. When he reached Dhu al-Hulayfah, he prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Asma’ bt. Umays gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr, so she sent word to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said, “Perform ghusl, bind a cloth, and enter ihram.” She did so. When the chest of the Messenger of God’s mount settled on the back of al-Bayda’, he entered ihram, and we entered ihram, not knowing it except as Hajj, and for that we had set out. The Messenger of God was among us, the Qur’an was being revealed to him, and he knew its interpretation; he only did what he was commanded. Jabir said: I looked before me, behind me, to my right, and to my left as far as I could see, and the people were on foot and riding. The Messenger of God ﷺ began to say the talbiyah: “Here I am, O God, here I am. Here I am, You have no partner. Here I am. Indeed, praise and blessing are Yours, and the dominion. You have no partner.” When we arrived in Makkah, he began by touching the corner, then he walked briskly for three circuits and walked normally for four. When he finished his tawaf, he went to the Maqam and said, “God said: ‘And take the station of Abraham as a place of prayer.’” So he prayed two rak’ahs behind the Maqam of Ibrahim. Ja’far said: My father said, “He recited in them the surah of Tawhid: ‘Say: O disbelievers’ and ‘Say: He is God, One.’” He said: “He did not mention that from Jabir.” Then he went to the corner and touched it, then he went to al-Safa and said, “We begin with what God began with: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of God.’” He climbed al-Safa until the House was visible to him, said “God is great” three times, and said: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death. In His hand is all good, and He has power over all things” three times. Then he supplicated. Then he descended from al-Safa and walked until, when his feet reached the bottom of the valley, he walked briskly, and when his feet emerged from the bottom of the valley, he walked to al-Marwah. He climbed al-Marwah until the House was visible to him, and said the same as he had said at al-Safa. He performed seven circuits and said, “Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram, and whoever has one should remain in ihram. Had I not brought a sacrificial animal, I would have exited ihram. If I had known at the beginning of my affair what I know now, I would have entered ihram for Umrah.” He said: Ali arrived from Yemen, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “With what did you enter ihram, O Ali?” He said, “I said, ‘O God, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger enters ihram.’” He said, “I have a sacrificial animal, so do not exit ihram.” Ali said: I entered upon Fatimah, and she had applied kohl and worn dyed clothes. I said, “Who ordered you to do this?” She said, “My father ordered me.” He said: Ali used to say in Iraq: “I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, agitated against Fatimah, seeking confirmation of what she said.” He said, “She has spoken the truth; I ordered her.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ sacrificed one hundred camels, sixty-three of them with his own hand, and Ali sacrificed the rest. Then he took a piece from each camel, cooked them together, and they ate some of the meat and drank some of the broth. Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju’shum said, “O Messenger of God, is this for this year of ours or forever?” He said, “No, rather forever. Umrah has entered into Hajj.” And he interlaced his fingers."],[2029,"We came to Jabir b. 'Abdullah then, and he mentioned something similar."],[2030,"Al-Hajjaj arrived and he used to delay the prayer, so we asked Jabir b. 'Abdullah about that. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Zuhr at midday when the sun declines, and 'Asr while the sun was still clear, and Maghrib when the sun sets, and 'Isha sometimes he would delay it and sometimes he would hasten it. If he saw that the people had gathered, he hastened, and if he saw that they had delayed, he delayed. And they, or he, used to pray Subh in the dark before dawn."],[2031,"Whoever does not abandon mukhabarah, let him give notice of war from Allah and His Messenger."],[2032,"When one of you lies on his back, let him not place one of his legs over the other."],[2033,"That he made the two sons of Suriya swear when he asked them about stoning. He made them swear: How do you find it in the Book of Allah, in your Book? He said: He made them swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, who sent down the Torah to Musa: How do you find the punishment of the adulterer in your Book?"],[2034,"I attended the 'Eid with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He prayed before he delivered the sermon, without any adhan or iqamah. Then he delivered the sermon after he had prayed, and he admonished the people and reminded them. Then he came to the women and admonished them, and Bilal was with him. He reminded them and commanded them to give charity. He said: The woman began to throw her ring, her earring, and the like. The Prophet ﷺ commanded Bilal and he gathered what was there. Then he said: 'Among you, few will enter Paradise.' A woman said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why?' He said: 'You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands.'"],[2035,"We used to perform tamattu' with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we would slaughter a cow on behalf of seven, and share in it."],[2036,"Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. If he is unable, let him give it to his Muslim brother and not rent it out."],[2037,"For every disease there is a remedy. When the remedy for the disease is applied, it heals by Allah's permission."],[2038,"Jabir b. 'Abdullah visited al-Muqanna', then said: 'I will not leave until you undergo cupping, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"In it there is healing.\"'"],[2039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that from every jadd of ten awsuq of dates, one bunch be hung in the mosque for the poor."],[2040,"The wife of Sa'd b. al-Rabi' said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Sa'd has died and left two daughters and his brother. His brother took possession of what Sa'd left, and women are only married for their wealth.' He did not answer her in that gathering. Then she came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the two daughters of Sa'd.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Summon his brother for me.' He came to him and said: 'Give his two daughters two-thirds, his wife one-eighth, and you will have what remains.'"],[2041,"Every good deed is charity, and what a man spends on his family and his wealth is recorded for him as charity, and what he uses to protect his honor is charity for him. He said: And every expenditure of a believer in other than disobedience—upon God is its recompense, guaranteed—except his expenditure on building."],[2042,"Any young man who marries in his youth—his devil cries out, 'Woe to him! Woe to him! He has protected his religion from me.'"],[2043,"If only one day remained of my life, I would meet God with a wife. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The worst of you are your unmarried ones.'"],[2044,"How will you be when a large bowl is brought to you in the morning and another in the evening? They said, 'O Messenger of God, on that day we will be in good.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Rather, you are better today.'"],[2045,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Describe God.' So God sent down: 'Say: He is God, the One' to its end."],[2046,"The most beloved food to God is that over which many hands gather."],[2047,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Our clothes in Paradise—will we weave them with our own hands?' The companions of the Prophet ﷺ laughed. The Bedouin said, 'Why do you laugh at a coarse man asking a learned one?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'You have spoken the truth, O Bedouin, but they are fruits.'"],[2048,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about Abu Talib: 'Does your prophethood benefit him?' He said, 'Yes, I brought him out from the depth of Hell to a shallow part of it.' He was asked about Khadijah because she died before the obligations and rulings of the Qur'an, and he said, 'I saw her by a river of the rivers of Paradise, in a house of reeds, with no clamor and no toil.' He was asked about Waraqah b. Nawfal, and he said, 'I saw him in the interior of Paradise, wearing fine silk.' He was asked about Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl, and he said, 'He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a community alone, between me and Jesus (peace be upon them both).'"],[2049,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the noon prayer when the sun had passed its zenith."],[2050,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas approached, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'This is my maternal uncle.'"],[2051,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he came upon two graves whose occupants were being punished. He said, 'Indeed, they are not being punished for something great. One of them used to backbite people, and the other was not careful from his urine.' He called for a fresh palm branch or two branches, broke them, then commanded each piece to be planted on a grave. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Indeed, it will lighten their punishment as long as they remain fresh, or as long as they do not dry.'"],[2052,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in a house with a group of the emigrants, among them Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Let each man go to his equal.' The Prophet ﷺ went to Uthman and embraced him, saying, 'You are my guardian in this world, and you are my guardian in the Hereafter.'"],[2053,"The people of Paradise will eat and drink therein, and they will not spit, nor urinate, nor blow their noses, nor defecate. He said: Then what happens to the food? He said: Belching and perspiration like the perspiration of musk; they will be inspired with glorification and praise just as you are inspired with breath."],[2054,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say three days before his death: Verily, none of you should die except while he has a good opinion of Allah."],[2055,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act for a matter that has already been decreed, or for a matter we are initiating? He said: For a matter that has already been decreed. Then Suraqah b. Malik said: Then what is the point of action? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Everyone is facilitated for that for which he was created."],[2056,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he came upon two graves whose occupants were being punished. He said: Verily, they are being punished, and not for something major: backbiting and urine. Then he called for a palm stalk and split it, and placed a piece on each of the two graves, and said: I hope it will be lightened for them as long as they do not dry."],[2057,"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus or blood is better for him than to have it filled with poetry with which I have been satirized."],[2058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Abu Taybah and he cupped him. Then he asked him: How much is your tax? He said: Three sa's. So he reduced it by one sa'."],[2059,"Use ithmid antimony at bedtime, for it clears the eyesight and makes the hair grow."],[2060,"Greeting comes before speaking."],[2061,"Do not invite anyone to food until he greets."],[2062,"We were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Battle of Badr when he smiled in his prayer. When he finished the prayer, we said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you smile. He said: Mikail passed by me, and on his wing there was a trace of dust, and he was returning from pursuing the people, and he laughed at me, so I smiled at him."],[2063,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."],[2064,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ picking kabath fruit, and he said: Choose the black ones from it, for they are the best. We said: Did you used to herd sheep? He said: Yes, and is there any prophet who did not herd them?"],[2065,"I saw myself being admitted into Paradise, and there was al-Rumaysa', the wife of Abu Talha. He said: And I heard footsteps in front of me. I said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Bilal. He said: And I saw a white palace in whose courtyard was a maiden. I said: To whom does this palace belong? She said: To 'Umar b. al-Khattab. I wanted to enter it and look at it, but I remembered your jealousy, O 'Umar. 'Umar said: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, would I be jealous of you?"],[2066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping."],[2067,"Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[2068,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by two graves and said: They are being punished, and they are not being punished for something major. As for one of them, he did not protect himself from his urine, and as for the other, he used to backbite people."],[2069,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[2070,"Qasim narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[2071,"Qasim narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[2072,"Qasim b. Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[2073,"Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or attributes himself to other than his patrons out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah. And whoever insults his parents or his parent, then likewise. And whoever sacrifices to other than Allah, then likewise. And whoever deems lawful anything of the sacred boundaries of Makkah, then likewise. And whoever says about me what I did not say, then likewise."],[2074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of the dogs of Madinah. Ibn Umm Maktum came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind, my dwelling is far, and I have a dog. He granted him a concession for some days, then he commanded that his dog be killed, and it was killed."],[2075,"Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind, my dwelling is far, and I hear the call to prayer. He said: If you hear the call to prayer, then respond, even if crawling or dragging yourself."],[2076,"There was a man who would carry wine from Khaybar to Madinah and sell it to the Muslims. He carried some of it with money and arrived in Madinah with it. A man from the Muslims met him and said: O so-and-so, wine has been forbidden. So he placed it where he ended up on a hill and covered it with cloaks. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that wine has been forbidden? He said: Yes. He said: Should I return it to the one from whom I bought it? He said: It is not proper to return it. He said: Can I give it as a gift?... And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[2077,"The feet of a servant do not become dusty for an hour of the day in the path of God but that they are forbidden to the Fire."],[2078,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have a slave woman, and I practice coitus interruptus with her. He said: Indeed, that does not prevent any matter that God intends. It was not long before he came and said to the Prophet ﷺ: She has become pregnant. The Prophet ﷺ said: I am the servant of God and His Messenger."],[2079,"A woman said: O Messenger of God, pray for me and for my husband. He said ﷺ: May God bless you and your husband."],[2080,"My community will not cease to prevail upon the truth until Jesus son of Mary descends, and their imam says: Come forward. He says: You are more entitled, some of you are commanders over others, a matter by which God has honored this community."],[2081,"My father ordered a meat and vegetable stew, and it was made. Then he ordered me and I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I came to him while he was in his dwelling. He said: He said to me: What do you have with you, O Jabir? Is this meat? He said: I said: No. He said: I came to my father, and he said to me: Did you see the Messenger of God ﷺ? I said: Yes. He said: Did you not hear him say anything? He said: I said: Yes, he said to me: What do you have with you, O Jabir? Is this meat? He said: Perhaps the Messenger of God ﷺ had a craving, so he ordered a domestic sheep of ours, and it was slaughtered. Then he ordered it and it was roasted. Then he ordered me and I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me: What do you have with you, O Jabir? I told him, and he said: May God reward the Ansar well on our behalf, especially Abdullah b. Amr b. Haram and Sa'd b. Ubadah."],[2082,"My father ordered a stew and it was made, then he ordered me and I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned something similar."],[2083,"The best jihad is one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed."],[2084,"On the day of the Trench, the Messenger of God ﷺ called upon the people for someone to bring him news of Banu Qurayzah. Al-Zubayr volunteered. Then he called upon them again and al-Zubayr volunteered, three times. The Prophet ﷺ said: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."],[2085,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Umm al-Sa'ib, or Umm al-Musayyib, while she was shivering. He said: What is with you, O Umm al-Sa'ib, or O Umm al-Musayyib, that you are shivering? She said: The fever, may God not bless it. He said: Do not revile the fever, for it removes the sins of the son of Adam just as the bellows removes the dross of iron."],[2086,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a man came to him with something like an egg of gold that he had obtained in one of the expeditions. He said: He came to him on his left side and said to him: O Messenger of God, take this from me as charity, for by God, I have not woken up owning any wealth other than it. He turned away from him. Then he came to him on his right side and said to him the like of that, and he turned away from him. Then he came to him from in front of him and said to him the like of that. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, angrily: Bring it. He said: When he gave it to him, he threw it at him; had it hit him it would have hurt or wounded him. Then he said: One of you comes with his wealth, or as he said, owning nothing other than it, giving it as charity, then afterwards sits begging from people? Charity is only from surplus wealth. Take your wealth from us, we have no need of it."],[2087,"Every good deed that one of you does for a rich or poor person is charity for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[2088,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us istikharah just as he taught us... and he mentioned the hadith."],[2089,"A cow toppled over onto some wine and drank from it, so they feared for it. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Eat it, and there is no harm in eating it.\""],[2090,"Whoever intends to fast, let him take the pre-dawn meal, even if it be with a little something."],[2091,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I slept, then woke up; then I slept, then woke up. A man among the Muslims stood up and said: \"The prayer, the prayer.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with his head dripping, and he led us in prayer. Then he said: \"Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would have liked them to pray this prayer at this hour.\" Al-Furat said: I think it was the night prayer."],[2092,"\"There are no days better in the sight of Allah than the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah.\" He said: A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, are they better or their equivalent in fighting in the path of Allah?\" He said: \"They are better than their equivalent in fighting in the path of Allah, except for a man who covers his face with dust (in battle). And there is no day better in the sight of Allah than the Day of Arafah. Allah descends to the lowest heaven and boasts to the inhabitants of heaven about the people of the earth, saying: 'Look at My servants, disheveled, dusty, and sun-scorched, coming from every deep valley, hoping for My mercy though they have not seen My punishment.' I have not seen a day on which more people are freed from the Fire than the Day of Arafah.\""],[2093,"When Quraysh accused me of lying on the night I was taken on the Night Journey to Jerusalem, I stood in the Hijr, and Allah displayed Jerusalem to me, and I began to inform them of its signs while I was looking at it."],[2094,"Whoever is given a lifetime gift for himself and his descendants, it is his outright; the giver may not impose any condition or reservation in it."],[2095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled: Any man who gives another man a lifetime gift for him and his descendants, saying: 'I give it to you and to your descendants as long as any of you remain,' then it belongs to the one to whom it was given, and it does not revert to its owner because he gave a gift in which inheritance rights take effect."],[2096,"Women are not married except to suitable matches, and only guardians may marry them off, and there is no dowry less than ten dirhams."],[2097,"Indeed Satan has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but he is still active in stirring up enmity among them."],[2098,"The Prophet ﷺ said in one of his hadiths: \"When the Arabs are humiliated, Islam is humiliated.\""],[2099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and a man from his companions entered upon a man from the Ansar while he was diverting water in his garden. He said: \"Do you have any water that has sat overnight in an old waterskin? Otherwise we will drink directly from the source.\" He said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I have water that has sat overnight in a waterskin.\" He said: So we went to the arbor. He went and milked a sheep over water that had sat overnight in an old waterskin. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank, then I did the same and his companion drank."],[2100,"I ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he prayed without performing a new ablution after his first ablution. Then I ate with Abu Bakr and he prayed without performing a new ablution. Then I ate with Umar and he prayed without performing a new ablution. Then I ate with Uthman and he prayed without performing a new ablution."],[2101,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a donkey that had been branded on its face, and he said, \"Did I not forbid this? May God curse the one who did it,\" and he forbade striking the face."],[2102,"He came to visit al-Muqannaʿ b. Sinān, who was the maternal uncle of ʿĀṣim, the brother of his mother. He greeted him while he was wearing a cloak and a waist-wrapper, and his sight had been affected. He said, \"What are you complaining of?\" after touching his head and beard with some yellow dye. He said, \"An abscess that has kept me from sleeping and made me sleepless.\" Jābir said, \"O boy, call a cupper for us.\" Al-Muqannaʿ said, \"What will you do with the cupper, O Abū ʿAbd Allāh?\" He said, \"I want to apply a cupping glass to it.\" He said, \"May God forgive you. By God, if a garment touches me or a fly lands on me it hurts me.\" When he saw his alarm at that, he began to narrate to us from the Messenger of God ﷺ saying, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'If there is good in any of your remedies—or if there is any—it is in a cupping incision, or a drink of honey, or a cauterization by fire that suits the ailment, but I do not like to be cauterized.'\" Then he called the cupper and had the cupping glass applied to his abscess. When it reached [the end of] his eyebrow, he incised it with a scalpel he had with him, and God, blessed and exalted, removed the harm that was in it, and he was healed."],[2103,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ approached. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"This is my maternal uncle.\""],[2104,"Between the servant and disbelief is the abandonment of prayer."],[2105,"When al-Ḥajjāj arrived, he began to delay the prayer. I asked Jābir—or he was asked—and he said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray ẓuhr at midday, pray ʿaṣr while the sun was still bright, pray maghrib when the sun had set, and for ʿishāʾ, if people had gathered he would hasten it, and if people were few he would delay it, and he used to pray ṣubḥ in the dark before dawn.\""],[2106,"I used to pray maghrib with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then return to my family in Banū Salima, who were a mile from Madinah—or he said, from the mosque—while I could still see the places where arrows fell. Then he said, \"Ẓuhr is as its name indicates, at midday; ʿaṣr while the sun is white and clear; maghrib as its name indicates; and ʿishāʾ—the Prophet ﷺ would sometimes delay it and sometimes hasten it.\""],[2107,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying in a single garment, wrapped around himself. Abū al-Zubayr said, \"I saw Jābir praying in a single garment, wrapped around himself.\""],[2108,"Whoever fears that he will not wake up at the end of the night should perform witr at the beginning of the night, and whoever of you hopes to wake up at the end of the night should perform witr at the end of the night, for prayer at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."],[2109,"One day the people complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ of thirst. The Messenger of God ﷺ called for a large wooden bowl. He said, \"Does anyone of you have water?\" He said, \"A small vessel for ablution was brought and he poured it into it.\" He said, \"Then the Prophet ﷺ placed his hand in the bowl.\" Jābir said, \"I was looking at the springs gushing between the fingers of the Messenger of God ﷺ while the people were drawing water.\""],[2110,"The Messenger of God ﷺ threw the pebble at the jamrah with stones like those thrown with the fingers."],[2111,"Whoever guarantees me what is between his two jaws and his two legs, I will guarantee him Paradise."],[2112,"O Messenger of God, do we act for a matter that has already been decreed or for a matter that we initiate anew? He said, \"For a matter that has already been decreed.\" Surāqa said, \"Then what is the point of action?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Everyone is facilitated for that for which he was created.\""],[2113,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon, his eyes would redden, his voice would rise, and his anger would intensify until it was as if he were warning of an army, saying: “They will raid you in the morning and in the evening.” And he would say: “I and the Hour have been sent like these two” – and he would join his index and middle fingers – and he would say: “To proceed: the best speech is the Book of God, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, the worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance.” Then he would say: “I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his family; and whoever leaves behind debt or dependents, they come to me and are my responsibility.”"],[2114,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on the Day of Sacrifice on his mount at Mina."],[2115,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a sermon on the Day of Sacrifice at Mina."],[2116,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the earnings of a cupper. He said – I think he said: “Feed it to your water-carrying camels.”"],[2117,"We did not call the hypocrites disbelievers during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[2118,"A man said on the Day of the Conquest: “O Messenger of God, I have vowed that if God grants you victory, I will pray in the Holy House (Jerusalem).” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Pray here.” The man repeated it to the Prophet ﷺ two or three times, each time he said: “Pray here.” When he insisted much, he said: “Then it is up to you.”"],[2119,"When one of you enters the mosque, let him pray two rak'ahs before sitting down."],[2120,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ learned of the death of the Negus, he stood with his companions and they formed two rows behind him, and he prayed over him."],[2121,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon, his eyes would redden, his anger would intensify, and his voice would rise until it was as if he were warning of an army. Then he said: “The Hour has come upon you morning and evening. I and the Hour have been sent like these two: the index and middle fingers. To proceed: the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, the worst of matters are their newly invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance.”"],[2122,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray on his mount in whatever direction it faced during the expedition of Anmar."],[2123,"War is deception."],[2124,"They would not put their hands in the food until the Messenger of God ﷺ began."],[2125,"I sold the Messenger of God ﷺ a camel, on condition that I could ride it until I returned to Madinah."],[2126,"That he sold the Prophet ﷺ a camel and stipulated that he could ride it back to his family."],[2127,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and he bought a camel from me and granted me its riding until I reached Madinah. When we arrived, I brought the camel to him and handed it over, and he ordered that I be given its price. Then I left, and behold, the Messenger of God ﷺ had caught up with me. He said: I thought, 'Perhaps he has changed his mind about it.' So when I came to him, he returned the camel to me and said, 'It is yours.' He said: Then I passed by a man from the Jews and told him about it. He said: He began to marvel. He said: 'He bought the camel from you, gave you the price, and then gave it back to you as a gift?' I said, 'Yes.'"],[2128,"We came to Jabir b. 'Abd Allah while he was among the Banu Salima, and we asked him about the farewell pilgrimage of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He told us that the Messenger of God ﷺ stayed in Madinah for nine years without performing Hajj. Then it was announced to the people that the Messenger of God ﷺ would perform Hajj that year. Many people came to Madinah, all seeking to follow the Messenger of God ﷺ and do what he did. The Messenger of God ﷺ set out when five days remained of Dhu al-Qa'da, and we set out until we reached Dhu al-Hulayfa, where Asma' gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr. She sent a message to the Messenger of God ﷺ asking, 'What should I do?' He said, 'Perform ghusl, wrap yourself with a cloth, and then enter ihram.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ went on until his she-camel stood him upright on al-Bayda', and he began the talbiya with tawhid: 'Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa-l-ni'mata laka wa-l-mulk, la sharika lak.' The people also began the talbiya, and they added 'Dha al-Ma'arij' and similar words, while the Prophet ﷺ heard them and said nothing to them. I looked and extended my gaze in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and there were riders and walkers, and behind him the same, and on his right the same, and on his left the same. Jabir said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was among us, and the Qur'an was being revealed to him, and he knew its interpretation, and whatever he did we did. He said: We set out intending nothing but Hajj. When we reached the Ka'ba, the Prophet of God ﷺ touched the Black Stone, then did ramal for three circuits and walked for four. When he finished, he went to the Station of Ibrahim and prayed two rak'as behind it, and he recited: 'And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.' He said: In those two rak'as he recited Surah al-Ikhlas and Surah al-Kafirun. Then he touched the Stone, then went out to al-Safa and said, 'We begin with what God began with,' and he recited: 'Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the symbols of God.' Then he climbed al-Safa until he could see the House, and he said takbir, then said: 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is able to do all things. There is no god but God alone. He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone.' Then he supplicated and returned to this same speech. Then he descended, and when his feet reached the bottom of the valley he ran, and when he ascended he walked, until he came to al-Marwa and climbed it, and when he could see the House he said upon it the same as he had said upon al-Safa. When he was on the seventh circuit at al-Marwa, he said: 'O people, if I had known beforehand what I now know, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal, and I would have made it an 'umra. So whoever among you does not have a sacrificial animal should exit ihram and make it an 'umra.' So all the people exited ihram. Suraqa b. Ju'shum said, 'O Messenger of God, is this for this year of ours or forever?' He said: The Prophet ﷺ interlaced his fingers and said, 'Rather, forever,' three times. 'The 'umra has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.' 'Ali arrived from Yemen, bringing with him a sacrificial animal, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had brought a sacrificial animal with him from Madinah. There was Fatima, who had exited ihram and put on dyed clothes and applied kohl, and she said, 'My father commanded me.' 'Ali objected to that. He said: Ja'far said: This phrase was not mentioned by Jabir b. 'Abd Allah; 'Ali said in Kufa: I went away, agitated, to seek confirmation from the Messenger of God ﷺ about what Fatima had mentioned. I said, 'O Messenger of God, Fatima has exited ihram, put on dyed clothes, applied kohl, and said, \"My father commanded me.\"' He said, 'She spoke the truth, she spoke the truth, she spoke the truth. I commanded her to do that.' Then he returned to the hadith of Jabir and said to 'Ali, 'With what did you enter ihram?' He said: I said, 'O God, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger entered ihram, and I have the sacrificial animal with me.' He said, 'Then do not exit ihram.' He said: The total number of sacrificial animals brought by the Prophet ﷺ and by 'Ali was one hundred. The Messenger of God ﷺ slaughtered sixty-three with his own hand, and he gave 'Ali the rest to slaughter, and he made him a partner in his sacrificial animal. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered that a piece be taken from each camel, and they were put in a pot, and they ate from its meat and drank from its broth. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I have slaughtered here, and Mina is all a place of slaughter.' Then he stood and said, 'I have stood here, and 'Arafa is all a place of standing.' And he stood at al-Muzdalifa and said, 'I have stood here, and al-Muzdalifa is all a place of standing.'"],[2129,"I asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah: Is hyena meat eaten? He said: Yes. I said: Is it game? He said: Yes. I said: Did you hear that from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Yes."],[2130,"Indeed, the thing I most fear for my community after me is the practice of the people of Lot."],[2131,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ set out for Makkah in the year of the conquest during Ramadan, and he fasted until he reached Kura' al-Ghamim. He fasted Ramadan, and the people fasted with him. It was said to him, 'The people are finding the fast difficult, and they are only looking at what you do.' So he called for a cup of water after 'Asr and drank while the people were watching. Some of the people fasted and some broke their fast. Then he learned that some people had fasted, and he said, 'Those are the disobedient ones.'"],[2132,"Cover the vessels, tie the waterskins, shut the doors, and keep your children close in the evening, for the jinn spread out and snatch. And extinguish the lamp when you go to sleep, for the little vermin may drag the wick and burn the people of the house."],[2133,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: Which prayer is best? He said: Long standing in supplication."],[2134,"That the Prophet ﷺ lifted the liability for natural disasters."],[2135,"He is not of us who wails, shaves, or tears his clothes."],[2136,"You are today upon a religion, and I will vie with the nations through you, so do not walk backward after me."],[2137,"The grazing animal is exempt; the well is exempt; the mine is exempt; and a fifth is due on buried treasure."],[2138,"Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will never guide you when they themselves have gone astray. Either you will believe in falsehood or you will disbelieve the truth. By Allah, if Musa were alive among you, it would not be lawful for him except to follow me."],[2139,"If you are given this, then take it; if you are not given it, then beware. Then he mentioned the two sons of Suriya until the Prophet ﷺ came to them and said to them: By the One who sent down the Torah upon Musa, by the One who parted the sea, and by the One who sent down upon you the manna and the quails, are you more knowledgeable? They said: Our people have attributed that to us. He said: One of them said: He adjures us by the like of this. He said: Do you find that looking is fornication, embracing is fornication, and kissing is fornication? So when four witnesses testify that they saw him begin and repeat as the applicator enters the kohl-pot, then stoning is due."],[2140,"Whoever is given a gift and finds the means, let him repay it. If he does not find the means, let him praise it. Whoever praises it has thanked him, and whoever conceals it has been ungrateful. Whoever adorns himself with what he was not given is like one wearing two garments of falsehood. He said with his fingers like this—the forefinger and the middle finger."],[2141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: O people, Allah has detachments of angels that settle and stand at the gatherings of remembrance on earth, so graze freely in the gardens of Paradise. They said: What are the gardens of Paradise, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The gatherings of remembrance. So go forth in the morning and the evening in remembrance of Allah, and remember Him by yourselves. Whoever loves to know his station with Allah, then Allah places the servant with Him where the servant places Him with himself."],[2142,"Whoever sells a slave who has property, the property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it."],[2143,"The Prophet ﷺ came to visit me, not riding a mule or a hackney."],[2144,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mukhabarah: renting land for half of the produce."],[2145,"Whoever has surplus water or land, let him cultivate it or let his brother cultivate it, and do not sell it."],[2146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited selling fruit until it has begun to ripen (tushaqqih)."],[2147,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the funeral prayer over the Negus and said four takbirs."],[2148,"Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[2149,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest wearing a black turban."],[2150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ʿArafah with tranquility, and he commanded tranquility. He hastened in Wādī Muḥassir and said: “Take your rites from me, for I do not know—perhaps you will not meet me after this year of yours or this day of yours.” And he threw pebbles like the small pebbles used for throwing."],[2151,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a donkey whose nostrils were smoking, having been branded on its face. He said: “Did I not curse the one who did this? Indeed, let no one brand on the face, nor strike on the face.”"],[2152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Banū al-Najjār and heard a sound, so he came out alarmed and said: “Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave.”"],[2153,"We slaughtered on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyah seventy camels, a camel for seven people. And he said: “Let a group share in the sacrificial animal.”"],[2154,"Indeed, Abraham made Allah's House sacred and secure, and I have made Madinah sacred. So it is sacred between its two lava tracts: its game is not to be hunted, nor its thorn trees cut."],[2155,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[2156,"The throne of Iblīs is upon the sea. He sends out raiding parties, and the greatest of them in his sight is the greatest of them in temptation."],[2157,"Indeed, Iblīs has despaired that the praying ones should worship him, but he is in inciting discord among you."],[2158,"On the day of Khaybar, he forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys and permitted the flesh of horses."],[2159,"The midday prayer is as its name, and the afternoon prayer while the sun is alive and white, and the sunset prayer as its name. The Prophet ﷺ used to pray with us, and we could see the places where arrows fell. The Prophet ﷺ used to hasten the night prayer, and the dawn prayer is as its name."],[2160,"The Banū Salimah mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ the distance of their homes. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Banū Salimah, your homes—for your footsteps are recorded.”"],[2161,"The Prophet ﷺ cauterized a man on his median cubital vein twice."],[2162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the hyena, and he said: \"It is game, and a ram is to be given for it if a pilgrim in ihram kills it.\""],[2163,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a woman of the Ansar, and she spread a mat for him near a palm trunk, sprinkled water around it, slaughtered a sheep, and made food for him. He ate and we ate with him. Then he performed ablution for the Zuhr prayer and prayed. The woman said: \"O Messenger of Allah, some of our sheep's meat is left over; would you like to have dinner?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He ate and we ate, then he prayed Asr without performing ablution."],[2164,"A Jew had a debt of dates owed by my father, and my father left two gardens. The Jew's dates would have consumed both gardens. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Would you take some this year and defer some until next year?\" The Jew refused. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"O Jabir, when the date harvest is ready, notify me.\" So I notified him, and the Prophet ﷺ came with Abu Bakr and Umar. They began measuring dates for him from the lower part of the palm trees while the Prophet ﷺ was supplicating for blessing. We paid him his due in full. Ammar said: \"I think it was from the smaller of the two gardens.\" Then we brought them fresh dates, and they ate and drank. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: \"This is among the blessings about which you will be asked.\""],[2165,"You are the radiant ones with white marks on their foreheads and limbs."],[2166,"On the day of al-Ta'if, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a private conversation with Ali, and it was prolonged. Some of his companions said: \"His private conversation with his cousin has gone on long.\" This reached him, and he said: \"I did not confide in him; rather, Allah confided in him.\""],[2167,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and said: \"O people, I have not stood among you with news that came to me from heaven, but news reached me and I rejoiced at it, and I would like you to rejoice at your Prophet's joy. While a group of riders were traveling in the sea, their food ran out, and an island was raised up for them. They went out seeking bread, and the Jassasah met them. I said to Abu Salamah: 'What is the Jassasah?' He said: 'A woman dragging the hair of her skin and her head.' She said: 'In this palace there is news of what you seek.' They came to it and found a man in chains. He said: 'Tell me, or ask me, and I will tell you.' The people remained silent. He said: 'Tell me about the date palms of Baysan, do they bear fruit?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Tell me about the marsh of Zughar, is there water in it?' They said: 'Yes.' They said: 'He is the Dajjal. The earth will be folded for him in forty days, except for what is in Taybah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Taybah is Madinah. There is no gate of its gates but an angel with a drawn sword is guarding it, and in Makkah it is the same.' Then he said: 'In the Persian Sea it is not; in the Roman Sea it is not,' three times. Then he struck his right palm on his left three times. Ibn Abi Salamah said to me: 'In this hadith there is something I did not memorize.' We said: 'What is it?' He said: 'Jabir testified that he is Ibn Sayyad.' I said: 'No, for Ibn Sayyad has died.' He said: 'Even if he died.' I said: 'He has accepted Islam.' He said: 'Even if he accepted Islam.' I said: 'He has entered Madinah.' He said: 'Even if he entered Madinah.'\""],[2168,"When one of you finishes his food, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies."],[2169,"A man freed a slave of his upon his death. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Who will buy him from me?\" Nuaym b. Abdullah bought him, and the Prophet took the price and gave it to him."],[2170,"If one of you is poor, let him begin with himself."],[2171,"Part of the perfection of prayer is straightening the rows."],[2172,"A town-dweller should not sell on behalf of a desert-dweller. Leave people alone, so that Allah may provide for some of them through others."],[2173,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it ripens."],[2174,"Whoever is a partner in a dwelling or in palm trees, he has no right to sell it until he informs his partner. If he is pleased, he takes it; if he dislikes it, he leaves it."],[2175,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went to reconcile between the Banu Amr b. Awf of the Ansar. He said: And the prayer became due. Bilal said to Abu Bakr: Shall I give the call and you lead the people in prayer? He said: Yes. So Bilal gave the iqamah, and Abu Bakr stepped forward and led the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came, and they began clapping with their hands for Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr would hardly turn when he was in prayer. When they clapped, he turned and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he stepped back. The Prophet ﷺ gestured with his hand to him to pray, but he refused. So the Messenger of God ﷺ stepped forward and prayed. When he finished his prayer, he said to Abu Bakr: What prevented you from praying? He said: It was not fitting for the son of Abu Quhafah to lead the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he turned to the people and said: What is this clapping? Clapping in prayer is only for women. If one of you needs something, let him say subhan Allah."],[2176,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Umm al-Sa'ib or Umm al-Musayyab while she was shivering from fever. He said to her: What is wrong with you, O Umm al-Sa'ib, that you are shivering? She said: The fever, may God not bless it. He said: Do not revile it, for it removes the sins of the children of Adam just as the blacksmith's bellows remove the dross of iron."],[2177,"A man came to Madinah as an emigrant. He said: He fell ill with a severe fever. He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, release me from the emigration. He said: No, by God, I will not release you. Islam cannot be released. Al-Hajjaj said: He mentioned that more than once, and each time he refused him. So he left without his permission. The Prophet ﷺ was told about it and said: It is good (Taybah); it expels the filth of men just as the bellows expel the dross of iron."],[2178,"Al-Tufayl b. Amr al-Dawsi came to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Makkah and said to the Messenger of God ﷺ: Come to a fortified stronghold, with number and equipment. Abu al-Zubayr said: Al-Daws is a fortress at the top of a mountain, reachable only through a path like a sandal strap. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Is there anyone with you behind you? He said: I do not know. He said: So he turned away from him, because of what God had reserved for the Ansar. He said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, al-Tufayl b. Amr came as an emigrant to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with him a man from his tribe. That man fell ill with a severe fever. He went out, took a knife, and cut his veins, and the blood flowed until he died. He was buried. Then he came in a dream at night to al-Tufayl b. Amr in a fine appearance, covering his hand. Al-Tufayl said to him: Is it so-and-so? He said: Yes. He said: What did you do? He said: My Lord did good to me; He forgave me for my emigration to His Prophet. He said: What happened to your hands? He said: My Lord said: We will never repair what you corrupted of yourself. Al-Tufayl related his dream to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he raised his hand and said: O God, and for his two hands, forgive. O God, and for his two hands, forgive. O God, and for his two hands, forgive."],[2179,"He used to prostrate on the top of his forehead with the hairline."],[2180,"The Prophet ﷺ used to stand by a piece of wood, leaning on it to deliver the sermon every Friday, until a man from the Romans came to him and said: If you wish, I will make for you something such that when you sit on it, it will be as if you are standing. He said: Yes. He said: So he made for him the minbar. When he sat on it, the piece of wood moaned like a she-camel longing for her young, until the Prophet ﷺ came down and placed his hand on it. The next day I saw that it had been moved. We said: What is this? He said: The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar came and moved it."],[2181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us one day on the minbar and said: While some people were traveling in the sea, the Jassasah met them. I said: What is the Jassasah? He said: A woman dragging the hair of her skin and her head. She said: In this palace is the news of what you want. So they went to it, and there was a man in chains. He said: Tell me, or ask me and I will tell you. The people were silent. He said: Tell me about the date palms of Baysan, the spring of Zughar, and Uman: has it borne fruit? They said: Yes. He said: Tell me about the marsh of Zughar: is there water in it? They said: Yes, it is full, and its sides overflow. He said: He said: He is the Messiah; the earth will be folded for him, and he will traverse it in forty, except what is of Taybah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: That is Madinah; there is no gate of its gates but an angel with a drawn sword is standing, preventing him from entering it, and the like is in Makkah. Then he said: In the Persian Sea it is not; in the Roman Sea it is not. Three times. He said: Ibn Abi Salamah said: In this hadith there is something I did not memorize. He said: Jabir testified that it is Ibn Sayyad. I said: Ibn Sayyad has died. He said: Even if he died. I said: He has embraced Islam. He said: Even if he has embraced Islam. I said: He has entered Madinah. He said: Even if he has entered Madinah."],[2182,"We did not hear the Messenger of God ﷺ, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar, disclose to us any supplication over the funerals."],[2183,"I fell ill, and the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me and blew into my face, and I recovered."],[2184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that any of us lie down placing one of his legs over the other."],[2185,"There will surely come upon the people a time when a contingent of their armies will go out and it will be said: Is there anyone among you who accompanied Muhammad, so that you may seek victory through him and be granted victory? Then it will be said: Is there anyone among you who accompanied Muhammad? It will be said: No. Then: Who accompanied his Companions? It will be said: No. Then it will be said: Who saw someone who accompanied his Companions? If they heard of him from beyond the sea, they would come to him."],[2186,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Which of the people is most knowledgeable? He said: The one who gathers the knowledge of the people to his own knowledge, and every possessor of knowledge is hungry."],[2187,"The people will become many and my Companions will become few, so do not revile them. May Allah curse whoever reviles them."],[2188,"I was in the second or third row when the Prophet ﷺ prayed over the Negus."],[2189,"Sulayk came to the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, so he commanded him to pray two light rak'ahs."],[2190,"The prophets were shown to me, and I am the one most resembling Ibrahim."],[2191,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and Asr at Arafat with one adhan and two iqamahs, and Maghrib and Isha with one adhan and two iqamahs."],[2192,"He granted them a concession to cut down the palm trees, then he made it strict upon them. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there sin upon us for what we cut, or upon us for what we left? Then Allah revealed: Whatever you cut down of the tender palm trees or left standing on their roots, it was by Allah's permission."],[2193,"Allah sent down the scrolls of Ibrahim on the first night of Ramadan, and the Torah was sent down upon Musa on the sixth night of Ramadan, and the Zabur was sent down upon Dawud on the eleventh night of Ramadan, and the Quran was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ on the twenty-fourth night of Ramadan."],[2194,"Between a man—or he said between a servant—and disbelief is the abandonment of the prayer."],[2195,"My maternal aunt was divorced, and she wanted to harvest her palm trees. A man forbade her from going out to them, so she went to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: Yes, go and harvest them, for perhaps you will give charity and do good."],[2196,"He heard Jabir b. Abd Allah mention withdrawal (coitus interruptus), and he said: We used to practice it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2197,"Do not revile the night and the day, nor the sun and the moon, nor the winds, for they are sent as a mercy to one people and as a punishment to another."],[2198,"Whoever revives dead land has a reward in it, and whatever the wild animals eat from it is a charity for him."],[2199,"Ask God for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge with God from knowledge that does not benefit."],[2200,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of people reciting the Quran in the mosque, and he said, “Recite the Quran before there comes a people who will straighten it as an arrow is straightened, hastening it and not delaying it.”"],[2201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood as a preacher on Friday and said, “It may be that a man is present for Friday prayer while he is within a mile of Madinah, yet he does not attend the Friday prayer.” He said, then he said a second time, “It may be that a man is present for Friday prayer while he is within two miles of Madinah, yet he does not attend it.” And he said a third time, “It may be that he is within three miles of Madinah, yet he does not attend the Friday prayer, and God will set a seal upon his heart.”"],[2202,"That he heard Jabir b. Abd Allah being asked about riding sacrificial camels, and he said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Ride her in a fair manner if you are forced to it, until you find another mount.’”"],[2203,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ stood on the pulpit and said, “While some people were traveling in the sea, their food ran out, and an island was raised up for them. They went out seeking bread, and the Jassasah met them.” I said to Abu Salamah, “What is the Jassasah?” He said, “A woman dragging the hair of her head.” She said to them, “In this palace is the news of what you seek.” So they came to it, and there they found a man who was bound. He said, “Tell me, or ask me, and I will inform you.” The people were silent, so he said, “Tell me about the date palms of Baysan and Ariha—or Ariha—has it fruited?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “Then tell me about the marsh of Zughar, is there water in it?” They said, “Yes.” They said, “He is the Dajjal. The earth will be folded up for him, and he will traverse it in forty days, except for what is in Taybah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed Taybah is Madinah. There is no gate among its gates but an angel has drawn his sword, preventing him from entering it. And in Makkah there is the like of that.” Then he said, “In the sea of Persia it is not, and in the sea of Byzantium it is not.” Abu Salamah said to me, “There is something in this hadith that I did not retain.” He said, “Jabir b. Abd Allah testified that he is Ibn Sayyad.” I said, “But he has died.” He said, “Even if he has died.” I said, “But he has embraced Islam.” He said, “Even if he has embraced Islam.” I said, “But he has entered Madinah.” He said, “Even if he has entered Madinah.”"],[2204,"Excellent is vinegar as a condiment. It is enough evil for a man that he despises what is offered to him."],[2205,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ jogged from the Black Stone to the Black Stone."],[2206,"We were on a journey, and a man fasted and then fainted. His companions stood over him, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by. They said, “He fasted.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[2207,"Ride her in a fair manner if you are forced to it, until you find another mount."],[2208,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ was cupped on the two jugular veins and between the shoulders, and he gave the cupper his wage. Had it been prohibited, he would not have given it to him."],[2209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Friday alone."],[2210,"I asked Jabir b. Abd Allah about wheat for dates with surplus, hand to hand. He said: During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to buy a sa' of wheat for six sa's of dates, hand to hand. If it is one type, then there is no good in it except like for like."],[2211,"He was on a journey in Ramadan. He and his companions came upon a pool. He said to the people: Drink. They said: We drink and you do not drink? He said: I am the least burdened of you; I am riding. He dismounted and drank, and they drank."],[2212,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Makkah, the cross-people who collect tallow came to him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we collect this tallow from carrion and other things, and it is only for seasoning and ships. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: May Allah curse the Jews. Fats were forbidden for them, but they sold them and consumed their price. He forbade them from that."],[2213,"Whoever supports three daughters, caring for them, being merciful to them, and being kind to them, he will be in Paradise. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two, until we said: If a person had said, 'One,' he would have said, 'One.'"],[2214,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand until we came to one of the chambers of his wives and he entered. Then he gave me permission and I entered. He said: Is there any lunch or any dinner? They said: Yes. Three small loaves were brought. He said: Is there any condiment? They said: No, except a little vinegar. He said: Bring it, for what an excellent condiment vinegar is. Jabir said: I have continued to love it since I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that about it."],[2215,"When a man relates a hadith to a group and then turns away, it is a trust."],[2216,"No Muslim plants a tree except that it is charity for him: what is eaten from it, what is stolen from it, what the birds eat from it, and what the wild animals eat from it."],[2217,"The 'umra is valid for the one to whom it is given, and the ruqba is valid for the one to whom it is given."],[2218,"A man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they mentioned and praised him. He said: Who will kill him? Abu Bakr said: I will. He went and found the man had marked out a spot for himself and was standing praying in it. When he saw him in that state, he returned and did not kill him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Who will kill him? Umar said: I will. He went and saw him praying standing in a marked spot, so he returned and did not kill him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Who will deal with him, or who will kill him? Ali said: I will. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You, but I do not think you will catch up with him. He went and found that he had left."],[2219,"We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of al-Hudaybiya and camped at al-Suqya. Muadh b. Jabal said: Who will draw water for us in our water-skins? Jabir said: I said: I will. I went out with a group of youths with me until we came to the water at al-Uthaya, between which there is about twenty-three miles. He said: We came to the water at al-Uthaya and drew water into our cistern and into our water-skins, until after nightfall, when there was a man whose camel was contending with him at the cistern. He said: Bring them to water. And behold, it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He brought them to water and took hold of his she-camel's halter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed Isha, with Jabir, as mentioned, beside him. Then after Isha he prayed thirteen rak'ahs."],[2220,"There is none of you, no soul born, upon whom a hundred years will come while it is still alive."],[2221,"I was sitting in my house when the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me. He gestured to me, so I got up and went to him. He took me by the hand and we went until he came to one of the rooms of his wives. He entered, then gave me permission, so I entered, while she was behind the veil. He said, 'Is there any lunch?' They said, 'Yes.' Three flat loaves were brought and placed down. The Messenger of God ﷺ took one loaf and placed it before himself, took another loaf and placed it before me, then took the third and broke it into two halves, placing one half before himself and one half before me. Then he said, 'Is there any condiment?' They said, 'No, except a little vinegar.' He said, 'Bring it, for what an excellent condiment it is.'"],[2222,"When you are in fertile land, give the mounts their fill and do not go beyond the camping spots. When you are in barren land, travel quickly, and upon you is the night journey, for the earth is folded up at night. If the ghouls appear to you, hasten to the call to prayer. Do not pray on the main roads, and do not camp on them, for they are the abode of snakes and beasts of prey. Do not relieve yourselves on them, for they are the places of cursing."],[2223,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with an egg of gold that he had found in one of the military expeditions, and said, 'Take it, O Messenger of God, as charity, for by God, I have not woken up owning anything besides it.' He turned away from him. Then he came to him from his left and said the same, then he came to him from in front of him and said the same. He said, 'Give it to me,' angrily, took it and threw it at him with a throw that, had it hit him, would have wounded or injured him. Then he said, 'One of you brings all his wealth and gives it as charity, then sits and begs from people. Indeed, there is no charity except from surplus wealth.'"],[2224,"When you hear the barking of dogs and the braying of donkeys, seek refuge in God from Satan, for they see what you do not see. Reduce your going out when the feet have quieted, for God disperses in His creation during His night whatever He wills. Close the doors, for Satan does not open a door that has been closed. Tie the mouths of the waterskins, cover the vessels, and extinguish the lamps."],[2225,"The Messenger of God ﷺ fixed the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Syria at al-Juhfah, for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam, for the people of Ta'if at Qarn, and for the people of Iraq at Dhat Irq."],[2226,"In livestock, two for one is no problem, but it is not permissible on credit."],[2227,"A man vowed to pray in Jerusalem. He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about that, and he said to him, 'Pray here,' meaning the Sacred Mosque. He said, 'O Messenger of God, I only vowed to pray in Jerusalem.' He said, 'Pray here.' He said, 'And I think he said the third time: Pray where you said.'"],[2228,"I asked Abu Salamah, 'Which part of the Qur'an was revealed first?' He said, 'O you wrapped in garments.' I said, 'Or Recite.' Jabir said, 'I will tell you what the Messenger of God ﷺ told us. He said: I stayed in Hira' for a month. When I finished my stay, I descended and entered the valley. I was called, so I looked in front of me, behind me, to my right and to my left, and saw no one. Then I was called again, and I looked and saw no one. Then I was called again, and I looked and saw no one. I raised my head, and there he was on the throne in the air, meaning Gabriel. A severe trembling seized me. I came to Khadijah and said, 'Wrap me up.' They wrapped me up and poured water over me. Then God revealed: O you wrapped in garments, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your garments purify.'"],[2229,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade onions and leeks. He said, 'Need overcame us, so we ate some of it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever eats of this foul plant, let him not approach our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what humans are harmed by,' or he said, 'the children of Adam.'"],[2230,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ghusl, he poured water over his head three times. A man from Banu Hashim said, 'My hair is thick.' He said, 'The hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ was thicker than your hair and better.'"],[2231,"The Prophet ﷺ prescribed blood-money for every clan, then wrote that it is not lawful to take as a client the freedman of a Muslim man without his permission."],[2232,"We used to sell our slave women who were mothers of children while the Prophet ﷺ was alive among us, and he did not see any harm in that."],[2233,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me on an errand. When I returned, he was on his mount. I greeted him, but he did not return anything to me. Zakariyya added: Then I greeted him again, but he did not return anything to me. Then their two narrations agree after that: I saw him raising his head and prostrating, so I moved aside from him. Then he said: What did you accomplish regarding your errand? I said: I did such and such. He said: Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was praying. Zakariyya added: When he finished his prayer, he called me and returned the greeting to me, and said: I was praying."],[2234,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing any animal by confinement (ṣabr)."],[2235,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he would teach us a surah from the Quran: In the name of God. All salutations, prayers, and pure words are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I ask God for Paradise, and I seek refuge in God from the Fire."],[2236,"Whoever says: Glory be to God, the Magnificent, and with His praise, a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."],[2237,"When one of you takes charge of his brother's funeral, let him make his shroud good."],[2238,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade branding on the face and striking the face."],[2239,"A man manumitted a slave of his to take effect after his death (tadbīr), and then the man fell into need. The Prophet ﷺ said: Who will buy him from me? Nuʿaym b. ʿAbd Allah bought him, and he took his price and gave it to him."],[2240,"Every Prophet has a supplication that he has made for his community, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection."],[2241,"Do not mix fresh dates with unripe dates, nor raisins with dried dates."],[2242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went on twenty-one military expeditions."],[2243,"I was present with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of ʿAqabah."],[2244,"I went on nineteen military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ. Jabir said: I did not witness Badr or Uhud; my father prevented me. He said: When ʿAbd Allah was killed on the day of Uhud, I never stayed behind from the Messenger of God ﷺ in any expedition at all."],[2245,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade wiping oneself with a bone or with dung."],[2246,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was carrying stones with them for the Kaaba, wearing his lower garment. His uncle al-Abbas said to him, \"O nephew, would that you untie your lower garment and put it on your shoulder, between you and the stones?\" He said: So he untied it and put it on his shoulder. He said: Then he fell down unconscious. He said: After that day he was never seen naked."],[2247,"He forbade images in the house, and he forbade a man to make that."],[2248,"No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop, and then a wild animal, a bird, or anything eats from it, except that he has a reward in it."],[2249,"None of you should wipe with a napkin until he licks his hand, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies for him. And Satan lies in wait for people at everything, even at their food. And he should not lift the bowl until he licks it, for the last part of the food contains the blessing."],[2250,"When one of you eats and a morsel falls from his hand, let him remove that which causes doubt, then eat it, and not leave it for Satan. For a man does not know in which of his food the blessing lies for him."],[2251,"When you see the new moon, fast, and when you see it, break the fast. If it is obscured for you, then count thirty days."],[2252,"The Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew from his wives for a month. He came out on the morning of the twenty-ninth, and some of the people said, \"O Messenger of God, we have reached the morning of the twenty-ninth?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed the month is twenty-nine.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ clapped his hands three times: twice with all his fingers, and the third time with nine of them."],[2253,"The Prophet ﷺ intended to forbid naming with Baraka, Aflah, Yasar, Nafi, and the like of that. Then I saw him fall silent about them afterwards and not say anything. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away without forbidding that. Then Umar intended to forbid that, then he left it."],[2254,"When Safiyya bt. Huyayy entered the tent of the Prophet ﷺ, some people attended, and I attended with them, so that I might have a share in her. The Prophet ﷺ came out and said, \"Arise from your mother.\" When evening came, we attended, and the Prophet ﷺ came out in his cloak with about a mudd and a half of ajwa dates. He said, \"Eat from the wedding feast of your mother.\""],[2255,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition he undertook, and that was in Ramadan. A man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ fasted and became extremely weak, and thirst nearly killed him, and his she-camel began to enter the thorny trees. The Prophet ﷺ was informed about him, so he said, \"Bring him to me.\" He was brought, and he said, \"Are you not in the path of God and with the Messenger of God? Break your fast.\" So he broke his fast."],[2256,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered seeking permission to see the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he found people sitting at his door, none of them having been given permission. He said: Permission was given to Abu Bakr, and he entered. Then Umar came and sought permission, and permission was given to him. He found the Prophet ﷺ sitting with his wives around him, silent and grieved. He said: I will say something to make the Prophet ﷺ laugh. He said, \"O Messenger of God, if you had seen the daughter of Kharija: she asked me for maintenance, so I stood up to her and struck her neck.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed and said, \"They are around me as you see, asking me for maintenance.\" Abu Bakr stood up to Aisha, striking her neck, and Umar stood up to Hafsa, striking her neck. Each of them said, \"Do you ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for what he does not have?\" They said, \"By God, we will never ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for anything he does not have.\" Then he withdrew from them for a month or twenty-nine days. Then this verse was revealed to him: \"O Prophet, say to your wives...\" until he reached, \"for the doers of good among you a great reward.\" He said: He began with Aisha and said, \"O Aisha, I want to present to you a matter, and I would not like you to hasten in it with anything until you consult your parents.\" She said, \"What is it, O Messenger of God?\" He recited the verse to her. She said, \"Should I consult my parents concerning you, O Messenger of God? Rather I choose God and His Messenger and the Hereafter, and I ask you not to inform any woman of your wives of what I said.\" He said, \"No woman among them asks me except that I inform her. God did not send me as one who makes things difficult, but He sent me as a teacher, one who makes things easy.\""],[2257,"Do not wear the samma' (a garment wrapped so that one side is raised and the other is lowered, exposing one side of the body) in a single cloth, and none of you should eat with his left hand, and he must not walk in a single sandal, and he must not sit wrapped up in a single cloth."],[2258,"We used to practice coitus interruptus during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not forbid us from it."],[2259,"When a slave marries without his master's permission, he is a fornicator."],[2260,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me, and I went off. Then I returned after I had accomplished it. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. Something came into my mind that God knows best. He said: I said: Perhaps the Messenger of God ﷺ was upset with me because I was slow. I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. Something came into my mind more severe than the first time. Then I greeted him, and he returned my greeting and said: Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was praying, and he was on his mount facing a direction other than the qibla."],[2261,"Cover the vessel, tie the water-skin, and extinguish the lamp, for Satan does not untie a water-skin, nor open a door, nor uncover a vessel. If one of you finds nothing but to place a stick across his vessel and mention God's name, let him do so, for the little vermin may set fire to the house of its inhabitants."],[2262,"Do not eat with the left hand, for Satan eats with the left hand."],[2263,"He forbade wearing the samma' (a garment wrapped in a way that leaves one side exposed), sitting wrapped up in a single cloth, and that a man place one leg over the other while lying on his back."],[2264,"All the prophets were presented to me. Moses was a man of medium build, as if he were one of the men of Shanu'a. I saw Jesus, and the closest person I have seen resembling him is Urwa b. Mas'ud. I saw Abraham, and the closest person I have seen resembling him is your companion — meaning himself. I saw Gabriel, and the closest person I have seen resembling him is Dihya."],[2265,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for it is not possible for Satan to assume my form. He also said: If one of you has a dream, he should not tell people about Satan's playing with him in his sleep."],[2266,"If one of you sees a dream that he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times, seek refuge in God from Satan three times, and turn over to the other side from the one he was on."],[2267,"The Messenger of God ﷺ kept away from his wives for a month. He came out on the night of the twenty-ninth, and we said: Only twenty-nine have passed. He said: The month is like this, and he clapped three times and folded one finger in the last."],[2268,"Hatib b. Abi Balta'a wrote to the people of Makkah mentioning that the Messenger of God ﷺ intended to raid them. The Messenger of God ﷺ was led to the woman who had the letter, and he sent for her. The letter was taken from her head. He said: O Hatib, did you do this? He said: Yes. Indeed, I did not do it out of treachery to the Messenger of God ﷺ or out of hypocrisy. I knew that God would make His Messenger victorious and complete His affair for him. However, I was among them, and my mother was with them, so I wanted to secure her with them. Umar said to him: Shall I strike this man's neck? He said: Would you kill a man from the people of Badr? And what do you know? Perhaps God has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish."],[2269,"The best thing toward which mounts are ridden is this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."],[2270,"Umm Salamah asked permission of the Messenger of God ﷺ for cupping, so he commanded Abu Taybah, and he cupped her. Abu Yala said: I think he said: He was her brother through suckling."],[2271,"When they were with the Messenger of God ﷺ as residents, he would send the sacrificial animal. Whoever of us wished entered ihram, and whoever of us wished left it."],[2272,"Whoever dies upon something, God will resurrect him upon it."],[2273,"The people of Paradise will eat and drink therein, and will not defecate, urinate, or blow their noses, but rather it will be a perspiration of musk."],[2274,"Any believer whom I have reviled or cursed, make it for him a purification and a reward."],[2275,"People are followers of Quraysh in good and evil."],[2276,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Which of the Muslims is best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."],[2277,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I saw in a dream as if my head was cut off. The Prophet ﷺ laughed and said: When Satan plays with one of you in his dream, he should not relate it to people."],[2278,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of a dog and a cat."],[2279,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Prophet ﷺ was giving a sermon. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: When one of you comes while the imam is giving a sermon, let him pray two brief rak'ahs."],[2280,"If I live, God willing, I will command, or forbid, my community not to name themselves Aflah, Nafi', or Barakah."],[2281,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: What are the two sure things? He said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire."],[2282,"Whoever of you fears that he will not perform witr at the end of the night, let him perform witr at its beginning, for the recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and it is better."],[2283,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Aisha and there was a child with him whose nostrils were dripping blood. She said: He has udhra. He said: Do not kill your children, but any woman whose child has udhra or a pain in his head should take Indian costus, then grind it with water, then administer it into his nose. Then he commanded Aisha and she did that, and he recovered."],[2284,"Indeed in the night there is an hour during which no Muslim asks Allah for good but He gives it to him, and that is every night."],[2285,"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. If they say it, they have protected from me their blood and their wealth, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[2286,"When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."],[2287,"When a morsel of one of you falls, let him take it and not leave it for Satan."],[2288,"When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced and not spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."],[2289,"When one of you finishes the prayer in the mosque, let him assign for his house a portion of his prayer, for Allah will place in his house from his prayer good."],[2290,"Ubayy b. Ka'b complained of an ailment, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a physician to him, and he cauterized him on his median cubital vein."],[2291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut a vein from Ubayy b. Ka'b and cauterized him on his median cubital vein."],[2292,"The food of one man suffices two, the food of two men suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."],[2293,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, three days before his death: \"Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah.\""],[2294,"There are men in Madinah: whatever distance you travel or valley you traverse, they are with you; excuse has held them back."],[2295,"The likeness of the prayers is that of a flowing river at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times every day."],[2296,"When Satan hears the mention of Allah, he departs until he is at the place of al-Rawha'."],[2297,"Satan has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but he is not despaired of stirring up enmity among them."],[2298,"A man from the Ansar called al-Nu'man b. Qawqal came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do you think that if I perform the prescribed prayers, treat the lawful as lawful and the unlawful as unlawful, and do no more than that, I will enter Paradise?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[2299,"A man asked him: \"Which prayer is best?\" He said: \"Length of the qunut (standing in supplication).\""],[2300,"The Prophet ﷺ was thrown from a horse and his leg was injured. We entered upon him while he was praying, and he gestured to us with his hand. Then we entered the next day while he was praying the prescribed prayer sitting, and he gestured to us with his hand that we should sit. Then he finished and said: \"When the imam prays sitting, pray sitting; and when he prays standing, pray standing.\""],[2301,"There is no Muslim male or female who sleeps at night without a knotted rope being placed on his head. If he wakes and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. If he gets up, performs ablution, and prays, all his knots are undone, and he wakes in the morning energetic and having attained good. But if he sleeps without remembering Allah, he wakes with his knots heavy upon him."],[2302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade ruqya (incantations). My maternal uncle came to him, and he used to perform ruqya for scorpion stings. He said: \"You have forbidden ruqya, and I perform ruqya for scorpion stings.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever can benefit his brother, let him do so.\""],[2303,"When you perfume the deceased with incense, make it an odd number."],[2304,"We gave allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ under the tree that we would not flee."],[2305,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: Have you come to ask me about such-and-such? We said: Yes. He said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya. He said: And you mentioned the Hour? We said: That was so. He said: There is no soul born that will have one hundred years come upon it."],[2306,"If the son of Adam had a palm grove, he would wish for another like it, and nothing fills his belly except dust."],[2307,"There was a slave girl belonging to Abdullah b. Ubayy called Musayka, and he forced her, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained of that to him, and Allah revealed: And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution if they desire chastity, to seek the transient goods of the worldly life."],[2308,"No believing man or believing woman, and no Muslim man or Muslim woman falls ill except that Allah thereby removes his sins."],[2309,"A military expedition is sent and it is said to them: Is there among you anyone who accompanied Muhammad? It is said: Yes. So he is sought and the man is found, and victory is sought and granted to them. Then a military expedition is sent and it is said: Is there among you anyone who saw the companions of Muhammad? He is sought and not found, even if he were beyond the sea you would come to him. Then there remain people who recite the Quran but do not know what it is."],[2310,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ on his journey, and a wind blew that almost buried the rider, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This wind was sent for the death of a hypocrite. When we arrived in Madinah, indeed a great one among the great hypocrites had died on that day."],[2311,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man perform ablution and water did not reach his heel, so he said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."],[2312,"Faith is among the people of the Hijaz, and harshness and coarseness are in Rabi'a and Mudar."],[2313,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and a foul wind blew, so the Prophet ﷺ said: These are a people among the hypocrites who mentioned some people and backbit them."],[2314,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying on a mat and prostrating on it, and I entered upon him while he was praying wrapped in a garment."],[2315,"Umar saw a man perform ablution and leave a spot the size of a fingernail on his foot, so he ordered him to repeat it."],[2316,"He was asked about a man who laughs in prayer, and he said: He repeats the prayer, but does not repeat the ablution."],[2317,"If I entered upon people praying, I would not greet them."],[2318,"I used to fetch water for my companions on the day of Badr."],[2319,"When he enters his grave—meaning the deceased—and the angel comes to him, he starts up as a sleeper starts up. Then they ask him and he answers them. They say: 'What is your religion?' He says: 'Islam.' 'Let me go out.' They say to him: 'Be still.'"],[2320,"I asked Jabir while he was staying in Makkah, and he was staying among Banu Fihr. A man asked him: 'Did you call anyone of the people of the qiblah an idolater?' He said: 'God forbid.' He was alarmed at that. He said: 'Did you call anyone among you an disbeliever?' He said: 'No.'"],[2321,"\"O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\" We said: \"O Messenger of God, do you fear for us, when we have believed in what you have brought?\" He said: \"Indeed, the hearts are between\"—and al-A'mash indicated with two fingers."],[2322,"The Prophet ﷺ was approached and it was said to him: \"The fever has persisted upon us.\" He said: \"If you wish it to be lifted from you, it will be lifted; and if you wish it to be a purification for you?\" They said: \"Let it be a purification for us.\""],[2323,"Jabir b. Abd Allah said to me: \"Your cousin al-Hasan b. Muhammad asked me about the ghusl of janabah, so I said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pour water with his hand over his head three times.' He said: 'My hair is abundant.' I said: 'O son of my brother, the hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ was more abundant than your hair and better.'\""],[2324,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned garlic and onion, or one of them, and said: \"Indeed, the angels are harmed by what the son of Adam is harmed by.\""],[2325,"Whoever eats garlic, onion, or leek, let him not approach our mosque."],[2326,"If aged sheep are difficult for you, a jadha' of sheep suffices."],[2327,"Do not slaughter except a musinnah, unless it is hard for you, then slaughter a jadha'ah of sheep."],[2328,"He forbade unripe dates with dried dates, and raisins with dried dates."],[2329,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever in seven intestines."],[2330,"When you hear the barking of dogs at night or the braying of donkeys, seek refuge in God, for they see what you do not see. And reduce going out when people's feet are still, for God spreads in His night of His creation what He wills. And close the doors and mention God's name over them, for Satan does not open a door that has been closed and God's name mentioned over it. And cover the jars, and turn over the vessels, and tie the waterskins."],[2331,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas delivering a sermon on the pulpit of Basra. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: There was no prophet but had a supplication that he hastened to use in this world, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection. I am the master of the children of Adam, and no boast. I am the first from whom the earth will split open, and no boast. In my hand is the banner of praise, and Adam and those below him are under my banner, and no boast. The Day of Resurrection will be long and severe for people, until some of them say to others: 'Come with us to Adam, the father of mankind, so that he may intercede for us with your Lord and He may judge between us.' So they go to Adam and say: 'O Adam, intercede for us with your Lord so that He may judge between us.' Adam says: 'I am not in that position. I was expelled from the Garden because of my sin, and today nothing concerns me but my own self. But go to Noah.' So they say: 'O Noah, intercede for us with your Lord so that He may judge between us.' He says: 'I am not in that position. I made a supplication that drowned the people of the earth, and today nothing concerns me but my own self. But go to Abraham, the friend of the Most Merciful.' So they come to Abraham ﷺ and say: 'O Abraham, intercede for us with your Lord so that He may judge between us.' He says: 'I am not in that position. I told three lies in Islam: his saying, \"I am sick,\" and his saying, \"Rather, the eldest of them did this,\" and his saying to the king when he passed by him.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'By God, he intended by them nothing but honor for God's religion. And today nothing concerns me but my own self. But go to Moses, a servant whom God chose with His message and spoke to.' So they come to Moses and say: 'O Moses, intercede for us with your Lord so that He may judge between us.' He says: 'I am not in that position. I killed a soul, and today nothing concerns me but my own self. But go to Jesus, God's spirit and His word.' So they come to Jesus and say: 'O Jesus, intercede for us with your Lord so that He may judge between us.' He says: 'I am not in that position. I was taken as a god besides God, and today nothing concerns me but my own self. Do you see that if a piece of goods were in a sealed container, could what is inside it be reached until the seal is broken?' They say: 'No.' He says: 'Then Muhammad ﷺ is the seal of the prophets, and he has arrived, and God has forgiven him his previous and future sins.' So they come to me and say: 'O Muhammad, intercede for us with your Lord so that He may judge between us.' I say: 'I am for it,' until God permits whom He wills and is pleased. Then when God wants to judge between His creation, a caller calls out: 'Where is Ahmad and his community? Where is Ahmad and his community?' So they come, and we are the first and the last: the last to be raised and the first to be judged. So the nations are moved aside from our path, and we proceed with bright faces and limbs from the traces of purification. Then the nations say: 'This community was almost all prophets.'"],[2332,"Indeed, the first thing God created was the Pen, and He commanded it, and it wrote everything."],[2333,"I was commanded to use the tooth-stick so much that I thought a Qur'an or revelation would be sent down to me about it."],[2334,"When your brothers were struck at Uhud, God placed their souls in the crops of green birds that frequent the rivers of the Garden and eat from its fruits and shelter in golden lamps suspended in the shade of the Throne. When they found the goodness of their food, drink, and resting place, they said: 'Who will convey to our brothers about us that we are alive in the Garden, provided for, so that they do not hold back in war and do not renounce striving?' He said: Then God said: 'I will convey to them about you.' So God, blessed and exalted, sent down: 'And do not reckon those who were killed in God's way as dead; rather, they are alive with their Lord...' the verse."],[2335,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and began speaking with eloquent speech. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery, and some poetry is wisdom.'"],[2336,"No contagion, no bird omen, no owl omen, and no month of Safar. A man said to him: 'We take a mangy sheep and throw it among the flock, and then they become mangy.' He said: 'Then who infected the first one?'"],[2337,"A sheep belonging to Sawda bt. Zam'a died. She said: 'O Messenger of God, so-and-so died,' meaning the sheep. He said: 'Why did you not take its hide?' She said: 'Should we take the hide of a sheep that has died?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He only said: \"Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to an eater who eats it...\" the verse. There is no harm in your tanning it and benefiting from it.' She said: So she sent for it and peeled its hide, and made from it a waterskin until it wore out."],[2338,"Umm Hufayd, my maternal aunt, daughter of al-Harith, gave the Messenger of God ﷺ a gift of clarified butter, dried curd, and dabb lizards. The Messenger of God ﷺ called for them, and they were eaten on his table, but he left them as if he found them distasteful. If they were forbidden, they would not have been eaten on the table of the Messenger of God ﷺ, nor would he have commanded eating them."],[2339,"There is no confederation in Islam, and whatever confederation existed in the Age of Ignorance, Islam only increased it in firmness or intensity."],[2340,"A man's camel threw him and crushed his neck, so the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that he be washed with water and lote-tree leaves, that he not be touched with perfume, that he not be shrouded, and that his head not be covered. And he said: 'He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with matted hair.'"],[2341,"Guard against reporting hadith from me except what you know, for whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. And whoever lies about the Qur'an without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2342,"The Prophet ﷺ only walked briskly around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa to show the people his strength."],[2343,"The Prophet ﷺ did not perform an 'umra except in Dhu al-Qa'da."],[2344,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived at Khaybar, he handed over its lands and palm trees as a sharecropping arrangement on a half share basis."],[2345,"A thief's hand was not cut off during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ except for the price of a shield or a buckler."],[2346,"Let the best among you give the call to prayer, and let those most versed in the Qur'an lead you in prayer."],[2347,"Whoever wishes to prohibit what God and His Messenger have prohibited, let him prohibit nabidh made in earthenware jars."],[2348,"Do not go out to meet the caravans, do not leave milk unmilked in the udder to deceive buyers, and let none of you bid against another to raise the price."],[2349,"God made the prayer obligatory through the words of your Prophet ﷺ: four rak'as when resident, two rak'as when travelling, and one rak'a in times of fear."],[2350,"Whoever sees something from his ruler that he dislikes, let him be patient, for whoever separates from the community by a handspan and then dies, dies a death of the days of ignorance."],[2351,"Whoever drinks a drink until it takes away the intellect that God has given him has approached one of the gates of major sins."],[2352,"The handles of Islam and the foundations of the religion are three, upon which Islam is built. Whoever abandons one of them is thereby an unbeliever whose blood is lawful: the testimony that there is no god but God, the prescribed prayer, and the fast of Ramadan. Then Ibn 'Abbas said: You will find a man with much wealth who does not pay zakat, and he will remain an unbeliever whose blood is lawful. And you will find a man with much wealth who has not performed the pilgrimage, and he will remain an unbeliever, though his blood is not lawful."],[2353,"A man from Banu 'Amir came to the Prophet ﷺ who used to treat and heal. He said to him: 'O Muhammad, you say things; would you like me to treat you?' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and then said to him: 'Would you like me to show you a sign?' Nearby were palm trees and other trees. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called one of its branches, and it came to him prostrating and rising, prostrating and raising its head, until it reached him and stood before him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to it: 'Return to your place,' and it returned to its place. He said: 'By Allah, I will never disbelieve you in anything you say after this, ever.' Then he said: 'O Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, by Allah, I will never disbelieve him in anything he says after this, ever.' He said: And the 'adhq is the palm tree."],[2354,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who cannot perform the Hajj. Should I perform it on his behalf?' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes, perform Hajj in place of your father.'"],[2355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder, then wiped his hand on a cloth that was beneath him, then stood and prayed."],[2356,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to set out on a journey, he would say: 'O Allah, You are the companion in the journey and the deputy in the family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from difficulty in travel, and from sorrow upon return. O Allah, contract the earth for us and make the journey easy for us.' When he intended to return, he would say: 'Returning, worshipping our Lord, praising.' When he entered upon his family, he would say: 'Repentance, repentance, to our Lord is the return, leaving no sin upon us.'"],[2357,"There will certainly be people from my nation who recite the Quran and leave Islam just as the arrow passes through the game."],[2358,"Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast at its sighting and break your fast at its sighting. If it is obscured from you, then complete thirty days."],[2359,"Do not go out to meet the caravans, do not leave animals unmilked, and let not some of you bid up the price for others."],[2360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on a reed mat."],[2361,"When the verse 'May the hands of Abu Lahab perish' was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came to the Prophet ﷺ while Abu Bakr was with him. When Abu Bakr saw her, he said: 'O Messenger of Allah, she is an abusive woman, and I fear she may harm you, so perhaps you should leave.' He said: 'She will never see me.' She said: 'O Abu Bakr, your companion has satirized me.' He said: 'He does not compose poetry.' She said: 'You are believed in my sight,' and she turned away. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, she did not see you?' He said: 'An angel kept screening me from her with his wing.'"],[2362,"Every division that has been divided is according to what was divided, and every division that Islam has reached remains according to what was divided."],[2363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while in ihram on the two sides of the neck and between the shoulders, and he gave the cupper his wage; had it been unlawful, he would not have given it."],[2364,"A righteous dream is a portion - I think he said - of forty-six portions of prophethood."],[2365,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping and gave the cupper his wage."],[2366,"A delegation of Banu Asad came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke, and they were eloquent. They said: \"O Messenger of God, all of Mudar fought you, but we did not fight you. We are not fewer than them in number, nor less in strength, and we have maintained ties of kinship with you.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ heard their words, he said to Abu Bakr and Umar: \"Do they speak like this?\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, their understanding is indeed little, and Satan indeed speaks upon their tongues.\""],[2367,"A sheep belonging to Sawdah bt. Zam'ah died. She said: \"O Messenger of God, so-and-so died,\" meaning the sheep. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Why did you not take its skin?\" She said: \"Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Say: 'I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden' ... up to 'or the flesh of swine' [Q 6:145]. Which of you would eat it?\" meaning: You tan it and benefit from it. He said: So she sent for it, flayed it, tanned it, and made from it a waterskin, until it wore out in her possession."],[2368,"God says: \"If I take the two precious things of My servant, and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not approve for him any reward less than Paradise.\""],[2369,"God's anger is intense upon one whom a Prophet of God killed in the way of God, and God's anger is intense upon a people who bloodied the face of the Prophet of God ﷺ."],[2370,"Ali, al-Fadl, and Usamah entered the grave of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: And Marhab informed me that they brought in Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and it is as if I can see them in the grave: four."],[2371,"The Prophet ﷺ traveled and stayed nineteen days shortening the prayer. He said: So when we travel and stay nineteen days, we shorten the prayer; if we exceed that, we complete it."],[2372,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not recite to the jinn, nor did he see them. The Messenger of God ﷺ set out with a group of his companions heading to the market of Ukaz. The devils had been barred from the news of heaven, and meteors were sent against them. The devils returned to their people, who said: \"What is wrong with you?\" They said: \"We have been barred from the news of heaven, and meteors were sent against us.\" He said: \"This is only because of something that has happened. So strike the eastern and western parts of the earth.\" The group that had taken the direction of Tihamah passed by him at Nakhlah, while he was heading to the market of Ukaz and praying the dawn prayer with his companions. When they heard the Quran, they listened to it and said: \"This is what has barred us from the news of heaven.\" They returned to their people and said: \"O our people, we have heard a wondrous Quran that guides to rectitude, so we believed in it.\" Then God revealed to His Prophet: \"Say: It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened\" [Q 72:1]."],[2373,"The banner of the Messenger of God ﷺ was black, and his standard was white."],[2374,"Give the prescribed shares to their entitled recipients, and whatever remains is for the nearest male relative."],[2375,"Religion is sincere counsel. They said: \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"To the Book of God, to His Prophet, and to the leaders of the Muslims.\""],[2376,"It was said: \"O Messenger of God,\" when he finished at Badr, \"you should go after the caravan; there is nothing to prevent you.\" He said: Then al-Abbas called out to him: \"That is not right.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why?\" He said: \"Because God promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised.\""],[2377,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came from al-Ta'if, he alighted at al-Ji'ranah and distributed the spoils of war there, then performed 'umrah from there, and that was for the two nights remaining of Shawwal."],[2378,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out and stopped for a rest at night, then slept and did not wake until sunrise. So the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Bilal, so he gave the call to prayer, then prayed two rak'ahs."],[2379,"The camels for sacrifice became scarce at the time of the Messenger of God, so he commanded the people to use cattle."],[2380,"The People of the Book used to let their hair hang down, and the polytheists used to part their hair, and the Messenger of God ﷺ liked to agree with the People of the Book in some things about which he had not been commanded, so the Messenger of God ﷺ let his forelock hang down, then he parted it afterwards."],[2381,"God does not look at a man who has sexual intercourse with a man or a woman in her anus."],[2382,"When the Prophet ﷺ left Makkah, 'Ali took out the daughter of Hamzah, and 'Ali, Zayd, and Ja'far disputed about her. 'Ali said: She is the daughter of my brother and I am more entitled to her. Ja'far said: She is the daughter of my paternal uncle and her maternal aunt is with me. Zayd said: She is the daughter of my brother for Hamzah; the Messenger of God ﷺ had made them brothers. So the Messenger of God ﷺ said: O Zayd, you are my client and their client. And he said to 'Ali: You are my brother and my companion. And he said to Ja'far: You resemble my physical form and my character. And she goes to her maternal aunt."],[2383,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade drinking from a defective vessel."],[2384,"The death of a stranger is martyrdom."],[2385,"I and al-Fadl were on a donkey, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying at 'Arafah. We passed by part of the row, so we dismounted from it and left it browsing in the row, and the Prophet ﷺ did not say anything to us."],[2386,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about a vow that was upon his mother, who had died before fulfilling it, so he said: Fulfill it on her behalf."],[2387,"A woman from Khath'am asked the Messenger of God ﷺ on the morning of the sacrifice, saying: The obligation of God in the hajj has come upon my father, and he is a very old man who cannot sit firmly on the saddle. Do you think we should perform the hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes."],[2388,"Any hide that is tanned has become pure."],[2389,"I was among those whom the Prophet ﷺ sent ahead from Muzdalifah to Mina among the weak ones of his family."],[2390,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew back the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and said: \"O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the good dream which a Muslim sees or is seen for him. Indeed, I have been forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, magnify the Lord therein; and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is worthy that you be answered.\""],[2391,"I am amazed at one who anticipates the month, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you see it, then fast; and when you see it, then break the fast. If it is obscured for you, then complete the number of thirty.\""],[2392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and was forbidden to tie back his hair or his garments."],[2393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while he was in a state of ihram."],[2394,"No man should seclude himself with a woman, and no woman should travel unless she has a mahram with her. A man stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have been enlisted for such-and-such an expedition, and my wife has set off on Hajj.' He said: 'Go and perform Hajj with your wife.'"],[2395,"We used to recognize the end of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ prayer by the takbir."],[2396,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in a state of ihram."],[2397,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah eight rak'ahs combined and seven rak'ahs combined."],[2398,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon: \"Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever does not find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers.\""],[2399,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, saying: \"You will meet Allah barefoot, naked, walking, and uncircumcised.\""],[2400,"Al-Muhassab is nothing; it is only a place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped."],[2401,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed it until as much of the night had passed as Allah willed. 'Umar said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, the women and children have gone to sleep.' He came out and said, 'Were it not that I would impose hardship on my community, I would have prayed it at this hour' - meaning the 'isha' prayer."],[2402,"A man died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and left no heir except a slave whom he had freed. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Give him his inheritance.'"],[2403,"A woman brought out a small boy from her howdah and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is there a hajj for this one?' He said, 'Yes, and you shall have a reward.'"],[2404,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ eight and seven [rak'ahs] together. He was asked, 'Why did he do that?' He said, 'He wanted not to put his community in difficulty.'"],[2405,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade breathing into a vessel or blowing into it."],[2406,"The people used to disperse in every direction, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'None of you should leave until his last act is at the House.'"],[2407,"When the Prophet ﷺ got up to pray at night, he would say, 'O Allah, to You belongs praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the King of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Truth. Your promise is true. The meeting with You is true. The Hour is true. Paradise is true. The Fire is true. The prophets are true. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have argued, and to You I have brought judgment. So forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have declared. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer. There is no god but You, and there is no god other than You.'"],[2408,"There is no evil likeness for us: the one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit."],[2409,"The Prophet ﷺ drank while standing."],[2410,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while they were paying in advance for dates - or fruit - for two or three years. He said, 'Whoever pays in advance for dates, let him pay in advance for a known measure and a known time, until a known term.'"],[2411,"I asked Jibril, 'Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill?' He said, 'The more complete and perfect of them.'"],[2412,"And what a day Thursday was! A day when the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ pain intensified. He said, 'Bring me [something] so I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.' They disputed - and there should be no dispute in the presence of a prophet. He said, 'Leave me, for what I am in is better than what you are asking about.' He said, 'He commanded them with three things.' He said, 'Expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula, and give gifts to delegations as I used to give them.' The third, I do not know whether he said it and I forgot it, or he did not say it."],[2413,"Adhere to white garments: let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them. And adhere to ithmid, for it clears the sight and grows the hair."],[2414,"Water is not made impure by anything."],[2415,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-five."],[2416,"He is not one of us who incites a slave against his master, and he is not one of us who corrupts a woman against her husband, and he is not one of us who urges on the horses on the day of betting."],[2417,"He forbade having intercourse with pregnant captives on the day of Khaybar, (saying) 'Do not water the crop of another,' and he forbade selling the spoils before they are distributed, and he forbade eating the flesh of domestic donkeys, and he forbade every beast of prey with fangs."],[2418,"Twelve thousand will come forth from Aden, supporting God and His Messenger; they are the best of those between me and them. Al-Mu'tamir said: I think he said: 'in the depths.'"],[2419,"I heard Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, or Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, who raised the hadith to the Prophet ﷺ."],[2420,"These words are a remedy for every disease: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God and in all His names, in general, from the evil of the venomous and the general, and from the evil of the evil eye, and from the evil of the envier when he envies, and from the evil of Abu Qatarah and what he begat. Thirty-three of the angels came to their Lord and said: 'A sickness, a sickness is in our land.' He said: 'Take from your land and wipe with your sickness the ruqyah of Muhammad ﷺ. Whoever takes a fee for it or conceals it from anyone will never succeed.'"],[2421,"The Messenger of God ﷺ drank milk, then rinsed his mouth, then said: 'This has richness.'"],[2422,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: 'Why did you not make use of its skin?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, it is dead.' He said: 'Only its eating is forbidden.'"],[2423,"A man was wounded in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ and then became junub. He sought a ruling and was told to perform ghusl, so he performed ghusl and died. That reached the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'They killed him, may God kill them. Was not the cure for ignorance to ask?' 94 - (2421) - 'Ata' said: It reached me that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about that and said: 'Had he washed his body and left his head where the wound had afflicted him, it would have sufficed him.'"],[2424,"A man was wounded in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ and then became junub. He sought a ruling and was told to perform ghusl, so he performed ghusl and died. That reached the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'They killed him, may God kill them. Was not the cure for ignorance to ask?' 94 - (2421) - 'Ata' said: It reached me that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about that and said: 'Had he washed his body and left his head where the wound had afflicted him, it would have sufficed him.'"],[2425,"He was praying, and one of us wanted to pass in front of him, so he began to ward him off."],[2426,"I came with a lad from Banu Hashim on a donkey, and we passed in front of the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying. We dismounted and left the donkey to eat from the vegetation of the earth—or he said, 'from the plants of the earth'—and we entered the prayer with him. A man said, 'Was there a short spear in front of him?' He said, 'No.'"],[2427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ conducted li'an between the two men of Banu 'Ajlan, or between a man and a woman—'Abd al-Rahman was uncertain. He said: Her husband said, 'By Allah, I have not approached her since we pollinated.' Al-'afr is when the palm trees are watered after being left unwatered for two months after pollination. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Allah, make it clear; make it clear.' He said: The woman's husband had reddish hair and lean forearms and shins. He said: The one with whom she was accused was Ibn al-Sahma'. He said: She gave birth to a black boy with curly, tightly coiled hair, thick forearms, and fleshy shins. Ibn Shaddad said, 'O Abu al-'Abbas, is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If I were to stone anyone without evidence, I would stone her\"?' He said: Ibn 'Abbas said, 'No.' And he said, 'That was a woman who had become notorious in Islam.' Another man said, 'O Abu 'Abbas, how was the description?' Ibn 'Abbas said, 'She brought him with the bad description.'"],[2428,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered a drink, he would say, 'Begin with the elder'—or he said, 'with the elders.'"],[2429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Zuhr, 'Asr, 'Isha', and Fajr prayers in Mina on the day of Tarwiyah."],[2430,"On the morning of the Jamrah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Bring me some pebbles.' So I picked up for him pebbles of the size used for khathf. When he placed them in his hand, he said, 'Yes, with the like of these; yes, with the like of these; yes, with the like of these. And beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion.'"],[2431,"Five [creatures] the pilgrim in ihram may kill: the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, and the rabid dog."],[2432,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House, he found in it an image of Ibrahim and an image of Maryam. He said, 'Indeed, they have heard that angels do not enter a house containing an image. This is Ibrahim depicted, so why is he practicing divination by arrows?'"],[2433,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick person, he would sit by his head and say seven times: 'I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you.' He said: If his appointed time was to be delayed, he would be cured of that ailment."],[2434,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven parts [of the body], and I was forbidden to gather up a garment or hair."],[2435,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, he said: 'If it was fresh blood, he should give a dinar in charity; and if there was yellowishness in it, then half a dinar.'"],[2436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the effeminate men and the masculinized women. I said, 'What are the masculinized women?' He said, 'The women who imitate men.'"],[2437,"Upon every joint of a person is a charity due each day. A man among the people said, 'This is difficult; who can bear this?' He said, 'Enjoining good and forbidding evil is a charity, carrying for the weak is a charity, and every step one of you takes to the prayer is a charity.'"],[2438,"Upon every joint of the son of Adam each day there is a charity."],[2439,"It was said: O Messenger of God, will we have intercourse with our wives in Paradise as we do in this world? He said: By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, a man will have intercourse with one hundred virgins in a single morning."],[2440,"It was said: O Messenger of God, which of our sitting companions is best? He said: One whose sight reminds you of God, whose speech increases your knowledge, and whose deed reminds you of the Hereafter."],[2441,"A red velvet cloak was missing on the day of Badr from what was taken from the polytheists, and some people said: Perhaps the Prophet ﷺ took it? Then God revealed: It is not for a prophet to be dishonest."],[2442,"When Ali married Fatimah, the Prophet ﷺ said: Give her something. He said: I have nothing. He said: Then where is your Huthamiyyah coat of mail?"],[2443,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man reciting the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, so he said: O you who recites the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, who is Shubrumah? He said: A brother of mine, or a relative of mine. He said: Have you performed Hajj for yourself? He said: No. He said: Then perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj for Shubrumah."],[2444,"Al-Fadl b. Abbas was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ from Arafah, and the young man kept glancing at the women and looking at them, and the Prophet ﷺ kept turning his face away with his hand from behind him, and the young man kept glancing at them. So the Prophet ﷺ said to him: O son of my brother, this is a day when whoever controls his hearing, his sight, and his tongue will be forgiven."],[2445,"Were it not that dogs are a nation, I would command the killing of every solid black one. So kill the black-spotted among dogs, for they are the accursed ones among the jinn."],[2446,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my sister has vowed to perform Hajj walking. He said: God does not need your sister to endure hardship. Let her perform Hajj riding, and let her expiate for her oath."],[2447,"Two people should not hold a private conversation to the exclusion of a third, for that grieves him, and God hates the grief of a believer."],[2448,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on Hira and the mountain trembled, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Be still, Hira, for upon you are none but a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr. And upon it were the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Ali, Uthman, Talhah, Al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, and Sa'id b. Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl."],[2449,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in a single garment, crossing its two ends and wrapping himself with it, using the extra part of the garment to guard against the heat of the ground and its cold."],[2450,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, he kept his back so straight that if water were poured on it, it would have stayed."],[2451,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating on his garment."],[2452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ underwent cupping while fasting and in ihram, and he fainted. That day he forbade people from cupping a fasting person, out of dislike of weakness for him."],[2453,"Sharpness of temper afflicts the best of my ummah."],[2454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the horse two shares and the man one share on the day of Badr."],[2455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died at the age of sixty-five."],[2456,"Tamim al-Dari and Adi b. Badda used to travel to Makkah, and a man from Quraysh of Banu Sahm accompanied them. He died in a land where there was no Muslim, and he bequeathed his estate to the two of them. When they arrived, they handed it to his family, but they concealed a silver bowl inlaid with gold that had been with him. They said, 'We did not see it.' They were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he made them swear by Allah that they had not concealed it nor had knowledge of it, and then he released them. Afterwards the bowl was found with some people of Makkah, who said, 'We bought it from Tamim al-Dari and Adi b. Badda.' The heirs of the Sahmi stood up and took the bowl, and two men from among them swore by Allah: 'This bowl is the bowl of our companion, and our testimony is more rightful than their testimony, and we have not transgressed; if we did, then we would be among the wrongdoers.' And these two verses were revealed: 'O you who believe, testimony among you when death approaches one of you...' to the end of the verse."],[2457,"I was not commanded to build high and decorated mosques."],[2458,"A woman from Khatham came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, I am a single woman and I want to marry. What is the right of the husband over his wife? If I can fulfill it, then good; otherwise I will remain unmarried.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The right of the husband over his wife is that if he desires her while she is on the back of his camel, she should not refuse him. Among the rights of the husband over the wife is that she should not give anything from his house except with his permission; if she does so, the sin is on her and the reward is for someone else. Among the rights of the husband over the wife is that she should not leave his house except with his permission; if she does so, the angels curse her until she returns or repents.'"],[2459,"When the wind stirred, the Prophet ﷺ would face it, kneel on his knees, and say: 'O Allah, make it winds and not a wind. O Allah, make it a mercy and not a punishment.'"],[2460,"Whoever takes in an orphan among Muslims, providing him his food and drink until Allah makes him self-sufficient, Allah will surely obligate Paradise for him, unless he commits a sin that is not forgiven. And whoever supports three daughters, spending on them and being kind to them, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. A man from the Bedouins stood up and said, 'Or two?' He said, 'Yes,' and even if he had said one, he would have said, 'Yes.' And there is no servant whose two precious organs Allah takes away except that his reward with Allah is Paradise.' He said, 'What are his two precious organs?' He said, 'His two eyes.' Ibn Abbas, when narrating this hadith, would say, 'By Allah, this is one of the precious and foremost hadiths.'"],[2461,"Indeed Allah has given every rightful one his right. Allah has ordained obligations, established sunnahs, set limits, permitted the lawful, forbidden the unlawful, and legislated Islam, making it easy, lenient, and wide, and did not make it narrow. O people, there is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant. Whoever violates Allah's protection, Allah will seek him out. Whoever violates my protection, I will contend with him, and whoever I contend with, I will prevail over him. Whoever violates my protection will not attain my intercession nor come to me at the Pond. Verily, Allah has not permitted killing except in three cases: an apostate after faith, an adulterer after being married, or one who kills a soul and is killed for it. O Allah, have I conveyed?'"],[2462,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ʿumrah, and between him and the people of Makkah there was a pact that he would not take anyone of its people out. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his ʿumrah, he left Makkah and the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by the daughter of Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib. She said: O Messenger of God, to whom are you leaving me? He did not turn to her due to the pact between him and the people of Makkah. Zayd b. Ḥārithah passed by her and she said: To whom are you leaving me? He did not turn to her. Jaʿfar passed by her, and she implored him, but he did not turn to her. Then ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib passed by her, and she said: O Abū Ḥasan, to whom are you leaving me? ʿAlī took her and placed her behind Fāṭimah. When they alighted, Zayd came to ʿAlī and said: I have more right to her than you; I am the mawlā of the Prophet of God ﷺ. ʿAlī said: I have more right to her than you. Jaʿfar said: I have more right to her; her maternal aunt is with me, Asmāʾ bt. ʿUmays al-Khathʿamiyyah. When their voices rose, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent for them. When they came to him, he said: As for you, O Jaʿfar, you resemble my physical form and my character. As for you, O ʿAlī, I am from you and you are my waṣī. As for Zayd, he is my mawlā and your mawlā. So hand the girl over to her maternal aunt, for she has more right to her."],[2463,"Of ninety-nine women, one is in Paradise and the rest are in the Fire. That distressed those of the Muhājirūn who were present with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: When a Muslim woman becomes pregnant, she has the reward of one who stands in prayer, fasts, is in a state of iḥrām, and strives in the path of God, until she gives birth. Then for the first suckling she gives him, she has the reward of giving life to a soul."],[2464,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in a house among the houses of his wives, he placed his head on the thigh of one of them and dozed off. He laughed in his sleep. After I saw him, some of the people of the house asked him: They said: O Messenger of God, what made you laugh? He said: I marveled at people of my community who ride this sea, despite the terror of the enemy, striving in the path. He mentioned to them a virtue that Muḥammad did not memorize. A woman who was there said: O Messenger of God, ask God to make me one of them. He prayed for her. Then a husband of hers took her out on a military expedition. While she was on the seacoast, riding on her mount, she fell and broke her thigh and died."],[2465,"Whomever you find having intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill the animal."],[2466,"Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lot, kill the doer and the one done to."],[2467,"I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones: the forehead—and he pointed with his hand to his nose—the two hands, the two knees, and the two feet, and not to gather up the clothes or the hair."],[2468,"He spent the night at his maternal aunt Maymūnah's. The Prophet ﷺ got up during the night and prayed. He said: I got up on his left, and he pulled me until he made me stand on his right. He said: He prayed thirteen rakʿahs, his standing in them being equal."],[2469,"When he arrived from a journey, he would kiss his daughter Fāṭimah."],[2470,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb saw a gold ring on my hand. He took it and threw it away, saying: Neither did I ask for it nor did he return it to me."],[2471,"I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about selling wine to the dhimmīs. He said: A man from Thaqīf or from Daws gave the Messenger of God ﷺ a skin of wine in the year of the conquest, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had been his friend in the Jāhiliyyah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: God has forbidden it. He leaned toward a servant of his who was with him and said: Take it to al-Ḥazwarah—a village near al-Madīnah—and sell it. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What did you order him? He said: I ordered him to sell it. He said: O so-and-so, the One who forbade drinking it has forbidden its price. So he ordered that it be poured out."],[2472,"O God, I seek refuge with You from the evil of what the wind brings, and from the evil of what the messengers bring."],[2473,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on a rainy day, shielding himself with a cloak, the mud on it, when he prostrated."],[2474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while he was fasting and in a state of ihram."],[2475,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about someone who shaved before slaughtering and the like, and he would say: 'No harm, no harm.'"],[2476,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'Come, pick up pebbles for me.' He said: So I picked up for him pebbles that were the size of throwing pebbles. When I placed them in his hand, he said: 'Yes, with the like of these. And beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion.'"],[2477,"A man was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a state of ihram, and his she-camel threw him and broke his neck, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, and shroud him in two garments, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with his hair matted.'"],[2478,"The Prophet ﷺ came assuming ihram for Hajj. He performed tawaf and sa'y, and did not exit ihram because of the sacrificial animal. He commanded those who did not have a sacrificial animal with them to perform tawaf and sa'y, then to shorten their hair or shave, and then to exit ihram."],[2479,"He used to recite the talbiyah for Umrah until he touched the Black Stone."],[2480,"He said: 'O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.' A man said: 'And those who shorten their hair.' He said: 'O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.' He said in the third or fourth time: 'And those who shorten their hair.'"],[2481,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped my head and supplicated for me for wisdom."],[2482,"I saw a man near the Maqam saying takbir in every raising and lowering. I met Ibn Abbas and said: 'I saw a man saying takbir in every raising and lowering.' He said: 'Is that not the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? May you have no mother, Ikrimah?'"],[2483,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: 'Allah knows best what they would have done.'"],[2484,"Duba'ah bt. al-Zubayr b. Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I intend to perform Hajj, so should I make a condition?' He said: 'Yes, make a condition.' She said: 'How should I say it?' He said: 'Say: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk. My place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.'"],[2485,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Maymunah, and she entrusted her affair to al-Abbas, and he married her to the Prophet ﷺ."],[2486,"The Prophet ﷺ affirmed Umayya b. Abi al-Salt in two verses of his poetry. He said: 'A man and a bull beneath his right foot, and the vulture for the other, and a lion lying in wait.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'And the sun rises at the end of every night, red, its light turning rosy; it refuses to rise for us in its gentleness except tormented, or else it is flogged.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He spoke the truth.'"],[2487,"Whoever enters upon a sick person whose death is not imminent and says: 'I ask Allah, the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,' seven times, he will be healed."],[2488,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote a document between the Muhajirun and the Ansar: that they should not neglect their strongholds, that they should ransom their captives with kindness and reconciliation among the people."],[2489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs then use the siwak."],[2490,"The Prophet ﷺ performed wudu. He scooped a handful and washed his face, then scooped a handful and washed his right hand, then scooped a handful and washed his left hand, then scooped a handful and wiped his head and his ears, the insides with his index fingers, and he crossed his thumbs over the outside of his ears, wiping their outside and inside, then scooped a handful and washed his right foot, then scooped a handful and washed his left foot."],[2491,"There is no wudu required for one who sleeps while prostrating until he lies down, for when he lies down his joints relax."],[2492,"While Jibril was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, he heard a creaking above him. He raised his head and said: 'A gate of heaven has been opened that was never opened before.' Then an angel came to him and said: 'Rejoice in two lights that you have been given and no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of Surat al-Baqara. You will not recite a letter of them except that you will be granted it.'"],[2493,"A servant-girl of the household of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ committed fornication. He said: 'O 'Ali, apply the hadd to her.' He said: 'So he left her until she delivered what was in her womb, then he struck her fifty lashes. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that. He said: 'You have done correctly.'"],[2494,"He used to deliver the khutba on Friday standing, then sit, then stand and deliver the khutba."],[2495,"He forbade eating every beast of prey with fangs, and killing children, and selling the spoils of war. He said: 'I think he also said: and against pregnant women being approached for intercourse.'"],[2496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal in his Hajj and his 'Umra, and Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, and the caliphs after them did likewise."],[2497,"The camels for sacrifice became scarce during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he commanded the people to use cows."],[2498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never fought any people until he had called them."],[2499,"The price of a shield in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ten dirhams."],[2500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouth of a cracked vessel."],[2501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the torture of the soul."],[2502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions did not perform any tawaf other than a single tawaf for their umrah and their hajj."],[2503,"When this verse was revealed: 'And those who hoard gold and silver...', he said: That weighed heavily on the Muslims, and they said: None of us can leave wealth for his child that will remain after him. Umar said: I will relieve you. So they set off, and Umar set off, and Thawban followed him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of Allah, this verse has weighed heavily on your companions. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: Allah did not make zakah obligatory except to purify what remains of your wealth, and He made inheritance laws in wealth so that it remains for those after you. He said: So Umar said Allahu Akbar. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Shall I not tell you what a person hoards? A righteous wife; when he looks at her she pleases him, when he commands her she obeys him, and when he is absent from her she guards him."],[2504,"Rukanah b. 'Abd Yazid, the brother of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, divorced his wife three times in one sitting, and he grieved over her intensely. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: How many times did you divorce her, O Rukanah? He said: Three times in one sitting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Then it is one."],[2505,"Quraysh said to the Jews: Give us something to ask this man about. They said: Ask him about the soul. So they asked him, and it was revealed: 'And they ask you about the soul. Say: The soul is of the affair of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.' They said: We have not been given of knowledge except a little, yet we have been given the Torah, and whoever is given the Torah has been given much good. So it was revealed: 'Say: If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord...' the verse."],[2506,"The devils had seats where they used to listen to the revelation. When they heard a word, they added to it ninety-nine. As for the word, it would be true, and as for what they added, it would be false. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent, they were prevented from their seats. They complained about that to Iblis, and before that the stars had not been thrown with. He said: This is because of something that has happened on earth. So spread out in the earth. They set off and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between the two mountains of Nakhlah praying. They came to him and informed him, and he said: This is the event that has happened on earth."],[2507,"When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked."],[2508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from his companions to a man from the Jews and ordered him to kill him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot do that unless you permit me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: War is deceit, so do what you want."],[2509,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Hudaybiyah, he said: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, the help of Allah and the victory have come, and the people of Yemen have come. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and who are the people of Yemen? He said: A people with tender hearts and gentle natures. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."],[2510,"An expedition in the morning or in the evening in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that it contains."],[2511,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade inciting animals against one another."],[2514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade inciting animals against one another."],[2515,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath and a witness."],[2516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the state of ihram after the prayer."],[2517,"I mentioned to Ibn 'Abbas the ihram of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the ihram obligatory when he finished his prayer, then he went out. When he mounted his riding camel and it stood upright with him, he entered the state of ihram. Some people caught that from him and said: He entered ihram when his camel stood upright with him. That was because they did not catch anything except that. Then he traveled until he ascended al-Bayda', and he entered ihram. Some men caught up with him and said: He entered ihram when he ascended al-Bayda'."],[2518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ conducted the li'an between the 'Ajlani and his wife. Her husband said that day: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I have not approached her since we became Muslim. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying that day: O Allah, make it clear. The woman's husband was a man with reddish hair, thin forearms and shins. The one she was accused with was the son of Sawda'. She gave birth to a black boy with curly, tight hair, thick forearms, and plump shins. A man said to him: O Abu 'Abbas, how did you say? He said: I said: She gave birth to him with the bad description. Ibn Shaddad b. al-Had said to him: Is she the one about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If I were to stone someone without evidence? He said: No, that was a woman who had openly professed Islam."],[2519,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died without leaving a will. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes."],[2520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and said: A woman should not travel except with a mahram. A man stood up and said: I have been enlisted in the military expedition, and I want to perform Hajj with my wife. The Prophet ﷺ said: Perform Hajj with your wife."],[2521,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by a pleasant fragrance. I said: What is this fragrance, O Jibril? He said: This is the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter. She was combing her hair and the comb fell from her hand. She said: In the name of Allah. Pharaoh's daughter said: My father? She said: My Lord and the Lord of your father. She said: Then I will tell him. She said: Tell him. He said to her: Do you have a lord other than me? She said: My Lord and your Lord, who is in heaven. He said: A copper cow was heated for her. She said: I have a request to you. He said: What is your request? She said: That you gather my bones and my children's bones. He said: That is yours, due to the right you have over us. He threw her children into the cow one by one. The last of them was an infant who said to her: O mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth. Ibn 'Abbas said: Four spoke as infants: the son of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter, the infant of Jurayj, 'Isa son of Maryam, and the fourth I do not remember."],[2522,"A lahd was dug for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2523,"If the people differ, then the truth is with Mudar. And if Rabi'a becomes mighty, that is the humiliation of Islam."],[2524,"A neighbor has the right to place a wooden beam on his neighbor's wall, even if he dislikes it. The customary road is seven cubits. And there is no harm and no reciprocated harm."],[2525,"Cursed is whoever diminishes anything of the boundaries of the land without his right."],[2526,"He is not from us who has intercourse with a pregnant woman."],[2527,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the funeral prayer over a deceased person after he had been buried."],[2528,"O Allah, I have made Madinah sacred as Makkah was made sacred."],[2529,"A woman embraced Islam during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, then her husband came after her and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, she had embraced Islam along with me,' so he returned her to him."],[2530,"A virgin girl came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that her father had married her off while she was unwilling, so the Prophet ﷺ gave her the choice."],[2531,"The Prophet ﷺ fasted until he reached 'Usfan, then he broke his fast."],[2532,"The Prophet ﷺ distributed on the day of Hunayn three shares for the horseman and one share for the foot soldier."],[2533,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I sighted the crescent moon tonight.' He said: 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Arise, O Bilal, and announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow.'"],[2534,"He used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[2535,"Ibn 'Abbas once delayed the Maghrib prayer, so a man said to him, \"The prayer!\" He remained silent. The man said to him again, \"The prayer!\" He replied, \"May you be bereft of your mother! Are you teaching us about the prayer? The Prophet ﷺ sometimes combined them in Madinah.\""],[2536,"Whoever changes his religion, kill him."],[2537,"Some people from the Zutt were brought to 'Ali; they had been found worshipping an idol, so he burned them. This reached Ibn 'Abbas, and he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him.\""],[2538,"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[2539,"When I was taken on the Night Journey, I rose to a level where I could hear the scratching of the pens."],[2540,"Whoever asks you by the Face of Allah, give him; and whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge."],[2541,"It is as if I am looking at him, black and bow-legged, tearing it down stone by stone."],[2542,"When he raised his head from bowing, he would say: \"O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will.\""],[2543,"May Allah curse whoever slaughters for other than Allah, may Allah curse whoever alters the boundary markers of the land, may Allah curse whoever misleads a blind person away from the path, may Allah curse whoever reviles his parents, may Allah curse whoever takes as patrons others than his true patrons, and may Allah curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lut. He said it three times."],[2544,"Whoever claims descent from other than his father or takes as patrons others than his true patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."],[2545,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate with these words at times of distress: \"There is no god but Allah, the Most Great, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne.\""],[2546,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the Valley of al-Azraq and asked, \"What is this valley?\" He was told, \"The Valley of al-Azraq.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Musa descending, crying out to his Lord with the talbiyah.\" Then he passed by the mountain pass of Kada' and asked, \"What is this?\" He was told, \"The mountain pass of Kada'.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Yunus b. Matta on a reddish, curly-haired camel, its rein of palm fiber, wearing a woolen jubbah.\""],[2547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, and we gave him some of this nabidh to drink—meaning the nabidh of the watering place—and he drank. Then he said: “You have done well. Do it like this.”"],[2548,"There is no one among the children of Adam who has not erred or entertained a sinful thought except Yahya b. Zakariyya. And it is not appropriate for anyone to say: “I am better than Yunus b. Matta.”"],[2549,"Al-‘Abbas said to me: “Spend the night with the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And make sure you do not sleep until you have observed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: The Prophet ﷺ prayed ‘Isha' and left the mosque until no one remained in it except me. He said: The Prophet ﷺ looked at me and said: “Who is this? ‘Abd Allah?” He said: I said: “Yes.” He said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: I said: “Al-‘Abbas commanded me to spend the night with you.” He said: “Go then.” He said: “Spread it out, ‘Abd Allah.” He said: I brought a cushion of coarse cloth stuffed with palm fiber. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ came forward and prayed two rak‘ahs, neither long nor short. Then he went to his bed and I heard his snoring or his breathing. Then he woke up and recited: “Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day” until he completed the surah. Then he wiped three times. Then he got up and urinated. Then he cleaned his teeth with his siwak. Then he performed ablution. Then he stood and prayed two rak‘ahs, neither long nor short. Then he returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring or his breathing. Then he woke up, sat up on his bed, and did as he had done the first time. Then he wiped three times, and recited the verses from the end of Surah Al ‘Imran: “Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day” until he completed the surah. Then he got up, cleaned his teeth with his siwak, performed ablution, then prayed two rak‘ahs, neither long nor short. Then he returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring or his breathing. Then he woke up and did as he had done the first two times. He prayed six rak‘ahs, then performed witr with three. Then he prayed the two rak‘ahs before Fajr. When he finished his prayer, he said: “O Allah, place light in my sight, light in my hearing, light in my heart, light before me, light behind me, light above me, light below me, light on my right, light on my left, and grant me light on the Day of Resurrection, and magnify light for me.”"],[2550,"When he wanted to prostrate after the rak‘ah, he would say: “O Allah, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will of anything after.”"],[2551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man's thigh uncovered, so he said: “Cover your thigh, for a man's thigh is ‘awrah.”"],[2552,"He was praying when two slave girls from Quraysh came and took hold of his knees. I think he said: He separated them or he pushed them apart, and he continued praying. I and a boy from Banu Hashim came on a donkey and passed in front of him, then we entered into the prayer, and he did not interrupt it."],[2553,"When he sent out his armies, he would say: “Go forth in the name of Allah. Fight in the way of Allah against those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, do not steal from the spoils, and do not kill children or those in monasteries.”"],[2554,"Najdah al-Haruri wrote to Ibn ‘Abbas asking him about the share of the near relatives—for whom is it? About killing children, mentioning in his letter that the learned man, the companion of Musa, had killed the boy. And about women—did they attend war with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and was a share allotted to them? Yazid said: I wrote Ibn ‘Abbas's letter for him, and he wrote back: You wrote asking me about the share of the near relatives—for whom is it? It is for us, the People of the House. ‘Umar b. al-Khattab invited us to use it to marry our unmarried, to serve our needy, and to pay the debts of our debtors, but we refused unless he handed it over to us, and he refused, so we left it. You wrote asking me about killing children and mentioned that the learned man, the companion of Musa, killed the boy. If you knew about children what that learned man knew, you would kill. But you do not know, so avoid them, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing them. You wrote asking me about women—did they attend war with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and was a share allotted to them? They did attend with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but no share was allotted to them; rather, he gave them a small amount."],[2556,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the most generous of people, and he was most generous in Ramadan when Jibril met him. Jibril used to meet him every night in Ramadan to study the Quran with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more generous than the sent wind when Jibril met him."],[2557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, and I placed water for his ablution for him. When he came out, he said: “Who placed this?” They said: “Ibn ‘Abbas.” He said: “O Allah, give him understanding in religion.”"],[2558,"He used to let his hair hang down, while the polytheists used to part their hair. The People of the Book used to let their hair hang down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked to conform with the People of the Book in matters not revealed to him, so he parted his hair."],[2559,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform witr with three rak‘ahs, reciting: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,” “Say: O disbelievers,” and “Say: He is Allah, the One.”"],[2560,"He rode behind the Prophet ﷺ one day, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"O boy, I shall teach you some words: Be mindful of God, and He will protect you. Be mindful of God, and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask God; and when you seek help, seek help from God. Know that if the entire community were to gather to benefit you with something, they would not benefit you except with something God has already written for you; and if they were to gather to harm you, they would not harm you except with something God has written against you. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried.\""],[2561,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him in the mosque, then left. He then stood, spread his legs, and urinated. The people were about to rush at him, but the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not interrupt the man's urination.\" Then he called him and said: \"Are you not a Muslim?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"What made you urinate in the mosque?\" He said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I thought it was just one of the open grounds, so I urinated in it.\" The Prophet ﷺ then ordered a bucket of water to be poured over his urine."],[2562,"I said to Abd Allah b. Abbas: \"They claim that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Perform ghusl on Friday, and wash your heads unless you are in a state of major ritual impurity, and apply perfume.'\" Ibn Abbas said: \"As for perfume, I do not know; as for ghusl, yes.\""],[2563,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night after the Isha prayer."],[2564,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died without leaving a will."],[2565,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs in which he recited Umm al-Kitab (the Opening Chapter) and did not add anything to it."],[2566,"\"Which of the two recitations do you consider the first recitation?\" They said: \"The recitation of Abd Allah.\" He said: \"Our recitation is the first recitation, and the recitation of Abd Allah is the last recitation. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to have the Quran presented to him once every Ramadan. In the year in which he was taken, it was presented to him twice. Abd Allah was present and witnessed what was abrogated from it and what was changed.\""],[2567,"\"I was granted victory by the east wind, and Ad was destroyed by the west wind.\""],[2568,"The Messenger of God ﷺ freed on the day of al-Taif those slaves of the polytheists who came out to him."],[2569,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I saw in a dream a canopy dripping clarified butter and honey. People were taking from it, some taking much and some taking little, and others in between. And it was as if a rope was let down from the sky. You came and took hold of it and ascended, and God raised you. Then a man came after you, took hold of it, and ascended, and God raised him. Then a man came after you two, took hold of it, and ascended. Then a man came after you, took hold of it, but it was cut off for him, then reconnected, and he ascended, and God raised him.\" Abu Bakr said: \"O Messenger of God, permit me to interpret it.\" He permitted him, and Abu Bakr said: \"As for the canopy, it is Islam. As for the clarified butter and honey, it is the Quran. As for the rope, it is what you are upon: you ascend and God raises you. Then there will be a man after you on your path who ascends and God raises him. Then there will be a man after you two who takes hold of what you two took hold of and ascends and God raises him. Then there will be a man after you on your path, but it will be cut off for him, then reconnected, and he ascends and God raises him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have been right and wrong.\" Abu Bakr said: \"I adjure you, O Messenger of God, to tell me.\" He said: \"Do not adjure me.\""],[2570,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not circumambulate any thing except that it is part of the House."],[2571,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, he saw the Jews fasting on Ashura. He said: \"What is this day that you fast?\" They said: \"This is a righteous day. This is the day on which God saved the Children of Israel from their enemy.\" He said: \"So Moses fasted on it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I am more entitled to Moses than you.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ fasted on it and commanded fasting on it."],[2572,"The Prophet ﷺ slaughtered, then shaved his head."],[2573,"Avoid drinking from gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels; drink from waterskins. If you fear their strong flavor, then dilute it with water."],[2574,"I stood with the Prophet ﷺ in prayer to his left, and he took my hand and made me stand on his right."],[2575,"Any Muslim who has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him or he accompanies them, they will cause him to enter Paradise."],[2576,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ prayed the Eid al-Fitr prayer with the people, two rak'ahs without any adhan, and delivered the sermon after the prayer. Then he took Bilal's hand and went to the women and preached to them. Then, after he had turned away from them, he commanded Bilal to go to them and command them to give charity."],[2577,"If the son of Adam had a valley full of wealth, he would love to have another like it. Nothing fills the soul of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents. Ibn 'Abbas said: I do not know whether it is from the Qur'an or not."],[2578,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions performed 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah. They jogged around the House three times and walked four times."],[2579,"The prayer was about to begin and I had not yet prayed the two rak'ahs. He saw me praying them, so he passed by me and said: Do you want to pray the morning prayer as four? It was said to Ibn 'Abbas: The Prophet ﷺ? He said: Yes."],[2580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in a single cloth, using its extra parts to guard against the heat of the ground and its cold."],[2581,"I was with Ibn 'Abbas when a man came to him and said: I am a man whose livelihood is from my own handiwork, and I make these images. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever makes an image, Allah will punish him on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes the spirit into it, and he will never be able to do so. The man began to pant heavily and his face turned pale. Ibn 'Abbas said: Woe to you! If you insist on making, then make these trees and everything that has no soul."],[2582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people and admonished them, saying: O people, you will be gathered to Allah barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. Then he recited: 'As We began the first creation, We will repeat it. [That is] a promise binding upon Us. Indeed, We will do it.' He said: Then some men will be brought and taken to the left side. I will say as the righteous servant said: 'And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them; but when You took me up, You were the Observer over them, and You are, over all things, Witness. If You should punish them, indeed they are Your servants; but if You forgive them, indeed it is You who is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.' He said: Then it will be said to me: They have not ceased turning back on their heels since you left them. He said: And the first one to be clothed will be Ibrahim ﷺ ."],[2583,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted a dyed garment for the pilgrim in ihram as long as it had no saffron or wars dye."],[2584,"Allah's Prophet ﷺ said to Ma'iz, \"Is it true what has reached me about you?\" He said, \"And what has reached you about me?\" He said, \"It has reached me that you fell upon the slave girl of Banu so-and-so.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"So he testified four testimonies, and he ordered regarding him, so he was stoned.\""],[2585,"A Bedouin came to Allah's Messenger ﷺ and began speaking with clear speech, so Allah's Messenger ﷺ said, \"Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery, and indeed, some poetry is wisdom.\""],[2586,"There is no evil omen, no contagion, no hama, and no Safar. A man said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, we take a mangy sheep and throw it among the flock, and it makes them mangy.\" He said, \"Then who infected the first one?\""],[2587,"Abu Talib fell ill, so the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him. At his head was a man's seat, so Abu Jahl stood and sat in it. They complained about him to Abu Talib and said, \"He insults our gods.\" He said, \"O son of my brother, what do you want from this?\" He said, \"O uncle, I only want from them a word by which the Arabs will submit to them, and by which the non-Arabs will pay the jizya to them.\" He said, \"And what is it?\" He said, \"There is no god but Allah.\" He said, \"Has he made the gods one God? Indeed, this is a strange thing.\""],[2588,"Allah's Messenger ﷺ came out in the illness in which he died, with his head bandaged with a cloth. He sat on the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, \"Indeed, there is no one among the people more gracious to me with his self and his wealth than Ibn Abi Quhafa. If I were to take a close friend from among the people, I would have taken Abu Bakr, but the brotherhood of Islam is better. Close every small door in the mosque except the small door of Abu Bakr.\""],[2589,"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire, and whoever speaks about the Quran without what he knows will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."],[2590,"In the end of times there will be a people called al-Rafida: they reject Islam and cast it out. So kill them, for they are polytheists."],[2591,"The best of companions are four, the best of raiding parties are four hundred, the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will never be defeated due to smallness."],[2592,"A man went out from Khaybar, and two men followed him, and another trailing them, saying, \"Go back, go back,\" until he turned them back. Then he caught up with the first and said, \"Indeed, these two are devils, and I did not cease dealing with them until I turned them back. When you come to Allah's Messenger ﷺ, convey peace to him and tell him that we are here collecting our zakat, and if it were fit to send, we would send it to him.\" He said, \"When the man came to Madinah, he informed the Prophet ﷺ, and at that point the Prophet ﷺ forbade seclusion.\""],[2593,"Hashim b. al-Harith narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Amr narrated to us, with its chain, similar to it."],[2594,"A man went out while wine was still lawful, and he gifted Allah's Messenger ﷺ a skin of wine. He came leading it on a camel until he found Allah's Messenger ﷺ sitting. He said, \"What is this with you?\" He said, \"A skin of wine that I gifted to you.\" He said, \"Do you know that Allah has forbidden it?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Indeed, Allah has forbidden it.\" He said, \"The man turned to the camel driver and spoke to him something between him and him. So he said, 'What did you say to him?' He said, 'I ordered him to sell it.' He said, 'Indeed, the One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it.' He said, 'So he ordered the mouth of the water skin to be opened, and it was opened, and it flowed into the dirt. I looked at it in the valley, and there was nothing in it.'"],[2595,"Allah's Messenger ﷺ never fought a people until he called them."],[2596,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would turn in his prayer to the right and left, but he would not twist his neck."],[2597,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a dead sheep that its owners had thrown away, and he said: 'By Him in Whose hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to God than this is to its owners.'"],[2598,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, and in it were six pillars. He stood at each pillar but did not pray."],[2599,"Ibn 'Abbas wrote to me: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If people were given what they claimed, some people would claim the blood of others and their wealth. But the oath is upon the defendant.'"],[2600,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent his wives ahead on the night of Muzdalifah before the crowding."],[2601,"Ibn al-Zubayr prayed Maghrib and said the salam after two rak'ahs, then he stood up to touch the corner, but the people said subhan Allah to him, so he returned and prayed one more rak'ah. He said: I went to Ibn 'Abbas and informed him of that, and he said: 'He did not deviate from the Sunnah of his Prophet ﷺ.'"],[2602,"A righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood."],[2603,"Circumambulating the House is like prayer, except that you speak during it. And whoever speaks during it should speak only good."],[2604,"The price of a dog is impure. And he said: 'If someone comes to you seeking the price of a dog, fill his palm with dust.'"],[2605,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in an open space with nothing in front of him."],[2606,"I asked Sa'id b. Jubayr about fasting Rajab: What do you think of it? He said..."],[2607,"A people who dye with black in the last times, like the crops of pigeons, will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."],[2608,"Abu Jahl said: \"If I were to see Muhammad praying at the Ka'bah, I would come to him until I trample on his neck.\" He said: So the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If he did that, the angels would seize him openly. And if the Jews were to wish for death, they would die and see their seats in the Fire. And if those who invoked mutual curses with the Messenger of God ﷺ were to go out, they would return finding neither family nor wealth.\""],[2609,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss the Yemeni corner and place his cheek upon it."],[2610,"Regarding the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"Mankind was one community,\" he said: \"Upon Islam, all of them.\" And al-Kalbi said: \"Meaning upon disbelief, all of them.\""],[2611,"Press together the rows, for I saw the devils passing through you as if they were small lambs."],[2612,"\"I saw my Lord in the most beautiful form. He said to me: 'O Muhammad.' I said: 'At Your service and at Your command.' He said: 'In what does the Highest Assembly dispute?' I said: 'Lord, I do not know.' So He placed His hand on my shoulder and I felt its coolness between my breasts, and I learned what is between the east and the west. Then He said: 'O Muhammad, in what does the Highest Assembly dispute?' I said: 'In the expiations: walking on foot to the Friday prayers, performing ablution thoroughly in adverse conditions, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer until the next prayer. Whoever maintains these lives well and dies well, and becomes free from his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him.'\""],[2613,"While they were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a shooting star was cast and it lit up. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: \"What would you say in the pre-Islamic era when something like this was cast?\" They said: \"God and His Messenger know best. We used to say: 'Tonight a great man was born, and tonight a great man died.'\" He said: \"It is not cast for anyone's death or life. But when our Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He, decrees a matter, the bearers of the Throne glorify Him, then the inhabitants of the heaven that follows them glorify Him, until the glorification reaches the inhabitants of the lowest heaven. Then they say to those who follow the bearers of the Throne: 'What did your Lord say?' They inform them, and the inhabitants of the heavens ask one another until the news reaches the inhabitants of the lowest heaven. Then the jinn snatch the hearing and cast it to their allies, and they are pelted. So what they bring as it is is true, but they distort it and add to it.\""],[2614,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ sleep until he snored or breathed heavily. I said: \"O Messenger of God, you have slept.\" He said: \"Ablution is only required for one who sleeps lying down, for when he sleeps lying down his joints relax.\""],[2615,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ looked in the mirror, he said: \"Praise be to God who has made my creation and character excellent, and adorned in me what He has disfigured in others.\" When he applied kohl, he put two in each eye and one between them. When he put on his sandals, he began with the right one, and when he took them off, he took off the left one first. When he entered the mosque, he entered with his right foot first. He loved beginning with the right side in everything, whether taking or giving."],[2616,"Sunday is a day for planting and building, Monday is a day for travel, Tuesday is a day of blood, Wednesday is a day of taking with no giving in it, Thursday is a day for entering upon the ruler, and Friday is a day for marriage and wedding."],[2617,"A man said: \"O Messenger of God, a sacrificial camel has become obligatory upon me, but camels have become scarce. What do you think?\" He said: \"Slaughter in its place seven sheep.\""],[2618,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died when he was sixty-five years old."],[2619,"A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: \"The cursed Hassan has come.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"He is not cursed. He fought alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ with his tongue and his self.\""],[2620,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to Caesar inviting him to Islam, and sent his letter with Dihya al-Kalbi. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered him to deliver it to the governor of Busra so that he would pass it on to Caesar. The governor of Busra delivered it to Caesar. When God had relieved Caesar of the armies of Persia, Caesar vowed that he would walk from Hims to Ilya' in gratitude for what God had granted him in that regard. When Caesar received the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said upon reading it: \"Look for any of his people here so that we may ask them about the Messenger of God.\""],[2621,"They were merchants in the Levant, and that was during the period of truce between the Messenger of God ﷺ and the disbelievers of Quraysh. Abu Sufyan said: \"The messenger of Caesar came to us and took me and my companions until we arrived at Ilya'. We were admitted to him, and there he was sitting in his royal court, wearing the crown, with the nobles of Byzantium around him. He said to his interpreter: 'Ask them which of them is closest in kinship to this man who claims to be a prophet.' Abu Sufyan said: 'I am the closest of them.' He said: 'How are you related to him?' I replied: 'He is my cousin, and in the caravan that day there was no man from Banu Abd Manaf other than me.'\" He said: \"Caesar said: 'Bring him near me,' and he ordered my companions to be placed behind me. Then he said to his interpreter: 'I will ask this man about this man who claims to be a prophet. If he lies, then declare him a liar.'\" Abu Sufyan said: \"Had it not been for the shame that my companions would report me as lying, I would have lied about him when he asked. But I was too ashamed for them to report me as lying, so I told the truth about him. Then he said to his interpreter: 'Say: How is this man's lineage among you?' I said: 'He is of noble lineage among us.' He said: 'Has anyone among you ever said such a thing before him?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Did you ever accuse him of lying before he said what he said?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Was any of his forefathers a king?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Do the nobles or the weak among the people follow him?' I said: 'Rather the weak.' He said: 'Are they increasing or decreasing?' I said: 'They are increasing.' He said: 'Does he ever betray?' I said: 'No, but we are currently in a truce with him, and we fear that he might.'\" Abu Sufyan said: \"No opportunity arose for me to say anything by which I could belittle him, because I was afraid that something else would be reported from me.\" He said: \"So he said: 'Have you fought him?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'How was your war and his war?' I said: 'It was alternating: sometimes he gained the upper hand over us, and sometimes we over him.' He said: 'What does he command you?' I said: 'He commands us to worship God alone without associating anything with Him, and he forbids us from what our forefathers worshipped. He commands us to pray, give charity, fulfill covenants, and render trusts.'\" He said: \"Then he said to his interpreter after I had said that: 'I asked you about his lineage among you, and you claimed that he is of noble lineage among you. Thus are messengers sent: among the noblest lineages of their people. I asked you whether anyone among you had said this before him, and you claimed no. I said to myself: If anyone among them had said this before him, I would have said he is a man following a statement said before him. I asked you whether you used to accuse him of lying before he said what he said, and you claimed no. I said to myself: He would not refrain from lying about people and then lie about God. I asked you whether any of his forefathers was a king, and you claimed no. I said to myself: If any of his forefathers had been a king, I would have said he is a man seeking his father's kingdom. I asked you whether the nobles or the weak follow him, and you claimed that the weak follow him, and they are the followers of the messengers. I asked you'\""],[2622,"Pharaoh and his courtiers discussed what God had promised Abraham, that He would make among his descendants prophets and kings. Some of them said: 'The Children of Israel are surely awaiting that, without any doubt. They had thought it would be Joseph son of Jacob, but when he died, they said: It is not so; God, Mighty and Majestic, promised Abraham.' Pharaoh said: 'What do you think about it?' They deliberated and agreed to send men with knives to go around among the Children of Israel and slaughter every newborn male they found. They did so. When they saw that the elders of the Children of Israel were dying of natural causes while the young were being slaughtered, they said: 'It is likely that you will wipe out the Children of Israel, and then you will have to undertake the labor they used to spare you. So kill every newborn male in one year, that their numbers may dwindle, and spare them in another year, so that the young may grow up in place of the elders who die. For they will not become numerous through those you let live to the point that you fear they will outnumber you, nor will they perish through those you kill to the point that you will need such killing.' So they agreed on that. The mother of Moses conceived Aaron in the year when boys were not slaughtered, and she gave birth to him openly and safely. The following year she conceived Moses, and anxiety and grief entered her heart—that is from the trials, O Ibn Jubayr—on account of what was intended for him. God, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to her: 'Fear not, nor grieve; indeed, We will return him to you and make him one of the messengers.' He commanded her, when she gave birth, to put him in a chest and cast it into the river. When she gave birth, she did that. When her son was hidden from her, Satan came to her, and she said to herself: 'What have I done with my son? Had he been slaughtered in my presence and I had buried him and shrouded him, that would have been dearer to me than casting him with my own hand into the waves of the sea and its fish.' The water carried him until it brought him to a landing place where the maidservants of Pharaoh's wife drew water. When they saw him, they took him, and they were about to open the chest, but one of them said: 'There is wealth in this, and if we open it, Pharaoh's wife will not believe us about what we found in it.' So they carried it as it was, without disturbing anything, until they delivered it to her. When she opened it, she saw a boy in it, and love for him was cast upon her such as she had never felt for any human being. The heart of Moses' mother became empty of remembrance of everything except remembrance of Moses. When the slaughterers heard of his affair, they came with their knives to Pharaoh's wife to slaughter him—that is from the trials, O Ibn Jubayr. She said to them: 'Leave him, for this one child will not increase the Children of Israel. Let me go to Pharaoh and ask him to give him to me. If he grants him to me, you will have done well and acted nobly, but if he orders him to be slaughtered, I will not blame you.' She took him to Pharaoh and said: 'He will be a comfort to me and to you.' Pharaoh said: 'He may be for you, but for me I have no need of that.'\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my oath, had Pharaoh acknowledged that he would be a comfort to him as his wife acknowledged, God would have guided him by him just as He guided his wife. But He deprived him of that. So she sent to every woman around her who had milk to choose a wet nurse for him. But every time one of them took him to nurse him, he would not accept her breast, until Pharaoh's wife feared he would refuse milk and die, and that grieved her. He was taken out to the market and gathering place of the people in hope of finding a wet nurse he would accept, but he refused. The mother of Moses became distraught, and she said to his sister: 'Follow him; trace his tracks and seek him. Do you hear any mention of him? Is my son alive or have the beasts eaten him?'—and she forgot what God had promised her concerning him. His sister spotted him from afar while they were unaware. Al-junub means when a person's eyesight rises to something far off while it is beside him and he is unaware of it. She said out of joy when the wet nurses failed: 'Shall I direct you to a household who will nurse him for you and be sincere to him?' They took her and said: 'What makes you know of their sincerity to him? Do you know him?'—until they doubted that; and that is from the trials, O Ibn Jubayr. She said: 'Their sincerity toward him and their compassion for him stem from desire for a connection to the king and hope of benefit from him.' They sent her, and she went to her mother and told her the news. His mother came, and when she placed him in her lap, he sprang to her breast and suckled until his sides were full. The bearer of good news went to Pharaoh's wife to give her the glad tidings that they had found a wet nurse for her son. She sent for her, and she was brought with him. When she saw what he did with her, she said to her: 'Stay with me and nurse this son of mine, for I have never loved anything as I love him.' Moses' mother said: 'I cannot leave my house and my son, for we would be ruined. If you are content to give him to me, I will take him to my house and he will be with me, and I will spare no effort for his good. Otherwise, I will not leave my house and my son.' The mother of Moses remembered what God, Mighty and Majestic, had promised her, and she was reluctant with Pharaoh's wife, certain that God would fulfill His promise. She returned to her house with her son. The people of the village became united, refusing forced labor and injustice as long as he was among them. When he had grown a little, Pharaoh's wife said to Moses' mother: 'I want you to show me my son.' She promised her a day to show him to her. Pharaoh's wife said to her treasurers, stewards, and nurses: 'Let none of you remain unless he meets my son today with a gift and honor, so that I may see that in him. I am sending a trustworthy person to count everything each of you does.' The gifts, honors, and presents kept coming to him from the time he left his mother's house until he was brought before Pharaoh's wife. When he entered upon her, she honored him, showed him respect, rejoiced in him, and was delighted with him, and she honored his mother for her good influence upon him. Then she said: 'I will bring him to Pharaoh, and he will surely honor and respect him.' When she brought him to him and placed him in his lap, Moses grabbed Pharaoh's beard and pulled it down to the ground. The evildoers, enemies of God, said to Pharaoh: 'Do you not see what God promised Abraham His prophet: that he will rear you, and rise above you, and throw you down?' So Pharaoh sent for the slaughterers to slaughter him—and that is from the trials, O Ibn Jubayr, after every affliction he was tried with. 'And I will expose you to trials.' Pharaoh's wife came running to Pharaoh and said: 'What has changed your mind about this boy whom you gave me?' He said: 'Do you not see he claims he will throw me down and rise above me?' She said: 'Let us settle the matter between us in a way that will reveal the truth: bring two live coals and two pearls, and place them before him. If he seizes the pearls and avoids the coals, you will know he has understanding; but if he takes the coals and not the pearls, you will know that no one with understanding would prefer coals over pearls.' So he brought them near, and Moses took the coals, and they snatched them from his hand for fear they would burn him. The woman said: 'Do you see?' So God turned him away from him after he had intended to kill him, for God, Mighty and Majestic, was to accomplish His purpose through him. When Moses reached full strength and became a man, no one of Pharaoh's clan could wrong any Israelite or impose forced labor on him as long as Moses was with them, until they completely resisted. While Moses was in one part of the city, he came upon two men fighting: one was an Egyptian and the other an Israelite. The Israelite called for his help against the Egyptian. Moses became very angry because he had seized the Israelite, while knowing Moses' standing with the Children of Israel and his protection of them. People did not know that this was because of his having nursed them, except Moses' mother—unless God had informed Moses of what He had not informed others. Moses struck the Egyptian and killed him, and no one saw them except God and the Israelite. When Moses killed the man, he said: 'This is from the work of Satan; indeed, he is a clear misleading enemy.' Then he said: 'My Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me,' and He forgave him; indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful. In the morning he was in the city, fearful and vigilant, awaiting news. Pharaoh was informed, and it was said to him: 'The Children of Israel have killed a man of Pharaoh's clan; take our due for us and do not be lenient with them.' He said: 'Find me his killer and someone who will testify against him. For a king, even if his favor is with a people, cannot rightly exact retribution without clear proof. Seek out knowledge of that for me, and I will obtain your right for you.' While they were searching and found no proof, the next day Moses saw that same Israelite fighting another man of Pharaoh's clan. The Israelite called for his help against the Egyptian. Moses, regretting what he had done before, disliked what he saw because of the Israelite's anger, while he intended to seize the Egyptian. He said to the Israelite about what he had done yesterday and today: 'You are clearly a misguided man.' The Israelite looked at Moses when he said what he said and saw him angry as he had been the day before, and he feared that Moses meant him and not the Egyptian. Moses had not meant him but the Egyptian. But the Israelite was afraid, and he restrained the Egyptian and said: 'O Moses, do you intend to kill me as you killed a soul yesterday?'—he said that only out of fear that Moses intended him, to kill him. They quarreled and fought, and the Egyptian went to his people and told them what he heard the Israelite say: 'Do you intend to kill me as you killed a soul yesterday?' Pharaoh sent the slaughterers to kill Moses. The messengers of Pharaoh took the main road, walking openly, seeking Moses, not fearing that he would escape. Then a man from Moses' own people came from the farthest part of the city and took a shortcut so as to reach Moses before them and tell him the news—and that is from the trials, O Ibn Jubayr. Moses left, heading toward Midian, having faced no affliction before that, and he had no knowledge of the way except his good opinion of his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for he said: 'Perhaps my Lord will guide me to the right way.' When he arrived at the watering place of Midian, he found there a crowd of people watering their flocks, and he found apart from them two women keeping back their flocks. He said to them: 'What is your situation, that you stand apart and do not water with the people?' They said: 'We have no strength to compete with the men, and we wait for the surplus from their troughs.' So he watered for them, and he drew abundant water with the bucket until he was the first of the shepherds to finish. They returned with their flocks to their father, and Moses withdrew and sought shade under a tree and said: 'My Lord, indeed I am in need of whatever good You send down to me.' Their father found it strange that they returned so quickly with their flocks full and well-fed, and he said: 'You have had some business today.' They told him what Moses had done. He told one of them to call him. She came to Moses and called him. When he spoke to him, he said: 'Fear not; you have escaped from the wrongdoing people. Pharaoh and his people have no authority over us, and we are not in his kingdom.' One of the two women said: 'O my father, hire him; indeed, the best you can hire is the strong and trustworthy.' Jealousy prompted him to say: 'What do you know of his strength and trustworthiness?' She said: 'As for his strength, I saw what he did with the bucket when he watered for us; I have never seen a man stronger at drawing water. As for his trustworthiness, when I came to him and he looked at me and noticed me, when he realized I was a woman, he lowered his head and did not raise it or look at me until I delivered your message. Then he said: Walk behind me and describe the way to me. He would not have done this unless he were trustworthy.' Her father was relieved and believed her, and he thought of him as she had described. He said to him: 'Would you like me to marry you to one of these two daughters of mine on condition that you serve me for eight years? If you complete ten, that will be from you, and I do not wish to make it difficult for you. You will find me, God willing, among the righteous.' So it was done. Eight years were obligatory upon the Prophet of God Moses ﷺ , and two years were a promise from him. God fulfilled his promise for him, and he completed them as ten. Sa'id said: A man from the scholars of the Christians met me and said: 'Do you know which of the two terms Moses fulfilled?' I said: 'No,' and at that time I did not know. I met Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: 'Do you not know that eight years were obligatory upon Moses, and the Prophet of God would not have diminished anything from them, and he knew that God would fulfill the promise he had made? Indeed, he completed ten years.' I met the Christian and told him that, and he said: 'The one you asked and who told you is more knowledgeable than you about that?' I said: 'Yes, and more worthy.' When Moses traveled with his family, there was the matter of the fire, the staff, and his hand, as God has related to you in the Qur'an. He complained to his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, about his fear of Pharaoh's clan regarding killing and the knot in his tongue, for he had a knot in his tongue that prevented him from much speech. He asked his Lord to aid him with his brother Aaron, to be a support for him and speak on his behalf for much that his tongue could not articulate. God granted his request and untied a knot from his tongue. God revealed to Aaron and commanded him to meet Moses. Moses set out with his staff until he met Aaron, and they went together to Pharaoh. They stood at his gate for a while without being granted permission, then they were admitted after a long delay. They said: 'We are messengers of your Lord.' He said: 'Who is your Lord, O Moses?' Moses told him what God has related to you in the Qur'an. He said: 'What do you want?' And Moses reminded him of the slain man and excused himself as you have heard, and said: 'I want you to believe in God and send with me the Children of Israel.' He refused that and said: 'Bring a sign if you are truthful.' He threw down his staff, and it became a great serpent with gaping mouth, rushing toward Pharaoh. When Pharaoh saw it heading for him, he feared it and leaped from his throne and sought Moses' help to keep it from him, and he did. Then he drew out his hand from his bosom and it was white without any blemish, meaning without leprosy. Then he returned it and it reverted to its original color. He consulted the assembly around him about what he had seen. They said to him: 'These two are surely sorcerers who want to drive you out of your land with their magic and take away your exemplary way'—meaning their kingdom and the life they were living. They refused to give him anything he asked, and they said to him: 'Gather for us the sorcerers, for they are many in your land, so that their magic may overcome the magic of these two.' He sent throughout the city and gathered every accomplished sorcerer. When they came to Pharaoh, they said: 'What does this sorcerer work with?' They said: 'He works with serpents.' They said: 'By God, there is no one on earth who works magic with serpents and staffs as we do. What is our reward if we prevail?' He said to them: 'You are my kinsmen and my close associates, and I will give you whatever you desire.' They agreed on the Day of Adornment, and that the people should be assembled at forenoon. Sa'id said:\""],[2623,"My intimate friend forbade me three things and commanded me three things: he forbade me from pecking like a rooster, from turning around like a fox, and from squatting like a beast of prey. He commanded me to pray witr before sleeping, to fast three days of every month, and to pray the Duha prayer."],[2624,"He used to deliver the Friday sermon standing, then sit, then stand and deliver the sermon."],[2625,"It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from al-Hajjaj, from Simak b. Harb, from Jabir b. Samura, from the Messenger of God ﷺ, something similar to that."],[2626,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon, and he said: \"Have you prayed?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then pray two rak'ahs, and make them brief.\""],[2627,"The night prayer is two by two; and when you fear the morning, then pray one rak'ah as witr. Indeed, God is single (witr) and loves the single (witr), because He is One."],[2628,"It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, something similar to that."],[2629,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Friday prayer should add another to it."],[2630,"It was read to Bishr: Abu Yusuf informed you, from al-Hajjaj, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, the like of that."],[2631,"He forbade that a funeral be accompanied by a loud voice or fire."],[2632,"The polytheists occupied the Messenger of God ﷺ from the prayers: the noon prayer, the afternoon prayer, the sunset prayer, and the night prayer until an hour of the night had passed. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Bilal, so he called the adhan and the iqamah, then he prayed the noon prayer. Then he commanded him, so he called the adhan and the iqamah and he prayed the afternoon prayer. Then he commanded him, so he called the adhan and the iqamah and he prayed the sunset prayer. Then he commanded him, so he called the adhan and the iqamah and he prayed the night prayer."],[2633,"He said regarding the martyrs on the day of Uhud: 'I am the witness over these on the Day of Resurrection. Wrap them with their wounds and their blood, and do not wash them.'"],[2634,"Najdah wrote to him asking: 'Does the slave have a share of the spoils? Did the women attend the war with the Messenger of God ﷺ? When is a share of the spoils due to a boy? And about the share of the near relatives?' He said: Ibn 'Abbas wrote to him that the slave has no right to the spoils, but he may be given a small amount. And he wrote that the women used to go out with the Prophet ﷺ tending the wounded, and that they were given a small amount. And that there is no right for a boy in the spoils until he reaches puberty. And he wrote to him regarding the share of the near relatives that 'Umar offered us that he would marry our unmarried women from it and pay our debts from it, but we refused that unless he handed it over entirely, and he refused that."],[2635,"I wrote the letter of Ibn 'Abbas to Najdah: 'You wrote to me asking about killing children? And that the learned man of Moses killed a child? And the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing children. If you knew about children what the learned man of Moses knew, that would be so. And you wrote: Did the women attend the war with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and are they given a small amount, and are they not allotted a share of the fay'? They did attend the war with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they were given a small amount, and they were not allotted a share.'"],[2636,"Whoever stands in prayer on the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[2637,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in his sandals."],[2638,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a bucket of Zamzam water while he was circumambulating, and he drank while standing."],[2639,"Abu Yala informed us, Jubbara narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, with the like of that."],[2640,"He used to pray on a donkey while heading to Khaybar."],[2641,"A woman asked her about a menstruating woman who makes up the fast but not the prayer. She said to her: 'Are you a Haruriyyah? We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ making up the fast and not making up the prayer.'"],[2642,"The first time prayer was prescribed it was two rak'ahs, then it was increased in the prayer at home, and the prayer of travel was left as it was."],[2643,"He saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray at night and he did not sit between the first two prostrations, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness in his place."],[2644,"Horses have good tied to their forelocks."],[2645,"Good is tied to the forelocks of horses."],[2646,"Good is tied to the forelocks of horses."],[2647,"I saw the head of al-Husayn b. Ali brought to Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad, and I saw the head of Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad brought to al-Mukhtar b. Abi Ubayd, and I saw the head of al-Mukhtar brought to Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr, and I saw the head of Mus'ab brought to Abd al-Malik b. Marwan."],[2648,"I prepared food and invited Sulayman al-A'mash. I heard about him that he said: 'Waddah invited us to a protruding bone and sour pomegranates.' He said: Then I met Raqabah b. Masqalah and complained about him. He said: 'I will suffice you.' He met him and said: 'O Abu Muhammad, a brother from our brothers invited you and honored you, then you say \"on a protruding bone and sour pomegranates\"? By Allah, I never knew you except as harsh in nature, constantly frowning, quickly bored, belittling the rights of visitors, as if you are snuffing mustard when asked to tell a story.'"],[2649,"I met Salamah b. Alqamah, and he narrated it to me, then he retracted it. Then he said: 'If you want your companion to be called a liar, then prompt him.'"],[2650,"Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to emigrate. He said to him: 'O uncle, remain in your place where you are, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will seal the emigration with you just as He sealed prophethood with me.'"],[2651,"This hadith keeps you from the remembrance of Allah, from prayer, and from maintaining ties of kinship. Will you then desist?"],[2652,"Ibn Abbas came asking permission to enter upon A'ishah while she was dying. He said: I came and at her head was Abd Allah b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr. I said: 'This is Ibn Abbas asking your permission.' She said: 'Leave me alone from Ibn Abbas, I have no need of him nor of his praise.' He said: Abd Allah said: 'O mother, Abd Allah b. Abbas is one of the righteous of your children, he wants to greet you.' She said: 'Let him in if you wish.' He said: Ibn Abbas came and sat down and said: 'Rejoice, for by Allah, between you and departing every hardship and meeting Muhammad and the loved ones there is only that your soul leaves your body.' She said: 'Is that so, O Ibn Abbas?' He said: 'You were the most beloved of the wives of the Messenger of Allah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved only what was good. Your necklace fell on the day of al-Abwa', so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained in the camp picking it up, and the people woke up without any water. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed that they should perform tayammum with clean earth. That was because of you, the concession Allah revealed for this nation. Then Allah revealed your innocence from above seven heavens, so there is no mosque among the mosques of Allah in which Allah is mentioned except that your innocence is recited in it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.' She said: 'Leave me, O Ibn Abbas, for by Allah, I wish I were a thing forgotten, utterly forgotten.'"],[2653,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was addressing the people on Friday, a man from Banu Layth b. Bakr b. Abd Manat b. Kinanah came stepping over the people until he approached him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, impose the prescribed punishment on me.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Sit down.' He sat down. Then he stood up a second time, and he said: 'Sit down.' Then he stood up the third time and said the same. He said: 'What is your prescribed punishment?' He said: 'I had unlawful intercourse with a woman.' The Prophet ﷺ said to some men of his companions, among them Ali b. Abi Talib, al-Abbas, Zayd b. Harithah, and Uthman b. Affan: 'Take him and flog him one hundred lashes.' The Laythi man had not been married. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will you not flog the woman with whom he committed adultery?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bring him to me after he has been flogged.' When he was brought, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who is your partner?' He said: 'So-and-so, a woman from Banu Bakr.' He summoned her and asked her about that. She said: 'He has lied, by Allah, I do not know him, and I am innocent of what he said, Allah is witness to what I say.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who testified that you committed adultery with her? For she denies it. If you have witnesses, I will flog her with the prescribed punishment, otherwise we will flog you with the punishment for slander.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have no witnesses.' So he ordered and he was flogged with the punishment for slander, eighty lashes."],[2654,"Do not kill the people of the monasteries."],[2655,"When this verse was revealed: 'It is not for a prophet to be treacherous' in relation to a red velvet cloak that was lost on the day of Badr, some people said: 'Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it.' Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'It is not for a prophet to be treacherous, and whoever is treacherous will bring what he treacherously took on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2656,"A sheep passed in front of the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, between him and the qibla, and it did not interrupt his prayer."],[2657,"Hassan b. Thabit recited some verses to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I bear witness, by God's permission, that Muhammad is the Messenger of Him who is above the heavens, from on high; and that Abu Yahya and Yahya, both of them, have a deed in His religion that is accepted; and that the brother of al-Ahqaf, when he stood among them, spoke of God's essence and was just.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"And I.\""],[2658,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for a man of the Ansar, and he was slow in coming to him. He said: \"What kept you?\" He said: \"When your messenger came to me, I was with the woman, so I got up and performed ghusl.\" He said: \"What was upon you that you should not perform ghusl as long as you did not ejaculate?\" He said: \"So the Ansar used to do that.\""],[2659,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in a red garment that he used to wear, and a shirt."],[2660,"\"When the lote tree was covered with what covered it\" (Q 53:16) — the Messenger of God said: \"I saw it until I gazed at it steadily, then golden moths came between me and it.\""],[2661,"Make the rows compact, for I saw the devils passing through your midst like the young of the hadhaf (small black sheep)."],[2662,"Concerning God's saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"Look at your food and your drink: it has not changed with time\" (Q 2:259), he said: \"It has not altered.\""],[2663,"Concerning God's saying: \"We increased them in punishment above the punishment\" (Q 16:88), he said: \"Scorpions were added to them, whose fangs are like tall palm trees.\""],[2664,"Concerning His saying: \"We increased them in punishment above the punishment\" (Q 16:88), he said: \"There are five rivers beneath the Throne; they are punished with some of them at night and with some of them by day.\""],[2665,"I prayed behind Ibn 'Abbas at a funeral, and he recited the Opening of the Book and a surah, and he recited aloud until he made us hear. When he finished, I took his hand and asked him about that. He said: \"It is a sunnah and a truth.\""],[2666,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ left Makkah, he said: \"By God, I will leave you, and I know that you are the most beloved of God's lands to me and the most honorable to God. Had your people not driven me out, I would not have left. O Banu 'Abd Manaf, if you are the guardians of this matter after me, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating the House of God at any hour of the night or day. Were it not that Quraysh would transgress, I would tell them what they have with God. O God, You made the first of them taste a calamity; so make the last of them taste a gift.\""],[2667,"Concerning His saying: \"And We sent down from the mu'sirat water pouring forth abundantly\" (Q 78:14), he said: \"The mu'sirat are the winds; 'pouring forth' means 'flowing down.'\""],[2668,"Regarding His saying: “Or like a rainstorm from the sky” (Q 2:19). He said: “al-sayyib is rain.”"],[2669,"Regarding His saying: “gently wherever it reaches” (Q 7:57). He said: “al-rukha' means obedient. As for His saying: ‘wherever it reaches,’ he said: ‘wherever He wills.’ And regarding His saying: ‘He sends the winds, so they stir up clouds, then He spreads them in the sky however He wills and makes them fragments’ — he says: ‘pieces, one above another. Then you see the rain’ — meaning the rain — ‘coming out from within them, from between them.’”"],[2670,"Regarding His saying: “a whirlwind with fire in it, so it burned” (Q 2:266). He said: “al-i'sar is a violent wind.”"],[2671,"Regarding His saying: “jumbled dreams” (Q 12:44). He said: “They are false dreams.”"],[2672,"Regarding His saying, mighty and glorious: “Those who consume riba do not stand except as one stands whom Satan has confounded by touch” (Q 2:275). He said: “They will be recognized on the Day of Resurrection by that; they will be unable to stand except as a madman being choked stands. That is because they said, ‘Trade is only like riba,’ and they lied against God. God made trade lawful and forbade riba. So whoever receives an admonition from his Lord and desists —” up to His saying: “— but whoever returns and consumes riba, those are the companions of the Fire, abiding eternally therein” (Q 2:275). And His saying: “O you who believe, fear God and give up what remains of riba, if you are believers. And if you do not, then be informed of war from God” (Q 2:278-279) to the end of the verse. It has reached us, and God knows best, that this verse was revealed concerning the Banu 'Amr b. 'Umayr b. 'Awf of Thaqif and the Banu al-Mughira of the Banu Makhzum. The Banu al-Mughira used to engage in riba with Thaqif. When God granted His Messenger victory over Makkah, he abolished all riba on that day. The people of al-Ta'if had made a treaty on the condition that they would keep their riba, but whatever riba was owed to them was declared void. The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote at the end of their treaty document: ‘They have what the Muslims have, and they owe what the Muslims owe: they are not to consume riba or be fed with it.’ Then the Banu 'Amr b. 'Umayr and the Banu al-Mughira came to 'Attab b. Asid — who was governor of Makkah — and the Banu al-Mughira said: ‘Why has He made us the most wretched of people regarding riba? It was abolished for everyone except us.’ The Banu 'Amr b. 'Umayr said: ‘We made a treaty on the condition that we would keep our riba.’ So 'Attab b. Asid wrote about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and this verse was revealed: ‘And if you do not, then be informed of war from God and His Messenger’ (Q 2:279). The Banu 'Amr recognized that the declaration of war from God and His Messenger was directed at them by His saying: ‘And if you repent, then you may have your principal; you do not wrong and you are not wronged. You do not wrong by taking more, and you are not wronged by being cheated out of it. And if someone is in difficulty, then deferring it is better for you, if you only knew. Then deferment until a time of ease; and that you give charity is better for you, if you only knew. And fear a day in which you will be returned to God; then every soul will be paid in full what it earned, and they will not be wronged’ (Q 2:279-281). They mentioned that this verse was revealed, and the last verse of Surat al-Nisa', as the last part of the Qur'an.”"],[2673,"It was revealed to me that I should prostrate on seven bones, and not tuck back hair or clothing."],[2674,"The Messenger of God ﷺ rinsed his mouth, sniffed water, washed his face, washed his forearms once, his hand once, and wiped his head and ears."],[2676,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed wudu, rinsing his mouth and sniffing water from a single handful."],[2677,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas, or he was asked: “Which charity is best?” He said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘The best charity is water. Have you not heard that when the people of the Fire sought help from the people of Paradise, they said: “Pour upon us some water or from what God has provided you” (Q 7:50)?’”"],[2678,"By God, I will certainly raid Quraysh; by God, I will certainly raid Quraysh; by God, I will certainly raid Quraysh, if God wills."],[2679,"By God, I will certainly raid Quraysh; by God, I will certainly raid Quraysh; by God, I will certainly raid Quraysh. Then he paused for a while and said: “If God wills.”"],[2680,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “How are you this morning?” He said: “Better than a people who have not visited the sick or attended a funeral.”"],[2681,"Then night prayer was mentioned, and some of them said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: half of it, a third of it, a quarter of it, the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, the interval between two milkings of a ewe."],[2682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined zuhr and 'asr, and maghrib and 'isha, without being on a journey and without rain. He said: I said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended to make things easier for his community."],[2683,"Damrah b. Jundub left his house as an emigrant and said to his family: Carry me and take me out of the land of the polytheists to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he died on the way before reaching the Prophet ﷺ, and the revelation came down: And whoever leaves his house as an emigrant to Allah and His Messenger, then death overtakes him, until he reached: And Allah is ever Forgiving, Merciful."],[2684,"I was granted victory by the east wind, and 'Ad was destroyed by the west wind."],[2685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray two rak'ahs during the night, then he would finish and use the toothstick."],[2686,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Qatadah regarding spoils he had taken: Leave him and his spoils."],[2687,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My mother died with a vow upon her, and she did not fulfill it. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Fulfill it on her behalf."],[2688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Uhud and said: It would not please me that it be gold for the family of Muhammad, spending it in the way of Allah, dying the day I die while I still have two dinars of it."],[2689,"And you are proudly heedless. He said: They used to pass by the Prophet ﷺ with haughty strides. Did you not see how the calf struts with its head held high?"],[2690,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to a woman of Quraysh called Sawdah and said to her: The best women who have ridden the backs of camels are the women of Quraysh, the most tender toward a child in his infancy and the most careful of a husband in what he possesses."],[2691,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in a single garment, wrapping himself with it and putting its two ends on opposite shoulders, using its extra part to guard against the heat of the ground and its cold."],[2692,"I have not been commanded to build lofty mosques."],[2693,"I was not commanded to build ornate mosques."],[2694,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar every fanged beast of prey and every bird with talons."],[2695,"I was with Ibn 'Abbas, and people began asking him for legal opinions, and he would give them legal opinions without mentioning the Messenger of God ﷺ in what he told them, until a man from Iraq, I think, came and said: \"I make these images.\" He said: \"Come closer, come closer,\" two or three times. \"I heard Muhammad ﷺ say: 'Whoever makes an image in this world will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the spirit into it, and he will not be able to breathe.'\""],[2696,"There is no harm in a man entering ihram in a garment dyed with saffron that has been washed, for it has no scent or trace."],[2697,"Five that the pilgrim in ihram may kill: the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, and the rabid dog."],[2698,"The Prophet ﷺ had a kohl container from which he applied kohl at bedtime, three times in each eye."],[2699,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died while his shield was pawned with a Jew for twenty sa's of barley, which he had taken as food for his family."],[2700,"When you have thrown the pebble at the pillar, everything becomes lawful for you except women. A man said: \"O Abu al-'Abbas, what about perfume?\" He replied: \"As for me, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ smear musk on his head. Is that perfume or not?\""],[2701,"The Messenger of God ﷺ continued the talbiyah until he threw the pebble at the pillar."],[2702,"No man who believes in God and the Last Day hates the Ansar, or else God and His Messenger hate him."],[2703,"The believer is not one who eats his fill while his neighbor beside him is hungry."],[2704,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed the circumambulation on the day of sacrifice until night."],[2705,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a day of Eid and he prayed, then delivered a sermon, then came to the women and admonished them, reminded them, and commanded them to give charity."],[2706,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to use the tooth-stick frequently, until we saw or feared that something would be revealed to him."],[2707,"He used to pray on a small mat."],[2708,"Abd Allah b. Tawus prayed beside me, and when he prostrated the first prostration and raised his head from it, he raised his hands opposite his face. I disapproved of that, so I said to Wuhayb b. Khalid, 'This one does something I have not seen anyone do.' He said, 'Wuhayb said to him, \"Do you do something we have not seen anyone do?\" Abd Allah b. Tawus said, \"I saw my father do it, and my father said, 'I saw Ibn Abbas do it,' and he mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ used to do it.\"'"],[2709,"God did not give security to any of His creation except Muhammad ﷺ. He said: 'That God may forgive you what is past of your sin and what is to come' [Quran 48:2]. And He said to the angels: 'And whoever of them says, \"I am a god besides Him,\" that one We will repay with Hell.'"],[2710,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to touch his beard in prayer."],[2711,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date."],[2712,"The Prophet ﷺ took up the recitation from where Abu Bakr had stopped."],[2713,"He said: 'No rafath.' He said: 'Al-rafath is sexual intercourse.' 'And no fusuq.' He said: 'Al-fusuq is acts of disobedience.' 'And no disputing in the Hajj.' He said: 'Al-jidal is quarrelling.'"],[2714,"When the verse of debt was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The first to deny was Adam; the first to deny was Adam. When God created him, He wiped his back and brought forth from him what He was going to create, and He presented them to him. He saw among them a man shining brightly, and said: \"O Lord, which of my sons is this?\" He said: \"Your son Dawud.\" He said: \"O Lord, how long is his lifespan?\" He said: \"Sixty years.\" He said: \"O Lord, increase his lifespan.\" He said: \"No, unless you increase it from your own lifespan.\" He said: Adam's lifespan was one thousand years, so he gave him forty years from his lifespan. God wrote a written record and made the angels witnesses. When Adam was dying, the angels came to take his soul, and he said: \"There remain forty years of my lifespan.\" They said: \"You gave them to your son Dawud.\" He said: \"I did not do it.\" So God brought out the written record and the angels bore witness against him. He completed one thousand years for Adam and completed one hundred years for Dawud.'"],[2715,"The one who drinks from vessels of gold and silver only pours the fire of Hell into his belly."],[2716,"Whoever abandons the Friday prayer three consecutive Fridays has cast Islam behind his back."],[2717,"The best with which you dye gray hair is henna and katam."],[2718,"The best of companions is four, the best of raiding parties is four hundred, the best of armies is four thousand, and no people who reach twelve thousand are defeated due to being few if they are truthful and patient."],[2719,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to trim his mustache, and Abraham used to trim his mustache."],[2720,"The little finger and the thumb are equal."],[2721,"It is not lawful for a Muslim man to give a gift and then take it back, except a father in what he gives to his child. The example of one who takes back his gift is like that of a dog that eats until when it is full it vomits, then returns to its vomit."],[2722,"On the day of al-Hudaybiyyah, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'May God have mercy on those who shave their heads.' They said: 'And those who shorten, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'May God have mercy on those who shave their heads.' They said: 'And those who shorten, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'May God have mercy on those who shave their heads.' They said: 'And those who shorten, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'And those who shorten.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, what is the matter with those who shave, why did you repeatedly invoke mercy for them?' He said: 'They did not hesitate.'"],[2723,"This Stone has a tongue and two lips that will testify on the Day of Resurrection for whoever touches it with truth."],[2724,"The Prophet ﷺ was taken on a night journey to Jerusalem, then he came back the same night and told them of his journey, of the landmarks of Jerusalem, and of their caravan. He said: 'Some people said: We do not believe Muhammad, so they apostatized as disbelievers, and God struck their necks along with Abu Jahl.' He said: 'Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad frighten us with the tree of Zaqqum? Bring dates and butter and eat as zaqqum.' He said: 'He saw the Dajjal in his true form with the vision of the eye, not a dream vision, and Jesus son of Mary, and Abraham.' He said: 'The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the Dajjal, and he said: I saw him as a huge man, whitish, one of his eyes protruding like a brilliant star, his hair like the branches of a tree. And I saw Jesus: a young man, fair, with curly hair, sharp-sighted, and a well-built body. And I saw Moses: dark-skinned, brown, with much hair and a strong build. And I saw Abraham, and I do not look at any limb of his without looking at it as if he were your companion.' He said: 'Gabriel said to me: Greet your father, so I greeted him.'"],[2725,"Beware of narrating from me except what you know, for whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire, and whoever denies the Quran without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2726,"The Messenger of God ﷺ drew four lines on the ground and said: 'Do you know what this is?' They said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadijah daughter of Khuwaylid, Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, Mary daughter of 'Imran, and Asiyah daughter of Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.'"],[2727,"A man from the Ansar married a woman from Banu 'Ajlan and consummated the marriage with her, spending the night with her. When morning came, he said: 'I did not find her a virgin.' He said: Their case was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who summoned the young woman and asked her. She said: 'Yes, I was a virgin.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered them to engage in mutual cursing, and he gave her the dowry."],[2728,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade gold rings, garments of qassi, and red saddlecloths saturated with saffron, and reciting the Quran while bowing or prostrating."],[2729,"The noon prayer on the day of tarwiyah, and the dawn prayer on the day of 'Arafah at Mina."],[2730,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married while in ihram, and had himself cupped while in ihram."],[2731,"The best of your kohl is ithmid; at bedtime it grows the hair and sharpens the eyesight. The best of your garments are the white ones: wear them and shroud your dead in them."],[2732,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam al-Zuhri to collect some of the sadaqah. He passed by Abu Rafi' and asked him to come along. Abu Rafi' went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \"O Abu Rafi', sadaqah is forbidden for Muhammad and for the family of Muhammad. The mawla of a people is one of them, or from themselves.\""],[2733,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas about white, green, and red earthenware jars. He said: \"The first to ask the Prophet ﷺ was the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays. He said: 'Do not drink from gourds, pitch-coated vessels, hollowed stumps, or green jars, and do not drink from earthenware jars. Drink from waterskins.' He said: 'They said: Pour water over them.' He said to him the third or fourth time: 'Pour it out.' Then he said: 'God has forbidden me - or forbidden - wine, gambling, the drum, and every intoxicant is forbidden.'\""],[2734,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade hollowed stumps, gourds, and pitch-coated vessels. He said: \"Do not drink except from a vessel.\" So they made skins of camels and gave them necks of sheepskins. That reached him, and he said: \"Do not drink except from what its top is above it.\""],[2735,"Abu Lu'lu'ah was a slave of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. He used to make millstones, and al-Mughirah used to take from him four dirhams every day. Abu Lu'lu'ah met 'Umar and said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, al-Mughirah has made my payment heavy on me. Speak to him to lighten it for me.\" 'Umar said to him: \"Fear God and be good to your master.\" 'Umar intended to meet al-Mughirah and speak to him to lighten it. The slave became angry and said: \"His justice has encompassed all the people except me.\" He resolved to kill him. He made a dagger with two heads, sharpened it, and poisoned it. Then he brought it to al-Hurmuzan and said: \"What do you think of this?\" He said: \"I think that you would not strike anyone with this except that you would kill him.\" Abu Lu'lu'ah waited for the opportunity and came at the dawn prayer until he stood behind 'Umar. When the prayer was called, 'Umar would speak, saying: \"Straighten your rows,\" as he used to say. When he said the takbir, Abu Lu'lu'ah stabbed him in his shoulder and stabbed him in his side. 'Umar fell, and he stabbed thirteen men with his dagger. Seven of them died and six recovered. 'Umar was taken to his home. The people shouted until the sun almost rose. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf called out: \"O people, the prayer, the prayer, the prayer.\" They rushed to prayer. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf came forward and led them with the two shortest surahs of the Qur'an. When he finished the prayer, they went to 'Umar. He called for a drink to see the extent of his wound. Nabidh was brought and he drank it; it came out from his wound, and he did not know whether it was nabidh or blood. He called for milk and drank it; it came out from his wound. They said: \"No harm upon you, O Commander of the Faithful.\" He said: \"If there is harm in being killed, then I have been killed.\" The people began praising him, saying: \"May God reward you well, O Commander of the Faithful. You did such and such.\" Then they would leave, and another group would come and praise him. 'Umar said: \"By God, despite what you say, I wish that I had left it even, with nothing against me or for me, and that the companionship of the Messenger of God ﷺ is safe for me.\" 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas spoke, and he was by his head. He was his close associate, as if he were from his family. Ibn 'Abbas used to recite the Qur'an. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas spoke and said: \"By God, you will not leave it even. You accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ and accompanied him in the best way a companion could. You were for him such and such, and such and such, until the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away while he was pleased with you. Then you accompanied the caliph of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then you took charge, O Commander of the Faithful. You took charge in the best way a ruler could: you did such and such, and such and such.\" 'Umar was comforted by Ibn 'Abbas's speech. 'Umar said: \"O Ibn 'Abbas, repeat your speech for me.\" He repeated it. 'Umar said: \"By God, despite what you say, if I had the fill of the earth of gold, I would ransom myself with it today from the terror of the place of rising. I have made it a consultation among six: 'Uthman, 'Ali, Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah, al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam, 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas. He made 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar with them as an advisor, not one of them. He set a term of three days for them, and he ordered Suhayb to lead the people in prayer.\""],[2736,"He used to sit with Ibn 'Abbas, and Ibn 'Abbas would keep people away from him. He said: I stayed away from him for some days. He said to me: \"What kept you away?\" He said: I said: \"Fever.\" He said to me: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with Zamzam water.'\""],[2737,"He saw Abu Hurayrah performing ablution and said: \"O Ibn 'Abbas, do you know what I am performing ablution from? From some curds I ate.\" He said: \"By God, I do not know what you performed ablution from. As for me, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eat bread and meat, then stand for prayer without performing ablution.\""],[2738,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eating a bone with meat on it. Then the muezzin came to him, so he put it down and stood for prayer without touching water."],[2739,"He forbade branding on the face. When al-'Abbas heard of that, he branded on the two hips."],[2740,"'Umar b. al-Khattab came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"I am ruined.\" He said: \"What has ruined you?\" He said: \"I changed my saddle's position last night.\" He said: He did not reply to him anything. He said: Then this verse was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish,\" meaning: front or back, but avoid the anus and menstruation."],[2741,"The sister of 'Uqba b. 'Amir vowed to walk to the Hajj. So he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has no need of your sister's vow. Let her ride and offer a camel as a sacrifice.'"],[2742,"I was forbidden to pray behind those who are conversing and those who are sleeping."],[2743,"When Najda al-Haruri came out during the strife of Ibn al-Zubayr, he sent to Ibn 'Abbas asking him about the share of the near relatives: for whom does he see it? He said: 'It is for the relatives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ apportioned it to them. 'Umar had offered us something of it that we considered less than our right, so we returned it to him and refused to accept it. That which he offered them was to help their one who wanted to marry, to pay the debt of their debtor, and to give to their poor; and he refused to increase them beyond that.'"],[2744,"And he was thereafter a governor over Egypt, and he was not attributed to any father."],[2745,"Abu Yala informed us: My father narrated to us: Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, with something similar."],[2746,"There is no Muslim man who has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him or he accompanies them, except that they will cause him to enter Paradise."],[2747,"Whomever you find having intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill it with him. And whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to."],[2748,"'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas invited al-Fadl b. 'Abbas to a meal on the day of 'Arafa, and he said: 'I am fasting.' 'Abd Allah said: 'Do not fast, for the Prophet ﷺ was brought a milking vessel containing milk and drank from it this very day. And the people follow your example.'"],[2749,"I prayed the eclipse prayer behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I did not hear a single letter from him during it."],[2750,"'O you who believe, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you'—this was revealed concerning 'Abd Allah b. Hudhafa b. Qays b. 'Adi, whom the Prophet ﷺ sent out in a raiding party."],[2751,"Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love each other."],[2752,"Whoever loves my natural disposition, let him follow my Sunnah, and part of my Sunnah is marriage."],[2753,"I was with Ibn 'Abbas, and we mentioned what interrupts the prayer. They said: The donkey and the woman. Ibn 'Abbas said: I came with a boy from Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, both of us riding on a donkey, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying with the people in open land. We left the donkey in front of them, then came and entered between their ranks, and he paid no heed to that. And the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying with the people when two slave girls from Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib came running, fighting each other. The Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of them and pulled one away from the other, paying no heed to that."],[2754,"Gabriel led me in prayer at the House twice. He prayed the noon prayer when the sun had declined, at the length of a sandal strap. Then he prayed the afternoon prayer when the shadow of everything was equal to its height. Then he prayed the sunset prayer with me when the fasting person breaks his fast. Then he prayed the evening prayer with me when the twilight disappeared. Then he prayed the dawn prayer when food and drink became forbidden for the fasting person. The next day he prayed the noon prayer when the shadow of everything was equal to its height. Then he prayed the afternoon prayer when the shadow of everything was twice its height. Then he prayed the sunset prayer with me at the same time as before, when the fasting person breaks his fast. Then he prayed the evening prayer when a third of the first part of the night had passed. Then he prayed the dawn prayer, but I do not know what he said. Then he turned to me and said: O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you. The time is between these two times."],[2755,"Whoever combines two prayers without an excuse has committed a door from the doors of major sins. And whoever conceals a testimony and thereby seizes the wealth of a Muslim man or sheds his blood has made the Fire obligatory."],[2756,"O 'A'ishah, whoever has two children who died in infancy from my community, he will enter Paradise because of them. She said: May my father be ransomed for you, what about one who has one? He said: And one who has one, O fortunate one. She said: May my father be ransomed for you, what about one who has none from your community? He said: Then I am the one who goes ahead of my community; they have not been afflicted with the like of me."],[2757,"It is as if I am looking at him, black with crooked legs, tearing it down stone by stone."],[2758,"Regarding the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: 'By your life,' he said: 'By your lifetime.'"],[2759,"Whoever asks you by the face of God, give to him. And whoever seeks refuge with God, grant him refuge."],[2760,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to deliver the sermon on Friday beside a wooden post, leaning his back against it. When the people became numerous, he said: Build for me a pulpit. They built for him a pulpit with two steps. When he stood on the pulpit to preach, the wooden post yearned for the Messenger of God ﷺ. Anas said: I was in the mosque, and I heard the wooden post when it yearned, yearning like a grieving mother. It kept yearning until the Messenger of God ﷺ came down to it and embraced it, and it became still."],[2761,"Four characteristics: one of them is for Me, one is for you, one is between Me and you, and one is between you and My servants. As for the one that is for Me: you worship Me and associate nothing with Me. As for the one that is for you upon Me: whatever good you do, I will reward you for it. As for the one between Me and you: from you is supplication, and upon Me is the answer. As for the one between you and My servants: be pleased for them with what you are pleased with for yourself."],[2762,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: When is the Hour? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Indeed, it is coming. What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much for it, except that I love God and His Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You will be with those you love, and you will have what you have hoped for. Then he said: You ask me about the Hour, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no soul on earth today that will live a hundred years. Anas said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed, and then said: Where is the one who asked about the Hour? The man was brought, his sides trembling. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at a boy from Daws called Sa'd and said: If this one lives, he will not grow old before the Hour comes. Anas said: And I was then about the age of that boy."],[2763,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out one day for one of his outings, and with him were some of his companions. They went along traveling, and the time for prayer came. The people dismounted but found no water with which to perform ablution. They said: O Messenger of God, we can find nothing with which to perform ablution. He saw reluctance in the faces of his companions. A man from the group went off and brought a cup with a little water. The Prophet ﷺ took it and performed ablution from it, then passed his four fingers over the cup, then said to the people: Come. The people came and performed ablution until they had enough for what they intended of ablution. It was said: How many were the people? He said: Seventy men, or about that."],[2764,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I desire jihad but I am not able to do it. He said: Do you have any of your parents remaining? He said: My mother. He said: Then strive to please God in being dutiful to her. If you do that, you are a pilgrim, a performer of 'umrah, and a mujahid. When your mother is pleased with you, then fear God and be dutiful to her."],[2765,"It was mentioned in the presence of Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad the Hawd (the Pool), and it was as if he denied it. That reached Anas, so he said: \"No doubt, I will displease him.\" So he came to him and said: \"What do you deny about the Hawd?\" He said: \"Have you heard it, O Abu Hamza, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes, more than such-and-such a number of times. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'The distance between the two ends of my Hawd is like that between Aylah and Makkah, or between Sana'a and Makkah, and its vessels are more than the number of stars in the sky.'\""],[2766,"The example of my companions is like the example of salt in food: food is not good except with salt."],[2767,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a man driving a sacrificial camel barefoot and said: \"Ride it.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial camel.\" He said: \"Ride it.\" So he rode it."],[2768,"Indeed I am ashamed before My servant and My maidservant who grow old in Islam, so that the beard of My servant turns white and the head of My maidservant turns white in Islam, then I punish them in the Fire after that."],[2769,"Indeed it is from extravagance that you eat everything you desire."],[2770,"Do not engage in sales involving uncertainty (gharar)."],[2771,"Do not touch each other's goods (talāmasū), do not raise prices artificially (tanājashū), do not engage in sales involving uncertainty (gharar), and a settled person should not sell on behalf of a bedouin. Whoever buys a camel or sheep with an inflated udder, let him milk it for three days; if he returns it, let him return it with a sā' of dates."],[2772,"He used to say the talbiyah: \"Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka lā sharīka laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, lā sharīka lak.\" (Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am. Indeed all praise, blessing and dominion belong to You. There is no partner for You.)"],[2773,"When death descended upon the Messenger of Allah, Fatimah said: \"What grief!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O my little daughter, there is no grief upon your father after this day.\""],[2774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never wanted to set out on a journey but that he said when rising from his sitting: \"O Allah, by You I have spread out, and to You I have turned, and in You I have sought protection. O Allah, You are my trust and You are my hope. O Allah, suffice me in what concerns me and what does not concern me, and what You know better than I. Provide me with piety, forgive me my sin, and direct me to good wherever I turn.\" He said: \"Then he would go out.\""],[2775,"Whoever has two tongues in this world, Allah will make for him two tongues of fire."],[2776,"Whoever has two tongues in this world, Allah will make for him two tongues in the Fire of the Day of Resurrection."],[2777,"Indeed the Qur'an is wealth such that after it there is no poverty, and without it there is no wealth."],[2778,"Prices rose during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they said, “O Messenger of God, would you set prices for us?” He said, “Indeed God is the One who withholds and the One who expands. I would withhold from you and not give it to you. I indeed hope to meet God while not one of you seeks me for an injustice I inflicted upon him in life or property.”"],[2779,"There are no two recording angels who raise to God what they have recorded, and God sees at the beginning of the page good or at its end, except that God says to His angels, “Bear witness that I have forgiven My servant for what lies between the two ends of the page.”"],[2780,"A settled person does not sell for a Bedouin, even if he is his brother or his father."],[2781,"Indeed a person is with the one he loves."],[2782,"The most beloved of names to God are: ʿAbd Allāh, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and al-Ḥārith."],[2783,"Three persons Paradise longs for: ʿAlī, ʿAmmār, and Salmān."],[2784,"Paradise longs for three: ʿAlī, ʿAmmār, and Salmān."],[2785,"He used to pray on his mount."],[2786,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with him was ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, while the Messenger of God was on a bed woven with palm-fiber straps, there being nothing between the side of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the strap. He said: And he had the thinnest skin of all people, so he turned slightly and the strap had left a mark on the skin of his belly, or on his side. Then ʿUmar wept. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “What makes you weep?” He said, “By God, O Messenger of God, I do not weep because I do not know that you are nobler before God than Caesar and Khosrow, for they revel in whatever worldly things they revel in, while you are the Messenger of God in the place I see!” He said, “O ʿUmar, are you not content that for us is the Hereafter and for them is this world?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then it is indeed so.”"],[2787,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a bed that was woven with palm-fiber straps. He said: Some people from among his companions entered upon him. He said: And ʿUmar entered, and the Prophet ﷺ turned, and behold the strap had left a mark on his side. So ʿUmar wept and said, “By God, we indeed know that you are nobler before God than Khosrow and Caesar, while they revel in whatever they revel in.” He said, “Are you not content that for them is this world and for us is the Hereafter?” He said, “Yes.” He said: Then he was silent."],[2788,"I have never smelled musk or ambergris more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[2789,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out intending the mosque, leaning on Usamah b. Zayd, wearing a cotton garment wrapped around himself, and he prayed with them."],[2790,"I kept interceding with my Lord and He kept allowing me to intercede until I said: 'My Lord, grant me intercession for those who said: There is no god but God.' He said: 'This is not for you, O Muhammad; it is for Me. By My might, My forbearance, and My mercy, I will not leave in the Fire anyone'—or he said: 'any servant'—who said: There is no god but God.'"],[2791,"I have not prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of God ﷺ who had a more complete prayer and was more concise than the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[2792,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited prayer between graves."],[2793,"Whoever walks to fulfill the need of his Muslim brother, God writes for him a good deed for every step he takes until he returns from where he left him. If his need is fulfilled, he emerges from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him; and if he dies, then what a one who has perished—he enters Paradise without reckoning."],[2794,"Shall I tell you about the most generous, the most generous? God is the Most Generous, the Most Generous, and I am the most generous of the children of Adam. The most generous of them after me is a man who learned knowledge and spread his knowledge; he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a single nation. And a man who gave his life in the way of God until he was killed."],[2795,"He used to come to Umm Sulaym and take a midday nap with her, and he used to pray on a leather mat and take a nap. He sweated profusely, and she would collect the sweat from the leather mat and put it into perfume bottles. He used to pray on a small mat."],[2796,"Bilal was commanded to make the call to prayer even and the iqamah odd."],[2797,"Bilal was commanded to make the call to prayer even and the iqamah odd."],[2798,"He ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four rak'ahs, and he prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah two rak'ahs, and I heard them shouting loudly with both: for Hajj and Umrah."],[2799,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to Umm Sulaym and take a midday nap with her, and he sweated profusely, and she would put it into the bottles. He used to pray on a small mat."],[2800,"When dinner is served and the prayer is established, begin with dinner."],[2801,"When dinner is served and the prayer is called, begin with dinner."],[2802,"The Hour will not come until people vie with one another in building mosques."],[2803,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan b. Musa narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said something similar."],[2804,"If one of you becomes drowsy while praying, let him leave until he understands what he is saying."],[2805,"If one of you becomes drowsy, let him leave until he knows what he is doing."],[2806,"If one of you becomes drowsy in prayer, let him leave and sleep."],[2807,"If one of you becomes drowsy in his prayer, let him leave and lie down."],[2808,"Bilal was commanded to repeat the adhan twice and to make the iqamah odd-numbered."],[2809,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with his companions, and when he finished his prayer he turned to face them and said: 'Do you recite in your prayer behind the imam while the imam is reciting?' They remained silent, and he said it three times. Then a speaker, or speakers, said: 'Indeed we do.' He said: 'Do not do so. Let one of you recite the Opening of the Book to himself.'"],[2810,"The Prophet ﷺ turned to two horned, black-and-white rams and slaughtered them with his own hand."],[2811,"Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[2812,"Every nation has a trusted one, and our trusted one, O nation, is Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[2813,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in his house, and the servant of the Messenger of God, called Anjasha, was singing to drive the camels. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Woe to you, O Anjasha, drive slowly with the glass vessels.'"],[2814,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon his wives while a camel driver, called Anjasha, was driving them. He said: 'Woe to you, O Anjasha, drive slowly, drive the glass vessels gently.'"],[2815,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the noon prayer in Madinah as four rak'ahs and prayed the afternoon prayer at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two rak'ahs."],[2816,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the noon prayer in Madinah as four rak'ahs and prayed the afternoon prayer at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two rak'ahs."],[2817,"Three qualities, whoever has them will find thereby the sweetness of faith: that God and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything else; that he loves a person only for God's sake; and that he hates to return to disbelief as he hates to have a fire lit and be thrown into it."],[2818,"I was riding behind Abu Talha, and they were crying out for both of them: the Hajj and the 'Umrah."],[2819,"Every community has a trustee, and our trustee, O community, is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[2820,"A group of eight from 'Ukl came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. They found the land unhealthy and their bodies fell ill, so they complained of that to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'Will you not go out with our shepherd among his camels and take of their urine and milk?' They did so and became healthy, then they killed the shepherd and drove off the camels. That news reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he sent in their pursuit. They were caught and brought, and he ordered regarding them. Their hands and feet were cut off, their eyes were gouged out, then they were thrown in the sun until they died."],[2821,"We went out with him to the sanctuary, and when prayer time came, he said: 'Will you not dismount and pray?' I said: 'If only you would go forward to this mosque.' He said: 'Which mosque?' It was said: 'The mosque of Banu so-and-so.' He became alarmed and said: 'I heard him say ﷺ: A time will come upon my community when they will vie with one another in [building] mosques but will not frequent them except a little.'"],[2822,"A man from the Jews killed a girl of the Ansar for some silver ornaments she had, then threw her into a well and crushed her head with stones. He was caught and brought to the Prophet ﷺ, who ordered that he be stoned, and he was stoned until he died."],[2823,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted a household of the Ansar to use incantations for fever, and permitted incantations for the evil eye and the sting."],[2824,"Some men of my community will meet 'Isa son of Maryam and witness the fighting against the Dajjal."],[2825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four rak'ahs, and prayed 'Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two rak'ahs. He spent the night there until morning. When he had prayed Subh, he mounted his riding camel. When his mount set off with him, he glorified Allah and proclaimed His greatness until it brought him to a level place at al-Bayda'. Then he combined them. When we arrived in Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to exit ihram. On the Day of Tarwiyah, they entered ihram for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered seven camels with his own hand while they were standing, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned, white sheep."],[2826,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he commanded them to exit ihram except those who had sacrificial animals with them. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered seven camels while they were standing."],[2827,"Seven for a virgin, and three for a previously married woman. Indeed, had I said it was from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would have spoken the truth, but it is a sunnah."],[2828,"The first li'an in Islam was that Sharik b. Sahma' was accused by Hilal b. Umayyah regarding his wife. The matter was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Hilal, four witnesses, or else a hadd punishment on your back.\" He replied: \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah knows that I am truthful, and Allah will surely reveal what will clear my back from flogging.\" Then Allah revealed the verse of li'an: \"And those who accuse their wives, and have no witnesses except themselves...\" until the end of the verse. The Prophet ﷺ summoned him and said: \"Testify by Allah that you are among the truthful in what you accused her of regarding adultery.\" He testified to that four times. Then he said to him the fifth time: \"And the curse of Allah be upon you if you are among the liars in what you accused her of regarding adultery.\" He did so. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned her and said: \"Stand and testify by Allah that he is among the liars in what he accused you of regarding adultery.\" She testified to that four times. Then he said to her the fifth time: \"And the wrath of Allah be upon you if he is among the truthful in what he accused you of regarding adultery.\" She said... Makhallad said: When it came to the fourth or fifth time, she paused briefly until they thought she would confess, then she said: \"I will not disgrace my people for the rest of the day.\" She continued with her statement. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated them and said: \"Observe her. If she gives birth to a curly-haired child with lean calves, he belongs to Sharik b. Sahma'. If she gives birth to a fair, straight-haired child with bright eyes, he belongs to Hilal b. Umayyah.\" She gave birth to a dark, curly-haired child with lean calves. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were it not for what Allah revealed about them, I would have had a matter with her.\""],[2829,"Hilal b. Umayyah accused his wife with Sharik b. Sahma'. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Observe her. If she gives birth to a fair, straight-haired child, he belongs to Hilal b. Umayyah. If she gives birth to one with dark eyelids, curly hair, and lean calves, he belongs to Sharik b. Sahma'.\" She gave birth to one with dark eyelids, curly hair, and lean calves."],[2830,"Whoever slaughtered before the prayer should repeat it. A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this is a day on which meat is desired,\" and he mentioned some shortcoming among his neighbors, as if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ believed him. He said: \"I have a jadha'ah that is dearer to me than two meat sheep.\" He said: So he granted him a concession. I do not know whether his concession reached others besides him or not. The people turned to some small sheep and divided them among themselves, or he said: \"and cut them up.\""],[2831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice, then ordered the camels to be slaughtered, and they were slaughtered. The barber was sitting near him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arranged his hair that day with his hand, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his hair on the right side of his head, then said to the barber: \"Shave.\" So he shaved. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed his hair that day among the people who were present, one hair or two hairs at a time. Then he took hold of the hair on the left side of his head with his hand, then said to the barber: \"Shave.\" So he shaved. Then he called Abu Talhah al-Ansari and gave it to him."],[2832,"On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed: \"The donkeys have been eaten.\" He ordered Abu Talhah to announce: \"Allah and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys, for it is impure.\" They said: So the pots were overturned."],[2833,"We asked Anas: \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye his hair?\" He said: \"He did not reach the stage of dyeing; there were only a few white hairs in his beard.\" He said: I asked him: \"Did Abu Bakr dye his hair?\" He said: \"Yes, with henna and katam.\""],[2834,"Abu Talhah learned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had no food, so he went and hired himself out for a sa' of barley and worked that day. He came with it and said: \"Bake this.\" He said: \"It is barley, but make it into khatifah.\" She made it. He sent Anas b. Malik and said: \"Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him privately.\" Anas went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was with his companions and said: \"Food?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Get up.\" So they got up. When Anas came to Abu Talhah, he said: \"I said that.\" He said: \"Food?\" I disliked lying, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and invited ten. They entered and ate until they were full. Then he invited ten more, and they entered and ate until they were full. Then he invited ten more, and they entered and ate until they were full. Then there remained for his family enough to satisfy them."],[2835,"Anas was asked about the dyeing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not have gray hair except a little, but Abu Bakr and 'Umar dyed with henna and katam.\" He said: Abu Bakr brought his father Abu Quhafah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: \"If you had left the old man in his house, we would have come to him, out of honor for Abu Bakr.\" He said: He accepted Islam with his beard and head like the thaghamah plant. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Change it, and keep him away from black dye.\""],[2836,"I said to Anas: \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform qunut in the Subh prayer?\" He said: \"Yes, after ruku'.\" He said: Then he was asked later: \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform qunut in the Subh prayer?\" He said: \"Yes, after ruku', briefly.\""],[2837,"I bear witness that Allah is true, that meeting Him is true, that the Hour is true, that Paradise is true, and that the Fire is true. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Dajjal, from the trials of life and death, from the punishment of the grave, and from the punishment of Jahannam."],[2838,"I asked Anas b. Malik: Did Umar perform qunut? He said: One better than Umar performed qunut; the Prophet ﷺ performed qunut."],[2839,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped and gave the cupper his wages."],[2840,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit us and mix with us. There was a young boy with us called Abu Umayr, and he said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?"],[2841,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[2842,"We were forbidden that a town-dweller sell on behalf of a desert-dweller."],[2843,"Anas narrated little hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he did narrate, he would say: 'or as he said.'"],[2844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the jamarat, and the barber was sitting. He ordered the sacrificial camels to be brought, and they were slaughtered. He said to the barber: 'Here,' and he pointed with his hand to the right side. He said: Then he distributed his hair among those near him. He said: Then he pointed to the barber to his left side, and he shaved it, and he gave it to Umm Sulaym."],[2845,"The head of al-Husayn was brought to Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad in a basin, and he said something about its beauty. Anas said: He was the one among them most resembling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2846,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he called upon Allah and was answered, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my Ummah."],[2847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ubayy: Allah has commanded me to recite to you. He said: Did Allah name me to you? He said: Allah named you to me. Then Ubayy began to weep."],[2848,"Allah does not wrong a believer for a good deed; he is rewarded for it with provision in this world and recompensed for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is given his good deeds until when he reaches the Hereafter, he has no good deed left by which to be given good."],[2849,"He used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, from deeds that are not raised, from a heart that does not humble itself, and from words that are not heard."],[2850,"He used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You"],[2851,"I said to Anas: How was the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: It was wavy hair, not curly and not straight, falling between his neck and his shoulders."],[2852,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[2853,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley for them. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to the one who repents."],[2854,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[2855,"No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop and a bird, a human, or an animal eats from it, but it is counted as charity for him."],[2856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while completing it fully."],[2857,"Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you stretch out his forearms like a dog."],[2858,"Whoever forgets a prayer should pray it when he remembers it."],[2859,"Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it."],[2860,"Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it. There is no expiation for it except that."],[2861,"The son of Adam grows old, and two things remain young in him: greed for wealth and greed for life."],[2862,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing will fill the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah relents to whoever repents."],[2863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered his sacrificial animal with his own hand and said takbir over it."],[2864,"Allah is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you who wakes up in a desolate land and finds his camel after having lost it."],[2865,"Prices became high in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said, 'O Messenger of Allah, fix prices for us.' He said, 'Allah is the One who withholds, extends, prices, and provides. I hope to meet Allah while none of you has a claim against me for a wrong concerning life or property.'"],[2866,"He would pass by a fallen date, and nothing prevented him from taking it except fear that it might be from charity."],[2867,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never addressed us except that he said, 'There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant.'"],[2868,"He was among the briefest of people in prayer while still complete."],[2869,"The servant remains in good as long as he does not seek to hasten. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how does he seek to hasten?' He said, 'He says, \"I supplicated, but I do not see it being answered.\"'"],[2870,"A girl was found with her head crushed between two stones. It was said to her, 'Who did this to you? So-and-so? So-and-so?' until a Jew was mentioned, and she nodded with her head. So the Jew was arrested, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that his head be crushed with stones."],[2871,"He forbade drinking while standing."],[2872,"He had a camel-driver called Anjasha, and he had a beautiful voice, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Gently, O Anjasha, do not break the glass vessels.'"],[2873,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: 'Ride it.' The man said: 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said: 'Ride it, woe to you.'"],[2874,"There is no contagion and no evil omen, but I like the good omen: the good word, the pleasant word."],[2875,"I said to Anas: 'Was the handshake practiced in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[2876,"The Prophet ﷺ performed four ‘umrahs, all of them in Dhul-Qa‘dah except the one that was with his Hajj: his ‘umrah from al-Hudaybiyyah or the time of al-Hudaybiyyah in Dhul-Qa‘dah, and his ‘umrah the following year in Dhul-Qa‘dah, and his ‘umrah from al-Ji‘ranah where he divided the spoils of Hunayn in Dhul-Qa‘dah, and his ‘umrah with his Hajj."],[2877,"I said to Anas: 'Which garment was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or most pleasing to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'The hibarah.'"],[2878,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed continuous fasting, and the people also observed continuous fasting, so he forbade them from continuous fasting and said: 'I am given food and drink, if Allah wills.'"],[2879,"He had large hands and large feet, a handsome face; I have not seen anyone like him after him."],[2880,"While I was walking in Paradise, I came to a river whose banks were domes of hollow pearls. I said: 'What is this, O Jibril?' He said: 'This is al-Kawthar which your Lord has given you.' The angel struck it with his hand, and its mud was fragrant musk."],[2881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams that were white with black markings. He placed his foot on their sides and slaughtered them with his own hand, saying the name of Allah and magnifying Him."],[2882,"We said to Anas: 'Who collected the Qur'an during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Four, all of them from the Ansar: Ubayy b. Ka‘b, Mu‘adh b. Jabal, Zayd b. Thabit, and a man from the Ansar called Abu Zayd.'"],[2883,"There is no one among the people of Paradise who would like to return to this world, even if he had ten times its like, except the martyr. He would wish to return to this world and be killed ten times because of the excellence he sees."],[2884,"That al-Zubayr b. al-‘Awwam and ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf complained to the Prophet ﷺ about lice, so he granted them a concession to wear silk shirts, and I saw a silk shirt on each of them."],[2885,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ‘Umar used to begin the recitation with “All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds.”"],[2886,"That a group from ‘Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we found Madinah unhealthy, so our bellies swelled and our flesh wasted away. He ordered them, and they came to the shepherd of the zakat camels, and they drank from their milk and urine until their bodies recovered. Then they killed the shepherd, drove off the camels, and apostatized. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent someone after them, and they were brought back. He cut off their hands and feet, gouged out their eyes, and threw them into the harrah."],[2887,"That a tailor in Madinah invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to barley bread and fat, and it had gourd in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like gourd, so I would push it forward before him. Anas said: And gourd has not ceased to please me."],[2888,"None of you should spit to his right, but let him spit to his left."],[2889,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[2890,"Some people will come out of the Fire after being scorched by it, then they will enter Paradise, and the people of Paradise will call them the Jahannamiyyin."],[2891,"A servant does not believe until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself of good."],[2892,"That a man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: A man loves a people but has not yet joined them? He said: A person is with whom he loves."],[2893,"One who said “There is no god but Allah” will come out of the Fire, having in his heart good the weight of a barley grain. Then he said: One who said “There is no god but Allah” will come out of the Fire, having in his heart good the weight of a wheat grain. Then: One who said “There is no god but Allah” will come out of the Fire, having in his heart good the weight of an atom."],[2894,"We used to come to Anas while his baker was standing, and he said: Eat, for I do not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever saw a thin loaf of bread or a roasted sheep with his own eyes until he joined Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[2895,"He forbade soaking dates and raisins together."],[2896,"The Hour will not come — or he said: among the signs of the Hour — until knowledge is lifted, ignorance becomes widespread, wine is drunk, adultery becomes widespread, men become few, and women become many, until for fifty women there is a single guardian."],[2897,"I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that stage; his gray hair was only at his temples. But Abu Bakr and Umar dyed with henna and katam."],[2898,"A man who had become drunk was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered about twenty men, who struck him with palm branches and sandals. Then a drunk man was brought to Abu Bakr, and he flogged him forty lashes. When Umar took charge and people became addicted to wine, he consulted the people, and Abd al-Rahman said: I think you should make it... And the text broke off for Abu Yala at one word, I believe he said: eighty."],[2899,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ with his companions near al-Zawra, or he said: near the houses of Madinah. He wanted to perform ablution, and a bowl containing a little water was brought to him. He placed his hand on the bowl, and water began to gush from between his fingers until all the people performed ablution. I said to Anas: How many were you? He said: About three hundred."],[2900,"Umm Sulaym sent with him something — Hammam named it as containing fresh dates — to the Prophet ﷺ, and he began to take a handful and send it to some of his wives, and take a handful while he himself desired it."],[2901,"He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from leprosy, elephantiasis, madness, and the worst of diseases."],[2902,"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as if it were a black and white ram, and it will be stood between Paradise and the Fire. Then a caller will call out: O people of Paradise? They will say: At Your service, our Lord. He said: Then it will be said: Do you recognize this? They will say: Yes, our Lord, this is death. Then it will be slaughtered as a sheep is slaughtered, so these will be safe, and the hope of those will be cut off."],[2903,"God will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be inspired to them, so they will say: If only we could intercede with our Lord to relieve us from our place. He said: Then they will come to Adam and say: O Adam, father of creation, God created you with His hand and made His angels prostrate to you, so intercede for us with your Lord to relieve us from our place. He will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his sin that he committed and feel ashamed before his Lord because of it, but go to Noah, the first messenger God sent. So they will come to Noah, and he will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his sin that he committed and feel ashamed before his Lord, but go to Abraham. He said: Then they will come to Abraham, and he will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his sin that he committed and feel ashamed before his Lord because of it, but go to Moses. So they will come to Moses, and he will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his sin that he committed and feel ashamed before his Lord because of it, but go to Jesus, the spirit of God and His word. He said: Then they will come to Jesus, and he will say: I am not the one for that, but go to Muhammad, a servant whom God has forgiven his past and future sins. He said: Then they will come to me, and I will ask permission and be granted permission. When I see my Lord, I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as God wills to leave me. Then He will say: Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return and fall prostrate and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return and fall prostrate and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then it will be said: O Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises He teaches me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise. And he said on the third or fourth time: None will remain in the Fire except those whom the Quran has detained."],[2904,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood in prayer until his feet or his legs became swollen. It was said to him: Has not God forgiven you your past and future sins? He said: Should I not be a grateful servant?"],[2905,"The Hour will not come until knowledge is lifted, ignorance becomes widespread, women become many, and men become few, until a single man is the guardian of fifty women."],[2906,"The lifespan of my community is between sixty and seventy, and the fewest of them are those who reach eighty."],[2907,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[2908,"When he went on a military expedition, he would say: O Allah, You are my support, and You are my helper, and by You I fight."],[2909,"When a strong wind blew, he would say: O Allah, I ask You for the good of what it has been commanded to do, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what it has been commanded to do."],[2910,"I asked Anas b. Malik: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He used to prolong his voice, a full prolongation."],[2911,"When the Prophet of Allah Musa ﷺ summoned his companion to the term that was between them, his companion said to him: Every ewe that gives birth to a lamb of a color other than its own, its offspring is yours. He said: So he went and placed ropes on the water, and when the ewes saw the ropes, they took fright and bolted, and they all gave birth to speckled lambs except one ewe. So he took their offspring that year."],[2912,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Khaybar, he said: When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned."],[2913,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[2914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Uhud, with Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and it quaked with them. He struck it with his foot and said: Be firm, Uhud! A Prophet, a steadfast truthful one, and two martyrs."],[2915,"He used to supplicate with the palms of his hands, and he would say: Like this, showing his palms."],[2916,"He used to pray in his leather socks and sandals."],[2917,"He forbade fasting on five days of the year: the day of Fitr, the day of sacrifice, and the three days of Tashriq."],[2918,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ related when he was taken up to the heaven, saying: I came upon Idris in the fourth heaven."],[2919,"He was leading them in prayer when a man came and entered the prayer, out of breath. He said: Allah is Greater; praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: Which of you spoke those words? The people remained silent. He said: Which of you spoke those words, for he did not say anything wrong? The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah; I came out of breath and said them. He said: I saw twelve angels rushing to see which of them would take them up."],[2920,"When the People of the Book greet you, say: 'And upon you.'"],[2921,"Do not let Bilal's call to prayer prevent you from taking the pre-dawn meal, for there is something wrong with his eyesight."],[2922,"What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky during their prayer? His words about that became severe, until he said: \"They must stop that, or their eyesight will be snatched away.\""],[2923,"The Prophet ﷺ saw some meat and said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"It was given as charity to Barirah.\" He said: \"It is charity for her, and a gift for us.\""],[2924,"Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If a woman sees that fluid and ejaculates, she must perform ghusl.\" Umm Sulaym said: \"O Messenger of God, does this happen?\" He said: \"Yes. The man's fluid is thick and white, and the woman's fluid is thin and yellow. Whichever of them prevails or is emitted first, the child will resemble that one.\""],[2925,"Usayyah, Dhakwan, and Banu Lihyan came to the Prophet ﷺ and sought reinforcements against their enemy, having embraced Islam. He reinforced them with seventy of the Ansar who were called the reciters. They would gather firewood by day and pray at night, until when they were at the well of Ma'unah, they killed them. The Messenger of God ﷺ then performed qunut for a month, supplicating against them."],[2926,"Every son of Adam sins, and the best of sinners are those who repent."],[2927,"Islam is outward, and faith is in the heart—then he pointed with his hand to his chest—piety is here, piety is here."],[2928,"The Messenger of God ﷺ liked gourd. He said: One day I saw him eating food that had gourd in it, so I kept putting it near him."],[2929,"I and the Hour were sent like these two—Abu Sa'id said, holding up his two fingers: the index and the middle finger."],[2930,"It will be said to a man on the Day of Resurrection: 'If you had the earth full of gold, would you ransom yourself with it?' He will say: 'Yes.' He said: Then it will be said to him: 'You were asked for something easier than that.'"],[2931,"Whoever said 'There is no god but God' and had in his heart good the weight of a grain of wheat will come out of the Fire. Then whoever said 'There is no god but God' and had in his heart good the weight of an atom will come out of the Fire."],[2932,"Every prophet had a supplication he made, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection."],[2933,"The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[2934,"Regarding His saying: “The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split,” he said: It had indeed split during the time of the Messenger of God."],[2935,"Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, fornication will spread, men will become few, and women will become many, so that there will be one guardian for fifty women."],[2936,"This verse was sent down upon the Prophet ﷺ: “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory,” upon his return from Ḥudaybiyyah, while he and his companions were still mingled with sorrow, and they had been prevented from their rites and had slaughtered the sacrificial animals at Ḥudaybiyyah. When this verse was sent down, he said to his companions: “A verse better than the whole world has been sent down to me.” When the Prophet of God ﷺ recited it, a man from the people said: “Congratulations, O Prophet of God! God has made clear what He will do with you, so what will He do with us?” Then God sent down after it: “That He may admit the believing men and the believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow.”"],[2937,"The general instruction of the Messenger of God ﷺ when death approached him was: “The prayer, and what your right hands possess,” until he began to gurgle it in his chest and his tongue could no longer utter it."],[2938,"I repent seventy times a day."],[2939,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would not raise his hands in any supplication except when praying for rain; then he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[2940,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man to put on his sandals while standing."],[2941,"Three men set out to seek provision for their families, and they were caught by the sky [i.e., a storm]. A rock fell upon them, leaving only a small opening through which they could not even see a chink. One of them said: “The rock has fallen and obliterated the trace, and no one knows your place except God. So call upon God by the most certain of your deeds.” A man said: “O God, You know that I had two parents, and I used to milk for them in their vessel. When I found them sleeping, I would stand by their heads until they woke up, whenever they woke, out of dislike to disturb their sleep. O God, if You know that I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us.” He said: A third of the rock moved away. The second said: “O God, if You know that a woman amazed me, and that I set a substitute for her, but when I had power over her, I gave her her full due and left her to herself. O God, if You know that I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us.” He said: A third of the rock moved away. The other said: “O God, You know that I hired a laborer for work he was to do for me. He came seeking his wages while I was angry, so I rebuffed him, and he went away leaving his wages. So I gathered it for him and invested it until it became a great amount of wealth. Then he came seeking his wages, and I gave him all of that. If I had wished, I would have given him only his original wages. O God, if You know that I did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then open a way for us.” He said: The rock moved away, and they came out walking."],[2942,"Three men among those who came before were..."],[2943,"A man said: “O Messenger of God, how many prayers has God made obligatory upon His servants?” He said: “Five prayers.” He said: “Is there anything before or after them?” He said: “God has made five prayers obligatory upon His servants.” The man swore by God that he would not add to them or subtract from them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If he is truthful, he will enter Paradise.”"],[2944,"A questioner said: “O Prophet of God, does he not intend [to go to] Madinah?”—meaning the Dajjal. He said: “He will indeed head for it, but he will find the angels at its mountain passes and its gates, guarding it from the Dajjal.”"],[2945,"He used to go around to his wives in a single hour of the night or day, and they were eleven. He [the sub-narrator] said: I said to Anas: “Could he manage that?” He said: “We used to say that he had the strength of thirty men.”"],[2946,"He used to go around to his wives with a single ghusl."],[2947,"“Look at whom you see in the mosque.” I looked, and there was Zayd b. Thabit, so I called him. We ate some dates and drank some water, then we went out to the prayer, and the prayer was commenced."],[2948,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ after performing wudu but leaving on his feet a spot the size of a fingernail [dry]. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Go back and perfect your wudu.”"],[2949,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ‘aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two rams."],[2950,"When the Prophet of God Musa ﷺ summoned his companion for the term that was between them, his companion said to him: “Every ewe that gives birth to a lamb of a color other than her own, its offspring is yours.” He said: So he set up ropes over the water. When the sheep saw the ropes, they became startled and bolted, and all of them gave birth to lambs of mixed colors except a single ewe. He said: So he took their offspring that year."],[2951,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to Bakr b. Wa’il: “From Muhammad, the Messenger of God, to Bakr b. Wa’il: Submit [become Muslims] and you will be safe.” We found no one to read it except a man from Banu Dubay‘ah, so they are called Banu al-Katib [the sons of the scribe]."],[2952,"Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."],[2953,"When the Prophet ﷺ went on a military expedition, he would say: “O God, You are my support, and You are my helper, and by You I fight.”"],[2954,"None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[2955,"If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would seek a second; and if he had a second, he would seek a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. And God turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[2956,"That a man used to buy during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and in his knot there was weakness, so his family came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, place a restriction on so-and-so, for he buys while in his knot there is weakness.\" So the Prophet ﷺ called him and forbade him from selling. He said, \"O Prophet of God, I cannot have patience away from selling.\" So he ﷺ said, \"If you are not going to leave off the transaction, then say: 'Here you are; there is no deception.'\""],[2957,"The two tribes of the Ansar, al-Aws and al-Khazraj, boasted. Al-Aws said, \"From us is the one washed by the angels, Hanzalah b. al-Rahib; from us is the one for whom the Throne of the Most Merciful shook, Sa'd b. Mu'adh; from us is the one protected by the swarm of bees, 'Asim b. Thabit b. Abi al-Aqlah; from us is the one whose testimony was accepted as the testimony of two men, Khuzaymah b. Thabit.\" And the Khazrajis said, \"From us are four who collected the Qur'an during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ; no one other than them collected it: Zayd b. Thabit, Abu Zayd, Ubayy b. Ka'b, and Mu'adh b. Jabal.\""],[2958,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to Chosroes and Caesar and to every tyrant, calling them to God."],[2959,"He will come out of the Fire whoever said, 'There is no god but God,' and had in his heart good the weight of a barley grain. Then he will come out of the Fire whoever said, 'There is no god but God,' and had in his heart good the weight of a wheat grain. Then he will come out of the Fire whoever said, 'There is no god but God,' and had in his heart good the weight of a dust particle."],[2960,"Abu Bistam made a mistake in it:"],[2961,"And Ibrahim had asked him for a fatwa about something, so 'Imran gave him a fatwa in it with a ruling, and Ibrahim gave a fatwa to men; 'Imran says: 'They were all killed':"],[2962,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ did not raise his hands in anything of supplication except in the prayer for rain, for he used to raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."],[2963,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a flea bit a man, and he cursed it. So the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not curse it, for it awakened a prophet among the prophets for prayer.'"],[2964,"There are no two servants who love each other for the sake of God, meeting each other and shaking hands, and invoking blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, except that they do not part before their sins are forgiven, the earlier and the later."],[2965,"Among the signs of the Hour is that knowledge will be lifted and ignorance will appear."],[2966,"There was a scare in Madinah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub, and he said, 'We have not seen any cause for fear, and indeed we found him to be a sea.'"],[2967,"There will be in my community disagreement and a faction who make good speech and do evil deeds, who recite the Qur'an but it does not go beyond their collarbones. One of you will belittle his prayer compared to their prayer and his fasting compared to their fasting. They are the worst of creation and creatures. Blessed is the one who kills them and whom they kill. They call to the Book of God, but they have nothing to do with it. Whoever kills them is closer to God than they are. They said, 'O Messenger of God, what is their mark?' He said, 'Shaving the head.'"],[2968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman followed him, and it quaked with them. He said: 'Stand firm, a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.'"],[2969,"What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky? And his words became stern concerning that. He said: 'They must stop that, or their eyes will be snatched away.'"],[2970,"He used not to raise his hands in any supplication except in seeking rain, for he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[2971,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, a servant does not believe until he loves for his neighbor or for his brother what he loves for himself."],[2972,"When one of you is in his prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but to his left under his foot."],[2973,"There was a fright in Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah. He said: 'We have seen nothing, and if we found it, it would be a sea.'"],[2974,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated for his community, and I have saved my supplication as intercession for my community."],[2975,"Complete the bowing and prostration, for by Allah I see you from behind my back."],[2976,"Do not practice continuous fasting. They said: 'But you practice continuous fasting.' He said: 'I am not like any one of you; I am fed and given to drink.'"],[2977,"He forbade drinking while standing."],[2978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams. He would place his foot on their sides and slaughter them with his own hand, pronouncing the name of Allah and saying Allahu Akbar."],[2979,"The Prophet ﷺ found a date and said: 'Were it not that I fear it might be charity, I would eat it.'"],[2980,"It will be said to the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection: 'If you had the like of the world in gold, would you ransom yourself with it?' He said: He will say: 'Yes.' Then it will be said: 'You were asked for something easier than that.'"],[2981,"One who said, 'There is no god but Allah,' and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a barley grain will come out of the Fire. Then one who said, 'There is no god but Allah,' and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a wheat grain will come out of the Fire. Then one who said, 'There is no god but Allah,' and had in his heart good equal to the weight of a speck of dust will come out of the Fire."],[2982,"Some peoples will certainly be scorched by the Fire as a punishment for sins they committed, then Allah will admit them to Paradise by the grace of His mercy and the intercession of the intercessors. They will be called the Jahannamiyyun (the people of Hell)."],[2983,"The son of Adam grows old, and two things grow young in him: greed for wealth and greed for life."],[2984,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin with 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'"],[2985,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin with 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'"],[2986,"Abu Musa Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us: Mu'adh b. Mu'adh narrated to us from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2987,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[2988,"Abu Musa narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah, from Anas, something similar, except that he said in his hadith: 'And sometimes he had doubt concerning Anas.'"],[2989,"Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[2990,"Be moderate in prostration, and none of you should spread his forearms like a dog."],[2991,"He did not raise his hands in any supplication except in the prayer for rain, until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen, except that Abd al-A'la said: until the whiteness of his armpit or the whiteness of his armpit could be seen."],[2992,"Abu Musa narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, that Anas b. Malik narrated to them from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[2993,"I certainly turn in repentance seventy times in a day."],[2994,"The general instruction of the Messenger of God ﷺ was prayer, and what your right hands possess, when death came to him, until it became a gurgling sound in his chest, and his tongue could not utter it."],[2995,"In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for—in Abu Ya'la's book: one thousand years—without traversing it."],[2996,"I served the Messenger of God ﷺ for ten years. He never said about something I did, 'Why did you do it?' nor about something I did not do, 'Why did you not do it?'"],[2997,"Whoever says, 'There is no god but God,' and has in his heart good equal to the weight of a barley grain will come out of the Fire; and whoever says, 'There is no god but God,' and has in his heart good equal to the weight of a wheat grain will come out of the Fire; and whoever says, 'There is no god but God,' and has in his heart good equal to the weight of an atom will come out of the Fire."],[2998,"The Ansar are my close companions and my trusted confidants. People will increase in number while they decrease, so accept from their good-doers and pardon their wrongdoers."],[2999,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Ubayy b. Ka'b, 'God has commanded me to recite to you: \"Those who disbelieve\" (Surah al-Bayyinah).' He said, 'And He named me?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then he wept.'"],[3000,"Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have prayed to God to make you hear the punishment of the grave."],[3001,"Make your rows straight, for straightening the rows is part of perfecting the prayer."],[3002,"There was a fright in Madinah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ borrowed a horse called Mandub. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'We saw no fright, but we found it to be a sea.'"],[3003,"I and the Hour were sent like these two."],[3004,"Three things, whoever has them will find the taste of faith: one who loves a person, loving him only for God; one for whom God and His Messenger are more beloved than anything besides them; and one for whom being thrown into the Fire is more beloved than returning to disbelief after God has saved him from it."],[3005,"He will find through them the sweetness of faith."],[3006,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gathered the Ansar and said: \"Is there anyone among you who is not of you?\" They said: \"No, except a nephew of ours.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The nephew of a people is one of them.\" He said: \"Quraysh are newly out of Jahiliyyah and a calamity, and I wanted to mend them and win their hearts. Are you not pleased that the people return with the worldly goods while you return with the Messenger of God to your homes? If the people were to take a valley and the Ansar a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar.\""],[3007,"O God, the true life is the life of the Hereafter, so honor the Ansar and the Muhajirun."],[3008,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought meat, and it was said to him: \"It was given as charity to Barirah.\" He said: \"For her it is charity, and for us it is a gift.\""],[3009,"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar and Uthman; they did not begin the recitation with 'In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.'"],[3010,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to love gourd. He said: \"He was brought food, or was invited to it.\" Anas said: \"I started to seek it out and place it before him, because I knew he loved it.\""],[3011,"Two men went out from the Prophet of God ﷺ on a dark night, and with them were what resembled two lamps illuminating before them. He said: \"When they parted, each one of them had one with him until he reached his family.\""],[3012,"I was serving drink to Abu Talhah, Abu Dujanah, and Suhayl b. Bayda from a waterskin of theirs containing a mixture of unripe dates and dates, when someone came in to us and said: \"A matter has occurred today.\" We said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"Wine has been made forbidden.\" So we poured it out, and that day we considered it wine."],[3013,"The Prophet of God ﷺ wanted to write to the Persians, and it was said to him: \"The Persians do not accept a letter except with a seal.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ made a silver seal, and it is as if I am looking at its whiteness in his hand."],[3014,"The son of Adam grows old, and two things in him remain young: greed for wealth and [desire for] long life."],[3015,"The Prophet ﷺ found a date and said: \"Had I not feared that it be charity, I would have eaten it.\""],[3016,"The garment most beloved to the Messenger of God ﷺ was the hibara."],[3017,"Some peoples will surely be touched by a scorching from the Fire as punishment for sins they committed, then God will surely admit them to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy."],[3018,"The Prophet ﷺ never ate at a low table or from a small bowl, nor was thin bread ever baked for him."],[3019,"The Prophet of God ﷺ flogged for wine with palm branches and sandals, then Abu Bakr flogged forty, then when Umar came and the people drew near to the countryside and villages, he said: What do you think about flogging for wine? Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said: I think you should make it the lightest of the prescribed punishments, so Umar flogged eighty."],[3020,"The Dajjal has written between his eyes: k f r. Qatadah mentioned that every believer, whether unlettered or literate, reads it. He will come forth amid scarcity of people and shortage of food, and he will enter all the cities of the Arabs except Taybah, which is Madinah. Someone said: O Prophet of God, does he not want Madinah? He said: Yes, but the angels are arrayed at its mountain passes and gates guarding it."],[3021,"There is no prophet but warned his community against the one-eyed Dajjal. He is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is 'unbeliever.'"],[3022,"He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, miserliness, senility, the punishment of the grave, and the trials of life and death."],[3023,"None of the people of Paradise would wish to return to this world except the martyr, for he loves to return to this world, saying: So that I may be killed ten times in the path of God, because of the honor he sees that God has given him."],[3024,"Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Anas narrating from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[3025,"It will be said to the disbeliever: What if you had the earth's fill of gold, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. Then it will be said to him: You were asked for something easier than that."],[3026,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he prayed for his community, and I have stored away my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection."],[3027,"A man from the desert asked the Prophet of God ﷺ — and they were more entitled to ask him than his Companions — saying: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it anything except that I love God and His Messenger. He said: Then you will be with those you love. Anas said: I never saw the Muslims rejoice at anything after Islam as intensely as they rejoiced at his saying."],[3028,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"When is the Hour?\" He said, \"What have you prepared for it?\" He said, \"I love Allah and His Messenger.\" He said, \"You will be with those you love.\""],[3029,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram for both Hajj and Umrah together."],[3030,"There is no contagion and no evil omen, but I am pleased by good omens.\" He said: It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is a good omen?\" He said, \"A good word.\""],[3031,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is a good omen?\" He said, \"A good word.\""],[3032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut for a month. Shu'bah said: \"Cursing.\" Hisham said: \"Supplicating against tribes of the Arab tribes.\" Then he abandoned it after bowing."],[3033,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunut for a month, cursing Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Banu Lihyan."],[3034,"\"I intend to fast; do you have anything?\" He said, \"So I brought him a plate with dates and a vessel with water after Bilal had given the call to prayer. He said, 'Look for someone to eat.' So I went out and found Zayd b. Thabit, and I invited him. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I drank a sip of sawiq while I intend to fast.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And I intend to fast.' So he ate the pre-dawn meal with him, then prayed two rak'ahs, then went out and the prayer was commenced.\""],[3035,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman beginning the recitation with 'Al-hamdu lillahi rabbi al-'alamin.'"],[3036,"O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar."],[3037,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ubayy b. Ka'b, \"My Lord commanded me to recite to you.\" He said, \"And He named me to you?\" He said, \"And He named you to me.\" He said, \"So Ubayy wept.\""],[3038,"When the funeral of Sa'd b. Mu'adh was carried, the hypocrites said, \"How light his funeral is!\" That was because of his judgment regarding Banu Qurayzah. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"The angels were carrying him.\""],[3039,"\"O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you, we see in ourselves what we love, and when we return to our families and mix with them, we disapprove of ourselves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If you were to persist in the state you are in when with me in seclusion, the angels would shake hands with you until they shade you with their wings visibly, but it is time after time.\""],[3040,"Some of the Prophet's companions ﷺ looked for water for ablution and did not find any. The Prophet ﷺ said: Here. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ place his hand in the vessel that had the water. He said: Perform ablution in the name of Allah. He said: I saw the water gushing from between his fingers, and the people were performing ablution until the last of them had done so."],[3041,"Indeed, a people will come out of the Fire, having been scorched by the Fire as punishment for sins they committed, and Allah will surely bring them out by the bounty of His mercy and admit them to Paradise."],[3042,"Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years and does not cross it."],[3043,"Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are: Maryam bt. Imran, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh."],[3044,"Among the signs of the Hour are: knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, adultery will spread, men will become few, and women will become many, to the point that one man will be the caretaker of fifty women."],[3045,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram on the top of his foot due to a pain he had."],[3046,"When wine was forbidden, he said: I was serving eleven men that day. He said: They ordered me, so I overturned it, and the people overturned their vessels with their contents until the streets were almost blocked by its smell. Anas said: Their wine that day was nothing but unripe dates and dried dates mixed together. He said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I had the wealth of an orphan, and I bought wine with it. Will you permit me to sell it and return the orphan's wealth? He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: May Allah fight the Jews; fat was forbidden to them, but they sold it and consumed its price. And he did not grant him permission to sell the wine."],[3047,"Regarding His saying: Evil was the morning of those who were warned, he said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Khaybar, he found them when they had gone out to their fields with their spades. When they saw him with the army, they retreated and returned to their fortress. The Prophet ﷺ said: Allah is greatest, Khaybar is ruined. Indeed, when we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned."],[3048,"A group from 'Ukl and 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — this is how Ma'mar said it. He said: They spoke of Islam, then they came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that they were people of livestock and not people of settled cultivation, and they found the climate of Madinah disagreeable, and they complained of its epidemic to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ ordered for them a herd of camels and a shepherd. He said: Go out from Madinah and drink of their urine and milk. They departed and camped at the edge of the Harrah, then they disbelieved after their Islam, killed the shepherd, and drove off the herd. The Prophet ﷺ sent after them, and they were brought back. He cut off their hands and feet, put out their eyes with heated nails, and left them at the edge of the Harrah gnawing at its stones until they died. Qatadah said: It has reached us that this verse was revealed concerning them: The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive upon earth for corruption... to the end of the verse."],[3049,"The verse: That Allah may forgive you what preceded of your sin and what will follow was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ on his return from al-Hudaybiyyah. The Prophet ﷺ said: A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than all that is on earth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it. They said: Congratulations and blessings, O Prophet of Allah. Allah has made clear to you what He will do for you, so what will He do for us? Then it was revealed: That He may admit the believing men and the believing women... until He reached: a great triumph."],[3050,"A man said: O Prophet of Allah, how will the disbeliever be gathered on his face on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Is not the One who made him walk on his feet in this world able to make him walk on his face on the Day of Resurrection?"],[3051,"I asked Anas b. Malik: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He would extend it with a full extension."],[3052,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped on the two posterior jugular veins and the upper back between the shoulders."],[3053,"None of you believes until I am dearer to him than his father, his child, and all people."],[3054,"The Prophet ﷺ married Safiyyah bt. Huyayy and made her manumission her dowry."],[3055,"The Dajjal will come to Madinah and find the angels guarding it, so the Dajjal will not enter it, nor will the plague, if Allah wills."],[3056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, but you fast continuously.\" He said, \"You are not like me. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.\""],[3057,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ having drunk wine, so he ordered him to be flogged with two sandals forty times. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Abu Bakr, and he did the same to him. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Umar, and he consulted the people about it. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said, \"I think you should make it the minimum of the prescribed punishments: eighty.\" So Umar flogged him eighty times."],[3058,"Some people will certainly be scorched by the Fire as a punishment for sins they committed, then Allah will admit them to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy; they will be called the Jahannamiyyun."],[3059,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the perfection — or from the perfection — of the prayer."],[3060,"No one who enters Paradise would wish to leave it, even if he had everything on earth, except the martyr, for he wishes to return and be killed ten times because of the honor he sees."],[3061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut for a month after ruku."],[3062,"There was a tree on the people's path that used to harm people. A man came to it and moved it away from the people's path. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I saw him enjoying himself in its shade in Paradise.'"],[3063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was once invited to a meal of barley bread and rancid melted fat."],[3064,"I certainly heard him one day saying: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there did not remain with Muhammad a ṣāʿ of grain or a ṣāʿ of dates, and he had that day nine wives.\""],[3065,"He indeed pawned a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madinah and took from him food, and he did not find anything with which to redeem it."],[3066,"Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will prevail, wine will be drunk, fornication will spread, men will become few, and women will become many until for fifty women there will be one caretaker."],[3067,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[3068,"The believers will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection and will be concerned about that. He said: They will say: 'If only we could intercede with our Lord so that He might relieve us from this place of ours.' He said: So they will set out until they come to Adam and say: 'O Adam, you are the father of mankind. Allah created you with His hand, made His angels prostrate to you, and taught you the names of all things. Intercede for us with your Lord so that He may relieve us from this place of ours.' He said: He will say: 'I am not in a position to do that,' and he will mention his error that he committed by eating from the tree. He said: He will say: 'But go to Nūḥ, the first messenger Allah sent.' He said: So they will set out until they come to Nūḥ, and he will say: 'I am not in a position to do that,' and he will mention his error that he committed by asking his Lord for what he had no knowledge of. He said: He will say: 'Go to Ibrāhīm, the intimate friend of the Most Merciful.' He said: So they will set out until they come to Ibrāhīm, and he will say: 'I am not in a position to do that,' and he will mention his three lies: his saying, 'Rather, this one, the greatest of them, did it'; his saying, 'Indeed, I am ill'; and his saying when he came upon the tyrant: 'Tell him that I am your brother, for I will tell him that you are my sister, for we are two believers in the Book of Allah; there are no believers on earth other than us.' He said: He will say: 'But go to Mūsā, the one to whom Allah spoke and gave the Torah.' So they will set out until they come to Mūsā, and he will say: 'I am not in a position to do that,' and he will mention his error that he committed before. He said: He will say: 'But go to ʿĪsā, the servant of Allah and His messenger, and His word and His spirit.' He said: So they will set out until they come to ʿĪsā, and he will say: 'I am not in a position to do that, but go to Muhammad ﷺ, may Allah forgive him his past and future sins.' He said: So they will come to me, and I will ask permission from my Lord, and permission will be granted to me. When I see Him, I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say to me: 'Raise your head, O Muhammad. Speak and you will be heard; intercede and your intercession will be accepted; ask and you will be given.' So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with a praise that He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return to my Lord a second time, and when I see my Lord I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it will be said to me: 'Raise your head, Muhammad. Speak and you will be heard; intercede and your intercession will be accepted; ask and you will be given.' So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with a praise that He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return a third time to my Lord, and when I see my Lord I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it will be said to me: 'Raise your head, Muhammad. Speak and you will be heard; intercede and your intercession will be accepted; ask and you will be given.' So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with a praise that He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and He will set a limit for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise, until I return to my Lord and it is said the fourth time. He said: Then I will say: 'O Lord, no one remains in the Fire except those whom the Quran has held back.' He said: He will say: 'Eternal abode has become due upon him.'"],[3069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who sleeps through the prayer or is heedless of it. He said: 'Its expiation is that he pray it when he remembers it.'"],[3070,"He used not to raise his hands in any of his supplication, or during any of his supplication, except in the prayer for rain, for he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[3071,"He used not to raise his hands in any supplication except in the prayer for rain, for he would raise them until his armpits appeared."],[3072,"He was among the lightest of people in prayer while still complete."],[3073,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt for a month after bowing, supplicating against some tribes of the Arab tribes."],[3074,"Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will prevail, wine will be drunk, fornication will spread, men will become few, and women will become many until for fifty women there will be one caretaker."],[3075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Kisrā, Qayṣar, and Ukaydir of Dūmah, calling them to Allah."],[3076,"A man from the desert people asked the Prophet of God ﷺ—and they were more entitled than his Companions to ask him—and said: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it anything great, except that I love God and His Messenger. He said: Then you will be with those whom you love. Anas said: I have not seen the people rejoice at anything after Islam more intensely than their rejoicing at his statement."],[3077,"Written between his eyes is 'k f r.' Abu Sa'id said: meaning 'kafir.' Qatadah said: And it was mentioned to us that every believer, whether unlettered or literate, will read it. He will come forth among few people and scarcity of food, and he will enter all the Arab cities except Taybah, which is Madinah. A speaker said: O Prophet of God, does he not want Madinah? He said: Yes, but the angels are standing in rows at its mountain passes, guarding it."],[3078,"He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, senility, the punishment of the grave, and the trial of life and death."],[3079,"When the Prophet of God ﷺ wanted to write to the non-Arabs, it was said to him: The non-Arabs do not accept a letter unless it has a seal. So he had a silver ring made; it is as if I am looking at its whiteness on his hand."],[3080,"He used to sacrifice two horned rams with black and white markings, and he would pronounce the name of God and say 'Allahu Akbar.' He (the narrator) said: I saw him slaughter them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides."],[3081,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited a man from putting on sandals while standing."],[3082,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the house of 'A'ishah and saw some meat. He said: Roast some of it for us. They said: O Messenger of God, it is charity. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Roast some of it for us, for it has reached its proper place."],[3083,"Wealth is not from abundance of worldly goods, but wealth is richness of the soul."],[3084,"The parable of the believer is like a stalk of grain: it bends sometimes and stands upright sometimes."],[3085,"A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he loves for people what he loves for himself of good."],[3086,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut only for a month after bowing."],[3087,"Umm Sulaym menstruated after she had performed the ifadah circumambulation, so the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded her to depart."],[3088,"Dawud b. Rushayd narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us something similar."],[3089,"Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will descend, wine will be drunk, women will become numerous, and men will become few, until one man will be the guardian of fifty women."],[3090,"Whoever sleeps through a prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers it."],[3091,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[3092,"Expectorating in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[3093,"A Jewish person passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'Al-sam 'alaykum (death be upon you).' The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ responded to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'He only said, al-sam 'alaykum.' So he called him and he admitted it. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Respond to him as he said.'"],[3094,"Which garment was most beloved to the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said, 'The hibara (a type of striped Yemeni cloak).'"],[3095,"How many times did the Messenger of God ﷺ perform Hajj? He said, 'One Hajj, and he performed four 'umrahs: his 'umrah from al-Hudaybiyyah, his 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah in Dhu al-Qa'dah when he divided the spoils of Hunayn, and his 'umrah with his Hajj.'"],[3096,"No prophet was sent except that he warned his nation about the one-eyed liar. Verily he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Between his eyes is written: kafir (disbeliever)."],[3097,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman used to begin the prayer with 'Al-hamdu li-llahi rabb al-'alamin' (Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds)."],[3098,"He would pass by a date, and nothing prevented him from taking it except fear that it might be charity."],[3099,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Bara'ah with Abu Bakr to the people of Makkah, then he called him back and sent 'Ali, saying, 'None shall convey it except a man from my own household.'"],[3100,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for a month, then he abandoned it."],[3101,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated and it was answered for him, and I have stored away my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection."],[3102,"His hair used to reach his shoulders."],[3103,"He forbade continuous fasting. It was said to him, “But you fast continuously.” He said, “I pass the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.”"],[3104,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was praying, and he said, “Praise be to God, good and blessed.” When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said, “Which of you said such-and-such words?” The people remained silent three times. Then a man from the group said, “I said them, and I intended nothing but good.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Twelve angels raced to it, and they did not know how to write it until they asked their Lord, and He said, ‘Write it as My servant said it.’”"],[3105,"The Prophet’s ﷺ sandal had two straps."],[3106,"He forbade soaking unripe dates and ripe dates together."],[3107,"Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us something similar."],[3108,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was on the pulpit and said, “O Messenger of God, ask God to send us rain.” He asked for rain, and we did not see even a wisp of cloud in the sky. Then we were rained upon, and it did not stop until the two lava fields were flowing with water. When Friday came, that same man or another stood and said, “Supplicate God to lift it from us.” He said, “I began to look at the clouds splitting to the north and right around Madinah, and not a drop fell in its midst.”"],[3109,"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."],[3110,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said, “Ride it.” The man said, “It is a sacrificial camel.” He said, “Woe to you, ride it.”"],[3111,"When one of you spits, let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."],[3112,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never had bread and meat for both lunch and dinner except when there were many guests."],[3113,"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is that he pray it when he remembers it."],[3114,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah twice. He said: I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah carrying a black banner."],[3115,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade drinking while standing and eating while standing."],[3116,"A jubbah of fine silk was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he used to forbid silk. The people marveled at it, so he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd b. Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this."],[3117,"The people of Makkah asked the Messenger of God ﷺ to show them a sign, so he showed them the splitting of the moon twice."],[3118,"A Jew came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Al-sam 'alaykum (death be upon you).' The people replied, so the Prophet of God ﷺ said: 'Do you know what he said?' They said: 'God and His Messenger know best. He greeted, O Prophet of God.' He said: 'No, but he said such and such. Bring him back to me.' He said: So they brought him back, and he said: 'Did you say al-sam 'alaykum?' He said: 'Yes.' The Prophet of God ﷺ then said: 'When one of the People of the Book greets you, say: Wa 'alayk (and upon you).' He said: 'Upon you be what you said, and when they come to you they greet you with what God has not greeted you with.'"],[3119,"There will be seen in it silver pitchers as numerous as the stars of the sky and more."],[3120,"She asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: 'When a woman sees that, she should perform ghusl.' Umm Sulaym said: 'I felt shy about that, so I said: Does this happen?' The Prophet of God ﷺ said: 'Yes, so where does resemblance come from? A man's fluid is thick, and a woman's fluid is thin and yellowish. Whichever of them prevails or comes first determines resemblance.'"],[3121,"There will be in my community disagreement and a faction who speak well but act badly. They recite the Qur'an but it does not pass beyond their collarbones. They pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through its target, then they do not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. They are the worst of creation and creatures. Blessed is the one who kills them, and blessed is the one whom they kill. They call to the Book of God, but they have nothing to do with it. Whoever fights them is closer to God than they are. They said: 'O Messenger of God, what is their mark?' He said: 'Shaving the head.'"],[3122,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams with white and black markings. He brought one of them near and said: 'In the name of God. O God, from You and to You, this is on behalf of Muhammad and his family.' He brought the other near and said: 'In the name of God. O God, from You and to You, this is on behalf of those of my community who affirm Your oneness.'"],[3123,"He used to wear a ring on his right hand."],[3124,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a flea bit a man and he cursed it. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Do not curse it, for it woke a prophet among the prophets for prayer.\""],[3125,"The Prophet ﷺ came out of the door of the house while heading to the room, and he heard people disputing about predestination, saying: \"Did God not say such-and-such a verse? Did God not say such-and-such a verse?\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ opened the door of the room, and it was as if pomegranate seeds had been burst in his face. He said: \"Is this what you were commanded, or is this what you were entrusted with? Those before you perished only because of things like this: they struck the Book of God against itself. God commanded you with a matter, so follow it; and He forbade you, so desist.\" He said: After that, people did not hear anyone speak about it until Ma'bad al-Juhani came, and al-Hajjaj seized him and killed him."],[3126,"The verse \"O people, fear your Lord\" up to His saying \"But the punishment of God is severe\" was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a journey. He raised his voice with it until his companions gathered to him. He said: \"Do you know what day this is? This is the day when God says to Adam: 'Arise and send a group to the Fire: from every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.'\" That weighed heavily on the Muslims. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Be moderate, draw near, and rejoice. By Him in whose hand is my soul, among the people you are only like a black mole on the side of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast. Indeed with you are two of the greatest creations that never were in anything but they increased it: Gog and Magog, and those who perished among the disbelieving jinn and humans.\""],[3127,"Regarding His saying \"He frowned and turned away\": Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was speaking with Ubayy b. Khalaf, and he turned away from him. So God revealed \"He frowned and turned away.\" He said: After that the Prophet ﷺ would honor him. Qatadah said: Anas b. Malik informed me, saying: \"I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah wearing a coat of mail and holding a black banner—meaning Ibn Umm Maktum.\""],[3128,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was more bashful than a virgin in her seclusion, and when he disliked something it was recognized in his face."],[3129,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ passed along one of the roads of Madinah, the scent of musk was found from him. They would say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed along this road today.\""],[3130,"The Prophet of God ﷺ came upon Anjashah while he was driving his wives, and said: \"O Anjashah, gently, do not break the glass vessels.\""],[3131,"The Prophet ﷺ punished for wine with sandals and palm branches, and Abu Bakr lashed with his hand. When it was the time of Umar and people had drawn near to villages and rural areas, he mentioned that to his companions. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said: \"Make it like the lightest of the prescribed punishments.\" He said: So he lashed eighty."],[3132,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to begin the recitation with \"Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.\""],[3133,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went around to his wives with a single bath."],[3134,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[3135,"The Prophet of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to begin the recitation in their prayer with \"Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.\""],[3136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and married her, making her manumission her dower."],[3137,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met the enemy, he would say: O Allah, You are my support and my helper, and with You I fight."],[3138,"The people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they pressed him with questioning. He said: You will not ask me about anything except that I will clarify it. A man who, when he quarreled, was called by other than his father stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Then Umar b. al-Khattab stood up and said: We are content with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Messenger. We seek refuge with Allah from the evil of trials. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: I have never seen in good and evil like today; Paradise and Hell were shown to me."],[3139,"Ubayd Allah narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar, but he did not say in Hisham's hadith: if Allah wills."],[3140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned, black-and-white rams, slaughtering them with his own hand. It is as if I am looking at their sides, his foot upon them, pronouncing the name of Allah and remembering Him."],[3141,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the perfection of prayer."],[3142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah twice. He said: I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah carrying a black banner."],[3143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Uhud and said: Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."],[3144,"It will be cast into the Fire, and it will say: Is there any more? until the Blessed and Exalted places His foot in it—or he said: His step—then it will say: Enough, enough."],[3145,"The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3146,"Three qualities, whoever has them will find the sweetness of faith: that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else; and that being thrown into the Fire is more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it."],[3147,"If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would seek a second; and if he had a second, he would seek a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah relents to whoever repents. He said: I do not know whether it was something Allah sent down or he used to say it."],[3148,"I enter the prayer intending to lengthen it, but I hear the cry of a child, so I shorten my prayer because I know how distressed his mother is by that."],[3149,"I asked Anas about nabidh. He said: I did not hear anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ about it."],[3150,"I and the Hour were sent like these two – with his two fingers: the index and the middle."],[3151,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3152,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam to wear silk because of an itch they had."],[3153,"A Jew passed by a young girl wearing jewelry; he snatched her jewelry and threw her into a well. She was found and brought out while still breathing. It was said: Who killed you? She said: So-and-so the Jew. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he executed him."],[3154,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the sahur."],[3155,"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, none of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself of good."],[3156,"There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah that had a short gait. The Prophet of God ﷺ returned and said: We found it to be a sea among seas. He said: After that it could not be outrun."],[3157,"A Jew passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was with his companions – or he said: and his companions were with him – and he greeted him. He said: Do you know what he said? They said: No. He said: Bring him back to me. He said: Did you say, 'Poison be upon you'? He said: Yes. He ﷺ said: When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you."],[3158,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to write to the non-Arabs, it was said to him: They will not accept a letter unless it has a seal. He said: So he adopted a seal and engraved on it: Muhammad, Messenger of God."],[3159,"A Jew killed a girl over some silver ornaments, so the Messenger of God executed him."],[3160,"Concerning spitting in the mosque: the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It is a sin, and its expiation is burying it.”"],[3161,"“Complete the bowing and prostrating, for by God I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate.” Then Qatadah said, “God shows him of that what you do not see.”"],[3162,"I heard Qatadah say: I heard Anas b. Malik report from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it, except that he did not say, “God shows him.”"],[3163,"“I enter the prayer intending to lengthen it, then I hear the crying of a child, so I shorten my prayer because I know the intensity of his mother’s distress from his crying.”"],[3164,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was approached by Riʿl, Dhakwan, ʿUsayyah, and Banu Lihyan, who claimed they had become Muslims and sought his help against their people. So the Messenger of God ﷺ reinforced them with seventy of the Ansar. Anas said, “In their time we used to call them the reciters: they would strive in battle by day and pray at night.” They set off with them until they reached the well of Maʿunah, where they betrayed them and killed them. So the Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for a month in the dawn prayer, supplicating against these tribes: Riʿl, Dhakwan, ʿUsayyah, and Banu Lihyan."],[3165,"“What is the matter with people who raise their eyes toward the sky during their prayer?” His words about that became severe until he said, “They must stop that, or their eyes will be snatched away.”"],[3166,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."],[3167,"The Prophet of God ﷺ and Zayd b. Thabit had the pre-dawn meal. When he finished his suhur—meaning, I said to him, “How much time was there between that and his entering into his prayer?” He said, “As long as it takes a man to recite fifty verses.”"],[3168,"“Complete the front row; if there is any deficiency, let it be in the back.”"],[3169,"Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet of God ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. The Prophet of God ﷺ said, “If that happens to her in her dream, let her perform ghusl.” Umm Sulaym said, “I felt shy about that, so I said, ‘Can that happen?’ The Prophet of God ﷺ said, ‘Yes. And from where does resemblance come? The man’s fluid is thick and white, and the woman’s fluid is yellow and thin. Whichever of them prevails or comes first, resemblance comes from it.’”"],[3170,"He forbade a man to drink standing. Qatadah said: We said, “And eating?” He said, “That is worse, or more vile.”"],[3171,"He used to sacrifice two salt-and-white, horned rams, placing his foot on their sides and slaughtering them with his own hand, saying, “In the name of God, and God is most great.”"],[3172,"The Prophet of God ﷺ came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: \"Ride it.\" The man said: \"It is a sacrificial camel.\" He said: \"Ride it, woe to you.\""],[3173,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was among the lightest of people in prayer while still complete."],[3174,"When one of you is in his prayer, let him not spit in front of him, nor before his face, for he is conversing with his Lord. Rather, to his left, or under his left foot."],[3175,"A group from ʿUkal and ʿUrayna came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, we were people of livestock, not people of cultivated land.\" They found Madinah unhealthy, so he ordered for them some camels and a shepherd to go out with them, and they drank from their urine and milk. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of God ﷺ, drove off the camels, and disbelieved after their Islam. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent after them, and they were brought. He cut off their hands and feet, gouged out their eyes, and left them in the lava field until they died."],[3176,"The Prophet of God ﷺ climbed Uhud, followed by Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman. It trembled with them, so he said: \"Be still, for upon you are a Prophet, a Siddiq, and two martyrs.\""],[3177,"He was at al-Zawra, and a vessel was brought containing water that did not cover his fingers—or he said: that did not conceal his fingers. He ordered his companions to perform ablution, and he placed his palm in the water. We saw water springing from between his fingers until the people performed ablution. We said to Anas: \"How many were you that day?\" He said: \"Three hundred, or about three hundred.\""],[3178,"The Prophet of God ﷺ freed Safiyya bt. Huyayy and made her emancipation her dower."],[3179,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered a people, he loved to stay in their open space for three days."],[3180,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to go around to his wives in one night."],[3181,"He used to go around to his wives in a single hour of the night or day, and they were eleven. He said: I said to Anas b. Malik: \"Was he able to do that?\" He said: \"We used to say that he was given the strength of forty.\""],[3182,"Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."],[3183,"Among the signs of the Hour are: knowledge is lifted, ignorance appears, fornication spreads, wine is drunk, men decrease and women remain, until there is one guardian for fifty women."],[3184,"The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Indeed, the People of the Book greet us, so how should we respond to them?\" He said: \"Say: 'And upon you.'\""],[3185,"When the servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him an arm's length. And when he draws near an arm's length, I draw near to him a fathom. And when he comes to Me walking, I come to him at speed."],[3186,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would wish for or seek a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents."],[3187,"None of you believes until he loves for his brother and his neighbor what he loves for himself."],[3188,"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, a servant does not believe until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[3189,"On the night he was taken on the Night Journey, the Prophet ﷺ was brought al-Buraq, saddled and bridled. It became difficult for him, so Jibril said to it: \"Do you do this to Muhammad? No one has ridden you who is more honored by Allah than him.\" He said: \"Then al-Buraq broke out in sweat.\""],[3190,"Regarding the words of Allah: \"At the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary,\" he said: Anas b. Malik informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary was raised for me in the seventh heaven. Its fruits were like the jars of Hajar, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants. From its trunk gushed two visible rivers and two hidden rivers. I said: 'O Jibril, what is this?' He said: 'As for the two hidden rivers, they are in Paradise. As for the two visible ones, they are the Nile and the Euphrates.'\""],[3191,"Regarding His words: \"Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar,\" the Prophet ﷺ said: \"I saw al-Kawthar, a river in Paradise, its banks were domes of pearl. I said: 'What is this, O Jibril?' He said: 'This is al-Kawthar which Allah has given you.'\""],[3192,"The people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a sign, and the moon split in Makkah twice. Then he said: \"The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has split. And if they see a sign, they turn away and say: 'Passing magic.'\" He says: \"Fleeting.\""],[3193,"Indeed, part of the completeness of prayer is establishing the row."],[3194,"Complete the bowing and the prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind my back when you bow or prostrate."],[3195,"Let none of you spit in his prayer in front of him or to his right, for he is conversing with his Lord."],[3196,"What is the matter with people who raise their eyes toward the sky during their prayer? His wording about that became stern until he said: They must stop doing that, or their eyesight will surely be snatched away."],[3197,"When one of you sleeps through a prayer or misses it because of sleep, let him pray it when he remembers it. God said: “And establish prayer for My remembrance.”"],[3198,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a vessel containing water enough to cover his fingers or not cover them — Saʿīd was unsure — and they began to perform ablution, and the water began to gush from between his fingers. He said: We said to Anas, “How many were you?” He said, “Three hundred.”"],[3199,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said, “Ride it.” He said, “It is a sacrificial camel.” He said, “Ride it, woe to you.”"],[3200,"He forbade drinking while standing. He said: He was asked about eating while standing. Khālid said: I do not know who was asked. He said: That is worse, or he said: That is more abominable."],[3201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ climbed Uhud, accompanied by Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān, and the mountain trembled with them. In Yazīd’s narration: He stamped with his foot and said, “Be still, Uhud, for upon you are a prophet, a ṣiddīq, and two martyrs.”"],[3202,"In it will be seen pitchers of gold and silver, as numerous as the stars of the sky."],[3203,"Anas informed them concerning those who had collected the Qurʾān during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ: they were Ubayy b. Kaʿb, Muʿādh b. Jabal, Zayd, and Abū Zayd. He said: All of them were from the Anṣār."],[3204,"They used to lay on their sides and sleep; some of them would perform ablution and some would not."],[3205,"My mother said, “O Prophet of God, your servant, so supplicate to God for him.” He said, “O God, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him in what You have given him.”"],[3206,"The Messenger of God ﷺ liked gourds, and one day I saw him eating food in which there was gourd, so I began bringing it close to him."],[3207,"“Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory” — he said: al-Ḥudaybiyah."],[3208,"He used to go around to his wives in a single hour of the night and day, and they were eleven. I said to Anas, 'Was he able to do that?' He said, 'We used to say that he was given the strength of thirty.'"],[3209,"This verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ on his return from al-Hudaybiyyah. It was revealed while his companions were overcome with grief, and they were prevented from completing their rites, so they slaughtered the sacrificial animals at al-Hudaybiyyah. When this verse was revealed, he said to his companions, 'A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the entire world.' When the Prophet of God ﷺ recited it, a man from the people said, 'Congratulations, O Prophet of God! God has made clear what He will do with you, but what will He do with us?' Then God revealed after it: 'That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow' – the verse."],[3210,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf married a woman for the weight of a date stone of gold."],[3211,"There are people who will come out of the Fire after being scorched by it, and they will enter Paradise; they will be called the Jahannamiyyun."],[3212,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gathered the Ansar and said, 'Are there any among you who are not of you?' They said, 'No, except a son of our sister.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The son of a people's sister is one of themselves' or he said, 'of the people.'"],[3213,"The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted confidants. The people will increase while they decrease, so accept from their good-doers and pardon their wrong-doers."],[3214,"There is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirin."],[3215,"There is no contagion and no evil omen, but I am pleased by good omens. I said, 'What is a good omen?' He said, 'A good word.'"],[3216,"There is no contagion and no evil omen."],[3217,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the perfection of prayer."],[3218,"Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the perfection of prayer."],[3219,"They said, 'O Messenger of God, when the People of the Book greet us, how should we respond to them?' He said, 'Say: And upon you.'"],[3220,"Do not practice uninterrupted fasting. They said, \"But you practice uninterrupted fasting.\" He said, \"You are not like me in that. I remain — or he said: I pass the night — being fed and given drink.\""],[3221,"Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."],[3222,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said, \"Woe to you — or: May you be ruined — ride it.\""],[3223,"Ride it."],[3224,"A man who had drunk wine was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered that he be struck with two sandals forty times. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Abu Bakr, and he did the same to him. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Umar, and he consulted the people about it. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said, \"The minimum of the prescribed punishments is eighty,\" so Umar struck him eighty."],[3225,"When one of you is in prayer, he is conversing privately with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but let him spit to his left under his left foot."],[3226,"When one of you is in prayer, he is only conversing privately with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but to his left under his foot."],[3227,"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, its expiation is burying it."],[3228,"There was an alarm in Madinah, and the Prophet ﷺ borrowed a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub. He said: He mounted it, and when he returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We saw no cause for alarm, and indeed we found it to be a sea."],[3229,"There is no servant who has good with Allah and wishes to return to this world, except the martyr, for he wishes to return and be killed ten times because of the excellence of the honour he sees."],[3230,"A silk garment was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they began to touch it and marvel at its softness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The handkerchiefs of Sa'd b. Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this — or: softer than this.\""],[3232,"Let none of you wish for death because of harm that has befallen him. If he must do something, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and cause me to die when death is better for me."],[3233,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the lightest of people in prayer while it was complete."],[3234,"When it was the day of the conquest and Quraysh came in the morning, the Ansar said: By Allah, this is indeed astonishing; our swords are dripping with the blood of Quraysh, while our spoils are being divided among them. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent specifically for the Ansar and said: What is this that has reached me about you? He said: And they would not lie. They said: It is what reached you. He said: Are you not pleased that the people go away with the spoils while you return with the Messenger of Allah to your homes? And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If the people were to travel through a valley — or he said: a mountain pass — I would travel through the mountain pass of the Ansar."],[3235,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gathered the Ansar and said: \"Is there anyone among you who is not of you?\" They said: \"No, except a nephew of ours.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The nephew of a people is one of them.\" He said: \"Quraysh are newly out of Jahiliyyah and a calamity, and I wanted to mend them and win their hearts. Are you not pleased that the people return with the worldly goods while you return with the Messenger of God to your homes? If the people were to take a valley and the Ansar a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar.\""],[3236,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed qunut for a month after the ruku', supplicating against certain Arab tribes; then he abandoned it."],[3237,"I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."],[3238,"Every prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated for his community, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection."],[3239,"He said concerning Madinah: The Dajjal will come to it and find the angels guarding it, so the Dajjal will not enter it."],[3240,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him."],[3241,"Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, that he heard Anas b. Malik, from Ubadah, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of the hadith of Hajjaj."],[3242,"Indeed the dream of a Muslim is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[3243,"O Messenger of Allah, Anas is your servant; supplicate to Allah for him. So he said: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him in what You have given him. Anas said."],[3244,"I heard Hisham b. Zayd narrating from Anas b. Malik, the like of that."],[3245,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sleep, then pray without performing ablution."],[3246,"I asked Anas about nabidh from earthenware jars, and he said: I have not heard anything about it from the Prophet ﷺ, but Anas used to dislike it."],[3247,"There was an alarm in Madinah, and the Prophet ﷺ borrowed a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub. He said: He mounted it, and when he returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We saw no cause for alarm, and indeed we found it to be a sea."],[3248,"The Prophet ﷺ used to like gourd, or squash. He said: I saw him one day eating it. He said: So I began placing it before him."],[3249,"Meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: What is this? They said: It is something given in charity to Barīrah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."],[3250,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, behind Abu Bakr, behind Umar, and behind Uthman, and they did not begin the recitation with 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.'"],[3251,"When 'Those who disbelieve' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ubayy b. Kaʿb: Allah has commanded me to recite to you: 'Those who disbelieve.' He said: Did He name me to you? He said: Yes. He said: So he wept."],[3252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams that were black and white, pronouncing the name of Allah and saying Allahu akbar, and I saw him placing his foot on their sides."],[3253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams that were black and white, and I saw him slaughtering them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides."],[3254,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted - or: permission was given - to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf and al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām to wear silk because of an itching they had."],[3255,"Permission was given to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf and al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām for silk shirts."],[3256,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf and al-Zubayr complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about lice, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted them to wear silk shirts. Anas said: I saw silk shirts on both of them."],[3257,"When this verse was revealed: 'Indeed, We have given you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you what has preceded of your sin and what will follow,' the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Congratulations and joy to you, O Messenger of Allah, but what about us? He said: Then this verse was revealed: 'That He may admit the believing men and believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow.'"],[3258,"'Indeed, We have given you a clear victory' was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he returned from al-Ḥudaybiyyah."],[3259,"The moon split twice."],[3260,"Four persons collected the Qur’an during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, all of them from the Ansar: Mu‘adh b. Jabal, Ubayy b. Ka‘b, Zayd b. Thabit, and Abu Zayd. Qatadah said: I said to Anas: Who is Abu Zayd? He said: One of my paternal uncles."],[3261,"There are three qualities, whoever has them will find the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything else; that being thrown into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it; and that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah."],[3262,"None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."],[3263,"None of you believes until I am dearer to him than his child, his father, and all people."],[3264,"None of you finds the sweetness of faith until Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything else, and until he loves a man only for the sake of Allah, and being thrown into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it."],[3265,"There is no servant who has good with Allah and wishes to return to this world, except the martyr, for he wishes to return and be killed ten times because of the excellence of the honour he sees."],[3266,"Do not sever relations, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers as Allah has commanded you."],[3267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the lightest of people in prayer while it was complete."],[3268,"I and the Hour have been sent like these two, as one of them surpassed the other."],[3269,"I and the Hour have been sent like these two."],[3270,"There is no prophet except that he warned his nation about the one-eyed liar. Indeed he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is kafir, which every believer will read."],[3271,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would wish for—or: seek—a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in forgiveness to whoever repents."],[3272,"If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would seek a second one, and if he had a second, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in forgiveness to whoever repents."],[3273,"The son of Adam grows old, but two things remain with him: greed and hope."],[3274,"When My servant draws near to Me a hand span, I draw near to him an arm's length; when he draws near an arm's length, I draw near him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him rushing."],[3275,"If My servant draws near to Me a hand span, I draw near to him an arm's length; if he draws near to Me an arm's length, I draw near to him a fathom; and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him rushing."],[3276,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote to the Romans, and it was said to him: They will not accept a letter unless it is sealed. So he took a ring of silver, and it is as if I am looking at its whiteness on his hand, with the inscription: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."],[3277,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to write to the Romans, it was said to him: They will not read a letter unless it is sealed. So he took a ring of silver, with the inscription: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. Anas said: It is as if I am looking at its whiteness on his hand."],[3278,"He will come out of the Fire—Shu'bah said: Bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and had in his heart good weighing a grain of wheat. Bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and had in his heart good weighing a speck. And Shu'bah said: a speck. And he will come out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, and had in his heart good weighing a grain of barley."],[3279,"He used to frequently supplicate with this supplication: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[3280,"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."],[3281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking on a road, and a black woman passed by. A man said to her: Make way! She said: Make way? Mind yourself! The Prophet ﷺ said: Leave her, for she is arrogant."],[3282,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour occur? After the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: Where is the one asking about the Hour? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It is indeed coming. What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it much in the way of deeds, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You will be with those you love. He said: And there was with him a young boy from the Ansar called Muhammad, and he said: If this boy lives, he will not reach old age before the Hour occurs."],[3283,"A man said: O Messenger of God, a man loves a people but has not done their deeds. He said: A person is with the one he loves. Hammad said: And he said in the hadith: The Muslims did not rejoice over anything after Islam as much as they rejoiced over this."],[3284,"Three things, whoever possesses them finds the sweetness of faith: that God and His Messenger be more beloved to him than that he should return to being a Jew or a Christian."],[3285,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: A man loves a people for the good deeds they do, but he has not done the like of it. The Prophet ﷺ said: A person is with the one he loves, or: with the one whom he loves. He said: The companions of the Prophet ﷺ rejoiced over that with a joy the like of which I did not see them rejoice over anything."],[3286,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I love God and His Messenger. He said: Then you will be with the one you love. Anas said: And I love God and His Messenger."],[3287,"The Messenger of God ﷺ practiced continuous fasting in Ramadan, so some of his companions practiced continuous fasting. He said: If the month were extended for me, I would continue fasting such a continuous fast that would make those who go to extremes give up their extremism. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."],[3288,"I took Abdullah b. Abi Talha to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God took him while he was wearing an aba and was applying tar to a camel of his. He said: Do you have any dates? I said: Yes. I handed him some dates, and he put them in his mouth and chewed them. Then he opened the mouth of the infant and put them into his mouth. The infant began to suck on them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The Ansar love dates. And he named him Abdullah."],[3289,"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community."],[3290,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot impersonate me. And the dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[3291,"The likeness of a believer is that of a stalk of grain: sometimes it bends and sometimes it stands upright."],[3292,"The people of Yemen came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Send with us a man to teach us. He said: So he took the hand of Abu Ubayda and sent him with them, and said: This is the trustworthy one of this community."],[3293,"A son was born to me tonight, and I named him after my father Ibrahim. Then I handed him over to Umm Sayf, the wife of a blacksmith in Madinah. In the hadith of Shayban: He set out to visit him. In the hadith of Hudba: The Messenger of God ﷺ set out to visit him, and I followed him. We came to Abu Sayf while he was blowing into his bellows, and the house was filled with smoke. I hurried ahead of the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Abu Sayf, the Messenger of God has come. So he stopped. The Messenger of God ﷺ called for the child, embraced him, and said whatever God willed that he should say. He said: I saw him after that as he was breathing his last in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ. In the hadith of Hudba: The eye of the Messenger of God shed tears. In the hadith of Shayban: The eyes of the Messenger of God shed tears. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The eye weeps and the heart grieves, but we do not say anything except what pleases our Lord. In the hadith of Shayban: By God, O Ibrahim, we are indeed grieved by you. In the hadith of Hudba: And we are indeed grieved by you, O Ibrahim."],[3294,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased by dreams. Perhaps a man would see a dream and he would ask about him if he did not know him, and if he was praised as good, he was more pleased with his dream. A woman came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I saw as though I was taken and brought out of Madinah and admitted into Paradise. I heard a crash that made Paradise tremble. I looked and saw so-and-so son of so-and-so, and so-and-so son of so-and-so. She named twelve men, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had sent a detachment of that number. They were brought wearing dark garments, their jugular veins gushing blood. It was said: Take them to the river of Baydhaj, or: al-Bayrah. He said: They were plunged into it and came out with faces like the moon on the night of the full moon. They were brought a platter of gold containing unripe dates, and they ate of its unripe dates as much as they wished. They did not turn it from any side except that they ate of the fruit they desired, and I ate with them. Then the bearer of good news came from that detachment and said: Our situation was such-and-such, and so-and-so and so-and-so were killed, until he counted twelve men. The Messenger of God ﷺ summoned the woman and said: Recount your dream. So she recounted it, and she began to say: So-and-so was brought, and so-and-so was brought, just as he had said."],[3295,"I was given al-Kawthar, so I struck my hand into its soil, and it was pungent musk, its pebbles were pearls, and its two banks were domes of pearl."],[3296,"Stand straight—twice or thrice—for by the One in whose hand is my soul, I surely see you from behind me just as I see you from in front of me. Humayd added in the hadith: Stand straight and press close together."],[3297,"Two men will come out of the Fire, then they will be presented to Allah, and He will direct them toward the Fire—then he mentioned something like the hadith of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān—then they will be admitted into Paradise."],[3298,"A young man from Aslam said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to go on jihad but I have nothing with which to equip myself. He said: Go to so-and-so the Anṣārī, for he had already equipped himself, and say to him: The Messenger of Allah sends you greetings of peace and says to you: Hand over to me what you have equipped yourself with. So he went to him, and the man said—I think to his wife—Do not hide any of it from him, for by Allah, if you do not hide any of it from him, we will be blessed in it."],[3299,"He would hear the crying of a child while he was in prayer, and he would recite a short surah and a light surah."],[3300,"He would go on military campaigns with Umm Sulaym, and with her were women from the Anṣār who would give water and treat the wounded."],[3301,"On the day the Prophet ﷺ entered Madinah, everything in it was illuminated, and on the day the Prophet ﷺ died, everything in it became dark. We had not yet removed our hands from the Prophet ﷺ—we were still burying him—before we even began to disapprove of our own hearts."],[3302,"A righteous trait may be in a man and through it Allah sets right all of his deeds, and a man's purification for his prayer: by his purification Allah expiates his sins, and his prayer remains for him as a supererogatory act."],[3303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Abū Dharr and said: O Abū Dharr, shall I not direct you to two traits that are lighter on the back and heavier in the balance than others? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You must have good character and prolonged silence, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, creation has not adorned themselves with the like of these two."],[3304,"I left the Prophet ﷺ heading to my family, and I passed by some boys, and their play pleased me, so I stood over the boys, and the Prophet ﷺ came to me while I was standing over them, and he greeted the boys, then he sent me on an errand of his. I returned to my mother after the time I usually returned to them, and my mother said to me: What kept you today, my son? I said: The Prophet ﷺ sent me on an errand. She said: What errand? I said: Mother, it is a secret. She said: My son, guard the secret of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. Thābit said: I said to Anas: O Abū Ḥamza, do you remember that errand today—or: do you recall it? He said: I surely remember it, and if I were to tell it to anyone, I would tell it to you, O Thābit."],[3305,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to go out at night with water skins, giving water to the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3306,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of Uhud, while wiping the blood from his face: \"How can a people prosper who wounded their Prophet and broke his front tooth, while he was calling them to God?\" Then God revealed: \"You have no part in the matter, whether He turns to them in mercy or punishes them, for they are indeed wrongdoers.\""],[3307,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he gave him a flock between two mountains. The man went to his people and said: \"O my people, embrace Islam, for by God, Muhammad gives the gift of a man who does not fear poverty.\" Indeed, a man would come to the Prophet ﷺ desiring nothing but worldly gain, and by evening his religion had become dearer to him than the world and all it contains."],[3308,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon a man to visit him and found him at the point of death. He greeted him and said: \"How do you find yourself?\" He said: \"I am well, O Messenger of God. I hope in God, Mighty and Majestic, and I fear my sins.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"They will not combine in the heart of a man at this moment except that God will grant him his hope and secure him from what he fears.\""],[3309,"One day the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ went out and said: \"O Messenger of God, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Kaaba!\" He said: \"And what is that?\" They said: \"Hypocrisy, hypocrisy.\" He said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"That is not hypocrisy.\" Then they returned a second time and said: \"O Messenger of God, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Kaaba!\" He said: \"And what is that?\" They said: \"Hypocrisy, hypocrisy.\" He said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"That is not hypocrisy.\" Then they returned a third time and said: \"O Messenger of God, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Kaaba!\" He said: \"And what is that?\" They said: \"Hypocrisy.\" He said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"That is not hypocrisy.\" They said: \"When we are with you, we are in a certain state, but when we leave you, the world and our families preoccupy us.\" He said: \"If, when you left me, you remained in the state you are in with me, the angels would shake your hands in the streets of Madinah.\""],[3310,"The Prophet ﷺ liked to break his fast with three dates or something not touched by fire."],[3311,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delayed the night prayer one night until the middle of the night, then came out and led them in prayer. And he did not mention ablution."],[3312,"He used to raid at dawn prayer, and would listen for the call to prayer. If he heard it, he would hold back; otherwise he would raid. One day he listened and heard a man saying: \"God is greatest, God is greatest.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Upon the natural disposition.\" Then he said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but God.\" He said: \"You have come out of the Fire.\""],[3313,"We used to pray the sunset prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then we would throw [arrows] and one of us could see where his arrow fell."],[3314,"The night prayer was commenced one night, and a man said: \"O Messenger of God, I have a need.\" He stood with him conversing privately until the people – or some of the people – dozed off, then he stood and prayed. And he did not mention ablution."],[3315,"Hudba narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, with something similar."],[3316,"Some people from Urayna came to the Prophet ﷺ and found Madinah unhealthy. The Prophet ﷺ sent them to the camels of zakat and ordered them to drink from their urine and milk."],[3317,"When he ate food, he would lick his three fingers and said: \"If a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove the dirt from it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan.\" And he ordered us to wipe the dish clean, and said: \"One of you does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies.\""],[3318,"They said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ have a ring? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once delayed the night prayer until half the night had passed — or: nearly half the night had passed — then he came and said: The people have already prayed, and you will continue to be in prayer as long as you wait for the prayer. Anas said: It is as if I can still see the gleam of his silver ring. He said: And Anas raised his left hand to show us."],[3319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went around to all his wives with a single ritual bath."],[3320,"Creation is the dependents of Allah, and the most beloved of them to Allah is the one most beneficial to His dependents."],[3321,"Whoever Allah has promised a reward for a deed, He will fulfill it for him; and whoever He has promised a punishment for a deed, He has the choice concerning it."],[3322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding this verse: He is worthy of reverence and worthy of forgiveness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Your Lord said: I am worthy to be revered, so no other should be associated with Me; and I am worthy, for whoever reveres Me so as not to associate anything with Me, to forgive him."],[3323,"On the day of Uhud he said: O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth."],[3324,"On the day of Uhud, when they pressed upon him while he was among seven of the Ansar and two men of Quraysh, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Who will repel them from us and be my companion in Paradise? A man of the Ansar stood up and fought until he was killed. Then he said the same, and another stood up and fought until he was killed. He kept saying the same until the seven were killed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We have not been fair to our companions."],[3325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Abu Ubaydah and Abu Talhah."],[3326,"When Allah created Adam, Iblis began circling him and looking at him. When he saw that he was hollow, he said: I have triumphed over a creature who cannot control himself."],[3327,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived at Badr, he gestured with his hand to the ground and said: This is the place where so-and-so will fall. By Allah, none of them moved from his place of falling."],[3328,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made peace with Quraysh on the day of Hudaybiyyah, he said to Ali: Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Suhayl b. Amr said: We do not recognize the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful; write: In Your name, O Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali: Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has agreed upon. Suhayl b. Amr said: If we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would have followed you and not denied you; write your lineage from your father. The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: Write: Muhammad b. Abdullah. He wrote: Whoever of you comes to us, we will return him to you; and whoever of us comes to you, we will leave him with you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, will you grant them this? He said: Whoever of us goes to them, may Allah distance him; and whoever of them comes to us and we return him to them, Allah will make for him a way out and an escape."],[3329,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say while digging the trench: We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad to fight as long as we live forever. And the Prophet ﷺ said: O Allah, the true life is the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun."],[3330,"I passed by Musa on the night I was taken on the Night Journey while he was standing praying in his grave at the red sandhill."],[3331,"The Messenger of God ﷺ left the slain of Badr for three days, then he came to them, stood over them, and called them, saying: 'O Abu Jahl b. Hisham, O Umayya b. Khalaf, O ʿUtba b. Rabiʿa, O Shayba b. Rabiʿa, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.' ʿUmar heard the words of the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, how can they hear, and how can they answer when they have become bloated corpses?' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, you are not more able to hear what I say than they are, except that they cannot answer.' Then he ordered concerning them and they were dragged to the well of Badr."],[3332,"I said to Anas: 'Tell me something of these wonders that no one but you narrates.' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed one day the noon prayer in Madinah, then he came to the seats where Jibril used to come to him, and he sat on them. Bilal came and called the afternoon prayer, so those who had families in Madinah got up to perform ablution and attend to their needs. Some men of the Emigrants remained who had no families in Madinah. The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a vessel – meaning a wide shallow bowl with water in it – and he placed his fingers in the vessel, but it did not accommodate all his fingers, so he placed these four. Then he said: \"Come and perform ablution.\" So they all performed ablution. I said to Anas: \"How many do you think they were?\" He said: \"Between seventy and eighty.\""],[3333,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us when there were only I, my mother, and my maternal aunt Umm Haram. He said: 'Get up, let me lead you in prayer,' and that was at a time other than the time of prayer. A man said to Thabit: 'Where did he place Anas?' He said: 'On his right.' He said: 'Then he supplicated for us, the people of the house, for every good of the good of this world and the Hereafter.' My mother said: 'O Messenger of God, your little servant Anas, supplicate to God for him.' So he supplicated for me for every good. The last thing he supplicated for me was: 'O God, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in them.'"],[3334,"The Prophet ﷺ called for water and was brought a wide shallow bowl. He said: 'The people began to perform ablution, and I estimated them between sixty and eighty.' He said: 'I began to look at the water springing from between his fingers.'"],[3335,"I do not recognize anything that I used to recognize in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ except your saying: 'There is no god but God.' He said: 'It was said: The prayer, O Abu Hamza?' He said: 'You have prayed it at sunset. Was that the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ? Besides, I have not seen a time better for a doer of good than this time of yours.'"],[3336,"When this verse was revealed: 'O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet and do not speak loudly to him,' Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas sat in his house and said: 'I am the one who used to raise his voice and speak loudly to him, and I am among the people of the Fire.' The Prophet ﷺ missed him and they informed him. He said: 'Rather, he is among the people of Paradise.' Anas said: 'We used to see him walking among us, and we knew that he was among the people of Paradise. When the day of Yamama came and that rout occurred, he put on his garments, perfumed himself, advanced, and fought until he was killed.'"],[3337,"When Zaynab's waiting period ended, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to Zayd: 'Go to her and mention me to her.' He said: 'Zayd set off and came to her while she was baking her dough.' He said: 'She became magnified in my chest, and I could not look at her once I knew that the Messenger of God ﷺ had mentioned her. So I turned my back to her and stepped backward. I said: \"O Zaynab, rejoice; the Messenger of God ﷺ has mentioned you.\" She said: \"I will do nothing until I consult my Lord.\" She rose to her place of prayer, and the Qur'an was revealed. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her without permission.' Anas said: 'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ feed us bread and meat on her account until the day extended.' He said: 'The people went out and a group remained in the house conversing, and the conversation had made them comfortable. The Messenger of God ﷺ went out and I followed him. He began to go around the rooms of his wives, greeting them, and they began to say: \"How did you find your wife, O Messenger of God?\" I do not know whether I informed him that the people had left or whether he was informed. The Messenger of God ﷺ went on until he entered the house. I went to enter with him, and he let down the curtain between me and him. The verse of the veil was revealed, and the people were admonished with what they were admonished.'"],[3338,"We used to be in awe of asking the Messenger of God ﷺ about anything, and we liked it when a man from the desert came and asked him while we listened. A man from them came to him and said: 'O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed that you claim that God has sent you.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then who created the heaven?' He said: 'God.' He said: 'Then who created the earth?' He said: 'God.' He said: 'Then who set up these mountains?' He said: 'God.' He said: 'Then who placed these springs in them?' He said: 'God.' He said: 'Then by the One who created the heaven and the earth, set up the mountains, and placed these springs in them, did God send you?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that we owe five prayers in our day and night.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did God command you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that we owe charity on our wealth.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did God command you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that we owe fasting a month in our year.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did God command you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Your messenger claimed that we owe pilgrimage to the House for whoever is able to find a way to it.' He said: 'He spoke the truth.' He said: 'Then by the One who sent you, did God command you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add to them or subtract from them anything.' He said: 'When he turned away, he said: \"If he is truthful, he will certainly enter Paradise.\"'"],[3339,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon, and the people rose to him and shouted, saying: 'O Prophet of God, the rain has failed, the trees have turned red, and the livestock have perished. Supplicate God to send us rain.' He said: 'O God, give us rain; O God, give us rain.' He said: 'By God, we did not see in the sky a wisp of cloud.' Then a cloud rose and spread, and then it rained. The Prophet of God ﷺ came down, prayed, and departed. It did not stop raining until the next Friday. When the Prophet ﷺ stood to deliver the sermon, they shouted to him, saying: 'O Prophet of God, the houses have collapsed and the roads have been cut off. Supplicate God to withhold it from us.' He said: 'O God, around us and not upon us.' He said: 'It cleared away from Madinah and began to rain around it, and not a drop fell in Madinah. I looked at Madinah, and it was like a crown.'"],[3340,"A man used to keep reciting 'Say: He is God, the One' in prayer in every unit while leading his companions. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'What makes you keep this surah?' He said: 'I love it.' He said: 'Loving it has admitted you to Paradise.'"],[3341,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, I love \"Say: He is God, the One.\"' He said: 'Your love for it will admit you to Paradise.'"],[3342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: O Allah, indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirin."],[3343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to establish brotherhood between two of his companions. The night would grow long for one of them until he would meet his brother, and he would meet him with affection and kindness. He would say: How have you been since I last saw you? As for the common people, three days would not pass for either of them without knowing his brother's circumstances."],[3344,"The Prophet ﷺ was in the house of Aisha, and some of his companions were waiting for food. He said: She was preceded by - 'Imran said: My strongest belief is that it was Hafsa - with a large dish containing tharid, and she said: I placed it. She said: Then Aisha came out and took the bowl. He said: That was before they were veiled. He said: She struck with it and it broke. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ took it and put it together, and he said with his palm - 'Imran demonstrated: and he put it together - and said: Eat, your mother is jealous. He said: When he finished, he sent the intact dish to Hafsa and sent the broken one to Aisha. Thus it became a ruling: whoever breaks something, it is his, and he owes its equivalent."],[3345,"Take the pre-dawn meal, even if with a gulp of water."],[3346,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from his companions to one of the leaders of the polytheists to call him to Allah. He said: This god to whom you call, is he of silver or of copper? His words weighed heavily on the chest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: Return to him and call him to Allah. He returned, and he said to him the same as his previous words. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said: Return and call him to Allah. Then Allah sent a thunderbolt upon him. He returned, and he said to him the same as his previous words. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said: Return to him and call him to Allah. And the Messenger of Allah was on the road, not knowing. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him that Allah had destroyed his companion. And it was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: 'He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute about Allah.'"],[3347,"Ishaq b. Abi Israel narrated to us, Ibn Abi Sara narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, similarly."],[3348,"There was a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Julaybib, who had an unattractive face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered him marriage. He said: Then you will find me unsaleable. He said: But with Allah you are not unsaleable."],[3349,"Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Daylam b. Ghazwan narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas b. Malik, who said: There was a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Julaybib... and he mentioned something similar."],[3350,"The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, al-Adba, would not be outpaced. A bedouin came with a young camel of his and raced her, and the bedouin outpaced her. This was difficult for the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: It is incumbent upon Allah that nothing is raised in this world except that He lowers it."],[3351,"Bassam b. Yazid narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, similarly."],[3352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit us, and I had a young brother nicknamed Abu Umayr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited us and said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the nughayr?"],[3353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some yellow color on Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and said: What is this? He said: I married a woman for the weight of a date stone of gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: May Allah bless you. Then he said to him: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."],[3354,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hold a wedding feast for any of his wives like the feast he held for Zaynab, for he slaughtered a sheep."],[3355,"A Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and he fell ill. The Prophet ﷺ came to visit him, and his father was at his head. The Prophet ﷺ called him, and the boy began looking at his father. His father said to him, “Obey Abu al-Qasim.” So he said, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.” Then the boy died, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out saying, “Praise be to Allah who saved him through me from the Fire.”"],[3356,"The Prophet ﷺ married Safiyyah and made her manumission her dower."],[3357,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and they praised it with good. He said, “It has become due.” Another funeral procession passed by him, and they spoke ill of it. He said, “It has become due.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, you said for this one, ‘It has become due,’ and for that one, ‘It has become due.’” He said, “Because of the testimony of the people.”"],[3358,"And you are Allah’s witnesses on earth."],[3359,"A Persian man was a neighbor of the Prophet ﷺ, and his broth had the most pleasant smell of anything. He made some food, then invited the Prophet ﷺ, with ʿAʾishah beside him. He said: He gestured to him, “Come.” He said, “And this one with me?” indicating ʿAʾishah. He said, “No.” Then he gestured to him a second time, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “And this one with me?” He said, “No.” Then he said a third time, and the Prophet ﷺ said, indicating ʿAʾishah, “Yes.”"],[3360,"ʿUbayd Allah b. Ziyad said, “O Abu Hamzah, have you heard the Prophet ﷺ mention the Pool?” He said, “I left behind in Madinah old women who frequently ask Allah to bring them to the Pool of Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[3361,"The Prophet ﷺ established a pact of brotherhood between the Ansar and the Muhajirun in the house of Anas in Madinah."],[3362,"And Murrah narrated it to us from ʿAsim, from Anas."],[3363,"There remains in Paradise as long as Allah wills it to remain, then Allah creates for it whatever creation He wills."],[3364,"Two men come out of the Fire—Abu ʿImran said four, and Thabit said two men—and they are presented to their Lord. He orders them to the Fire, and one of them turns around and says, “O Lord, I had hoped that if You brought me out of it, You would not return me to it.” So Allah saves him from it."],[3365,"I never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was more concise than the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while being complete. His prayer was moderate, and Abu Bakr’s prayer was moderate. When ʿUmar came, he lengthened the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he stood until we would say, “He has made a mistake,” then he prostrated, and he sat between the two prostrations until we would say, “He has made a mistake.”"],[3366,"I was giving Abu 'Ubaydah, Abu Talhah, Ubayy b. Ka'b, Simak b. Kharashah, and Suhayl b. Bayda' a drink of mixed dried dates and unripe dates until it took effect on them. Then a man passed by calling out: 'Indeed wine has been forbidden.' He said: So they said: 'O Anas, tip over your vessel.' By Allah, they did not wait to find out whether he was truthful or lying. By Allah, it never returned to their heads until they met Allah."],[3367,"I was the cupbearer of the people on the day it was forbidden in the house of Abu Talhah, and their drink was nothing but fadikh: unripe dates and dried dates. Then a caller called out: 'Indeed wine has been forbidden.' He said: So it flowed in the streets of Madinah. Abu Talhah said: 'Go out and pour it out.' He said: So I poured it out. Then they said - or some of them said: 'So-and-so was killed and so-and-so was killed while it was in their bellies' - and I do not know whether this is from the hadith of Anas. He said: Then Allah revealed: 'There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten' - the verse."],[3368,"Indeed I do not fail to pray with you as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying with us. Thabit said: I saw Anas do something that I do not see you do. When he raised his head from bowing, he stood until someone would say: 'He has forgotten.' And when he raised his head from the first prostration, he stood until someone would say: 'He has forgotten.'"],[3369,"Anas was asked about the Messenger of Allah's dyeing. He said: 'If I wished to count white hairs in his head, I could do so.' And he said: 'He did not dye.' Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam, and 'Umar dyed with henna."],[3370,"Whoever recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One' two hundred times in a day, one thousand five hundred good deeds are written for him, unless he has a debt."],[3371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand. I passed by some boys and sat with them, so I was late in returning to him. He came out and saw me with the boys, and he greeted them with salam."],[3372,"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years, and he never said 'Uff' to me, nor did he say about anything a servant did: 'Why did you do such and such?' or 'Why didn't you do such and such?'"],[3373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: 'O so-and-so, did you do such and such?' He said: 'No, by Allah besides whom there is no god, I did not do it,' while the Messenger of Allah knew that he had done it. He said to him: 'Allah has expiated your lie by your affirmation of there is no god but Allah.'"],[3374,"They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you we are in one state, but when we leave you we are in another.' He said: 'How are you and your Prophet?' They said: 'You are our Prophet in secret and in public.' He said: 'That is not hypocrisy.'"],[3375,"Creation is the dependents of Allah, and the most beloved of them to Allah is the one most beneficial to His dependents."],[3376,"He used to supplicate with these supplications when he entered morning and when he entered evening: 'O Allah, I ask You for sudden good, and I seek refuge in You from sudden evil, for the servant does not know what will suddenly come to him when he enters morning and when he enters evening.'"],[3377,"Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely will be given it, even if he is not struck by it."],[3378,"Joseph was given half of all beauty."],[3379,"Gabriel came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was playing with the boys. He took him, threw him down, split open his heart, and extracted from it a clot of blood, saying: “This is Satan’s share in you.” Then he washed it in a golden basin with Zamzam water, then stitched it up, and then returned it to its place. The boys came running to his mother—meaning his wet nurse—and said: “Muhammad has been killed!” She met him while his color had drained. Anas said: “I used to see the trace of that stitching on his chest.”"],[3380,"I was brought al-Buraq, an animal white and long, larger than a donkey but smaller than a mule, which placed its hoof at the limit of its gaze. He said: I mounted it until I came to Jerusalem. He said: I tied it to the ring where the prophets tie it. Then I entered the mosque and prayed two rak‘ahs in it, then I left."],[3381,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ heard the crying of a child with its mother during prayer, he would recite a short surah—or a brief one."],[3382,"He used to lick his three fingers after eating, and he said: “If a morsel of one of you falls down, let him remove whatever harm is on it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan. And let him wipe the plate, for you do not know in which of your foods the blessing lies.”"],[3383,"On the day the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah, everything in it lit up. On the day the Messenger of God ﷺ died, everything in it darkened. He said: We had not finished shaking the dust of the grave of the Messenger of God ﷺ from our hands before we found our hearts altered."],[3384,"Fatimah said to me: “O Anas, how could you find it in yourselves to heap dust upon the Messenger of God ﷺ?”"],[3385,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ became gravely ill, he began stretching out one leg and drawing in the other, stretching out one hand and drawing in the other. Fatimah said: “O my grief, for your suffering, O father!”—al-Qawariri said: Hammad said: “Preserve it: he said ‘O my grief,’ and he did not say ‘O my grief, for your suffering, O father.’” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O my little daughter, there is no grief upon your father after this day.” When he passed away, Fatimah said: “O father, he answered a Lord who called him! O father, to Gabriel we announce his death! O father, how near he is to his Lord! O father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode.” Anas said: When we buried him, Fatimah said to me: “O Anas, how could you find it in yourselves to heap dust upon the Messenger of God ﷺ?”"],[3386,"When it was revealed: “O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet” up to His saying: “while you do not perceive,” Thabit b. Qays said: “By God, I am the one who used to raise his voice in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I fear that I may be among the people of the Fire. I used to raise my voice in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Rather, he is among the people of the Garden,” or something similar."],[3387,"For every treacherous one there will be a banner."],[3388,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave Ali and Fatimah a servant boy and said: “Treat him well, for I saw him praying.”"],[3389,"He used to deliver the sermon standing by the trunk of a palm tree. When he had the pulpit built and delivered the sermon from it, the trunk yearned. The Prophet ﷺ came to it and embraced it. He said: “Had I not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[3390,"The Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salama for goods worth ten dirhams."],[3391,"You name them Muhammad, then you curse them."],[3392,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to go out to the mosque, and in it were the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār, none of them lifting his head from his huddled posture except Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. He would smile at them, and they would smile at him."],[3393,"I hope to meet the Messenger of God ﷺ on the Day of Resurrection and say: 'O Messenger of God, your little servant.'"],[3394,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ during his illness in which he died, and he said to me: 'Convey peace to your people, and tell them that they are—as far as I know—chaste and patient.'"],[3395,"\"When will I meet my brothers?\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, are we not your brothers?\" He said: \"Rather, you are my companions. My brothers are those who believed in me and did not see me.\""],[3396,"\"Ṭūbā for one who saw me and believed in me, once, and ṭūbā for one who did not see me and believed in me, seven times.\""],[3397,"To sit with people who remember God after the dawn prayer until the sun rises is dearer to me than freeing four descendants of Ishmael, the blood money of each man being twelve thousand. And to sit with people who remember God after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is dearer to me than freeing four descendants of Ishmael, the blood money of each man being twelve thousand."],[3398,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah, the people looked up at him, and he lowered his head over his saddle in humility."],[3399,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah, the people of Makkah stood in two rows. ʿAbd Allāh b. Rawāḥa said:'Make way, sons of the disbelievers, from his path.Today we strike you upon his revelation,a striking that removes heads from their resting placeand makes the dear friend forget his dear friend.O Lord, I believe in his word.'ʿUmar said: \"O Ibn Rawāḥa, do you recite poetry before the Messenger of God and within God's sanctuary?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Enough, O ʿUmar, this is harder on them than the falling of arrows.\""],[3400,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say on the day of the Trench:\"O God, were it not for You, we would not be guided,nor fast, nor pray.So send down tranquility upon us.\""],[3401,"The sister of al-Rubayyiʿ, Umm Ḥāritha, wounded a person. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Retaliation, retaliation.\" The mother of al-Rubayyiʿ said: \"O Messenger of God, is retaliation taken from so-and-so? No, by God, retaliation will never be taken from her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Glory be to God, O Umm al-Rubayyiʿ, retaliation is God's decree.\" She said: \"No, by God, retaliation will never be taken from her.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Among God's servants are those who, if they swear by God, He would fulfill their oath.\""],[3402,"They said to Anas, 'Supplicate for us.' He said, 'O Allah, give us good in this world, and good in the hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.' They said, 'Add more for us,' so he repeated it. They said, 'Add more for us.' He said, 'What do you want? I asked for you the good of this world and the hereafter.' Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate frequently: 'O Allah, give us good in this world, and good in the hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.'"],[3403,"Abu Talha had a son who was given the kunya Abu Umayr. He said: The Prophet ﷺ used to say, 'Abu Umayr, what happened to the little bird?' He said: The child died while Abu Talha was away in one of his gardens. Umm Sulaym got up, washed him, shrouded him, and covered him with a cloth. She said, 'No one is to inform Abu Talha until I am the one who tells him.' Abu Talha came back tired while he was fasting. She adorned herself and beautified herself for him, and brought his dinner. He said, 'What happened to Abu Umayr?' She said, 'He has settled down.' So he ate dinner and had intercourse with her as a man does with his wife. Then she said, 'O Abu Talha, what do you think about a household that lent something to another household, and its owners asked for it back? Should they return it or keep it?' He said, 'Rather, they should return it to them.' She said, 'Then seek reward for Abu Umayr.' He said: He became angry and went as he was to the Prophet ﷺ and told him about Umm Sulaym's words and actions. He said, 'May Allah bless you both in the remainder of your night.' He said: She became pregnant with Abdullah b. Abu Talha. When she gave birth to him and it was the seventh day, Umm Sulaym said to me, 'O Anas, take this boy to the Prophet ﷺ, along with this basket containing some pressed dates, so that he may be the one to perform tahnik on him and name him.' The Prophet ﷺ stretched out his legs, laid him in his lap, took a date, chewed it, and put it in the baby's mouth. The baby began to smack his lips. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The Ansar love dates, and nothing will stop them.'"],[3404,"He liked gourd, which is squash."],[3405,"I have never touched with my hand anything softer than the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, not silk nor ambergris — and other things he mentioned which I do not remember — and I have never smelled a fragrance more pleasant than the fragrance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I accompanied him for ten years, and he never said to me about anything, 'Why did you do such-and-such?'"],[3406,"The muezzin — or Bilal — would give the iqama, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would enter, and a man would meet him and stand with him until most of them began to nod their heads."],[3407,"The angel of rain asked his Lord for permission to visit the Prophet ﷺ, and He granted him permission. That was on Umm Salama's day. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Umm Salama, guard the door for us; let no one enter upon us.' He said: While she was at the door, Husayn b. Ali came and burst in, opened the door, and entered. The Prophet ﷺ began to embrace him and kiss him. The angel said, 'Do you love him?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Your community will kill him. If you wish, I will show you the place where they will kill him.' He said, 'Yes.' He said: He took a handful from the place where he would be killed and showed it to him. Then a soft reddish soil came. Umm Salama took it and placed it in her garment."],[3408,"Let one of you ask his Lord for all his needs, even for a sandal strap when it breaks."],[3409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between his companions: he established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda', and between Awf b. Malik and Sa'b b. Jaththama."],[3410,"Treat Allah's blessings well as neighbors; do not drive them away, for rarely do they leave a people and return to them."],[3411,"Those who frequent the houses of Allah are the people of Allah."],[3412,"Labbayk with a Hajj and an Umrah together."],[3413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over the gathering of Banu Salima and said, 'O Banu Salima, what is a raqub among you?' They said, 'One who has no child.' He said, 'Rather, it is one who has no child who died in infancy.' He said, 'What is a mu'dim among you?' They said, 'One who has no wealth.' He said, 'Rather, it is one who comes forward while he has no good with Allah.'"],[3414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the girls of Banū al-Najjār while they were beating the duff and saying: “We are girls from Banū al-Najjār; how wonderful is Muḥammad as a neighbor.” The Prophet of Allah said: “O Allah, bless them.”"],[3415,"On the day of the Trench, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, were it not for You, we would not have been guided, nor fasted, nor prayed. O Allah, send down tranquility upon us.”"],[3416,"Umm Sulaym was with Abū Ṭalḥah on the day of Khaybar, and she had a dagger with her. Abū Ṭalḥah said to her: “Umm Sulaym, what is this?” She said: “A dagger I took up so that if any of the polytheists comes near me, I will rip him open.” Abū Ṭalḥah said: “O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says? She says such-and-such”—something that escaped Abū Ḥarb—“she will kill them.” He said: “Allah has sufficed and been gracious.”"],[3417,"Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī was shooting on the day of Uḥud in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with the Messenger of Allah behind him. Abū Ṭalḥah was an archer, and whenever he shot, the Prophet ﷺ would raise himself to see where his arrow landed."],[3418,"Abū Ṭalḥah recited Sūrat Barāʾah and came upon this verse: “Go forth, light and heavy.” He said: “Do I not see my Lord calling me to go forth, young and old? Equip me.” His sons said to him: “You campaigned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he passed away, and with Abū Bakr until he died, and with ʿUmar, so we will campaign on your behalf.” He said: “Equip me.” So they equipped him, and he sailed the sea and died. They did not find an island to bury him on until after seven days, and he had not changed."],[3419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while ʿAbdullāh b. Salām was in his palm grove. When he heard of him, he came and said: “I will ask you about things that no one knows except a prophet. If you tell me them, then you are the Messenger of Allah.” He asked him about resemblance, about the first thing with which people will be gathered, and about the first thing the people of Paradise will eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gabriel told me them just now.” He said: “That is the enemy of the Jews.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for resemblance, if the man’s fluid precedes the woman’s fluid, the child resembles him, and if the woman’s fluid precedes the man’s fluid, the child resembles her. The first thing with which people will be gathered is a fire that comes from the east and gathers the people to the west. The first thing the people of Paradise will eat is the extra lobe of a fish’s liver.” So ʿAbdullāh b. Salām believed. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people, and if they hear of my Islam they will slander me and speak ill of me. So hide me and send for them and ask them about me.” So he sent for them and they came—while he hid him—and he said: “What kind of man is ʿAbdullāh b. Salām among you?” They said: “The best of us and the son of the best of us, our master and the son of our master, our scholar and the son of our scholar.” He said: “Do you think that if he believes, you will believe?” They said: “May Allah protect him from that.” He said: “Come out to them, O Ibn Salām.” So he came out and said: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah.” They said: “Rather, he is the worst of us and the son of the worst of us, our ignorant one and the son of our ignorant one.” He said: “Did I not tell you, O Messenger of Allah, that they are a slanderous people?”"],[3420,"The women came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the merit; they fight in jihad and we do not fight.” He said: “The service of one of you in her home will attain the jihad of the mujahidun, if Allah wills.”"],[3421,"The women came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the merit through jihad in the path of Allah. What deed do we have by which we can attain the deed of the mujahidun in the path of Allah?” He said: “The service of one of you in her home will attain the deed of the mujahidun in the path of Allah.”"],[3422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a man of the Anṣār to visit him, and found him at the point of death. He greeted him and said: “How do you find yourself, O so-and-so?” He said: “Well, O Messenger of Allah. I hope in Allah and fear my sins.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They do not come together in the heart of a man at this moment except that Allah gives him what he hopes for and grants him safety from what he fears.”"],[3423,"The king of Dhū Yazan sent the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a robe that was purchased for thirty-three camels."],[3424,"No two men have ever loved each other for the sake of Allah except that the better of them was the one with stronger love for his companion."],[3425,"Whoever concerns himself with the hunger of his Muslim brother and feeds him until he is full and gives him drink until he is quenched, Allah will forgive him."],[3426,"O Allah, indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirin."],[3427,"Indeed Allah grasped a handful and said: 'For Paradise, by My mercy.' And He grasped a handful and said: 'For the Fire, and I do not care.'"],[3428,"I was harmed in the cause of Allah as no one has been harmed, and I was frightened in the cause of Allah as no one has been frightened, and indeed there came upon me and Bilal three days between a day and a night when we had no food except what was hidden under Bilal's armpit."],[3429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man being supported between his two sons, and he said: 'What is the matter with him?' They said: 'He vowed to perform Hajj walking.' He said: 'Indeed Allah is free of need from this man's walking, so let him ride.'"],[3430,"The prophets are alive in their graves, praying."],[3431,"Rain fell upon us while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered himself from it and said: 'Indeed it has recently been with its Lord.'"],[3432,"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas was the orator of the Ansar. When this verse was revealed: 'O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet and do not speak loudly to him as you speak loudly to one another,' Thabit said: 'I am the one who used to raise my voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I am among the people of the Fire.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Rather, he is among the people of Paradise. Rather, he is among the people of Paradise.'"],[3433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to prostrate, and al-Hasan or al-Husayn would come and climb onto his back, so he would prolong the prostration. It would be said: 'O Prophet of Allah, you have prolonged the prostration.' He would say: 'My son mounted me, and I disliked to hurry him.'"],[3434,"What an evil thing you have said. Why did you not ask Allah to grant you good in this world and good in the Hereafter and to protect you from the punishment of the Fire? He said: So the Prophet ﷺ commanded him, and he supplicated with that, and the Prophet ﷺ supplicated for him. He said: Then he stood up as if he had been released from a tether. He said: When we went out, Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you urged us just now to visit the sick. What do we get for that?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed when a Muslim man goes out of his house to visit his Muslim brother, he wades in mercy up to his waist. When he sits with the sick person, mercy envelops him and mercy envelops the sick person. The sick person is in the shade of His Throne, and the visitor is in the shade of His Holiness. Allah says to His angels: \"Look how much the visitors have stayed with the sick person.\" He said: They say: \"O Lord, a breathing interval\"—if they stayed for a breathing interval. Then Allah says to His angels: \"Write for My visiting servant the worship of a thousand years: standing in prayer at night and fasting during the day. And inform him that I have not written down a single sin against him.\" He said: And He says to His angels: \"Look how long they stayed.\" He said: They say: \"An hour.\" He said: If they stayed for an hour, He says: \"Write for him a dahr,\" and a dahr is ten thousand years. If he dies before that, he enters Paradise; and if he lives, not a single sin is written against him. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening, and he is in the harvested fruits of Paradise. If it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning, and he is in the harvested fruits of Paradise.'"],[3435,"The dream of the believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[3436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the best fasting. He said: 'Sha'ban, in veneration of Ramadan.'"],[3437,"When you pass by the meadows of Paradise, graze therein. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what are the meadows of Paradise?' He said: 'Circles of remembrance.'"],[3438,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have not left any need or want except that I have committed it.\" He said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God?\" three times. The man said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"That covers that.\""],[3439,"God has every Friday six hundred thousand freed ones whom He frees from the Fire.\" One of them said in his version: \"All of them have deserved the Fire.\""],[3440,"God has in every hour of the hours of this world six hundred thousand freed ones whom He frees from the Fire, all of them having deserved the Fire."],[3441,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would hear the crying of a child and would recite the short surah."],[3442,"Safiyya learned that Hafsa had said to her: \"Daughter of a Jew!\" The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was crying and said: \"What makes you cry?\" She said: \"Hafsa said to me: 'I am the daughter of a Jew.'\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You are the daughter of a prophet, your uncle was a prophet, and you are married to a prophet. So what does she boast over you with?\" Then he said: \"Fear God, O Hafsa.\""],[3443,"Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba wanted to marry a woman and mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"Go and look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you two.\" He said: \"So he did that and married her, and he mentioned their compatibility.\""],[3444,"When wine was forbidden, he said: \"On that day I was serving wine to eleven men. They ordered me, so I overturned it, and the people overturned their vessels with what was in them, until the streets were almost blocked by its smell.\" Anas said: \"Their wine in those days was nothing but unripe dates and ripe dates mixed together.\" He said: \"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I had property belonging to an orphan, and I bought wine with it. Do you think I should sell it and return to the orphan his property?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'May God curse the Jews! Fat was forbidden to them, but they sold it and ate its price.' The Prophet ﷺ did not permit him to sell the wine.\""],[3445,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah for the compensatory umrah, with Ibn Rawaha before him, saying: 'Clear the way, sons of the disbelievers, from his path! Today we will strike you for its true interpretation, a strike that removes heads from their resting place, and makes the friend forget his friend.' Umar said to him: 'O Ibn Rawaha, in the sanctuary of God and before the Messenger of God you recite this poetry?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Leave him, O `Umar, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, his words are harder on them than the falling of arrows.'"],[3446,"When the Prophet ﷺ felt the severity of death that he felt, Fatima said: \"O the distress of my father!\" He said: \"There is no distress for your father after today. What has come upon your father is something from which God will not spare anyone: his meeting on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3447,"A man said: \"O Messenger of God, I love so-and-so for God's sake.\" He said: \"Have you told him?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Go to him and tell him.\" He said: \"So he went to him and told him, saying: 'O so-and-so, I love you for God's sake.' The other said: 'May He for whose sake you loved me love you.'\""],[3448,"Whoever hears of a virtue from God and does not believe in it will not attain it."],[3449,"The Messenger of God ﷺ felt some pain. When morning came, it was said: \"O Messenger of God, the trace of pain is clear on you.\" He said: \"I am as you see, but last night I recited the seven long surahs.\""],[3450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us and said in his sermon: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant."],[3451,"Whoever asks for martyrdom sincerely from his heart, Allah will give him the reward of a martyr even if he dies on his bed."],[3452,"When I was taken up to the seventh heaven, there I was with Ibrahim leaning his back against the Frequented House, and every day seventy thousand angels enter it and do not return to it."],[3453,"Whoever has three daughters or three sisters, and fears Allah regarding them and takes care of them, will be with me in Paradise like this—and he gestured with his index and middle fingers."],[3454,"Tell me about the most amazing thing you saw. He said: Yes, O Thabit, I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years, and he never criticized me for anything I did wrong. And when the Prophet of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bt. Jahsh, my mother said to me: O Anas, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has become a bridegroom this morning, and I do not know whether he has any breakfast. Bring that small butter-skin. So I brought her the butter-skin and some dates, and she made hais for him. She said: O Anas, take this to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and his wife. When I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a stone vessel containing that hais, he said: Put it in a corner of the house, and invite for me Abu Bakr, Umar, Ali, Uthman, and a group of his companions, then invite for me the people of the mosque and whoever you see on the road. He said: I began to marvel at the small amount of food and the large number of people he was commanding me to invite, so I disliked to disobey him until the house and the room were full. He said: O Anas, do you see anyone? I said: No, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Bring that vessel. So I brought that vessel and placed it in front of him. He dipped three fingers into the vessel, and the vessel began to swell and rise. They began to eat breakfast and leave, until when they had all finished, there remained in the vessel about as much as I had brought. He said: Put it in front of Zaynab. So I left and closed a door made of palm branches. Thabit said: I said to Anas: How many do you think ate from that vessel? He said to me: I counted seventy-one or seventy-two."],[3455,"When I was taken up to the seventh heaven, he took me to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants, and its fruits were like large jars. When it was covered by what covered it from the command of Allah, it changed, and no one among people is able to describe it because of its beauty. Then He revealed to me what He revealed."],[3456,"Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him; if he does it, ten are recorded for him. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is recorded against him; if he does it, one evil deed is recorded for him."],[3457,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes descend from the pulpit after the prayer had been called, and a man would approach him and speak to him at length, then he would advance to his prayer place."],[3458,"Allah took a handful and said: To Paradise by My mercy. And He took a handful and said: To the Fire, and I do not care."],[3459,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a grave."],[3460,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say frequently: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[3461,"A man from the desert people named Zahir used to bring gifts to the Prophet ﷺ from the desert, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would equip him when he wanted to leave. The Prophet ﷺ said: Zahir is our desert, and we are his city. The Prophet ﷺ loved him, and he was an ugly man. The Prophet ﷺ came to him while he was selling his goods, and embraced him from behind while the man could not see him. He said: Let go, who is this? Then he recognized the Prophet ﷺ, and he began to press his back against the Prophet’s belly once he recognized him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to say: Who will buy this slave? The man said: O Messenger of Allah, in that case you will find me unsellable. The Prophet ﷺ said: But you are not unsellable with Allah. Or he said: With Allah you are precious."],[3462,"Fever is a bellows of the bellows of Hell. Whoever is afflicted with any of it, it will be his portion of the Fire."],[3463,"He said to a woman of his family: Do you know so-and-so? The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by her while she was weeping at a grave, and he said to her: Fear God and be patient. She said: Away from me, for you do not care about my calamity—and she did not know him. It was said to her: He is the Messenger of God! Then something like death seized her, and she came to his door but found no doorkeeper at it. She said: O Messenger of God, I did not recognize you. He said to her: Patience is only at the first shock."],[3464,"When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, the Abyssinians played with their spears out of joy at that."],[3465,"The hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ reached the middle of his ears."],[3466,"Let none of you wish for death."],[3467,"I was the cupbearer of the people in the house of Abu Talhah on the day wine was forbidden. Their drink that day was fadikh—unripe and ripe dates. Among them were men from the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ. A caller called out and said to me: Go out and look. I went out, and there was a caller announcing: Wine has been forbidden. He said: And there it was, flowing in the streets of Madinah. I came and informed Abu Talhah. He said: Go out and spill it. Some of the people said: So-and-so and so-and-so were killed while it was in their bellies. Then God sent down: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten—the verse."],[3468,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a trace of yellow and said: What is this? He said: O Messenger of God, I married a woman for the weight of a date stone of gold. He said: May God bless you. Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep."],[3469,"I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ hold a wedding feast for any of his wives like the feast he held for Zaynab, for he slaughtered a sheep."],[3470,"A man said: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for the Hour? He said: Nothing, except that I love God and His Messenger. He said: Then you will be with those you love. Anas said: We were not so happy about anything after Islam as we were about the words of the Messenger of God ﷺ: You will be with those you love. He said: I love the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar, and I hope to be with them because of my love for them, even if I do not do deeds like theirs."],[3471,"A funeral passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ and the people praised it well, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: It is assured. Then another passed by and was spoken of badly, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: It is assured. It was said: O Messenger of God, you said for this one, \"It is assured,\" and for that one, \"It is assured\"? He said: The testimony of the people. The believers are the witnesses of God on earth."],[3472,"A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, and some of the people jumped up. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not interrupt him. Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over it."],[3473,"The Messenger of God ﷺ once sent a man to one of the pharaohs of the Arabs, saying: Go and call him to me. He said: O Messenger of God, he is more arrogant than that. He said: Go and call him to me. He said: So he went to him and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ calls you. The man said to the messenger of the Messenger of God: What is God? Is He of gold, or of silver, or of copper? He said: He returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him, saying: O Messenger of God, I told you that he is more arrogant than that. He said to me such-and-such. He said: Return to him a second time. He said to him the like of it. He returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I told you that he is more arrogant than that. He said: Return to him and call him. So he returned to him a third time. He said: He repeated that speech to him. While he was talking to him, God sent a cloud over his head. It thundered, and a thunderbolt fell from it and carried away the top of his skull. Then God sent down: And He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills—the verse."],[3474,"I met ʿItbān after that, and he narrated to me and it pleased me, so I said to my son, 'Write it down,' and he wrote it. ʿItbān, whose sight had gone, said: I said, 'O Prophet of God, if you would come to me and pray in my house in a place I would adopt as a prayer area.' He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came and began praying while his companions were talking among themselves. He said: We mentioned what they were encountering from the hypocrites in the way of harm, and they made the greatest part of that to be upon Mālik b. Dukhshum. It pleased them that they would induce the Prophet ﷺ to supplicate against him and that God would destroy him. They said, 'O Prophet of God, his affair is such-and-such.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Does he not testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?' They said, 'He only says that with his tongue, and there is no form of it in his heart.' The Prophet of God ﷺ said, 'No one testifies that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God but that God will admit him—or he said: but that it will feed him—the Fire forever.'"],[3475,"The Prophet ﷺ was with one of his wives, and a man passed by him. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'She is my wife, so-and-so.' The man said, 'O Prophet of God, the one I would suspect, I would not suspect you.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Satan runs through the son of Adam like blood.'"],[3476,"I never saw a man at all take hold of the ear of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the Prophet turn his head away until the man turned his head away. And I never saw anyone at all take the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the Prophet let go of his hand until the man was the one who let go of his hand. And I never touched anything softer than the skin of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I never found any scent more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[3477,"A woman had something wrong in her mind. She said, 'O Messenger of God, I have a need to bring to you.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'O Umm so-and-so, take whichever road you wish and stand in it until I come to you.' The Messenger of God ﷺ went aside with her and spoke privately with her until she fulfilled her need."],[3478,"The Prophet of God ﷺ spoke a hadith, and we did not rejoice at anything since we came to know Islam more intensely than our rejoicing at it. He said, 'The believer is rewarded for removing harm from the road, for guiding to the way, for interpreting on behalf of the speech-impaired, and for giving the gift of milk—even rewarded for merchandise tied up in his garment that he touches but his hand misses.'"],[3479,"The Prophet ﷺ had hair down to the middle of his ears."],[3480,"The likeness of the believer is the likeness of an ear of grain: it bends at times and stands upright at times. And the likeness of my community is like the rain: one does not know whether its beginning is better or its end."],[3481,"He is not one of us who does not honor our elder and have mercy on our younger."],[3482,"A funeral bier was brought to the Prophet ﷺ for him to pray over it. He said, 'Does he owe a debt?' They said, 'Yes.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Gabriel forbade me to pray over a man who owes a debt. He said: The debtor is held in pledge in his grave until his debt is paid on his behalf.' The Prophet ﷺ refused to pray over him."],[3483,"Creation is the dependents of God, and the most beloved of His creation to Him is the one most beneficial to His dependents."],[3484,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar, al-Ḥajjāj b. ʿIlāṭ said, 'O Messenger of God, I have wealth in Makkah and family there. I want to go to them. Am I absolved if I speak ill of you or say something?' The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted him to say whatever he wished. He said: He went to his wife when he arrived and said, 'Gather whatever you have, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muḥammad and his companions, for they have been plundered and their wealth taken.' He said: That spread in Makkah and grieved the Muslims, while the polytheists showed joy and delight. The news reached al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he was crippled in his sitting place and could not stand. Maʿmar said: Al-Jazarī informed me, from Miqsam, who said: Al-ʿAbbās took a son of his called Qutham, who resembled the Messenger of God ﷺ, lay on his back, placed him on his chest, and said: 'My beloved Qutham, resembling the one with the prominent nose, always in blessings, in spite of the nose of whoever is spiteful.' Maʿmar said: Thābit said: Anas said: Then he sent a servant of his to al-Ḥajjāj b. ʿIlāṭ and said, 'Woe to you! What have you brought, and what are you saying? What God has promised is better than what you have brought.' Al-Ḥajjāj said to his servant, 'Convey greetings to Abū al-Faḍl and tell him to vacate one of his rooms for me so I can come to him, for the news is as he would like.' His servant came, and when he reached the door, he said, 'Rejoice, Abū al-Faḍl.' Al-ʿAbbās jumped up in joy until he kissed him between the eyes. He told him what al-Ḥajjāj had said, and he freed him. Then al-Ḥajjāj came and told him that the Messenger of God ﷺ had conquered Khaybar and taken their wealth as spoils, that God's shares ran in their wealth, that the Messenger of God ﷺ had chosen Ṣafiyya bt. Ḥuyayy for himself and taken her as his own, and gave her the choice between freeing her so she would be his wife or joining her family, and she chose that he free her and be his wife. 'But I came for what I had here; I wanted to gather it and leave with it. I sought permission from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he permitted me to say whatever I wished. Keep it hidden from me for three days, then mention whatever occurs to you.' He said: His wife gathered what she had of jewelry and goods, collected it, and gave it to him. Then he departed with it. After three days, al-ʿAbbās came to the wife of al-Ḥajjāj and said, 'What has your husband done?' She told him that he had gone and said, 'May God not grieve you, O Abū al-Faḍl. What reached you was hard on us.' He said, 'Indeed, may God not grieve me. By the praise of God, it was nothing but what we loved, indeed.'"],[3485,"He heard voices and said, 'What are these voices?' They said, 'They are pollinating date palms.' He said, 'If they did not do it, it would still be sound.' He said: So they refrained and did not pollinate that year, and the dates turned out to be inferior. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'If it is a matter of your worldly affairs, then it is your concern; but if it is a matter of your religion, then it is to me.'"],[3486,"There is no Muslim who dies and four people of households from his nearest neighbors testify that they know nothing but good of him, but Allah says: 'I have accepted your knowledge and forgiven him what you do not know.'"],[3487,"Women and perfume were made beloved to me, and the delight of my eye was placed in prayer."],[3488,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and with him was a daughter of his. Anas said: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and offered herself to him. His daughter said: 'How little modesty she has!' He said: 'She is better than you; she offered herself to the Prophet.'"],[3489,"Indeed, Friday and the night of Friday are twenty-four hours. There is no hour in them but that Allah has in it six hundred freed from the Fire. He said: Then we left him and entered upon al-Hasan and mentioned to him the hadith of Thabit. He said: 'I heard it,' and he added: 'All of them had deserved the Fire.'"],[3490,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in his supplication: 'O Allah, turn my heart to Your religion and protect those behind us by Your mercy.'"],[3491,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated, he was riding with Abu Bakr behind him. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq knew the road from his frequent travels to Syria. He would pass by people and they would say: 'Who is this with you?' He would say: 'A guide who guides me.' When they drew near Madinah, the two sent to the people who had become Muslims among the Ansar, to Abu Umamah and his companions, and they went out to them and said: 'Enter securely, obeyed.' So they entered. Anas said: I never saw a day more radiant or more beautiful than the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr entered Madinah."],[3492,"When he performed ablution, he would run his fingers through his beard."],[3493,"Nothing erases Islam as stinginess does."],[3494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out to the mosque where the Muhajirun and the Ansar were. None of them would raise his head from his sitting posture except Abu Bakr and Umar, for he would smile at them and they would smile at him."],[3495,"A man from the people of Paradise will look down upon the people of the Fire, and a man from the people of the Fire will call to him: 'O so-and-so, do you not recognize me?' He will say: 'No, by Allah, I do not recognize you. Who are you, woe to you?' He will say: 'I am the one you passed by in the world and asked me for a drink of water, and I gave you a drink, so intercede for me with your Lord because of it.' He said: That man will enter upon Allah in his visit and say: 'O Lord, I looked down upon the people of the Fire, and a man from the people of the Fire stood up and called: \"O so-and-so, do you not recognize me?\" I said: \"No, by Allah, I do not recognize you, and who are you?\" He said: \"I am the one you passed by in the world and asked me for a drink, and I gave you a drink, so intercede for me with your Lord.\" O Lord, let me intercede for him.' He said: Allah will grant him intercession for him and will bring him out of the Fire."],[3496,"When I came to Anas, he was informed of my location, and I entered upon him. I took his hands and kissed them and said: 'May my father be sacrificed for these two hands that touched the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' And I kissed his eyes and said: 'May my father be sacrificed for these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[3497,"When I came to Anas, he called for perfume and wiped his hands and his cheeks with it."],[3498,"Thabit, when he came to Anas, Anas would say: O slave girl, bring me perfume to wipe my hands, for the son of Umm Thabit, when he comes, is not satisfied until he kisses my hands."],[3499,"A man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with white head and beard, and he said: Are you not a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: Then dye your hair."],[3500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to us this verse: 'Indeed, those who say, Our Lord is Allah, and then remain steadfast' (41:30). And he said: People have said it, then most of them disbelieved. So whoever says it until he dies is among those who remained steadfast upon it."],[3501,"Shall I inform you of the best among you? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best among you are those with the longest lives, if they are guided aright."],[3502,"A man from the people of Paradise will be brought, and He will say: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? He will say: O Lord, the best abode. He will say to him: Ask and wish. He will say: I do not ask or wish except that You return me to the world so that I may be killed ten times, because of what he sees of the excellence of martyrdom. And a man from the people of the Fire will be brought, and He will say: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? He will say: O Lord, the worst abode. Then He will say: Would you ransom yourself with the earth's fill of gold? He will say: Yes, O Lord. He will say: You have lied. I asked you for what was easier than this. Then he will be returned to the Fire."],[3503,"There is no soul that dies having good with Allah that would be pleased to return to the world, except the martyr, for he would be pleased to return to the world and be killed, because of what he sees of the excellence of martyrdom."],[3504,"I rode it until it carried me, until I came to the Sacred House (Jerusalem). I tied the animal to the ring to which the prophets tie it. Then I entered the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs in it. Then I came out, and Jibril came to me with a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk. I took the milk, and Jibril said to me: You have chosen the fitrah. He said: Then he ascended with us to the lowest heaven. Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Adam. He welcomed me and supplicated for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the second heaven. Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with the two maternal cousins, Yahya and 'Isa. They welcomed me and supplicated for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the third heaven. Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Yusuf, and he had been given half of all beauty. He welcomed me and supplicated for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the fourth heaven. Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Idris. He welcomed me and supplicated for good for me. He said: Allah says: 'And We raised him to a high station' (19:57). Then he ascended with us to the fifth heaven. Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there was Harun. He welcomed me and supplicated for good for me. Then he ascended with us to the sixth heaven. Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Ibrahim, and he was leaning his back against the House, into which seventy thousand angels enter every day, then they do not return to it. Then he took me to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants and its fruits like large jars. When it was covered by what covered it of the command of Allah, it changed, and no one of Allah's creation can describe it because of its beauty. He said: Then it was revealed to me what was revealed, and fifty prayers were made obligatory upon me every day. He said: Then I descended to Musa, and he said: What did your Lord make obligatory upon your ummah? I said: Fifty prayers every day and night. He said: Your ummah cannot bear that. Go back to your Lord and ask Him for reduction. He said: So I went back to my Lord and said: O Lord, lighten it for my ummah. He reduced five from me. I returned to Musa, and he said: What did you do? I said: He reduced five from me. He said: Your ummah cannot bear that. Go back to your Lord and ask Him for reduction. I kept going back to my Lord and asking Him for reduction, between my Lord and Musa, until He said: O Muhammad, they are five prayers every day and night, for each prayer ten, so that is fifty prayers. And whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, one good deed is written for him; if he does it, ten are written. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is against him; if he does it, one evil deed is written. So I returned to Musa and told him. He said: Go back to your Lord and ask Him for reduction. He said: I have gone back to my Lord until I felt ashamed."],[3505,"Harithah went out as a scout, and an arrow struck him and killed him. His mother said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the place of Harithah in my heart. If he is in Paradise, I will be patient; otherwise, you will see what I do. He said: O mother of Harithah, it is not one Paradise, but many gardens, and Harithah is in the best of them. Or he said: In the highest Firdaws."],[3506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed continuous fasting at the end of the month, and some people also observed continuous fasting. That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: If the month were extended for us, I would have fasted continuously in a way that would make the exaggerators abandon their exaggeration. You are not like me. I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."],[3507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[3508,"I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water, milk, nabidh, and honey to drink in this cup."],[3509,"I heard Anas b. Malik say to a woman among his family: Do you not know so-and-so? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by her while she was weeping at a grave, and he said to her: Fear Allah and be patient. She said to him: Go away from me, for you do not care about my calamity. He said: She had not recognized him. Then it was said to her: This is the Messenger of Allah. Something like death seized her, and she came to his door but did not find a doorkeeper. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not recognize you. He said: Patience is only at the first shock."],[3510,"I entered Paradise and heard a soft sound, so I said: What is this soft sound? It was said: Al-Rumaysaʾ bt. Milhan."],[3511,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it with his hand."],[3512,"Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was playing with the boys, and he took him, threw him down, split open his chest, and extracted from it a clot. He said: This is the share of Shaytan in you. Then he washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, then he closed him up and returned it to its place. The boys went running to his mother — meaning his wet-nurse — and said: Muhammad has been killed. She met him while his color was changed. Anas said: I used to see the trace of the needle in his chest. And Hammad sometimes said: A visitor came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3513,"Some people from ʿUrayna came to Madinah and found its climate disagreeable, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them to the camels of sadaqah and said: Drink their urine and milk. They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, drove off the camels, and apostatized from Islam. They were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he cut off their hands and feet on opposite sides, gouged out their eyes, and threw them into the harrah. Anas said: I used to see one of them gnawing the ground with his mouth until they died. And Hammad sometimes said: biting the ground with his mouth until they died."],[3514,"The people said: O Messenger of Allah, the wealth is destroyed, we are afflicted by drought, O Messenger of Allah, and the wealth is destroyed, so pray for rain for us. He stood on Friday while he was on the minbar and prayed for rain — and Hammad described his extending his hands opposite his chest, with the palms of his hands facing the ground — and there was not even a small cloud in the sky. He did not leave until the strong young man was concerned about returning to his family. He said: Then we received rain until the next Friday. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the buildings have collapsed and the travelers are cut off, so supplicate to Allah to remove it from us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: Then it cleared away until Madinah was as if it were in a crown."],[3515,"Umm Sulaym was with Abu Talha on the day of Hunayn, and with Umm Sulaym was a dagger. Abu Talha said: What is this with you, O Umm Sulaym? She said: I have taken it so that if any of the disbelievers comes near me, I will rip open his belly with it. Abu Talha said: O Prophet of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says? She says such and such. She said: O Messenger of Allah, kill those after us from the freed prisoners; they fled with you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Umm Sulaym, Allah has sufficed and done well."],[3516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a man from his companions to visit him, and he had become like a chick. He said to him: Have you asked Allah? He said: I said: O Allah, whatever punishment You would give me in the hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: You have no strength for Allah's punishment. Why did you not say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire?"],[3517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a man from the Ansar and said: O maternal uncle, say: There is no god but Allah. He said: A maternal uncle or a paternal uncle? He said: No, rather a maternal uncle. And he said: Is it better for me to say it? He said: Yes."],[3518,"I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to drink with this cup of mine all kinds of drink: honey, nabidh, and milk."],[3519,"Stand straight, stand straight, for by Allah I see you from behind me as I see you from in front of me."],[3520,"When the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they said: Send with us a man to teach us the Sunnah and Islam. He took the hand of Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah and said: This is the trusted one of this ummah."],[3521,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, where is my father? He said: In the Fire. When he turned away, he called him back and said: My father and your father are in the Fire."],[3522,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was met one day by the boys and slave women of the Ansar, and he said: By Allah, I love you."],[3523,"A woman had something wrong with her mind. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. He said: O mother of so-and-so, look at whichever road you want. He stood with her, speaking privately, until she fulfilled her need."],[3524,"The sister of al-Rubayyiʿ b. Haritha injured someone, and they brought the dispute to the Prophet ﷺ. They said: O Messenger of Allah, retaliation, retaliation. The mother of al-Rubayyiʿ said: O Messenger of Allah, will you exact retaliation from so-and-so? No, by Allah, you will not exact retaliation from her. She kept at it until they accepted blood money. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Among Allah's servants are those who, if they swore by Allah, He would honor it."],[3525,"Every treacherous one will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known."],[3526,"The person among the people of Paradise who was most severely afflicted in this world will be brought, and Allah will say: Dip him in Paradise once. He will be dipped once in it. Then Allah will say: O son of Adam, have you ever seen hardship or anything you dislike? He will say: No, by Your might, I have never seen anything I dislike. Then the person among the people of the Fire who was most blessed in this world will be brought, and Allah will say: Dip him once in the Fire. He will be dipped once in it. He said: Then He will say: O son of Adam, have you ever seen any good or any delight? He will say: No, by Your might, I have never seen any good or any delight."],[3527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman used to begin the prayer with \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of all the worlds.\" Humaid did not mention the Prophet ﷺ."],[3528,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: Praise be to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, sufficed us, and sheltered us. How many have no one to suffice them or shelter them."],[3529,"There will remain of Paradise what Allah wills to remain, then Allah will create for it a creation as He wills."],[3530,"He used to say often: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[3531,"The Hour will not come until it is no longer said on earth: Allah, Allah."],[3532,"We used to say that the Hour will not come until the sky does not rain and the earth does not grow plants, until fifty women have one caretaker, and until a woman passes by a man and he seizes her and looks at her and says: This one once had a man. Hammad mentioned it this way, and Hammad also mentioned it from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, without doubt. He also said: from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, as I think."],[3533,"I saw as if I were in the house of ʿUqba b. Rafiʿ, and we were brought fresh dates of the Ibn Tab variety. I interpreted it that we will have elevation in this world, a good outcome in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become good."],[3534,"He recited this verse: “Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was given al-Kawthar, and behold, it is a river flowing without having been dug. Its two banks are domes of pearl. I struck my hand into its soil, and behold, it was pungent musk, and its pebbles were pearls.”"],[3535,"Women and perfume were made beloved to me from this world, and the coolness of my eyes was placed in prayer."],[3536,"The Prophet ﷺ heard sounds and said: “What are these sounds?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, they are pollinating the date palms.” He said: “If they did not do it, it would be fine.” He said: So they did not pollinate them that year, and they produced unripe dates. He said: They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “If something concerns a matter of your world, it is up to you; and if something concerns a matter of your religion, then it is to me.”"],[3537,"He saw an old man being supported between his two sons, and said: “What is the matter with this man?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, he vowed to walk.” He said: “Allah is in no need of this man’s tormenting himself,” meaning: then he commanded him, so he rode."],[3538,"The Jews, when a woman menstruated, would not eat with her or be intimate with her in the houses. The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ asked the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah revealed: “They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation,” the verse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do everything except intercourse.” This reached the Jews, and they said: “This man wants to leave nothing of our affair without contradicting us in it.” Usayd b. Hudayr and Abbad b. Bishr came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, the Jews say such and such; should we not be intimate with them?” The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed color until we thought he was angry with them. They left, and a gift of milk met them. He sent after them and gave them to drink, so we knew he was not angry with them."],[3539,"When he supplicated, he turned the backs of his hands toward his face."],[3540,"He would fast until it was said: “He has fasted,” and he would break his fast until it was said: “He has broken his fast.”"],[3541,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a silver ring on his right hand, with an Abyssinian stone, and he used to place its stone on the inside of his palm."],[3542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a ring of silver, and its stone was Abyssinian."],[3543,"He saw on the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a ring of silver. He said: The people made rings of silver, so he threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings."],[3544,"The Prophet ﷺ entered on the day of the conquest, and on his head was a helmet. It was said: “This is Ibn Khatal clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba.” He said: “Kill him.”"],[3545,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah wearing a helmet."],[3546,"The Prophet ﷺ arrived in the year of the conquest wearing a helmet. It was said, 'This is Ibn Khatal clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba.' He said, 'Kill him.'"],[3547,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah wearing a helmet."],[3548,"When he entered the privy, he would remove his ring."],[3549,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a ring of silver with an Abyssinian bezel, and its inscription was 'Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.'"],[3550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade soaking nabidh in gourds and in vessels smeared with pitch."],[3551,"When supper is served and the prayer is called, begin with supper."],[3552,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, something similar."],[3553,"The last time I looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Monday. He drew aside the curtain while the people were behind Abu Bakr. I looked at his face as if it were a page of a mushaf. The people wanted to move, but he gestured to them to stay, and he let the curtain fall. He died at the end of that day."],[3554,"Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and do not cut off relations with one another. Be, O servants of Allah, brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[3555,"Do not cut off relations with one another, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and do not turn your backs on one another. Be, O servants of Allah, brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[3556,"Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Sufyan b. Husayn reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3557,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty. My mothers used to urge me to serve him. He entered our house, and we milked for him from a domestic sheep, mixed for him with water from a well in the house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank, and Umar said to him—while Abu Bakr was on his left—'O Messenger of Allah, give it to Abu Bakr,' but he gave it to a bedouin on his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The right, then the right.'"],[3558,"The Prophet ﷺ arrived, similarly."],[3559,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah when I was ten years old, and he passed away when I was twenty years old, and my mothers used to urge me to serve him."],[3560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered our house, and we milked a domestic sheep for him, and it was mixed with water from a well in the house. The Messenger of God ﷺ drank, with Abu Bakr on his left, a Bedouin on his right, and Umar aside. Umar said: Give Abu Bakr. The Messenger of God ﷺ handed it to the Bedouin and said: The right, then the right."],[3561,"A man said: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: He did not mention much good, but I love God and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with those whom you love."],[3562,"A man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the Hour, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much of deeds for it, except that I love God and His Messenger. He said: A person is with those whom he loves."],[3563,"The Prophet ﷺ fell from a horse and his right side was bruised. The prayer time came and he prayed with us seated. When he finished his prayer, he said: The imam is only appointed to be followed. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he says: God hears those who praise Him, say: Our Lord, to You belongs praise; and when he prays seated, pray seated, all of you."],[3564,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyya. I think he said: with dates and sawiq."],[3565,"The Prophet ﷺ drank standing."],[3566,"The Prophet ﷺ drank standing, with a Bedouin on his right and Abu Bakr on his left, and he gave it to the Bedouin and said: The right, then the right."],[3567,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought milk and drank. He said: Abu Bakr was on his left, and a Bedouin on his right, so Umar said: O Messenger of God, hand it to Abu Bakr. He said: Then he handed it to the Bedouin."],[3568,"He used to say the talbiya: At Your service, O God, at Your service; at Your service, You have no partner, at Your service; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and the dominion; You have no partner."],[3569,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drinking, with Abu Bakr on his left and a man from the Bedouins on his right, and he gave the Bedouin his leftover, then said: The right, then the right."],[3570,"He saw upon the Messenger of God ﷺ a silver ring one day, so he made rings of silver and they wore them. Then the Prophet ﷺ threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings. And he saw on a man's hand a ring of gold and struck his finger with a blow. And he saw on Umm Salamah two gold earrings and turned away from her until she threw them off."],[3571,"The Messenger of God ﷺ recited: 'And We ordained therein for them: a life for a life, and an eye for an eye.'"],[3572,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ fell ill with the sickness in which he died, Bilal came to him and called the adhan for the prayer. He said: 'O Bilal, you have conveyed; so whoever wills, let him pray, and whoever wills, let him refrain.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, who shall lead the people in prayer?' He said: 'Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' When Abu Bakr advanced, the curtains were lifted from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we looked at him, and it was as if he were a white leaf, upon him a black cloak. Abu Bakr thought that he wanted to come out, so he stepped back, but the Messenger of God ﷺ gestured to him: 'Pray in your place.' So Abu Bakr prayed, and we did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ again until he died that day."],[3573,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Hamzah — his nose had been cut off and he had been mutilated — and said: 'Were it not that Safiyyah would be distressed, I would leave him so that God would gather him from the bellies of beasts and birds.' He was shrouded in a striped cloak; when they covered his head, his feet showed, and when they covered his feet, his head showed. So they covered his head. And he did not pray over any of the martyrs, and he said: 'I am a witness over you today.' He would place three in one grave and two in one grave, and he would ask which of them knew more Qur'an, and he would put him first in the niche of the grave. And he would shroud two or three men in a single garment."],[3574,"He used to gesture during the prayer."],[3575,"I asked God for those who play among the descendants of mankind, and He gave them to me."],[3576,"The Prophet ﷺ entered during the compensatory 'Umrah with Ibn Rawahah before him, and he was saying: 'Clear the path of the sons of the disbelievers; the Most Merciful has revealed in His revelation that the best killing is in His path.'"],[3577,"The Messenger of God ﷺ became a prophet at the age of forty years. He stayed in Makkah for ten and in Madinah for ten, and he died at the age of sixty years, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."],[3578,"Every religion has a character, and the character of this religion is modesty."],[3579,"Every community has a trustworthy one, and this is our trustworthy one — and he took the hand of Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[3580,"The one among them most resembling the Prophet ﷺ was al-Hasan b. 'Ali."],[3581,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: 'But Hamzah has no weepers.' This reached the women of the Ansar, and they wept for Hamzah. The Messenger of God ﷺ slept, then woke while they were still weeping, and he said: 'Woe to them! Have they not stopped weeping since today? Let them weep, but let them not weep for any dead one after today.'"],[3582,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is established, begin with it, and do not rush away from your evening meal."],[3583,"O Allah, place in Madinah double the blessing that is in Makkah."],[3584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah during the Umrah of al-Qada, and Ibn Rawahah was holding his stirrup, saying: Clear the sons of the disbelievers from his path; the Most Merciful has sent down in His revelation that the best killing is in His path."],[3585,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with sawiq and dates."],[3586,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say while he was in Madinah: O Allah, place in it double the blessing that is in Makkah."],[3587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized As'ad b. Zurarah for a thorn wound."],[3588,"The Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah while it was feverish, so people fell ill. The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque while people were sitting and praying. He said: The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing. So people endured the prayer standing."],[3589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a silver ring on his right hand with an Abyssinian stone, and its stone was facing his palm."],[3590,"Al-Hasan b. Ali was the one among them most resembling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in face."],[3591,"I saw on Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a silken striped garment."],[3592,"Indeed my basin is between Aylah and San'a' of Yemen, and in it are as many pitchers as the stars of the sky."],[3593,"He used to gesture in prayer."],[3594,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid what is made in jars, in pitch-coated vessels, and from gourds, and he said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[3595,"He received prophethood at the age of forty, and he stayed in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and he died at the age of sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs on his head and beard."],[3596,"If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have two valleys, and nothing will fill his mouth except dust, and God turns to whoever repents."],[3597,"He forbade a man from selling the stud service of his horse."],[3598,"He used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was high and alive, and a traveler would go to al-Awali while the sun was still high."],[3599,"Some people of the Ansar said on the day of Hunayn, when God granted His Messenger spoils from the wealth of Hawazin, and the Messenger of God ﷺ began giving men of Quraysh a hundred camels each. They said: May God forgive the Messenger of God; he gives Quraysh and leaves us while our swords drip with their blood? Anas said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was told of their words, so he sent for the Ansar and gathered them in a leather tent, and he did not call anyone else with them. When they gathered, the Messenger of God ﷺ came to them and said: What is this talk that has reached me from you? The learned ones among the Ansar said: As for those of sound judgment among us, O Messenger of God, they said nothing, but some people among us who are young in age said: May God forgive the Messenger of God; he gives Quraysh and leaves us while our swords drip with their blood? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: I give to those who are new in Islam to win their hearts. Are you not pleased that the people go with wealth while you return to your homes with the Messenger of God? By God, what you return with is better than what they return with. They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, we are pleased. He said to them: You will find after me severe favoritism, so be patient until you meet God and His Messenger, for I will be at the Basin. Anas said: They said: Yes."],[3600,"The Messenger of God ﷺ fell from a horse and injured his right side, so we entered to visit him. The prayer time came and he prayed sitting, and we prayed behind him sitting. When he finished the prayer, he said: The imam is appointed only to be followed, so when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he says, 'God hears the one who praises Him,' say, 'Our Lord, to You be praise;' and when he prays sitting, pray sitting, all of you."],[3601,"The last look I had of the Messenger of God ﷺ was when he lifted the curtain on the day he died, and I looked at his face as if it were a page of a mushaf, then he signaled to the people to stay—and he let down the curtain, and he died at the end of that day—while they were in rows behind Abu Bakr."],[3602,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Hour, and he said: What have you prepared for it? He said—as if he did not mention much—: Nothing except that I love God and His Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You will be with the one you love."],[3603,"When dinner is served and the prayer is called, begin with dinner."],[3604,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade making nabidh in gourds and pitch-coated vessels."],[3605,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty, and my mothers used to urge me to serve him. He entered our house, and we milked a domestic sheep for him, and we mixed its milk with water from the well of the house, with Abu Bakr on his right and Umar to one side. The Prophet ﷺ drank, and Umar said: O Messenger of God, give it to Abu Bakr. He handed it to the Bedouin and said: The right, then the right."],[3606,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out when the sun had declined and prayed the noon prayer. When he had said the salutation, he stood on the pulpit and mentioned the Hour, and mentioned that before it there are great matters. He said: Whoever wishes to ask about anything, let him ask about it. For by God, you will not ask me about anything but that I will tell you of it as long as I remain in this station of mine. Anas said: A man rose to him and said: Where is the entrance of my father, O Messenger of God? He said: The Fire. Then Abdullah b. Hudhafah rose and said: Who is my father, O Messenger of God? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Then he repeated many times: Ask me. Umar knelt on his knees and said: We are content with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. The Messenger of God ﷺ fell silent when Umar said that. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, Paradise and the Fire were displayed to me just now in the breadth of this wall, and I have not seen as today in good and evil. Al-Zuhri said: And Ubayd Allah b. Abdullah b. Utbah informed me: The mother of Abdullah b. Hudhafah said: I have never seen a son more disobedient than you. Did you feel secure that your mother might have committed something in the pre-Islamic period, and you would expose her before the women? Abdullah said: By God, if he had attached me to a black slave, I would have attached myself to him."],[3607,"When the evening meal is served and the call to prayer is given, begin with the evening meal."],[3608,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ raising his voice in talbiyah for an umrah and a hajj."],[3609,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray the afternoon prayer, then a person would go to al-Awali while the sun was still high."],[3610,"He used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was white and lively, then a person would go to al-Awali and reach it while the sun was still high."],[3611,"On the day of Hunayn, the people fled from the Messenger of God ﷺ except al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered that it be called out: O companions of Surat al-Baqarah, O assembly of the Ansar. Then the call intensified among the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj. When they heard the call, they came forward. By God, I likened them only to camels coming to their young. When they met, the fighting became fierce. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Now the oven is heated. He took a handful of white pebbles and threw them and said: They are defeated, by the Lord of the Kabah. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ was that day the fiercest of the people in fighting before him."],[3612,"Whoever is pleased to be safe, let him keep to silence."],[3613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to walk in front of the funeral procession."],[3614,"Whoever loves that his lifespan be extended and his provision be expanded - I think he said: in it - let him maintain his kinship ties."],[3615,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: But Hamzah has no weepers. That reached the women of the Ansar, and they wept for Hamzah. The Messenger of God ﷺ slept, then woke while they were weeping. He said: Alas for them, they have been weeping since today. Let them weep, but let them not weep for any dead person after today."],[3616,"No servant says: There is no god but God, in an hour of night or day, but the evil deeds in his record are erased until he settles into the like of it of good deeds."],[3617,"Do not envy one another, and do not compete with one another, and do not hate one another, and do not turn your backs on one another. Be servants of God as brothers. It is not lawful for a man to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[3618,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ drink milk, with Abu Bakr on his left and a man from the Bedouins on his right. He gave the leftover to the Bedouin, then said: \"The right, then the right.\""],[3619,"The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah. Gabriel descended and opened my chest, then washed it with water from Zamzam. Then he brought a golden basin filled with wisdom and faith, poured it into my chest, and closed it."],[3620,"They said: \"O Messenger of God, shall we not help with the ransom of al-Abbas?\" He said: \"Not even with a dirham.\""],[3621,"The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah. Gabriel ﷺ descended and opened my chest, then washed it with water from Zamzam. Then he brought a golden basin filled with wisdom and faith, poured it into my chest, and closed it. Then he took my hand and ascended with me to the heaven. When he came to the lowest heaven, Gabriel said to the keeper of the heaven: \"Open.\" He said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"Gabriel.\" He said: \"Is there anyone with you?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Has he been sent for?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he opened. When we ascended to the lowest heaven, there was a man sitting with dark figures on his right and dark figures on his left. When he looked to his right, he smiled, and when he looked to his left, he wept. He said: \"Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous son.\" He [the Prophet] said: I said to Gabriel: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"This is Adam, and these dark figures on his right and left are his descendants. The people of the right are the people of Paradise, and the dark figures on his left are the people of Hell. When he looks to the right, he laughs, and when he looks to his left, he weeps.\" He said: Then Gabriel ascended with me until he came to the second heaven and said to its keeper: \"Open.\" Its keeper said to him the like of what the keeper of the lowest heaven had said, and he opened. Anas said: He mentioned that he found in the heavens Adam, Idris, Musa, Isa, and Ibrahim, but he did not make clear how their stations were, except that he mentioned that he found Adam in the lowest heaven and Ibrahim in the third heaven. Anas said: When Gabriel and the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Idris, he said: \"Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous brother.\" He said: Then I said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"This is Idris.\" Then I passed by Musa, and he said: \"Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous brother.\" He said: I said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"This is Musa.\" He said: Then I passed by Isa, and he said: \"Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous brother.\" He said: I said: \"Who is this?\" I think he said: \"Isa.\" He said: Then I passed by Ibrahim, and he said: \"Welcome to the righteous prophet and the righteous son.\" He said: I said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"This is Ibrahim.\""],[3622,"Indeed, Ayyub, the prophet of God, remained in his affliction for eighteen years. Near and far relatives shunned him, except for two men from among his brothers who were among his closest brothers. They would come to him in the morning and evening. One of them said to his companion: \"Do you know, by God, Ayyub has committed a sin that no one else has committed?\" His companion said: \"What is that?\" He said: \"For eighteen years God has not had mercy on him and relieved him.\" When they went to him, the man could not bear it until he mentioned that to him. Ayyub said: \"I do not know what you are saying, except that God knows that I used to pass by two men who were disputing and mentioning God, and I would return to my house and expiate for them, out of dislike that God should be mentioned except in truth.\" He said: And he used to go out for his need, and when he had finished his need, his wife would hold his hand until he reached home. One day he was late, and it was revealed to Ayyub in his place: \"Strike with your foot: this is a cool bathing place and a drink.\" She found him late and met him waiting, and he came toward her, God having removed what was in him of affliction, and he was in the best state he had ever been. When she saw him, she said: \"May God bless you! Have you seen God's prophet, this afflicted one? By God, I have not seen anyone more like him than you when he was healthy.\" He said: \"Indeed, I am he.\" He had two threshing floors: one for wheat and one for barley. God sent two clouds. When one of them was over the wheat floor, it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver over the barley floor until it overflowed."],[3623,"When the land is fertile, dismount from your mounts and give them their due of pasture. When the land is barren, travel on them with their marrow, and keep to night travel, for the earth is folded up by night."],[3624,"When he wanted to combine Zuhr and Asr during travel, he would delay Zuhr until the time of Asr entered and then combine them."],[3625,"O God, make in Madinah twice the blessing that is in Makkah."],[3626,"Dye with henna, for it is pleasant in fragrance and calms dizziness."],[3627,"A man traveled with the Prophet ﷺ and cursed his camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O servant of God, do not travel with us on a cursed camel.\""],[3628,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would hear the crying of a child behind him and would shorten the prayer, fearing that its mother would be distressed."],[3629,"My dear son, keep my secret and you will be a believer. My mother and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to ask me about the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ, but I would not tell them, and I will never tell the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ to anyone ever. And he said: My dear son, be thorough in performing ablution, and your guardian angels will love you and your lifespan will be increased. O Anas, be thorough in washing from major impurity, for you will emerge from your bath with no sin or error upon you. He said: I said: \"How is thoroughness, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Wet the roots of the hair and cleanse the skin. My dear son, if you can always be in a state of ablution, then do so, for whoever death comes to while he is in a state of ablution will be granted martyrdom. My dear son, if you can always be praying, then do so, for the angels pray for you as long as you pray. O Anas, when you bow, place your palms firmly on your knees, spread your fingers, and raise your elbows from your sides. My dear son, when you raise your head from bowing, let every limb of yours return to its place, for God will not look on the Day of Resurrection at one who does not straighten his back between his bowing and prostration. My dear son, when you prostrate, place your forehead and palms firmly on the ground, and do not peck like a rooster, and do not sit like a dog—or he said: a fox. Beware of turning around in prayer, for turning around in prayer is destruction. If it is necessary, then in the voluntary prayer, not in the obligatory. My dear son, when you go out of your house, let not your eye fall upon anyone of the people of the qibla without greeting him, for you will return forgiven. My dear son, when you enter your home, greet yourself and your family. My dear son, if you can wake up in the morning and evening with no deceit in your heart toward anyone, then do so, for it will be easier for you in the reckoning. My dear son, if you follow my advice, then let nothing be dearer to you than death.\""],[3630,"He said to a man driving a sacrificial camel: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Even so. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it, as long as it is not injured."],[3631,"A Bedouin came and urinated in the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that the place be dug up and a bucket of water poured over it. The Bedouin said: O Messenger of God, a man loves a people but has not yet done their deeds? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A man is with those whom he loves."],[3632,"Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to it."],[3633,"I served the Messenger of God ﷺ for nine years, and he never said to me about anything I did that he disliked: What have you done? Nor did he ever say about anything that pleased him: How well you have done."],[3634,"Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to it."],[3635,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ reciting the talbiyah for Hajj and 'Umrah together, and my knee was touching his knee."],[3636,"While I and the Messenger of God ﷺ were leaving the mosque, a man met us at the entrance of the mosque and said: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What have you prepared for it? He said: It was as if the man hesitated, then said: O Messenger of God, I have not prepared for it much prayer, nor fasting, nor charity, but I love God and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with those whom you love."],[3637,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: When is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it much prayer, nor fasting, nor charity, except that I love God and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with those whom you love."],[3638,"I prayed the noon prayer with the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah four rak'ahs, and the afternoon prayer at Dhu al-Hulayfah two rak'ahs."],[3639,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the noon prayer in Madinah four rak'ahs, and he prayed the afternoon prayer at Dhu al-Hulayfah two rak'ahs while he was traveling to Makkah."],[3640,"I prayed the noon prayer with the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah four rak'ahs, and he prayed the afternoon prayer at Dhu al-Hulayfah two rak'ahs."],[3641,"I asked my Lord for the heedless among the descendants of humankind, and He granted them to me."],[3642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent at the age of forty, and he passed away when he was sixty years old, with not twenty white hairs in his beard or on his head."],[3643,"There were not twenty white hairs on the head and beard of the Prophet ﷺ."],[3644,"The Dajjal will emerge from the Jewry of Isfahan, with him seventy thousand Jews wearing the sijan."],[3645,"There were not twenty white hairs on the head and beard of the Prophet ﷺ."],[3646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away when he was sixty years old, with not twenty white hairs on his head and beard."],[3647,"He witnessed a gate of Baqi' al-Gharqad, with a crowd sitting behind him, among them Anas b. Malik. He said: I heard him mention the description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and among what he mentioned he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent as a prophet when he was forty years old. He remained in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and he passed away when he was sixty, with not twenty white hairs on his head and beard."],[3648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had wavy hair, neither straight nor tightly curly. He was fair, neither dark nor very white. He was of medium height among the people, neither short nor very tall. He was sent at the age of forty, he stayed in Makkah for ten years and in Madinah for ten years, and he passed away at the age of sixty, with not twenty white hairs on his head and beard."],[3649,"The leaders are from Quraysh: when they judge, they are just; when they make a covenant, they fulfill it; and when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy."],[3650,"I entered with my father upon Abu Barzah al-Aslami, and at that time I had two earrings in my ears—that is, I was a boy. Abu Barzah said: I praise Allah that I have come to condemn this tribe of Quraysh. So-and-so here fights for worldly gain, and so-and-so fights for worldly gain—meaning 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan—until he mentioned Ibn al-Azraq. Then he said: The most beloved people to me are this band with matted hair, whose bellies are empty of the wealth of the Muslims, and whose backs are light of their blood. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The rulers are from Quraysh\"—three times—\"You have a right over them, and they have a right over you as long as they do three things: when they judge, they are just; when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; and when they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.\""],[3651,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ pronouncing talbiyah for Hajj and 'Umrah together."],[3652,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating while sitting on his heels, eating quickly, and he was distributing it and sending me with it. I think he meant dates."],[3653,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Bayda'—and he was riding behind Abu Talhah—pronouncing talbiyah for 'Umrah and Hajj together."],[3654,"The Messenger of God ﷺ granted the Ansar land from al-Bahrayn, so they said, \"O Messenger of God, and our brothers from the Muhajirun, so grant them also.\" He said, \"You will encounter after me preferential treatment, so be patient until you meet me.\""],[3655,"\"Shall I inform you of the best dwellings of the Ansar?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"The dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then the dwellings of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then the dwellings of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the dwellings of Banu Sa'idah.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"And in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good.\""],[3656,"\"You will be afflicted after me with preferential treatment, so be patient until you meet me.\""],[3657,"A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, and his companions wanted to stop him, but the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Leave him,\" and he ordered water to be poured over it."],[3658,"He saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying on a donkey – while he was going to Khaybar – with the qiblah behind him."],[3659,"A Bedouin entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, then stood toward a side of the mosque and urinated. The people shouted at him, but the Messenger of God ﷺ restrained them until he finished. Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over the Bedouin's urine."],[3660,"Prayer is the light of the believer."],[3661,"Envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes firewood, and charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire, and prayer is the light of the believer, and fasting is a shield from the Fire."],[3662,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and he withdrew to relieve himself. Then he came and said, \"Is there any water?\" So I brought him a vessel of water and he performed ablution with it, then wiped over his leather socks."],[3663,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and he withdrew to relieve himself. Then he caught up with me and said, \"Is there any water?\" So he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then caught up with the army and led them in prayer."],[3664,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ went out to relieve himself, I and a boy would bring him a vessel of water and a spear, and he would clean himself with water."],[3665,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over his son Ibrahim and said the takbir over him four times."],[3666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never had a retaliation case brought to him except that he commanded forgiveness in it."],[3667,"I used to go out with the Prophet ﷺ while I was a boy, and I had with me a water vessel and a short spear. He would relieve himself, then perform ablution."],[3668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would go out to relieve himself, and I would bring him water and he would wash himself with it."],[3669,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far away until he was almost out of sight."],[3670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four rak'ahs, and at Dhu al-Hulayfah two rak'ahs — meaning 'Asr."],[3671,"Umm Sulaym sent me with fresh dates to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a plate, at the first ripening of the palm fruit. He said: I entered upon him and placed it before him, and he ate some of it. Then he took my hand and we went out. He had recently wed Zaynab bt. Jahsh. He said: He passed by some of his wives, and with them were men conversing. He said: They congratulated him, and the people congratulated him, saying: Praise be to Allah who has delighted your eye, O Messenger of Allah. Then he went on until he came to 'A'ishah, and there were men with her. He said: He disliked that, and when he disliked something it would show in his face. He said: I went to Umm Sulaym and told her, and Abu Talhah said: If it is as your son says, something will surely happen. He said: When evening came, the Prophet ﷺ went out and ascended the minbar, and recited this verse: 'O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you for a meal.' He said: Then he commanded the veil."],[3672,"I said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray in sandals? He said: Yes."],[3673,"A man was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who had inflicted harm on the enemy and exerted himself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I do not know this man. He said: Rather I describe him as such and such. He said: I do not know him. While we were like that, the man appeared. They said: It is this one, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I did not know this one. This is the first horn I have seen in my community. There is in him a touch from Satan. When the man drew near, he greeted, and he returned the greeting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: I adjure you by Allah, did you tell yourself when you appeared to us that there is no one among the people better than you? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: Then he entered the mosque and prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: Arise and kill him. Abu Bakr entered and found him praying. Abu Bakr said to himself: Prayer has sanctity and a right, and if only I had consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: Did you kill him? He said: No, I saw him praying, and I considered prayer to have sanctity and a right, and if you wish for me to kill him, I will kill him. He said: You are not the one for him. Go, you, O 'Umar, and kill him. 'Umar entered the mosque and found him prostrating. He waited for him for a long time, then said to himself: Prostration has a right, and if only I had consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for someone better than me has already consulted him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Did you kill him? He said: No, I saw him prostrating, and I considered prostration to have a right, and if you wish for me to kill him, I will kill him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You are not the one for him. Arise, O 'Ali, you are the one for him if you find him. He entered and found that he had left the mosque. He returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Did you kill him? He said: No. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Had he been killed today, no two men of my community would have differed until the Dajjal appears. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to them about the nations and said: The community of Musa split into seventy-one sects, seventy of them in the Fire and one in Paradise. The community of 'Isa split into seventy-two sects, seventy-one of them in the Fire and one in Paradise. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: And my community will exceed both groups together by one sect: seventy-two in the Fire and one in Paradise. They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The congregations. Ya'qub b. Zayd said: When 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he recited from the Qur'an: 'And among the people of Musa is a community that guides by the truth and by it establishes justice.' Then he mentioned the community of 'Isa and said: 'If only the People of the Book had believed and been mindful, We would have removed from them their misdeeds' up to His saying: 'Evil is what they do.' Then he mentioned our community: 'And among those We created is a community that guides by the truth and by it establishes justice.'"],[3674,"I prayed Zuhr with 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz, then we went to Anas b. Malik ؓ. When we entered upon him, he said: Have you prayed? We said: Yes. He said: O servant girl, bring me water for ablution. I have not prayed behind any imam after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whose prayer more closely resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than this imam of yours."],[3675,"The excellence of 'A'ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."],[3676,"The excellence of 'A'ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."],[3677,"The excellence of 'A'ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."],[3678,"The excellence of 'A'ishah over other women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."],[3679,"A sheep was milked for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and its milk was brought. He called for water and poured it onto the milk, then drank while 'Umar was facing him, Abu Bakr was on his left, and a Bedouin was on his right. 'Umar said, 'Abu Bakr is here with you.' He said, 'Those on the right.' So he handed it to the Bedouin."],[3680,"The Messenger of God ﷺ reclined at the house of the daughter of Milhan. He dozed off, then woke up smiling. She said, 'O Messenger of God, what made you smile?' He said, 'Some people of my community who will travel upon this green sea; they will be like kings upon thrones.' She said, 'O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them.' He said, 'O God, make her one of them.' She later married 'Ubadah b. al-Samit and traveled by sea with the daughter of Qarazah. When she returned, her mount threw her and she died, and she was buried."],[3681,"When she returned, she rode a mount on the coast, and it threw her; she fell and died."],[3682,"The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his head in the house of the daughter of Milhan, who was one of his maternal aunts. Then he raised his head and smiled. She said, 'What makes you smile, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'Some people of my community will travel upon this sea, like kings upon thrones.' She said, 'O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them.' So he prayed that God make her one of them. Then he placed his head, then raised it and smiled. She said, 'What makes you smile?' He said the like of what he said the first time. She said, 'Pray to God to make me one of them.' He said, 'You are among the first, but you are not among the last.' He said that twice or three times. Then 'Ubadah b. al-Samit married the daughter of Milhan, and he took her across the sea. When she was on the coast, she rode his mount, and it threw her; she was knocked down and died."],[3683,"A newborn, until he reaches the age of accountability: whatever good he does is recorded for his parent, or his parents; and whatever evil he does is not recorded against him or against his parents. When he reaches the age of accountability, the pen flows over him. The two angels who are with him are commanded to preserve and to be strict. When he reaches forty years in Islam, God protects him from three afflictions: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty, God lightens his reckoning. When he reaches sixty, God grants him turning to Him in repentance in a manner He loves. When he reaches seventy, the inhabitants of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, God writes down his good deeds and overlooks his bad deeds. When he reaches ninety, God forgives his past and future sins, and lets him intercede for the members of his household, and he becomes a prisoner of God on His earth. When he reaches the most abject age, so that he knows nothing after having known, God writes for him the like of the good he used to do when he was healthy, and if he does an evil deed, it is not written against him."],[3684,"Indeed, supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah, so supplicate."],[3685,"Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is answered, so supplicate."],[3686,"Whoever mentions me, let him invoke blessings upon me. Whoever invokes blessings upon me once, God will bless him ten times."],[3687,"Whoever asks God for Paradise three times, Paradise says, 'O God, admit him to Paradise.' Whoever seeks refuge in God from the Fire three times, the Fire says, 'O God, protect him from me.'"],[3688,"There is no servant who asks for Paradise three times except that Paradise says, 'O God, admit him to Paradise.' There is no servant who seeks refuge in God from the Fire three times except that the Fire says, 'O God, protect him from me.'"],[3689,"In the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, we used to steep fresh ripe dates and unripe dates. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, we poured them out of the vessels and then left them."],[3690,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ one day while he was sitting sad — some of the people of Makkah had struck him — and said: \"What is wrong with you?\" He said: \"These people did such-and-such to me, and they did such-and-such.\" He said: \"Would you like me to show you a sign?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then look at a tree beyond the valley.\" He said: \"Call that tree.\" He said: \"So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him. Then he said to it: 'Go back.' He said: 'So it returned to its place.'\""],[3691,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ one day while he was sitting sad, having been struck by some of the people of Makkah. He said: \"These people did such-and-such to me, and they did such-and-such.\" He said: \"Would you like me to show you a sign?\" Then he looked at a tree beyond the valley and said: \"Call that tree.\" So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him. Then he said to it: \"Go back.\" So it returned until it came back to its place. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is enough for me.\""],[3692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say frequently: \"O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we have believed in you and in what you have brought. Do you fear for us?\" He said: \"Yes. Indeed, the hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; He turns them.\""],[3693,"Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ, he used to say frequently: \"O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we have believed in you and in what you have brought. Do you fear for us?\" He said: \"Yes. Indeed, the hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; He turns them.\""],[3694,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out angry and addressed the people, saying: \"Do not ask me about anything today except that I will inform you of it.\" We thought that Jibril was with him. A man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we have only recently come from ignorance. Who is my father?\" He said: \"Your father is Hudhafah,\" referring to the father to whom he was attributed. Then he asked him about other things. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we have only recently come from ignorance, so do not expose our faults to us.\" He said: \"Will you disgrace us with our secrets? Pardon us, may Allah pardon you. We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger.\" He said: \"Then he was relieved. Then he looked and said: 'I have never seen a day like today in good and evil. Paradise and the Fire were shown to me, just beyond the wall. I have never seen more veiled faces than on that day.'\""],[3695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day angry, and we thought that Jibril ﷺ was with him, until he ascended the minbar. I have never seen a day with more weeping and veiling of faces. He said: \"Ask me, for by Allah, you will not ask me about anything except that I will inform you of it.\" A man stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?\" He said: \"Your father is Hudhafah, the one to whom you are attributed.\" Then another stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, am I in Paradise or in the Fire?\" He said: \"In the Fire.\" Then a man stood up to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj obligatory upon us every year?\" He said: \"If I said yes, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory, you would not be able to do it, and if you did not do it, you would be punished.\" Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: \"We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet. Do not disgrace us with our secrets, and pardon us, may Allah pardon you.\" He said: \"Then he was relieved. Then he turned toward the wall and said: 'I have never seen a day like today in good and evil. Paradise and the Fire were shown to me behind this wall.'\""],[3696,"They struck the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once until he lost consciousness. Abu Bakr ؓ stood up and began calling out: \"Woe to you! Will you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah?\" They said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"The son of Abu Quhafah, the madman.\""],[3697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution for every prayer. He said: \"And you?\" He said: \"We are sufficed by the ablution as long as we have not invalidated it.\""],[3698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a ruin belonging to Banu al-Najjar to relieve himself. Then he came out to us alarmed and said: \"Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would ask Allah to make you hear some of the punishment of the grave so that you would hear it.\""],[3699,"He and his father entered upon Anas b. Malik in Madinah during the time of 'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz, when he was governor. He prayed a light prayer, as if it were the prayer of a traveler or close to it. When he said the salam, he said: \"May Allah have mercy on you. Do you think this prayer is the prescribed prayer or something you prayed voluntarily?\" He said: \"It is the prescribed prayer, and it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I did not miss anything except something I forgot. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'Do not make things hard on yourselves, lest Allah make things hard on you. A people made things hard on themselves, so Allah made things hard on them. Those are their remnants in the monasteries and hermitages: and monasticism they invented; We did not prescribe it for them.' Then they went out the next morning and said: \"Let us ride and look and take a lesson.\" He said: \"Yes.\" So they all rode, and behold, there were deserted dwellings whose people had perished, become extinct, and been expelled, collapsed upon their roofs. They said: \"Do you recognize these dwellings?\" He said: \"How well I know them and their people! These are the people of dwellings whom transgression and envy destroyed. Indeed, envy extinguishes the light of good deeds, and transgression confirms that or belies it. The eye commits adultery, as do the palm, the foot, the hand, and the tongue, and the private part confirms that or belies it.\""],[3700,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had supplications that he would not abandon. He used to say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety, sadness, grief, incapacity, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, the burden of debt, and the domination of men.\""],[3701,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik after we had prayed Zuhr. His slave girl said to him: \"The prayer.\" I said: \"Which prayer, O Abu Hamzah?\" He said: \"'Asr.\" I said: \"We have just prayed Zuhr.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'That is the prayer of the hypocrite. He leaves the prayer until it is at the horn of Shaytan — or: between the two horns of Shaytan — then he stands and prays, not remembering Allah except a little.'\""],[3702,"I never prayed behind an imam whose prayer was lighter than the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[3703,"Abu Ma'mar narrated to us: Isma'il narrated to us, from al-'Ala' b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[3704,"Abu Ma'mar narrated to us: Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, something similar."],[3705,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had supplications he never abandoned: O God, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from miserliness and cowardice, from the burden of debt, and from being overpowered by men."],[3706,"Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ when he returned with the army was: O God, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from cowardice and miserliness, from the burden of debt, and from being overpowered by men."],[3707,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at Uhud and said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. O God, Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred, and I declare sacred what lies between its two lava tracts."],[3708,"Find for us a servant from your young men to serve me. He said: So Abu Talhah went out with me, riding me behind him. I continued to serve the Messenger of God ﷺ whenever he halted. I kept hearing him frequently say: O God, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from miserliness and cowardice, from the burden of debt, and from being overpowered by men. I did not cease serving him until we returned from Khaybar, and he returned with Safiyyah bt. Huyayy, having taken her as his share. I saw him doing so, making a seat for her behind him with a cloak or a blanket, then seating her behind him. When we were at al-Sahba', he prepared hays on a leather mat, then sent me, and I invited men, and they ate. That was his wedding feast for her. Then he set out until Uhud appeared to him, and he said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. When he overlooked Madinah, he said: O God, I declare sacred what lies between its two mountains just as Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred. O God, bless them in their mudd and their sa'."],[3709,"The Prophet ﷺ selected Safiyyah for himself – or: by himself – until when he came to al-Sahba', he stopped with her. He ordered me, and I invited those around him, and he brought sawiq and dates. That was the wedding feast of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: And I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ gathering for her – or: making a seat for her – then placing his leg for her so she could mount."],[3710,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade three things: the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, visiting graves, and this nabidh in these containers. Then he said: Indeed I forbade you three things, but then it became clear to me that people keep their condiments, honor their guests, and save for those absent. So eat and keep as much as you wish. I forbade you visiting graves – I think, Abu Bakr doubted – so visit them and do not say anything improper. It was as if he said: It softens the heart, makes the eye weep, and reminds of the Hereafter. And I forbade you nabidh, so make nabidh in whatever you wish; whoever wishes may tie his waterskin upon sin."],[3711,"Abu Hammam al-Walid b. Shuja' narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahim b. Sulayman narrated to us with his chain, something similar."],[3712,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade visiting graves, eating meat of sacrificial animals after three days, and nabidh in gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels. He said: Then after three days the Messenger of God ﷺ said: I had forbidden you three things, but then it became clear to me concerning them. I forbade you visiting graves, but then it became clear to me that it softens the heart, makes the eye weep, and reminds of the Hereafter. So visit them and do not say anything improper. I forbade you eating meat of sacrificial animals beyond three nights, but then it became clear to me that people keep their condiments, honor their guests, and save for those absent. So keep as much as you wish. I forbade you nabidh in these vessels, so drink in whatever you wish, but do not drink any intoxicant; whoever wishes may tie his waterskin upon sin."],[3713,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform ablution for every prayer. He said: I said: Then what about you? How do you do? He said: We used to pray several prayers with one ablution as long as we had not broken it."],[3714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have cupping done, and he would not wrong anyone of their wages."],[3715,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done, and he would not wrong anyone of their wages."],[3716,"When My servant is afflicted with the loss of his two beloved ones (his eyes), then he remains patient, I will compensate him for them with Paradise."],[3717,"Al-Juhani said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in a place as you know, and we cannot attend the month. Inform us of the Night of Decree.' He said: 'Attend the last seven of the month.' He said: 'I cannot do that.' He said: 'Then seek it on the night of the seventh that remains, and it is this night.' He said: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the night of the twenty-third, and it is for eight remaining.' He said: 'Thus this month decreases, and it is seven remaining.'"],[3718,"There is no wealthy person who would not be pleased on the Day of Resurrection that what he was given in this world was only bare sustenance."],[3719,"The best of your condiments is salt."],[3720,"Indeed before the Hour there will be years of deception, in which the truthful one is disbelieved, the liar is believed, the treacherous is trusted, and the ruwaybidah speaks. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the ruwaybidah?' He said: 'The insignificant corrupt man who speaks about the affairs of the common people.'"],[3721,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3722,"The example of my ummah is like the rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[3723,"He used to go around to all his wives in one night with a single bath."],[3724,"The Prophet ﷺ went around to his wives in one night with a single bath."],[3725,"Be straight in your prayer and be close together, for I see you from behind my back. Anas said: 'I saw one of us pressing his shoulder to the shoulder of his companion and his foot to his foot, and if you tried to do that today, you would see one of them like a restive mule.'"],[3726,"Make your rows straight and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back."],[3727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one of the lightest of people in prayer and the most concise."],[3728,"I am in the row during prayer and I hear the sound of a child crying, so I shorten my prayer for fear that it should cause hardship for his mother."],[3729,"The Prophet ﷺ heard the sound of a child while he was praying, so he lightened the prayer, and we thought that he lightened it because the child's mother was praying."],[3730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer and heard the crying of a child in the row, and we thought that he did that only out of mercy for him."],[3731,"I entered Paradise and there I was by a river whose two banks were tents of pearl. I struck my hand into the flowing water and it was pungent musk. I said, 'O Jibril, what is this?' He said, 'This is al-Kawthar which Allah has given you,' or 'which your Lord has given you.'"],[3732,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a wall belonging to Banu al-Najjar and heard a sound. He said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'A person who died in the Jahiliyyah.' He said, 'Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would ask my Lord to let you hear the punishment of the grave.'"],[3733,"The Prophet ﷺ swore an oath to stay away from his wives for a month and sat in an upper room of his, and his foot had become dislocated. He said: They entered upon him, and when the prayer time came, he prayed with them sitting, and they prayed standing. Then he came down after twenty-nine days, and they said, 'You swore a month.' He said, 'The month is twenty-nine.'"],[3734,"The white hair that was on the Prophet ﷺ did not reach twenty hairs."],[3735,"A woman came to him whose son had been killed, and she had no other child, and his name was Harithah. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if he is in Paradise I will be patient, but if he is elsewhere, you will see what I do.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There are many gardens, and he is in the highest Firdaws.'"],[3736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a she-camel called al-Adba' that was never outrun. A Bedouin came on a young camel of his and outran her, and that was hard on the Muslims. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, al-Adba' has been outrun!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'It is a right upon Allah that nothing of it rises except that He lowers it,' meaning the worldly life."],[3737,"Abu Talhah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I have dedicated my garden to Allah, and if I could have concealed it, I would not have made it known.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Give it to the poor among your relatives.'"],[3738,"The Prophet ﷺ went out for the prayer after the iqamah had been called, and a man intercepted him and spoke to him until the people nearly dozed off."],[3739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and Abu Bakr prayed, sitting wrapped in a garment during the illness in which he died."],[3740,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the prayer, he said the takbir and raised his hands until his thumbs were level with his ears. Then he said: 'Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika, wa tabaraka ismuka, wa ta'ala jadduka, wa la ilaha ghayruka.'"],[3741,"I entered Paradise and found a palace of gold. I said: 'To whom does this palace belong?' It was said: 'To a young man of Quraysh.' I thought I was that man, so I said: 'And who is he?' It was said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' By Allah, O Abu Hafs, nothing prevented me from entering it except what I knew of your jealousy.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, whoever I might be jealous over, I would never be jealous over you.'"],[3742,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Bayda, while I was riding behind Abu Talha, pronouncing the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah."],[3743,"The Prophet ﷺ had his incisor broken on the day of Uhud, and his forehead was wounded until blood flowed over his face. He said: 'How can a people prosper who did this to their Prophet while he calls them to their Lord?' Then this verse was revealed: 'You have no part in the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers.'"],[3744,"The delegation of Thaqif said: 'O Messenger of Allah, our land is a cold land. What is sufficient for us for the ghusl of janabah?' He said: 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times.'"],[3745,"He forbade selling fruits until they ripen. It was said: 'And what does ripen mean?' He said: 'Until they turn red.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you not see that if Allah withholds the fruit, for what would one of you take his brother's wealth?'"],[3746,"The complexion of the Prophet ﷺ was brown."],[3747,"Abdullah b. Salam asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'What is the first of the signs of the Hour?' He said..."],[3748,"The hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached halfway to his ears."],[3749,"He forbade selling fruit until it ripens, selling grapes until they turn black, and selling grain until it hardens."],[3750,"The prayer was called [the iqamah was given], and there was something between the Messenger of God ﷺ and his wives, so he began to turn some of them away from others. Then Abu Bakr ؓ came and said: Put dust in their mouths and go out to prayer."],[3751,"The best treatment you use is cupping, and do not torture your sons by pressing the uvula."],[3752,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by with a group of his companions, and there was a young boy on the road. His mother feared he would be trampled, so she ran saying: My son, my son, and she grabbed him. The people said: O Messenger of God, this woman would never throw her son into the Fire. He said: Nor would God throw His beloved into the Fire."],[3753,"Wahb b. Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid reported to us, from Humayd, from Anas, and he mentioned something similar from the Prophet ﷺ."],[3754,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned something similar."],[3755,"A man would come to the Messenger of God ﷺ and embrace Islam for some worldly thing; he would only embrace Islam for that. By evening, Islam would become dearer to him than the world and all it contains."],[3756,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed behind Abu Bakr ؓ wearing a single garment."],[3757,"He used to raise his hands in bowing and prostration."],[3758,"Umm Sulaym took his hand when the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah and said: O Messenger of God, this is Anas, and he is a boy who can write. Anas said: I served him for nine years, and he never said to me about anything I did: You did wrong, or How bad what you did."],[3759,"The dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[3760,"One night the Prophet ﷺ was praying in his room. Some of his companions came and prayed with his prayer. He entered the house and then came out and repeated that several times, each time praying. In the morning they said: O Messenger of God, we prayed with you and would like you to prolong your prayer. He said: I knew you were there, and I did that deliberately."],[3761,"Do not be impressed by the deeds of anyone until you see how his life ends. A person may work for a time with a righteous deed such that if he died he would enter Paradise, then he changes and does an evil deed. And a servant may work for a time with an evil deed such that if he died he would enter the Fire, then he changes and does a righteous deed. When God wants good for a servant, He uses him before his death. They said: O Messenger of God, how does He use him? He said: He grants him success in a righteous deed, then takes his soul."],[3762,"The call to prayer was given. Those whose houses were near the mosque rose and performed ablution, while those who lived far from the mosque remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a stone basin containing water. The Prophet ﷺ pressed his fingers together in it because of its narrowness, and the people performed ablution from it. He said: and they were about eighty men."],[3763,"Anas was asked about the earnings of a cupper, and he did not say it was lawful or unlawful. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done; Abu Tayba cupped him, and he ordered that he be given two sa's of food. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to his family, meaning that they reduce his kharaj or his tax. And he said: The best with which you treat yourselves is cupping and costus marinus, and do not torment your children by pressing the uvula."],[3764,"The Prophet ﷺ visited a man who had become like a plucked chick. The Prophet ﷺ said: What were you supplicating and asking Him? He said: I used to say: O Allah, whatever punishment You would inflict on me in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. He said: Glory be to Allah! Can you bear that? Why did you not say: O Allah, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire. He said: Then he supplicated to Allah, and He healed him."],[3765,"A funeral procession passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they praised it with good, until the tongues followed one another with good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It has become due. Then another passed by him and they praised it with evil. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It has become due. Then he said: You are Allah's witnesses on earth."],[3766,"I have never smelled the scent of musk or ambergris more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3767,"I have never touched silk or brocade softer than the palm of the Prophet ﷺ."],[3768,"The Prophet ﷺ was neither tall nor short, his hair reached the lobes of his ears, neither curly nor straight."],[3769,"When the Prophet ﷺ walked, it was as though he were leaning forward."],[3770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man from Banu al-Najjar: O uncle, submit to Islam. He said: I find myself averse to it. He said: Even if you are averse to it and are compelled to it."],[3771,"On the day he set out to Badr, the Prophet ﷺ consulted the people. He consulted the Muslims. Abu Bakr ؓ gave him his opinion, and he remained silent. Then he consulted again, and Umar ؓ gave him his opinion. A man from the Ansar said: He means you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we do not say as the Children of Israel said: Go, you and your Lord, and fight; we are sitting here. Rather, by Allah, if you strike their livers at Bark al-Ghimad, we will be with you."],[3772,"The Prophet ﷺ was delayed from the prayer because of something between his wives, and some of them began answering others back. Abu Bakr ؓ stood up and began calling out: O Messenger of Allah, throw dust into their mouths and come out to the prayer."],[3773,"The Dajjal is one-eyed in the left eye, written between his eyes: kafir."],[3774,"He used to come to Umm Sulaym and sleep on her bed. He was a heavy sleeper and sweated a great deal. She would take his sweat with a piece of cotton and put it in a bottle, then put it in perfume she had."],[3775,"The Prophet ﷺ came out one day with his head bandaged. Some men of the Ansar met him, and he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I love you. The Ansar have fulfilled what was upon them, and what is upon you remains, so accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers."],[3776,"Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of God, brothers."],[3777,"Thabit b. Qays gave a speech at the arrival of the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: We will protect you from what we protect ourselves and our children from, so what is for us, O Messenger of God? He said: Paradise is for you. They said: We are content."],[3778,"The Muhajirun came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, we have never seen people more generous with much, nor better in consoling with little, than the Ansar. When we came to al-Madinah, they shared with us in the good things. We fear that they will take all the reward. He said: No, not as long as you praise them and supplicate for them."],[3779,"The Prophet ﷺ was with one of his wives, and she sent him a bowl containing food. When the one in whose house he was came, she struck the servant's hand, and the bowl fell and broke. The Prophet ﷺ took it and began putting the food back into it, saying: Your mother has become jealous. When she brought her bowl, he took it and sent it to the one whose bowl had been broken."],[3780,"A morning spent in the path of God is better than the world and what it contains, and the space of one of your bows in Paradise is better than the world and what it contains. If a woman from among the women of the people of Paradise were to look upon the earth, she would fill what is between them with the fragrance of musk and illuminate what is between them. Her head-covering is better than the world and what it contains."],[3781,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Give me a mount. He said: We will mount you on the offspring of a she-camel. The man said: What would I do with the offspring of a she-camel? The Prophet ﷺ said: Do camels give birth to anything but she-camels?"],[3782,"The Prophet ﷺ returned from Khaybar, and when he was between al-Madinah and Khaybar, he consummated his marriage with Safiyyah. He stayed with her for three days and held a wedding feast. Umm Sulaym baked bread, spread a leather mat, and they poured dates, clarified butter, and dried curds onto it, and there was nothing else. Then he mounted his riding animal. The people said: If he veils her, she is among the Mothers of the Believers. When he mounted, he seated her behind him and veiled her with a cloth. When he entered al-Madinah, he would urge his camel to a faster pace. When he entered, he urged his camel, and the people climbed up. The Mothers of the Believers were looking at the Messenger of God ﷺ and at her. The she-camel stumbled, and the Prophet ﷺ was thrown. He was concerned only with arranging her clothes over her. He said: It was as if they gloated over her."],[3783,"Abu Talhah was shooting arrows in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ would raise his head to look at the place where his arrow fell. Abu Talhah raised his chest to shield him and said: Like this, O Messenger of God, may God make me your ransom."],[3784,"I attended the wedding feast of two of the Prophet's wives ﷺ, and he did not feed us bread or meat. He said: I said: Then what? He said: Hays."],[3785,"The Muhajirun said: O Messenger of God, we have never seen the like of a people we came to, better in generosity with much, nor better in consoling with little. They have spared us the burden and shared with us in the good things. We fear that they will take all the reward. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Not at all, not as long as you praise them and supplicate to God for them."],[3786,"When ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf arrived as an emigrant, the Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ. Saʿd said to him, “I have wealth, so half of it is yours, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them is dearer to you and I will divorce her; when her waiting period ends, you may marry her.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said to him, “May God bless you in your family and your wealth. Show me to the market.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ missed him for some days, then he came to him with traces of yellow perfume on him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “What is this?” He said, “I married a woman of the Anṣār.” He said, “What did you give her as a bridal gift?” He said, “A date-stone of gold” – or: “the weight of a date-stone of gold.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.”"],[3787,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām asked the Prophet ﷺ about the first signs of the Hour, and he said:"],[3788,"“Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise.” They said, “Give us more, O Messenger of God.” He said, “For every man, seventy thousand.” They said, “Give us more, O Messenger of God,” and he was on a sand hill, so he scooped with his hand. They said, “Give us more, O Messenger of God.” He said, “This,” and scooped with his hand. They said, “O Prophet of God, may God keep far from the Fire whoever enters the Fire after this.”"],[3789,"There was no person in the world whose sight they loved more than the Messenger of God ﷺ. Yet when they saw him, they did not stand for him, because they knew how much he disliked that."],[3790,"Anas was asked about the hair of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: The hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ did not go beyond his ears, as if it were the hair of Qatāda. Qatāda rejoiced that day, for the hair of Qatāda was lank."],[3791,"The Prophet ﷺ entered a house – or a place – and saw a rope stretched out. He said, “What is this?” They said, “So-and-so prays, and when she becomes tired, she holds onto it.” He said, “Let her pray; when she becomes tired, let her sleep or sit.”"],[3792,"He was in al-Baqīʿ when a man called out, “O Abū al-Qāsim!” The Messenger of God ﷺ turned around, and the man said, “I did not mean you.” He said, “Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya.”"],[3793,"I gave the Messenger of God ﷺ to drink from this very cup honey, nabīdh, water, and milk."],[3794,"For a virgin, seven [days]; for a previously married woman, three."],[3795,"When a wind blew, the Messenger of God ﷺ would show it on his face."],[3796,"The period for a woman after childbirth is forty days, unless she sees purity before that."],[3797,"I never saw the Prophet ﷺ pray Maghrib before breaking his fast, even if it was only with a drink of water."],[3798,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raise his hands when he began the prayer, when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[3799,"When one of you has a fever, let him pour cold water over himself for three nights from the pre-dawn time."],[3800,"Something occurred among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and he began forbidding them. He was delayed from the prayer, so Abu Bakr called out: O Messenger of God, throw dust in their faces and come out to the prayer."],[3801,"The Prophet ﷺ made one of his wives stand and measured a span or two from the hem of her garment, and said: Do not add to this."],[3802,"There is no servant who dies and has good with God who would love to return to this world, even if he had the world and all that is in it, except the martyr, because of what he sees of the excellence of martyrdom. For he would love to return to this world and be killed again."],[3803,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out one day with his head bandaged. The Ansar met him with their faces and their young men, and he said: By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I love you. The Ansar have fulfilled what was upon them, and what remains is upon you, so be good to those who do good among them and overlook those who do wrong among them."],[3804,"None of you should wish for death because of harm that befalls him in this world, but let him say: O God, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me."],[3805,"Anas was asked: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ take a ring? He said: Yes. It is as if I am looking at the gleam of his ring. He delayed the last evening prayer one night until half the night had passed, then he prayed. When he finished his prayer, he turned his face to us and said: The people have prayed and gone to sleep, but you will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it. He said: It is as if I am looking at the gleam of his ring. He said: His ring was of silver, and its bezel was of the same."],[3806,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the time of the dawn prayer. When we awoke the next day, he ordered at the break of dawn that the prayer be established. On the following day, he delayed it until it became light, then he ordered that the prayer be established, and he led us in prayer. Then he said: Where is the one who asked about the time of the prayer? What is between these two is the time."],[3807,"He visited a Muslim man. He entered upon him while he was like a plucked chick, in weakness. He asked: Were you not praying for something or asking for it? He said: Yes, I used to say: O God, whatever punishment You would bring upon me in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Prophet ﷺ said: Glory be to God! You cannot bear it – or: you cannot manage it. Why did you not say: O God, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed for him, and God, Mighty and Majestic, healed him."],[3808,"The Prophet ﷺ went out one day and traveled toward Badr. He began consulting the people, and Abu Bakr gave him his opinion. Then he consulted them again, and Umar gave him his opinion. He kept consulting, and the Ansar said: By God, he wants none but us. A man from the Ansar said: I see that you consult, and they give their opinions. We do not say as the Children of Israel said: Go, you and your Lord, and fight. Rather, by Him who sent you with the truth, if you struck the livers of their camels until you reached Ghimad, we would be with you."],[3809,"When the Prophet ﷺ raided a people, he did not attack until morning, so that he could observe. If he heard the call to prayer, he refrained from them, and if he did not hear the call to prayer, he raided them. He said: We went out to Khaybar and reached it. When morning came and he did not hear the call to prayer, he mounted, and I mounted behind Abu Talha, and my foot was touching the foot of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: They came out to us with their baskets and their tools. When they saw the Prophet ﷺ, they said: Muhammad and the army. When the Prophet ﷺ saw them, he said: God is most great. Khaybar is destroyed. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned."],[3810,"Labbayka bi-ʿumratin wa-ḥajjin"],[3811,"We traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and no fasting person criticized one who broke his fast, nor did one who broke his fast criticize a fasting person. The people had exerted themselves one day in Ramadan during the journey, so the Messenger of God ﷺ called for a vessel and drank from it so that the people would see that he was not fasting."],[3812,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey in Ramadan while he was fasting. A vessel of water was brought to him; he placed it on his hand and drank from it while the people were watching, so they drank."],[3813,"He stood at night over the well in which Abu Jahl and his companions lay at Badr, three days after they had been killed, and called out: “O Abu Jahl b. Hisham! O ʿUtba b. Rabiʿa! O Shayba b. Rabiʿa! O Umayya b. Khalaf! Have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” Some of his companions whom God willed came out to him and said: “O Messenger of God, do you call a people who have rotted for three days?” He said: “You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, except that they cannot answer me.”"],[3814,"Masruq b. al-Marzuban narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. ʿAyyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: The Messenger of God ﷺ looked over the well, then he mentioned something similar."],[3815,"While a man was driving a sacrificial camel, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Ride it.” He said: “It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Ride it, even if it is a sacrificial camel.”"],[3816,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Baqiʿ al-Gharqad, and there was a man calling his companion: “O Abu al-Qasim!” The Prophet ﷺ turned, and the man said: “I did not mean you, O Messenger of God; I meant so-and-so.” He said: “Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya.”"],[3817,"The dream of a believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[3818,"A man looked in on the Prophet ﷺ through a gap, so he aimed a headless arrow at him."],[3819,"When one of you comes to the prayer, let him walk calmly. Let him pray what he catches up with and make up what he missed."],[3820,"When the Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsah, he was commanded to take her back, so he took her back."],[3821,"He liked the Muhajirun and the Ansar to be close to him so that they could learn from him."],[3822,"The prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ was close in its parts to one another, and the prayer of Abu Bakr ؓ was close in its parts, then Umar lengthened the dawn prayer."],[3823,"That a morsel fell from his hand and he searched for it until he found it, and he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If a morsel of one of you falls, let him wipe off whatever is on it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan."],[3824,"He used to fast during the month until we would say: He will not break his fast, and he would break his fast until we would say: He will not fast any of it."],[3825,"That the Ansar had two days in which they used to play during the Jahiliyyah, and when the Messenger of God ﷺ came he said: God has given you two days better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Adha."],[3826,"When God intends good for a servant, He puts him to work. They said: O Messenger of God, how does He put him to work? He said: He grants him success so that he does a righteous deed before his death."],[3827,"I entered Paradise and heard before me a rustling sound. She said: I am al-Ghumaysa' bt. Milhan."],[3828,"I entered Paradise and there I was by a river flowing, its two banks were tents of pearl. He said: I struck my hand into the mud and it was pungent musk. I said: O Gabriel, what is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar which God has given you."],[3829,"When Abd al-Rahman b. Awf emigrated to the Prophet ﷺ, he established brotherhood between him and Sa'd b. al-Rabi'. Sa'd said to him: I have wealth, so half of it is yours, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them is more pleasing to you and I will divorce her, and when her waiting period is over you may marry her. Abd al-Rahman said to him: May God bless you in your family and your wealth. Show me the market. And he did not return that day until he came with something he had obtained from the market. The Messenger of God ﷺ missed him for some days, then he came to him with a trace of yellow on him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: What is the matter? He said: I have married a woman from the Ansar. He said: What did you give as a dowry for her? He said: A gold date stone - or he said: the weight of a gold date stone. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Hold a wedding feast, even if with one sheep."],[3830,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ swore an oath to stay away from his wives for a month, and he was in an upper room of his. His foot became dislocated, and his companions came to visit him, and he prayed with them sitting while they were standing. Then they came for another prayer, and he sat and they stood, so he gestured to them to sit, and they prayed behind him while sitting. When twenty-nine nights had passed, he came down to them, and it was said: O Messenger of God, only twenty-nine nights have passed! He said: The month is twenty-nine."],[3831,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions used to pray toward Jerusalem. When this verse was revealed: 'Turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque,' a man from the Banu Salimah passed by and called out to them while they were bowing in the dawn prayer toward Jerusalem: Indeed the qiblah has been changed. So they turned as they were, while bowing, toward the qiblah."],[3832,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ took a ring of silver whose stone was also from it."],[3833,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast the month until we would say: He will not break his fast, and he would break his fast the month until we would say: He will not fast."],[3834,"A man may perform deeds of the people of Paradise for a period of his life, but when just before his death he turns and performs deeds of the people of Hell, then he dies and enters Hell. And a man may perform deeds of the people of Hell for a period of his life, but when just before his death he performs deeds of the people of Paradise, then he dies and enters Paradise."],[3835,"Prices rose during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. They said: O Messenger of God, prices have risen, so set prices for us. He said: Indeed, God is the One who sets prices, the Withholder, the Expander, the Provider. I hope to meet God while none of you is seeking a claim against me for blood or property."],[3836,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a rope stretched between two pillars in the mosque. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What is this rope? It was said: O Messenger of God, Hamnah bt. Jahsh prays, and when she becomes exhausted she holds onto it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Let her pray, and when she becomes exhausted let her sit."],[3837,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was of medium height, well-built, neither tall nor short. His hair was neither curly nor straight. He was brown-skinned. When he walked, he leaned forward."],[3838,"Persist in saying: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."],[3839,"The Prophet married Safiyyah and made her manumission her dower. He made the wedding feast for three days. He spread a leather mat that Umm Sulaym brought, and he placed on it dried curds and dates, and he fed the people for three days."],[3840,"Abu Musa asked the Prophet ﷺ for a mount, but found him busy. He swore that he would not give me a mount. He said: But I swear that I will give you a mount. So he gave him a mount."],[3841,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf migrated to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Sa'd b. al-Rabi'. Sa'd b. al-Rabi' said to him: O Abd al-Rahman, I am among the wealthiest of the Ansar, and I will share my wealth with you. I have two wives, so I will divorce one of them for you, and when her waiting period ends, marry her. Abd al-Rahman said to him: May God bless you in your family and wealth, but show me the market. So he showed him. He did not return that day until he had obtained some ghee and dried curds, having profited. He stayed for some days, then he passed by the Prophet ﷺ and the Prophet saw a trace of yellow perfume on him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: What is the matter? He said: I have married, O Messenger of God. He said: Whom? He said: A woman from the Ansar. He said: What did you give as dower? He said: A date-stone's weight—or the weight of a date-stone—of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."],[3842,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited a man who had become like a plucked chick. He said: Did you used to supplicate for anything or ask for it? He said: I used to say: O God, whatever punishment You would inflict on me in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Glory be to God! You cannot bear that, nor are you able to endure it. Why did you not say: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire?"],[3843,"Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. They said: O Messenger of God, we help him when he is oppressed, but how do we help him when he is an oppressor? He said: You prevent him from oppression."],[3844,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the expedition of Tabuk and drew near to Madinah, he said: Indeed, in Madinah there are people who, whatever distance you traveled or valley you crossed, they were with you in it. They said: O Messenger of God, while they are in Madinah? He said: Yes, a valid excuse kept them."],[3845,"You should not be impressed with anyone until you see how his life ends. For a worker may perform righteous deeds for a period of his life—or a span of his time—such that if he died upon them he would enter Paradise, then he turns and performs evil deeds. And a servant may perform evil deeds for a period of his life such that if he died upon them he would enter Hell, then he turns and performs righteous deeds. When God wills good for a servant, He employs him. They said: O Messenger of God, how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success in righteous deeds, then takes him upon that."],[3846,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah — and they had two days on which they played — so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I came to you, and you had two days on which you played, and God has substituted for you two days better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice.\""],[3847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man being supported between his two sons, so he said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"He vowed to walk to the House.\" So he said: \"God is indeed free from need for this man to torment himself.\" Then he ordered him, and he rode."],[3848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque and saw a rope stretched between two pillars, so he said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"It belongs to so-and-so; she prays, and when she becomes tired she clings to it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Let her pray as long as she is able, and when she fears being overcome, let her sleep.\""],[3849,"The prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ was similar, until it was Umar ؓ who extended the morning prayer."],[3850,"\"A people are coming who are more tender of hearts than you.\" Then the Ash'aris arrived, among them Abu Musa ؓ, and they began to recite rajaz verses, saying: \"Tomorrow we shall meet the beloved, Muhammad and his party.\""],[3851,"The Dajjal is blind in one eye, with a thick film over it, and between his eyes is written K F R."],[3852,"None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him, but let him say: \"O God, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when You know death is better for me.\""],[3853,"He used to like the Muhajirun and the Ansar to follow him closely in prayer so they could learn from him."],[3854,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in one of his wives' houses, and a woman among them sent the Prophet ﷺ a bowl of tharid, and she struck it with her hand, so it fell and the bowl broke. The Messenger of God ﷺ began taking the tharid with his hand and putting it back into the bowl, saying: \"Eat; your mother became jealous.\" Then he waited until the other bowl came, took it, and gave it to the owner of the broken bowl."],[3855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had Abu Tayba cupping him, so he ordered two sa's of food for him, and spoke to his masters so they reduced his levy. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best with which you treat yourselves is cupping and sea costus, and do not torture your children by pressing the uvula.\""],[3856,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it ripens. We said: \"What is its ripening?\" He said: \"It turns red.\" Anas said: \"Do you see, if God withholds the palm trees, with what would you make your brother's wealth lawful?\""],[3857,"We did not wish to see the Messenger of God ﷺ praying at night except that we saw him, and we did not wish to see him sleeping at night except that we saw him sleeping."],[3858,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque and saw sputum in its direction—its severity was visibly apparent on him—and he said: “When one of you stands to pray, he is only standing to converse with his Lord—or: his Lord is between him and the qiblah. So if one of you spits, let him spit to his left under his foot, or let him spit like this.” And he spat into the edge of his cloak and rubbed it together."],[3859,"A funeral procession was brought past the Prophet ﷺ, and they praised it with good, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is affirmed.” Then a funeral procession was brought past, and they praised it with evil, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is affirmed. You are God’s witnesses on the earth.”"],[3860,"“Shall I not inform you of the best dwellings of the Ansar?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then the dwellings of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the dwellings of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the dwellings of Banu Sa’idah.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “And in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good.” One of the two said: “And he raised his voice with it.”"],[3861,"Abdullah b. Salam came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I will ask you about three things that none but a prophet knows.” He said: “Ask.” He said: “What is the first matter of the Hour, or the signs of the Hour? What is the first thing the people of Paradise will eat? And what causes a child to incline to its father, and a child to its mother?” He said: “Gabriel informed me of them just now.” He said: “Gabriel?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “That is the enemy of the Jews among the angels.” He said: “As for the first sign of the Hour, it is a fire that comes out from the east and drives the people to the west. As for the first thing the people of Paradise will eat, it is the extra lobe of a fish’s liver. As for what makes a child incline to its father and what makes a child incline to its mother, when the man’s fluid precedes the woman’s fluid, it inclines to its father, and when the woman’s fluid precedes the man’s fluid, it inclines to its mother.” He said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God and that you are the Messenger of God.” Then he said: “O Messenger of God, the Jews are a slanderous people, so hide me from them, then ask them about me—before they know of my Islam—what kind of man I am among them.” A group of them came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: “What kind of man is Abdullah among you?” They said: “Our best and the son of our best, our master and the son of our master, our most learned and the son of our most learned.” He said: “What would you think if Abdullah were to embrace Islam?” They said: “May God protect him from that.” Then Abdullah came out to them and said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” They said: “Our worst and the son of our worst,” and the like. Abdullah said: “O Messenger of God, this is what I feared.”"],[3862,"The Muslims heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: “O Abu Jahl b. Hisham, O Umayyah b. Khalaf, O Utbah b. Rabi’ah, O Shaybah b. Rabi’ah, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” They said: “O Messenger of God, are you calling people who have become corpses?” He said: “You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, but they cannot respond.”"],[3863,"After the prayer had been announced and before he said the takbir, the Prophet ﷺ turned his face toward the people and said: “Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back.” He said: “I would see a man in the row pressing his shoulder against his companion’s shoulder.”"],[3864,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed one night in his room, and the people heard his voice. On the second night, people came and prayed with his prayer, so the Messenger of God ﷺ made it light and then left. When morning came, they said: “O Messenger of God, we prayed with you last night, and we would like you to lengthen your recitation.” He said: “I knew where you were, and I did that deliberately.”"],[3865,"I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I said: “Whose is this?” They said: “For a young man of Quraysh.” I thought that I was him, so I said: “For whom?” It was said: “For Umar b. al-Khattab.”"],[3866,"The Messenger of God ﷺ held a wedding feast for Zaynab and fed the Muslims bread and meat until they were full. Then he went out as he used to do when he married, going to the rooms of the Mothers of the Believers, greeting them and praying for them, and they greeted him and prayed for him. Then he returned and there were two men in the house who had become engrossed in conversation. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw them, he turned back. When the two men saw that, they jumped up in alarm and left. I do not know who told him—I told him or someone else. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ returned."],[3867,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the time of the dawn prayer, and he ordered Bilal to give the call for the dawn prayer, then he made the iqamah and prayed. The next day he delayed it until the sky brightened, then he ordered him and he made the iqamah and prayed. When he finished, he said: “Where is the questioner?” The man stood up, and he said: “Between this and this is the time.”"],[3868,"Did the Messenger of God ﷺ raise his hands in supplication? He said: “Yes. One Friday while he was addressing the people, it was said: ‘O Messenger of God, the rain has stopped, the land has become barren, and wealth has perished. Supplicate to God.’ So he raised his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, and he prayed for rain, and I saw no cloud in the sky. We had not finished the prayer before a young man whose house was near was anxious to return to his family. It lasted for a week. On the second Friday, they said: ‘O Messenger of God, houses have collapsed, travelers have been detained, and wealth has perished.’ The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled, then made a gesture with his hand and parted between them, and said: ‘O God, around us and not upon us.’ He made a parting motion in front of him, and it cleared away from Madinah.”"],[3869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in his house when a man looked in through the door. The Prophet ﷺ pointed a headless arrow toward him, and the man drew back."],[3870,"When the verse 'You will never attain righteousness until you spend from what you love' or 'Who is it that will lend Allah a goodly loan' was revealed, Abu Talha said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my garden in such-and-such a place is for Allah, and if I could have kept it secret I would not have made it public.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Assign it to your relatives,' or he said, 'to your kin.'"],[3871,"I never smelled a scent, musk or ambergris, more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I never touched silk or brocade softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3872,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combining melon and fresh dates."],[3873,"I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water, milk, nabidh, and honey in this cup."],[3874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said, 'Ride it.' He said, 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said, 'Ride it.'"],[3875,"He was asked about the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'I never saw hair more resembling the hair of the Prophet ﷺ than the hair of Qatada.' Qatada rejoiced that day."],[3876,"Some people from 'Urayna came to Madinah and found its climate unsuitable, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them to the camels of the zakat. He said, 'Drink their urine and their milk.' They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, drove off the camels, and apostatized from Islam. The Prophet ﷺ was brought them, and he cut off their hands and feet on opposite sides, branded their eyes, and cast them into the harra."],[3877,"This was before the prescribed punishments were revealed."],[3878,"When he entered upon a sick person, he would say, 'Remove the affliction, Lord of mankind. Heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healer but You. Heal with a healing that leaves no sickness.'"],[3879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman used to begin the prayer with 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'"],[3880,"Strive against the polytheists with your hands and your tongues."],[3881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer. A man came after the Prophet ﷺ had stood, and he hastened his pace. He reached the people breathless - or panting - and when he reached the row he said, 'Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise.' When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said, 'Who was the speaker?' - or 'the one who said these words?' The people remained silent. He said the like again, then said, 'Who is he? For he said nothing wrong' - or 'he said good.' The man said, 'I came, O Messenger of Allah, and hastened my pace. I reached the row breathless - or panting - and I said what I said.' He said, 'I saw twelve angels racing to it, which of them would raise it up.' Then he said, 'When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk calmly. Let him pray what he catches and complete what he missed.'"],[3882,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us hate death. He said: That is not the hatred of death; but when the bringer of good tidings comes to him from Allah with what he is heading towards, he loves to meet Allah and Allah loves to meet him. And the disbeliever — or: the wicked — when he is attended by death, there comes to him what he will encounter, so he hates to meet Allah and Allah hates to meet him."],[3883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Sulaym, and she brought him some ghee and dates. He said: Return your ghee to its waterskin and your dates to their container, for I am fasting. Then he stood and prayed a prayer other than the prescribed one, and we prayed. Then he supplicated for Umm Sulaym and for her household. Umm Sulaym said: I have a small special request. He said: And what is it? She said: Your servant Anas. He said: So he supplicated for me for the good of this world and the Hereafter, and said: O Allah, grant him wealth and children and bless him in them. He said: Indeed I am among the Ansar with the most children. He said: And Ummaynah informed me that from my loins up to the arrival of al-Hajjaj in Basra, one hundred and twenty-some were buried."],[3884,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man from Banu al-Najjar: Become Muslim. He said: I find myself reluctant. He said: Become Muslim, even if you are reluctant."],[3885,"A man would ask the Prophet ﷺ for something of this world, and he would grant it to him. Then before evening came, Islam would become dearer to him than the world and all that is in it."],[3886,"He saw an old man being supported between his two sons. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he vowed to walk. He said: Allah is indeed free of any need for this man to torment himself. Then he ordered him, and he rode."],[3887,"A son of Abu Talhah fell ill, so he went to the mosque, and the boy died. Umm Sulaym set her house in order, prepared his dinner, and said to her family: Let none of you mention to Abu Talhah the death of his son. Abu Talhah returned with some people from his companions among the people of the mosque. He said: What did the boy do? Umm Sulaym said: The best he has ever been. Then she served his dinner, and he and his companions ate. When they left, she attended to what a woman attends to. When it was the last part of the night, she said: Did you not see, O Abu Talhah, the family of so-and-so? They borrowed a loan and enjoyed it, and when it was demanded back from them, it was hard on them! He said: They did not act fairly. She said: Your son was a loan from Allah, and He took him back. So he said: 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return.' Then he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning, and he said: May Allah bless you both in your night. She became pregnant with 'Abd Allah. When she gave birth at night, she disliked to perform tahnik on him until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it. He said: I went with him and some 'ajwah dates to the Prophet ﷺ while he was applying tar to some camels of his and branding them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym gave birth tonight, and she disliked to perform tahnik on him until you perform tahnik on him. He said: Do you have anything with you? I said: Some 'ajwah dates. He took some of those dates, chewed them, gathered his saliva, and put it in his mouth. The baby smacked his lips. He said: The Ansar love dates. I said: Name him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He is 'Abd Allah."],[3888,"When he returned from a journey and saw the walls of Madinah, he would urge his she-camel on, and if he was on a mount, he would make it move, out of love for it."],[3889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and Abu Bakr prayed sitting in his garment, wrapping it around himself, during his illness in which he died."],[3890,"The Prophet ﷺ went out for the prayer and the prayer had been established. A man presented himself to him and spoke to him until the people almost dozed off."],[3891,"The Prophet ﷺ went around to his wives in one night with a single ghusl."],[3892,"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf married for a date-stone — or the weight of a date-stone — of gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Hold a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."],[3893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to dye himself with saffron."],[3894,"He forbade a man from using saffron as a dye."],[3895,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had freed Safiyya, and he made her emancipation her dower."],[3896,"Let none of you wish for death due to some harm that has befallen him. But if he must be someone who wishes, then let him say: O God, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me to You when death is better for me."],[3897,"Let not the believer wish for death due to some harm that has befallen him. But if he must do it, then let him say: O God, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me to You when death is better for me."],[3898,"Qatada asked Anas: Which supplication did the Prophet ﷺ make most often? He said: The supplication the Prophet ﷺ made most often was his saying: O God, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[3899,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: O God, I seek refuge with You from senility, and I seek refuge with You from cowardice, and I seek refuge with You from miserliness, and I seek refuge with You from laziness."],[3900,"No servant believes until I am dearer to him than his family, his wealth, and all people."],[3901,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took a ring of gold and engraved on it: Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and he forbade engraving on his engraving."],[3902,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to be concise and complete."],[3903,"He used to be concise and complete."],[3904,"The Prophet ﷺ said: O Mu'adh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: Give glad tidings to the people that whoever says: There is no god but God, will enter Paradise."],[3905,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[3906,"Take the predawn meal, for in the predawn meal there is blessing."],[3907,"When he entered the privy, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils."],[3908,"I was serving my uncles fadikh made from unripe dates when we heard a caller announcing: Indeed, wine has been forbidden. He said: They said, 'Spill it, O Anas.' He said: By Allah, they did not say, 'Let us wait and ask.' He said: Fadikh was among their wines that day. He said: He mentioned that among those present that day were Abu Talha, Suhayl b. Bayda, and some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3909,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[3910,"Some people of Urayna came to Madinah and found its climate disagreeable. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: If you wish, go out to the camels of the sadaqa and drink of their urine and milk. He said: They did so and recovered. Then they turned upon the herdsmen, killed them, and drove off the small herd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and disbelieved after their Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent in pursuit of them. They were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet, put out their eyes, and left them in the lava field until they died."],[3911,"I looked for the Prophet ﷺ one day and was told: He is at the tailor of the family of al-Muttalib; he invited him and he accepted. I went until I entered upon him, and there the tailor had prepared food containing gourd. I began taking the gourd and placing it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because I knew he loved it."],[3912,"The likeness of my community is that of a river in which one bathes five times; what dirt would remain on him? He rises to perform ablution and washes his hands, and every sin his hands have touched falls away. He rinses his mouth, and every sin his tongue has uttered falls away. Then he washes his face, and every sin his eyes have looked upon falls away. Then he wipes his head, and every sin his ears have heard falls away. Then he washes his feet, and every sin his feet have walked toward falls away."],[3913,"There will be in my community people who pass through the religion as an arrow passes through the game. They are the worst of those killed under the sky. Glad tidings to the one who kills them, and glad tidings to the one they kill, and glad tidings to the one they kill."],[3914,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the believer. He said: The one whose neighbor feels safe from him and does not fear his harmful acts. The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand people are safe."],[3915,"Shall I not inform you of the worst among you? They said: Yes. He said: The worst among you is the one whose evil is feared and whose good is not hoped for. The best among you is the one whose good is hoped for and whose evil is not feared."],[3916,"Three things will not cease in my community until the Hour comes: wailing, boasting about lineages, and attributing rain to the stars."],[3917,"Three things will never cease in my community."],[3918,"The Muhajirun and the Ansar were digging the trench around Madinah, carrying the earth on their backs, and saying: 'We are those who pledged allegiance to Muhammad upon Islam as long as we remain forever.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, answering them: 'O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so bless the Ansar and the Muhajirun.' He said: And they would be brought two cupped hands full of barley, and it would be prepared for them with rancid fat, which was repulsive in the throat and had an offensive smell, and it was placed before the people."],[3919,"That when he entered the privy, he would say: 'I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils.'"],[3920,"Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, the like of it."],[3921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent seventy men for a purpose, called the Qurra'. Two tribes of Banu Sulaym, Ri'l and Dhakwan, intercepted them at a well called Bi'r Ma'unah. The people said: 'By Allah, we did not intend you; we are only chosen for a purpose of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' But they killed them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated against them for a month in the dawn prayer, and that was the beginning of the Qunut, and we had not used to perform Qunut."],[3922,"I and Thabit entered upon Anas, and Thabit said to him: 'O Abu Hamzah, I have fallen ill.' Anas b. Malik said to him: 'Shall I not perform ruqyah for you with the ruqyah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes, O Allah, Lord of the people, remove the affliction, heal, You are the Healer, there is no healer but You, with a healing that leaves no sickness.'"],[3923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated his marriage with Zaynab bt. Jahsh and provided food for her, and held a walimah for her with bread and meat. He said: I was sent, and the food was covered, and I invited people. A group would come and eat, then leave. I kept inviting until I found no one left to invite. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I find no one left to invite.' He said: 'Then remove your food.' And Zaynab was sitting in a side of the house. He said: She was a woman who had been given beauty. Three men remained in the house conversing. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ went out and headed toward A'ishah's room, and said: 'Peace be upon you, O people of the house, and the mercy of Allah. How are you this morning?' She replied: 'And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah. How have you found your wife? May Allah bless you in them.' He said: Then he visited the rooms of all his wives, saying to them what he had said to A'ishah, and they replied as A'ishah had replied. Then the Prophet of Allah returned, and the three men were still conversing in the house. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was extremely shy, so he went toward A'ishah's room. I do not know whether I informed him or he was informed that the people had left, so he returned. When he placed one of his feet on the threshold of the door and the other outside it, he let down a curtain between me and him, and the verse of hijab was revealed."],[3924,"A man was a Christian and accepted Islam during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he recited al-Baqarah and Al 'Imran. He said: He used to write for the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. He said: Then he reverted to Christianity and would say: 'Muhammad knows nothing except what I used to write for him.' So Allah caused him to die, and they buried him. In the morning, the earth had ejected him. They said: 'This is the work of Muhammad and his companions; it is only because they were not pleased with his religion that they dug up our companion.' So they went to him. He said: They dug for him and made it deeper, but in the morning the earth had ejected him. They said: 'This is the work of Muhammad and his companions; they dug up our companion and threw him out.' He said: Then they dug for him and made it as deep as they could in the earth, but in the morning the earth had ejected him. They knew that it was not from people but from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so they cast him aside."],[3925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the prayer, and a man intercepted him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour come?' He said: 'What have you prepared for it?' He said: 'Nothing except that I love Allah and His Messenger.' He said: 'Then you will be with those you love.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: 'Where is the one who asked about the Hour?' He said: He came and stood. He said: 'O this one.' Anas said: 'And a boy from Daws, he and I were the same age.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If this boy lives a long life, he will not die of old age until the Hour comes.'"],[3926,"On the day of Uhud, some people fled from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while Abu Talhah was in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shielding him with a shield that he had. He said: Abu Talhah was an archer with a strong draw, and he broke two or three bows that day. A man would pass by a quiver containing arrows, and he would say: 'Scatter them for Abu Talhah.' He said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ would raise his head to look at the people, and Abu Talhah would say: 'O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, do not raise your head lest an arrow from the people's arrows strike you. My neck is before your neck.' I saw A'ishah bt. Abi Bakr and Umm Sulaym, and they were tucking up their garments so that I saw the anklets on their calves, carrying water on their backs, then pouring it into the mouths of the people, then returning to fill them again, then coming and pouring it into the mouths of the people. The sword fell from Abu Talhah's hand from drowsiness, either twice or three times."],[3927,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[3928,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[3929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out to us for three days. The prayer was called, and Abu Bakr went to step forward, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'With the curtain,' and raised it. When the whiteness of the Messenger of Allah's face appeared to us, we had never seen a sight more pleasing to us than the face of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ when it appeared to us. He said: The Prophet ﷺ signaled to Abu Bakr to step forward. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ let down the curtain, and we could not reach him until he died."],[3930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to dye his skin with saffron."],[3931,"I heard Anas b. Malik mention the Prophet's ﷺ marriage to Safiyyah. Thabit said: What did he give her as dower? Anas said: He gave her herself as dower—he manumitted her and married her."],[3932,"He who has three children die before they reach the age of accountability, Allah will admit him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them."],[3933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two white sheep with black markings. Anas said: So I sacrifice two sheep."],[3934,"A drought befell the people of Madinah in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The people stood up to him on a Friday while he was on the pulpit delivering a sermon, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen and rains have been withheld, so supplicate Allah to send us rain. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands and prayed for rain. He said: Then we were rained upon, and we did not cease to be rained upon until the following Friday. He said: The people stood up to him while he was on the pulpit and said: O Messenger of Allah, the riders have been cut off and the buildings have collapsed, so supplicate Allah to remove it from us. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, then raised his hands and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: Then it shifted, and Madinah became like a crown, while around it there was rain."],[3935,"Whoever wears it in this world will never wear it in the Hereafter."],[3936,"When he entered the privy, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils."],[3937,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer when he came from Khaybar in the darkness before dawn, then he mounted and said: Allah is greatest, Khaybar is destroyed. When we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. He said: They came out running through the streets, saying: Muhammad and the army. Hammad said: that is, the army. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared, killed their fighting men, and took their offspring captive. He said: Safiyyah belonged to Dihyah al-Kalbi, then afterward she became the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ, and he married her and made her dower her manumission. Abd al-Aziz said to Thabit: O Abu Muhammad, did you ask Anas what he gave her as dower? And he said to you: He gave her herself as dower? Thabit smiled."],[3938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would make the prayer brief yet complete."],[3939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade men from dyeing with saffron."],[3940,"Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[3941,"The Prophet ﷺ adopted a silver signet ring and engraved on it 'Muhammad, Messenger of Allah,' and said to the people: I have adopted a signet ring and its engraving is Muhammad, so let no one engrave with its engraving."],[3942,"The Prophet ﷺ seated Mu'adh b. Jabal behind him and said: “O Mu'adh,” raising his voice. He said: “At your service, Messenger of Allah.” Then he called him a second time, then he called him a third time, raising his voice. He said: “At your service, Messenger of Allah.” Then he ﷺ said: “Whoever does not associate partners (with Allah), for him is Paradise.”"],[3943,"The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and my nation will split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except the great majority."],[3944,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Glad tidings for him, if he was not a ‘arif (a chief or overseer).”"],[3945,"When he entered the privy, he said: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils.”"],[3946,"“O Mu'adh,” he said. He said: “At your service, Messenger of Allah.” Then he said: “O Mu'adh,” he said: “At your service, Messenger of Allah,” three times—each time saying: “At your service, Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Give glad tidings to the people: whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah’ will enter Paradise.”"],[3947,"Some people will come to my pool and be driven away before reaching me. I will say: “O Lord, my companions!” It will be said: “You do not know what they innovated after you.”"],[3948,"I have had a ring made, so let no one engrave upon an inscription like its inscription."],[3949,"The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and my nation will split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except the great majority."],[3950,"There will be in this nation sinking of the earth, metamorphosis, earthquakes, and casting of stones."],[3951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: “Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.”"],[3952,"Prophethood and messengership have come to an end, so the people grieved. He said: “Glad tidings remain, and they are part of prophethood.”"],[3953,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah: “O best of creation!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “That is Ibrahim ﷺ .”"],[3954,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O best of creation. He said: That is Abraham ﷺ."],[3955,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: O best of creation. He said: That is Abraham ﷺ ."],[3956,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was among us one day, he dozed off briefly, then raised his head smiling. I said: What made you laugh, O Messenger of God? He said: A surah was just revealed to me, and he recited: In the name of God, the Compassionate, the Merciful. Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar. So pray to your Lord and sacrifice. Indeed, your enemy is the one cut off. Then he said: Do you know what al-Kawthar is? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: It is a river my Lord promised me, abundant good. It is a pool at which my nation will come on the Day of Resurrection. Its vessels are as numerous as the stars of the sky. Then a servant from among them will be snatched away, and I will say: My Lord, he is of my nation. He will say: You do not know what they innovated after you."],[3957,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer one day. When he finished the prayer, he turned to face us and said: O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, prostration, or standing. I see you from in front of me and from behind me. Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw, you would laugh little and weep much. They said: What did you see, O Messenger of God? He said: I saw Paradise and the Fire."],[3958,"Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise promised to me by my Lord, Mighty and Majestic."],[3959,"I asked Anas about drinking from vessels. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade al-muzaffat, and he said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[3960,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed on the ground for the obligatory prayer while seated, and he sat during the voluntary prayer on the ground and gestured."],[3961,"I asked Anas b. Malik about praying after Asr. He said: Umar b. al-Khattab used to strike people for praying after Asr. He said: We used to pray two rak'as after sunset before the Maghrib prayer during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. I said: Was the Messenger of God ﷺ the one who prayed them? He said: He used to see us praying them, and he neither commanded us nor forbade us."],[3962,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said one day, after finishing the prayer: By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw, you would laugh little and weep much. We said: O Messenger of God, what did you see? He said: I saw Paradise and the Fire."],[3963,"The Prophet ﷺ came and entered a garden. Then someone came and knocked on the door. He said: O Anas, get up and open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and give him glad tidings of the caliphate after me. I said: O Messenger of God, shall I tell him? He said: Tell him. It was Abu Bakr. I said: Rejoice in Paradise and rejoice in the caliphate after the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then someone came and knocked on the door. He said: O Anas, get up and open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and give him glad tidings of the caliphate after Abu Bakr. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, shall I tell him? He said: Tell him? He said: I went out and it was Umar. He said: I said to him: Rejoice in Paradise and rejoice in the caliphate after Abu Bakr. Then someone came and knocked on the door. He said: O Anas, get up and open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and give him glad tidings of the caliphate after Umar, and that he will be killed. He said: I went out and it was Uthman. He said: I said to him: Rejoice in Paradise and in the caliphate after Umar, and that you will be killed. He said: He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, why? By God, I have not sung, nor wished, nor touched my private part since I pledged allegiance to you. He said: That is it, O Uthman."],[3964,"I am the first to intercede for Paradise, and I am the prophet with the most followers."],[3965,"I am your imam, so do not hasten before me in bowing or prostration, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me."],[3966,"People will not cease asking, 'What is this? What is that?' until they say, 'Allah created the creation, so who created Allah?'"],[3967,"Uthman b. Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned something similar."],[3968,"O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostrating, nor in standing, nor in sitting, nor in departing, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw, you would laugh little and weep much. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what did you see?' He said, 'I saw Paradise and the Fire.'"],[3969,"I am the first to knock on the gate of Paradise."],[3970,"I am your imam, so do not rush me in bowing or in prostrating, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me."],[3971,"I asked Anas b. Malik about drinks, and he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade pitch-coated vessels, and he said, \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\"' He said, 'I said to him, \"You have spoken the truth; intoxication is unlawful. I only drink a sip or two after food.\"' He said, 'He said to me, \"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful.\"' He said, 'Then wine was made unlawful, and it is from grapes, dates, honey, wheat, barley, and corn, and whatever you ferment from that is wine.'"],[3972,"I am the first of people to intercede for Paradise, and I am the prophet with the most followers."],[3973,"I am the first intercessor in Paradise."],[3974,"Allah said, 'Your community will not cease asking, \"What is this? What is that?\" until they say, \"This Allah created everything, so who created Allah?\"'"],[3975,"No prophet among the prophets was believed as I have been believed. Indeed, among the prophets is a prophet whom only one man of his community believed."],[3976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a drink in Yemen called al-bit' and al-mizr, and he said, 'Whatever intoxicates is unlawful.'"],[3977,"No prophet was believed as I have been believed. Indeed, among the prophets is one who will come on the Day of Resurrection with no one from his community but one man."],[3978,"I am the first of people to intercede for Paradise, and I am the one with the most followers."],[3979,"Ribat for a day in the path of God is better than one of you standing in prayer among his family for a thousand years, fasting its days and standing in prayer its nights. The year is three hundred and sixty days, and the day is a thousand years."],[3980,"The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed one day, or smiled, and said to his companions: 'Will you not ask me what I laughed about?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, what did you laugh about?' He said: 'I marvel at the dispute of a servant with his Lord on the Day of Resurrection. He says: \"O Lord, did You not promise me that You would not wrong me?\" He says: \"Yes.\" He says: \"Then I will not accept any witness against me except from myself.\" So He says: \"Is it not enough that I am a witness, and the noble recording angels are witnesses?\" He said: Then he repeats the words several times. He said: Then his mouth is sealed, and his limbs speak of what he used to do. He said: Then he says: \"Away with you and far off! It was on your behalf that I used to argue.\""],[3981,"The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection is prayer. If it is complete, the rest of his deeds are complete, and if it is deficient, it will be said: 'Look, does he have any voluntary prayers?' If he has voluntary prayers, He will say: 'Complete his obligatory prayer with them.'"],[3982,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ and he laughed, then said: 'Do you know what I am laughing about?' He said: We said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'From the address of a servant to his Lord. He says: \"O Lord, did You not protect me from wrongdoing?\" He said: He, Mighty and Majestic, says: \"Yes.\" He says: \"Then I will not accept against myself any witness except from me.\" He said: Then He says: \"Your own self suffices as a witness against you, and the noble recording angels as witnesses.\" He said: Then his mouth is sealed, and his limbs are told: \"Speak.\" He said: Then they speak of his deeds. Then he said: 'He is released from speech, and he says: \"Away with you and far off! It was on your behalf that I used to strive.\""],[3983,"He would pass by the door of Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet, at the time of the dawn prayer for six months, and say: 'The prayer, O people of the house,' three times. 'God only desires to remove impurity from you, O people of the house, and to purify you with a thorough purification.'"],[3984,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Shadhan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd, from Anas, that the Prophet ﷺ would pass by the house of Fatimah for six months, and he mentioned something similar."],[3985,"The king of Rome sent a gift to the Prophet ﷺ of a fur garment of fine silk, and the Prophet ﷺ wore it, and it was as if I could see its sleeves swaying. His companions said: 'O Messenger of God, was this sent down to you from heaven?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, a handkerchief from the handkerchiefs of Sa'd b. Mu'adh in Paradise is better than this.' Then he sent it to Ja'far, and Ja'far wore it. He said: 'I did not send it to you for you to wear it.' He said: 'What should I do with it?' He said: 'Send it to your brother the Negus.'"],[3986,"When al-Husayn was killed, his head was brought to Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad, and he began tapping with his stick on his front teeth, and said: 'His teeth were indeed beautiful.' I said: 'By God, I will indeed grieve you.' He said: 'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing the place where your stick is on his mouth.'"],[3987,"A young girl among the young girls of the Muslims would come and take the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would not pull his hand from her hand until she took him wherever she wished."],[3988,"The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a troop. When he met with the Prophet ﷺ, he would kneel before him, and say: 'My self be a ransom for your self, and my face be a protection for your face.'"],[3989,"I attended the wedding feast of two of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not feed us bread or meat. He said: I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Hays.'"],[3990,"None of you will enter Paradise by his deeds. He said: We said: Not even you? He said: Not even me, unless my Lord envelops me in mercy from Him and grace."],[3991,"Zakariyya b. Yahya narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd b. Jud'an, from Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ, a similar report to this hadith."],[3992,"Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: Every weak, oppressed person with two worn garments, who is not paid attention to; if he swore by Allah, He would fulfill it. Among them is al-Bara' b. Malik."],[3993,"The example of the five prayers is like a sweet flowing river, or a deep one, at the door of one of you, from which he bathes five times every day. What dirt remains on him?"],[3994,"I am the first to take hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise and rattle it. Anas said: It is as if I am looking at him turning it with his hand."],[3995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Uhud when they pressed upon him, while he was among seven of the Ansar and two men other than them: Who will repel them from us and be my companion in Paradise? A man from the Ansar stood up and fought until he was killed. Then he said the like of that, and another man stood up and fought until he was killed. He kept saying that until the seven were killed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We have not been fair to our companions."],[3996,"The voice of Abu Talha in the army is better than a detachment."],[3997,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I came upon men whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are the preachers of your community who command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book. Will they not understand?"],[3998,"Abu Talha, when he was in an army, would scatter his quiver before him and say: My life be your ransom, and my face be your protection. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The voice of Abu Talha in the army is better than a detachment."],[3999,"When news of the killing of the people of Bi'r Ma'una came to the Prophet ﷺ, he stood in the morning prayer, in the last rak'a after bowing, and said: O Allah, curse Ri'l, Dhakwan, and 'Usayya, for they disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. He said it three times, then said the takbir, then prostrated. I memorized that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for thirty days, he would do it."],[4000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the polytheists pressed upon him on the day of Uhud, said: Who will repel them from us and be my companion in Paradise? A man from the Ansar stood up and fought until he was killed. Then another stood to repel them until seven were killed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We have not been fair to our companions."],[4001,"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I passed by a people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: Who are these? He said: These are preachers from the people of this world, among those who used to command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book. Will they not understand?"],[4002,"It is as if I am looking at the Prophet ﷺ while he is saying: I take hold of the door ring and rattle it."],[4003,"Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr intended to kill the 'arif of the Ansar. Anas b. Malik entered upon him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Enjoin good treatment of the Ansar and kindness; accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrong-doers. He said: Mus'ab came down from his couch onto his carpet and pressed his skin, or his cheek, against it—or he said: he rolled on it—and said: The command of the Prophet ﷺ is upon the head and the two eyes, the command of the Prophet ﷺ is upon the head and the two eyes. So he left him."],[4004,"The sky rained hail. Abu Talhah said to us, while we were boys: Hand me some of that hail, O Anas. He began eating it while fasting. I said: Are you not fasting? He said: Yes, but this is not food or drink; it is only a blessing from the sky with which we cleanse our bellies. Anas said: I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: Take from your uncle."],[4005,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon the slain of Bi'r Ma'unah, he stood in the morning prayer. He said: When he raised his head from the last rak'ah, he stood upright, then said: O Allah, curse Ri'l, Dhakwan, and 'Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger—three times. Then he said the takbir and prostrated. He said: I memorized that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it for thirty days."],[4006,"Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4007,"Whoever I am mentioned in his presence, let him invoke blessings upon me, for whoever invokes blessings upon me once, Allah will invoke blessings upon him tenfold."],[4008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had supplications he never abandoned. He used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, incapacity and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the burden of debt, and the oppression of men."],[4009,"I said to Anas: Tell me about the timing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer. He said: He used to pray Zuhr at the sun's decline, pray 'Asr between your two prayers—the first and 'Asr—pray Maghrib at sunset, pray 'Isha at the disappearance of the twilight, and pray the morning prayer at dawn when sight begins. All between that is a time—or he said: a prayer."],[4010,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated marriage with a woman. He sent me, and I invited men to the food."],[4011,"The people of the Fire will be presented on the Day of Resurrection in rows. The believers will pass by them. A man from the people of the Fire will see a man from the believers whom he knew in this world and say: O so-and-so, do you not remember the day you sought my help in such-and-such a need? He said: The believer will remember and recognize him, and will intercede for him with his Lord, and He will grant his intercession for him."],[4012,"We would not bend our backs until we saw the Prophet ﷺ prostrating."],[4013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a coat of mail pledged with a Jew, and he did not find anything to redeem it until he died."],[4014,"Woe to the slave from the master, woe to the master from the slave, woe to the rich from the poor, woe to the poor from the rich, woe to the strong from the weak, woe to the weak from the strong."],[4015,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon a man to visit him, and behold he had become like a fledgling from the severity of illness. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Would you not supplicate? Would you not ask?\" He said, \"Yes, I used to say: O God, whatever You would punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Then you would not be able to bear that. Why did you not say: 'Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire'?\" So he said it, and he was healed."],[4016,"When a man marries a woman, if she is a virgin, he stays with her for seven days; and if she is previously married, he stays with her for three days, then he divides after that."],[4017,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he saw the wind, became alarmed and said, \"O God, I ask You for the good of what it has been commanded with. O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what it has been sent with.\""],[4018,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man moving pebbles while he was in prayer. When he finished, he said to the man, \"That is your share of your prayer.\""],[4019,"The Messenger of God ﷺ traveled during Ramadan and he fasted and broke his fast. His companions fasted and broke their fast, and none of them blamed the other."],[4020,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would be invited to barley bread and rancid fat and he would accept. He had a coat of mail pawned with a Jew, and he could not find anything to redeem it until he died."],[4021,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon a man to visit him and said, \"Do you desire anything? Do you desire cake?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So they sought it for him."],[4022,"A boy of ours was martyred on the day of Uhud, and a stone was found tied to his stomach from hunger. His mother wiped the dust from his face and said, \"May Paradise be pleasant for you, my son.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What makes you know? Perhaps he used to speak about what did not concern him and withhold that which did not harm him.\""],[4023,"Whoever builds a mosque for God like the scrape of a sandgrouse, God builds for him a house in Paradise."],[4024,"No decree is decreed for the believer but it is good for him."],[4025,"He used to use the tooth-stick with the leftover water of his ablution."],[4026,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out one night, intending to tell us about the Night of Decree, and"],[4027,"Anas b. Malik recited this verse: “Indeed, the hours of the night are more effective for concurrence [of heart and tongue] and more suitable for speech” (Q 73:6). A man said to him: “We only recite it as: ‘and more upright in speech’ (wa-aqwamu qīlā).” He said: “Aqwam, aṣwab, and ahyā, and the like of this, are one [and the same].”"],[4028,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established a pact of brotherhood between the Quraysh and the Anṣār in my house in Madinah."],[4029,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established a pact of brotherhood between the Quraysh and the Anṣār in my house in Madinah."],[4030,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4031,"I asked him about the qunūt: before the bowing or after the bowing? He said: Before the bowing. He said: I said: But some people claim that the Messenger of God ﷺ performed the qunūt after the bowing. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ only performed the qunūt for a month, supplicating against people who had killed some of his companions called the reciters."],[4032,"I asked Anas b. Malik: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ declare Madinah inviolable? He said: Yes, it is inviolable. God and His Messenger made it inviolable: its herbage is not to be cut. Whoever does that, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people."],[4033,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established a pact of brotherhood between the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār in the house of Anas in Madinah."],[4034,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: O you with the two ears."],[4035,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in a single garment, placing its two ends on opposite sides."],[4036,"I asked Anas b. Malik about the qunūt. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ performed the qunūt for a month after the bowing. One day he had sent seventy men to a people among the polytheists. He said: And a people among the polytheists had a treaty between them and the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the polytheists with whom the Messenger of God ﷺ had a treaty killed them. So the Messenger of God ﷺ performed the qunūt for a month, supplicating against them."],[4037,"We were in a house when the Messenger of God ﷺ stood at the door of the house and said: The imams are from Quraysh. I have a right over you, and they have the like of it over you, as long as they do three things: when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; when they judge, they are just; and when they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people."],[4038,"The Messenger of God came to us while we were in the house of a man from the Ansar, and he took hold of the two doorposts, then said: \"The leaders are from Quraysh. I have a right over you, and they have the like of that: when they judge, they are just; when mercy is asked of them, they show mercy; and when they make a covenant, they fulfill it. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people.\""],[4039,"\"There is no god but God\" protects the servant from God's wrath as long as they do not prefer the transaction of their worldly life over their religion. If they do that, then say, \"There is no god but God,\" God says: \"You have lied.\""],[4040,"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."],[4041,"There is no day except that the one after it is worse than it. We heard that from your Prophet ﷺ."],[4042,"We complained to Anas about what we were encountering from al-Hajjaj. He said: \"Be patient, for no year, or day, will come upon you except that the one after it is worse than it, until you meet your Lord. I heard it from your Prophet ﷺ.\""],[4043,"Let none of you purchase against the purchase of his brother, and let him not propose against the proposal of his brother."],[4044,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade sleeping before the evening prayer and conversing after it."],[4045,"This community will continue to be in good as long as when it speaks it is truthful, when it judges it is just, and when mercy is asked of it it shows mercy."],[4046,"I said to Anas: \"How will people be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection?\" He said: \"They will be resurrected while the sky is drizzling upon them.\""],[4047,"He used to turn away to his right."],[4048,"The Messenger of God ﷺ turned away from the prayer to his right."],[4049,"We were riding behind Abu Talhah, and his knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they were both raising their voices together with the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah."],[4050,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about wine being made into vinegar. He said: No."],[4051,"Muʿādh said: O Messenger of God, what do you think if we have rulers who do not follow your Sunnah and do not adopt your command—what do you command me regarding their affair? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: There is no obedience to the one who does not obey God."],[4052,"Indeed, muzzāt is forbidden: a mixture of unripe and ripe dates."],[4053,"Indeed, muzzāt is forbidden: a mixture of unripe and ripe dates."],[4054,"The boldest of people in questioning the Messenger of God ﷺ were the Bedouins. A Bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of God, when is the Hour? He did not answer him until he came to the mosque and prayed, and he made the prayer light. Then he turned to the Bedouin and said: Where is the one asking about the Hour? Saʿd passed by, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: If this one lives long enough to consume his lifespan, not an eye among you will remain blinking."],[4055,"One hundred years will not come from the Hijrah while an eye among you blinks."],[4056,"Abū Ṭalḥah asked the Prophet ﷺ about orphans who inherited wine. He said: Pour it out. He said: Shall I not make it vinegar? He said: No."],[4057,"The Prophet ﷺ had a bird, and he said: O God, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to eat with me from this bird. Abū Bakr came, and he sent him back. Then ʿUmar came, and he sent him back. Then ʿAlī came, and he permitted him."],[4058,"I asked Anas b. Mālik, saying: Tell me something you understood from the Messenger of God ﷺ: where did he pray ẓuhr on the Day of Tarwiyah? He said: At Minā. I said: Where did he pray ʿaṣr on the Day of Nafr? He said: At al-Abṭaḥ. Then he said: Do as your rulers do."],[4059,"Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ when he returned from Khaybar was: O God, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, incapacity and laziness, cowardice and miserliness, the burden of debt and the domination of men."],[4060,"Before the emergence of the Dajjāl there will be more than seventy Dajjāls."],[4061,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ in a funeral procession, and he saw some women. He said: Will you carry him? He said: Will you bury him? They said: No. He said: Then return, burdened with sin, not rewarded."],[4062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunya of a vegetable I had gathered."],[4063,"Regarding His saying: 'So by your Lord, We will surely question them all about what they used to do' (Q 15:92), he said: about [the testimony that] there is no god but Allah."],[4064,"He used to say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, old age, cowardice, miserliness, the torment of the grave, and the evil of the false messiah.'"],[4065,"Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he invoked Allah's mercy on one of them and left the other. He said: 'This one praised Allah, while this one did not praise Allah.'"],[4066,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4067,"Zahmawayh narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[4068,"He said: 'Who will see what Abu Jahl has done?' Abd Allah b. Mas'ud went and found him struck by the two sons of Afra' until he became still. He said: 'O enemy of Allah, are you Abu Jahl?' He replied: 'Is there any [shame] greater than a man killed by his own people, or whom you have killed?'"],[4069,"There was a man called Anjasha who was driving the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'O Anjasha, drive gently with the glass vessels.'"],[4070,"He forbade mixing unripe dates with ripe dates."],[4071,"Among you are people who worship until they impress people and are impressed with themselves. They pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game."],[4072,"On the night he was taken on the Isra', the Prophet ﷺ passed by Musa while he was praying in his grave."],[4073,"The Prophet ﷺ gouged their eyes only because they had gouged the eyes of the shepherds."],[4074,"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I saw people whose tongues were being cut with scissors of fire—or he said: of iron. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: Orators from your community."],[4075,"Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4076,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a month before his death, and he wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[4077,"When the call to prayer is given, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered."],[4078,"Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he responded to one of them—or he said: he blessed one of them—and left the other. It was said: Two men sneezed, and you responded to one—or you blessed one—and left the other? He said: This one praised Allah, and this one did not praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic."],[4079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr: Who will see what Abu Jahl has done? Ibn Mas'ud went and found that the two sons of 'Afra' had struck him until he became cold. He said: Are you Abu Jahl? He said: Is there anyone above a man you have killed? Sulayman said: Or his people killed him."],[4080,"Umm Sulaym was with the wives of the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and the Prophet ﷺ came upon them while a driver was driving them. He said: O Anjasha, gently, drive the glass vessels slowly."],[4081,"Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[4083,"He forbade combining unripe dates and ripe dates."],[4084,"A man would assign to the Prophet ﷺ some of his palm trees as charity, until Qurayzah and al-Nadir were conquered. After that, the Messenger of Allah began to return them. My family ordered me to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him for what they had given him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had given them to Umm Ayman. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave them to me. Then Umm Ayman came and twisted the garment around my neck, saying: No, by the One besides whom there is no god, he will not give them to you when he has given them to me. The Prophet ﷺ was saying: You will have such and such, and such and such. I think he said: And she was saying: No, by Allah, until he gave her ten times its like."],[4085,"A man would assign to the Prophet ﷺ palm trees from his land, until Qurayzah and al-Nadir were conquered for him. After that, he began to return what he had been given. Anas said: My family ordered me to go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him for what he had given or part of it. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ had given it to Umm Ayman. I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave them to me. Umm Ayman came and put the garment around my neck and said: By Allah, he will not give them to you when he has given them to me. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: O Umm Ayman, leave him, and you will have such and such. She said: No, by the One besides whom there is no god. He kept saying: Such and such, until he gave her ten times its like, or close to ten times its like."],[4086,"I saw Paradise and the Fire in this garden, and I have never seen like today in good and evil."],[4087,"One of us would keep his back straight in prayer behind the Prophet ﷺ until the Prophet ﷺ was firmly prostrating, or he said: on the ground, then he would prostrate at that moment."],[4088,"It was said: O Prophet of God, would that you go to Abd Allah b. Ubayy. The Prophet ﷺ went off and rode a donkey, and the Muslims went off walking, and it was salty ground. When the Prophet ﷺ came to him, he said: Away from me, for by God, the stench of your donkey has harmed me. A man of the Ansar said: By God, the donkey of the Messenger of God ﷺ has a better smell than you. A man of his people became angry on behalf of Abd Allah, and the companions of each of them became angry. So there was among them striking with palm branches, hands, and sandals. It reached us that this was revealed about them: And if two factions of the believers fight, make peace between them."],[4089,"On the night he was taken on the night journey, the Prophet ﷺ passed by Musa while he was praying in his grave. Anas said: He mentioned that he was carried on al-Buraq and he tethered the beast, or he said: the horse. Abu Bakr said: Describe it to me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: .... and he mentioned a word, then he said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God, and Abu Bakr had already seen it."],[4090,"I passed by Musa while he was praying in his grave."],[4091,"Whoever performs ablution has done well, and excellent it is; and whoever performs the full bath, the full bath is better."],[4092,"And from the late afternoon until sunset is dearer to me than that I free eight of the descendants of Ismail, all of them Muslims."],[4093,"When he related this hadith to us, Anas used to say to us: By God, it is not what you and your companions do, meaning one of you sits and you gather around him and he delivers a sermon. They would only, when they prayed the dawn prayer, sit in circles, circle by circle, reciting the Quran and learning the obligatory duties and the sunnahs."],[4094,"Gabriel came to me with a white mirror in which there was a black spot. He said: What is this? He said: This is Friday, and in it there is an hour."],[4095,"Children are the servants of the people of Paradise."],[4096,"We were sitting with the Prophet of God ﷺ, perhaps he said: sixty men, and he would relate a hadith to us, then he would enter for his need, and we would review it among ourselves, this one then this one, and we would get up as if it had been planted in our hearts."],[4097,"Among those of my brethren the prophets who passed away were eight thousand prophets, then there was Isa son of Maryam, then I was."],[4098,"Whoever helps his brother in his need and is kind to him, it is incumbent upon God to serve him from the servants of Paradise."],[4099,"The sea was split for the Children of Israel on the day of Ashura."],[4100,"No Muslim attends the funeral of a Muslim person but that he has a qirat of reward; and if he sits until it is completed, he has two qirats of reward, each qirat like Uhud."],[4101,"Abu Musa sat in his house, and people gathered to him, and he began to recite the Quran to them. He said: A man came to the Messenger of God and said, O Messenger of God, shall I not amaze you about Abu Musa, that he sat in a house and people gathered to him, and he began to recite the Quran to them? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, Can you seat me where none of them can see me? He said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ went out, and the man seated him where none of them saw him, and he heard Abu Musa's recitation. He said: He said, He recites upon one of the flutes of the family of David."],[4102,"Whoever is pleased to have his lifespan extended and his provision increased, let him maintain his ties of kinship."],[4103,"Three traits, whoever has them is a hypocrite even if he fasts, prays, performs Hajj and Umrah, and says, I am a Muslim: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays."],[4104,"I said, O Abu Hamza, there are people who testify against us of disbelief and polytheism. Anas said, Those are the worst of creation and creatures. He said, And they deny the Pool. He said, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, I have a Pool whose width is like that between Ayla and the Kaaba—or he said, Sanaa—whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, in it vessels like the number of the stars of the sky, fed by two spouts from Paradise. Whoever denies it will not drink from it."],[4105,"Between the servant and disbelief and polytheism is the abandonment of prayer; so if he abandons prayer, he has disbelieved."],[4106,"I asked my Lord regarding the heedless ones among the offspring of mankind that He not punish them, and He granted them to me."],[4107,"Salih b. Malik narrated to us, Abdul Aziz b. al-Majishun narrated to us, something similar."],[4108,"If a stone like seven pregnant camels with their fat and offspring were cast into Hell, it would fall for seventy years and not reach its bottom."],[4109,"Charity and maintaining ties of kinship: God increases lifespan through them, averts an evil death, and through them God repels the disliked and the feared."],[4110,"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community."],[4111,"Indeed, Allah bestowed favor upon the people of Arafat, boasting of them to the angels, saying, “O My angels, look at My servants—disheveled and dusty—they came striking toward Me from every deep valley. I call you to witness that I have answered their supplications, interceded for their desires, granted their wrongdoers to their doers of good, and given their doers of good all that they asked of Me, except for the retaliatory claims that are between them. Then when the people depart to Muzdalifah and stand and return in desire and request to Allah, He says, ‘O My angels, My servants stood and returned in desire and request. I call you to witness that I have answered their supplications, interceded for their desires, granted their wrongdoers to their doers of good, given their doers of good all that they asked of Me, and I have taken responsibility for them regarding the retaliatory claims that are between them.’”"],[4112,"Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, so beware that Allah should seek you for anything of His protection."],[4113,"O people, indeed your Lord is modest and generous; He is ashamed that one of you should stretch out his hands to Him and that He should return them empty."],[4114,"When the muezzin calls the adhan, the gates of heaven are opened, and supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah."],[4115,"There is no patch of ground upon which Allah is remembered with prayer or remembrance except that it rejoices at that to its utmost extent from the seven earths, and it boasts over the surrounding patches of ground. And there is no servant who stands in a desert of the earth intending prayer except that the earth adorns itself for him."],[4116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on the three days of Tashriq, after the Day of Sacrifice."],[4117,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to pray over Abdullah b. Ubayy, but Jibril took hold of his garment and said, “And do not pray over any of them who has died, ever, and do not stand at his grave.”"],[4118,"Whoever dies on Friday is protected from the punishment of the grave."],[4119,"Whoever seeks refuge with Allah ten times in a day from Satan, Allah appoints an angel for him to repel the devils from him."],[4120,"“My intercession is for the people of major sins from my Ummah.” He said: “The confirmation of this is in the Quran.” He said: Then he recited to us: “If you avoid the major sins that you are forbidden from, We will expiate for you your misdeeds and admit you to a noble entrance” (Quran 4:31). So these are the ones who avoid major sins, and those who commit major sins—the intercession of Muhammad ﷺ remains for them. He said: Then Yazid said to Anas, “You have spoken the truth.”"],[4121,"The sun and the moon are two gored bulls in the Fire."],[4122,"He forbade fasting on five days of the year: the Day of Fitr, the Day of Sacrifice, and the days of Tashriq."],[4123,"Can any of you not recite: Say, He is God, One, three times in a night? For it equals a third of the Quran."],[4124,"Whoever is kind to a believer or lightens for him some of his needs, small or great, it is a right upon God that He will serve him from the servants of Paradise."],[4125,"Whoever prays the morning prayer and then his protection is violated, his sanctity has been violated and God's sanctuary has been breached, and I am the claimant for his protection."],[4126,"The son of Adam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as if he were a lamb—and perhaps he said: as if he were a camel—and He will say: Son of Adam, I am the best divider. Look to the work you did for Me, and I will reward you for it, and look to the work you did for other than Me, and you will be recompensed by the one for whom you did it."],[4127,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came and said: O Messenger of God, so-and-so has died. He said: Was he not with us just now? They said: Yes. He said: Glory be to God, it is as if it were a sudden seizure upon anger. The deprived one is he who is deprived of his will."],[4128,"Whoever wishes to have his life extended and his provision increased, let him maintain his kinship ties."],[4129,"The first thing God made obligatory upon people of their religion is prayer, and the last thing to remain is prayer, and the first thing they will be called to account for is prayer. God says: Look at My servant's prayer. If it is complete, it is recorded as complete. If it is found deficient, He says: Look, does he have voluntary prayers? If voluntary prayers are found for him, the obligatory prayer is completed from the voluntary prayers. Then He says: Look, is his zakat complete? If his zakat is found complete, it is recorded as complete. If it is deficient, He says: Look, does he have charity? If he has charity, his zakat is completed for him from the charity."],[4130,"That I sit with a people who remember God from the morning until the sun rises is dearer to me than what the sun rises upon."],[4131,"That I sit with a people who remember God from the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is dearer to me than freeing eight of the descendants of Ishmael."],[4132,"There was a man at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ who would go on expeditions with the Messenger of God. When he returned and dismounted from his riding beast, he would head to the mosque of the Messenger and pray in it, prolonging the prayer, until some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ came to think he had merit over them. One day he passed by while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting among his Companions. Some of his Companions said to him: O Prophet of God, this is that man. Either the Prophet of God sent for him, or he came of his own accord. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw him approaching, he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, between his eyes is a mark from Satan. When he stood before the assembly, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: When you stood before the assembly, did you say to yourself: There is no one in the group better than me? He said: Yes. Then he left and went to a corner of the mosque, drew a line with his foot, then placed his heels together and stood to pray. The Messenger of God said: Which of you will go to this man and kill him? Abu Bakr stood up. The Messenger of God said: Did you kill the man? He said: I found him praying, so I was in awe of him. The Messenger of God said: Which of you will go to this man and kill him? Umar said: I will. He took the sword, but found him standing in prayer, so he returned. The Messenger of God said to Umar: Did you kill the man? He said: O Prophet of God, I found him praying, so I was in awe of him. The Messenger of God said: Which of you will go to this man and kill him? Ali said: I will. The Messenger of God said: You are the one for him if you catch him. Ali went but did not find him, so he returned. The Messenger of God said: Did you kill the man? He said: I do not know which way he went in the land. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: This is the first horn to emerge from my community. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If you had killed him, or if he had killed him, no two in my community would have differed. The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and this community—meaning his community—will split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except one. We said: O Prophet of God, who is that one sect? He said: The main body."],[4133,"O Messenger of God, what do you think about one of us speaking to himself about something, such that falling from the sky and being cut into pieces is dearer to him than speaking of it? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: That is pure faith."],[4134,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me: O my son, ask for ablution water for me from this house. I said: The Messenger of God ﷺ is asking for ablution water? They said: Tell him that our bucket is the hide of a dead animal. He said: Ask them, did they tan it? They said: Yes. He said: Its tanning is its purification."],[4135,"I will knock on the gate of Paradise, and a gate of gold will be opened for me, its rings of silver. The greatest light will receive me, and I will fall down prostrating. I will be inspired with praise of God such as no one before me was inspired with. It will be said to me: Raise your head, ask and you shall be given; speak and you shall be heard; intercede and your intercession shall be accepted. I will say: My community. It will be said: You shall have those in whose hearts there is the weight of a barley grain of faith. He said: Then I will prostrate a second time, and the like will be inspired to me, and the like will be said to me. I will say: My community. It will be said to me: You shall have those in whose hearts there is the weight of a mustard seed of faith. Then I will prostrate a third time, and the like will be said to me. Then I will raise my head and say: My community. It will be said to me: You shall have whoever said, There is no god but God, sincerely."],[4136,"Indeed, a dream has an inner meaning. Therefore, give it a kunya by its kunya and name it by its names. The dream is for the first interpreter."],[4137,"God sent eight thousand prophets: four thousand to the Children of Israel and four thousand to the rest of mankind."],[4138,"There is no servant but has two gates in the heaven: a gate through which his deed enters and a gate through which his deed and speech go out. When he dies, they miss him and weep over him. Then he recited this verse: 'So the heaven and the earth did not weep over them' (Quran 44:29). He mentioned that they did not perform righteous deeds on the earth for which it would weep over them, and no good speech or righteous deed of theirs ascended to the heaven, so that it would miss them and weep over them."],[4139,"O people, weep. If you do not weep, then make yourselves weep. For the people of the Fire will weep in the Fire until their tears flow down their faces like streams, until the tears cease and blood flows—meaning—and the eyes become ulcerated. If ships were launched in it, they would sail."],[4140,"I fear for my community after me five things: denial of the divine decree and belief in the stars."],[4141,"Is not one of you able to recite in the night, 'Say: He is God, the One' (Quran 112)? Indeed, it equals the entire Quran."],[4142,"I will knock on the gate of Paradise, and a gate of gold will be opened for me, its rings of silver. The greatest light will receive me, and I will fall down prostrating. I will be inspired with praise of God such as no one before me was inspired with. It will be said to me: Raise your head, ask and you shall be given, intercede and your intercession shall be accepted, speak and you shall be heard. I will say: My community. It will be said: You shall have those in whose hearts there is the weight of a barley grain of faith. He said: Then I will prostrate a second time, and the like will be inspired to me. I will say: My community. It will be said to me: You shall have those in whose hearts there is the weight of a mustard seed of faith. Then I will prostrate a third time, and the like will be inspired to me, and the like will be said to me. Then I will raise my head and say: My community. It will be said: You shall have whoever said, There is no god but God, sincerely."],[4143,"The Messenger of God ﷺ halted for a rest one night. Bilal gave the call to prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever says the like of his words and bears witness to the like of his testimony will have Paradise."],[4144,"No two Muslims meet and one of them takes the hand of his companion, but it is incumbent upon God to answer their supplication and not to withhold their hands until He forgives them."],[4145,"No Muslim servant comes to a brother of his, visiting him for the sake of God, but a caller from the heaven calls out: You are good, and Paradise is good for you. And otherwise God says in the dominion of His Throne: He visited for My sake, and upon Me is his hospitality. I will not be satisfied with hospitality for him less than Paradise."],[4146,"No people gather together remembering God, desiring nothing thereby but His face, but a caller from the heaven calls out: Rise forgiven; your evil deeds have been turned into good deeds."],[4147,"Maymun b. Siyah, the chief of the Quran reciters."],[4148,"In the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ there was a man whose devotion and exertion impressed us. We identified him by name to the Messenger of God ﷺ, but he did not recognize him. We described him by his appearance, but he did not recognize him. While we were mentioning him, the man appeared. We said, 'This is he.' He said, 'You are telling me about a man on whose face there is a mark from Satan.' He approached until he stood before them without greeting. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'I adjure you by God, did you say when you stood before the assembly: There is no one among the people better or more virtuous than me?' He said, 'O God, yes.' Then he entered to pray. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Who will kill the man?' Abu Bakr said, 'I will.' He entered upon him and found him praying. He said, 'Glory be to God! Should I kill a man who is praying, when the Messenger of God ﷺ has forbidden striking those who pray?' So he came out. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'What did you do?' He said, 'I disliked killing him while he was praying, and you forbade striking those who pray.' He said, 'Who will kill the man?' Umar said, 'I will.' He entered and found him placing his face (in prostration). Umar said, 'Abu Bakr is better than me.' So he came out. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'What happened?' He said, 'I found him placing his face for God, so I disliked killing him.' He said, 'Who will kill the man?' Ali said, 'I will.' He said, 'You, if you catch him.' He entered upon him and found that he had left. He returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said to him, 'What happened?' He said, 'I found that he had left.' He said, 'If he had been killed, no two men of my community would have differed. He would have been the first and last of them.'"],[4149,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade striking those who pray."],[4150,"Abu Talha sent me to the Messenger of God ﷺ to invite him, and he had prepared food for him. I came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was with the people. He looked at me, and I felt shy, so I said, 'Accept Abu Talha's invitation.' He said to the people, 'Get up.' Abu Talha said, 'O Messenger of God, I only prepared something for you.' He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ wiped it and prayed for blessing in it.' Then he said, 'Admit a group of my companions, ten.' He said, 'Eat.' He brought out something between his fingers, and they ate until they were full and left. He said, 'Admit ten.' They ate until they were full and left. He kept admitting ten and sending out ten until there was none left who had not entered and eaten until full. Then he prepared it, and it was as it had been when they ate from it."],[4151,"The Prophet ﷺ had two freedmen: an Abyssinian and a Nabatean. They insulted each other while the Prophet ﷺ was listening. One said to the other, 'O Abyssinian,' and the other said, 'O Nabatean.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not say this. You are both men from the companions of Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[4152,"Supplication is not rejected between the call to prayer and the iqama."],[4153,"The son of the sister of a people is one of them. He said: Yes."],[4154,"I do not recognize anything of people's affairs except the qibla."],[4155,"Let the menstruating woman wait five, seven, eight, nine, ten (days). When ten have passed, she is one with istihada."],[4156,"Abu Talha saw the Messenger of God ﷺ hungry, so he went to Umm Sulaym and said, 'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ hungry. Do you have anything?' She said, 'We have nothing but about a mudd of barley flour.' He said, 'Knead it and prepare it; perhaps we can invite the Messenger of God ﷺ to eat with us.' She kneaded it and baked it into a loaf. He said to me, 'Invite the Prophet ﷺ.' I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and with him were people. Mubarak said, 'I think he said: eighty-some.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, Abu Talha invites you.' He said to his companions, 'Respond to Abu Talha's invitation.' I hurried back and told him that his companions had come. Bakr said: He nudged me. Thabit said: Abu Talha said, 'The Messenger of God knows better what is in my house than I do.' Both said, from Anas: Abu Talha met him and said, 'O Messenger of God, we have nothing but a loaf. I saw you hungry, so I ordered Umm Sulaym to make you a loaf.' He asked for the loaf and for a large bowl, and he placed it in the bowl. He said, 'Is there any ghee?' Abu Talha said, 'There was something in the skin.' He brought it. The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Talha squeezed it until something came out. The Prophet ﷺ wiped his forefinger, then wiped the loaf, and it swelled. He said, 'In the name of God,' and the loaf swelled. He kept doing that, and the loaf kept swelling until I saw it overflowing in the bowl. He said, 'Invite ten of my companions.' I invited ten for him. The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand in the middle of the loaf and said, 'Eat, in the name of God.' They ate from around the loaf until they were full. Then he said, 'Invite another ten for me.' I invited another ten. He said, 'Eat, in the name of God.' They ate from around the loaf until they were full. He kept inviting ten at a time, and they ate from that loaf until they were full, while the middle of the loaf where the Messenger of God ﷺ had placed his hand remained as it was."],[4157,"We used to pray with the Messenger of God ﷺ in intense heat. When one of us could not place his face firmly on the ground, he spread his garment and prostrated on it."],[4158,"When we prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, we prostrated on our garments out of fear of the heat."],[4159,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered ihram for both of them together. He said: I mentioned that to Ibn Umar, and he said: He entered ihram for hajj. Then I mentioned that to Anas, and he said: Do you consider us as nothing but children?"],[4160,"Labbayk for a hajj and an umrah."],[4161,"We used to pray with the Messenger of God ﷺ in intense heat. One of us would take pebbles in his hand, and when they cooled, he would place them down and prostrate on them."],[4162,"The prohibition of wine came down, and I entered upon some of my companions while it was before them. I kicked it with my foot, then I said: Go to the Messenger of God ﷺ, for the prohibition of wine has come down. He said: Their drink in those days was unripe dates and dried dates."],[4163,"When a man speaks and then turns away, it is a trust."],[4164,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and Ali, and they used to begin the recitation with 'Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds', and they recited 'Master of the Day of Judgment'."],[4165,"I came upon the lowest heaven on the night I was taken on the night journey, and I saw in it men whose tongues and lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are the speechmakers among your community."],[4166,"When death was present to Abu Salama, Umm Salama said: To whom do you entrust me? He said: O God, You are better for Umm Salama than Abu Salama. When he died, the Messenger of God ﷺ proposed to her, and she said: I am advanced in age. He said: I am older than you in age. And the dependents are upon God and His Messenger. As for jealousy, I hope that God will remove it. So the Messenger of God ﷺ married her, and he sent her two millstones and a water jar."],[4167,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyya and made her freedom her dowry."],[4168,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married Safiyya bt. Huyayy and made her dowry her freedom."],[4169,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyya and made her freedom her dowry."],[4170,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a basket with unripe dates on it, and he said: 'The example of a good word is like a good tree, its root firm and its branches in the sky, yielding its fruit every season by permission of its Lord.' He said: It is the date palm. 'And the example of a bad word is like a bad tree, uprooted from above the ground, having no stability.' He said: It is the colocynth."],[4171,"The most complete of people in faith is the best of them in character. Indeed, good character certainly reaches the degree of fasting and prayer."],[4172,"The Prophet ﷺ manumitted Safiyyah and made her manumission her dowry."],[4173,"The Messenger of God ﷺ manumitted Safiyyah and made her manumission her dowry."],[4174,"Whoever prays over a funeral, a qirat is written for him. If he waits until its burial is completed, two qirats are written for him."],[4175,"He liked gourd."],[4176,"I have emphasized the toothstick to you extensively."],[4177,"Make things easy and do not make them difficult. Bring calm and do not drive people away."],[4178,"Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."],[4179,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray in sheepfolds before the mosques were built."],[4180,"Love of the Ansar is a sign of every believer and hypocrite. Whoever loves them loves them because of love for me, and whoever hates them hates them because of hatred for me."],[4181,"Hear and obey, even if a black slave whose head is like a raisin is placed in authority over you."],[4182,"Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."],[4183,"The site of the Prophet's mosque ﷺ belonged to Banu al-Najjar. In it there were palm trees, cultivated land, and graves from the graves of the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'Sell it to me.' They said: 'We seek no price for it except from Allah.' He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the palm trees to be cut down, the cultivated land to be ruined, and the graves to be dug up. Before that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray in sheep enclosures and wherever the prayer overtook him."],[4184,"Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will become firmly established, wine will be drunk, and fornication will appear openly."],[4185,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, he stayed in an elevated area of Madinah, in a quarter called Banu Amr b. Awf. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed among them for fourteen nights. Then he sent for a group of Banu al-Najjar, and they came wearing their swords. Anas said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his riding camel, with Abu Bakr riding behind him, and a group of Banu al-Najjar around him, until he dismounted in the courtyard of Abu Ayyub. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray wherever the prayer overtook him, and he used to pray in sheep enclosures. Then he ordered the construction of the mosque, and he sent for a group of Banu al-Najjar, and they came. He said: 'O Banu al-Najjar, sell me this walled garden of yours.' They said: 'No, by Allah, we will seek no price for it except from Allah.' Anas said: In it there was what I am telling you: there were graves of the polytheists, it was ruined, and there were palm trees in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the graves of the polytheists to be dug up, the ruins to be leveled, and the palm trees to be cut down. They placed the palm trunks as the qiblah side of the mosque, and they made its two doorposts of stone. He said: They carried those rocks while chanting, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with them, and they were saying: 'O Allah, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun.'"],[4186,"Ammar b. Yasir was a strong man, so he would carry two stones. The Prophet ﷺ learned of that and met him, then he pushed him in the chest and said: 'Carry me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to brush the dust from his head and chest, saying: 'O son of Sumayyah, the transgressing party will kill you.'"],[4187,"I entered Paradise and found a palace of gold. I said: 'For whom is this palace?' They said: 'For a young man of Quraysh.' I thought it was for me, so I said: 'Who is he?' They said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' O Abu Hafs, were it not for what I know of your jealousy, I would have entered it. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, whoever I have been jealous over, I would never be jealous over you.'"],[4188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O Anas, perform ablution thoroughly and your lifespan will be increased. Greet with peace whoever you meet from my community and your good deeds will multiply. When you enter your house, greet your family members with peace and the good of your household will increase. Pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning ones before you.' And he said: 'O Anas, show mercy to the young, honor the old, and be among my companions.'"],[4189,"I do not recognize anything that existed at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was said to him: 'Then where is the prayer, O Abu Hamzah?' He said: 'Have you not done in the prayer what you already know?'"],[4190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set a time limit for us in trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, and shaving the pubic hair: that they should not be left for more than forty days."],[4191,"Allah will say to the one with the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire: 'If you had the world and everything in it, would you ransom yourself with it?' He will say: 'Yes.' He will say: 'I asked of you something easier than this while you were in the loins of Adam: that you not associate partners with Me.' I think he said: 'And that I not enter you into the Fire, but you refused except to associate partners.'"],[4192,"The believer is one from whom people feel safe. The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The emigrant is one who abandons evil. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no servant will enter Paradise if his neighbor does not feel safe from his harms."],[4193,"When food is brought near to one of you while he has sandals on his feet, let him remove his sandals, for it is more comfortable for the feet and it is from the Sunnah."],[4194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Zayd, Ja'far, and Abdullah b. Rawahah, and he gave the banner to Zayd. He said: 'And if they are all struck down?' He said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced their death to the people before the news came. He said: 'Zayd took the banner and was struck down, then Ja'far took it and was struck down, then Abdullah took it and was struck down. Then a sword from the swords of Allah, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner.' He said: He began to speak to the people with his eyes flowing with tears."],[4195,"Zayd took the banner and was struck. Then Ja'far took it and was struck. Then Abd Allah b. Rawaha took it and was struck. Then Khalid b. al-Walid took it without being commanded, and God granted him victory. It does not please them—or it does not please me—that they are with us, while his eyes were shedding tears."],[4196,"I was riding behind Abu Talha, and his knee was touching the knee of the Prophet ﷺ. They were both shouting: At your service for Hajj and Umrah."],[4197,"I have not seen anyone more merciful to children than the Messenger of God ﷺ. He had arranged for his son Ibrahim to be suckled at the outskirts of Madinah. Her husband was a blacksmith. He would come to him, and the boy would come to him with traces of smoke on him, and he would embrace him, kiss him, and smell him."],[4198,"I saw Anas b. Malik and al-Hasan praying on the day of Eid before the imam came out. He said: And I saw Muhammad b. Sirin come and sit down without praying."],[4199,"Anas became too weak to fast, so he prepared a large bowl of tharid and invited thirty needy people and fed them."],[4200,"I have not seen anyone more merciful to children than the Messenger of God ﷺ. Ibrahim was being suckled in the highlands of Madinah. He would set out with us, enter the house, which was filled with smoke—his wet nurse's husband was a blacksmith—take him, kiss him, and then return. Amr said: When Ibrahim died, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Ibrahim is my son, and he died while still nursing, and he will have two wet nurses to complete his suckling in Paradise."],[4201,"I have not seen anyone more merciful to children than the Messenger of God."],[4202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was most merciful to children. He had a son being suckled in a part of Madinah. His wet nurse's husband was a blacksmith. He would go to him, and we with him, while the house had been filled with smoke. He would smell him and kiss him, then return."],[4203,"I asked Anas b. Malik about shortening the prayer. He said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ traveled a distance of three miles, or three farsakhs—Shu'ba was the one uncertain—he would pray two rak'ahs."],[4204,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a man who divorced his wife three times, and she married another husband who died before consummating the marriage with her. May the first one remarry her? He said: No, not until he tastes her sweetness."],[4205,"When one of you has intercourse with his wife, let him be truthful with her. If he finishes before her, let him not hasten her."],[4206,"When one of you has intercourse with his wife, let him be sincere toward her. Then when he has fulfilled his need before she fulfills her need, let him not hurry her until she fulfills her need."],[4207,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Mu'adh b. Jabal: Know that whoever bears witness that there is no god but God will enter the Garden."],[4208,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. Among us were those fasting and among us were those not fasting. We alighted at a stopping place on a hot day. The ones with the most shade among us were the owners of cloaks, and among us were those who shielded themselves from the sun with their hands. He said: The fasting ones collapsed and the non-fasting ones stood up, struck the tents, and watered the mounts. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The non-fasting ones have gone today with the reward."],[4209,"Every community has a monasticism, and the monasticism of this community is striving in the path of God."],[4210,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar did not recite 'In the name of God, the Compassionate, the Merciful.'"],[4211,"One of my paternal uncles prepared food for the Prophet ﷺ and said: I would like you to eat in my house and pray in it. He said: So he came to him, and in the house there was a stallion from those stallions. He ordered a side of it to be swept and sprinkled, then he prayed and we prayed with him."],[4212,"You perform deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them among the destructive sins in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4213,"The Prophet ﷺ was informed on Monday, and the funeral prayer was said over him on Tuesday."],[4214,"You have left behind in Madinah men who did not travel any distance, nor spend any expense, nor cross any valley except that they were with you in it. They said: O Messenger of God, how can they be with us when they are in Madinah? He said: A valid excuse detained them."],[4215,"A servant in Hell will call out for a thousand years: O Compassionate, O Bestower. He said: Then God will say: O Gabriel, bring Me My servant. He said: So Gabriel will go and see the people of the Fire fallen on their faces. He said: Then he will return and say: O Lord, I did not see him. He said: Then God will say: He is in such-and-such a place. He said: So he will come to him, and he will come to his Lord, and God will say to him: O My servant, how did you find your place and your resting place? He said: Then he will say: O Lord, the worst place and the worst resting place. He said: Then He will say: Return My servant. He will say: O Lord, I did not hope that You would return me after You brought me out. He will say: Leave My servant."],[4216,"I entered upon Anas b. Malik. He said to me: When did your sight go? He said: When I was two years old, as my family told me. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings? I said: Yes. He said: Ibn Umm Maktum passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, greeted him, and then went on. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God says: For the one whose two precious eyes I have taken, there is no reward with Me except the Garden."],[4217,"Two men traversed a desert: one was a worshipper, and the other had some wrongdoing about him. The worshipper became thirsty until he collapsed. His companion looked at him while he had a small water vessel with some water in it. He kept looking at him while he was fallen. He said: By God, if this righteous servant dies of thirst while I have water, I will never attain any good from God; but if I give him my water, I will surely die. So he trusted in God, Mighty and Majestic, resolved, sprinkled some of his water on him, and gave him the rest to drink. He said: Then he rose until they crossed the desert. He said: The one who had wrongdoing will be brought to a halt on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning, and he will be ordered to the Fire. The angels will drive him, and he will see the worshipper and say: O so-and-so, do you not recognize me? He will say: Who are you? He said: I am so-and-so who preferred you over myself on the day of the desert. He said: He will say: Yes, I recognize you. He said: Then he will say to the angels: Stop. He said: So he will be stopped, and he will come until he stands and calls upon his Lord, saying: O Lord, You know his favor toward me, and how he preferred me over himself. O Lord, grant him to me. He will say: He is yours. He said: Then he will come, take him by the hand, and admit him to the Garden."],[4218,"She had a ewe, so she collected its clarified butter in a leather container and filled the container, then sent it with a foster daughter, saying: “O foster daughter, deliver this leather container to the Messenger of God ﷺ so that he may use it as a condiment.” The foster daughter set off with it until she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, a leather container of clarified butter that Umm Sulaym has sent to you.” He said: “Empty her container for her.” So the container was emptied and returned to her, and she left with it. Then Umm Sulaym came and saw the container full, dripping. Umm Sulaym said: “O foster daughter, did I not tell you to take it to the Messenger of God ﷺ?” She said: “I did, and if you do not believe me, go and ask the Messenger of God ﷺ.” So Umm Sulaym went with her foster daughter and said: “O Messenger of God, I sent with her to you a leather container containing clarified butter.” He said: “She did what you told her; she brought it.” She said: “By the One who sent you with guidance and the true religion, it is indeed full, dripping with clarified butter.” He said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: ‘Do you marvel that God has fed you as you fed His Prophet? Eat and feed others.’” She said: “Then I came to the house and divided it in a bowl of ours such and such, and left in it enough for us to use as a condiment for a month or two.”"],[4219,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stoned, and Abu Bakr and Umar stoned, and their practice is a Sunnah."],[4220,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stoned, and Abu Bakr and Umar stoned, and their practice is a Sunnah."],[4221,"Do not pray at sunrise or at sunset, for it rises and sets on a devil's horn. And pray between those times as much as you wish."],[4222,"How wonderful is the affair of the believer: nothing is decreed for him but it is good for him."],[4223,"The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and then said: “I marvel at the believer. God does not decree anything for him but it is good for him.”"],[4224,"I have not prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of God ﷺ whose prayer was lighter than that of the Messenger of God ﷺ, nor more concise yet complete."],[4225,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was not given to cursing or obscenity. When he rebuked one of us, he would say: “What is the matter with him? May his right hand be dusty!”"],[4226,"I indeed recognize the supplication of the Messenger of God ﷺ for me, that God would bless me in my wealth and my children."],[4227,"When God wills good for a people, He tests them."],[4228,"Three birds were gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, and he fed his servant one of them. The next day she brought it back to him, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: “Did I not forbid you to set aside anything for tomorrow? For God brings the provision of every tomorrow.”"],[4229,"Four will be brought on the Day of Resurrection: the infant, the mentally disabled, the one who died during the interval between prophets, and the aged old man. Each will present his argument. The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will say to a neck of the Fire: ‘Emerge.’ Then He will say to them: ‘I used to send to My servants messengers from among themselves, and I am the Messenger of Myself to you. Enter this.’ Then the one for whom wretchedness was decreed will say: ‘O Lord, how can we enter it when it was from it that we used to flee?’ And the one for whom felicity was decreed will move forward and plunge into it swiftly. Then He, Blessed and Exalted, will say: ‘You are more guilty than My messengers of denial and disobedience.’ So He will admit these to Paradise and those to the Fire."],[4230,"Abu Tayba passed by us in Ramadan. We said, \"Where have you come from?\" He said, \"I cupped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4231,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if you were to err until your sins filled what is between the heaven and the earth, then you sought forgiveness from Allah, He would forgive you. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you were not to err, Allah would bring a people who err, then seek forgiveness from Allah, and He would forgive them."],[4232,"One of my paternal uncles made food for the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"I would love for him to eat in my house and pray.\" He said, \"So he came to him, and in the house there was a stallion from those stallions. He ordered a side of it to be swept and sprinkled with water. Then he prayed, and we prayed with him.\""],[4233,"Gabriel came to me with something like a white mirror in which there was a black speck. I said, \"O Gabriel, what is this?\" He said, \"This is Friday. Allah has made it a festival for you and your nation. You are before the Jews and the Christians. In it there is an hour in which no servant asks Allah for good but that He gives it to him.\" He said, \"I said, 'What is this black speck?' He said, 'This is the Day of Resurrection. It will occur on a Friday. We call it among ourselves the Day of Increase.'\" He said, \"I said, 'What is the Day of Increase?' He said, 'Allah has made in Paradise a wide valley, and He has made in it dunes of white musk. When Friday comes, Allah descends into it. Then pulpits of gold are placed in it for the prophets, and chairs of pearls for the martyrs, and the wide-eyed houris descend from the chambers. They praise Allah and glorify Him.'\" He said, \"Then Allah says, 'Clothe My servants,' so they are clothed. He says, 'Feed My servants,' so they are fed. He says, 'Give drink to My servants,' so they are given drink. He says, 'Perfume My servants,' so they are perfumed. Then He says, 'What do you desire?' They say, 'Our Lord, Your good pleasure.'\" He said, \"He says, 'I am pleased with you.' Then He commands them, and they depart, and the wide-eyed houris ascend to the chambers, which are of green emerald and red ruby.\""],[4234,"I attended a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which there was neither bread nor meat."],[4235,"I came to Anas b. Malik and said, \"Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He ordered his family, and he led us in the Zuhr and Asr prayers. He recited to us in a low voice, and he recited al-Mursalat, al-Nazi'at, 'Amma yatasa'alun, and similar surahs."],[4236,"The lifespan of a fly is forty nights, and all flies are in the Fire except bees."],[4237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a bedouin to visit him while he was feverish. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is an expiation and a purification.\" The bedouin said, \"Rather, it is a fever boiling over an old man, driving him to the graves.\" The Prophet ﷺ got up and left him."],[4238,"When Allah afflicts a Muslim with an affliction in his body, He says to the angel, \"Write for him the equivalent of the righteous deeds he used to do.\" If He heals him, He washes and purifies him, and if He takes his soul, He forgives him and has mercy on him."],[4239,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a daughter who is such and such,\" and she mentioned her beauty and loveliness, \"and I preferred you with her.\" He said, \"I have accepted her.\" She did not cease praising her until she mentioned that she had never had a headache or complained of anything at all. He said, \"I have no need of your daughter.\""],[4240,"When Allah afflicts a servant with an affliction in his body, He says to the angel, \"Write for him the equivalent of the righteous deeds he used to do.\" If He heals him, He washes and purifies him, and if He takes his soul, He forgives him and has mercy on him."],[4241,"My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, here is your little servant. Pray to Allah for him.\" He said, \"O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, prolong his life, and forgive him.\" He said, \"So my wealth increased until it came to be that he fed people twice a year, and my children increased until I buried from my own loins more than a hundred, and my life was prolonged until I became shy before my family and longed to meet my Lord. As for the fourth, meaning forgiveness...\""],[4242,"When I take the two precious eyes of My servant, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise. He said: I asked: O Messenger of God, even if it was one? He said: Even if it was one."],[4243,"Make the journey brisk, for between you and the polytheists is a water source. If the polytheists get there first, it will be hard on the people and you will be overcome by severe thirst, you and your riding beasts and mounts. The Messenger of God ﷺ lagged behind with eight men, he being the ninth of them, and said to his companions: Would you like us to halt for a little rest, then catch up with the people? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. So they halted, and nothing awakened them except the heat of the sun. The Messenger of God ﷺ woke up and his companions woke up, and he said to them: Get up and relieve yourselves. They did so, then returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: Does any of you have water? A man among them said: O Messenger of God, there is a small vessel with some water in it. He said: Bring it. He brought it, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took it, wiped it with his hands, and prayed for blessing. Then he said to his companions: Come and perform ablution. They came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ poured for them until they had performed ablution. One of them called the adhan and the iqamah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ led them in prayer. He said to the owner of the vessel: Take good care of your vessel, for it will have a story. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions mounted before the people, and he said to his companions: What do you think the people have done? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said to them: Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and they will guide the people. The people arrived when the polytheists had already reached that water, and it was hard on the people; they and their mounts and beasts suffered severe thirst. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Where is the owner of the vessel? He said: Here he is, O Messenger of God. He said: Bring your vessel. He brought it, and in it was some water. He said to all of them: Come and drink. The Messenger of God ﷺ poured for them until they all drank, and they gave their beasts and mounts to drink, and filled every water skin and container. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions advanced against the polytheists, and God sent a wind that struck the faces of the polytheists, and God, Blessed and Exalted, sent down His help and gave them the upper hand, so they killed a great number of them, took many captives, and seized much booty, and the Messenger of God ﷺ and the people returned safe and sound."],[4244,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ traveled or went on a military expedition, he would take a man from his companions behind him each day. The one riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ was Mu'adh b. Jabal. He called him while he was behind him, and said: O Mu'adh b. Jabal. I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: Do you know what is God's right upon the servants? That they testify that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that they worship Him, associating nothing with Him. He repeated this hadith three times. Then he called out: O Mu'adh. I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: Do you know what is the servants' right upon God if they do that? I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: The servants' right upon God, if they do that, is that He not punish them and that He admit them to Paradise."],[4245,"The believers with the most complete faith are those with the best character."],[4246,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he raised his head and saw an old man approaching. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: He is not one of us who does not honor our elders and show mercy to our young."],[4247,"An old man came to the Prophet ﷺ for a need, and the people were slow to make room for him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: He is not one of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elders."],[4248,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would answer the call of a servant, visit the sick, and ride a donkey."],[4249,"I entered with my father upon Anas b. Malik, and we said to him: Tell us a hadith by which God may benefit us. I heard him say: Whoever among you can die without debt, let him do so, for I saw the Prophet of God ﷺ when a funeral of a man who had a debt was brought to him. He said: I will not pray over him until you guarantee his debt, for my prayer over him will benefit him. They did not guarantee his debt, and he did not pray over him, and he said: He is held in pledge in his grave."],[4250,"Fear God and render trusts to their owners."],[4251,"There is no Muslim who lives forty years in Islam but God diverts from him three types of affliction: leprosy, madness, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty, God makes his reckoning easy for him. When he reaches sixty, God grants him repentance toward what He loves. When he reaches seventy, God loves him and the inhabitants of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, God accepts his good deeds and overlooks his bad deeds. When he reaches ninety, God forgives his past and future sins, and he is called a captive of God on earth, and he intercedes for his household."],[4252,"I am God's captive on His earth."],[4253,"Whoever God grants forty years in Islam, God keeps from him types of affliction: leprosy, vitiligo, and the deceit of Satan. Whoever God grants fifty years in Islam, God makes his reckoning easy on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever God grants sixty years in Islam, God grants him repentance toward God in what God loves. Whoever God grants seventy years in Islam, the inhabitants of heaven and the inhabitants of earth love him. Whoever God grants eighty years in Islam, God erases his bad deeds and records his good deeds. Whoever God grants ninety years in Islam, God forgives his sins, and he is a captive of God on His earth, and he intercedes for his household on the Day of Resurrection."],[4254,"No person who reaches forty years in Islam but that Allah wards off from him varieties of affliction: insanity, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty, Allah makes the reckoning easy for him. When he reaches sixty, Allah grants him turning to Allah with what Allah loves. When he reaches seventy, Allah loves him and the inhabitants of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, his good deeds are recorded and his evil deeds are erased. When he reaches ninety, Allah forgives his past and future sins, and he becomes a prisoner of Allah on His earth, and intercession is granted for his household."],[4255,"Yahya b. Sulaym said: And Abdullah b. Uthman also informed me, from Sa'd b. Abi al-Hakam al-Madani, from Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Amr b. Uthman, from Anas b. Malik, with the like of the hadith of the two Harranis:"],[4256,"Charity is not accepted from embezzled property, nor is prayer without purification."],[4257,"He is not a believer whose neighbor is not safe from his wrongful actions."],[4258,"Greatness of reward is with greatness of trial."],[4259,"When Allah intends good for a servant, He hastens punishment for him in this world, and when Allah intends evil for a servant, He withholds his sin until He meets him on the Day of Resurrection."],[4260,"Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid, from Ibn Sinan, from Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet ﷺ that he used to say: then he mentioned something similar."],[4261,"Deliberation is from Allah and haste is from Satan. Nothing offers more excuses than Allah, and nothing is more beloved to Allah than praise."],[4262,"Accept six things from me and I will accept Paradise for you. They said: What are they? He said: When one of you speaks, let him not lie; when he makes a promise, let him not break it; when he is entrusted, let him not betray; lower your gazes; restrain your hands; and guard your private parts."],[4263,"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, Allah does not place His mercy except upon a merciful one. They said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us show mercy. He said: It is not the mercy of one of you to his companion; rather, mercy is shown to all people."],[4264,"The two who insult each other are as they say, so the sin is upon the one who initiated, until the wronged one transgresses."],[4265,"Before the Hour there will be trials like patches of dark night: a man will wake up a believer and become an disbeliever by evening, and wake up a disbeliever and become a believer by evening, and a people will sell their religion for a paltry worldly gain."],[4266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for a month in the morning prayer after the bowing, supplicating against Riʿl and Dhakwān."],[4267,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for a month after the bowing, supplicating against Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya, who disobeyed God and His Messenger."],[4268,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for a month after the bowing, supplicating against Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya, who disobeyed God and His Messenger."],[4269,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for a month, supplicating against Riʿl and Dhakwān."],[4270,"The rewards of my community were shown to me, even the speck that a man removes from the mosque, and the sins of my community were shown to me, and I did not see a sin greater than the verse or surah that a man learns and then forgets."],[4271,"Whoever helps a distressed person, God records for him seventy-three good deeds: one of them by which God sets right for him the affair of his world and his Hereafter, and seventy-two in degrees."],[4272,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Tabuk, and the sun rose with a brilliance, rays, and light the like of which it had not been seen to rise with before. Then Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “O Gabriel, why do I see the sun today rose with a brilliance, light, and rays the like of which I have not seen it rise with before?” He said: “That is because Muʿāwiya b. Muʿāwiya al-Laythī died in Madinah today, so God sent to him a thousand angels praying over him.” He said: “And why is that?” He said: “He used to recite ‘Say: He is God, the One’ frequently night and day, in his walking, standing, and sitting. Would you like, O Messenger of God, that I fold up the earth for you so that you may pray over him?” He said: “Yes.” So he prayed over him."],[4273,"Gabriel descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Muʿāwiya b. Muʿāwiya al-Laythī has died. Would you like to pray over him?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “He struck the earth with his wing, and there remained no tree or hillock but it was flattened. Then he raised his bier, and he looked at him and said the takbir over him, and behind him were two rows of angels, in each row seventy thousand angels.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Gabriel, by what did he attain this station with God?” He said: “By his love of ‘Say: He is God, the One’, and his recitation of it going and coming, standing and sitting, and in every state.”"],[4274,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when he washed his face he took a handful of water and ran it through his beard from inside it, and said: “Thus my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, commanded me.”"],[4275,"When one of you comes to his wife, let him be truthful to her, and if he precedes her, let him not rush her."],[4276,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rakʿas, and with ʿUmar two rakʿas, and with ʿUthmān at the beginning of his reign."],[4277,"He forbade a man to eat with his left hand or drink with his left hand."],[4278,"When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for the devil eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[4279,"He forbade that a man eat with his left hand or drink with his left hand."],[4280,"Seventy prophets passed by the rock of al-Rawḥāʾ, barefoot, wearing cloaks, heading to the Ancient House of God; among them was Moses, the prophet of God, may God bless him."],[4281,"When the verse of the veil was revealed, I used to enter as I used to enter, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'Keep back, my son.'"],[4282,"A dish containing gourd was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he liked it. He said: I saw him put his finger in, seeking the gourd. He said: Then a man entered upon him and saw on him a trace of yellow dye, and the Messenger of God ﷺ disliked it; and he would not confront a man to his face with something he disliked. So when the man stood up, he said to some of the people: 'If only you would command this man to leave off this yellow dye.'"],[4283,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: How will people be gathered on their faces? He said: 'The One who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces.'"],[4284,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: How will people be gathered on their faces? He said: 'The One who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces.'"],[4285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar did not omit the takbir."],[4286,"The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to complete the takbir when they raised and when they lowered."],[4287,"Three qualities, whoever has them is forbidden from the Fire and the Fire is forbidden from him: faith in God, love for the sake of God, and that being thrown into the Fire and burned is dearer to him than returning to disbelief."],[4288,"Whoever guards for one night on the seacoast is better than the worship of a man among his family for a thousand years, the year being three hundred and sixty days, each day worth a thousand years."],[4289,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ in a funeral procession, and he saw women, so he said: 'Will you carry him?' They said: No. He said: 'Will you bury him?' They said: No. He said: 'Then go back, burdened with sin and without reward.'"],[4290,"Whoever I deprive of his two precious ones, then he is patient and seeks reward, his recompense will be Paradise."],[4291,"The Prophet ﷺ performed qunut in the Fajr prayer after ruku'. He said: I heard him supplicating in his qunut against the disbelievers. He said: And I heard him saying: 'Make their hearts like the hearts of disbelieving women.'"],[4292,"It was said: 'O Messenger of God, should some of us bow to others when we meet?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then should some of us embrace others?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then should some of us shake hands with others?' He said: 'Shake hands.'"],[4293,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ, so he wiped her face—and they used to come to him and he would wipe their faces and supplicate for them—so she said: 'O Messenger of God, lower your hand.' He said: So he pushed her away and said: 'Get away from me.'"],[4294,"It was said: 'O Messenger of God, should some of us bow to others when we meet?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Then should some of us embrace others?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then should some of us shake hands with one another?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[4295,"The lifespan of a fly is forty days, and the fly is entirely in the Fire."],[4296,"Whoever eats of these two plants—garlic and onion—let him not come near our place of prayer, and let him come to me so I may wipe his face and seek refuge for him."],[4297,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited Umm Sulaym and prayed a voluntary prayer in her house. He said: 'O Umm Sulaym, when you pray the obligatory prayer, say: \"Glory be to God\" ten times, and \"God is most great\" ten times. Then ask whatever you wish, for He will say to you: \"Yes\"—three times.'"],[4298,"The Messenger of God ﷺ advised me, saying: 'O Anas, perform ablution thoroughly and your lifespan will be increased. O Anas, pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning ones before you. O Anas, greet your household and your good deeds will increase. O Anas, greet whomever you meet of my community and your good deeds will increase. O Anas, pray much by night and day and your guardian angels will love you. O Anas, sleep while you are ritually pure, for if you die, you die a martyr. O Anas, honor the elderly and show mercy to the young.'"],[4299,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: 'Which of your household is dearest to you?' He said: 'Al-Hasan and al-Husayn.' He said: He used to say to Fatimah: 'Bring my two sons,' and he would kiss them and hug them to him."],[4300,"The example of a righteous companion is like the example of a perfume seller: if he does not give you some of it, its fragrance will still reach you. And the example of an evil companion is like the example of a blacksmith: if his sparks do not hit you, his smoke will still reach you."],[4301,"The one who guides to good is like the one who does it, and God loves aiding the distressed."],[4302,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ascended an elevated area of land, he would say: O God, to You belongs elevation over every elevation, and to You belongs praise in every condition."],[4303,"Whoever builds a mosque for God, small or large, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[4304,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to a tree and shook it until as much of its leaves fell as God willed to fall. Then he said: Pains and calamities are faster in [removing] the sins of the son of Adam than I am in [shaking] this tree."],[4305,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he entered a house among the houses of Banu al-Najjar. He came out to us with his color changed and said: Who are the people of these graves? They said: They are graves of people who died in the pre-Islamic era. He then turned to us and said: Seek refuge in God from the punishment of the grave. For by the One in whose hand is my soul, I have seen their bodies and how they are being punished in their graves."],[4306,"Indeed, Satan lays his snout on the heart of the son of Adam. If he remembers God, he withdraws; and if he forgets, he devours his heart. That is the slinking whisperer."],[4307,"While a man from those before you was walking out in two cloaks, he became arrogant in them, so God commanded the earth and it seized him; he will be sinking into it until the Day of Resurrection."],[4308,"The Fire complained to its Lord, saying: My Lord, parts of me have consumed other parts. So He gave it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. The intense heat you experience is from its heat, and the intense cold you experience is from its extreme cold."],[4309,"Intercession is for the major sinners of my community."],[4310,"I am the master of the children of Adam, and [there is] no pride. I am the first one for whom the earth will split open, and [there is] no pride. I am the first one to take hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise, and [there is] no pride. The banner of praise is in my hand, and [there is] no pride."],[4311,"A Jewish youth used to serve the Prophet ﷺ. He fell ill, so the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him and said: Do you testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God? He began looking at his father, who said to him: Say what Muhammad is telling you. He then accepted and died. The Prophet ﷺ said to his companions: Pray over your companion."],[4312,"A mudd [of water] suffices one of you for ablution, and a sa' [suffices] for the ritual bath."],[4313,"The sign of a believer is love for the Ansar, and the sign of a hypocrite is hatred for the Ansar."],[4314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and one of his wives used to bathe from a single vessel."],[4315,"When Allah created the earth, it began to sway, so He created the mountains and cast them upon it, and it became stable. The angels marveled at the creation of the mountains and said: 'O Lord, is there anything among Your creation stronger than the mountains?' He said: 'Yes, iron.' They said: 'O Lord, is there anything among Your creation stronger than iron?' He said: 'Yes, fire.' They said: 'O Lord, is there anything among Your creation stronger than fire?' He said: 'Yes, water.' They said: 'O Lord, is there anything among Your creation stronger than water?' He said: 'Yes, wind.' They said: 'O Lord, is there anything among Your creation stronger than wind?' He said: 'Yes, a human being who gives charity with his right hand and conceals it from his left hand.'"],[4316,"Three things are from the foundation of Islam: refraining from harming one who says 'La ilaha illa Allah' (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah), not declaring him a disbeliever for a sin, and not expelling him from Islam for an action; jihad, which continues from when Allah sent me until the last of my community fights the Dajjal, neither the tyranny of a tyrant nor the justice of a just ruler will nullify it; and belief in all that has been decreed."],[4317,"Three things are from the foundation of faith: refraining from harming one who says 'La ilaha illa Allah' (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah), not declaring him a disbeliever for a sin, and not expelling him from Islam for an action; jihad, which continues from when Allah sent me until my community fights the Dajjal, neither the tyranny of a tyrant nor the justice of a just ruler will nullify it; and belief in all that has been decreed."],[4318,"How amazing is the affair of the believer! Indeed, Allah does not decree anything for him except that it is good for him."],[4319,"You perform deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair, but we used to consider them, at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to be among the destructive sins."],[4320,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted at a place, he would not depart from it until he had bidden it farewell with two rak'ahs."],[4321,"When the Prophet ﷺ traveled and halted at a place and wanted to depart, he would bid farewell to the place with two rak'ahs."],[4322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O my dear son.'"],[4323,"We used to pray 'Asr with the Prophet ﷺ while the sun was white and high, then I would go to my clan and find them sitting, and I would say to them: 'Get up and pray, for the Messenger of Allah has already prayed.'"],[4324,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate with the people of a household, he would say: 'May the fasting break their fast with you, and may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels send blessings upon you.'"],[4325,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ broke his fast with the people of a household, he would say: 'May the fasting break their fast with you, and may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you.'"],[4326,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ broke his fast with a people, he said: \"May the fasting break their fast with you, and may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you.\""],[4327,"When he broke his fast with a household, he said: \"May the fasting break their fast with you, and may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels descend upon you.\""],[4328,"There will be after me wicked leaders who pray the prayer at other than its time. When they do that, pray the prayer at its time, and make the prayer with them a supererogatory one."],[4329,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ encamped at a place, he would not depart until he had prayed the noon prayer."],[4330,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ encamped at a place, he would not depart until he had prayed the noon prayer."],[4331,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ encamped at a place, he would not depart from it until he had prayed the noon prayer."],[4332,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to hear and obey. He said: \"In what you are able.\""],[4333,"It was said: \"O Messenger of God, so-and-so, your client, has been martyred.\" He said: \"No, indeed I saw upon him a cloak that he had stolen on such-and-such a day.\""],[4334,"We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ when the sun had declined."],[4335,"He used to pray the afternoon prayer at the extent that a man could go to the Banu Harithah b. al-Harith and return before sunset, and at the extent that a man could slaughter a camel and cut it up before sunset. He would not pray the Friday prayer until the sun declined. When he went out to Makkah, he prayed the noon prayer at al-Shajarah as two rak'ahs."],[4336,"Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of God ﷺ to invite him, and he had prepared food for him. He said: I came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was with the people. He said: He looked at me and I felt shy, so I said: \"Respond to Abu Talhah.\" He said to the people: \"Arise.\" Abu Talhah said: \"O Messenger of God, I only prepared something for you.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ touched it and invoked blessing upon it, and said: \"Admit ten of my companions.\" He said: \"Eat.\" He brought out for them something from between his fingers, and they ate until they were full and left. He kept admitting ten and sending out ten until none of them remained except that he entered and ate until he was full. He said: Then he arranged it, and behold, it was as it had been when they ate from it."],[4337,"God is pleased with a servant who eats a meal or drinks a drink and then praises Him for it."],[4338,"I served the Messenger of God ﷺ for nine years, and I do not know that he ever said to me: “Why did you do such-and-such?” or ever found fault with me for anything."],[4339,"God is surely pleased with a servant who takes a morsel and praises God for it, or drinks a drink."],[4340,"I served the Messenger of God ﷺ for nine years, and I do not know that he ever said to me: “Why did you do such-and-such?” nor ever found fault with me for anything."],[4341,"The prayer of one sitting is like half the prayer of one standing."],[4342,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would not pray the Duha prayer except when he arrived from a journey or departed."],[4343,"Whoever guards his tongue, God will conceal his faults. Whoever restrains his anger, God will withhold His punishment from him. Whoever apologizes to God, God will accept his excuse."],[4344,"There is no one on the Day of Resurrection, rich or poor, but will wish that he had been given only bare sustenance in this world."],[4345,"A time will come upon people when they will be rained upon with general rain, but the earth will not grow anything."],[4346,"There is no possessor of wealth but will wish on the Day of Resurrection that he had been given only bare sustenance in this world."],[4347,"“Did the Messenger of God ﷺ pray wearing his sandals?” He said: “Yes.”"],[4348,"Whoever leaves—meaning wealth—it is for his family, and whoever leaves a debt, it is upon God and His Messenger."],[4349,"I entered the house of Anas b. Malik and asked him about nabidh. He said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade gourd vessels and vessels smeared with pitch.” I said: “And hantam?” He repeated it to me. We said: “What is hantam?” He said: “The green jar.” Anas b. Malik said: “O servant girl, bring me that green jar.” She brought him a jar, and he poured a cup of nabidh for me in it, and I drank it. Then he said: “I did not see a green jar until the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away, but hantam is green jars that used to come to us from Egypt.” Then the servant girl came to him and said: “The prayer, may God keep you righteous.” He said: “Which prayer?” She said: “The ‘Asr prayer.” I said: “I prayed it before entering upon you.” He said: “Wait, the ‘Asr has not yet come.” Then she reminded him again, and he said to her the like of his first statement. Then she reminded him again and spoke to him, and he said: “I have heard what you said. Bring me water for ablution, for people are praying this prayer before its time.” Then he prayed."],[4350,"We set out proclaiming the talbiyah for Hajj. When we arrived in Makkah, the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to make it an 'Umrah, and he said: \"Had I known beforehand what I came to know afterward, I would have made it an 'Umrah, but I have driven the sacrificial animal and combined the Hajj and the 'Umrah.\""],[4351,"Two eyes the Fire will never touch: an eye that stayed awake guarding the Muslims in the path of God, and an eye that wept out of fear of God."],[4352,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out and saw a prominent dome. He said: \"What is this?\" His companions said to him: \"This belongs to a man from the Ansar.\" He remained silent and kept it in his heart, until when its owner came to the Messenger of God and greeted him among the people, he turned away from him. He did that to him repeatedly, until the man recognized the anger in him and his turning away from him. He complained about that to his companions, saying: \"By God, I certainly find the Messenger of God ﷺ's gaze strange; I do not know what has happened concerning me and what I have done.\" They said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out and saw your dome, and he said: 'To whom does this belong?' and we told him.\" So he returned to his dome and leveled it to the ground. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and did not see the dome, and he said: \"What happened to the dome that was here?\" He said: \"Its owner complained to us about your turning away from him, so we informed him, and he demolished it.\" He said: \"Indeed, every building that is built will be a burden upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection, except for what is indispensable.\""],[4353,"Anas came to Kufa. He said: The people came to him and said: \"Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said: while he was saying: \"Leave me alone, O people,\" until they pressed him to the wall of the palace. Then he said: \"O people, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. O people, go away from me.\" So they left."],[4354,"Whoever marries has been given half of worship."],[4355,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the people will surge into one another. Adam will be brought, and they will say: \"O Adam, intercede for your progeny.\" He will say: \"I am not the one for it, but go to Ibrahim, for he is the intimate friend of God.\" Ibrahim will be brought, and he will say: \"I am not the one for it, but you should go to Musa, for he is the one to whom God spoke.\" Musa, the chosen one of God, will be brought, and he will say: \"I am not the one for it, but you should go to 'Isa, for he is the spirit of God and His word.\" 'Isa will be brought, and he will say: \"I am not the one for it, but you should go to Muhammad ﷺ.\" So I will be brought, and I will say: \"I am the one for it.\" I will go and ask permission from my Lord, and permission will be granted to me. I will stand before Him in a station where He will inspire me with praises that I am not able to articulate now, and I will praise Him with those praises. Then I will fall down in prostration before Him, and it will be said to me: \"O Muhammad, raise your head, and speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.\" I will say: \"O Lord, my community, my community.\" It will be said to me: \"Go, and whoever has in his heart the weight of a grain of wheat or the weight of a grain of barley of faith, bring him out.\" So I will go and do that. Then I will return and praise Him with those praises, and fall down in prostration before Him. It will be said: \"O Muhammad, raise your head, and speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.\" I will say: \"O Lord, my community, my community.\" It will be said to me: \"Go, and whoever has in his heart the weight of an atom or the weight of a mustard seed of faith, bring him out of it.\" So I will go and do that. Then I will return and praise Him with those praises, and fall down in prostration before Him. It will be said: \"O Muhammad, raise your head, and speak and you will be heard; ask and you will be given; intercede and your intercession will be accepted.\" I will say: \"O Lord, my community, my community.\" It will be said to me: \"Go, and whoever has in his heart even the least, the least, less than the weight of a mustard seed of faith, bring him out of the Fire, out of the Fire, out of the Fire.\" When we returned from Anas, I said to my companions: \"Would you like to go to al-Hasan? He is hiding in the house of Abu Khalifah among 'Abd al-Qays.\" So we came to him and entered upon him, and we said: \"We have come from your brother Anas, and we have never heard the like of what.\""],[4357,"Anas b. Malik prayed in the mosque of Banu Rifa'ah here. He ordered a man from his companions to give the call to prayer, and he led them in the morning prayer. When he finished his prayer, he turned to face the people and said: \"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with his companions, he would turn to face the people and say: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from a deed that disgraces me. O God, I seek refuge in You from wealth that makes me transgress. O God, I seek refuge in You from a companion who destroys me. O God, I seek refuge in You from a matter that distracts me. O God, I seek refuge in You from poverty that makes me forget.'\""],[4358,"Eat the evening meal, even if it is just a handful of bad dates, for abandoning the evening meal causes weakness."],[4359,"Umm Sulaym heard the words of the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, if only you would supplicate to God for him with some supplications.\" Anas said: The Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated for me with three supplications. I have seen two of them in this world, and I hope to see the third in the Hereafter."],[4360,"Anas b. Malik passed by us in the mosque of Banu Tha'labah and said: \"Have you prayed?\" He said: We said: \"Yes, and that was the morning prayer.\" He ordered a man, who gave the call to prayer and the iqamah, then he prayed with his companions."],[4361,"The Prophet ﷺ consummated his marriage with one of his wives. He said: Umm Sulaym made some hais for him, then put it in a stone vessel, then said to me: \"Take this to the Messenger of God ﷺ and convey our greetings to him, and tell him that this is from us, a little gift.\" Anas said: They were in severe hardship that day. He said: I brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, Umm Sulaym sent this to you, and she conveys her greetings to you and says: 'This is for you from us, a little gift.'\" He said: He looked at it and said: \"Put it down.\" He said: I put it down. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Go and invite so-and-so and so-and-so,\" until he named many men, \"and whoever you meet.\" He said: I came and the house, the suffah, and the room were full of people."],[4362,"She entered upon 'A'ishah and saw in her house a spear placed there. She said: \"O Mother of the Believers, what do you do with this spear?\" She said: \"We kill these geckos with it, for the Prophet of God ﷺ\""],[4363,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing the snakes that are in houses, except the one with two white stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause blindness and cause miscarriages in pregnant women. Whoever does not kill them is not one of us."],[4364,"When a woman gives charity from her husband's house without causing harm, she has her reward, and her husband has the reward of what he earned, and she has the reward of what she intended, and the treasurer has the like of that."],[4365,"Every intoxicant is unlawful. Whatever intoxicates in a faraq, a handful of it is unlawful."],[4366,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the Hajj as ifrad."],[4367,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the Hajj as ifrad."],[4368,"Did you not see that when your people built the Ka'bah, they fell short of the foundations of Ibrahim? She said: I said: O Messenger of God, will you not restore it to the foundations of Ibrahim? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Were it not that your people are recent in disbelief. He said: Abdullah b. Umar said: If Aisha heard this from the Messenger of God, I do not think the Messenger of God ﷺ left off touching the two corners that are next to the Hijr, except because the House was not completed on the foundations of Ibrahim."],[4369,"I do not care whether I pray in the Hijr or in the House."],[4370,"Whoever prays Fajr - or he said: the morning prayer - then sits in his place and does not engage in any idle talk of worldly matters, and remembers God until he prays four rak'ahs of Duha, he departs from his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him, with no sin upon him."],[4371,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray four rak'ahs of Duha, not separating between them with any speech."],[4372,"He used to forbid continuous fasting, and he commanded hastening the breaking of the fast and delaying the pre-dawn meal."],[4373,"The growth of hair in the nose is protection from leprosy."],[4374,"The past nations were one hundred nations: when they testified for a servant of good, Paradise became obligatory for him. And my nation - the fifty of them are a nation: when they testify for a servant of good, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[4375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed witr during every part of the night, and his witr ended at the time before dawn."],[4376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a choice, so we chose him, and he did not count it as divorce."],[4377,"Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us; Isma'il b. Zakariyya narrated to us; al-A'mash narrated to us; from Muslim; from Masruq; from Aisha; something similar."],[4378,"He would not add anything to the tashahhud in the two rak'ahs."],[4379,"What is forbidden by breastfeeding is what is forbidden by birth."],[4380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never struck a woman, nor struck a servant of his, nor struck anything with his hand, except when striving in the cause of Allah. And nothing was taken from him such that he would avenge it upon its taker, unless the sacred limits of Allah were violated, in which case he would avenge."],[4381,"When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him clean himself with three stones, for they will suffice him."],[4382,"Hassan b. Thabit asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to lampoon the polytheists. He said: What about my lineage among them? He said: I will surely extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough."],[4383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, but you fast continuously? He said: That is only a mercy; may Allah have mercy on you. I am not like you. I spend the night with Allah feeding me and giving me drink."],[4384,"The hand of a thief was not cut off during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except for the price of a shield or a buckler."],[4385,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ become angry regarding the affair of Banu Ka'b with an anger I had not seen him display for a long time. He said: May Allah not help me if I do not help Banu Ka'b. She said: And he said to me: Tell Abu Bakr and Umar to prepare for this expedition. She said: They came to Aisha and said: Where does the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intend to go? She said: I saw him become angry regarding the affair of Banu Ka'b with an anger I had not seen him display for a long time."],[4386,"There was in Makkah a witty woman, and she stayed with a woman like her. That reached Aisha, so she said: My beloved spoke the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Souls are troops collected together; those among them that became acquainted with one another are in harmony, and those among them that repelled one another are at variance."],[4387,"He was never given a choice between two matters but that he chose the easier of them, so long as it was not sinful. If it was sinful, he was the farthest of people from it. The Messenger of God ﷺ never took revenge for himself unless a sacred ordinance of God was violated, in which case he would take revenge for God's sake."],[4388,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a boy upon whom they had hung amulets. He said: 'Why do you kill your children? Use Indian costus in water, then administer it into his nose.'"],[4389,"Seek sustenance in the hidden treasures of the earth."],[4390,"Eat and drink until Bilal gives the call to prayer."],[4391,"God loves that when one of you does a deed, he does it well."],[4392,"Draw near to the qiblah."],[4393,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed night prayer in his house, and 'Abbad b. Bishr performed night prayer in the mosque. The Messenger of God ﷺ heard his voice and said: 'O 'A'ishah, is this 'Abbad b. Bishr?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'O God, have mercy on 'Abbad.'"],[4394,"Three men of the Ansar, all from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, no one surpassed them in excellence after the Messenger of God ﷺ: Sa'd b. Mu'adh, Usayd b. Hudayr, and 'Abbad b. Bishr."],[4395,"Abu Muslim al-Khawlani performed Hajj and entered upon 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. She began asking him about Syria and its cold, and he began telling her. She said: 'How do they endure its cold?' He said: 'O Mother of the Believers, they drink a beverage called tila'.' She said: 'God has spoken the truth and conveyed my beloved's message. I heard my beloved say: \"Some people of my community will drink wine, calling it by other than its name.\"' She said: 'And what do the women do?' He said: 'They enter the bathhouses.' She said: 'God has spoken the truth and conveyed my beloved's message. I heard my beloved say: \"No woman removes her garment in other than her own house but that God removes His covering from her.\"'"],[4396,"I perfumed the Messenger of God ﷺ for his entering ihram, and I perfumed him for his exiting ihram with a perfume unlike this perfume of yours."],[4397,"The protection of Muslims is one. If a slave girl grants protection on their behalf, do not violate it, for every treacherous person will have a banner by which he will be known on the Day of Resurrection."],[4398,"A man sat in the courtyard of 'A'ishah's chamber and began to talk. 'A'ishah said: 'Were it not that I was engaged in glorifying God, I would have said to him: The Messenger of God ﷺ did not string words together the way you do; rather, the speech of the Messenger of God ﷺ was distinct, understood by hearts.'"],[4399,"I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he would send the offering while he remained with us, not avoiding anything that the pilgrim in Ihrām avoids. We heard that Ziyād sent an offering and then stripped off his garments, so she said: 'Did he have a Kaʿba to circumambulate when he put on his clothes? For we do not know anyone for whom clothes are forbidden and then become lawful for him until he circumambulates the Kaʿba.'"],[4400,"A woman said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Should a woman bathe if she has a sexual dream and sees fluid?' He said: 'Yes.' Then ʿĀʾisha said to her: 'May your hands be rubbed in dust!' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Leave her. And is resemblance from anything other than that? If her fluid prevails over the man's fluid, the child resembles his maternal uncles, and if the man's fluid prevails over the woman's fluid, the child resembles him.'"],[4401,"We used to steep for the Messenger of God ﷺ in a water-skin whose top was tied and which had a spout, steeping it in the morning and he would drink it in the evening, or steeping it in the evening and he would drink it in the morning."],[4402,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to travel, he would draw lots among his wives, and whichever of them her arrow came out, he would take her."],[4403,"No Muslim dies and a community of Muslims prays over him reaching one hundred, and they intercede for him, except that their intercession is accepted for him."],[4404,"Eat fresh dates with dried dates, for when the son of Adam eats, Satan becomes angry, saying: 'The son of Adam has remained until he ate the old with the new.'"],[4405,"The pen is lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the boy until he has a wet dream, and from the insane until he regains his senses."],[4406,"It used to be steeped for the Prophet ﷺ in a water-skin; we would take a handful of raisins or a handful of dates and throw it into the skin, then pour water over it at night and he would drink it during the day, or during the day and he would drink it at night."],[4407,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in three white cotton garments from Saḥūl, with no shirt and no turban. As for the ḥulla, the people were merely confused about it: it had been bought for him to be shrouded in, but the ḥulla was left aside, and ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr took it and said: 'I will keep it to be shrouded in.' Then he said: 'Had God been pleased with it for His Messenger, he would have been shrouded in it.' So he sold it and gave its price as charity."],[4408,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came back from a journey. She said: I hung on my door a thin curtain with images of winged horses on it. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw it, he said to me: 'Remove it.'"],[4409,"The bedding of the Messenger of God ﷺ on which he slept at night was of tanned leather stuffed with palm fiber."],[4410,"Umm Ḥabība bt. Jaḥsh suffered from prolonged bleeding. She had been married to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf for seven years, and she complained about that to the Messenger of God. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'This is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When the menstruation comes, leave the prayer, and when it departs, bathe and pray.' ʿĀʾisha said: She used to bathe for every prayer, and she would sit in a large tub belonging to her sister Zaynab bt. Jaḥsh until the redness of the blood rose above the water."],[4411,"I asked for the door to be opened while the Prophet ﷺ was praying a voluntary prayer, and the door was in the direction of the qiblah. The Prophet ﷺ walked to his right or to his left until he opened the door, then returned to his prayer."],[4412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform ablution, then kiss, then pray, and he would not renew his ablution."],[4413,"My community will not perish except by stabbing and the plague. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know stabbing, but what is the plague?\" He said, \"A gland like the gland of camels. The one who remains in it is like a martyr, and the one who flees from it is like one who flees from the battlefield.\""],[4414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I had hung a curtain with images. His face changed color, then he took hold of the curtain and tore it down. Then he said, \"Among the people with the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate Allah's creation.\""],[4415,"Umm Habibah bt. Jahsh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—she had been afflicted with prolonged bleeding for seven years—and complained about that to him and asked him for a ruling. He said, \"This is not menstruation, but it is a vein, so perform ghusl and then pray.\" She said: So she would perform ghusl for every prayer, and she would sit in a large tub until the redness of the blood rose above the water, then she would pray."],[4416,"The hand is cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[4417,"He used to perform ghusl from a vessel that was a faraq. She said, \"And I used to perform ghusl with him from the same vessel.\""],[4418,"I used to part the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the crown of his head, and I would let it fall over his forehead when I oiled it."],[4419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in a khamisah (a striped cloak) that had markings. He glanced at its markings once, and when he said the salam, he said, \"Take this khamisah of mine to Abu Jahm, for it distracted me just now from my prayer, and bring me Abu Jahm's anbijaniyyah (a coarse woolen cloak).\""],[4420,"There were women among the believing women who used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped in their cloaks, then they would return to their homes, and no one would recognize them because of the darkness before dawn."],[4421,"Some believing women used to pray the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped in their cloaks, then they would return to their families, and no one would recognize them."],[4422,"Whoever dies while owing a fast, his guardian may fast on his behalf."],[4423,"The wealth of no one has benefited us as the wealth of Abū Bakr has benefited us."],[4424,"Saʿd and ʿAbd b. Zamʿah disputed before the Messenger of God ﷺ. Saʿd said, “My brother enjoined me, when I came to Makkah, to take the son of the slave woman of Zamʿah, and he is my son.” ʿAbd b. Zamʿah said, “O Messenger of God, he is my brother and the son of my father’s slave woman; he was born on my father’s bed.” Then he saw a clear resemblance to ʿUtbah. He said, “He is yours. The child belongs to the bed, and veil yourself from him, O Sawdah.”"],[4425,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray the ʿaṣr prayer while the sun was still rising in her room and the shade had not yet appeared."],[4426,"A group of Jews asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Al-sām ʿalayka (death be upon you).” ʿĀʾishah said, “I said, ‘Upon you be death and the curse.’” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O ʿĀʾishah, God loves gentleness in all matters.” She said, “I said, ‘Did you not hear what they said?’” He said, “I said, ‘And upon you.’”"],[4427,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me one day pleased, saying, “O ʿĀʾishah, did you not see Mujazziz al-Mudlijī? He entered upon me and saw Usāmah and Zayd with a velvet covering over them, having covered their heads while their feet were visible. He said, ‘These feet are from one another.’”"],[4428,"The wife of Rifāʿah al-Quraẓī came to the Messenger of God and said, “Rifāʿah divorced me and made my divorce irrevocable. After him I married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Zubayr, and what he has is like the fringe of a garment.” The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said, “Do you wish to return to Rifāʿah? No, not until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his.”"],[4429,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn over a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband."],[4430,"I entered Paradise and heard in it a recitation. I said, “What is this?” They said, “Ḥārithah b. al-Nuʿmān. Such is your dutifulness; such is your dutifulness; such is your dutifulness.” And he had been dutiful to his mother."],[4431,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān performed ablution in the presence of ʿĀʾishah, and she said, “O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, complete the ablution, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Woe to the heels from the Fire.’”"],[4432,"A man asked the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was standing behind the door listening. He said, “The prayer may come upon me while I am in a state of major ritual impurity, and I intend to fast.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The prayer may come upon me while I am in a state of major ritual impurity, and I intend to fast; then I perform the major ablution and fast.” The man said, “I am not like you; God has forgiven you your past and future sins.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed, I hope that I am the most God-fearing of you and the most knowledgeable of you of the limits of God.”"],[4433,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss some of his wives while he was fasting. Then she laughed."],[4434,"I and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe from one vessel, both drawing from it together."],[4435,"When he wanted to perform ghusl from janābah, he poured water over his hands and washed them, then performed wuḍūʼ as for prayer, then placed his hands in the vessel once, then took them out and put them into his hair, tracing the roots of the hair until he had wetted the skin of his hair and it seemed to him that he had cleansed it, he poured three handfuls of water over his head, then poured what remained over his body."],[4436,"When the prayer is ready and dinner is served, begin with dinner."],[4437,"We entered upon ʻĀʼishah, and she brought out to us a coarse izār of the kind made in Yemen, and a kisāʼ of those you call mulabbadah, and she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away in these two garments."],[4438,"Sawdah was a large woman, and when she went out she towered over the [other] women. ʻUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb saw her and said to her: Watch how you go out, for by God you do not escape our notice when you go out. Sawdah mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ while a bone with meat was in his hand. He said: The bone fell from his hand out of awe of the revelation, and he said: God has granted you a dispensation to go out for your needs."],[4439,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: My mother died suddenly, and I think that if she had spoken she would have given charity. Shall I give charity on her behalf? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Yes."],[4440,"Barīrah came to me and said: I have contracted with my owners for nine ūqiyyahs, one ūqiyyah each year, so help me. ʻĀʼishah said to her: If your owners like that I pay it to them in a single payment and your walāʼ be mine, I will do it. Barīrah went to her owners and told them, but they refused unless the walāʼ be theirs. The Messenger of God heard that, so he asked her [ʻĀʼishah], and she informed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Take her and stipulate the walāʼ for them, for the walāʼ belongs only to the one who manumits. ʻĀʼishah said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood among the people, praised God, and said: Now then, what is the matter with men who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of God? Whatever is not in the Book of God is invalid, even if it be a hundred conditions. And he said: God's decree is more worthy, and God's condition is more binding, and the walāʼ belongs only to the one who manumits."],[4441,"Barīrah was a mukātabah belonging to some people of the Anṣār. She said: I wanted to buy her and manumit her, so I ordered her to go to them and inform them. They said: If you make her walāʼ ours, we will sell her. I sought the ruling of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: Buy her and manumit her, for the walāʼ belongs only to the one who gives the price. She said: She was married to a slave, and when she was manumitted, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: Choose: if you wish, remain under this slave, or if you wish, separate from him. She said: Then I have separated from him. She said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while the cooking pot was boiling with meat, and he said: What is this, O ʻĀʼishah? She said: Barīrah gave it to us as a gift; it had been given to her as charity. He said: It is charity for Barīrah, and it is a gift for us."],[4442,"Abū Bakr came asking permission to enter upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was wearing a mirṭ of the Mother of the Believers. He gave him permission, and he completed his need with him, then left. Then ʻUmar asked permission to enter, and he gave him permission while he was in that same state, and he completed his need with him, then left. Then ʻUthmān asked permission, and the Messenger of God ﷺ sat up straight and said to ʻĀʼishah: Gather your garments about you. Then he gave him permission. When he left, ʻĀʼishah said to him: Why did you not become alert for Abū Bakr and ʻUmar as you became alert for ʻUthmān? He said: ʻUthmān is a shy man, and if I had given him permission while I was in that state, I feared he would not fully convey his need."],[4443,"I bought for the Messenger of God ﷺ a numruqah (cushion) and placed it for him, and it was as though he disliked that. ʻĀʼishah said: I seek refuge in God from the anger of God and the anger of His Messenger. He said: What is this, O ʻĀʼishah? She said: So that when someone enters upon you or a delegation comes to you [it may be used]. He said: O ʻĀʼishah, the makers of these images will be punished with a punishment with which no one in the worlds will be punished. It will be said to them: Bring to life what you have created."],[4444,"Whoever is appointed to an office and God intends good for him, God will provide him a truthful minister: if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him."],[4445,"The Prophet ﷺ took my hand and pointed to the moon, and said: O ʻĀʼishah, seek refuge in God from the evil of this ghāsiq (darkening one) when it becomes dark."],[4446,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a wild animal [or pet], and it would come and go. When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered, it would crouch down and not stir, out of dislike of harming the Messenger of God."],[4447,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ related a hadith, and a woman among them said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is as if this hadith is the hadith of Khurafah.' He said: 'Do you know what Khurafah is? Khurafah was a man of 'Udhrah whom the jinn captured in the pre-Islamic era. He remained among them for a long time, then they returned him to humankind. He would relate to the people the marvels he had seen among them, so the people said: the hadith of Khurafah.'"],[4448,"I never saw the Prophet ﷺ hasten to any of the supererogatory prayers as he hastened to the two rak'ahs of dawn, nor to any spoil."],[4449,"There is no divorce and no manumission in a state of closure."],[4450,"Vinegar is an excellent condiment."],[4451,"The womb is suspended from the Throne, saying: 'Whoever maintains me, Allah maintains him; and whoever severs me, Allah severs him.'"],[4452,"They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the Bedouins bring us meat, and we do not know whether they mentioned the name of Allah over it or not.' He said: 'Pronounce the name of Allah over it yourselves and eat.'"],[4453,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on a mat? For I heard in the Book of Allah: 'And We have made Hell for the disbelievers a mat [hasir].' She said: 'He did not used to pray on it.'"],[4454,"He used to pass by the cooking pot and take a bone with meat from it and eat some of it, then pray without performing ablution."],[4455,"I entered upon the Mother of the Believers, Aisha ؓ, among a group of women from 'Abd al-Qays, and we asked her about nabidh. She said: 'May Allah not benefit you, O 'Abd al-Qays, with nabidh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the hantam, the dubba', and the naqir.' She said: 'But drink from all leather vessels, or what you have tied or hung.'"],[4456,"I entered upon Abu Bakr and saw death upon him, so I said: 'Hayj, hayj! One whose tears never cease to be veiled, for he is, at one time, poured forth.' He said to her: 'Do not say that, but say: \"And the agony of death comes with the truth—that is what you used to turn away from.\"' Then he said: 'On which day did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ die?' She said: 'I said: Monday.' He said: 'I hope [to die] between now and nightfall.' She said: 'He did not die until evening fell on Tuesday night, and he was buried before morning.' She said: 'He had said before that: In how many garments was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shrouded?' I said: 'In three white Sahuli garments, with no shirt and no turban.' He looked at a garment in which he had been nursed, which had a stain of saffron or red clay, and said: 'Wash this garment of mine, add two more garments to it, and shroud me in them.' She said: 'I said: This is worn out.' He said: 'The living are more entitled to the new than the dead; it is only for the pus.'"],[4457,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever seeking revenge for a wrong done to him unless the sacred limits of Allah were violated. If any of the sacred limits of Allah were violated, he was the most severe of them regarding that. And he was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them."],[4458,"Everyone who is called to account on that day will perish. So I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah says: \"He will be judged with an easy reckoning.\"' He said: 'That is only the presentation, O Aisha. As for everyone whose account is scrutinized on that day, he will perish.'"],[4459,"Whoever supplicates against one who wronged him—or he said: against the wrongdoer—has indeed exacted retribution."],[4460,"I am your forerunner at the Pond, waiting for those of you who come to me. By Allah, men will be snatched away from me, and I will say, ‘My Lord, from me and from my Ummah.’ It will be said, ‘You do not know what they innovated after you; they kept turning back on their heels.’"],[4461,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over Madinah to lead the people in prayer."],[4462,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from janabah from a single vessel, both of us dipping into it together, but he would begin and perform wudu."],[4463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me one day to wash the face of Usamah b. Zayd while he was a young boy. She said: I had not given birth and did not know how boys are washed. She said: So I took him and washed him, but not thoroughly. She said: Then he took him and began washing his face, saying, ‘We have been favored that you are not a girl. Had you been a girl, I would have adorned you and given you gifts.’"],[4464,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick person, he would place his hand on the place that pained the sick person, then say: ‘Bismillah, no harm, no harm. Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healing except Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness.’ Aisha said: When the Prophet ﷺ fell ill, I placed my hand on him to say these words, but he pulled my hand away and said, ‘O Allah, You are the Most Exalted Companion.’"],[4465,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever quote poetry? She said: When he entered his house, he would quote, saying: ‘If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would desire a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah relents to whoever repents. Wealth was only created so that prayer may be performed and zakat may be given.’ She said: We used to think that this was from what was abrogated from the Quran."],[4466,"A dabb lizard was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he did not eat from it. I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, shall I not feed it to the beggars?’ He said, ‘Do not feed the beggars except what I eat from it.’"],[4467,"He forbade (using) gourds and vessels smeared with pitch."],[4468,"A beggar came to her, and Aisha ordered something for him. When the servant came, she called her and inspected it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ‘Does anything leave without your knowledge?’ She said: ‘Indeed I know.’ He said: ‘Do not count, lest Allah count against you.’"],[4469,"When he threw the pebbles, slaughtered, and shaved, everything became lawful for him except women."],[4470,"Abu Bakr narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu Bakr b. Abdullah b. Abi al-Jahm, from Amrah, from Aisha, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4471,"I asked Aisha about the vessels that the Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited. She said: The gourd and the mazaffat—which are green jars coated with pitch, brought from Egypt."],[4472,"When Surah al-Baqarah was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited wine and usury."],[4473,"There was a curtain on my door with figures on it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Remove this, for it reminds me of the world.' She said: And we had a velvet cloth with silk."],[4474,"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate God's creation."],[4475,"The Negus sent a gift to the Messenger of God ﷺ, including a gold ring with an Abyssinian stone. The Messenger of God ﷺ took it with a stick and gave it to Umamah, as if turning away from it, and said: 'Adorn yourself with this.'"],[4476,"A gift was given to the Messenger of God ﷺ containing a necklace of onyx. He said: 'I will give it to the most beloved of my household to me.' The women said: 'The daughter of Abu Quhafah has taken it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ called Umamah bt. Zaynab and hung it around her neck."],[4477,"He used to say: 'O God, make me among those who, when they do good, rejoice, and when they do wrong, seek forgiveness.'"],[4478,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught her to say: 'O God, I ask You for all good, the immediate and the delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, the immediate and the delayed, what I know of it and what I do not know. O God, I ask You for the good that Your servant and Prophet asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil that Your servant and Prophet sought refuge from. I ask You for Paradise and whatever word or deed brings one near to it, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and whatever word or deed brings one near to it. I ask You to make every decree You decree for me good.'"],[4479,"He used to say: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire and the trial of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave and the trial of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the false Messiah, and from laziness, old age, sin, and debt, and from the evil of the trial of wealth and poverty. O God, wash me from my sins with water of snow and hail. O God, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west.'"],[4480,"Three traits: either you abandon them or I will fight you. He said: What are they? She said: Beware of rhymed prose; do not use rhymed prose, for the Prophet ﷺ and his companions did not use rhymed prose. When you come to a people who are conversing, do not interrupt their conversation. Do not weary people with the Book of God, and do not address the people on Friday more than once; if you refuse, then twice."],[4481,"I brought the Prophet ﷺ some khazirah that I had cooked for him, and I said to Sawdah—while the Prophet ﷺ was between me and her—'Eat.' She refused. I said: 'You will eat, or I will smear your face.' She refused, so I put my hand in the khazirah and smeared her face. The Prophet ﷺ laughed and placed his hand for her, saying to her: 'Smear her face.' The Prophet ﷺ laughed for her. Then Umar passed by and said: 'O Abdullah, O Abdullah,' and he thought he would enter. He said: 'Get up and wash your faces.' Aisha said: 'I did not cease to hold Umar in awe because of the awe of the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[4482,"Sa'd b. Mu'adh was struck in his median vein, so the Prophet ﷺ pitched a tent for him in the mosque to visit him from nearby. Sa'd said: 'O God, You know that the people most beloved to me to fight are a people who denied Your Prophet, expelled him, and did such and such. I think You have ended the war between us and them. O God, if You have kept any war between us and them, keep me alive for them; and if You have ended the war between us and them, then open this wound and make my death in it.' While he was one night, his wound burst open from his chest, and beside him were the people of a tent. The blood flowed until it entered the tent, and they called to them: 'O people of the tent, what is this coming to us from your direction?' They looked and found Sa'd b. Mu'adh's wound had burst open from his chest, and his blood was gushing and roaring. He said: And he died from it."],[4483,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during his illness: “Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.” Aisha said to Hafsa: “Tell him that Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man, and if he stands in your place, the people will not hear him due to weeping. Command Umar to lead the people.” Hafsa said that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Let Abu Bakr lead the people.” Aisha repeated to Hafsa what she had said before, and he said: “Let Abu Bakr lead the people.” Aisha repeated to Hafsa her words to the Prophet ﷺ once more, and he said: “Leave me. You are indeed like the companions of Yusuf. Let Abu Bakr lead the people.”"],[4484,"Ibrahim narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Aisha, something similar. Then Ibn Abi Mulayka said: “And what caliphate could be clearer than this?”"],[4485,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was shining in my room."],[4486,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to perform ghusl from janaba, he would wash his hands three times, then take water with his right hand and pour it over his left, washing his private part until it was clean. Then he washed his left hand thoroughly, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face, washed his forearms three times each, poured water over his head three times, then washed his body, and when he finished his ghusl, he washed his feet."],[4487,"When he wanted to perform ghusl from janaba, he would perform wudu as for prayer, then put his hand into the vessel and trace the roots of the hair with his right hand on his right side, and with his left hand trace the roots of the hair on his left side, until he thought he had reached the entire skin, then he poured water over his head. Hisham said: Except that before that he would begin by washing his hands three times each and washing his private part."],[4488,"I and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a single vessel. Asim said: Aisha said: He would race me, racing."],[4489,"I and the Messenger of God used to perform ghusl from a single vessel."],[4490,"He was praying and felt cold, so he said: “O Aisha, throw your cloak over me.” She said: “I am menstruating.” He said: “Is it a defect and stinginess? Your menstruation is not in your hands.”"],[4491,"Fatima bt. Abi Hubaysh said: “O Messenger of God, I am a woman who has istihada, so should I abandon prayer?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When the menstruation comes, abandon prayer, and when its main flow ceases, wash the blood from yourself, perform wudu, and pray.”"],[4492,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to touch my head while I was menstruating, and between me and him there was a garment."],[4493,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: “Hand me the prayer mat.” She said: “I am menstruating.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Your menstruation is not in your hands.”"],[4494,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed a prayer, he would make it a regular practice."],[4495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was lying crosswise between him and the qiblah, like a corpse lies, under my cloak."],[4496,"You have made us like dogs and donkeys! I saw myself under my cloak between the hands of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the qiblah while he was praying, and I disliked to pass in front of him, so I slipped away from under the cloak stealthily."],[4497,"A man stood at night and recited, raising his voice with the Quran. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'May Allah have mercy on so-and-so. How many a verse he reminded me of tonight that I had dropped.'"],[4498,"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had seen from women what we see, he would have forbidden them from the mosques as the Children of Israel forbade their women. I saw us praying the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in our cloaks, and we would depart without some of us recognizing the faces of others."],[4499,"They differed about washing the Prophet ﷺ, and sleep was cast upon them, so there was none of them but his chin was on his chest. Then they were called from the side of the house: 'Wash him from behind his shirt.' Aisha said: 'If I could revisit my affair, none would have washed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except his wives.'"],[4500,"Abu Bakr said to Aisha: 'On which day did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ die?' She said: 'On Monday.' He said: 'What day is this?' She said: 'Monday.' He said: 'As Allah wills. I hope for what is between me and night.' He said to them: 'With what did you shroud him?' She said: 'In three white Sahuli Yemeni garments, with no shirt and no turban.' Abu Bakr said: 'Wash this garment of mine from the stain of saffron or red clay, and with it two other garments.' Aisha said: 'O father, this is worn out.' He said: 'The living are more entitled to the new. It is only for the body.' Abdullah b. Abi Bakr had given them a striped Hullah, and the Messenger of Allah was wrapped in it, then taken out of it, and he was shrouded in three white Sahuli Yemeni garments. Abdullah found the Hullah and said: 'I will shroud myself in something that touched the skin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Then he said after that: 'No, by Allah, I will not shroud myself in something Allah prevented His Messenger from being shrouded in.' Abu Bakr died on Tuesday night and was buried at night."],[4501,"His companions entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his illness while he was praying sitting, and they stood praying behind him. He gestured to them with his hand to sit, and they sat. When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he said: 'The Imam is only to be followed. When he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; if he prays standing, pray standing; and if he prays sitting, pray sitting.'"],[4502,"When the Prophet ﷺ bathed from janabah, he would pour with his right hand over his left and wash his private part, and sometimes she concealed the private part. Then he would perform wudu as for prayer. Then he would put his hand in the water, then rub it through his hair. If he thought the water had reached the skin, he poured water over his head three times, and left some water in the vessel and poured it over himself after finishing."],[4503,"I saw you in a dream. I said: When the angel brought you in a piece of silk, he said: 'This is your wife.' When I uncovered your face, there you were. I said: 'If it is from Allah, He will bring it to pass.'"],[4504,"The statement of Ibn Umar about the one bewailed was mentioned in her presence, and she said: 'May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman. He heard the hadith but did not memorize it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said, when a funeral of a Jew passed by him while his family was weeping over him: 'They are weeping, and he is being punished.''"],[4505,"O Messenger of Allah, all your wives have kunyas except me. He said: 'Take the kunya of your son Abdullah b. al-Zubayr.' So she was called Umm Abdullah."],[4506,"The brother of Abu Quays sought permission to enter upon her, and she refused to permit him. She mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'He is your paternal uncle, so let him in.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the woman nursed me, not the man.' He said: 'He is your paternal uncle, so let him in.'"],[4507,"Hamza b. Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of God, I am a man who keeps continuous fasting; should I fast while travelling? He said: Fast if you wish, and break the fast if you wish."],[4508,"Five are vicious creatures that may be killed in the Haram: the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, the crow, and the biting dog."],[4509,"We set out to coincide with the new moon of Dhu al-Hijjah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever wishes to enter ihram for Hajj, let him do so, and whoever wishes to enter ihram for Umrah, let him do so. I was among those who entered ihram for Umrah. She mentioned that when she was at Sarif, she menstruated. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to me while I was weeping. I said: I wish I had not come out this year. He said: Undo your hair, abandon your Umrah, comb your hair, and do what the Muslims do in their Hajj. So she obeyed God and His Messenger. When it was the night of departure, he commanded Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr to take her to al-Tanim, so he took her to al-Tanim, and she entered ihram from there for Umrah."],[4510,"It is as if I am looking at myself twisting the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he does not refrain from anything from which a person in ihram refrains."],[4511,"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ intended to observe itikaf, he would pray the morning prayer and then enter his place of seclusion. On the morning of the twenty-first, he finished the morning prayer and entered the mosque, where he saw tents: the tent of Aisha, who had asked his permission, and that of Zaynab. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do you intend righteousness by them?\" Then he postponed his itikaf until Shawwal."],[4512,"The reinforcements of the Arabs became numerous upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and crowded him to the house of Aisha. He said: \"O God, curse them.\" Aisha said: O Messenger of God, the people are ruined. He said: No, by God, O daughter of al-Siddiq, I made a condition with my Lord that cannot be broken. I said: O God, I am only human; I become distressed by what distresses humans and hasten to what humans hasten to. So for any person from whom a slip occurs from me, make it an expiation for him."],[4513,"The Messenger of God made an appointment with Jibril (peace be upon them both) at an hour when he would come to him. That hour came but he did not come, and in his hand was a staff; he threw it from his hand and said: God does not break His promise, nor do His messengers. Then he turned and saw a puppy under the bed. He said: O Aisha, when did this dog enter here? She said: By God, I did not notice it. He ordered it to be taken out, and it was removed. Then Jibril came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: You made an appointment with me, and I sat waiting for you, but you did not come. He said: The dog that was in your house prevented me. We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."],[4514,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ command the firstborn offering from sheep: from five, one."],[4515,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was dying, and there was a cup with water beside him. He put his hand into the cup, then wiped his face with it, and said: O God, help me against the agonies of death."],[4516,"The jihad of women is the Hajj."],[4517,"The fastest good deed in reward is maintaining family ties, and the fastest evil in punishment is transgression."],[4518,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade continuous fasting."],[4519,"Command your husbands to wash off the traces of excrement and urine, for I feel shy before them, and indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[4520,"He recited: “farawḥun wa rayḥān” (Q 56:89)."],[4521,"The drink most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sweet and cold."],[4522,"\"Ten are part of the fiṭrah: trimming the mustache, letting the beard grow, using the siwāk, rinsing the nose with water, clipping the nails, washing the finger joints, plucking the armpit hair, shaving the pubic hair, and washing with water.\""],[4523,"\"They certainly knew that what I called them to in the world was true, and Allah has said: ‘You cannot make the dead hear’ (Q 27:80).\""],[4524,"We said, “O Messenger of Allah, shall we not build you a house to shade you?” He said, “No, Minā is a resting place for whoever arrives first.”"],[4525,"I purchased Barīrah to manumit her, but her owners stipulated the right of walāʾ for themselves. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Manumit her, for walāʾ belongs to the one who frees.” Her husband was a free man while she was a slave, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice."],[4526,"For a boy, two sheep of equal age are slaughtered as ʿaqīqah; for a girl, one sheep. ʿĀʾishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered two sheep for each of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn on the seventh day, and commanded that the filth be removed from the child’s head. He said: “Slaughter in his name, and say: ‘In the name of Allah; Allah is most great. O Allah, from You and to You; this is the ʿaqīqah of so-and-so.’” He said: In the Jāhiliyyah, a piece of cotton would be taken and dipped in the blood of the ʿaqīqah, then placed on the child’s head. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they put perfume in place of the blood."],[4527,"When he wanted to sleep while in a state of janābah, he would perform ablution as he did for prayer."],[4528,"\"Every drink that intoxicates is forbidden.\""],[4529,"The Prophet ﷺ came in to me while I had screened myself with a curtain containing images. When he saw it, his face changed color and he tore it down, saying: “The people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate Allah’s creation.”"],[4530,"\"Whoever perseveres in twelve rakʿahs of the sunnah, apart from the obligatory prayers, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four before ẓuhr, two after ẓuhr, two after ʿishāʾ, and two before fajr.\""],[4531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rak'ahs between evening and night prayer, performing witr from them with five, saying the salam in the fifth."],[4532,"When a person fell ill, he would say with his saliva and then put it in the dust, and he would say: 'The dust of our earth with the saliva of some of us cures our sick by the permission of our Lord.'"],[4533,"He would not interpret anything of the Quran according to his own opinion, except for a few numbered verses which Gabriel taught him."],[4534,"How much did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray al-duha? She said: Four rak'ahs, and he would add what Allah willed."],[4535,"Indeed, whoever is given his share of gentleness has been given his share of the good of this world and the Hereafter, and whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has been deprived of his share of the good of this world and the Hereafter."],[4536,"He would not perform ablution after the major bath."],[4537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaned toward me to kiss me while I was fasting, so I said: 'I am fasting.' He said: 'And I am fasting.' Then he kissed me."],[4538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked which action is most beloved to Allah. He said: 'The most constant of it, even if it is little.'"],[4539,"We used to hear that a prophet does not die until he is given the choice between this world and the Hereafter. She said: During the illness in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, he was seized by hoarseness, and I heard him saying: 'With those whom Allah has favored among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and excellent are those as companions.' So I knew that he had been given the choice."],[4540,"Whatever condition is not in the Book of Allah is invalid, even if it is a hundred conditions."],[4541,"I have never seen anyone with more severe pain than the Messenger of Allah."],[4542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the revenue belongs to the one who bears liability."],[4543,"I entered upon Aisha, and she called for food for me, then said to me: Eat, for I never ate my fill of food but that I wished to weep, except that I did weep. I said: Why is that? She said: I remember the condition in which the Messenger of God ﷺ left this world. The Messenger of God never ate his fill of wheat bread twice in one day until he met God."],[4544,"The family of Muhammad never ate their fill of wheat food for three consecutive nights from the time he arrived in Madinah until he passed away."],[4545,"The family of Muhammad never ate their fill of barley bread for lunch or dinner for three consecutive days until he met God."],[4546,"The Messenger of God never ate his fill of barley bread for two days until he died."],[4547,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died leaving neither a dinar nor a dirham, nor a sheep, nor a camel, and he did not bequeath anything."],[4548,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed the Hajj as ifrad."],[4549,"The Prophet ﷺ used to touch our faces while he was fasting."],[4550,"He used to seek refuge from debt. I said: O Messenger of God, I see you seeking refuge from debt. He said: Yes, for when a debtor speaks he lies, and when he promises he breaks his promise."],[4551,"He used to perform ghusl from a qadah, which is the faraq. She said: And I and he used to perform ghusl from a single vessel."],[4552,"Mu'adhah narrated to me, from Aisha, she said: So I would say to him: Leave some for me, leave some for me."],[4553,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to us every day at the two ends of the day. One day he came to us at the height of noon and said: O Abu Bakr, is there anyone watching me? He said: O Messenger of God, there is only Umm Ruman, Asma', and Aisha. He said: For my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has granted me permission to go out. He said: The companionship, O Messenger of God? He said: The companionship. Abu Bakr had prepared two mounts, so he said: O Messenger of God, take one of my mounts and ride it. He said: No, rather the price, O Abu Bakr."],[4554,"A thief, or a female thief, was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that her hand be cut off. It was cut off, and he said: If it were Fatimah, I would have carried out the punishment on her."],[4555,"When a man had a sore or something on his hand, he would point with his finger like this, then say: In the name of Allah, the dust of our earth with the saliva of one of us, and our sick is healed by the permission of our Lord."],[4556,"Dawn would overtake him while he was junub, then he would fast."],[4557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not love except one possessed of piety."],[4558,"A young boy from the children of the Ansar was brought to the Prophet ﷺ for him to pray over him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, blessed is this one; he did not attain evil nor see it — or did not comprehend it, or do it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Aisha, is it other than that?! Allah created Paradise and created people for it, and created it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers, and created the Fire and created people for it, created it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers."],[4559,"Amputation was for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[4560,"We traveled by night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-Batḥāʾ."],[4561,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a land called Ghadira and named it Khaḍira."],[4562,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade al-dubbāʾ, al-ḥantam, and al-muzaffat."],[4563,"My mother used to treat me with samna, wanting to bring me to the Prophet ﷺ. That did not succeed for her until I ate fresh dates with cucumber, and I became plump with the best plumpness."],[4564,"War is deception."],[4565,"Ask Allah for everything, even the shoe strap, for if Allah does not make it easy, it will not be easy."],[4566,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked during the campaign of Tabuk about the sutra of the one praying, and he said: Like the back of a saddle."],[4567,"The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted; so may Allah guide the imams and pardon the mu'adhdhins."],[4568,"Sometimes the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come in to us and say to us, \"Do you have anything?\" We would say, \"No,\" and he would say, \"Then I am fasting.\" She said: And once he came in to us, and we said to him, \"Some hays was given to us as a gift, and we have kept some aside for you.\" He said, \"Bring it, for I had been fasting.\" She said: So he ate."],[4569,"Night and day will not pass away until al-Lat and al-'Uzza are worshipped. She said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I had thought that when Allah said, 'He it is who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all religion, even if the polytheists detest it,' that that would be complete.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There will be of that whatever Allah wills; then Allah will send a pleasant wind and take the soul of everyone in whose heart is an atom's weight of good, and the rest will remain and return to the religion of their forefathers.\""],[4570,"I missed the Prophet ﷺ one night from the bed, so I felt for him with my hand, and my hand fell upon his feet while they were upright and he was prostrating, saying: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot enumerate praise of You; You are as You have praised Yourself.\""],[4571,"Three things I swear by: Allah will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share. The shares of Islam are three: fasting, prayer, and charity. Allah will not take charge of a servant and then hand him over to another on the Day of Resurrection. And a man does not love a people except that he will come with them on the Day of Resurrection. And the fourth, if I were to swear by it, I would not fear sinning: Allah does not conceal for His servant in this world except that He will conceal for him in the Hereafter."],[4572,"Ishaq said: And 'Abd Allah b. 'Utbah b. Mas'ud narrated to me, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[4573,"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[4574,"The siwak is a purification for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord. And in the black seed there is healing for every disease except death. I said, \"What is death?\" He said, \"Death.\""],[4575,"There is no divorce and no manumission in a state of compulsion."],[4576,"I said to her, \"O my mother, show me the grave of the Prophet ﷺ and his two companions.\" She showed me three graves, flat and level with the red gravel of the courtyard. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the front, Abu Bakr with his head between the Prophet's shoulders ﷺ, and 'Umar with his head at the Prophet's feet ﷺ."],[4577,"There was not with the Prophet ﷺ when he migrated from Makkah to Madinah except Abu Bakr, 'Amir b. Fuhayrah, and a man from Banu al-Dil who was a polytheist and was their guide."],[4578,"'A'ishah and Umm Salamah were asked, \"Which deed was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" They both said, \"That which its doer persists in, even if it is little.\""],[4579,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to me. I feared that something had been commanded concerning me, and he gave me a choice, so I said: Have you mentioned this to anyone before me? He said: No. I said: I have chosen you. And he gave all his wives a choice, and they chose him, and he did not consider it anything."],[4580,"The Messenger of God ﷺ decreed that the revenue belongs to the one who bears liability."],[4581,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ embrace Ali and kiss him, saying: May my father be ransomed for the unique martyr! May my father be ransomed for the unique martyr!"],[4582,"When I wanted to part the hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ, I made the parting from the crown of his head and let his forelock hang between his shoulders."],[4583,"When the verse was revealed: \"And leave Me with the deniers, possessors of ease, and allow them respite a little,\" he said: It was not but a short while until the Battle of Badr occurred."],[4584,"Ja'far narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr, from 'Amra, from 'A'isha."],[4585,"A woman asked Aisha about the continuous fasting of the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: Do you perform deeds like his, for he has been forgiven his past and future sins, and his deeds were supererogatory? Then Aisha said: As for me, by God, I never fasted through the night at all. God said: \"Then complete the fast until the night.\""],[4586,"Did the Messenger of God ﷺ fast three days of every month? She said: Yes. I said: Which days of the month did he fast? She said: He did not mind which days of the month he fasted."],[4587,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was wrapped in a striped Yemeni garment, then it was removed from him."],[4588,"It is not permissible for a Muslim to shun a Muslim for more than three days. If he meets him and greets him three times, and each time he does not return it, then he bears his sin along with his own sin."],[4589,"The last of his words was a word I heard from him, saying: Rather, the highest companion in Paradise. She said: I said: Then, by God, he will not choose us, and I knew that what he used to tell us: A prophet of God is not taken until he is given a choice."],[4590,"The Messenger of God ﷺ returned and lay down in my room that day when he entered from the mosque. A man from the family of Abu Bakr came in to me with a green tooth-stick in his hand. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at it while it was in his hand, a look by which I knew he wanted it. I said: O Messenger of God, would you like me to give you this tooth-stick? He said: Yes. So I took it and chewed it for him until I softened it, then gave it to him. She said: He cleaned his teeth with it as beautifully as I had ever seen him clean his teeth with a tooth-stick before. She said: Then he laid it down, and I felt the Messenger of God ﷺ growing heavy in my lap. She said: I went to look at his face, and behold, his gaze was fixed, and he was saying: Rather, the highest companion in Paradise. She said: I said: You have been given a choice, and you have chosen, by the One who sent you with the truth. She said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away."],[4591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died between my chest and my throat, and in my house; I did not wrong anyone concerning it. It was from my foolishness and young age that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken while he was in my lap, then I placed his head on a pillow and stood striking my face and lamenting with the women."],[4592,"Ja'far narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr, from 'Amra, from 'A'isha."],[4593,"When the verse of stoning and the suckling of an adult ten times was revealed, it was indeed on a sheet under my bed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, we were occupied with his death, and a domestic animal entered and ate it."],[4594,"The son of Adam was created with three hundred and sixty joints. So if he praises Allah, declares His oneness, seeks His forgiveness, praises Allah, and removes a thorn from the path of the Muslims, and a stone from the path of the Muslims, and commands good, and forbids evil, to the number of those three hundred and sixty joints, then he is moved away from the Fire, and he has secured - or guarded - himself that day from the Fire."],[4595,"Gabriel kept advising me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."],[4596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to place a pulpit in the mosque for Hassan b. Thabit, on which he would stand and recite poetry, defending the Messenger of Allah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: 'Indeed Allah supports Hassan with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends the Messenger of Allah.'"],[4597,"The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice in prayer for every addition and omission."],[4598,"I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and followed him. He came to al-Baqi' and said: 'Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. You are our forerunners, and we shall join you. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, and do not test us after them.'"],[4599,"Whoever introduces into this matter of ours something that is not part of it, it is rejected."],[4600,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would not sleep until he performed ablution. And when he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands, then eat."],[4601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come in to us and say: 'Has anything come to you this morning?' We would say: 'No,' and he would say: 'I am fasting.' She said: One day he came in to us and said: 'Do you have anything?' She said: I said: 'Yes, some hais was gifted to us.' He said: 'I began the morning fasting,' then he called for it and ate."],[4602,"Usama stumbled on the threshold of the door and was cut in his face. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'O 'A'isha, remove the harm from him.' I found it disgusting, so the Prophet ﷺ began sucking his wound and spitting it out, saying: 'If Usama were a girl, I would have adorned him and clothed him until I made him desirable.'"],[4603,"The siwak is a purification for the mouth, a means of pleasing the Lord."],[4604,"The womb is a branch of the Most Merciful. Whoever maintains it, He maintains him; and whoever cuts it off, He cuts him off."],[4605,"I was brought, in what the sleeper sees, a girl in a silk garment. I examined her and found she was you. I said, “If it is from Allah, He will carry it out,” twice or thrice. Aisha said: He married me after the death of Khadija and before his departure to Madinah by two or three years, and I was seven years old. When we arrived, some women came to me while I was playing on a swing. They prepared me and adorned me, then brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old."],[4606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the briber and the bribed."],[4607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said, “O Aisha, is there any piece of bread?” I brought him a loaf and he put it to his mouth, then said, “O Aisha, has anything of it entered my stomach? Such is the kiss of a fasting person. Breaking the fast is only from what enters, not from what comes out.”"],[4608,"He used to pray the two rak‘ahs of Fajr and lighten them, so that I would say, “Did he recite in them the Opening of the Book?”"],[4609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in my house, on my day, between my chest and my neck, and Allah joined my saliva with his. Aisha said: Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr entered with a siwak, and the Prophet ﷺ became too weak for it. I took it, chewed it, then used it to clean his teeth."],[4610,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the wind grow strong, his face would change."],[4611,"She saw the Prophet ﷺ supplicating with raised hands, saying, “O Allah, I am only a human, so do not punish me. Any man among the Muslims whom I have harmed or insulted, do not punish me.”"],[4612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a severe hardship that will occur before the Dajjal. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, where will the Arabs be on that day?” He said, “O Aisha, the Arabs on that day will be few.” I said, “What will suffice the believer on that day as food?” He said, “Tasbih, tahlil, and takbir.” I said, “Which wealth will be best on that day?” He said, “A servant who gives his family water to drink. As for food, there will be no food.”"],[4613,"Whoever dies on this journey for Hajj or Umrah, and dies therein, he will not be brought to account nor judged, and it will be said, “Enter Paradise.”"],[4614,"Indeed, Allah boasts about those performing tawaf."],[4615,"I sat weeping at the head of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me: 'What makes you weep? If you desire to join me, let provision like that of a rider suffice you from this world, and do not mix with the wealthy.'"],[4616,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man performing talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: 'Who is Shubrumah?' The man mentioned a kinship tie. He said: 'Have you performed Hajj on your own behalf?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Perform Hajj on your own behalf, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.'"],[4617,"I spent the morning with Aisha, and when morning came, she arose, performed ghusl, then entered a room of hers and shut the door behind her, leaving me outside. I said: 'O Mother of the Believers, I came to stay with you only for this moment.' She said: 'Enter.' So I entered and she prayed eight rak'ahs. I did not know whether their standing, their bowing, or their prostrating was longer. Then she turned to me, struck my thigh, and said: 'O Rumaythah, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying them, and if my father were brought back to life and asked me to abandon them, I would not abandon them.'"],[4618,"The Prophet ﷺ had fresh water drawn for him from the well of al-Suqya, and sometimes he said: water was made sweet for him."],[4619,"Al-kharaj is by al-daman."],[4620,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I love to pray in the House.' He took me by the hand and brought me into the Hijr, then said: 'Pray here, for this is part of the House, but your people — or his people — fell short, so they excluded it from the House.'"],[4621,"A dried strip of gazelle meat was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in ihram, and he returned it."],[4622,"Abu Musa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, at the season before the notables. Abu Musa Harun al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad b. Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Qays b. Muslim, from al-Hasan b. Muhammad b. Ali, from Aisha, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. Harun said: I heard Sufyan say: al-washiqah is meat that is cooked then dried."],[4623,"A man entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he welcomed him and brought his seat close. When he left his presence, she said: 'O Messenger of Allah, were you not complaining about this man?' He said: 'Yes, but among the worst of people are those who are honored out of fear of their evil.'"],[4624,"The Prophet ﷺ got up from his bed during part of the night, and I thought he intended to go to one of his wives, so I followed him until he stood at the graves. He said: 'Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. We shall surely join you.' Then he said: 'O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward and do not test us after them.' She said: Then he turned and saw me, and noticed me, and said: 'Woe to her, if she could she would have done it.'"],[4625,"I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night, so I followed him and found him at al-Baqi'. I heard him saying: 'Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. You are our forerunners and we shall join you. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward and do not test us after them.' Then he turned and looked at me and said: 'Woe to her, if she could she would have done it.'"],[4626,"When Sawdah grew old, she gave her day to Aisha. She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to allocate to me my day and her day, and she was the first woman he married.'"],[4627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to bring a woman in to her husband, and she had not received any of her dowry."],[4628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be brought young boys and he would pray for them and bless them. A young boy was brought to him and urinated on him, so he called for water and followed it over the spot."],[4629,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rak'ahs before dawn and would make them brief, so much so that I would think he had not recited anything in them except the Opening of the Book, or that he did not recite the Opening of the Book."],[4630,"She heard a woman asking Aisha about a woman whose menstrual bleeding had become irregular, and she did not know how to pray. Aisha said to her: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman whose menstrual bleeding became irregular and she shed blood, and she did not know how to pray. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to tell her to look at the amount she used to menstruate each month when her menstruation was regular, and she should refrain from prayer for that number of nights and days and reckon them. Then she should perform the ghusl for her purity, then wrap a cloth securely as a loincloth, then pray. I hope that this is from Satan and that Allah will remove it from her, if Allah wills. She said: So I ordered her to do that, and Allah removed it from her. So order your companion to do that."],[4631,"I was given nine things that no woman was given except Maryam bt. Imran: Jibril came down with my image in his palm until he commanded the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to marry me. He married me as a virgin, and he married no other virgin besides me. His soul was taken while his head was in my lap. I buried him in my house. The angels surrounded my house. Revelation used to descend upon him while he was with his family and they would disperse from him, and it used to descend upon him while I was with him under his blanket. I am the daughter of his successor and his closest companion. My innocence was sent down from heaven. I was created good and for a good man. I was promised forgiveness and a generous provision."],[4632,"I asked him about the Hijr: Is it part of the House? He said: Yes. I said: Then why did they not include it in the House? He said: Your people ran short of funds. She said: I said to him: Why is its door raised up? He said: Your people did that to let in whomever they wished. Were it not that your people are recently out of ignorance and I fear their hearts would reject it, I would consider including the Hijr in the House and attaching its door to the ground."],[4633,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her: Were it not that your people are recently out of ignorance, I would attach it to the ground and add six cubits from the Hijr to the House, and make for it an eastern door."],[4634,"Umm Habibah and Umm Salamah mentioned a church in Abyssinia they had seen with images in it, and they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Those people, when a righteous man among them died, they built a mosque over his grave and made those images in it. Those are the worst of creation in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection."],[4635,"When I am awake."],[4636,"Whoever supplicates against the one who wronged him has indeed obtained redress."],[4637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would lean his head out to me while he was in i'tikaf in the mosque, and I would comb his hair while I was menstruating."],[4638,"I asked Aisha about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and she said: He would fast until we would say, 'He has fasted,' and he would break his fast until we would say, 'He has broken his fast.' I never saw him fast more in any month than in Sha'ban. He would fast the whole of Sha'ban; he would fast Sha'ban except for a little."],[4639,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about turning around in prayer, and he said: \"It is a snatching away which Satan snatches from the prayer of the servant.\""],[4640,"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."],[4641,"Hind bt. Utba said: \"O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, and he does not give me what suffices me and my child, and I take from him without his knowledge.\" So he said: \"Take what suffices you and your child, according to what is reasonable.\""],[4642,"Dawn would overtake him while he was junub, then he would begin the day fasting."],[4643,"The day of Ashura was a day that Quraysh used to fast in the Jahiliyya, and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast it. When he came to Madinah, he fasted it and commanded fasting it. When the fast of Ramadan was revealed, Ramadan became the obligatory fast, and Ashura was left. So whoever wished fasted it, and whoever wished did not fast it."],[4644,"Hafsa and I were fasting, and food that we desired was presented to us, so we ate from it. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came, and Hafsa rushed to him before me, and she was the daughter of her father. She said: \"O Prophet of God, we were fasting today, and food that we desired was presented to us, so we ate from it.\" He said: \"Make up another day instead.\""],[4645,"She circumambulated with Aisha three circuits. Every time she completed a circuit, she sought refuge between the door and the Hijr until she completed two rak'ahs for each circuit, and with her were some women. They mentioned Hassan b. Thabit and fell upon him, insulting and reviling him. Aisha said: \"Do not revile him. What God said has befallen him: 'For him is a painful punishment.' And he has become blind. By God, I hope that God will admit him to Paradise because of words he said for Muhammad ﷺ, when he said to Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith: 'You satirized Muhammad, so I answered on his behalf. With God is the reward for that. My father, his father, and my honor are a protection for the honor of Muhammad from you. Would you satirize him when you are not his equal? The worse of you two is the ransom for the better of you two.'\""],[4646,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would not leave anything in his house that had a cross on it but that he would remove it."],[4647,"Shall I not tell you about the prayer of a hypocrite? He leaves the 'Asr prayer until it is between the two horns of Satan—or on the two horns of Satan—then he stands and pecks them like the pecking of a rooster, not remembering God in them except a little."],[4648,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite every night: Tanzil al-Sajdah and al-Zumar."],[4649,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite this variant reading: 'fa rawḥun wa rayḥān' (so rest and fragrance)."],[4650,"The first time prayer was made obligatory, in travel and at home, it was two rak'ahs. Then it was increased at home, and it was left in travel as it was."],[4651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from a journey, and I hung on my door a curtain with winged horses on it. He ordered me, and I removed it."],[4652,"A freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, and his wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Is there anyone here from his relatives?\" They said: \"Yes.\" So he gave them his wealth."],[4653,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded for the 'aqiqah of a boy two similar sheep, and for a girl one sheep."],[4654,"A man said to 'A'ishah: \"One of us speaks to himself about something, which if he uttered it his hereafter would be destroyed, and if it appeared upon him he would be killed.\" He said: She said takbir three times, then said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about it and he said takbir three times, then said: 'Indeed the believer is tested by this.'\""],[4655,"The prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night was eight rak'ahs, besides the witr."],[4656,"There was a woman from Banu Asad with 'A'ishah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said: \"Who is this?\" 'A'ishah said: \"This is so-and-so, she does not sleep; she mentions her prayer.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take upon yourselves what you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire.\" 'A'ishah said: \"The most beloved religion is that which its companion persists in.\""],[4657,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in three types: among us were those who entered ihram for hajj and 'umrah together, among us those who entered ihram for hajj alone, and among us those who entered ihram for 'umrah alone. Whoever entered ihram for hajj and 'umrah together did not exit ihram from anything forbidden to him until he completed the rituals of hajj. Whoever entered ihram for hajj alone did not exit ihram from anything forbidden to him until he completed the rituals of hajj. Whoever entered ihram for 'umrah alone and circumambulated the House and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah exited ihram from what was forbidden to him until he began hajj."],[4658,"It was said to her: \"What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do in his family?\" She said: \"He would sew his garment and mend his sandal, or something like that.\""],[4659,"Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"I travel; should I fast?\" He said: \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[4660,"A Jew saw in a dream: \"How excellent a people is the nation of Muhammad, were it not that they say: 'What Allah wills and Muhammad wills.'\" He said: That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Do not say: 'What Allah wills and Muhammad wills,' but say: 'What Allah alone wills.'\""],[4661,"Delay the Zuhr prayer in the heat."],[4662,"The Prophet ﷺ performed witr with five rak'ahs, not sitting except in the last of them. He stood in all of them except the fifth."],[4663,"I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would send them and stay behind. Then he would do what a man outside the state of pilgrimage does before the sacrificial animal reached Makkah."],[4664,"I twisted the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of God ﷺ with my own hands, and he sent them and stayed behind. He did not leave off anything that he used to do."],[4665,"The family of the Messenger of God ﷺ had a small wild animal. When the Messenger of God ﷺ went out, it would play and run about, coming and going. When it sensed that the Messenger of God ﷺ had entered, it would lie down and not stir as long as the Messenger of God ﷺ was in the house, for fear of annoying him."],[4666,"It was my night with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he slipped away. I thought he had slipped away to one of his other wives. I went out, jealous, and found him prostrating like a thrown garment. I heard him saying: 'My black form and my imagination prostrate to You, and my heart believes in You. My Lord, this is my hand and what I have committed against myself. O Great One, from whom every great thing is hoped, forgive the great sin.' She said: Then he raised his head and said: 'What brought you out?' She said: 'A thought I had.' He said: 'Some suspicion is sinful. Seek God's forgiveness. Gabriel came to me and commanded me to say these words that you heard. Say them in your prostration, for whoever says them will not raise his head before he is forgiven.' I think he said: 'for him.'"],[4667,"Dawn never found him with me except sleeping."],[4668,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, I am burned.' He asked him what was the matter. He said: 'I broke the fast in Ramadan.' Then he sat down, and a large basket called al-ʿaraq full of dates was brought. He said: 'Where is the burned one?' The man stood up. He said: 'Give this as charity.'"],[4669,"The plague was mentioned, and I remembered that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'It is a puncture that afflicts my community from their enemies among the jinn, a gland like the gland of camels. Whoever remains in it is like one stationed in a frontier post, and whoever is struck by it is a martyr, and whoever flees from it is like one who flees from battle.'"],[4670,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say in his supplication: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire, from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the grave, from the evil of wealth and poverty, from the evil of life and death, and from the trial of the false Messiah. O God, wash away my sins with water of snow and hail, and purify my heart from sins as the white garment is purified from dirt, and distance between me and my sins as You have distanced between the west and the east. O God, I seek refuge in You from laziness, senility, debt, and sin.'"],[4671,"Hand me the prayer mat from the mosque. I said: 'I am menstruating.' He said: 'Your menstruation is not in your hand.'"],[4672,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to open the prayer with the takbir and the recitation with 'Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.' When he raised his head from bowing, he would not prostrate until he stood straight. When he prostrated and raised his head, he would not prostrate again until he sat straight. He used to say the greeting in every two rakʿahs. He used to forbid the squatting of Satan, and he forbade us to spread the left foot and sit on the right foot. He used to finish the prayer with the salutation."],[4673,"A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise, while it is written in the Book that he is among the people of the Fire. Then when death approaches, he changes and does the deeds of the people of the Fire, and so he enters the Fire. And a man may do the deeds of the people of the Fire, while it is written in the Book that he is among the people of Paradise. Then when death approaches, he changes and does the deeds of the people of Paradise, and so he enters Paradise."],[4674,"He used to say often: 'O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion and obedience.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, you often supplicate with this. Do you fear?' He said: 'What makes me secure, when the hearts of the servants are between two of the fingers of God? When He wants to turn the heart of a servant, He turns it.'"],[4675,"My baggage was in it and it was light, and it was on a swift camel, while Safiyya's baggage was in it and it was heavy, and it was on a slow, lumbering camel that lagged behind the caravan. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Transfer Aisha's baggage onto Safiyya's camel, and transfer Safiyya's baggage onto Aisha's camel so that the caravan may proceed.' Aisha said: When I saw that, I said: 'O servants of God, this Jewish woman has overcome us with the Messenger of God.' She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O Umm Abd Allah, your baggage was light, while Safiyya's baggage was heavy, so it slowed the caravan. We transferred her baggage onto your camel, and transferred your baggage onto her camel.' She said: I said: 'Do you not claim that you are the Messenger of God?' She said: He smiled and said: 'Are you in doubt, O Umm Abd Allah?' She said: I said: 'Do you not claim that you are the Messenger of God? Then why have you not been just?' Abu Bakr heard me, and he had sharpness, meaning a temper, so he turned to me and slapped my face. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Gently, O Abu Bakr.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, did you not hear what she said?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The jealous woman cannot see the bottom of the valley from its top.'"],[4676,"I indeed know how the Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite the talbiya, and she used to say: 'Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka.'"],[4677,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, Ibn Jud'an used to entertain guests, show kindness to neighbors, maintain kinship ties, and refrain from causing harm. Will any of that benefit him?' He said: 'No, O Aisha, for he never once said: My Lord, forgive me on the Day of Judgment.'"],[4678,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married her when she was six years old, and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine years old. Abu Bakr gave her in marriage to him."],[4679,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old."],[4680,"A man recited this verse: 'Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it,' and said: 'Shall we be recompensed for everything we have done? Then we are ruined.' This reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'Yes, the believer is recompensed for it in this world, in his misfortunes in his body, and in what harms him.'"],[4681,"The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three reasons: a life for a life, the married adulterer, and the one who abandons his religion."],[4682,"Abu Hurayra sat by Aisha's chamber while she was praying, and he was talking, saying: 'Will you not listen, O lady of the chamber?' When she finished her prayer, she said: 'O Urwa, do you not hear this man and his talk? The Messenger of God ﷺ used to speak in such a way that if a counter had counted it, he would have enumerated it.'"],[4683,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the doors to be closed, except the door of Abu Bakr, or the small door of Abu Bakr. He said: And Aisha said: 'I did not find my parents except that they both professed this religion.'"],[4684,"Bring us the blessed morning meal, meaning the pre-dawn meal, and sometimes it was nothing but two dates. Al-Zuhri said: The pre-dawn meal is a sunna."],[4685,"Any woman who takes off her clothes in other than her husband's house has torn every veil between her and God."],[4686,"I heard Aisha weeping, so I said: 'O Mother of the Believers, what makes you weep?' She said: 'I ate my fill today, and I remembered that the Messenger of God ﷺ never ate his fill twice in one day.'"],[4687,"Any woman who is married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid."],[4688,"She used to carry Zamzam water in glass vessels, and she mentioned that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to carry it."],[4689,"The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice for every addition and omission."],[4690,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was addressing the people, saying: \"For your place in Paradise.\""],[4691,"The Messenger of God ﷺ held a wedding feast for one of his wives with two mudds of barley."],[4692,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up for ablution, he would tip the vessel, then mention the name of God, then perform the ablution thoroughly."],[4693,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was dying, and there was a cup with water near him. He would put his hand in it and wipe his face, then say: \"O God, help me against the agonies of death.\""],[4694,"\"Do you know what the most wicked fornication is in the sight of God?\" They said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"The most wicked fornication in the sight of God is to deem lawful the honor of a Muslim man.\" Then he recited: \"And those who harm believing men and believing women without what they have earned.\""],[4695,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"O God, grant me well-being in my body, grant me well-being in my sight, and make it the inheritor from me. There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the Mighty Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.\""],[4696,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[4697,"Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, from the Prophet."],[4698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a sinking, a metamorphosis, and a pelting that will occur in the last part of this community. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will we perish while there are righteous people among us?” He said, “Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.”"],[4699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who sees in a dream that he has had a wet dream but finds no wetness. He said, “He does not have to perform ghusl.” Umm Sulaym said, “O Messenger of Allah, and if a woman sees that?” He said, “Women are the counterparts of men.”"],[4700,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution washing each part three times."],[4701,"He used to kiss while fasting? He said: He was silent for a while, then said to me: “Yes,” as if he considered me too young."],[4702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intimate contact with her without ejaculating. She said: “So we performed ghusl.”"],[4703,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that the mosque be built among the dwellings and that they be cleaned and perfumed."],[4704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah in all his states."],[4705,"I have never seen anyone more truthful than Fatimah other than her father. There was something between them, so she said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask her, for she does not lie.”"],[4706,"Eleven women gathered and made a pact and covenant not to conceal anything about their husbands. The first said: “My husband is the flesh of a lean camel on top of a mountain, not easy to climb, nor fat to be carried down.” The second said: “My husband, I will not spread his news. I fear I cannot leave him. If I mention him, I mention his visible and hidden faults.” The third said: “My husband is tall and thin. If I am silent, I remain suspended; if I speak, I am divorced.” The fourth said: “My husband is like the night of Tihamah, neither hot nor cold, and there is no fear or boredom with him.” The fifth said: “My husband, when he eats, he devours; when he drinks, he gulps; when he sleeps, he wraps himself up, and he does not extend his hand to know my grief.” The sixth said: “My husband is inept—or impotent, ‘Isa was uncertain—utterly incompetent. Every ailment is his ailment. He may crack your skull or break your bone, or do both to you.” The seventh said: “My husband, when he enters, he is like a lion; when he leaves, he is like a leopard, and he does not ask about what he entrusted.” The eighth said: “My husband’s touch is the touch of a rabbit, and his scent is the scent of carnation.” The ninth said: “My husband is lofty in stature, long in sword-belt, great in ash, and his house is near the assembly.” The tenth said: “My husband is Malik, and what is Malik? He is better than that. He has camels that are few in pastures but many in resting places. When they hear the sound of the lute, they are certain that they are doomed.” The eleventh said: “My husband is Abu Zar‘, and what is Abu Zar‘? He adorned my ears with jewelry, filled my upper arms with fat, and made me happy, so I became pleased with myself. He found me among people of a small flock in a rugged place, and he placed me among people of neighing, creaking, threshing, and winnowing. With him I speak and am not rebuked; I sleep and wake late; I drink and quench my thirst. The mother of Abu Zar‘, and what is the mother of Abu Zar‘? Her bundles are ample, and her house is spacious. The son of Abu Zar‘, and what is the son of Abu Zar‘? His bed is like a drawn sword, and the foreleg of a young goat satisfies him. The daughter of Abu Zar‘, and what is the daughter of Abu Zar‘? She is obedient to her father, obedient to her mother, fills her garment, and is the envy of her neighbor. The slave girl of Abu Zar‘, and what is the slave girl of Abu Zar‘? She does not spread our talk, does not scatter our provisions, and does not fill our house with clutter. Abu Zar‘ went out when the skins were being churned, and he met a woman with two sons like leopards playing beneath her waist with two pomegranates. He divorced me and married her. After him I married a noble man who rode a fine horse and took a spear, and he brought me abundant livestock. He said: ‘Eat, Umm Zar‘, and give to your family.’ She said: ‘If I gathered everything he gave me, it would not reach the smallest vessel of Abu Zar‘.’” ‘A’ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O ‘A’ish, I am to you as Abu Zar‘ was to Umm Zar‘.”"],[4707,"Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rayhan b. Sa‘id al-Naji narrated to us, from ‘Abbad b. Mansur, from Hisham b. ‘Urwah, from his father, from ‘A’ishah, with the hadith of Umm Zar‘, or something close to it."],[4708,"She narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Abu Zar‘ and Umm Zar‘, and she mentioned the poetry of Abu Zar‘ about Umm Zar‘."],[4709,"Satan comes to one of you and says: ‘Who created the heavens?’ He says: ‘Allah.’ Then he says: ‘Who created the earth?’ He says: ‘Allah.’ Then he says: ‘Who created Allah?’ When that happens, let him say: ‘I believe in Allah and His messengers.’"],[4710,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had intercourse with one of his wives, then slept until morning while he was in a state of major ritual impurity, then he performed the full bath and fasted that day."],[4711,"A man asked, \"O my mother, a man wakes up in a state of major ritual impurity—may he fast that day?\" She said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ woke up in a state of major ritual impurity from intercourse, not from a wet dream, for an obligatory fast, not a voluntary one, then he performed the full bath and prayed, and he completed his fast.\""],[4712,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would wake up in a state of major ritual impurity and complete his fast."],[4713,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would go out to the dawn prayer while his head was dripping from intercourse, not from a wet dream, then he would fast."],[4714,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would spend the night, then Bilal would call him with the call to prayer, so he would get up and perform the full bath, and I would see the water streaming down over his skin and his hair, then he would go out and pray, and I would hear his weeping, then he would remain fasting."],[4715,"Little or much of suckling makes unlawful."],[4716,"When Rafi' b. Khadij died, 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar said, \"Do not weep over him, for the weeping of the living over the dead is punishment for the dead.\" 'A'isha said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ only said about a Jewish woman whose family were weeping over her: 'They are weeping over her, and she is being punished in her grave.'\""],[4717,"I perfumed the Messenger of God ﷺ with these two hands of mine for his entering the sacred state when he entered ihram, and for his exiting it before he circumambulated the House."],[4718,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw a cloud formation, he became alarmed at it and his color changed, and he went back and forth, and entered and exited; then when it rained, his distress was relieved. 'A'isha said, \"I asked him about that, and he said, 'What would make you know? Perhaps it is as He said: \"Then when they saw it as a cloud advancing toward their valleys, they said, 'This is a cloud bringing us rain'\" (the verse).'\""],[4719,"He used to kiss her while he was fasting. He said, \"Yes.\""],[4720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would kiss while he was fasting."],[4721,"He would kiss during the month of fasting."],[4722,"She said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “I consider jihad the best of deeds, so should we not engage in jihad?” He said: “The best jihad is an accepted Hajj.”"],[4723,"I asked Aisha about a fasting person’s touching, and she disliked it. I said to her: “I have heard that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to touch while fasting.” She said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had more control over his desires than all other people.”"],[4724,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending only Hajj. When we were at Sarif—or near it—I menstruated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was crying and said: “What is the matter with you? Have you menstruated?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “This is a matter that Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam, so perform what the pilgrim performs, except do not circumambulate the House until you bathe.” When we were at Mina, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered cows on behalf of his wives."],[4725,"They liked that when a man finished the prayer, he should say: “O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[4726,"He used to say these words."],[4727,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray any part of the night prayer sitting down, until he became older; then he prayed sitting and recited. When thirty or forty verses remained of the surah, he stood and recited them, then bowed."],[4728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me after a journey, and I had hung a curtain over a shelf of mine containing images. When he saw it, he tore it with his hand and said: “The people with the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate Allah’s creation.” Aisha said: So we cut it up and made from it a cushion or two cushions."],[4729,"I saw Ali b. Abi Talib praying after Asr."],[4730,"Najiya bt. Qaraza sent me to Aisha to ask her about praying after Asr. She said: I came to her, and I did not care what she said after what I had seen from Ali. She said: She informed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray after Asr."],[4731,"The Prophet ﷺ and I used to bathe from a single vessel while we were in a state of janabah."],[4732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating, then recite the Quran."],[4733,"He would pray standing and sitting. When he prayed standing, he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting."],[4734,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to sleep in a state of major ritual impurity just as he was, without touching water."],[4735,"I said to her: “Mother, I do not mind not going between al-Safa and al-Marwah.” She said: “What a bad thing you have said, son of my sister. Those who used to enter ihram for Manat, which is at al-Mushallal, did not go between them – or did not circumambulate between them; Sufyan was uncertain – so God revealed: ‘Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of God’ (the verse). The Messenger of God ﷺ did go between them, so it is a sunnah.”"],[4736,"The first thing by which Islam is overturned, just as a vessel is overturned in a drink called tila' (a type of cooked wine)."],[4737,"I said to Aisha: “Mother of the Believers, which of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ was dearest to him?” She said: “Abu Bakr.” I said: “Then who?” She said: “Then Umar.” He said: I said: “Then who?” She said: “Then Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah.” He said: I said: “Then who?” He said: She fell silent."],[4738,"A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ about her washing after menstruation, and he instructed her how to wash. Then he said: “Take a piece of musk-scented cloth and purify yourself with it.” She said: “How do I purify myself with it?” He said: Then he covered his face with the edge of his garment and said: “Glory be to God, purify yourself with it.” Aisha said: I pulled the woman aside and said: “Follow with it the traces of blood.”"],[4739,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss some of his wives while fasting, then she laughed."],[4740,"She mounted a camel and cursed it, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not ride it.”"],[4741,"Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images. He said: I said: “Let us go to Aisha,” and we informed her of what Abu Talha had said. She said: “I do not know. I will tell you what I saw him do. The Messenger of God ﷺ went out on one of his expeditions, and I was waiting for his return. I took a piece of cloth of ours and hung it over the side of the room. She said: When he returned, I stood up and said: ‘Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. Praise be to God who honored you, helped you, and dignified you.’ She said: He raised his head and looked at the cloth but did not answer me at all. I recognized displeasure in his face. He went on until he tore down the cloth, then said: ‘Aisha, God has not commanded us, concerning what He has provided us, to clothe stones and bricks.’ She said: I took it and made it into a cushion and stuffed it with palm fibers, and he did not find fault with me for that.”"],[4742,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray nine rak'ahs at night."],[4743,"The Messenger of God used to prefer the prayer for which he used the tooth-stick over the prayer for which he did not use the tooth-stick by seventy times. And the Messenger of God ﷺ used to prefer hidden remembrance, which the recording angels do not hear, by seventy times. He said: On the Day of Resurrection, when God gathers the creatures for their reckoning and the recording angels bring what they have recorded and written, God will say to them: “Look, is there anything left for him?” They will say: “Our Lord, we have not left anything that we knew and recorded without counting and writing it.” Then God, Blessed and Exalted, will say to him: “You have with Me something hidden that you do not know, and I will reward you for it – and that is the hidden remembrance.”"],[4744,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was praying in my house. Ali b. Abi Talib came and stood beside him on his right. Then a scorpion came toward the Prophet ﷺ, and when it drew near to him it was turned away from him. Then it came toward Ali, and he took a sandal and killed it while praying. When he finished his prayer, he said: “May God curse it. It came toward the Prophet ﷺ and was turned away from him, then it came toward me, intending me.” The Messenger of God ﷺ saw no harm in killing it during the prayer."],[4745,"By God, I repeatedly argued with the Messenger of God. Nothing made me argue with him so much except that it never occurred to my mind that people would ever love a man who took his place."],[4746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love sweets and honey."],[4747,"A gift was given to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was fasting, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, were it not for your fasting we would have presented you with something. He said: Bring it."],[4748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask for lunch, and we would say: There is none... and he would say: I am fasting."],[4749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from the last part of his day when he prayed Zuhr, then returned and stayed in Mina for the nights of the days of Tashriq, throwing the jamrah when the sun had declined, each jamrah with seven pebbles. He would stand at the first and at the second, prolonging the standing and supplicating humbly, then he would throw the third jamrah and not stand at it."],[4750,"Woe to the commanders, woe to the chiefs, woe to the trustees. A day will surely come upon one of them when he would wish that he were suspended by a star, and that he had never held any office."],[4751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place a pulpit for Hassan in the mosque, upon which he would stand and boast on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or defend him. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Indeed Allah supports Hassan with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends or boasts on behalf of the Messenger of Allah."],[4752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would go out to these highlands."],[4753,"I missed him at night—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—and there he was at al-Baqi'. He said: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. You are our forerunners, and we shall join you. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, and do not test us after them."],[4754,"There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."],[4755,"A woman is not married except with the permission of her guardian. If she is married without that, her marriage is void. If he has consummated with her, she is entitled to her dowry for what he has taken from her, and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."],[4756,"He used to fast Sha'ban and Ramadan, and he would seek to fast on Mondays and Thursdays."],[4757,"He used to perform Witr with one rak'ah."],[4758,"I asked her about the woman who adds hair extensions, and she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who adds hair extensions and the one who asks for it."],[4759,"Hind bt. Utba b. Rabi'a came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him. He looked at her hands and said to her: 'Go and change your hand.' She said: So she went and changed it with henna, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'I accept your pledge on the condition that you do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, and do not commit adultery.' She said: 'Would a free woman commit adultery?' He said: 'And do not kill your children for fear of poverty.' She said: 'Have you left us any children that we might kill them?' He said: Then she pledged allegiance to him. Then she said to him, while wearing two gold bracelets: 'What do you say about these two bracelets?' He said: 'Two embers from the embers of Hell.'"],[4760,"Whoever does not beautify his voice with the Quran is not of us."],[4761,"She wanted to free two of her slaves who were a married couple, and she mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: 'Begin with the man.'"],[4762,"I found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a writing: 'The most insolent of people is one who strikes someone who did not strike him, and a man who kills someone other than his killer, and a man who allies himself with other than his benefactors. Whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger. Allah will not accept from him any ransom or justice. Believers are equal in their blood, and the lowest of them may give protection on their behalf. A Muslim is not killed for a disbeliever, nor a covenant holder while in his covenant. The people of two religions do not inherit from each other. A woman is not married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. There is no prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, and a woman does not travel three nights without a mahram.'"],[4763,"Whenever it was her night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would go out at the end of the night to al-Baqi' and say: 'Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. What you were promised has come to you tomorrow, delayed. And we, if Allah wills, will join you. O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi' al-Gharqad.'"],[4764,"Seek good with those who have handsome faces."],[4765,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about poetry, and he said: 'It is speech; its good is good, and its bad is bad.'"],[4766,"Whoever dies while owing a fast, his guardian fasts on his behalf."],[4767,"I heard Umar b. al-Khattab at Mina saying: 'O people, the departure is tomorrow, so no one should depart until he has circumambulated the House, for the last of the rites is the circumambulation.'"],[4768,"Let her depart."],[4769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite every night: 'Tanzil' al-Sajdah and al-Zumar."],[4770,"Water is not made impure by anything."],[4771,"The two rak'ahs of Fajr are better than the world and what is in it."],[4772,"By Allah, besides Whom there is no god, the blood of a Muslim person who bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful."],[4773,"Al-A'mash said: I narrated it to Ibrahim, and he narrated to me from al-Aswad, from Aisha, something similar:"],[4774,"The sciatic nerve, which is the flank, used to seize the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a month, so that he was unable to go out to the people. And I saw him becoming distressed until I took his hand and spat into it reciting the Quran, then I turned it over onto his face, seeking thereby the blessing of the Quran and the blessing of his hand. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are one whose supplication is answered, so supplicate to Allah to relieve you of what you are in. He said: O Aisha, I am the most severely tried of people."],[4775,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during his illness: Pour over me seven waterskins from seven different wells. So they did."],[4776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be brought a vessel, and I would take it and place my lips on it, then he would take it and place his lips where my lips had been. And I would take a bone and bite from it, then he would place his mouth where my mouth had been, while I was menstruating."],[4777,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to his bed and wanted to sleep while he was in a state of major ritual impurity before washing, he would perform a complete ablution and then sleep."],[4778,"I do not accept a gift from a Bedouin. Then Umm Sunbulah al-Aslamiyyah came to him with a skin of milk, which she gave him as a gift. He said: Pour some of it into this bowl. She poured, and he took it and drank. I said: Did you not say, 'I do not accept a gift from a Bedouin'? He said: The Bedouins of Aslam are not Bedouins; rather, they are the people of our desert, and we are the people of their settled area. If they call us, we answer them, and if we call them, they answer us."],[4779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would order his bed to be prepared for him, so it would be spread out for him facing the qiblah. When he retired to it, he would rest his head on his right palm and then whisper something we did not know what he was saying. At the end of that, he would raise his voice and say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, God—or Lord—of everything, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Criterion, Splitter of the grain and the date stone, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock You hold. O Allah, You are the First, before whom there is nothing, and the Last, after whom there is nothing, and You are the Outward, so there is nothing above You, and You are the Inward, so there is nothing beneath You. Settle our debt and enrich us from poverty."],[4780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died with an empty stomach."],[4781,"He forbade killing snakes, except the short-tailed one and the one with two white stripes, for they snatch away sight and cause what is in women's wombs to miscarry. Whoever leaves them alone is not of us."],[4782,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me and was overcome by that which used to overcome him from Allah, so he was covered with his garment, and a leather cushion was placed under his head. Then he sat down, and sweat was pouring from him like pearls, while he was wiping it away."],[4783,"When the Prophet ﷺ received revelation, he experienced what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'Indeed, We will cast upon you a heavy word.'"],[4784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs before the break of dawn, then say in his prayer place: 'O Allah, Lord of Jibril and Mika'il, and Lord of Israfil, and Lord of Muhammad, I seek refuge with You from the Fire.' Then he would go out to his prayer."],[4785,"Blessed is He whose hearing encompasses all things. I could hear the words of Khawlah bt. Tha'labah, though part of it was hidden from me, as she complained about her husband to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, he consumed my youth, and I bore him children, until when my age advanced and my children were cut off, he declared zihar against me. O Allah, I complain to You.' She said: She did not leave until Jibril came down with these verses: 'Allah has heard the words of the one who argues with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah.'"],[4786,"Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him, so I got up and closed the door between me and him. When it was lifted from him, he said: 'O Aisha, Jibril sends you greetings of peace.'"],[4787,"When he wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform the ablution he performed for prayer. If he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands, then eat."],[4788,"There is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."],[4789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not sleep before the 'Isha' prayer, nor did he engage in night talk after it."],[4790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intercourse with his wife and did not perform ghusl until morning, then performed ghusl, prayed, and fasted that day."],[4791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two light rak'ahs between the call to prayer and the iqamah."],[4792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray between the last 'Isha' prayer and the break of dawn eleven rak'ahs, saying the taslim after every two, and performing witr with one. He would remain in his prostration for as long as it would take one of you to recite fifty verses. When the first mu'adhdhin fell silent for the dawn prayer, he would stand and pray two light rak'ahs, then lie on his right side until the mu'adhdhin came to him."],[4793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one night in Ramadan to the mosque after 'Isha' and prayed. Some people saw him and prayed following his prayer. On the second night, he went out again, and the people saw him, so they gathered, said 'Allahu akbar,' and prayed following his prayer. On the third night, the mosque was filled, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out to them. They began acting as if they were calling him to come out to them. He said: 'O Aisha, what is the matter with the people?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, they prayed with you these two nights, and they would like you to come out to them.' Then he went out to them and said: 'O people, take on of deeds what you are able to bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire. The most beloved of deeds to Allah is that which is constant, even if small. If you had kept on, I feared it would be made obligatory upon you.' Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray eleven rak'ahs standing, and two rak'ahs sitting. When he wanted to bow, he would stand and recite, then bow, then perform witr with one. Abu Salamah said: I said: 'How was his prayer in the month of Ramadan?' She said: 'He did not increase in Ramadan beyond this.'"],[4794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk, gold, drinking from silver vessels, and the red saddle cushion. Aisha said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a small thing of gold used to tie the musk?\" He said: \"Make it silver and dye it yellow with a little saffron.\""],[4795,"Whoever tells you that the Prophet ﷺ used to urinate standing, then deny it. I saw him urinating sitting."],[4796,"He used to pray at night nine rak'ahs."],[4797,"Sometimes the Messenger of Allah ﷺ applied kohl while fasting."],[4798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray at night nine rak'ahs."],[4799,"I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ at night. She said: \"He used to sleep at the beginning of the night and get up at its end, then pray whatever was decreed for him. When he finished his prayer, he turned to his bed. If he had a need for his wife, he went to his wife, then slept as he was without touching water. When he heard the first adhan - or the caller - he got up. If he was in a state of janabah, he performed ghusl; if he was not in a state of janabah, he performed the wudu for prayer, then prayed two rak'ahs, then went out to the mosque.\""],[4800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed standing, he bowed standing; and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting."],[4801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he got up for wudu, he tilted the vessel, then pronounced the name of Allah, then performed the wudu thoroughly."],[4802,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in the prayer over the deceased: \"O Allah, forgive him, and have mercy on him, and bless him, and bring him to the Hawd of Your Messenger.\""],[4803,"\"Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, would you order someone else to pray?\" He said: \"It is not proper for my Ummah that an imam lead them while Abu Bakr is among them.\""],[4804,"The woman with istihadah may pray, even if the blood drips on the mat."],[4805,"I asked Aisha: \"Who was the most beloved of the people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said: \"Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah.\""],[4806,"They both met Aisha among a group of women, and a woman among the women asked her about drinks. She said: I do not deem lawful nabidh of hantam, nor of naqir, nor of muzaffat, nor do I forbid except what the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade."],[4807,"The Messenger of God ﷺ and I used to sleep in a single undergarment while I was menstruating. If something of it touched him, he washed that spot and did not go beyond it, then prayed in it."],[4808,"Consult women concerning their marriages, for the virgin is shy and keeps silent, and that is her consent."],[4809,"We were with Aisha when food was brought. Al-Qasim stood up to pray, and she said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Let no one pray when food is present, nor while he is suppressing the two urges."],[4810,"Call for me one of my companions. I said: Abu Bakr? He said: No. I said: Umar? He said: No. I said: Your cousin Ali? He said: No. I said: Who? He said: Uthman. When he came, he said: Move aside. Then he began to speak to him in confidence, and Uthman's color changed. When the day of the house came and he was besieged, we said: O Commander of the Believers, will you not fight? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ made a covenant with me, and I am patiently restraining myself for it."],[4811,"No Muslim dies and a community of Muslims prays over him, reaching one hundred, and they intercede for him, but that they are granted intercession for him."],[4812,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led the people in prayer during his illness while seated. They stood, so he gestured to them, and they sat. Then he said: The imam is only to be followed. When he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he prays seated, pray seated."],[4813,"Sawdah was a large, heavy woman. She asked permission of the Messenger of God ﷺ to depart from Muzdalifah at night, and he permitted her. Aisha said: Would that I had asked permission of the Messenger of God ﷺ as Sawdah asked him. Ayyub said: Aisha would not depart except with the imam."],[4814,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I am burnt. He asked him what was wrong with him, and he said: I broke the fast in Ramadan. Then he sat down, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a large basket called al-araq containing dates. He said: Where is the burnt one? He stood up, and he said: Give it in charity."],[4815,"The Prophet ﷺ would order one of us, when she menstruated, to wrap a waistcloth, then he would caress her."],[4816,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon a sick person, or a sick person was brought to him, he would say: Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal; You are the Healer; a healing that leaves no sickness."],[4817,"One suckling or two do not create the prohibited relationship."],[4818,"The Prophet ﷺ only meant by “al-usaylah”: sexual intercourse."],[4819,"One or two sucklings do not make (marriage) prohibited."],[4820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying in his house with his thighs—or his shins—uncovered. Abu Bakr asked permission to enter, and he gave him permission while he was in that state, and he talked. Then Umar asked permission, and he gave him permission while he was like that, and he talked. Then Uthman asked permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat up and straightened his garment—Muhammad said: I do not say that this happened on one day—and he entered and talked. When he left, Aisha said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr entered and you did not sit up or pay attention to him, then Umar entered and you did not stir for him or pay attention to him, then Uthman entered and you sat up and straightened your garment. He said: Should I not be shy before a man before whom the angels are shy?"],[4821,"He asked Aisha about the two prostrations that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray after the afternoon prayer. She said: He used to pray them, then he was distracted from them, or forgot them, and he prayed them after the afternoon prayer, then he kept them up. Whenever he prayed a prayer, he would keep it up."],[4822,"When I parted the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I made his parting from his crown, and I let his forelock fall between his eyes."],[4823,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was lying on his bed, wearing Aisha’s cloak. He gave Abu Bakr permission while he was like that. He said: He settled his need with him, then left. And Uthman said: Then Umar asked permission, and he gave him permission while he was in that state, and he settled his need with him, then left. He said: Then Aisha said: I did not see you startle for Abu Bakr and Umar as you startled for Uthman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Uthman is a shy man, and I feared that if I gave him permission while I was in that state, he would not fully convey his need."],[4824,"The Prophet ﷺ would pray while she was lying crosswise on his right and on his left."],[4825,"He would pray while she was lying crosswise in front of him."],[4826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform ablution, then kiss, then pray, and he would not renew his ablution."],[4827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry me until Jibril came to him with my image and said: This is your wife. And he married me when I was a young girl wearing a red-dyed garment, and when he married me, Allah cast modesty upon me."],[4828,"A man asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard his voice, he said: What an evil man, what an evil son of the clan. But when he entered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cheerful and friendly to him. When he left, Aisha spoke to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you said: What an evil man, what an evil son of the clan, but when he entered you were cheerful to him. He said: O Aisha, among the worst of people is one from whose obscenity people guard themselves."],[4829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never raised his head to the sky except that he said: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon obedience to You."],[4830,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that Ibn Zurara be cauterized."],[4831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to place people in their proper ranks."],[4832,"A dried piece of gazelle meat was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in ihram, so he returned it and did not eat it."],[4833,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in three Sahuli garments, a lahd was dug for him, and bricks were set up over him in an upright manner."],[4834,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ shielding me with his garment while I was watching the Ethiopians playing, and I was a young girl. So estimate the age of an inexperienced, young girl. She said: It was a day of Eid, and the Sudanese were playing with shields and spears. Either I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or he said: Would you like to watch? I said: Yes. So he stood me behind him, my cheek against his cheek, and he was saying: Go ahead, Banu Arfida! Until when I became tired, he said: Is that enough for you? I said: Yes. He said: Then go."],[4835,"Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Bakr b. Mudar informed me, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salama b. Abd al-Rahman, from Aisha, similarly. She said: The Prophet ﷺ said: Is that enough for you? I said: Do not be hasty, O Messenger of Allah. She said: It was not that I loved watching them, but I wanted the women to know of your standing and my position with you."],[4836,"Whenever it was her night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would go out at the end of the night to al-Baqi and say: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. What you were promised has come to you, tomorrow you are granted respite, and we, if Allah wills, will join you. O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi al-Farqad."],[4837,"A man sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Who is this? They said: So-and-so. He said: What an evil man and what an evil son of his clan—or as he said—give him permission. When he entered, he was affable toward him. Aisha said: You said: What an evil man and what an evil son of his clan, then you were affable toward him? He said: O Aisha, the worst of people in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the one whom people avoid out of fear of his evil."],[4838,"I perfumed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he entered ihram, and I saw the perfume in the parting of his hair after three days while he was in ihram."],[4839,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform wudu after ghusl."],[4840,"The Prophet ﷺ did not come to me in the pre-dawn hours except that he was asleep."],[4841,"The hand of a thief is cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more."],[4842,"Whichever woman is married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid; her marriage is invalid; her marriage is invalid. And if he has consummated the marriage, she is entitled to her dower because of what he has attained from her private part. And if they dispute, then the sultan is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."],[4843,"Whoever from my community carries a debt, then strives to repay it, and dies before he can repay it, then I am his guardian."],[4844,"A man recited this verse: Whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it. Then he said, “Shall we be recompensed for everything we have done? Then we are ruined.” That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Yes, the believer is recompensed for it in this world, in the affliction that befalls his body and in whatever harms him.”"],[4845,"Adhere closely to the qiblah."],[4846,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he stood with the people in the mosque, and they formed rows behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for a long time during the day, until some men collapsed from the heat, until I saw men whose faces were dripping with water. Then he bowed for a time similar to his standing, until I saw men also collapsing. Then he raised his head, then prostrated. Then he stood for a duration less than his first standing. Then he bowed for a duration less than his first bowing. Then he raised his head, then prostrated. Then he stood again for a duration less than that. Then he bowed, then raised his head, then prostrated."],[4847,"I said to Aisha, Mother of the Believers, “Some people read the entire Quran in a night twice or three times.” She said, “Those have recited but have not truly recited. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand in prayer the entire night reciting Surah al-Baqarah, Al Imran, and al-Nisa. He would not pass by a verse containing good news except that he would supplicate.”"],[4848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died of pleurisy."],[4849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid prayer when the sun rises until it has risen high, and he would say, “It rises between the horns of a devil.” And he used to forbid prayer when it nears setting until it has set."],[4850,"I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said, “He used to pray four rak’ahs before Zuhr, then go out and pray Zuhr, then return and pray two rak’ahs, then go out for Maghrib, then return and pray two rak’ahs, then go out for Isha, then return and pray two rak’ahs.”"],[4851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes perform ghusl from janabah, then come to me, and I would embrace him and warm him, though I had not performed ghusl after him."],[4852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in his house like one of you in his house: he would mend his garment and work as one of you works."],[4853,"The chapter “Abasa wa Tawalla” was revealed regarding Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began saying, “O Messenger of Allah, guide me.” At that time, with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there were some of the notables of the polytheists. The Prophet ﷺ began to turn away from him and face the others, saying, “Do you see any harm in what I say?” They would say, “No.” And it was about this that it was revealed: “Abasa wa Tawalla” (He frowned and turned away)."],[4854,"Two rak'ahs before dawn are better than this world and all it contains."],[4855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated, and Umar followed him with a vessel of water. He said, 'What is this, O Umar?' He said, 'Water for you to perform ablution, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I was not commanded to perform ablution every time I urinate, and if I did so, it would become a sunnah.'"],[4856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved to begin with the right in his purification when he purified himself, in combing his hair when he combed it, and in putting on his sandals when he put them on."],[4857,"The Prophet ﷺ would send the sacrificial animal and twist its garlands, then he would not refrain from what a pilgrim in ihram refrains from."],[4858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ garlanded his sacrificial animal and marked it, and sent it with Abu Bakr, then he did not give up anything Allah had made lawful for him until the sacrificial animal was slaughtered."],[4859,"I would rub it off the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; if you see it, wash it, otherwise sprinkle it."],[4860,"When he wanted to perform ghusl from janabah, he would begin with his hands and wash them, then wash his armpits and pour water over them; when he had cleansed them, he would move them to a wall, then he would perform ablution as for prayer, then pour water over his head."],[4861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had insomnia one night, then he said, 'Would that a righteous man from my companions came to guard me tonight.' She said, 'Then we heard the sound of weapons.' He said, 'Who is this?' He said, 'I am Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas; I came to guard you.' She said, 'Then he slept until I heard his snoring.'"],[4862,"I entered with my mother upon Aisha and she asked her about Ali. She said, 'I have not seen a man who was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than him, nor a woman more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than his wife.'"],[4863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform ghusl with a sa' of water and perform ablution with a mudd."],[4864,"Command your husbands to wash off the traces of excrement and urine, for I am too shy to command them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[4865,"O mother, tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, 'His prayer at night in the month of Ramadan and in other months was thirteen rak'ahs, including the two rak'ahs of dawn.' I said, 'Tell me about his fasting.' She said, 'He would fast until we said he has fasted, and he would break his fast until we said he has broken his fast, and I never saw him fast in any month more than he fasted in Sha'ban; he would fast all of Sha'ban, he would fast Sha'ban except a little.'"],[4866,"I would owe fasts from Ramadan, and I would not make them up until Sha'ban came."],[4867,"I was a man who sought out the authorities, so my father seized me and imprisoned me — Mubarak said: and I do not think he said anything except: and he shackled me — then he said to me: By God, you will not leave until you have memorized the Book of God. So I memorized the Book of God, and God benefited me through it, and the world left me, and I began to dislike marrying and doing things. So I entered upon Aisha and said: Sa'd b. Hisham b. Amir. She said: May God have mercy on Amir; he was struck down on the day of Uhud as a martyr. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, I want to become celibate, so I came to ask you about that. She said: O Hisham, do not become celibate, for God said: 'Indeed in the Messenger of God you have a good example,' and the Messenger of God ﷺ married and had children. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me about the character of the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: O my son, do you not recite the Quran? God said: 'And indeed you are upon a great character.' The character of Muhammad is the Quran. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said: O my son, who can endure the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ? The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he prayed, prayed two rak'ahs, then slept a short sleep, then got up and prayed two rak'ahs, and two, and two, and two, and two, and one — or she said: he prayed two, and two, and two, and two, and one — a prayer after Isha of nine rak'ahs, and eleven. When the Messenger of God ﷺ became heavy and his flesh increased, he prayed two, and two, and one, and prayed two rak'ahs sitting."],[4868,"Whoever vows to disobey God, let him not disobey Him."],[4869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he got up for ablution, would tilt the vessel, then pronounce the name of God, then perform the ablution thoroughly."],[4870,"His mother and his maternal aunt entered upon Aisha and said: O Mother of the Believers, how did one of you act when she was menstruating? She said: She would tie a waist wrapper tightly, then the Prophet ﷺ would embrace her belly and what was above that. They said: How did he perform the major ablution? She said: He would pour water over his hands, then clean himself with water, then strike the ground with his hand, then pour water over his head three times. She said: As for us, we pour five times because of the braids. They said: Tell us about Ali. She said: What do you ask about a man who placed his hand in a spot of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and his soul flowed into his hand, and he wiped his face with it? They differed about his burial, and he said: The most beloved of places to God is the place where His Prophet was taken."],[4871,"I and the guardian of an orphan will be in Paradise like these two — and he joined the index finger and the middle finger — and the one who strives for the orphan, the widow, and the poor is like the one who strives in the path of God, and the one who fasts and stands in prayer without slackening."],[4872,"Make some of your prayers in your homes."],[4873,"Aisha passed by a watering place of the Banu Amir called al-Haw'ab, and the dogs barked at her. She said: What is this? They said: A watering place of the Banu Amir. She said: Return me, return me. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: How will it be for one of you when the dogs of al-Haw'ab bark at her?"],[4874,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about a man who steps with his sandals in filth. He said: Earth is a purifier for them."],[4875,"I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about Ibn Jud'an. The Prophet ﷺ said: And what was he? She said: I said: He used to slaughter the humped camel, honor the neighbor, host the guest, speak truthfully, fulfill covenants, maintain ties of kinship, ransom the captive, feed food, and return trusts. He said: Did he ever say one day: O God, I seek refuge in You from the fire of Hell? She said: No, and he did not know what Hell was. He said: Then no."],[4876,"Aisha came one day from the graves, so I said to her: Where have you come from, O Mother of the Believers? She said: From the grave of my brother Abd al-Rahman. I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, did the Messenger of God ﷺ prohibit visiting graves? She said: Yes, he prohibited visiting them, and he had prohibited eating the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, then he commanded eating it, and he prohibited drinking nabidh from earthenware jars."],[4877,"I and the Prophet ﷺ used to perform the major ablution from one vessel; he would begin before me."],[4878,"It was said to Aisha: What did the Messenger of God ﷺ do in his house? She said: He was a human being among human beings; he would delouse his garment, milk his sheep, and serve himself."],[4879,"No Muslim dies and a group of Muslims numbering one hundred pray over him and intercede for him, but their intercession will be accepted."],[4880,"I entered upon Aisha with men with me, and we asked her about a man who touches his private part. She said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'I do not care whether I touch it or my nose.'"],[4881,"She was asked: What did the Prophet ﷺ do in his house? She said: He would sew his garment, mend his sandal, and do what men do in their houses."],[4882,"She was asked about the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ. She said: He would pray sitting, and when he wanted to bow, he would stand and recite thirty or forty verses, then bow and prostrate."],[4883,"I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ sleeping before the evening prayer, nor occupied in idle talk after it; either he was remembering God and gaining reward, or sleeping and being safe."],[4884,"Night conversation is for three: a bride, a traveler, or one who prays at night."],[4885,"It reached Aisha about a woman who wore sandals. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade women from imitating men."],[4886,"Al-usaylah is sexual intercourse."],[4887,"The Prophet ﷺ was bewitched until he would imagine that he had done something when he had not done it. Then one day, while he was with me, he called upon God and supplicated, then said: 'Do you realize, O Aisha, that God has answered me regarding what I asked Him about?' I said: 'What is that, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'Two angels came to me; one sat at my head and the other at my feet. Then one of them said to his companion: What is the man's ailment? They said: He is bewitched. They said: Who bewitched him? He said: Labid b. al-A'sam the Jew from Banu Zurayq. They said: In what? He said: In a comb and combed hair. They said: Where is it? He said: In the well of Dhu Arwan.' Then the Prophet ﷺ and some of his companions went to the well and looked at it and its palm trees. Then he returned to Aisha and said: 'By God, its water was like the infusion of henna, and its palm trees were like the heads of devils.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, did you take it out?' He said: 'No. As for me, God has healed and cured me, and I feared that I might stir up evil for the people from it.' So he ordered it and it was buried."],[4888,"When he wanted to marry a woman to one of his wives, he would say: 'So-and-so b. So-and-so is proposing to So-and-so bt. So-and-so.'"],[4889,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ founded the mosque of Madinah, he brought a stone and placed it, and Abu Bakr brought a stone and placed it, and Umar brought a stone and placed it, and Uthman brought a stone and placed it. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about that, and he said: 'This is the matter of the caliphate after me.'"],[4890,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite while seated; when he wanted to bow, he would stand for as long as a person recites forty verses."],[4891,"We used to go out with the Messenger of God ﷺ having perfumed ourselves with saffron and wars, while in a state of ihram; we would sweat and it would flow down our faces, and the Messenger of God ﷺ would see that and not disapprove of it for us."],[4892,"Which of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ was most beloved to him? She said: Abu Bakr. He said: I said: Then whom? She said: Then Umar. He said: I said: Then whom? She said: Then Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah. He said: I said: Then whom? He said: She fell silent."],[4893,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray while I was lying crosswise in front of him in the house; when he wanted to perform the witr, he nudged me with his foot and said: Move aside."],[4894,"The Prophet ﷺ once sent a gift of sheep to the House and put garlands on them."],[4895,"Consult women about their marriages. They said: O Messenger of God, a virgin is shy? He said: Her silence is her consent."],[4896,"When he wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform ablution as for prayer; and when he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands then eat."],[4897,"He liked sweets and honey."],[4898,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: I know when you are angry with me and when you are pleased with me. When you are angry with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Ibrahim; and when you are pleased with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Muhammad. She said: Yes, by God, I only abandon your name."],[4899,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me. She said: I said: From where do you know that? He said: When you are pleased with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Muhammad; and when you are angry with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Ibrahim. I said: Yes, by God, I only abandon your name."],[4900,"She and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a single vessel."],[4901,"The Messenger of God ﷺ loved sweets and honey; when he prayed the afternoon prayer, he would go around to his wives and draw near to them. He entered upon Hafsa and stayed with her longer than he used to. So I asked about that, and I was told: A woman of her people gave her a skin of honey, and she gave the Prophet a drink. I said: By God, we will devise a plan against him. So I mentioned that to Sawda, and I said: When he enters upon you, he will draw near, so say to him: O Messenger of God, did you eat maghafir? He will say to you: Hafsa gave me a drink of honey. So say to him: Its bees grazed on the urfut. And I will say that to him, and you too, O Safiyya. When he entered upon Sawda, she said: Sawda says: By the One besides whom there is no god, I thought to initiate what you said while he was at the door, out of fear of you. When he drew near, she said: O Messenger of God, did you eat maghafir? He said: No. She said: What is this smell? He said: Hafsa gave me a drink of honey. She said: I said: Its bees grazed on the urfut. When he entered upon me, I said the same to him, then he entered upon Safiyya, and she said the same to him. When he entered upon Hafsa, she said: O Messenger of God, shall I give you a drink? He said: I have no need of it. She said: Sawda says: Glory be to God, we have deprived him. She said: I said: Be quiet."],[4902,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married me when I was a girl of six years, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was a girl of nine years. Then we came to Madinah, and I fell ill for a month, and my hair grew to a bob. Umm Ruman came to me while I was on a swing, and she called out to me, so I went to her, not knowing what was wanted from me. She took me by the hand and stood me at the door, and I said, 'Hah, hah,' until my breath went away. Then she brought me into a house, and there were women of the Ansar. They said to me, 'Upon goodness and blessing, upon the best omen.' Then she handed me over to them, and they washed my head and groomed me. Nothing startled me except the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they handed me over to him."],[4903,"By God, I was in my house one day, and the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions were in the courtyard, with a curtain between me and them, when Talha b. Ubayd Allah approached. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever is pleased to look at a man walking on the face of the earth who has fulfilled his vow, let him look at Talha.'"],[4904,"By God, I was in my house one day, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was in the courtyard with his companions, with a curtain between me and them, when Abu Bakr approached. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever is pleased to look at one freed from the Fire, let him look at Abu Bakr. His name which his family gave him was Abd Allah b. Uthman, but the name Atiq prevailed over him.'"],[4905,"I asked Aisha about this verse that mentions the vision. She said: 'I am the most knowledgeable of this ummah about this. I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about that.' He said: 'I saw Jibril.' Then she said: 'Whoever claims that Muhammad saw his Lord has fabricated a great lie against God.'"],[4906,"I said to her: 'O my mother'—meaning Aisha—'did Muhammad see his Lord?' She said: 'My hair stood on end because of what you said.'"],[4907,"He saw Jibril in his true form twice."],[4908,"I asked al-Zuhri: 'Which of the wives of the Messenger of God ﷺ sought refuge from him?' He said: ..."],[4909,"We used to place the toothstick of the Messenger of God ﷺ with his things for purification. She said: I said: 'O Messenger of God, you do not neglect the toothstick.' He said: 'Yes, if I were able to do that at every prayer, I would do it.'"],[4910,"No wealth has benefited us; no wealth of Abu Bakr has benefited us."],[4911,"There is no marriage without a guardian. Hushaym said: 'And the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian.'"],[4912,"There is no marriage without a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."],[4913,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would come in to me while I was playing with dolls, and he would sit with me and watch me for a long time, then he would get up."],[4914,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted incantations (ruqya) for the poison (or venomous sting)."],[4915,"The Messenger of God ﷺ once did something and permitted it. It reached him that some men abstained from it. He stood and delivered a sermon, saying: \"What is the matter with men who, knowing that I have done something and permitted it, abstain from it? By God, I am the most knowledgeable of them about God and the most fearful of Him among them.\""],[4916,"He used to fast all of Sha'ban. She said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, is Sha'ban the most beloved month for you to fast?\" He said: \"God decrees for every soul that dies in that year; I like my term to come while I am fasting.\""],[4917,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to observe i'tikaf, he would pray the dawn prayer and then enter his place of seclusion. On the morning of the twenty-first, he left after the dawn prayer and entered the mosque, where he saw tents: the tent of Aisha, who had asked his permission, and of Hafsa and Zaynab. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Is it piety you intend by them?\" He then delayed his i'tikaf until Shawwal."],[4918,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about turning around during the prayer. He said: \"It is a snatching away that Satan steals from a servant's prayer.\""],[4919,"He said to her: \"Hand me my cloak.\" She handed it to him, and he went out and ascended the pulpit. The people gathered around him, and he said: \"O people, God says: 'You shall enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong before you become barren and ask for rain but are not given rain.' O people, God says: 'You shall enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong before you supplicate and it is not answered for you.'\""],[4920,"The tooth-stick (siwak) is a purification for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord."],[4921,"The tooth-stick (siwak) is a purification for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord."],[4922,"Regarding His saying: 'And those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful that they will return to their Lord' (23:60), he said: \"O daughter of al-Siddiq\"—or \"O daughter of Abu Bakr\"—\"those who pray and fast while fearing that it will not be accepted from them, and give charity while fearing that it will not be accepted from them.\""],[4923,"Whoever sleeps after the afternoon prayer and loses his mind should blame no one but himself."],[4924,"Hamza b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"O Messenger of God, should I fast while traveling?\" He said: \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[4925,"\"O Aisha, if I wished, mountains of gold would travel with me. An angel came to me whose belt was as large as the Ka'ba and said: 'Your Lord sends you greetings of peace and says: If you wish, be a prophet-servant, and if you wish, a prophet-king.'\" He said: \"I looked at Jibril, and he gestured to me to humble yourself. So I said: 'A prophet-servant.'\" After that, the Messenger of God ﷺ would not eat reclining, saying: \"I eat as a servant eats and sit as a servant sits.\""],[4926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set the waiting period of Barirah, when her husband separated from her, as the waiting period of a divorced woman."],[4927,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seek refuge in his prayer from the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal."],[4928,"A gazelle hide with beads was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he divided it between the free and the slave woman. She said: My father used to divide between the free and the slave."],[4929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided Surah al-Baqarah into two rak'ahs."],[4930,"It was mentioned to her that some people say: There is no ghusl except from water. She said: I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that, and we performed ghusl."],[4931,"They discussed in a circle in which I was present what makes ghusl obligatory. Some said: When the man has intercourse, and others said: Until the water (semen) is emitted. He said: I said: I will bring you knowledge of that. I came to Aisha, Mother of the Believers, and said to her: O Mother of the Believers, I want to ask you about something, and I am shy to ask you about it. She said: Do not be shy to ask me about what you would ask your mother, for I am only your mother. I said: O mother, what makes ghusl obligatory? She said: You have come to one well informed. When he sits between her four limbs and the two circumcised parts meet, then ghusl becomes obligatory."],[4932,"Who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached my family? By Allah, by Allah, by Allah - three times - I have known nothing but good from my family. And they have mentioned a man about whom I knew nothing but good, and he never entered upon my family except with me. Sa'd b. Mu'adh stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, I, by Allah, will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, we will strike his neck; and if he is from our brothers, the Khazraj, you command us and we will do your command regarding him. Sa'd b. 'Ubadah stood up, and he was the chief of the Khazraj. Before that he was a righteous man, but partisanship carried him away, and he said: You lie, by the life of Allah. By Allah, you will not kill him, and you cannot kill him. Usayd b. Hudayr stood up and said: You lie, by the life of Allah. By Allah, we will surely kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites. He said: The two tribes, the Aws and the Khazraj, arose until they advanced, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He said: He descended and calmed them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I wept that day, my tears would not stop, and I could not sleep. My parents came to me in the morning; I had wept for two nights and a day, until I thought that weeping would split my liver. She said: While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission, and I permitted her. She sat weeping with me. While we were thus, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and sat. He had not sat with me since the day what was said was said before that, and he had remained a month without receiving revelation concerning my affair. She said: He pronounced the testimony of faith, then said: To proceed, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such-and-such. If you are innocent, Allah will declare your innocence; and if you have committed a sin, then seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant acknowledges his sin and then repents, Allah turns to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears stopped, so much so that I felt not a drop. I said to my father: Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf regarding what he said. She said: He said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said to my mother: Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf regarding what he said. She said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: I was a young girl, not reading much of the Quran. I said: By Allah, I know that you have heard what has been spoken, and it has settled in your hearts, and you have believed it. If I say to you that I am innocent - and Allah knows that I am innocent - you will not believe me. And if I confess to you a matter - Allah knows that I am innocent of it - you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me and you except the father of Yusuf when he said: 'So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe.' She said: Then I turned on my bed, hoping that Allah would declare my innocence, but by Allah, I did not think that revelation would be sent down concerning my affair that would be recited. I considered myself too insignificant for the Quran to speak about my matter, but I hoped that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ would see a dream in his sleep that would declare my innocence. She said: By Allah, he did not leave his seat, and no one of the household went out, until revelation came upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him of the intense distress, until sweat like pearls poured from him on a cold day. She said: When the revelation was lifted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he was smiling, and the first word he spoke was: O Aisha, praise Allah, for He has declared your innocence. My mother said to me: Rise to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: By Allah, I will not rise to him, and I will praise none but Allah. And Allah sent down: 'Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you...' all the verses. When Allah sent down this regarding my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq - and he used to spend on Mistah b. Uthathah because of his kinship to him - said: By Allah, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha. Then Allah sent down this verse: 'And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give to the near of kin, the needy, and the emigrants in the way of Allah; and let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.' Abu Bakr said: Yes, by Allah, I love that Allah should forgive me. So he returned to Mistah the provision he used to give him. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair, saying: O Zaynab, what do you know, and what have you seen? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I guard my hearing and my sight. By Allah, I know nothing but good about her. Aisha said: She was the one who rivaled me, but Allah protected her through piety."],[4933,"Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Rabi'ah b. Abi 'Abd al-Rahman and Yahya b. Sa'id, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad b. Abi Bakr, something similar."],[4934,"Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hisham b. 'Urwah, from his father, from Aisha and 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, something similar."],[4935,"The people of the slander were flogged with the legal punishment, and we do not know that."],[4936,"The people talked about this matter, and it spread among them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to give a sermon, and I was unaware of it. She said: One night I went out with Umm Mistah to relieve myself, and she stumbled and said: May Mistah perish. I said: Glory be to Allah, why do you insult your son when he is among the first emigrants and witnessed Badr? She said: By Allah, I do not insult him except because of you. I said: What is my affair? She informed me of the matter, and my need went away, and I felt nothing. I became feverish and went home, and there was my mother below, and my father on top of the house praying. She embraced me and wept, and I wept. Abu Bakr heard our weeping and said: What is the matter with my daughter? My mother said: She has heard that news. He said: Stay where you are until we go in the morning to the Messenger of Allah. We went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was a woman of the Ansar. The presence of that woman did not prevent the Prophet ﷺ from speaking. He said: O Aisha, if you have done wrong or erred, then seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. I said to my father: Speak. He said: What shall I say? I said to my mother: Speak. She said: What shall I say? I praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: By Allah, if I say, 'I did it,' and Allah knows I did not do it, you will say, 'She has confessed.' And if I say, 'I did not do it,' and Allah knows I did not do it, you will say, 'She has lied.' I find no example for me and you except what the righteous servant said - I forgot his name - I said: the father of Yusuf: 'So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a Nubian slave girl and said: O so-and-so, what do you know of Aisha? She said: By Allah, I know no fault in Aisha except that she sleeps, and the domestic animal enters and eats her dough and her mat. When she realized what he wanted, she said: By Allah, I know nothing of Aisha except what the goldsmith knows of pure red gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: Advise me, O assembly of Muslims, regarding people who have slandered my family. By Allah, I have never known any evil from my family, and they slandered them because of whom? By Allah, I have never known any evil from him, and he never entered my house except with me present, and I never traveled except with him. Sa'd b. Mu'adh said: I think, O Messenger of Allah, that you should strike their necks. Men from the Khazraj stood up and said: By Allah, if they were from your tribe, the Aws, you would not have ordered their necks to be struck, until there was almost a conflict between the Aws and the Khazraj. And revelation came upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Aisha said: It was not lifted from him until I saw joy between his eyes. He said: Rejoice, O Aisha, Allah has sent down your excuse. My parents said: Rise, and kiss the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: I praise Allah, not you two. He recited to them the Quran: 'Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you. Do not think it bad for you; rather, it is good for you. For each person among them is what he earned of sin, and the one who took upon himself the greater part of it will have a great punishment. And why, when you heard it, did you not say, 'It is not for us to speak of this. Exalted are You, this is a great slander'?' Among those who took upon themselves the greater part were Hassan b. Thabit, Mistah b. Uthathah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh. It was spoken of in the presence of 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy, and he would hear it, seek it out, and spread it. When Hassan b. Thabit was insulted in the presence of Aisha, she said: Do not insult Hassan, for he used to defend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then she said: What punishment is greater than the loss of his two eyes? And the one about whom it was said what was said said: By Allah, I have never uncovered the side of any female, and he was killed as a martyr in the way of Allah. Hassan b. Thabit said, contradicting himself: 'Chaste and composed, she is not suspected of any fault, and she rises hungry from the flesh of the heedless. If I have said what you have claimed, then may my whip never be carried by my fingers. How could it be, when my love, as long as I live, and my support are for the family of the Messenger of Allah, the adornment of gatherings? Would I insult the best of people as a husband, as a father, and as a soul? I have indeed been brought down to the worst of stations.'"],[4937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged those who said what they said about Aisha, eighty lashes each: Hassan b. Thabit, Mistah b. Uthathah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh."],[4938,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he intended to set out on a journey, would draw lots among his wives; whichever of them her lot came out, he took her out with him. Aisha said: So he drew lots among us for a raid he undertook; my lot came out for it, and I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ after the veil had been revealed. I was carried in a howdah and let down from it. We traveled until, when the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished that raid of his and turned back, and we drew near Madinah returning, he gave us permission to set out at night. I got up when he gave permission and walked until I had passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business, I came back to my baggage and felt my chest, and found that a necklace of mine made of Dhafir beads had broken. I went back and searched for my necklace, and its search detained me. She said: The party who used to load my howdah came and lifted it up and placed it on my camel that I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. Women in those days were light, not yet weighed down by flesh; we ate only morsels of food. The people did not notice the lightness of the howdah, so they lifted it and loaded it. I was a girl of young age. They sent the camel off and departed. I found my necklace after the army had moved on. I came to their camp, but there was no one calling or answering. I made for the place where I had been staying, and I thought they would miss me and return to me. While I was sitting at my place, sleep overcame me and I slept. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army; he had set out late and reached my place in the morning. He saw the dark shape of a sleeping person and recognized me when he saw me, for he used to see me before the veil. I woke up at his saying 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we return' when he recognized me, and I covered my face with my outer garment. By God, I did not speak a word, and I did not hear from him a word other than his 'Indeed we belong to God' when he made his riding camel kneel and stepped on its foreleg. I got up and mounted it. He set off leading the camel until we came to the army while they were encamped. She said: Then those who perished perished, and the one who took the greatest part in it among them was 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. 'Urwa said: I was told that it was being circulated and talked about in his presence, and he would affirm it, spread it, and seek it out. Ibrahim said: meaning he would seek it out. 'Urwa said: No one among the people of the slander was named except Mistah b. Uthatha and Hamna bt. Jahsh, along with others I do not know, except that they were a group, as God said, and the greatest part of it was attributed to 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. 'Urwa said: Aisha disliked that Hassan b. Thabit be reviled in her presence, and she said: It is he who said: 'Indeed my father, his father, and my honor are a protection for the honor of Muhammad from you.' Aisha said: I arrived in Madinah and fell ill for a month after my arrival, while the people were engrossed in the talk of the people of the slander, and I was unaware of any of that. What troubled me in my sickness was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of God ﷺ the kindness I used to see when I was ill; he would only come in to me and say, 'How is this one of yours?' and leave. That is what troubled me, and I did not realize until I went out after I had recovered. I went out with Umm Mistah toward al-Manas', which was our place for relieving ourselves. Our practice was that of the early Arabs regarding sanitation: before the privy, we disliked the latrines and did not adopt them near our houses. She said: I set off, I and Umm Mistah, who was the daughter of Abu Ruhm b. al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf, and her mother was the daughter of Sakhr b. 'Amir, the maternal aunt of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and her son was Mistah b. Uthatha b. 'Abbad b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. I came, I and Umm Mistah, toward my house after we had finished our business. Umm Mistah stumbled in her long garment and said, 'May Mistah perish!' I said to her, 'How bad is what you said! Do you revile a man who was present at Badr?' She said, 'O you, have you not heard what he said?' I said, 'And what did he say?' She told me what the people of the slander had said. She said: I increased in sickness upon my sickness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me and said, 'How is this one of yours?' I said, 'Permit me to go to my parents.' She said: I wanted to ascertain the news from them. The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted me, so I went to them and said to my mother, 'O Mother, what are the people saying?' She said, 'Take it lightly, for by God, seldom has a woman been beautiful and loved by her husband, having co-wives, except that they exaggerate against her.' She said: I said, 'Glory be to God! Have the people really been talking about this?' She said: I wept that night until morning; my tears did not cease, and I did not taste sleep. She said: Then I woke up weeping. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ called 'Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd to consult them about separating from his wife. She said: As for Usama b. Zayd, he advised the Messenger of God ﷺ according to what he knew of his wife's innocence and what he knew of his own feelings toward them. Usama b. Zayd said, 'O Messenger of God, she is your family, and we know nothing but good.' As for 'Ali, he said, 'O Messenger of God, God has not made women scarce for you; women other than her are many. Ask the slave girl, and she will tell you the truth.' She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ called Barira and said, 'O Barira, have you seen anything that troubles you?' Barira said to him, 'By Him who sent you with the truth, I have never seen anything about her that I could find fault with, except that she is a young girl who sleeps over her family's dough, and then the domestic animal comes and eats it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up that day and sought to be excused from 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul while he was on the pulpit. He said, 'O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harm concerning my family has reached me? By God, I know nothing but good about my family, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he never entered my family except with me.' Sa'd b. Mu'adh, one of the Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, stood up and said, 'O Messenger of God, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, I will strike his neck; if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj, you commanded us, and we will do what you commanded us.' He said: A man from the Khazraj stood up, and Umm Hassan was a daughter of his paternal cousin from his clan, and he was Sa'd b. 'Ubada, the chief of the Khazraj. He was a righteous man, but partisanship carried him away. He said to Sa'd b. Mu'adh, 'You have lied! By the life of God, you will not kill him, nor can you kill him. If he had been from your clan, you would not have liked to kill him.' Usayd b. Hudayr, who was the cousin of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, stood up and said to Sa'd b. 'Ubada, 'You have lied! By the life of God, we will surely kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.' She said: The two tribes, the Aws and the Khazraj, rose up until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting on the pulpit. The Messenger of God ﷺ kept calming them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I wept that whole day; my tears did not cease, and I did not taste sleep. She said: My parents came to me in the morning; I wept all that day and night; my tears did not cease, and I did not taste sleep. She said: Until I thought that weeping would split my liver. She said: While my parents were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission to enter upon me, and I permitted her. She sat down weeping with me. She said: While we were in that state, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered, greeted, and sat down. She said: He had not sat with me since what was said to me had been said. He had remained a month without receiving revelation concerning my affair. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ recited the shahada when he sat, then said, 'To proceed, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, God will declare you innocent; if you have committed a sin, ask God's forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses and repents, God turns to him.' She said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his speech, my tears dried up so that I felt not a drop. I said to my father, 'Answer the Messenger of God on my behalf regarding what he said.' He said, 'By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' She said: I said to my mother, 'Answer the Messenger of God on my behalf regarding what he said.' She said, 'By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' She said: I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Quran, 'Indeed, by God, I know, and you have heard, until it settled in your hearts and you believed it. If I say to you that I am innocent, you will not believe me. If I confess to something, and God knows that I am innocent of it, you will believe me. By God, I find no example for me and for you except the father of Joseph when he said: So patience is most fitting, and God is the One sought for help against what you describe.' She said: Then I turned and lay down on my bed. God knew then that I was innocent, and God would declare me innocent with my innocence, but by God, I did not think that God would send down revelation concerning my affair, for my affair was too insignificant in my own eyes for God to speak about me with a clarifying matter. But I hoped that the Messenger of God ﷺ would see a dream in which God would declare me innocent. She said: By God, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not rise from his seat, nor did anyone of the household leave, until God sent down upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him from the intense revelation, until sweat dripped from him like pearls, even though it was a cold day, because of the weight of the Quran that was being sent down upon him. She said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ was relieved, and he was laughing. The first word he spoke was, 'O Aisha, as for God, He has declared you innocent.' She said: My mother said, 'Get up to him.' I said, 'By God, I will not get up to him, and I praise no one but God.' God sent down: 'Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you. Do not think it bad for you...' the verses. When God sent this down concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who was spending on Mistah b. Uthatha because of his kinship and poverty, said, 'By God, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha.' Then God sent down: 'Let not those of virtue among you and abundance swear not to give to the near of kin...' until His saying: 'And God is Forgiving, Merciful.' Abu Bakr said, 'Yes, by God, I love that God should forgive me.' He returned to Mistah the spending he used to give him. He said, 'By God, I will never take it away from him.' She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ had asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair. He said to Zaynab, 'What do you know or what have you seen?' She said, 'O Messenger of God, I guard my hearing and my sight. By God, I know nothing but good.' Aisha said: She was the one who used to rival me among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, but God protected her through piety. Her sister Hamna began to fight, and she perished among those who perished. Ibn Shihab said: This is what reached me from the account of these people."],[4939,"By God, the man about whom what was said was said would say: Glory be to God! By God, I never uncovered the side of any female. She said: Then he was killed after that in the way of God."],[4940,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he intended a journey, would draw lots among his wives; whichever of them her lot came out, the Messenger of God ﷺ took her out with him. When it was the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq, he drew lots among his wives as he used to do, and my lot came out over theirs, so the Messenger of God ﷺ took me out with him. She said: Women in those days only ate morsels; they were not stuffed with meat so as to become heavy. When my camel was loaded and I sat in my howdah, the people who loaded it for me would come and lift me from below the howdah, then place it on the back of the camel and tie it with its ropes, then take the head of the camel and set off. She said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished that journey of his, he turned back returning, until when he came near Madinah, he stopped at a place and spent part of the night there. Then permission was given to the people to set out, and the people departed. I went out for some need of mine, and around my neck was a necklace of mine made of Dhafir beads. When I finished, it slipped from my neck without my knowing. When I returned to the baggage, I went to feel for it on my neck and did not find it. The people had already begun to depart. I went back to the place I had gone to and searched for it until I found it. The people who loaded the camel for me came behind me and had finished loading it. They took the howdah thinking I was in it, as I used to be, and lifted it up and tied it on the camel without doubting that I was in it, then took the head of the camel and set off with it. I returned to the army, but there was no one calling or answering; the people had gone. She said: I wrapped myself in my outer garment and lay down in my place, knowing that if I were missed, they would return to me. She said: By God, while I was lying down, Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami passed by me. He had stayed behind from the army for some need of his and had not followed the people. He saw my dark shape and came until he stood over me. He used to see me before the veil was imposed. When he saw me, he said, 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we return, a wife of the Messenger of God ﷺ,' while I was wrapped in my garments. He said, 'What kept you back, may God have mercy on you?' She said: I did not speak to him. Then he brought the camel close and said, 'Ride,' and he kept back from me. She said: I rode, and he took the head of the camel and set off quickly seeking the people. By God, we did not catch up with the people, and I was not missed until morning when the people had stopped. When they had settled, the man appeared leading me. The people of the slander said what they said, and the army was thrown into turmoil. By God, I knew nothing of that. Then we arrived in Madinah, and it was not long before I fell severely ill, and none of that reached me. The matter had reached the Messenger of God ﷺ and my parents, but they did not mention anything of it, little or much, except that I sensed something from him: when he entered upon me while my mother was with me nursing me, he said, 'How is this one of yours?' and added nothing. She said: Until I felt something in myself. I said, 'O Messenger of God, when I saw what I saw of his coldness, if you permit me, let me move to my mother's so she can nurse me.' He said, 'No harm.' She said: I moved to my mother, not knowing anything of what had happened, until I recovered from my illness after twenty-some nights. We were an Arab people; we did not adopt these latrines that the non-Arabs adopt in our houses. We disliked and hated them. We used to go to the open grounds of Madinah. Women used to go out every night for their needs. I went out one night for some need, and with me was Umm Mistah, daughter of Abu Ruhm b. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf. Her mother was the daughter of Sakhr b. 'Amir b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Taym, the maternal aunt of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. She said: By God, while she was walking with me, she stumbled in her long garment and said, 'May Mistah perish!' She said: I said, 'How bad, by the life of God, is what you said about a man among the Emigrants who was present at Badr!' She said, 'Has the news not reached you, O daughter of Abu Bakr?' She said: I said, 'What news?' She told me what the people of the slander had said. She said: I said, 'Has this happened?' She said, 'Yes, by God, it has.' She said: By God, I could not finish my need and returned. By God, I kept weeping until I thought that weeping would split my liver. She said: I said to my mother, 'May God forgive you! The people have been talking about what they talked about, and you do not mention anything of it to me?' She said, 'O my little daughter, take the matter lightly. By God, seldom has a beautiful woman been loved by a man who loves her, having co-wives, except that they and the people exaggerate against her.'"],[4941,"O son of my sister, I saw from the Messenger of God ﷺ an amazing thing in his honoring of al-Abbas. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to be seized by pleurisy, and it would become very severe for him. She said: We used to say, 'The Messenger of God has been seized by the vein of the kidney,' but we did not know the word for pleurisy. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ was seized by pleurisy, and it became so severe that he fainted. We feared for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the people rushed to him in alarm. She said: We thought he had pleurisy, so we gave him medicine by the side of the mouth. She said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ was relieved and regained consciousness. She said: He realized that we had given him the medicine and found its effect. He said, 'Did you think that God would give it power over me? God would not give it power over me. By Him in whose hand is my soul, no one in the house will remain without being given that medicine except my uncle.' Aisha said: I saw them that day being given the medicine one by one. Aisha said: Those in the house that day whose excellence is mentioned were given it. She said: All the men were given the medicine. She said: Then, by God, the medicine reached us, the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and we were given it, by God, one by one. She said: Until the medicine reached a woman among us. She said: 'Indeed, by God, I am fasting.' We said to her, 'How bad is what you think, that we would leave you when the Messenger of God ﷺ has sworn?' She said: We gave her the medicine, by God, O son of my sister, while she was fasting. He said: 'Urwa said: 'Abbas, by God, took the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ when the seventy of the Ansar came to him at al-'Aqaba. He took for the Messenger of God ﷺ from them and stipulated for them, and that was in the early dawn of Islam and its beginning, before anyone worshiped God openly.'"],[4942,"He used to remember God in all his states."],[4943,"I asked Aisha about the incantation for venomous stings. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted incantation for every venomous creature."],[4944,"When she had her menses, the Messenger of God ﷺ would say to her: O daughter of Abu Bakr, tie your waist-wrapper tightly. He would enjoy her at night as God willed, and he would say the takbir for his prayer, and he seldom slept at night, because God said: 'Arise at night, except a little.'"],[4945,"Two prayers the Messenger of God ﷺ never abandoned, secretly or openly: two rak'ahs before dawn and two rak'ahs after 'Asr."],[4946,"He asked Aisha and said: I have become old, and I can only pray sitting. What do you think? She said: I heard the Messenger of God, or the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The prayer of one sitting is half of his prayer standing."],[4947,"I used to twist the garlands for the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would send them off, then he would not avoid anything that the pilgrim in ihram avoids."],[4948,"We entered upon Aisha, and she brought out to us a coarse waist-wrapper of the kind made in Yemen and a cloak of these that you call mulabbada. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ passed away in these two garments."],[4949,"Hudba narrated to us; Sulayman b. al-Mughira narrated to us with his chain something similar."],[4950,"I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ ever quote poetry? She said: Sometimes, when he entered his house, he would say: 'And he brings you news of what you did not provision.'"],[4951,"A man sneezed in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: What should I say, O Messenger of God? He said: Say: 'Praise be to God.' The people said: What should we say to him, O Messenger of God? He said: Say: 'May God have mercy on you.' The man said: How should I respond to them, O Messenger of God? He said: Say: 'May God guide you and set your affairs aright.'"],[4952,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the briber and the bribe-taker."],[4953,"Whoever prays twenty rak'ahs between Maghrib and Isha, God will build for him a house in Paradise."],[4954,"Delay the Zuhr prayer in intense heat."],[4955,"Whoever would be pleased to outstrip the diligent striver, let him refrain from sins."],[4956,"He would tilt the vessel for the cat, and it would drink from it; then he would perform ablution for prayer."],[4957,"There is no emigration after the conquest, but there is jihad and intention; and if you are called to mobilize, then mobilize."],[4958,"Pardon the slips of people of dignity."],[4959,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered and said: O Aisha, is there any morsel? I brought him a loaf, and he put it to his mouth and said: O Aisha, has anything of it entered my stomach? Such is the kiss of the fasting person; breaking the fast is only from what enters, not from what comes out."],[4960,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was crying. He said: What makes you cry? I said: Fatimah insulted me. So he summoned Fatimah and said: O Fatimah, did you insult Aisha? She said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: O Fatimah, do you not love whom I love? She said: Yes. And hate whom I hate? She said: Indeed. He said: Indeed, I love Aisha, so love her. Fatimah said: I will never say anything to Aisha that hurts her again."],[4961,"The Prophet ﷺ used to love sweets and honey."],[4962,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed the afternoon prayer, he would go around to his wives and draw near to them."],[4963,"The bed of the Prophet ﷺ on which we would sleep was made of tanned leather stuffed with palm fiber."],[4964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered in the year of the conquest from Kadaʾ, from the upper part of Makkah, and he entered in the ʿUmrah from Kuda."],[4965,"It was very hard on the Prophet ﷺ for any [bad odor] to be found coming from him."],[4966,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors: one of them has his door facing my door, and the other is far from my door but closer in the wall. With which of them should I begin? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Begin with the one whose door faces your door."],[4967,"“What is the matter with you, O ʿAʾishah?” She said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am in pain and have a headache.” He said: “Rather, O my head!” She said: “I did not wait but a little while before he was brought to me carried in a cloak. She said: I nursed him, though I had never nursed a sick person before, nor had I ever seen a dead person. She said: He raised his head, so I took hold of him and rested him against my chest. She said: Usamah b. Zayd entered with a fresh toothstick of arak wood in his hand. She said: He glanced toward it. She said: I thought he wanted it, so I took it, chewed it with my mouth to soften it, and handed it to him. She said: He took it and brought it toward his mouth. She said: His hand fell limp, and it dropped from his hand. Then he turned his face toward me until his mouth was at my mouth, and a cold drop flowed from his mouth which made my skin shudder, and the scent of musk rose in my face. Then his head inclined, and I thought he had fainted. She said: I took him and laid him on the bed and covered his face. She said: My father Abu Bakr entered and said: “How do you see him?” I said: “He has fainted.” He drew near, uncovered his face, and said: “O what a faint! How unlike a faint this is!” Then he uncovered his face, recognized death, and said: “Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we return.” Then he wept. I said: “For the sake of Allah—the ceasing of revelation and the entry of Jibril into my house.” Then he placed his hands on his temples, put his mouth on his forehead, and wept until his tears flowed over the face of the Prophet ﷺ. Then he covered his face and went out to the people weeping, saying: “O assembly of Muslims, does anyone among you have a covenant regarding the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” They said: “No.” Then he turned to ʿUmar and said: “O ʿUmar, do you have a covenant regarding the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “No.” He said: “By the One besides whom there is no god, he has tasted death. He had said to them: ‘I am dying, and you are dying.’” The people wailed and wept bitterly. Then they left him with his family. ʿAli b. Abi Talib washed him while Usamah b. Zayd poured water over him. ʿAli said: “I did not forget any part of him that I had not washed except that it was turned over for me so I could see and wash it without seeing anyone, until I finished with him.” Then they shrouded him in a red Yemeni cloak and two white garments that had been dyed then washed. Then he was laid on the bier, and permission was given to the people. They entered upon him in groups, praying over him without an imam, until no one remained in Madinah, free or slave, except that he prayed over him. Then they disputed about where to bury him. Some said: “By the pulpit where he used to stand and under his minbar.” Others said: “In al-Baqiʿ, where he used to bury his dead.” They said: “We will not do that, for then a slave or slave-girl of yours might become angry with his master and seek refuge at his grave, and it would become a custom.” So their opinion settled on burying him in his house, under his bed where his soul was taken. When Abu Bakr died, he was buried with him. When death came to ʿUmar b. al-Khattab, he left instructions: “When I die, carry me to the door of ʿAʾishah’s house and say to her: ‘This is ʿUmar b. al-Khattab, who sends you greetings of peace and says: May I enter or shall I depart?’” He said: She was silent for a while, then said: “Let him enter, and bury him with him—Abu Bakr on his right and ʿUmar on his left.” She said: When ʿUmar was buried, I took the outer garment and wrapped myself in it. He said: It was said to her: “Why the outer garment?” She said: “This was my husband, and this was my father, so when ʿUmar was buried I wrapped myself.”"],[4968,"Juwayriyah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I fell to the share of Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas, or to a cousin of his, and I made a contract with him to purchase my freedom. I have come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to seek his help with my contract.” He said: “Would you like something better than that? I will pay off your contract and marry you.” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Then I have done so.”"],[4969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who divorced his wife irrevocably—meaning three times—then she married another man who divorced her before consummating the marriage. May she return to the first? He said: “No, not until he tastes her sweetness as her first husband tasted it.”"],[4970,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar narrated to us; Yahya b. Zakariyya narrated to us, from Yahya b. Saʿid, from al-Qasim, from ʿAʾishah, the like of it."],[4971,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar narrated to us; Yahya b. Zakariyya narrated to us, from Yahya b. Saʿid, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, the like of it."],[4972,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque, and around the Kaʿbah were three hundred and sixty idols. He began striking them with a stick he had with him and saying: “The truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is bound to vanish.”"],[4973,"The moon split into two pieces in the time of the Messenger of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bear witness.”"],[4974,"I entered with my father upon Abdullah, and he said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Remorse is repentance”? He said: Yes."],[4975,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave, and there was sent down upon him: “By those sent forth in succession” (al-Mursalat). I took it from his mouth, and his mouth was moist. I do not know with which of them he concluded: “Then in what statement after it will they believe?” or “And when it is said to them, ‘Bow,’ they do not bow.” A snake raced ahead of us and entered a hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have been protected from its evil, and it has been protected from your evil.”"],[4976,"We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ and he would respond to us, meaning during the prayer. When we came from the land of Abyssinia, I greeted him and he did not respond to me. I was seized by anxiety over what was far and near. I sat until he finished the prayer, then I said to him: You used to respond to us. He said: “Allah brings about whatever He wills, and He has brought about in His command a decree that you should not speak during the prayer.”"],[4977,"I saw Abdullah b. Mas'ud stone Jamrat al-Aqabah from the bottom of the valley and say: This, by the One besides whom there is no deity, is the standing place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down."],[4978,"The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."],[4979,"The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."],[4980,"Indeed, Islam began as something strange, and it will return as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. He said: It was said, “Who are the strangers?” He said: Those who withdraw from the tribes."],[4981,"Make the Hajj and the Umrah follow one another, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron, gold, and silver. And there is no reward for an accepted Hajj except Paradise."],[4982,"The sun rises, when it rises, between the two horns of a devil. He said: We used to be forbidden from praying at sunrise, at sunset, and at midday."],[4983,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need. He said: Bring me something to cleanse myself with, and do not bring me any dung or dry bones."],[4984,"There will be people in the Fire as long as Allah wills, then Allah will have mercy on them and bring them out. They will be in the lowest part of Paradise and will bathe in the River of Life. The people of Paradise will call them the Jahannamis. If one of them were to host the people of this world, he would feed them, give them drink, clothe them, and spread for them. He said – and I think he said – and marry them, without that diminishing anything of what he has."],[4985,"The last person to enter Paradise is a man who walks on the bridge, stumbling at times and the Fire scorching him at times. When he turns to it, he says: Praise be to Allah who saved me from you. Allah has given me something He did not give to anyone among the first or the last. Then a tree is raised up for him, and he says: O Lord, bring me near this tree so I may shade myself with its shade and drink from its water. Allah says: O son of Adam, perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for something else. He makes a covenant with Him not to ask Him, but his Lord knows that he will ask for something else, because he sees what he cannot bear to do without. So Allah brings him near it, and he shades himself with its shade and drinks from its water. Then another tree is raised up for him, more beautiful than that one, and he says: O Lord, bring me near this tree so I may shade myself with its shade and drink from its water. Allah says: O son of Adam, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for anything else? He says: Yes, O Lord, but this tree – I will not ask You for anything else. He makes a covenant with Him not to ask Him, but his Lord knows that he will ask for something else, and his Lord excuses him because he sees what he cannot bear to do without. So Allah brings him near it, and he shades himself with its shade and drinks from its water. Then a tree is raised up for him at the gate of Paradise, more beautiful than those first two trees. He says: O Lord, bring me near this tree so I may shade myself with its shade and drink from its water. Allah says: O son of Adam, did you not covenant not to ask Me for anything else? He says: O Lord, bring me near this tree so I may shade myself with its shade and drink from its water. Allah says to him: Perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for something else. He makes a covenant with Him not to ask Him for anything else, but his Lord knows that he will ask for something else, and his Lord excuses him because he sees what he cannot bear to do without. So He brings him near it, and he hears the voices of the people of Paradise. He says: O Lord, admit me into Paradise. Allah says: Would it please you if I gave you the world and the like of it along with it? He says: O Lord, do You mock me while You are the Lord of the worlds? He said: I do not mock you, but I am Able to do whatever I will."],[4986,"The one who consumes usury, the one who gives it, its two witnesses, and its scribe are cursed. He said: When adultery and usury appear among a people, they have brought upon themselves the punishment of Allah."],[4987,"The disbeliever will be choked by sweat on the Day of Resurrection and will say, 'Give me relief, even to the Fire.'"],[4988,"Allah spoke to Musa ﷺ while he wore a wool jubbah, a wool cloak, wool trousers, a wool cap, and his sandals were made from the skin of an unslaughtered donkey."],[4989,"Al-Ash'ath b. Qays bought some slaves from the emirate's slaves, and they differed about the price. Ibn Mas'ud said, 'I sold you for twenty thousand,' and al-Ash'ath said, 'I only bought from you for ten thousand.' Abd Allah said, 'If you wish, I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'Proceed.' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When the two parties to a sale differ and there is no evidence between them, the statement is that of the seller, or they both revoke the sale.' He said, 'Then I revoke the sale.'"],[4990,"I was a young boy tending sheep belonging to Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt. The Prophet ﷺ came with Abu Bakr and said, 'O boy, do you have any milk?' I said, 'Yes, but I am entrusted.' He said, 'Bring me a ewe that has not been mounted by a ram.' I brought him a young goat or a yearling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held it, then began wiping the udder and supplicating until it produced milk. Abu Bakr brought him a rock, and he milked into it. Then he said to Abu Bakr, 'Drink.' Abu Bakr drank, then the Prophet ﷺ drank after him. Then he said to the udder, 'Shrink,' and it shrank, returning as it was. He said: Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ later and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me some of this speech, or of this Qur'an.' He wiped my head and said, 'You are a taught boy.'"],[4991,"When the verse 'Who is it that will lend Allah a goodly loan' was revealed, Abu al-Dahdah said, 'O Messenger of Allah, does Allah want a loan from us?' He said, 'Yes, O Abu al-Dahdah.' He said, 'Show me your hand.' He said, 'So he extended his hand to him.' He said, 'I have lent my walled garden to my Lord.' His garden had six hundred palm trees. He came walking until he reached the garden, while Umm al-Dahdah and her family were inside. He called out, 'O Umm al-Dahdah.' She said, 'At your service.' He said, 'Leave, for I have lent it to my Lord.'"],[4992,"Allah is one and loves that which is odd-numbered, so perform witr, O people of the Qur'an. A bedouin said, 'What are you saying, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'It is not for you nor for your companions.'"],[4993,"Fighting a believer is disbelief, and insulting him is wickedness."],[4994,"Your permission is that you may raise the veil and hear my confidential talk until I forbid you."],[4995,"He forbade meeting caravans before they reach the market."],[4996,"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[4997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed the spoils of Hunayn at al-Ji'irranah. They crowded around him, and he said, 'A servant among the servants of Allah was sent by Allah to a people, but they denied him, beat him, and wounded him.' Abd Allah said, 'It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the size of a saddle, and he said like this: My Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know.'"],[4998,"I saw Jibril at the Lote Tree, upon him six hundred wings, from whose feathers scattered splendors of pearls and rubies."],[4999,"He used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan: from his pricking, his blowing, and his spitting."],[5000,"The superiority of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-some degrees."],[5001,"We prayed with Ibn Mas'ud in his house, one of us on his right and the other on his left, and he said: Thus we prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5002,"A black slave caught up with the Prophet ﷺ, then died, and the Prophet ﷺ was informed of it. He said: See whether he left anything. They said: Two dinars. The Prophet ﷺ said: Two brands."],[5003,"The likeness of me and the world is only as a rider who took midday rest in the shade of a tree on a hot day, then departed and left it."],[5004,"Satan has a touch and the angel has a touch. As for Satan's touch, it is threatening with evil and denying the truth. As for the angel's touch, it is promising good and affirming the truth. Whoever finds the latter, let him praise Allah; whoever finds the other, let him seek refuge from Satan. Then he recited: 'Satan promises you poverty...' the verse."],[5005,"The prayer of the congregation surpasses the prayer of a man alone by twenty-some portions."],[5006,"Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr narrated to us; Ibn Idris narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir."],[5007,"When one of you doubts, let him seek what is correct and prostrate twice."],[5008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the ways of guidance in prayer in the mosque in which the call to prayer is given."],[5009,"Beware, the extremists have perished; beware, the extremists have perished; beware, the extremists have perished."],[5010,"When he slept, he would say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You gather Your servants. And he would place his hand under his cheek."],[5011,"They used to recite behind the Prophet ﷺ in prayer, and he said: You have confused the Quran for me."],[5012,"Beware, the extremists have perished — three times."],[5013,"We were with Abdullah, and with us was Ziyad b. Hudayr. Khabbab entered upon us and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, do all these recite as you recite? He said: If you wish, I will command one of them to recite to you. He said to me: Recite. Ibn Hudayr said to him: You command him to recite though he is not the best reciter among us? He said: If you wish, I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to your people and his people. So I recited fifty verses of Maryam to him, and Khabbab said: Enough for you."],[5014,"The millstone of Islam will turn for thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perish; and if they remain, their religion will remain for them for seventy years."],[5015,"We traveled one night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, if only we touched the ground and slept, and our mounts grazed? He said: Then who will guard us? I said: I will. He said: But sleep overcame me, and nothing woke us except that the sun had risen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not wake except by our talking. He said: He commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan, then he stood and prayed with us."],[5016,"Indeed, the closest of people to me on the Day of Resurrection are those who send the most blessings upon me."],[5017,"Paradise has eight gates: seven are closed and one gate is open for repentance until the sun rises from its direction."],[5018,"The companions of Ibn Mas'ud were bitten by the cold, so they became shy to come in turbans and cloaks. He missed them, and it was said to him: Their matter is such and such. So Abu Abd al-Rahman came one morning in a cloak, and they said: Ibn Mas'ud has come in his cloak. Then came the second day, then came the third day. When they saw him in the cloak, they came in their garments all together, and he recognized faces that he had missed. He said: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No one will enter Paradise in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of pride, or he said: an atom's weight of pride."],[5019,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the evening, he would say: We have entered the evening, and sovereignty belongs to Allah, and praise belongs to Allah; there is no god but Allah alone with no partner. O Allah, I ask You for the good of this night and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from laziness, senility, the evil of old age, the trial of this world, and the punishment of the grave."],[5020,"Two men were worshiping Allah, and they asked Allah to cause them both to die together; so they both died together and were buried. Abdullah said: If I had been there, I would have shown you their graves by the description that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ described to us."],[5021,"For thirty cattle: a tabīʿ or tabīʿah, and for forty: a musinnah."],[5022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray, and when he prostrated, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn would jump onto his back. When they wanted to stop them, he gestured to them to leave them. When he finished the prayer, he placed them in his lap and said: “Whoever loves me, let him love these two.”"],[5023,"“The heart did not lie about what it saw.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Jibrīl ﷺ in two garments of rafraf, having filled what is between the heaven and the earth."],[5024,"Abū Bakr narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us, Misʿar narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Murrah, from Ibrāhīm, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAbdullāh: “Recite to me.” He said: “Should I recite to you when it was sent down upon you?” He said: “I love to hear it from someone other than myself.” He said: So he recited to him from the beginning of Sūrat al-Nisāʾ up to His saying: “So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?” And he wept."],[5025,"A witness against them as long as I am among them, or he said: as long as I was among them."],[5026,"He used to say: “My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.”"],[5027,"Maʿn b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān brought out to me a book and swore that it was in his father’s handwriting, and in it: ʿAbdullāh said: By the One besides whom there is no god, I have not seen anyone harsher against the mutanaṭṭiʿūn than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor have I seen anyone harsher against them after him than Abū Bakr, and I think ʿUmar was the most fearful of the people of the earth for them, or concerning them."],[5028,"We saw that no one stayed away from the prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, or a sick person. A sick person would walk between two men until he came to the prayer. And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the sunan of guidance, and among the sunan of guidance is prayer in the mosque in which the call to prayer is given."],[5029,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, about thirty men, among whom there was none but a Qurayshī. No, by Allah, I have never seen the surfaces of men’s faces more beautiful than their faces that day. He said: They mentioned women and spoke about them, and he spoke with them, until I wished he would be silent. Then I came to him, and he said the tashahhud, then said: “Now then, O assembly of Quraysh, you are the people of this affair as long as you obey Allah. But when you disobey Him, He will send against you someone who will strip you as this twig is stripped” – for a twig in his hand – then he stripped his twig, and there it was, white and hard."],[5030,"Whoever keeps a dog that is not a dog for livestock or a hunting dog, two qīrāṭs are deducted from his reward every day."],[5031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a donkey called ʿUfayr."],[5032,"Labbayka Allāhumma labbayk, labbayka lā sharīka laka labbayk, inna al-ḥamda wa-l-niʿmata laka."],[5033,"Learn the Qur'an, learn knowledge and teach it to the people, and learn the shares of inheritance and teach them to the people, for I am a man who will be taken, and knowledge will be taken away until two men dispute over an obligatory share and find no one to inform them."],[5034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut for a month invoking against Usayya and Dhakwan. When he prevailed over them, he abandoned the qunut."],[5035,"Whoever lends a Muslim man a dirham twice, for him is the reward of their charity once."],[5036,"We were sitting with Abdullah after Maghrib while he was teaching us the Qur'an, and a man asked him, 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ how many caliphs this nation will have?' Ibn Mas'ud said, 'No one has asked me about it since I came to Iraq before you.' He said, 'Yes, I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Twelve, like the chieftains of the Children of Israel.\"'"],[5037,"We were sitting waiting for Ibn Mas'ud to come out to us when Yazid b. Mu'awiya came to us. We said, 'Sit down.' He said, 'Not until I go in to your companion; if he comes out, then fine, otherwise I will return to you.' He said, 'He went in to him, and they both came out.' Ibn Mas'ud said, 'I am informed of your gathering—or of your place—and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you. The Prophet ﷺ used to space out his admonitions to us over the days, fearing tedium for us.'"],[5038,"The Muhajirun, the Ansar, the Tulaqa' of Quraysh, and the Utaqa' of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."],[5039,"He was asked, 'Did the Prophet ﷺ deliver the sermon standing?' He said, 'Yes,' then recited: 'And they leave you standing.'"],[5040,"A man among the Children of Israel, when he saw his brother committing a sin, would forbid him as an excuse. Then the next day, what he saw of him did not prevent him from being his table companion, his associate, and his drinking companion. When Allah saw that from them, He struck the hearts of some of them against others and cursed them upon the tongue of their prophet Da'ud and 'Isa son of Maryam. That was because they disobeyed and were transgressing. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By Him in Whose hand is my soul, you must enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, seize the hand of the wrongdoer, and compel him to the truth firmly, or Allah will strike the hearts of some of you against others and curse you as He cursed them.'"],[5041,"The Buraq was brought to me, and I rode it behind Jibril. He traveled with us, and whenever he came to a mountain, its legs would rise, and whenever it descended, its hands would rise. He traveled with us through a land that was gloomy and stinking, and we emerged into a land that was spacious and fragrant. I said, 'O Jibril, we were traveling through a gloomy and stinking land, and we have emerged into a spacious and fragrant land.' He said, 'That is the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise.' We came upon a man standing in prayer. He said, 'Who is this with you, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is your brother Muhammad.' He welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me, saying, 'Ask ease for your nation.' I said, 'Who is this, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is your brother 'Isa.' Then he traveled on, and we came upon a man. He said, 'Who is with you, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is your brother Muhammad.' He welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me, saying, 'Ask ease for your nation.' I said, 'Who is this, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is your brother Musa.' Then we traveled on and saw lamps and light. I said, 'What is this, O Jibril?' He said, 'This is the tree of your father Ibrahim. Shall we draw near to it?' I said, 'Yes.' We drew near to it, and he welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me. Then we went on until we came to Jerusalem, and the prophets were presented to me—those whom Allah named and those He did not name—and I prayed with them, except these three individuals: Musa, 'Isa, and Ibrahim.'"],[5042,"A man from the Companions of the Suffa died, and they found two dinars in his cloak. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Two brands of fire.'"],[5043,"We asked our Prophet ﷺ about walking with the funeral procession. He said, 'Less than a brisk pace. If it is good, it will be hastened; if it is other than that, then far be it for the people of the Fire. The funeral procession is followed, not following. It is not from it whoever goes ahead of it.'"],[5044,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar, and they did not raise their hands except at the opening of the prayer."],[5045,"Shall I not lead you in the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Then he led them, and he did not raise his hand except once."],[5046,"I was praying and had placed my left hand over my right, when the Prophet ﷺ came to me and took my right hand and placed it over my left."],[5047,"Usury, even if it increases, its outcome will ultimately come to little."],[5048,"The Prophet ﷺ only performed qunut for a month, supplicating against a clan of the clans of Banu Sulaym who were disobedient—they disobeyed God and His Messenger. Then he did not perform qunut after that."],[5049,"The polytheists detained the Messenger of God ﷺ from the afternoon prayer until the sun turned yellow—or red. He said: They have distracted us from the middle prayer. May God fill their bellies and their graves with fire—or may God stuff their bellies and their graves with fire."],[5050,"He recited into the ear of an afflicted person, and he recovered. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: What did you recite into his ear? He said: I recited: 'Did you think that We created you in vain...' until the end of the surah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If a man of certainty recited it over a mountain, it would move."],[5051,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution with nabidh."],[5052,"Be shy before God with the shyness due to Him. Let one guard the head and what it contains, and guard the belly and what it holds, and remember death and decay. Whoever desires the Hereafter abandons the adornment of this world. Whoever does that has been shy before God with the shyness due to Him."],[5053,"They said: O Messenger of God, how will you recognize those of your community whom you have not seen? He said: They will have white marks on their foreheads and limbs from the traces of ablution, and will be piebald from the effects of purification."],[5054,"I cannot count how many times I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in the two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer and in the two rak'ahs after sunset: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is God, One.'"],[5055,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the first rak'ah of the witr: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' in the second: 'Say: O disbelievers,' and in the third: 'Say: He is God, One.'"],[5056,"It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of God ﷺ as he turned to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of God and His blessings, and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of God."],[5057,"I am astonished at the people and their abandoning my recitation and adopting the recitation of Zayd, though I have taken from the mouth of the Messenger of God ﷺ seventy surahs, while Zayd b. Thabit was a youth with locks of hair, coming and going in Madinah."],[5058,"Shall I not tell you who is forbidden to the Fire, or to whom the Fire is forbidden? To everyone who is gentle, near, and easygoing."],[5059,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who makes lawful [a woman for her former husband] and the one for whom it is made lawful."],[5060,"A man entered Paradise though he had done no good. When death came to him, he said to his family, 'When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter half of me on land and half of me in the sea.' So He commanded the sea and the land, and they gathered him. He said, 'What made you do what you did?' He said, 'Fear of You.' So He forgave him for that."],[5061,"Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiya b. Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, a similar hadith: The man was a grave robber, but He forgave him because of his fear."],[5062,"Two men disputed over a surah. One said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me it,' and the other said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me it.' They came to the Prophet ﷺ and he was informed of that. His face changed, and he said, 'Recite as you have been taught.' Then he mentioned something further, and said, 'Those before you were destroyed only by their differing over their prophets.' Each man of us arose, not reciting according to the recitation of his companion."],[5063,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by with Abu Bakr and Umar while Abd Allah was praying, and he began reciting Surah al-Nisa, reciting it fluently. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd.' Then he sat and made supplication. The Messenger of God ﷺ kept saying, 'Ask and you will be given.' Among his supplications he said, 'O God, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, blessing that does not run out, and the companionship of our Prophet ﷺ in the highest Garden of Eternity.' Umar came to give him glad tidings of that, but found Abu Bakr already outside, having preceded him. He said, 'If you have done so, you are indeed foremost in good.'"],[5064,"I was praying in the mosque when the Messenger of God ﷺ entered with Abu Bakr and Umar. I recited Surah al-Nisa fluently and read it. When I finished, I sat and began praising God, Mighty and Glorious, and invoking blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then I supplicated for myself. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Ask and you will be given; ask and you will be given.' Then he said, 'Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh, let him recite as Ibn Umm Abd recites.' I returned to my home, and Abu Bakr came to me and said, 'Do you remember anything of what you supplicated?' I said, 'Yes: O God, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, blessing that does not run out, and the companionship of our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in the highest Garden of Eternity.' Then Umar also came to me and gave me glad tidings."],[5065,"Whoever is easygoing, gentle, and near, God has forbidden him to the Fire."],[5066,"He performed tamattuʿ with the Prophet ﷺ, the tamattuʿ of Hajj."],[5067,"Last night I spent the night reciting to the jinn, companions at al-Hajun."],[5068,"Have mercy on those on earth, and He who is in heaven will have mercy on you."],[5069,"When this verse was revealed: “There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten, if they fear [Allah]...” to the end of the verse, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It was said to me: ‘You are one of them.’”"],[5070,"No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride, and no one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a seed of faith."],[5071,"No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride, and no one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith."],[5072,"I heard Ibn Yusuf say while he was on the pulpit: “Compile the Quran as Gabriel compiled it: the surah in which the Cow is mentioned, the surah in which the family of Imran is mentioned, the surah in which the Women are mentioned.” Al-A'mash said: “I met Ibrahim and told him, and he cursed him, then Ibrahim said...”"],[5073,"I came to Homs, and a group of them said to me: “O Abu Abd al-Rahman, recite to us.” So I recited Surah Yusuf, and a man said to me: “It was not revealed like that.” I said to him: “Woe to you! By Allah, I recited it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: ‘You have done well.’” He said: “While I was arguing with him, I noticed the smell of wine on him. I said to him: ‘Do you drink filth and deny the Quran? No doubt, you will not leave until I flog you with the prescribed punishment.’ So I flogged him with the prescribed punishment.”"],[5074,"“Recite to us.” He said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, should I recite to you when the Quran was revealed to you?’ He said: ‘I like to hear it from someone other than myself.’ So I recited Surah al-Nisa' to him until when I reached: ‘So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?’ He nudged me, so I looked at him and his eyes were flowing with tears ﷺ.”"],[5075,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the moon split into two parts: one part was behind the mountain and one part was on this side. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bear witness.”"],[5076,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for what we did in the pre-Islamic era?” He said: “Whoever does good in Islam will not be held accountable for what he did in the pre-Islamic era, but if he does evil in Islam, he will be held accountable for the first and the last.”"],[5077,"It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ imitating one of the prophets: his people struck him until they made his face bleed, and he began wiping the blood from his face while saying: “O Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know.”"],[5078,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."],[5079,"He disliked ten traits: saffron dye—meaning khaluq—, dragging the lower garment, wearing a gold ring, plucking gray hairs, playing with dice, displaying adornment inappropriately, using incantations except with the mu'awwidhat, hanging amulets, withdrawing semen at its time from its place, and corrupting a child without making it unlawful."],[5080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, You have made my physical form good, so make my character good.”"],[5081,"A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-some degrees."],[5082,"He used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the devil, from his prodding, his blowing, and his spitting. His prodding is madness, his blowing is poetry, and his spitting is pride."],[5083,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and empowered him to spend it in the way of truth, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, so he judges by it and teaches it."],[5084,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[5085,"The closest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who sends the most prayers upon me."],[5086,"Regret is repentance."],[5087,"We used to say, when we sat in prayer: Peace be upon Allah before His servants, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il, peace be upon so-and-so. He said: Then we would say: His angels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to us and said: Allah is the Peace, so when you sit, say: The greetings are for Allah, and the prayers, and the good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no deity but He, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. Then we choose the speech."],[5088,"A woman should not touch another woman and then describe her to her husband so that it is as if he is looking at her."],[5089,"Black banners will come from the direction of the east, and the horses will wade through blood up to their chests. They will manifest justice and seek justice, but will not be given it, so they will prevail. Then justice will be sought from them, but they will not give it."],[5090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the mosque, and there were some women from the Ansar in it. He came to them, admonished them, and reminded them, and said: There is not one of you women who loses three children except that she will enter Paradise. A woman from among the noblest of them said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the one who loses two? He said: There is not one of you women who loses two except that she will enter Paradise."],[5091,"The best Hajj is the raising of voices and the shedding of blood. As for the raising of voices, it is the talbiyah, and as for the shedding of blood, it is the sacrificing of camels."],[5092,"Indeed Allah has protective jealousy for His believing servant, so let him have protective jealousy for himself."],[5093,"The believer is not one who taunts, nor curses, nor is obscene, nor is indecent."],[5094,"I asked Murrah al-Hamdani about His saying: 'There is none of you but will pass over it (Hell)', so he narrated to me that Abdullah narrated to them, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'They will come to the Sirat and pass over it according to their deeds. The first of them will pass like the wind, then like the galloping of a horse, then like a rider in his saddle, then like a man running, then like a man walking.'"],[5095,"Whoever dies while setting up a rival to Allah, He will admit him to the Fire. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: 'And another thing I said: Whoever dies while not setting up a rival to Allah, Allah will admit him to Paradise. And these prayers, the prescribed ones, are expiations for the sins between them as long as major sins are avoided.'"],[5096,"A man was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so slept last night until morning.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Satan urinated in his ear.'"],[5097,"Tiyarah (belief in bad omens) is shirk. There is none of us but [has some inclination to it], but Allah removes it through reliance on Him."],[5098,"It is as if I am looking at Musa b. Imran in this valley, in the state of ihram, between two Qatwani garments."],[5099,"Indeed, those before you from the Children of Israel, when a man among them committed a sin, someone would forbid him as a mere excuse. Then the next day he would sit with him, eat with him, and drink with him, as if he had not seen him commit the sin the day before. When Allah saw that from them, He struck the hearts of some of them against others and cursed them on the tongue of their Prophet Dawud and Isa b. Maryam. That was because they disobeyed and used to transgress. By the One in whose hand is my soul, you must enjoin good and forbid evil, and you must compel him to adhere to the truth forcefully, or Allah will strike the hearts of some of you against others and curse you as He cursed them."],[5100,"Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Our companion is sick; shall we cauterize him?' He fell silent for a while, then said: 'If you wish, cauterize him; and if you wish, use heated stones.'"],[5101,"I was tending the sheep of the family of Abu Mu'ayt, and the Prophet ﷺ came to me with Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O boy, do you have any milk to give us to drink?' I said: 'Yes, but I am entrusted.' He said: 'Do you have a ewe that is shasum (young, not yet covered by a ram and without an udder)?' I said: 'Yes.' So I brought him a shasum ewe. Salam said: 'Not yet covered by a ram, and it is one that has no udder.' The Prophet ﷺ wiped the place of the udder, and it had no udder, and suddenly there was an udder full of milk. I brought him a hollowed-out rock, and he milked it and gave Abu Bakr to drink and gave me to drink, then he drank. Then he said to the udder: 'Shrink,' and it returned to as it was. He said: 'I saw this with my own eyes from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me.' He wiped my head and said: 'May Allah bless you, for you are a taught boy.' So I embraced Islam and came to the Prophet ﷺ. While we were with him on Hira, Surat al-Mursalat was revealed to him, and I learned it while his mouth was still moist with it. I do not know with which of the two verses it ended: 'And when it is said to them: Bow down, they do not bow down' or 'Then in what statement after it will they believe?' I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs, and I took the rest of the Quran from his companions. He said: 'While we were sleeping on Hira, nothing woke us except the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: The one who prevented it from you is the one who prevented you from it. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is that? He said: A snake came out from the side of the mountain.'"],[5102,"Musaylimah sent two men, one of them Ibn Uthal b. Hajar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you both bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?' They said: 'We bear witness that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I believe in Allah and His messengers. If I were to kill envoys, I would kill you both.' While Ibn Mas'ud was in Kufa, the man who was with Ibn Uthal, and he was a relative of his, was brought to him, so he ordered his execution. He said to the people: 'Do you know why I killed this man?' They said: 'We do not know.' He said: 'Musaylimah sent this man with Ibn Uthal b. Hajar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do you both bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? They said: We bear witness that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. If I were to kill envoys, I would kill you both.' He said: 'So that is why I killed him.' Abu Wa'il said: 'And the man was a disbeliever at that time.'"],[5103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which sin is greatest in the sight of Allah?' He said: 'That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.' He said: 'Then which?' He said: 'Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.' He said: 'Then Allah sent down its confirmation: And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery.'"],[5104,"The first thing to be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection will be concerning bloodshed."],[5105,"Indeed the believer sees his sins as if he were sitting beneath a mountain, fearing that it fall upon him, while the sinner sees his sins as a fly that passed over his nose and he said to it thus. He said: And he said: Allah is more delighted with the repentance of a servant than a man who alighted in a desolate, deadly wilderness, having with him his mount carrying his food and drink. He laid down his head and slept a sleep, then woke to find his mount with his food and drink had gone. He set out seeking it until thirst or hunger overcame him—Abu Shihab was uncertain—and said: I shall return to my place and die there. So he returned to his place, laid down his head, and woke to find his mount beside him, with his food and drink upon it."],[5106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the takbir with every rising and lowering, and standing and sitting, as did Abu Bakr and Umar."],[5107,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give salutation to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,' until the whiteness of his cheeks could be seen."],[5108,"The best of my community is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony precedes their oath and whose oath precedes their testimony. He said: Ibrahim said: We were forbidden to swear by the covenant and testimonies."],[5109,"Indeed in poetry there is wisdom."],[5110,"There was a man with much wealth. When death came to him, he said to his family: 'If you do what I command you, I will leave you abundant wealth.' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'When I die, burn me, then grind me, and on a windy day ascend to the top of a mountain and scatter me. For if Allah gets hold of me, He will not forgive me.' So they did that to him. He was gathered in the hands of Allah, and He said: 'What made you do what you did?' He said: 'My Lord, fear of You.' He said: 'Go, for I have forgiven you.'"],[5111,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'So-and-so slept last night and missed the prayer.' He said: 'Satan urinated in his ear—or in his ears.'"],[5112,"The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."],[5113,"Abu Musa and Salman b. Rabi'a were asked about a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister. They said: 'The sister gets half and the daughter gets half.' Abdullah was asked, and he said: 'Then I would have gone astray and not be among the rightly guided. I say as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: the daughter gets half, the son's daughter gets one-sixth to complete two-thirds, and what remains goes to the sister.'"],[5114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left us and there is no bird in the sky flapping its wings but that he mentioned to us some knowledge from it."],[5115,"We arrived with Abdullah before Uthman. Uthman said to Abdullah: 'What desire do you still have for women?' He said: 'Come close, O Alqama'—and I was a young man—so I came close. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out upon a group of unmarried youths and said: Whoever among you has the means, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity. And whoever cannot, then fasting is for him a restraint.'"],[5116,"Let those of maturity and understanding stand nearest to me, then those who follow them. Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. And beware of the clamor of the marketplaces."],[5117,"Give charity, O assembly of women, for you are the majority of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. A woman who was not among the elite of women said: And why are we the majority of the people of Hell? He said: Because you curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. Ibn Mas'ud said: I have not found any who are deficient in intellect and religion and more overpowering over men of sound judgment in their affairs than these women. It was said: O Ibn Mas'ud, what is the deficiency in their intellects and their religion? He said: As for the deficiency in their intellects, it is that the testimony of two women equals the testimony of one man. As for the deficiency in their religion, it is that one of them goes through whatever Allah wills of days and nights without prostrating to Allah a single prostration."],[5118,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Will we be held accountable for what we did in the pre-Islamic era? He said: If you do good in Islam, you will not be held accountable for it; but if you do evil in Islam, you will be held accountable for the first and the last."],[5119,"A woman should not have intimate contact with another woman and then describe her to her husband or describe her to a man as if he is looking at her. If there are three people, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, for that grieves him. Whoever swears a false oath in order to seize thereby the property of his brother or the property of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him."],[5120,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, one of the people of the Suffah, died and left two dinars. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Two brands of fire."],[5121,"Whoever offers up three children who have not reached the age of accountability, they will be a strong fortress for him against the Fire. Abu Dharr said: I have offered up two, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And two. Ubayy b. Ka'b, Abu al-Mundhir, the leader of the reciters, said: I have offered up one, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And one. He said: But that is only at the first shock."],[5122,"Whoever performs the prayer well when people see him, and performs it badly when he is alone, that is a belittlement by which he belittles his Lord, Blessed and Exalted."],[5123,"The poor person is not the one who goes around among you and is turned away with a morsel or two morsels, a date or two dates. We said: Then who is the poor person, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one who does not find what suffices him and is too shy to ask people, and no one notices him so that charity is given to him."],[5124,"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief. The sanctity of his property is like the sanctity of his blood."],[5125,"When one of you is brought food by his servant, let him begin and feed him or seat him with him, for he has endured its heat and smoke."],[5126,"Do you know which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The gift: that you grant your brother dinars, or dirhams, or a cow, or a sheep, or the back of a riding animal, or the milk of a sheep, or the milk of a cow. He did not say: the cow and the sheep."],[5127,"Satan has despaired of being worshiped in the land of the Arabs, but he will be content with you with less than that, with the trivial sins, which are the destructive ones on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of injustices as much as you can, for the servant will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds, thinking that they will save him. A servant will keep standing and saying: O Lord, Your servant wronged me in some way. And He will say: Erase from his good deeds. It will continue like that until no good deed remains for him because of the sins. The parable of that is like a group of travelers who stopped in a desert with no firewood with them. The people dispersed to gather firewood, and it was not long before they gathered it, made a great fire, and cooked what they wanted. Thus are sins."],[5128,"No one is more jealous than Allah, and because of His jealousy He forbade immoralities, both apparent and hidden."],[5129,"Indeed, Allah commands a caller on the Day of Resurrection: 'O Adam, arise and send forth from your progeny a contingent to the Fire.' Adam stands and says: 'O Lord, from every how many?' He says: 'From every hundred, ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.' That distressed those of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who heard it. They said to him: 'Who among us is saved after this?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You are among two created peoples: Gog and Magog, and they descend from every mound. You are in the world only like a spot on the foreleg of a beast, or like a hair on the side of a camel.'"],[5130,"Hands are three: the Hand of Allah, Exalted is He, is the highest; the hand of the giver that follows it; and the hand of the beggar is the lowest until the Day of Resurrection. So refrain from asking and from begging as much as you can. If you are given something—or he said: good—let it be shown upon you. Begin with those you support, give what you can from surplus, and you will not be blamed for chastity."],[5131,"May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and memorizes it until he conveys it."],[5132,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he went to relieve himself. He said: 'Find me three stones.' I found only two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw back the dung, saying: 'This is filth.'"],[5133,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say the takbir at every lowering, raising, standing, and sitting, and he would give the salutation to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen. Abu Bakr and Umar used to do that."],[5134,"I entered with my father upon Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and he said: 'Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Remorse is repentance?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[5135,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which sin is greatest in the sight of Allah?' He said: 'That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you.' I said: 'That is indeed great.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'That you kill your child fearing that he will eat with you.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife.'"],[5136,"Some people said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Will we be held accountable for what we did in the pre-Islamic era?' He said: 'As for one of you who does good in Islam, he will not be held accountable for it. But one who does evil will be taken to account for his deeds in the pre-Islamic era and in Islam.'"],[5137,"When you are three, let not two men converse privately excluding the third until you mix with people, because that saddens him. And let not a woman touch a woman and then describe her to her husband, until it is as if he is looking at her."],[5138,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave preference in the spoils. He gave al-Aqraʿ b. Ḥābis a hundred camels, gave ʿUyaynah the like of that, and gave people among the nobles of the Arabs, preferring them in the division. A man said: 'By Allah, this is a division in which justice has not been observed, and the face of Allah has not been sought.' I said: 'By Allah, I will certainly inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I came to him and told him what the man said. His face changed until it was like red ochre. Then he said: 'Who then is just if the Messenger of Allah is not just?' Then he said: 'May Allah have mercy on Musa. He was harmed with more than this, and he was patient.' I said: 'No doubt, after this I will not raise anything to him.'"],[5139,"A man came to me today and asked me about something I did not know how to answer. He said: 'What do you think of a dutiful, active man who goes out on military expeditions, and they bind us to things we cannot avoid?' I said to him: 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to you, except that we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and perhaps he would not bind us to a matter more than once until we did it. One of you will remain in good as long as he fears Allah, and if he doubts something in himself he asks a man who can cure it. It is near that you will not find him. By the One besides whom there is no deity, I do not remember what has passed of the world except as a pool whose clear water has been drunk and whose dregs remain.'"],[5140,"We used to say in prayer behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Peace be upon so-and-so.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us one day: 'Indeed, Allah is the Peace. When one of you sits in prayer, let him say: The greetings are for Allah, and the prayers and the good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah—when he says that, it reaches every righteous servant in heaven and earth—I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. Then let him choose whatever supplication he wills.'"],[5141,"How bad it is for one of you to say, 'I forgot such and such a verse,' rather he was made to forget. Recall the Quran, for it is swifter in slipping away from the hearts of men than camels from their hobbles."],[5142,"Abdullah used to remind the people every Thursday. A man said to him, 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, would that you reminded us every day?' He said, 'What prevents me from that is that I dislike wearying you. I choose times to admonish you as the Messenger of God ﷺ used to choose times to admonish us, for fear of boredom on our part.'"],[5143,"Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. A man keeps telling the truth until he is recorded as a truthful one. Lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. A man keeps lying until he is recorded with God as a liar."],[5144,"I know the last of the people of the Fire to come out of it and the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise: a man who comes out of the Fire crawling. God says, 'Go and enter Paradise.' He comes to it, and it seems to him that it is full, so God says, 'Enter, for you have the like of the world and ten times its like.' He says, 'Do You mock me—or laugh at me—while You are the King?' He said: Then I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ laugh until his molars showed. He said: It was said, 'That is the lowest of the people of Paradise in station.'"],[5145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, 'Which people are best?' He said, 'My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then will come a people whose testimony hastens ahead of their oath and whose oath hastens ahead of their testimony.' Ibrahim said: They used to forbid us, while we were boys, from making covenants and bearing testimonies."],[5146,"God curses women who tattoo, those who have themselves tattooed, those who pluck facial hair, and those who file gaps between their teeth for beauty, altering God's creation. He said: This reached a woman of Banu Asad called Umm Yaqub, who used to recite the Quran. She came and said, 'What is this report that has reached me from you, that you cursed women who tattoo, those who have themselves tattooed, those who pluck facial hair, and those who file gaps between their teeth for beauty, altering God's creation?' Abdullah said, 'Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of God ﷺ cursed, and it is in the Book of God?' The woman said, 'I have read what is between the two covers of the mushaf and I have not found it.' He said, 'By God, if you have read it, you have found it.' Then he said, 'Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it.' The woman said, 'I see something of this on your wife.' He said, 'Go and look.' She went in to Abdullah's wife and saw nothing. She came back to him and said, 'I saw nothing.' He said, 'If that had been the case, we would not have shared her bed.'"],[5147,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed a prayer. Ibrahim said: I do not know whether he added or omitted. When he said the salam, it was said to him, 'O Messenger of God, has something new happened in the prayer?' He said, 'No, and what is that?' They said, 'You prayed such and such.' He said: He folded his leg, faced the qiblah, and made two prostrations, then said the salam. When he said the salam, he turned his face toward us and said, 'If something new had happened in the prayer, I would have informed you of it. But I am only a human being like you; I forget as you forget. So when I forget, remind me. If one of you doubts in the prayer, let him seek what is right and complete accordingly, then say the salam, then make two prostrations.'"],[5148,"There is none of you but has been appointed a companion from the jinn. They said, 'Even you, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'Even me, except that God helped me against him and he became Muslim, so he only commands me to good.'"],[5149,"O company of women, give charity, even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the people of Hell. A woman who was not among the elite of women said, 'Why are we, O Messenger of God, the majority of the people of Hell?' He said, 'Because of your frequent cursing and your ingratitude to your husbands.'"],[5150,"When he saw people turning away, he said, 'O God, seven like the seven of Joseph.' Then a year seized them that stripped away everything, until they ate the flesh of dead animals, skins, and carcasses, and one of them would look at the sky and see smoke from hunger. Abu Sufyan came to him and said, 'O Muhammad, you have come commanding obedience to God and the ties of kinship. Your people have perished, so pray to God for them.' God said: 'So watch for the day when the sky brings a visible smoke... We will take retribution.'"],[5151,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who consumes usury and the one who pays it. He said: I said, 'And its two witnesses and its scribe?' He said, 'We only narrate what we heard.'"],[5152,"The most blameless people in killing are the people of faith."],[5153,"The child belongs to the owner of the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone."],[5154,"If I were to take a close friend from the people of the earth, I would have taken Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah as a close friend, but your companion is the close friend of Allah. The Quran was revealed in seven harfs; for every verse there is an outward and an inward, and for every limit there is a point of ascent."],[5155,"\"Recite to me.\" I said, \"Did I not learn it from you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"I love to hear it from other than me.\" So I recited Surat al-Nisa' to him until I reached: \"So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these?\" Then his eyes overflowed."],[5156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked ten qualities: wearing a gold ring, dragging the lower garment, saffron dye — meaning khaluq —, changing gray hair — Jarir said: meaning plucking it —, ruqyah except with the two protective surahs, tying amulets, striking with dice, displaying adornment to other than its proper place, withdrawing water from its place, and corrupting a boy without making it forbidden."],[5157,"I struck a man from the nobles of Persia on the day of Mihran. He said: I took his spoils to the ruler. He said: I took a gold ring of his. He said: It had been seen on my hand. He said: I said, \"If I go out to the land of the Persians and something befalls me, it will be useful as a means of support.\" Then I entered upon Abdullah while it was on my hand. He said, \"What is this ring?\" So I told him the story. He took it from me, put it in his mouth, chewed it, then threw it to me and said, \"The Prophet ﷺ forbade gold rings.\""],[5158,"Your Prophet has been given everything except the keys of the five: 'Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs' — the entire verse."],[5159,"We asked the Prophet ﷺ about walking with a funeral procession. He said: \"Walking is less than a trot. If it is good, it is hastened to it; if it is other than that, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral procession is followed, and it is not followed by one who goes ahead of it.\""],[5160,"The first man among the Muslims — or in the Muslims — whose hand was cut off was a man from the Ansar. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and it was said, \"He stole.\" He said, \"Take your companion and cut off his hand.\" It was as if the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was covered with ashes. One of those sitting with him said, \"It seems this has distressed you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"And what should prevent it? You should not be helpers of Satan — or of Iblis. It is not appropriate for a ruler to have a legal punishment brought to him except that he carry it out. Allah is Forgiving and loves forgiveness.\" Then he recited this verse: \"And let them pardon and overlook. Do you not like that Allah should forgive you?\""],[5161,"There will be after me selfishness and matters you will disapprove of.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how do you command those of us who experience that?\" He said, \"You fulfill the right that is upon you, and you ask Allah for what is yours.\""],[5162,"The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty days, then he is a clot for the like of that, then he is a lump of flesh for the like of that. Then Allah sends the angel with four words: his provision, his deeds, his lifespan, and whether he is wretched or blessed. By the One in whose hand is my soul, one of you does the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only a cubit between him and it, then what was decreed for him in the Book overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it. And one of you does the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only a cubit between him and it, then what was decreed for him in the Book overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise and enters it."],[5163,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cave, suddenly \"By those sent forth in succession\" descended upon him, and we received it from his mouth while his mouth was still moist with it. Then a snake came out, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it.\" We rushed at it, but it got ahead of us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It has been protected from your evil, and you have been protected from its evil.\""],[5164,"When this verse was revealed: \"Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing,\" it was hard on the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they said, \"Which of us has not mixed his faith with wrongdoing?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not that. Did you not hear the saying of Luqman: 'Indeed, associating partners with Allah is great wrongdoing'?\""],[5165,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “Indeed, God holds the heavens on one finger, the earths on one finger, the mountains and trees on one finger, the water and soil on one finger, and all creatures on one finger.” Then he said: “I am the King.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then recited this verse: “They have not appraised God with true appraisal, while the earth entirely will be [within] His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand” [Q 39:67], the verse. I said to Ibrahim: “In this world or in the Hereafter?” He said: “In this world.”"],[5166,"I was in the mosque on the night before Friday when a man from the Ansar entered and said: “If a man were to find another man with his wife—if he speaks, you flog him; if he kills, you kill him; if he remains silent, he remains silent in rage. By God, I will ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about it.” When the next day came, he went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him, saying: “If a man were to find another man with his wife—if he speaks, you flog him; or if he kills, you kill him; or if he remains silent, he remains silent in rage.” He said: “O God, make it clear,” and continued to supplicate. Then the verse of li‘an was revealed: “And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses except themselves…” [Q 24:6] these verses. The man was tested among the people, so he and his wife came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and performed li‘an. The man testified four testimonies by God that he was indeed truthful, then invoked the fifth: that the curse of God be upon him if he was among the liars. She went to swear, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Stop.” She swore. When they turned away, he said: “Perhaps she will bring a black, curly-haired child.” She brought a black, curly-haired child."],[5167,"“What do you consider the childless one among you?” He said: We said: “The one who has no child.” He said: “That is not the childless one. Rather, the childless one is the one who has not sent ahead any of his children.” He said: “And what do you consider the strong wrestler among you?” He said: We said: “The one whom men cannot throw down.” He said: “That is not him. Rather, it is the one who controls himself when angry.”"],[5168,"“Which of you loves his own wealth more than the wealth of his heir?” They said: “O Messenger of God, none of us but loves his own wealth more than the wealth of his heir.” He said: “Know what you are saying.” They said: “We know nothing but that, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Is there any man among you who loves the wealth of his heir more than his own wealth?” They said: “How is that, O Messenger of God?” He said: “A man’s wealth is only what he sends ahead, and his heir’s wealth is what he leaves behind.”"],[5169,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was suffering from fever. I touched him with my hand and said: “O Messenger of God, you are suffering from a severe fever.” The Messenger of God said: “Yes, I suffer fever as two men among you would.” I said: “That is because you have two rewards?” The Messenger of God said: “Yes.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No Muslim is afflicted with any harm, of illness or otherwise, but God removes some of his sins by it, as a tree sheds its leaves.”"],[5170,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and he prolonged it until I thought of doing something bad.” He said: “And what did you think of doing?” He said: “I thought of sitting down and leaving him.”"],[5171,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about a man who loves a people but has not joined them?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A person is with those whom he loves.”"],[5172,"A man said: “O Messenger of God, which sin is greatest in the sight of God?” He said: “That you set up a rival to God when He created you.” He said: “Then which?” He said: “Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor’s wife.” He said: Then God sent down confirmation of it: “And those who do not invoke with God another deity or kill the soul which God has forbidden except by right…” [Q 25:68] the verse."],[5173,"I will precede you to the Cistern, and I will surely contend for certain men among you, but I will be overcome concerning them. It will be said: “You do not know what they introduced after you.”"],[5174,"No one loves praise more than God, Mighty and Majestic; for that reason He praised Himself. And no one is more jealous than God; for that reason He forbade immoralities."],[5175,"A woman must not have physical contact with another woman and then describe her to her husband as if he were looking at her."],[5176,"Today a man asked me about something I did not know what to say to him. He said: “What do you think about a man who is diligent, energetic, eager for jihad, while our commanders order us to do things we cannot count?” He said: I said: “By God, I do not know what to say to you except that we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and perhaps he would not command us anything but we did it. What remains of this world is like a muddy pool whose clear water has been drunk and whose dregs remain. One of you will remain in good as long as he fears God, and if something troubles his soul, he goes to a man and asks him, and he heals him. By God, it will soon be that you will not find him.”"],[5177,"We were walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we passed by some boys among whom was Ibn Sayyad. The boys fled, and Ibn Sayyad sat down. It was as if the Messenger of God ﷺ disliked that, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"May your hands be dusty. Do you testify that I am the Messenger of God?\" He said: \"No, rather you testify that I am the Messenger of God.\" Umar said: \"Will you permit me, O Messenger of God, to kill him?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If he is the one you think, you will never be able to kill him.\""],[5178,"It was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"By those sent forth in succession\" while we were in a cave, and he recited it to me. Indeed I recite it close to what he recited to me, yet I do not know with which of its endings he concluded: \"And when it is said to them, 'Bow down,' they do not bow down\" or \"Then in what statement after it will they believe?\""],[5179,"Let none of you make for Satan a portion of himself, that he sees it as a duty upon him to turn away from his right side. Indeed I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ most often turning away from his left side. Umarah said: Then I came to Madinah and saw the dwellings of the Messenger of God ﷺ on his left side."],[5180,"Al-Ash'ath b. Qays entered upon Abdullah while he was having lunch. He said: \"Come and eat.\" Al-Ash'ath said: \"Is today not the day of Ashura?\" Abdullah said: \"And what lets you know what Ashura is? The Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast it, but when Ramadan was revealed, he left it.\""],[5181,"I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray any prayer except at its proper time, except for two prayers: I saw him pray Maghrib and Isha together at Muzdalifah, and he prayed the Fajr prayer before its time in the darkness of dawn."],[5182,"I entered upon Abdullah to visit him while he was ill, and he narrated to us two hadiths: a hadith from himself and a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"Indeed the believer sees his sins as if he is at the base of a mountain, fearing that it will fall upon him. And indeed the wicked person sees his sins like a fly that passed over his nose, so he waved it away from himself.\" He said: \"And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: 'God is more intensely pleased with the repentance of His believing servant than a man in a desolate, dangerous land, with him his riding camel upon which is his food and drink, who fell asleep, then woke up and it had gone. He stood up seeking it, and he sought it until thirst overtook him. Then he said: I will return to my place where I was until I die. He said: So he placed his head on his forearm to die, then he woke up and his riding camel was with him, upon it his provisions, his food, and his drink. So God is more intensely pleased with the repentance of His servant than this man with his riding camel and his provisions.'\""],[5183,"There is no one to whom praise is more beloved than God; for that reason He praised Himself. And there is no one more jealous than God; for that reason He forbade immoralities. And there is no one to whom excuse is more beloved than God; for that reason He sent down the Book and sent the messengers."],[5184,"There is no soul killed unjustly except that upon the first son of Adam is a share of its blood, because he was the first to establish killing."],[5185,"I absolve myself to every close friend from his close friendship, and if I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend. Indeed your companion is the close friend of God."],[5186,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"O God, You have made my physical form good, so make my character good.\""],[5187,"Nothing transmits infection to anything, three times. A bedouin among the people said: \"O Messenger of God, what about the camel that is among a large herd of camels and has a scab on its tail or its lip, and then all the camels become mangy?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Then who made the first one mangy?\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no infection, no evil omen, no Safar, no Hama. God created every soul and wrote its life, its provision, and its afflictions.\""],[5188,"Indeed God has not sent down any disease except that He has made for it a cure. He who knows it knows it, and he who is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."],[5189,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to relieve himself, and he did so. He said: 'Find me something to cleanse myself with, but do not bring me anything dry (like dung) or bones.' He said: 'Then he performed wudu and stood to pray. I saw that whenever he bowed, he bent — meaning he clasped his hands together and placed them between his knees.'"],[5190,"I was with Abdullah until he reached Jamrat al-Aqabah, and I got ahead of him. He said: 'Hand me some stones.' I handed him seven stones while he was reciting the talbiyah. Then he said: 'Take hold of the she-camel's reins.' He came to the bottom of the valley, turned toward the tree, then said: 'Allahu akbar.' Then he threw, saying 'Allahu akbar' with each pebble until he had thrown seven pebbles. Then he said: 'O Allah, make it an accepted Hajj and a forgiven sin.' Then he said: 'Thus did the one to whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed.'"],[5191,"There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and empowered him to spend it in the way of truth, and another to whom Allah has given wisdom, so he judges by it and teaches it."],[5192,"On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What do you think about these captives?' Abdullah b. Rawahah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you are in a valley with much firewood, so set the valley ablaze upon them, then cast them into it.' Al-Abbas said: 'May Allah sever your kinship.' Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, they are the leaders and chiefs of the polytheists. They denied you and fought you. Strike their necks.' Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah, they are your kin and your people. Spare them so that Allah may save them through you from the Fire.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then went in to relieve himself. One group said: 'The correct view is what Umar said,' and another group said: 'The correct view is what Abu Bakr said.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: 'What do you say about these two men? Their likeness is that of brothers who came before them. Nuh said: \"My Lord, do not leave upon the earth any dweller from among the disbelievers. If You leave them, they will mislead Your servants\" (71:26–27). Musa said: \"Our Lord, obliterate their wealth and harden their hearts so they will not believe until they see the painful punishment\" (10:88). Ibrahim ﷺ said: \"Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me — indeed, You are Forgiving and Merciful\" (14:36). Isa said: \"If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, indeed You are the Exalted in Might, the Wise\" (5:118). You are a people in need, so let none of you return except with a ransom or a stroke of the neck.' Abdullah said: 'I said: Except Suhayl b. Bayda', for he should not be killed, for I heard him speaking of Islam.' He fell silent. No day ever came upon me that I feared more that stones would be thrown down upon me from the sky than that day, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Except Suhayl b. Bayda'.'"],[5193,"We used to greet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, and he would respond to us. When we returned from the Negus, we greeted him and he did not respond. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we used to greet you during prayer and you would respond to us.' He said: 'Indeed, in prayer there is sufficient occupation.'"],[5194,"We used to greet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during prayer and he would respond to us. Then one day I greeted him and he did not respond to me. I felt something in myself. When he finished, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when I greeted you during prayer, you used to respond to me.' He said: 'Indeed, Allah brings about whatever He wills of His command.'"],[5195,"The excellence of a man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-some degrees."],[5196,"Alqamah and al-Aswad asked permission to enter upon Abdullah, and they had prolonged sitting at his door until midday. He said: 'I went out and sought permission for them, and he admitted them. He said to them: \"What kept you from entering?\" They said: \"We thought you were asleep.\" He said: \"I would not like you to think that of me. We used to equate prayer at this hour with night prayer, or something like night prayer.\" Then he said: \"You will be ruled by commanders who will be distracted from the time of prayer, so pray it at its proper time.\" Then he stood and prayed between him and it, then said: \"Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\""],[5197,"I was walking with Abdullah in Mina when he met Uthman and stood with him talking. Uthman said to him: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, shall we marry you to a young slave girl, perhaps she will remind you of what has passed of your time?' Abdullah said: 'If you say that, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"O young men, whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and guarding chastity. Whoever cannot, then let him fast, for it is a shield for him.\"'"],[5198,"Abdullah recited Surat Yusuf in Homs, and a man said: 'It was not revealed like that.' Abdullah drew near to him and detected the smell of wine. He said: 'Do you deny the truth and drink the filth? By Allah, this is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to me. By Allah, I will not leave you until I flog you with the prescribed punishment.' He said: 'So he flogged him with the prescribed punishment.'"],[5199,"Uthman prayed four rak'ahs in Mina. Abdullah said to him: 'I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ in Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs. Then the ways parted with you. I wish that from four rak'ahs I had two accepted ones.'"],[5200,"Abdullah threw Jamrat al-Aqabah from the bottom of the valley with seven pebbles, saying 'Allahu akbar' with each pebble. It was said to him: 'Some people throw it from above.' Abdullah said: 'This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the one to whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed.'"],[5201,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Mina when the moon split, until a piece of it went behind the mountain. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Bear witness.'"],[5202,"Whoever swears an oath while he is false in it, in order to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man, will meet God while He is angry with him. Al-Ash'ath said: 'By God, it was concerning me. That was between me and a man from the Jews over some land, and he denied me. So I brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God said to me: \"Do you have evidence?\" He said: I said: \"No.\" He said to the Jew: \"Swear.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, then he will swear and take my property.\" So God sent down: \"Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...\"'"],[5203,"Whoever dies while not associating anything with God will enter Paradise. He said: And I said: 'And whoever dies while associating something with God will enter the Fire.'"],[5204,"I will be your forerunner at the Cistern, and I will surely contend with some peoples, then I will surely be overcome concerning them. I will say: 'O Lord, my companions!' Then He will say: 'You do not know what they innovated after you.'"],[5205,"Do not acquire estates, lest you become desirous of the world. Then Abdullah said: 'And in Madinah, what is in Madinah, and in Radhan, what is in Radhan.'"],[5206,"He is not one of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of the people of the pre-Islamic ignorance."],[5207,"The blood of a Muslim man who bears witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God is not lawful, except for one of three: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."],[5208,"When one of you bows, let him spread his forearms on his thighs and lean forward. He said: It is as if I am looking at the interlocking of the fingers of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: Then he clasped his hands and showed them."],[5209,"I was hiding behind the curtains of the Ka'bah. He said: Then three people came, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding in their hearts. He said: A Qurashi and his two sons-in-law, Thaqafis, or a Thaqafi and his two sons-in-law, Qurashis. They spoke words that I did not understand, and one of them said: 'Do you think that God hears this speech of ours?' The other said: 'If we raise our voices, He hears it, and if we do not raise them, He does not hear it.' The other said: 'If He hears any of it, He hears all of it.' He said: I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and it was sent down to him: \"And you were not covering yourselves, lest your hearing and your eyes and your skins should bear witness against you,\" up to His saying: \"so you have become among the losers.\""],[5210,"It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of God ﷺ while he is relating about a prophet whose people struck him, and he is wiping the blood from his face and saying: 'My Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know.'"],[5211,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed a distribution, and a man from the Ansar said: 'This is a distribution by which the face of God is not intended.' He said: Abdullah said: I said: 'O enemy of God, I will surely inform the Messenger of God of what you said.' He said: I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: His face turned red, and he said: 'May God have mercy on Moses. He was harmed with more than this, and he was patient.'"],[5212,"For me to swear by God nine times that Ibn Sa'id is the Dajjal is more beloved to me than to swear once, and for me to swear nine times that the Messenger of God ﷺ was killed a killing is more beloved to me than to swear once, and that is because God took him as a prophet and made him a martyr."],[5213,"\"Indeed, incantations, amulets, and love charms are shirk.\" She said: I said, \"Why do you say this? My eye used to discharge, and I would go to a certain Jew who would recite over it, and when he recited over it, it would calm down.\" He said: \"That is only the work of Satan. He was pricking it with his hand, and when you recited over it, he would stop. It would have sufficed you to say as the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal; You are the Healer, a healing that leaves no sickness behind.'\""],[5214,"Indeed, the people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."],[5215,"The Messenger of God ﷺ made the blood-money for accidental killing into fifths."],[5216,"Paradise is closer to one of you than his shoelace, and the Fire is the same."],[5217,"I was with Masruq in a portico containing statues, and he looked at one of them. They said, \"This is a statue of Mary.\" Masruq said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers.\""],[5218,"God has angels who roam the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community."],[5219,"He used to greet to his right and to his left: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of God, peace be upon you and the mercy of God,\" until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[5220,"The first thing to be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed."],[5221,"It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of God ﷺ relating about a prophet from among the prophets whom his people struck, and he was wiping the blood from his face while saying, \"Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know.\""],[5222,"Whoever asks while he has wealth that suffices him, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches or gashes on his face. They said, \"O Messenger of God, what is his sufficiency?\" He said, \"Fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold.\""],[5223,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated at the Star (surah al-Najm), and the Muslims prostrated, except for a man from Quraysh who took a handful of dust and raised it to his forehead and prostrated on it. Abdullah said: I saw him killed as an unbeliever."],[5224,"Belief in omens is shirk, and there is none of us except... but God removes it through reliance on Him."],[5225,"When you are three, then two should not converse secretly apart from the one, for that would grieve him."],[5226,"Were it not that you are a messenger, I would have killed you. As for today, you are not a messenger. Arise, O Kharasha, and strike his neck."],[5227,"A man came to Abdullah and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how do you recite this verse: 'from water not stale'? He said: Abdullah said to him: Have you enumerated all of the Quran except this? He said: I recite the Mufassal in one rak'ah. Abdullah said to him: Hastily, like the recitation of poetry? Among the best acts of prayer are bowing and prostration. Peoples will surely recite the Quran but it will not go beyond their collarbones, but when it is recited and takes root in the heart, it benefits. I know the corresponding surahs which the Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in each rak'ah. Then he stood, and Alqama entered upon him. Then he said: Ask him for us about the corresponding surahs which the Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite. He said: Then he came out to us and said: Twenty surahs from the Mufassal in Abdullah's arrangement."],[5228,"We were walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he passed by Ibn al-Sayyad. The Messenger of God said: I have hidden something for you. Ibn al-Sayyad said: Al-dukhkh. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Be off! You will never exceed your station."],[5229,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to sleep lying on his back until he snored, then he would get up and pray without performing ablution."],[5230,"Alqama led us in prayer and prayed five rak'ahs, and the people shuffled about and criticized him. He said: I said: You have done so. He said: And you, O one-eyed one, say that? He said: He turned and prostrated twice, then he narrated to them, from Abdullah, that the Prophet ﷺ prayed five rak'ahs with them, and that was mentioned to him, so he turned and prostrated twice, and said: I am only a human being; I forget as you forget."],[5231,"Abdullah used to come out to us and say: I am informed of your location, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except the dislike of wearying you. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to give us admonition at intervals on some days, disliking boredom for us."],[5232,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom God has given wealth and empowered him to spend it in the way of truth, and a man to whom God has given wisdom, and he judges by it and teaches it."],[5233,"Recite to me. I said: O Messenger of God, how can I recite to you when it was sent down upon you? He said: I love to hear it from someone other than myself. He said: I recited Surat al-Nisa' to him, until I came to this verse: 'So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?' He said: I looked at him and his eyes were flowing with tears."],[5234,"What have I to do with the world? My likeness and the likeness of the world is only like a rider who takes shade under a tree on a summer day, then departs and leaves it."],[5235,"When 'When the help of God and victory comes' was sent down upon the Prophet ﷺ, he would often say, when he recited it and bowed: Glory be to You, O God, our Lord, and with Your praise. O God, forgive me; You are the Oft-Forgiving, the Merciful, three times."],[5236,"The Prophet ﷺ gave me the sword of Abu Jahl as booty on the day of Badr."],[5237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the two rak'ahs as if he were on hot coals. I said: Until he stands? He said: Until he stands. Waki' said: On burning stones."],[5238,"Indeed, praise belongs to Allah; we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can lead astray, and whomever He leads astray, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but He, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he recites verses from the Book of Allah: 'Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims'; 'Fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs; indeed Allah is ever watchful over you'; 'Fear Allah and speak a right word, He will amend your deeds and forgive your sins; and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has achieved a great success.'"],[5239,"Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas and Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, the like of it."],[5240,"A man came to Abu Musa and Salman b. Rabi'ah and asked them about a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister. They said: For the daughter is half, and the remainder is for the sister. Then the man came to Abdullah and asked him, and informed him of what they had said. He said: Then I have gone astray and I am not of the rightly guided. Rather, I judge by what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged: For the daughter is half, for the son's daughter is one sixth to complete the two thirds, and the remainder is for the sister."],[5241,"Follow between the Hajj and the Umrah, for indeed they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron, gold, and silver, and there is no reward for an accepted Hajj except Paradise."],[5242,"I said to Ibn Mas'ud: Did any of you accompany the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the jinn? He said: None of us accompanied him, but we lost him one night in Makkah and said: He has been assassinated, or snatched away. We spent the worst night a people could spend. When it was the time before dawn - or he said: morning - there he was coming from the direction of Hira'. We said: O Messenger of Allah, and they mentioned to him what they had been through. He said: Indeed, a caller from the jinn came to me, so I went and recited to them. Then he went and showed us their traces and the traces of their fires."],[5243,"Let not any of you be prevented by Bilal's call to prayer - or he said: Bilal's announcement - from his pre-dawn meal, for he calls the adhan - or he said: announces - at night, so that one who is praying may return, and your sleeping one may wake. And he said: It is not that you say like this and like this - and he lowered his hand and raised it - until he says like this - and he spread his fingers."],[5244,"He forbade going out to meet merchandise (before it reaches the market)."],[5245,"A man kissed a woman, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and this verse was revealed: 'Establish prayer at the two ends of the day.' He said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for me? He said: And for whoever acts upon it from my Ummah."],[5246,"The consumer of riba, the one who pays it, its scribe, and its two witnesses when they know of it, the woman who tattoos and the woman who is tattooed, the one who withholds charity, and the one who reverts to being a bedouin after his migration are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ."],[5247,"Indeed, destroyed are the nitpickers - three times."],[5248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a square line for us, and he drew lines in its middle like this, to the side of the line, and he drew a line outside. He said: Do you know what this is? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is the human being - for the line which is in the middle of the line - and this is the appointed time, and these are the things that harm him - for the lines - they bite him; if this one misses him, this one strikes him, and that is hope - for the outer line."],[5249,"An amir in Makkah used to give two salams. Abdullah said: 'How did he learn it?' Al-Hakam said in his hadith: 'The Prophet ﷺ used to do it.'"],[5250,"I was hiding behind the curtains of the Kaaba when three men entered: a Thaqafi and his two Qurayshi in-laws. They talked among themselves. One of them said: 'Do you think Allah hears what we say?' One of them said: 'He hears if we raise our voices, but does not hear if we lower them.' The other said: 'If He hears anything from us, He hears all of it.' I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and this verse was revealed: 'And you were not concealing yourselves lest your hearing testify against you...'"],[5251,"Mansur narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah, with something similar."],[5252,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: 'Were it not that you are a messenger, I would have killed you' - meaning the messenger of Musaylima."],[5253,"The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."],[5254,"If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but he is my brother and companion, and Allah has taken your companion as a close friend."],[5255,"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot imitate me."],[5256,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[5257,"He is not one of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."],[5258,"A wind blew while we were with Abdullah. Ibn Mas'ud became angry until we recognized anger on his face. He said: 'Woe to you! The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and no booty is rejoiced over.' Then he pointed with his hand toward Syria and said: 'An enemy gathers against the Muslims from here. They meet, and he stipulates a detachment for death that does not return except victorious. They fight until the sun sets from here. They meet, and he stipulates a detachment for death that does not return except victorious. They fight until the sun sets, and neither side is victorious, and the detachment is annihilated. Then he stipulates a detachment for death that does not return except victorious. They fight until the sun sets. These and those return, and neither side is victorious, and the detachment is annihilated. Then they meet on the fourth day, and they kill them and rout them until the blood reaches the horses' saddle straps. They fight until the sons of one father count themselves among a hundred and are killed, leaving no man among them. So what inheritance will be divided after this, and what booty will be rejoiced over? Then they conquer Constantinople. While they are dividing dinars with shields, a greater terror comes to them: that the Dajjal has appeared among your families. So they abandon what is in their hands and return, sending out a vanguard of horsemen.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'They on that day are the best horsemen on earth. I know their names, their fathers' names, their tribes, and the colors of their horses.'"],[5259,"He said: Whoever buys a camel or sheep with milk retained in its udder and then returns it, let him return with it a sa' of dates."],[5260,"When you are three, let not two converse secretly excluding the third, for that grieves him."],[5261,"There was no more than four years between our embracing Islam and our being taken to task by this verse: 'Has the time not come for those who believe that their hearts should become humbly submissive for the remembrance of Allah and what has come down of the truth?' And we began to turn to one another, saying: What new thing have we introduced? What have we done?"],[5262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the sermon of need. Sufyan said: Indeed, all praise belongs to Allah. And Shu'bah said: All praise belongs to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help. Sufyan said: We seek refuge in Him. And Shu'bah said: We seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our own souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can lead astray, and whomever He leads astray, none can guide. And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he recited three verses: 'O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims'; 'And fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs'; 'Fear Allah and speak a proper word,' until His saying: 'a mighty triumph.' Then he would speak about his need."],[5263,"When the heat becomes intense, then delay the prayer until it is cooler—or: delay the prayer."],[5264,"When you are told something from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then think of the Messenger of Allah in the way that is most becoming, most God-fearing, and most guided."],[5265,"Were it not that you are a Messenger, I would have killed you."],[5266,"It was said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes."],[5267,"I heard a man recite a verse from the Book of Allah which I had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ differently, so I took him by the hand and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. I saw the Prophet's ﷺ face change, and he said: Both of you are doing well, and do not differ about it, for those before you differed about it, and he mentioned destruction."],[5268,"I came upon Abu Jahl while he was lying fallen, with a helmet on him, and I had a worn sword. I began to strike his head with my sword, remembering how he used to strike my head in Makkah, until his hand went limp and I took his sword. He raised his head and said: On whose side was the defeat? Against us or for us? Are you not our little shepherd boy in Makkah? He said: Then I killed him. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have killed Abu Jahl. He said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, you killed him? And he made me swear three times. Then he stood with me against them and supplicated against them."],[5269,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray a prayer except at its proper time, except that he joined Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah, and he prayed Fajr before its usual time."],[5270,"I have permitted you to raise the screen and listen to my private talk until I forbid you. He said: It has reached me that it is the secret conversation."],[5271,"I was sitting with Abdullah when a man asked him: What is suht (ill-gotten gain)? He said: Bribes. The man said: In judging? He said: That is disbelief. Then he recited: 'And whoever does not judge by what Allah has sent down—those are the disbelievers.'"],[5272,"When you invoke blessings upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then do it well, for you do not know—perhaps it will be presented to him. They said: Teach us, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: Say: O Allah, place Your blessings, Your mercy, and Your benedictions upon the master of the messengers, the imam of the God-fearing, the seal of the prophets, Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, the imam of good, the leader of good, the Messenger of mercy. O Allah, raise him to a praiseworthy station that the first and the last will envy him for. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious."],[5273,"I have not lied since I became Muslim except for one lie. I was preparing a mount for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a man from al-Ta'if came and said, 'Which mount is most pleasing to the Messenger of God ﷺ?' I said, 'The al-Ta'ifi munkabba.' He said, 'And the Messenger of God ﷺ disliked it.' He said, 'When he saddled it and brought it, he said, \"Who saddled this for us?\"' They said, 'The one you brought from al-Ta'if saddled it for you.' He said, 'Return the mount to Ibn Mas'ud.'"],[5274,"If one of your animals escapes in a desolate land, let him call out: 'O servants of God, restrain it! O servants of God, restrain it!' For God has a presence on earth that will restrain it."],[5275,"God is odd and loves the odd, so when you clean yourself with stones, make it an odd number."],[5276,"The two feet of the son of Adam will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about five things: about his life and how he spent it; about his youth and how he wore it out; about his wealth, from where he earned it and on what he spent it; and what he did with what he knew."],[5277,"Our Lord marvels at two men: a man who rises from his bed and blanket, from among his people and family, to perform prayer, out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me; and a man who fights in the path of God and flees, then knows what is upon him for fleeing and what is for him in returning, so he returns until his blood is shed. God says to His angels: 'Look at My servant; he returned out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me, until his blood was shed.'"],[5278,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, when Ramadan had begun: 'If the servants knew what is in Ramadan, my community would wish that Ramadan lasted the whole year.' A man from Khuza'ah said, 'Tell us about it.' He said: 'Paradise is adorned for Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the next, until when the first day of Ramadan comes, a wind blows from beneath the Throne and rustles the leaves of Paradise. The houris with wide eyes look at that and say, \"O Lord, grant us husbands from Your servants in this month, so that our eyes may be delighted with them and their eyes may be delighted with us.\"' He said: 'There is no servant who fasts Ramadan except that he is married to a wife from the houris with wide eyes in a pavilion of hollow pearl, as God has described: \"Houris, restrained in pavilions.\" For each woman among them are seventy garments, no garment of them being the color of another. She is given seventy types of perfume, no type of them having the scent of another. For each woman among them are seventy couches of red ruby studded with pearls. On each couch are seventy beds whose linings are of silk brocade, and above the seventy beds are seventy sofas. For each woman among them are seventy thousand serving girls for her needs and seventy thousand serving boys. With each serving boy is a plate of gold containing a type of food whose last morsel one finds a pleasure that he does not find in its first. Her husband is given the like of that on a couch of red ruby, upon which are two bracelets of gold studded with red ruby. This is for every day that he fasted in Ramadan, apart from the good deeds he did.'"],[5279,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eat meat, then stand for prayer without touching a drop of water."],[5280,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went to relieve himself and said: 'Bring me something with which to clean myself, and do not bring me anything that is a barrier or dung.' He said: 'I brought him water for ablution, and he performed ablution and then prayed.'"],[5281,"Insulting a Muslim – or a believer – is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[5282,"The Messenger of God ﷺ liked us to supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times."],[5283,"It is not appropriate for anyone to say: 'I am better than Yunus b. Matta.'"],[5284,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the noon prayer with five units. It was said to him, 'Has something been added to the prayer?' So he prostrated twice after he had said the salutation."],[5285,"Paradise is closer to any one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is the like of that."],[5286,"The millstone of Islam will turn for thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven [years]. If they perish, then it is in the way of those who perished; and if their religion endures for them, it will endure for them for seventy years. I said, 'From what has passed or from what remains?' He said, 'From what remains.'"],[5287,"All people will enter the Fire, then they will come out of it according to their deeds."],[5288,"He used to say: O God, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and sufficiency."],[5289,"He said to the women: Give charity, for you are the majority of the inhabitants of the Fire. A woman who was not from the elite of women said: Why—or in what, or because of what—are we? He said: Because you curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. There is none more deficient in intellect and religion and more overwhelming to men of authority than women. It was said: What is the deficiency of her intellect? He said: He made the testimony of two women equal to the testimony of one man. It was said: What is the deficiency of her religion? He said: She remains—I do not know how many days—without praying."],[5290,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from al-Hudaybiyyah, he stopped at a resting place and halted there at night. He said: Who will guard us? Abdullah said: I said: I will. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You will sleep—saying that twice or thrice—then he said: Then you. So I guarded them until when it was near dawn, what the Messenger of God ﷺ said overtook me, and I did not wake except from the heat of the sun on our backs. The Messenger of God ﷺ arose, did as he usually does, then prayed the Morning Prayer. Then he said: If God had willed, you would not have slept through it, but if it should happen for those after you, then thus is it for one who sleeps or forgets."],[5291,"I said: O Messenger of God, which deeds are most beloved to God? He said: Prayer at its proper times. I said: Then which? He said: Then dutifulness to parents. I said: Then which? He said: Then striving in the way of God."],[5292,"I and my paternal uncle entered upon Abdullah b. Mas'ud at noon, and he commenced the prayer. We went back behind him, but he took the hand of one of us with his right hand and the other with his left, and placed us on his right and left. When he prayed, he said: Thus the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do when they were three."],[5293,"God has not forbidden any sacred thing except that He knew someone among you would look into it. Indeed, I am holding you back by your waist-wrappers from the Fire, lest you tumble into it like the tumbling of moths, or flies, or beetles."],[5294,"He who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride will not enter Paradise."],[5295,"The last person to enter Paradise will be a man who walks across the Bridge. He will stumble once and walk once, and the Fire will scorch him once. When he has crossed the Bridge, he will turn to it and say: Blessed be the One who saved me from you. He has given me what He has not given anyone among the first and the last. A tree will be raised for him and he will look at it and say: O Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may shade myself with its shade and drink from its water. He will say: O servant, perhaps if I bring you near it you will ask Me for something else. He will say: No, O Lord. He will covenant with Him that he will not ask for anything else, and the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, knows that he will ask for something else because he sees what he cannot bear to do without. So He will bring him near it. Then a tree better than it will be raised for him, and he will say: O Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may shade myself with its shade and drink from its water. He will say: O servant, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for anything else? He will say: O Lord, this one I will not ask You for anything else. So He will bring him near it. Then a tree better than it will be raised for him at the gate of Paradise, and he will say: O Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may shade myself with its shade and drink from its water. He will say: O servant, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for anything else? He will say: O Lord, this one I will not ask You for anything else. He will covenant with Him—and the Lord knows that he will ask for something else because he sees what he cannot bear to do without—so He will bring him near it. Then he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise and say: O Lord, Paradise, Paradise. He will say: O My servant, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for anything else? He will say: O Lord, admit me into Paradise. He, Blessed and Exalted, will say: What will satisfy you from Me, O My servant? Will it please you that I give you the world and the like of it with it? Abdullah laughed until his molar teeth showed, then said: Will you not ask me why I laughed? They said: Why did you laugh? He said: Because of the laughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[5296,"I was not veiled from three—or not prevented from three—from private conversation, and from such-and-such, and from such-and-such. Abdullah said: My uncle forgot one, and I forgot the other, and this one remained. I came to him while Malik al-Rahawi was with him, and I caught the end of their conversation while he was saying: O Messenger of God, I am a man who has been given a share of beauty such as you see, and I do not love that anyone should surpass me even by two sandal-straps or more. Is that insolence? He said: No, but insolence is one who treats the truth lightly and belittles people."],[5297,"The Messenger of God ﷺ slept on a straw mat that left marks on his side. We said, \"O Messenger of God, why did you not inform us so that we could spread something softer than it beneath you?\" He said, \"What have I to do with the world? My similitude and that of the world is but that of a rider who travels on a scorching day, stops in the shade of a tree, then departs and leaves it.\""],[5298,"They detained us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May God fill their bellies and their graves with fire."],[5299,"On the night the Prophet ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, he met Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa (may the blessings of God be upon them). They discussed the Hour, when it would be. They began with Ibrahim and asked him about it, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they asked Musa, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they referred the matter to 'Isa, who said, \"God entrusted me with knowledge of what precedes its occurrence; as for its actual occurrence, none knows it except God.\" Then he mentioned the emergence of the Dajjal: \"I will descend and kill him. Then people will return to their lands, and Ya'juj and Ma'juj will come forth to meet them, pouring down from every elevation. They will not pass by any water but drink it, nor by anything but corrupt it. The people will cry out to me, so I will supplicate God, and He will cause them to die. The earth will stink from their odor. I will supplicate God to send rain from the sky, which will carry their bodies and cast them into the sea. Then the mountains will be pulverized, and the earth will be stretched out like leather.\" 'Isa said, \"God, Blessed and Exalted, entrusted me that when that happens, the Hour will be to people like a pregnant woman at full term: her family does not know when she will suddenly give birth, whether at night or day.\" Al-'Awwam said, \"I found confirmation of that in the Book of God,\" then he recited: 'Until when Ya'juj and Ma'juj are let loose...' [Qur'an 21:96]."],[5300,"A man came to Abu Musa and Salman b. Rabi'a and asked them about a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister through father and mother."],[5301,"May God brighten the face of a person who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it. For perhaps the one to whom it is conveyed retains it better than the hearer."],[5302,"No servant ever says, when afflicted by worry and grief: 'O God, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, my forelock is in Your hand, Your decree is executed upon me, Your judgment upon me is just. I ask You by every name with which You have named Yourself, or which You have sent down in Your Book, or which You have taught any of Your creation, or which You have kept to Yourself in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Qur'an the spring of my heart, the light of my sight, the removal of my sadness, and the dispelling of my worry,' but that God removes his worry and replaces his sadness with joy.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, should we learn these words?\" He said, \"Yes, whoever hears them should learn them.\""],[5303,"The mill of Islam will revolve around the age of thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven. If they perish, it will be in the manner of those who perished. If they remain, their religion will remain for them for seventy years."],[5304,"I had forbidden you to visit graves, but now visit them. I had forbidden you to keep the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, but now keep it. I had forbidden you these vessels, but now make nabidh in them, and avoid every intoxicant."],[5305,"It was said, 'O Messenger of God, how will you recognize those of your community whom you have not seen on the Day of Resurrection?' He said, 'They will have white blazes on their foreheads and white marks on their limbs from the traces of ablution.'"],[5306,"On the night of the jinn, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do you have any water for purification?' He said, 'No, except a little nabidh in a water skin.' He said, 'Bring it. A good date and purifying water.'"],[5307,"Shall I not lead you in prayer as the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed? Then he led them in prayer and did not raise his hands except once."],[5308,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, he reached the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, which is in the sixth heaven. To it ends whatever is taken up from the earth, and it is taken from there; and to it ends whatever descends from above it, and it is taken from there—when the Lote Tree was covered by what covered it. He said: Moths of gold. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was given three things: the five prayers, the concluding verses of Surat al-Baqarah, and the major sins were forgiven for those of his community who do not associate anything with God."],[5309,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in a leather tent with about forty men. He said: 'You will be granted victory, made triumphant, and given spoils. Whoever of you lives to see that, let him fear God, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and maintain his kinship ties. Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. The likeness of one who helps his people in wrongdoing is that of a camel in a well, pulling itself out by its tail.'"],[5310,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to fast three days at the beginning of each lunar month, and he rarely broke his fast on Friday."],[5311,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delayed the night prayer one night, then went out to the mosque, and found the people waiting for the prayer. He said: 'There is no one among the people of the religions who remembers God at this hour except you.' He said: And these verses were revealed: 'They are not all alike; among the People of the Scripture is an upright community...' to '...and God knows the God-fearing.'"],[5312,"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[5313,"If I were to take a close friend from my community, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend."],[5314,"He used to fast while traveling and break his fast, and he would pray two rak'ahs without omitting them, saying: 'He does not add to it,' meaning the obligatory prayer."],[5315,"I used to gather a miswak from an arak tree for the Messenger of God ﷺ. The wind would bend him over, and there was something about my shins, so the people laughed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'What makes you laugh?' They said: 'The thinness of his shins.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Balance than Mount Uhud.'"],[5316,"I was a young boy, and I used to tend sheep for Ibn Abi Mu'ayt. The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr came, having fled from the idolaters. They said: 'O boy, do you have any milk to give us to drink?' I said: 'Yes, but I am entrusted, and I am not going to give you drink.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do you have a young ewe that no male has mounted?' I said: 'Yes.' I brought it to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ hobbled it, wiped the udder, and supplicated, and the milk began to flow. Abu Bakr brought him a hollowed-out rock, and he milked into it and drank, and Abu Bakr drank, and I drank. Then he said to the udder: 'Contract,' and it contracted. Later I came to him and said: 'O Messenger of God, teach me some of this speech—or this Qur'an.' He said: 'You are a taught boy.' But he taught me, and I took from his mouth seventy surahs that no one disputes with me about."],[5317,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was praying in the shade of the Ka'bah, and Abu Jahl and some men of Quraysh, having slaughtered a camel in a corner of Makkah, sent someone to bring its placenta, which they threw between his shoulders. Fatimah came and removed it from him. When he finished, he said—and he used to repeat three times—: 'O God, deal with Quraysh'—three times—'with Abu Jahl b. Hisham, with 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, with Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, with al-Walid b. 'Utbah, with Umayyah b. Khalaf, and with 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt.' 'Abdullah said: 'I saw them dead in the well of Badr—or in a well.' Abu Ishaq said: 'I forgot the seventh.'"],[5318,"Umm Habibah said: 'O God, bless me in my husband, the Messenger of God ﷺ, in my father Abu Sufyan, and in my brother Mu'awiyah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'You have asked God about fixed terms, allotted provisions, and destined traces—nothing of them is hastened before its time. If you had asked God to protect you from the punishment of the Fire or the punishment of the grave, it would have been better or more virtuous.' He said: Then monkeys were mentioned—he said: I think he said pigs—were they among those transformed among the Children of Israel? He said: 'God has not destroyed a people and left them descendants or posterity. Monkeys—and I think he said pigs—existed before that.'"],[5319,"They asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about monkeys and pigs: Are they from the descendants of the Jews? The Messenger of God said: 'God has not cursed a people and transformed them so that they have descendants until He destroys them. Rather, this is a creation that existed before. When God became angry with the Jews, He transformed them, and they became like them.'"],[5320,"Shayban narrated to us: Dawud b. Abi al-Furat narrated to us with his chain, the like of it."],[5321,"Among the worst of people is one whom the Hour overtakes while he takes graves as mosques."],[5322,"Whoever is afflicted by poverty and lays it before the people, his poverty will not be closed; but if he lays it before Allah, Allah will soon bring him sufficiency, either a swift sufficiency or a delayed death."],[5323,"The nations were presented to the Prophet ﷺ until his nation was presented, and he was pleased by their great number. It was said: 'With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.'"],[5324,"When the last third of the night remains, Allah descends to the lowest heaven. Then the gates of heaven are opened, then they are spread out, then He says: 'Is there any asker?' And He continues thus until dawn rises."],[5325,"While Ibn Mas'ud was delivering a sermon one day, he noticed a snake walking on the wall. He cut off his sermon and struck it with a small stick until he killed it, then said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed a polytheist man.'"],[5326,"Shayban narrated to us: Dawud b. Abi al-Furat narrated to us with his chain, the like of it."],[5327,"We were sitting with Ibn Mas'ud one night after Maghrib while he was teaching us the Quran. A man asked him: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, did you ask the Messenger of Allah how many caliphs this nation will have?' Ibn Mas'ud said: 'No one has asked me this since I came to Iraq before you.' He said: 'Yes, we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Twelve, the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israel.'"],[5328,"Shayban narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us with his chain, similar to it."],[5329,"Let those of you who possess maturity and understanding stand nearest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them. Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Beware of the clamor of the marketplaces."],[5330,"Al-Qawariri narrated to us: Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, the like of it."],[5331,"Indeed, do not turn back after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks."],[5332,"He used to recite: “Is there any that will remember?”"],[5333,"Salma bt. Jabir reported that her husband was martyred. She came to Abdullah b. Mas'ud and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, my husband was martyred, and men have proposed to me. Do you hope that if Allah gathers me and him together in Paradise, I will be among his wives? He said: Yes. Some of the people said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we have not seen you do this with any woman other than this one. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The first of my ummah to join me in Paradise will be a woman from Ahmas."],[5334,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: That you pray the prayers at their proper times. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Then dutifulness to parents. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Then jihad in the path of Allah. And if I had asked for more, he would have increased for me."],[5335,"No one will enter the Fire who has in his heart an atom's weight of a mustard seed of faith, and no one will enter Paradise who has in his heart an atom's weight of a mustard seed of arrogance."],[5336,"Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Muslim narrated to us, similarly."],[5337,"Fighting a believer is disbelief, and insulting him is wickedness."],[5338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite: “Indeed, I am the Provider, Possessor of Strength, the Strong.”"],[5339,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir in every rising, lowering, and standing, and he gave the greeting to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until I saw the whiteness of his cheeks. And I saw Abu Bakr and Umar do that."],[5340,"He said to a group of people who were staying away from Jumu'ah: I was about to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then burn the houses of men who stay away from Jumu'ah."],[5341,"The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself and ordered me to bring him three stones. I took two stones and sought the third but did not find it, so I took a piece of dung and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ. He took the two stones and threw away the dung and said: This is filth."],[5342,"I came to Zirr b. Hubaysh. He said: Affection for me was cast upon him, and there were young men with him. They said to me: Ask him – for he was at a distance of two bow-lengths or nearer – so I asked him, and he said: Abdullah b. Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Jibril, and he had six hundred wings."],[5343,"There will be in the Fire a people as long as Allah wills. Then Allah will have mercy on them, and they will be in the lowest part of Paradise. They will be washed in the River of Life, and the people of Paradise will call them the Jahannamiyyun. If one of them were to host the people of the world, he would feed them, give them drink, spread bedding for them, and cover them – and I think he said: and marry them – without that diminishing anything from him."],[5344,"The prophets were presented to me tonight with their nations and their followers from their nations. Then a prophet would pass with three from his ummah, and a prophet would pass with a group from his ummah, and a prophet would pass with a small number, and a prophet would pass with a single man from his ummah, and a prophet would pass with none of his people. Indeed, Allah has informed you about Lot, and He said: 'Is there not among you a right-minded man?' He said: Until Moses came to me in a multitude of the Children of Israel. When I saw them, they amazed me. He said: I said, 'Who are these?' He said, 'This is your brother Moses, son of Imran, and those who followed him from the Children of Israel.' He said: I said, 'My Lord, where is my ummah?' He said, 'Look to your right.' And behold, the hillocks—the hillocks of Makkah—were filled with the faces of men. He said: I said, 'My Lord, who are these?' He said, 'These are your ummah.' He said to me, 'Are you satisfied?' He said: I said, 'My Lord, I am satisfied.' He said: It was said to me, 'Look to your left.' And behold, the horizon was filled with men. He said: 'Indeed, with these there are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.' He said: Then 'Ukkasha b. Mihsan, the brother of Banu Asad b. Khuzayma, stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate your Lord to make me one of them.' He said, 'O Allah, make him one of them.' He said: Then another man stood up, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'Ukkasha has preceded you to it.' He said: Then he said that day, 'I hope that those who follow me from my ummah will be a quarter of the people of Paradise.' He said: So we said takbir. Then he said, 'I hope that you will be a third.' He said: Then we said takbir. Then he said, 'I hope that you will be half.' Then he recited: 'A multitude from the former generations and a multitude from the later generations.' Then he mentioned to us that some men among the believers discussed among themselves, saying, 'What do you think—do you think the deeds of these seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning are such that they are people born in Islam and did not cease until they died upon it?' He said, in what he narrated to them, until it reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, 'It is not so. Rather, they are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqya, and do not practice tiyara, and upon their Lord they rely.' He said: And the Prophet ﷺ said that day, 'If you can—may my father and mother be sacrificed for you—be among the seventy thousand, then be among them. But if you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the hillocks. And if you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the horizon. For I saw with it many people assembling in crowds.'"],[5345,"The nations were presented to me at the season, and I saw my ummah. Then I saw them again, and their large number and their appearance amazed me—they had filled the plain and the mountain. He said, 'Are you satisfied, O Muhammad?' He said: I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Indeed, with these you have seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. They are those who do not seek ruqya, do not cauterize, and upon their Lord they rely.' Then 'Ukkasha b. Mihsan stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.' So he supplicated for him. Then another stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me one of them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Ukkasha has preceded you to it.'"],[5346,"I heard a man reciting a verse differently from what I had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: So I took him by the hand and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'Both of you are good.' Shu'ba said: And I think he said, 'Do not differ, for those before you differed about it and were destroyed.'"],[5347,"A banner will be erected for every treacherous person on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said, 'This is the treachery of so-and-so.'"],[5348,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I fell upon a woman in the garden and did everything with her except that I did not have intercourse. So do with me what you will.' He said nothing to him, and the man left. Then he called him and recited to him: 'And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.'"],[5349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the consumer of riba, the one who gives it, its two witnesses, and its scribe."],[5350,"Indeed, your companion is the intimate friend of Allah."],[5351,"A Muslim's fighting his brother is kufr, and insulting him is fusuq."],[5352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the tashahhud, with my palm between his two palms, just as he taught me a surah from the Qur'an: 'All greetings, prayers, and good things are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.' This was while he was among us. When he passed away, we said, 'Peace be upon the Prophet ﷺ.'"],[5353,"Riba, even if it is abundant, its outcome ultimately becomes little."],[5354,"Riba, even if it is abundant, its outcome ultimately becomes little."],[5355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the consumer of riba, the one who gives it, the woman who joins hair extensions, the one who has them joined, and the one who makes a woman lawful (through a temporary marriage) and the one for whom she is made lawful."],[5356,"The polytheists distracted the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of the Trench from four prayers until as much of the night had passed as Allah willed. He said: Then he commanded Bilal, and he gave the call to prayer, then he made the iqamah and prayed Zhuhr, then he made the iqamah and prayed Asr, then he made the iqamah and prayed Maghrib, then he made the iqamah and prayed Isha."],[5357,"There are no two Muslims for whom three children die except that they will be a strong fortress for them against the Fire. He said: We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what if it was two?' He said, 'Even if it was two.' He said: Abu Dharr said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have not offered up any but two?' He said, 'Even if it was two.' He said: Ubayy b. Ka'b, Abu al-Mundhir, the master of the reciters, said, 'I have not offered up any but one?' He said, 'Even if it was one.' He said, 'That is only at the first shock.'"],[5358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the fear prayer. They stood in two rows, one row behind the Prophet ﷺ and one row facing the enemy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one unit with the row that was next to him, then they rose and went and took the place of those others facing the enemy, and those others came and took their place, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with them and then said the salam. Then they rose and prayed one unit for themselves and then said the salam. Then they went and took the place of those others facing the enemy, and those others returned to their place and prayed one unit for themselves, then said the salam."],[5359,"The Prophet ﷺ cut off for the value of five dirhams."],[5360,"A black slave caught up with the Prophet ﷺ and died, and the Prophet ﷺ was informed of it. He said, 'Look, did he leave anything?' They said, 'He left two dinars.' He said, 'Two brands of cauterization.'"],[5361,"Your permission over me is that you may raise the veil and hear my whisper until I forbid you."],[5362,"Your permission over me is that you may uncover the curtain."],[5363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: How will you be when you are a quarter of the people of Paradise, a quarter of it for you and for the rest of the people three quarters of it? He said: They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: Then how will you be when you are a third of it? He said: They said, 'That is the good.' He said: Then how will you be when you are half? They said, 'That is the good.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: The people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection will be one hundred and twenty rows, of which you will be eighty rows."],[5364,"On the Day of Badr, every three of us shared one camel. Abu Lubabah and Ali b. Abi Talib were the two riding companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Whenever the turn of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to walk came, they said, 'We will walk instead of you.' He said, 'You two are not stronger than me, and I am not less in need of the reward than you two.'"],[5365,"Regarding this verse: 'And he certainly saw him in another descent,' he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I saw Jibril at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, upon him six hundred wings, from whose feathers were scattered wonders: pearls and rubies.'"],[5366,"Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, marvels at two men: a man who rises from his blanket and his bed, from among his tribe and his family, to his prayer. Allah says to His angels, 'O My angels, look at this servant of Mine. He rose from between his bed and his blanket, from among his tribe and his family, to his prayer, out of desire for what is with Me and out of fear of what is with Me.' And a man who fought in the way of Allah and his companions fled, and he knew what was upon him for fleeing and what was for him in returning, so he returned until his blood was shed. Allah says to His angels, 'Look at this servant of Mine. He returned out of desire for what is with Me and out of fear of what is with Me.'"],[5367,"Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath and Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ata b. al-Sa'ib, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it or something similar."],[5368,"Abdullah used to say: Indeed, lying is not proper in seriousness or jest, nor should a man promise another something and then not fulfill it for him."],[5369,"The two eyes commit zina, the two hands commit zina, the two feet commit zina, and the private part commits zina."],[5370,"He used to gather a siwak for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from an arak tree, and the wind would bend him, and there was slenderness in his legs, so the people laughed. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What makes you laugh?' They said: 'The slenderness of his legs.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier on the scale than Mount Uhud.'"],[5371,"I lent Alqama two thousand dirhams, and when his stipend came out, I said to him: 'Pay me back.' He said: 'Delay me until next year.' He said: I refused him, so I took it from him. He said: I came to him after that, and he said: 'You distressed me, and you withheld from me.' I said: 'Yes, it is your doing.' He said: 'What is my affair?' I said: 'You narrated to me from Ibn Mas'ud that the Prophet ﷺ said: A loan runs the course of half of charity.'"],[5372,"We performed Hajj with Ibn Mas'ud until when the first dawn rose, he stood and prayed the morning prayer. He said: I said to him: 'You never used to pray this prayer at this hour,' and he used to delay the prayer until it was bright. He said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on this day, in this place, at this hour,' meaning at Muzdalifa."],[5373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray, and when he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn would jump on his back, and when they wanted to prevent them, he gestured to them: 'Leave them.' When he finished the prayer, he placed them in his lap and said: 'Whoever loves me, let him love these two.'"],[5374,"The believer is not a curser, nor a defamer, nor obscene, nor indecent."],[5375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sleep during his prostration, and his sleep was not known except by his snoring; then he would stand up in his prayer."],[5376,"I came to Abdullah b. Mas'ud while he was on a rooftop, and I sat with him while he was saying: 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us that the Night of Qadr is in the middle of the last seven nights, and that the sun rises on its morning without rays.' So I climbed up and saw it like that, and I said: 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.'"],[5377,"Abdullah heard of an eclipse, and he said: 'We, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, used to count signs as blessings, while you count them as warnings. While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had no water, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek someone who has water.\" We did so, and water was brought. He poured it into a vessel, then placed his palm in it, and water began to flow from between his fingers. Then he said: \"Come to the blessed purification, and blessing is from Allah.\" I filled my belly from it, and he asked for water and people were given to drink.' Abdullah said: 'We used to hear the glorification of food while it was being eaten.'"],[5378,"Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, with this chain something similar, except that he did not mention Alqama."],[5379,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cave, and 'By those sent forth in succession' was revealed to him, and we began receiving it from him. Then a snake came out from the side of the cave, and he said: 'Kill it.' We rushed toward it, but it preceded us. He said: 'It has been protected from your evil just as you have been protected from its evil.'"],[5380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Recite Surah al-Nisa' to me.\" He said: I said, \"Should I recite it to you when it was revealed to you?\" He said: \"I love to hear it from someone other than myself.\" He said: So I recited to him until when I reached: \"So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?\" his eyes overflowed."],[5381,"Beware of these testimonies, that a man says: \"So-and-so was killed as a martyr,\" for a man fights out of zeal, and a man fights while he is brave-hearted, and he does not know for what he is fighting; and a man fights for worldly gain. And I shall tell you about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a group of people as a raiding party. They did not remain except a little while until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: \"Your brothers met the enemy and they cut them off, and not a single man of them escaped. They met their Lord and said: 'Our Lord, convey to our people that we are pleased and He is pleased with us.' And I am their messenger to you: that they are pleased and He is pleased with them.\" So bear witness to the like of these."],[5382,"I was with Abdullah at Mina. When Uthman prayed four rak'ahs there, Abdullah said when he finished his prayer: \"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this place two rak'ahs, and Abu Bakr prayed two rak'ahs, and Umar prayed two rak'ahs.\" He said: I think he mentioned that Uthman had prayed two rak'ahs, then he said: \"Today he prayed four.\" Al-Aswad said: I said to him: \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why did you not say the salam after the first two rak'ahs and pray the other two rak'ahs afterwards as voluntary prayer?\" He said: \"Disagreement is evil.\""],[5383,"No night talk except for one of two men: one who prays, or a traveler."],[5384,"The believer is not a defamer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed."],[5385,"He used to seek refuge from Satan the stoned: from his spurring, his blowing, and his puffing. He said: His spurring is madness, his blowing is sorcery, and his puffing is pride."],[5386,"A black wind blew in Kufa, and a man came whose only refrain was: \"O Abdullah b. Mas'ud, the Hour has come!\" He was reclining, and he sat up and said: \"The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and no booty is rejoiced over.\" And he said: \"An enemy will gather against the people of Islam, and the people of Islam will gather against them.\" And he gestured with his hand towards Syria. I said: \"Do you mean the Romans?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"And at that fighting there will be a severe apostasy. A detachment will be pledged for death that will not return except victorious. They will fight until night separates them, and these and those will withdraw, neither being victorious, and the detachment will perish. Then the Muslims will pledge a detachment for death that will not return except victorious. They will fight until evening, and night separates them, and these and those will withdraw, neither being victorious, and the detachment will perish. Then the Muslims will pledge a detachment for death that will not return except victorious. They will fight until evening, and these and those will withdraw, neither being victorious, and the detachment will perish. Then on the fourth day the rest of the people of Islam will advance against them, and Allah will put defeat upon them, and they will be slain with a slaughter—either he said: the like of which will not be seen, or he said: the like of which has not been seen—until a bird passes by their sides, it will not pass them without falling dead. Then the sons of one father will count themselves; they were a hundred and they will not find that any of them remains except one man. So what booty is rejoiced over, or what inheritance is divided? While they are thus, they hear of people more numerous than that: the cry comes to them that the Dajjal has taken their place among their offspring. So they leave what is in their hands and turn back, and they send ten horsemen as a scouting party. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I indeed know their names, their fathers' names, and the colors of their horses. They are the best horsemen on the face of the earth on that day'—or he said: 'They are the best horsemen on the face of the earth on that day.'\""],[5387,"We used to go on raids with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had no women. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should we not castrate ourselves?' He forbade us from that and commanded us to marry a woman for a garment. Then Abdullah recited: 'O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you.'"],[5388,"While a man was in his kingdom, he reflected and knew that what he was in would come to an end, and that it had distracted him from worshiping his Lord. So he slipped away from his palace at night until he came to another's kingdom. He came to the seashore and began making bricks, living by that and worshiping his Lord. The king in whose kingdom he was learned of his worship and his condition, so he sent for him, but he refused to come to him. When he saw that, he rode to him. When the worshiper saw him, he fled from him, and he followed him on his mount. He said: 'O servant of Allah, you have nothing to fear from me.' Then he dismounted to him and asked him about his affair. He said: 'I am so-and-so, owner of such-and-such a kingdom. I reflected and knew that what I was in would come to an end, and that it had distracted me from worshiping my Lord.' He said: 'You are no more deserving of what you did than I am.' Then he let his mount go and followed him. They worshiped Allah together, and they asked Allah to cause them to die together, and they died together and were buried. Abdullah said: 'If I were at the sand dunes of Egypt, I would show you their graves by the description that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ described to us.'"],[5389,"About the saying of Allah: 'And whoever intends therein a deviation with wrongdoing, We will make him taste a painful punishment,' he said: 'If a man intended therein a deviation while he was in Aden Abyan, Allah the Exalted would make him taste a painful punishment.'"],[5390,"Whoever says on the night of Arafah these ten phrases a thousand times, he will not ask Allah for anything except that He gives it to him, except severing ties of kinship or a sin: 'Glory be to the One whose Throne is in the heaven; Glory be to the One whose footstool is on the earth; Glory be to the One whose path is in the sea; Glory be to the One whose authority is in the Fire; Glory be to the One whose mercy is in Paradise; Glory be to the One whose decree is in the graves; Glory be to the One whose spirit is in the air; Glory be to the One who raised the heaven; Glory be to the One who placed the earth; Glory be to the One from whom there is no escape except to Him.'"],[5391,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to us while we were at Mina, and he leaned his back against a red tent, then he began to speak to us, saying: 'No soul will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul,' three times. Then he said: 'Are you not pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Are you not pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. I will inform you about that. The parable of the believers among others is like a white hair on a black ox, or a black hair on a white ox.'"],[5392,"A Jewish rabbi came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'On the Day of Resurrection, God will place the heavens on one finger, the earths on one finger, the mountains and trees on one finger, the water and the moist earth on one finger, and all creatures on one finger; then He will shake them and say, \"I am the King, I am the King.\"' I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ laugh until his molars showed, in amazement at what he said and in confirmation of it. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited, 'They have not appraised God with true appraisal' up to 'from what they associate'."],[5393,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to his companions, 'Let none of my companions convey anything to me about anyone, for I love to come out to you with a sound heart.'"],[5394,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, I met a woman in the garden and embraced her, touched her, kissed her, and did everything with her except that I did not have intercourse with her.' The Prophet ﷺ remained silent about it. Then this verse was revealed: 'Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.' The Prophet ﷺ called him and recited it to him. Umar said to him, 'O Messenger of God, is this for him specifically or for all people?' He said, 'No, rather for all people.'"],[5395,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in a cultivated field in Madinah, and he was leaning on a palm branch. He came upon a group of Jews. Some of them said, 'Do not ask him,' but they asked him. He leaned on the palm branch as if receiving revelation, and said, 'They ask you about the spirit. Say, \"The spirit is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.\"'"],[5396,"When the verse 'There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds' was revealed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'It was said to me, \"You are among them.\"'"],[5397,"Suwayd b. Sa'id and Abd al-Ghaffar narrated something similar."],[5398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the Night of Decree. He said, 'Which of you remembers the night of the two reddish hills?' Abdullah said, 'I do, by my father and mother, O Messenger of God. In my hand were some small dates with which I was having my pre-dawn meal, shielding myself from the dawn, until the dawn rose. That was the night of the twenty-seventh, if God wills.'"],[5399,"The sun eclipsed during the time of Uthman b. Affan, and Abdullah b. Mas'ud was in Madinah. Uthman went out and led the people in that prayer: two rak'ahs and two prostrations in one rak'ah. Then Uthman left and entered his house. Abdullah b. Mas'ud sat by A'isha's room, and we sat with him. He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us to pray at the eclipse of the sun or the moon. So if you see that it has been eclipsed, hasten to prayer, for if it is what you fear, it will have come while you are not heedless, and you will have attained or acquired good.'"],[5400,"Nabidh is a means of purification if we find nothing else."],[5401,"A man came to him and said, 'Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything about horses?' He said, 'Yes, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. Buy on God's account and borrow on God's account.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of God, how do we buy on God's account and borrow on God's account?\" He said, \"Say, 'Lend us until our shares come, and sell to us until God opens for us.' You will remain in good as long as your jihad is fresh. At the end of time there will be people who doubt jihad, so wage jihad in their time, and then go on raids, for raiding then is fresher.\"'"],[5402,"The people used to recite aloud behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God said to them, 'You have confused the Qur'an for me.'"],[5403,"And we used to greet during the prayer, but it was said to us, 'In the prayer there is indeed occupation.'"],[5404,"Whoever is afflicted by poverty and takes it to the people, his poverty will not be relieved. And whoever takes it to God, He will soon grant him sufficiency, either soon or later, later."],[5405,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on one of his journeys, we heard a crier calling: 'God is greatest, God is greatest.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Upon the natural disposition.' He said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but God, I bear witness that there is no god but God.' The Prophet said: 'He has come out of the Fire.' We hurried to him, and he was a livestock keeper whom the prayer overtook, so he called it."],[5406,"People pardon one another regarding fixed punishments as long as they are not brought to the rulers. But when they are brought to the ruler, he judges among them according to the Book of God."],[5407,"A people will come forth in the last days, young in age, foolish in minds, speaking from the best of speech, reciting the Qur'an, it does not pass beyond their throats. They leave Islam as an arrow passes through the game. So whoever meets them should fight them, for killing them carries reward from God for the one who kills them."],[5408,"The Qur'an was revealed in seven modes, each mode has an outward and an inward meaning."],[5409,"We asked our Prophet ﷺ about walking with a funeral procession. He said: 'Less than a trot. If it is good, it is hastened to it; and if it is other than that, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral procession is followed and does not follow; the one who walks ahead of it is not part of it.'"],[5410,"Ibn Mas'ud sold al-Ash'ath some slaves from the slaves of the emirate. He came to him seeking payment, and they differed over the price. Ibn Mas'ud said: 'Do you accept that I judge between me and you with the judgment of the Messenger of God ﷺ? When the two parties to a sale differ, the word is what the seller says, or they return the goods.'"],[5411,"O God, bless my community in its early morning."],[5412,"When it was revealed: 'When the help of God and victory comes' to the end of the surah, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say frequently: 'Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise. O God, forgive me. Indeed, You are the Ever-Relenting.'"],[5413,"Whoever comes to a soothsayer, or a magician, or a diviner, and asks him and believes what he says, has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad."],[5414,"My community has been blessed in its early morning."],[5415,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit, we would face him with our faces."],[5416,"The Prophet ﷺ slept until he snored, then he got up and prayed."],[5417,"Do not reject a gift, answer the invitation, and do not strike the Muslims."],[5418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine between the two prayers while traveling."],[5419,"The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account is prayer, and the first thing to be judged among people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed."],[5420,"He forbade selling fruit until its ripeness was apparent, and he forbade selling fruit for dried dates."],[5421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession for 'araya."],[5422,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur'an and he recites it throughout the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it throughout the hours of the night and the hours of the day."],[5423,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats will be deducted from his reward each day."],[5424,"A man saw that the Night of Decree was the twenty-seventh night, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'I see that your visions agree in the last ten nights, so seek it in the odd nights among them.'"],[5425,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he started the prayer raise his hands level with his shoulders, and when he bowed, and when he rose, and he did not raise them between the two prostrations."],[5426,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[5427,"When he was in a hurry while traveling, he would combine Maghrib and 'Isha'."],[5428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhul-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd at Qarn—this was mentioned to Ibn Umar, and he did not hear it—and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam."],[5429,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man admonishing his brother regarding modesty, so he said, “Modesty is part of faith.”"],[5430,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “What clothing should the pilgrim in ihram wear?” He said, “He should not wear a shirt, a turban, a hooded cloak, trousers, or any garment touched by saffron or wars, nor leather socks, except for one who cannot find sandals. If he cannot find sandals, let him cut them off below the ankles.”"],[5431,"If the wife of any of you asks permission to go to the mosque, let him not prevent her."],[5432,"Whoever sells a slave who has property, the property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it. Whoever sells palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it."],[5433,"Five creatures there is no sin upon one who kills them in the Haram or while in ihram: the mouse, the crow, the kite, the scorpion, and the rabid dog."],[5434,"Kill snakes, the one with two stripes, and the short-tailed one, for they blind the sight and cause miscarriages. He said: Abdullah used to kill every snake he found."],[5435,"Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: By Allah, I never swore by them after that, intentionally or unintentionally."],[5436,"The night prayer is two rak‘ahs at a time. If you fear the dawn, then perform witr with one rak‘ah."],[5437,"Bilal gives the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the adhan."],[5438,"Ill omen is in three things: the horse, the woman, and the house."],[5439,"Do not leave fire burning in your houses when you sleep."],[5440,"He used to pray two rak'ahs after the Friday prayer."],[5441,"You will find people like a hundred camels, among which there is no riding camel."],[5442,"Ghaylan b. Salama al-Thaqafi embraced Islam while he had ten wives under him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: choose four of them. Then in the era of Umar he divorced his wives and divided his wealth among his sons. That reached Umar, so he met him and said: I think Satan, in what he overhears from the hearing, heard of your death and cast it into your heart. Perhaps you will remain only a little while. By Allah, you will take back your wives and you will take back your wealth, or I will make them inherit, and I will order that your grave be stoned as the grave of Abu Righal was stoned."],[5443,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs."],[5444,"The Prophet ﷺ combined them at Muzdalifa, and he prayed each one of them with an iqama, and he did not pray voluntary prayers before either of them or after."],[5445,"He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Order him to take her back, then let him divorce her when she is pure or pregnant."],[5446,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for hunting or livestock, two qirats are deducted from his deeds every day. He said: And Salim said: Abu Hurayra said: or a dog for farming. He said: And he was a farmer."],[5447,"The oath of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: No, by the Turner of hearts."],[5448,"If your women ask your permission to go to the mosques, permit them."],[5449,"Indeed, whoever lies about me, a house will be built for him in the Fire."],[5450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to be brief, and he would lead us in the morning prayer with al-Saffat."],[5451,"I was with Salim b. Abdullah on a journey, and a caravan belonging to Umm al-Banin passed by containing bells. Salim narrated from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell. So how many bells are in this one?"],[5452,"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been bereft of his family and his property."],[5453,"When you sight the crescent, then fast, and when you sight it, then break your fast. If it is obscured from you, then estimate for it."],[5454,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then faced the rising of the sun and said: 'Verily, trials come from here,' three times, 'and from there rises the horn of Satan.'"],[5455,"He was among a group of his companions, and the Messenger of God ﷺ came to them and said: 'Do you not know that I am the Messenger of God to you?' They said: 'Yes, we bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.' He said: 'Do you not know that whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and that obedience to me is part of obedience to God?' They said: 'Yes, we bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed God, and that obedience to you is part of obedience to God.' He said: 'Indeed, it is part of obedience to God that you obey me, and part of obedience to me that you obey your leaders. Obey your leaders, and if they pray sitting, then pray sitting.'"],[5456,"A man from the people of Syria sat with Abdullah b. Umar while I was with him, and said to him: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what do you think of performing tamattu with an umrah to the hajj?' Abdullah said to him: 'It is good and beautiful for whoever does that.' The man said to him: 'But your father used to forbid it.' Abdullah became angry, then said: 'Woe to you! Consider: if my father forbade it, and the Messenger of God ﷺ practiced it, would you follow the command of the Messenger of God or the command of my father?' He said: 'No, rather the command of the Messenger of God.' He said: 'Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ did that, so go about your business.'"],[5457,"When you sight the crescent, then fast, and when you sight it, then break your fast. If it is obscured from you, then estimate."],[5458,"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been bereft of his family and his property."],[5459,"Verily, your remaining among the nations that came before you is only like the time between the Asr prayer and the setting of the sun: the people of the Torah were given the Torah and they acted upon it until midday, then they were unable, so they were given a qirat. Then the people of the Gospel were given the Gospel and they acted until the Asr prayer, then they were unable, so they were given a qirat. Then we were given the Quran, and we acted until sunset, so we were given two qirats, two qirats. The people of the two scriptures said: 'O our Lord, why have You given these two qirats, two qirats, and given us a qirat, a qirat, while we did more work than them?' God said: 'Have I wronged you in anything of your reward?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Then that is My bounty, which I give to whom I will.'"],[5460,"Do not sell fruit for dates, and do not sell fruit until its ripeness appears."],[5461,"The keys of the unseen are five: Indeed, God has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, God is Knowing, Aware."],[5462,"People are like a hundred camels: you can hardly find a single riding camel among them."],[5463,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not say that Jesus was red, but the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'While I was sleeping, I saw myself circumambulating the Kaaba, and there was a brown man with lank hair, between two men, with water dripping from his head - or his head was pouring water. I said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"This is the son of Mary.\" Then I turned to look, and there was a red, bulky man with curly hair, blind in the right eye, his eye like a floating grape. I said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"The Dajjal. The person most resembling him is a man from Khuza'ah called Ibn Qatan.\"'"],[5464,"He used to perform Witr on his riding camel."],[5465,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was approached while he was at al-Muʿarras of Dhu al-Hulayfah in the belly of the valley, and it was said to him, “You are in a blessed stony watercourse.”"],[5466,"When Ibn ʿUmar passed by Dhu al-Hulayfah, he would spend the night there until morning, and he reported that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do that."],[5467,"He used to narrate from the Messenger of God ﷺ that when he appointed Usama b. Zayd as commander, he learned that the people criticized Usama and disparaged his command. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up just as..."],[5468,"“O Messenger of God, tell us about what we do: is it in a matter already decreed or in a matter newly begun or innovated?” He said, “In what has already been decreed—Shuʿba was uncertain—so act, O Ibn al-Khattab, for everyone is facilitated. As for one who is among the people of felicity, he will act for felicity, and one who is among the people of wretchedness, he will act for wretchedness.”"],[5469,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman used to walk in front of the funeral procession."],[5470,"He forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys."],[5471,"Every intoxicant is unlawful."],[5472,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful; a little of it and a lot of it are alike."],[5473,"Whoever sells a slave, his property belongs to the one who sold him unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. Whoever sells a palm that has been pollinated, its fruit belongs to the one who sold it unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."],[5474,"While I was sleeping, I saw myself circumambulating the Kaʿbah, and there was a man with lank hair between two men, water dripping—or being poured—from his head. I said, “Who is this?” They said, “The son of Maryam.” I turned to look, and there was a ruddy, heavyset man with curly hair and one eye blind, his eye like a floating grape. I said, “Who is this?” They said, “The Dajjal. The person most resembling him among people is Ibn Qatan.”"],[5475,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote the document of zakat and attached it to his sword. He did not send it out to his governors until he passed away. Abu Bakr acted upon it until he passed away, then ʿUmar acted upon it. It contained: for five camels, one ewe; for ten, two ewes; for fifteen, three ewes; for twenty, four ewes; for twenty-five, a bint makhad up to thirty-five. If they increase, then a bint labun up to forty-five. If they increase, then a hiqqah up to sixty. If they increase, then a jadhaʿah up to seventy-five. If they increase, then two bint labuns up to ninety. If they increase, then two hiqqahs up to one hundred twenty. If they increase beyond one hundred twenty, then for every fifty, a hiqqah, and for every forty, a bint labun. And regarding zakat on sheep: for every forty sheep, one ewe up to one hundred twenty. If they increase, then two ewes up to two hundred. If they increase, then three ewes up to three hundred. If they increase, then for every hundred sheep, one ewe. There is nothing on them until they reach one hundred. Neither is a combined herd separated nor a separated herd combined out of fear of zakat. If two partners mix their herds, they settle between themselves equally. Neither an old decrepit animal nor one with a defect is taken in zakat."],[5476,"Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Abbad b. al-Awwam narrated to us with his chain something similar."],[5477,"The oath of the Prophet ﷺ upon which he used to swear was: No, by the Turner of hearts."],[5478,"I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch anything except the two Yemeni corners."],[5479,"Ibn Umar, when he passed by Dhu al-Hulayfah, would spend the night there until morning, and he would report that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[5480,"The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn. He said: It was mentioned to me, but I did not hear it. He said: And the people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam."],[5481,"He forbade selling fresh dates for dry dates."],[5482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession for araya."],[5483,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom Allah has given the Quran and he stands with it through the hours of the night and the day."],[5484,"Whoever buys palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."],[5485,"He said on the pulpit: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[5486,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raise his hands when he began the prayer, raising his hands to his shoulders, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and he did not raise them between the two prostrations."],[5487,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[5488,"The Prophet ﷺ heard Umar while he was swearing by his father, so he said: \"Indeed, Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers.\" Umar said: \"By Allah, I never swore by it after that, neither intentionally nor inadvertently.\""],[5489,"I see that your dreams have concurred regarding the last ten nights, so seek it in the remaining seven, or in the odd ones among them."],[5490,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combining Maghrib and Isha when travel urged him on."],[5491,"Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."],[5492,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He heard a man admonishing his brother about modesty, and he said to him: \"Modesty is part of faith.\""],[5493,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"What clothing should the pilgrim in ihram wear?\" He said: \"Do not wear shirts, trousers, turbans, hooded cloaks, or any garment touched by wars or saffron, and do not wear leather socks, except for a man who has no sandals; then let him cut them so that they are below the ankles.\""],[5494,"He forbade selling fruit until its ripeness becomes apparent."],[5495,"Bad omen is in three things: the house, the riding beast, and the woman."],[5496,"If one of your wives asks permission to go to the mosque, do not prevent her."],[5497,"Indeed, Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until you hear the call of Ibn Umm Maktum."],[5498,"Kill snakes, especially the one with two white stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause blindness and cause miscarriage. Ibn Umar used to kill every snake he found. Abu Lubabah b. Abd al-Mundhir, or Zayd b. al-Khattab, saw him pursuing a snake and said: \"He has indeed forbidden killing the snakes that live in houses.\""],[5499,"The night prayer is two units at a time, and if you fear the approach of dawn, then perform one unit as witr, which will make odd what you have prayed."],[5500,"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."],[5501,"Verily, the one who misses the prayer — the Asr prayer — it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."],[5502,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: What animals may a pilgrim in ihram kill? He said: Five animals, there is no blame on the one who kills them in the Haram and outside it: the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, the kite, and the rabid dog."],[5503,"Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause blindness and cause miscarriage. Abdullah b. Umar said: While I was chasing a snake, Abu Lubabah saw me and said... I said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded killing it. Abu Lubabah said: He forbade it after that."],[5504,"When he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands and said: Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, and to You is all praise."],[5505,"They both spoke to Abdullah during the nights when the army encamped against Ibn al-Zubayr before he was killed, and said: It will not harm you not to perform Hajj this year. We fear that you may be prevented from reaching the House. He said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the disbelievers of Quraysh prevented us from reaching the House. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed his hady and shaved his head. I call you to witness that I have made Umrah obligatory upon myself. If Allah wills, I will set out. If I am allowed to reach the House, I will perform tawaf. If I am prevented from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did while I was with him. He entered into ihram for Umrah at Dhul-Hulayfah. Then he traveled for a while and said: Their matter is one. I call you to witness that I have made Hajj obligatory upon myself along with my Umrah. He did not exit ihram from either of them until he exited on the Day of Sacrifice. He used to say: Whoever combines Hajj and Umrah and enters into ihram for both of them, he does not exit ihram until he exits from both of them together on the Day of Sacrifice, performing a single tawaf for both of them around the House, and between al-Safa and al-Marwah on the day he enters Makkah."],[5506,"Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking permission for Umrah. He said: O my brother, supplicate, and do not forget us in your righteous supplication."],[5507,"When the shadow is a cubit and a half to two cubits, then pray the Zuhr prayer."],[5508,"The Prophet ﷺ consulted the Muslims about what should gather them for the prayer. They said: the horn, but he disliked it because of the Jews. Then the bell was mentioned, but he disliked it because of the Christians. That night the call was shown to a man from the Ansar called Abdullah b. Zayd, and Umar b. al-Khattab. The Ansari came to him at night, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal, and he gave the call with it. 90 - (5504) - Al-Zuhri said: Bilal added in the call for the Fajr prayer 'prayer is better than sleep', and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ approved it. Umar said: Indeed I saw the like of what he saw, but he preceded me."],[5510,"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."],[5511,"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."],[5512,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard thunder and thunderbolts, he said: O Allah, do not kill us with Your anger, and do not destroy us with Your punishment, and grant us well-being before that."],[5513,"Whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it. And whoever sells palm trees that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it."],[5514,"Do not raise your eyes to the sky lest they be snatched away."],[5515,"When your women ask your permission to go to the mosques, grant them permission."],[5516,"Indeed, the trial will come from here—and he pointed with his hand toward the east, where the horn of Satan rises—while you strike one another's necks. Indeed, Moses killed the one he killed from the people of Pharaoh by mistake. Allah said to him: 'And you killed a soul, but We saved you from grief and tried you with a trial.'"],[5517,"It is not fitting for anyone to spend three nights except with his will at hand. He said: I did not spend a night except with my will placed with me."],[5518,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Hajj or Umrah, whenever he ascended a hill or a mountain pass, he would say the takbir three times, then say: 'There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things capable. Returning, repenting, to our Lord praising. Allah has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone.'"],[5519,"I saw in a dream that I was drawing water with a bucket from a well. Abu Bakr came and drew one or two buckets, drawing weakly, and Allah forgive him. Then Umar came and drew, and it turned into a large bucket, and I have never seen a mighty man among people perform as he did, until the people were quenched and they settled at the watering place."],[5520,"Usama went out wearing a full garment, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Tear it into veils for your family.'"],[5521,"For the inside of the son of Adam to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry."],[5522,"Whoever buys palm trees after they have been pollinated and does not stipulate their fruit, he has nothing. And whoever buys a slave and does not stipulate his property, he has nothing."],[5523,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Usama b. Zayd, the people spoke about him. The Prophet ﷺ heard of that—or something of it—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What you said about Usama has reached me. You said the same about his father before him. Indeed, he is worthy of command, indeed he is worthy of command, indeed he is worthy of command, and indeed he is the most beloved of people to me.' He did not make an exception for Fatima or anyone else."],[5524,"He used to walk in front of the funeral procession, and indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to walk in front of it."],[5525,"The oath of the Prophet ﷺ was: Nay, by the Turner of hearts."],[5526,"The oath of the Prophet ﷺ by which he used to swear was: Nay, by the Turner of hearts."],[5527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Did you write this letter?\" He said: \"Yes. By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, it was not that I lacked faith in my heart, but there was no one among Quraysh who did not have family and servants to protect his family, so I wrote a letter hoping that Allah would protect my family by it.\" Umar said: \"Give me permission regarding him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Would you have killed him?\" He said: \"Yes, if you permit me regarding him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And what would make you know? Perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: 'Do whatever you wish.'\""],[5528,"You will fight the Jews until the stone says: 'O Muslim, this is a Jew behind me; come and kill him.'"],[5529,"I saw people gathered for the reckoning, and Abu Bakr stood and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and may Allah forgive him. Then Umar stood and it turned into a large bucket, and I have never seen a chief among the people who could perform his feat, until the people watered their camels."],[5530,"I saw a black woman with disheveled hair come out of Madinah until she reached Mahya'ah—that is, al-Juhfah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ interpreted the dream: the fever of Madinah moving to al-Juhfah."],[5531,"He forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys."],[5532,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in his supplication: 'A protection like the protection of a newborn.'"],[5533,"The sale of fruit is not valid until its ripeness is apparent."],[5534,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on the pulpit: 'Whoever of you comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform the ritual bath.'"],[5535,"When he was in a hurry on a journey, he used to combine Maghrib and Isha."],[5536,"Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."],[5537,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[5538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: What clothing should the pilgrim in ihram wear? He said: He should not wear the shirt, the turban, the hooded cloak, the trousers, or any garment touched by saffron or wars, nor leather socks, except for one who cannot find sandals. Whoever cannot find sandals should cut them so that they are below the ankles."],[5539,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he began the prayer he raised his hands level with his shoulders, and when he intended to bow, and after bowing, but he did not raise them between the two prostrations."],[5540,"Ill omen is in three things: the horse, the woman, and the house."],[5541,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man admonishing his brother about modesty, and he said: Modesty is part of faith."],[5542,"The Prophet ﷺ heard Umar saying: By my father, by my father. He said: Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: By Allah, I never swore by them after that, neither intentionally nor quoting."],[5543,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."],[5544,"If one of you's wife asks permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her."],[5545,"Kill snakes, and the one with two white stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause blindness and cause miscarriage. Ibn Umar used to kill every snake he found, and Abu Lubabah or Zayd b. al-Khattab saw him pursuing a snake and said: He forbade the house snakes."],[5546,"Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until you hear Ibn Umm Maktum."],[5547,"A man saw in a dream that it was such-and-such night of the ten - meaning Laylat al-Qadr. The Prophet ﷺ said to them: I see that your visions have agreed that it is in the last ten nights, so seek it in the last ten nights, in the odd nights among them."],[5548,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given the Quran and he recites it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day."],[5549,"Five are the creatures in which there is no fault for the one who kills them in the state of consecration and within the Sanctuary: the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, the biting dog. Sufyan said: and the lion, the wolf, and the biting hornet."],[5550,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a white shirt on Umar and said: \"Is your shirt new or washed?\" He said: I think he said: \"Washed.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Wear new, live praiseworthy, and die a martyr.\""],[5551,"It is not right for a person that three nights pass over him while his will is with him."],[5552,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed in the dawn prayer so-and-so and so-and-so, people from the hypocrites. Then God Most High sent down: \"You have no part in the matter, whether He relents toward them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers.\""],[5553,"The oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: \"No, by the Turner of hearts.\""],[5554,"People are like a hundred camels, among which there is no riding camel."],[5555,"Umar asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to perform the minor pilgrimage, and he permitted him. He said: \"O my brother, include us in your righteous supplication and do not forget us.\""],[5556,"A fire will come out from the sea of Hadramawt—or from Hadramawt—driving the people. We said: \"O Messenger of God, what do you command us?\" He said: \"You must go to Syria.\""],[5557,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog of livestock or a dog of hunting, a carat is deducted from his deeds every day. Abdullah said: Abu Hurayrah said: \"or a dog of cultivation.\""],[5558,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would indeed command us to be brief, and he would lead us in the dawn prayer with [Surah] al-Saffat."],[5559,"The gate of my community through which they will enter Paradise—its width is the distance traveled by a swift, swift rider, three times; they will indeed be pressed upon it until their shoulders almost dislocate."],[5560,"He would glorify God while on the back of the riding beast, wherever his face was turned."],[5561,"Three will not enter Paradise, and three Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who is undutiful to his parents, the cuckold, and the woman who imitates men. And three Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: so he repeated the one undutiful to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of what he has given."],[5562,"I traveled with the Prophet ﷺ and with Umar, and they would not exceed two rak'ahs. We had been astray and Allah guided us, so we follow him."],[5563,"Both of Allah's hands are right hands. He folds the heavens and takes them with His hand, then says: 'I am the King. Where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?' He said: Then He takes the earths with His other hand and says: 'I am the King. Where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?'"],[5564,"If anyone's wife asks permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her."],[5565,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward each day. Abu Hurayrah said: 'Or a farm dog.' He said: And Abu Hurayrah used to farm."],[5566,"Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to take her back."],[5567,"A believer is not a curser."],[5568,"He heard a man from the people of Syria asking Abdullah b. Umar about performing umrah and then hajj as a mutamatti'. Abdullah said: 'It is permissible.' The Syrian said: 'But your father forbade it.' Abdullah said: 'Tell me, if my father forbade it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it, do you follow my father's command or the Messenger of Allah's command?' The Syrian said: 'Rather the Messenger of Allah's command.' So he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it.'"],[5569,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he entered prayer, raise his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing; and he did not do that in prostration."],[5570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah at the start of his journey, and he prayed in its mosque."],[5571,"Your remaining time compared to the nations that have passed is like the time between the afternoon prayer and sunset. The people of the Torah were given the Torah and they worked until midday, then they became unable, so they were given a qirat, a qirat. The Christians were given the Gospel and they worked until the afternoon prayer, then they became unable, so they were given a qirat, a qirat. Then we were given the Quran and we worked from the afternoon prayer until sunset, so we were given two qirats, two qirats. The Jews and Christians said: 'Our Lord, we worked more than them, yet You gave us a qirat, a qirat.' Then the Blessed and Exalted said: 'Have I wronged you in anything of your rewards?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Then it is My bounty which I give to whomever I will.'"],[5572,"Whoever eats any of this meat should wash his hand from its odor and harm, so that he does not annoy the one beside him."],[5573,"Do not eat with your left hands, and do not drink with them, for Satan eats with them and drinks with them."],[5574,"He used to glorify Allah while riding on the mount, whichever direction it faced."],[5575,"O people of Iraq, how little you ask about the minor matters while leaving the major ones! I heard my father Abdullah b. Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The trial will come from here,' and he gestured with his hand toward the east, 'and you will be striking the necks of one another. Moses ﷺ only killed the one he killed from the people of Pharaoh by mistake. Allah said: \"And you killed a soul, but We saved you from distress and tried you with a trial.\"'"],[5576,"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about what we do: is it a matter already decreed and finished, or a matter newly initiated—or newly begun? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Rather, it is a matter already decreed and finished.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, then should we not rely on that?' He said: 'Act, for everyone is facilitated. Whoever is among the people of happiness will act for happiness, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will act for wretchedness.'"],[5577,"Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5578,"That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."],[5579,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: \"And with Him is the knowledge of the Book.\""],[5580,"Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves unless you are weeping, lest the like of what befell them befall you."],[5581,"There is no contagion and no evil omen."],[5582,"When he threw the first pebble at the Jamrah that is next to the mosque—the mosque of Mina—he threw seven pebbles, saying Allahu Akbar with each pebble. Then he went forward in front of it and stood facing the qiblah, raising his hands and supplicating, and he would prolong the standing. Then he came to the second Jamrah and threw seven pebbles, saying Allahu Akbar with each pebble. Then he descended to the left, toward the valley, and stood facing the qiblah, raising his hands and supplicating. Then he came to the Jamrah at the Aqabah and threw seven pebbles, saying Allahu Akbar with each pebble. Then he departed and did not stand at it. Al-Zuhri said: I heard Salim narrate this from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, and Ibn Umar used to do it."],[5583,"When your women ask your permission to go to the mosque, permit them."],[5584,"He used to give extra shares of spoils to some of those he sent out in raiding parties for themselves, apart from the general division of the army, and the fifth is obligatory in all of that."],[5585,"No servant forms an image but that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: 'Bring to life what you have created.'"],[5586,"Begging will cling to a man until he meets Allah with no flesh on his face."],[5587,"When a punishment descends upon a people, the punishment afflicts those who were among them, then they will be resurrected according to their deeds."],[5588,"Allah has cursed wine, and cursed its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the consumer of its price."],[5589,"When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[5590,"When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise and the people of the Fire have entered the Fire, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and the Fire, then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will call out: 'O people of Paradise, there is no death; O people of the Fire, there is no death.' So the people of Paradise will increase in joy upon their joy, and the people of the Fire will increase in sorrow upon their sorrow."],[5591,"We were talking during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, and we did not know what the Farewell Pilgrimage was. He praised Allah—His Messenger—alone, and extolled Him, then he mentioned the false messiah and spoke at length about him. Then he said: 'Allah has not sent any prophet except that he warned his nation about him. Noah warned his nation, and the prophets after him. He will emerge among you, and whatever of his condition is unclear to you is not unclear to you. He is blind in the right eye, as if it were a floating grape.' Then he said: 'Indeed, Allah has made your blood and your wealth sacred, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I not conveyed?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'O Allah, bear witness.' Then he said: 'Woe to you—or may you be shown mercy—beware, do not return after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.'"],[5592,"An oath is only either a violation or regret."],[5593,"He used to pray on his mount, wherever it turned with him."],[5594,"This affair will remain among Quraysh as long as two people remain among mankind."],[5595,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being asked about water in a desert land and what comes to it from beasts and predators. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'When the water is the amount of two qullahs, it does not carry impurity.'"],[5596,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed wine, and its drinker, its pourer, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, and the consumer of its price."],[5597,"Do not revert to being disbelievers after me, striking one another's necks."],[5598,"How will you be, O Abdullah b. Umar, when you remain among the worthless dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted, and they have differed and become like this? And he interlaced his fingers. He said: Then how, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take what you recognize and leave what you reject, and turn to your own close affairs and leave their common folk."],[5599,"A man came to Abdullah b. Umar and said: How should I perform witr? He said: Perform witr with a single rak'ah. He said: I fear people will say it is the severed one. He said: Do you want the Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger? This is the Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger."],[5600,"Ibn Umar was asked about fasting on the day of Arafah. He said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ and he did not fast, and I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and Umar and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Uthman and he did not fast it, and I do not fast it, and I do not command it, and I do not forbid it."],[5601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition, and we retreated in a hasty retreat and entered Madinah and hid. We said: We are ruined, O Messenger of Allah; we are the ones who fled. He said: No, rather you are the ones who return to fight, and I am your party (fi'ah)."],[5603,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu once each. He said: This is the wudu without which Allah does not accept prayer. Then he performed wudu twice each. He said: This is the moderate way of wudu; its performer's reward is multiplied twice. Then he performed wudu three times each. He said: This is my wudu and the wudu of Allah's intimate friend Ibrahim, and the wudu of the prophets before me, and it is the prescribed norm of wudu. Whoever performs this wudu of mine and then says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; he may enter from whichever he wishes."],[5604,"I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: Did Uthman witness Badr? He said: No. He said: Did he witness the Pledge of Ridwan? He said: No. He said: Was he among those who turned away on the day the two armies met? He said: Yes. The man left, and it was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, this man will report that you disparaged Uthman. He said: Bring him back to me. Ibn Umar said to him: As for the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left him behind for his need, and allotted him a share, and he would not allot a share to an absent person. As for the Pledge of Ridwan, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to the people of Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ extended his hands and wiped them over his own palm, saying: This is for Uthman. The hand of the Messenger of Allah is better than the hand of Uthman. As for the day the two armies met, Allah has pardoned them. Go and strive against me as hard as you can."],[5605,"One prostration of yours is longer than three prostrations of the Prophet ﷺ."],[5606,"We used to say during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: The Prophet, then Abu Bakr, then Umar. And Ali b. Abi Talib was given three qualities; if I had even one of them it would be dearer to me than red camels: he married Fatimah and she bore him children, and the doors were closed except his door, and the banner was given to him on the day of Khaybar."],[5607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we do not equate anyone with him. Then we say: The best of people is Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Uthman, then we do not distinguish."],[5608,"Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Ismail b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, something similar."],[5609,"Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, from Layth b. Sa'd, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Ibn Umar something similar. He said: That would reach the Prophet ﷺ and he would not deny it."],[5610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud in the prayer just as the schoolteacher teaches the children."],[5611,"I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a young man passed by trailing his lower garment. He said to me: 'Call this one, call this one.' So I called him. He said to him: 'Raise your waist wrapper.' So he raised it to above his heels. Ibn Umar said: 'This is how the Messenger of Allah used to wrap his waist wrapper,' or he said: 'This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to wrap our waist wrappers.'"],[5612,"Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days. If he dies during that period, he will enter the Fire."],[5613,"Ibn Umar saw me praying after the break of dawn. He said: 'O Yasar, how many rak'ahs have you prayed?' I said: 'I do not know.' He said: 'May you never know. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were praying this prayer, and he said: \"Let those of you who are present convey to those who are absent that there is no prayer after dawn except two prostrations.\"'"],[5614,"Indeed Allah accepts the repentance of His servant as long as the death rattle has not begun."],[5615,"I asked Ibn Umar: 'From where is it permissible for me to enter ihram for umrah?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ designated it for the people of Madinah as Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham as al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd as Qarn.'"],[5616,"I heard Ibn Umar, and a man asked him about selling fruit. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fruit until its ripeness becomes evident.'"],[5617,"I heard Abdullah b. Umar saying at the pulpit – and he pointed to the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ –: 'The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about beverages. He forbade them from using gourds, hollowed-out stumps, and green jars.' I said: 'O Abu Muhammad, and the pitch-coated vessels?' We thought he had forgotten it. He said: 'I did not hear it that day from Abdullah b. Umar, and he used to dislike it.'"],[5618,"Whoever guides a blind person forty steps, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[5619,"No prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from ill-gotten gains."],[5620,"Amr b. Muhammad narrated to us; Muawiyah b. Amr narrated to us; Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak b. Harb, from Mus'ab b. Sa'd, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[5621,"Amr b. Muhammad narrated to us; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Mus'ab b. Sa'd, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[5622,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed inside the House, and someone will come to you who will forbid you from that, while Ibn Abbas was sitting beside him."],[5623,"The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear or dread the approach of dawn, then pray one."],[5624,"I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid nabidh made in earthen jars and gourds? He said: Yes."],[5625,"The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear the approach of dawn, then make witr with one."],[5626,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful."],[5627,"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful."],[5628,"Do not let the bedouins overpower you regarding the name of your prayer. Indeed, it is al-isha, while they call it al-atama because they delay milking the camels until darkness."],[5629,"I was with Abdullah b. Umar when a man came to bid him farewell. Ibn Umar said to him: Wait so that I may bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bid us farewell: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the final outcome of your deeds."],[5630,"When you are three, let not two converse privately excluding their companion, for that grieves him. He said: What if they are four? He said: It does not harm you."],[5631,"The Prophet ﷺ used to go to relieve himself at al-Mughammas. Nafi said: About two miles from Makkah."],[5632,"I asked Ibn Umar about a man who came for Umrah and circumambulated the House but did not walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah; may he go to his wife? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah seven times. Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have a good example."],[5633,"Do not be importunate in asking, for whoever extracts something from us by means of it will not be blessed in it."],[5634,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakʿahs behind the Maqam, and performed saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwah. And you have in the Messenger of God an excellent example."],[5635,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded the killing of dogs, except a livestock dog or a hunting dog. It was said to Ibn Umar: “Abu Hurayrah says: ‘or a farm dog’?” He said: “Abu Hurayrah has a farm.”"],[5636,"He bought some thirsty camels from Sharik al-Nawwas and found something wrong with them, so he said: “We are content with the ruling of the Messenger of God ﷺ: there is no contagion.”"],[5637,"Umar asked the Prophet ﷺ about an obligatory retreat upon himself, and he ordered him to perform retreat and fast. While he was in retreat, the people shouted “Allahu akbar,” so he said: “What is this, O Abdullah?” He said: “The captives of Hawazin; the Messenger of God ﷺ freed them.” Umar said: “And that slave girl, send her with them.”"],[5638,"He said to a man who ate a lot: “The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.’” The man said: “As for me, I believe in God and His Messenger.”"],[5639,"We asked him about a man who circumambulated the House but did not perform saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwah in an ʿumrah, may he have intercourse with his wife? He said: “No.” They also asked Ibn Umar about it, and Ibn Umar said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakʿahs behind the Maqam, and performed saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwah. And you have in the Messenger of God an excellent example.”"],[5640,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the night prayer – while I was between them – he said: The Prophet ﷺ said: “Two by two; and when you fear the dawn, pray one rakʿah, and two rakʿahs before the morning prayer.”"],[5641,"Whoever fasts Wednesday and Thursday, a release from the Fire is recorded for him."],[5642,"Suwayd narrated to us: Baqiyyah b. al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[5643,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in the mosque of Qubaʾ, and some people from the Ansar came to greet him while he was in prayer. Suhayb was with him, so I asked him: “How did he respond to them?” He said: “He gestured to them.”"],[5644,"Two men came from the east and delivered speeches, and the people marveled at their praise. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Some eloquence is magic,” or “Indeed, some eloquence is magic.”"],[5645,"Two men came during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ and delivered speeches, and the people marveled at their speech. The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to us and said: “Indeed, some eloquence is magic,” or “Indeed, some eloquence is magic.”"],[5646,"He used to see Ibn Umar with his shirt button undone. He was asked about that, and he said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ doing it."],[5647,"Abdullah b. Umar used to dye his beard yellow with khaluq. It was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, you dye your beard yellow with khaluq? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dyeing with it, and no dye was dearer to him than it. He used to dye all his garments with it, even his turban."],[5648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque of Quba—that is, the mosque of Banu Amr b. Awf—to pray in it. Some men of the Ansar entered upon him and greeted him while he was praying. I asked Suhayb, who had entered with him: How did the Prophet ﷺ respond when he was greeted? He said: He would gesture with his hand."],[5649,"Allah does not look at one who drags his lower garment out of pride."],[5650,"He used to dye with yellow. He was questioned about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dye with it. I saw him dyeing his garments with it, even his turban."],[5651,"Every creature among the beasts of the land and the sea that has no flowing blood has no proper slaughter."],[5652,"He used to pray on his mount wherever it turned him. He mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on his mount wherever it turned him, and Ibn Umar recited: 'Wherever you turn, there is the face of Allah.'"],[5653,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ counting the fast of Arafah as the fast of a year."],[5654,"He led them in prayer at Jam with an adhan and an iqamah for the Maghrib prayer, then he said: The prayer! And he prayed Isha. He was asked about that, and he said: Thus I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this place."],[5655,"He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned her to me until I divorced her while she was pure."],[5656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the two who had taken the oath of condemnation: Your reckoning is with Allah; one of you is lying. There is no way for you over her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my property! He said: There is no property for you. If you were truthful about her, it is in return for what you made lawful of her private part; and if you were lying, that is even further for you."],[5657,"Ibn Umar passed by some youths of Quraysh who had set up a bird as a target and were shooting at it, and they had given the owner of the bird every arrow that missed. When they saw Ibn Umar, they dispersed. Ibn Umar said: Who did this? May Allah curse the one who did this! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed whoever takes anything with a soul as a target."],[5658,"He forbade the sale of the offspring of the offspring in the womb."],[5659,"I saw Ibn Umar when he owed silver, he would pay its value in dinars if the price was fixed. And when he owed dinars, he would pay silver according to its value."],[5660,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he said: If you take one of them in exchange for the other, then do not part from your companion while there remains any outstanding transaction between you."],[5661,"The Prophet ﷺ called for the woman and recited to her, admonished her, reminded her, and informed her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, he has not spoken the truth, and he has lied. He said: The Prophet ﷺ began with the man, and he testified four times by Allah that he was indeed among the truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he was among the liars. Then the Prophet ﷺ called for the woman, and she testified four times by Allah that he was indeed among the liars, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he was among the truthful. Then the Prophet ﷺ separated them."],[5662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw as if there were two bracelets of gold on his hands. The Prophet ﷺ said: I blew on them and they flew away. They are the two liars of my community: the man of Yamamah and the man of Yemen, and they will not harm my community at all."],[5663,"It is not appropriate for a man to take charge of his slave's hot food and cold, and when it is served, to keep it away from him."],[5664,"There came upon us a time when we did not consider any of us more entitled to dinars and dirhams than his Muslim brother, until lately, when dinars and dirhams became dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When people become stingy with dirhams and dinars, and engage in 'inah transactions, and follow the tails of cattle, and abandon jihad, Allah will send humiliation upon them, and He will not remove it from them until they return to their religion."],[5665,"He was on a journey of his, and when the time for prayer came, the people dismounted. A shepherd noticed them, so he dismounted and struck the ground with his hand, performed tayammum, then gave the call to prayer. He said: Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: He is upon the natural disposition. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: He has come out of the Fire."],[5666,"He would not wake at any hour of the night without passing the siwak over his mouth."],[5667,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a bedouin came to him and said: Would you like something good? You testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. He said: And who will testify for you? He said: This salmah tree. So he called it while it was on the bank of the valley, and it came cleaving the earth until it stood before him. He asked it to testify, and it testified three times, then it returned to its place. The bedouin said: I will go to my people, and if they follow me, I will bring them to you; otherwise I will return to you and stay with you."],[5668,"The Prophet ﷺ and his companions did not perform more than one tawaf for both their 'umrah and their hajj."],[5669,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on a donkey while heading toward Khaybar."],[5670,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying while he was facing Tabuk."],[5671,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying on a donkey while he was facing Khaybar."],[5672,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed witr on a camel."],[5673,"Ibn Umar heard a man say, 'By my father,' so Ibn Umar said: Do not swear by it; for Umar used to swear by it, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not swear by it."],[5674,"I came to Madinah, and Abdullah b. Umar came to me and said: Do you know why I came to you? I said: No. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever wishes to maintain ties with his father in his grave, let him maintain ties with his father's brothers after him. Indeed, between my father Umar and your father there was brotherhood and affection, so I wished to maintain that."],[5675,"He used to raise his hands every time he bowed and every time he raised. I said: What is this? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he stood after the two rak'ahs, said takbir and raised his hands."],[5676,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade gourd vessels and green jars. He said: And I think he said: and hollowed-out stumps."],[5677,"Two men brought a dispute to Muharib. He said: A man testified against one of them, and the one testified against said: By God, I did not know that he was a truthful man, and if you ask about him he will be praised—or commended—yet he has testified falsely against me; I do not know what emboldened him to do that. Muharib b. Dithar said: O you, fear God! For I heard Abdullah b. Umar say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The false witness's feet will not move until the Fire becomes incumbent upon him, and indeed the birds on the Day of Resurrection will beat their wings and cast out what is in their bellies, having no desire for it. And the Prophet ﷺ was admonishing a man."],[5678,"When we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey and it was a dark night—or a rainy night—the Messenger of God's muezzin would call the adhan, or his caller would announce: Pray in your dwellings."],[5679,"I was with Abdullah b. Umar when a man came to bid him farewell. Ibn Umar said: Wait, let me bid you farewell as the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bid us farewell: I entrust to God your religion, your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds."],[5680,"The Prophet ﷺ stood on the steps of the Ka'bah on the Day of the Conquest and said: Praise be to God who fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and alone defeated the confederates. Indeed, the intentional killing by mistake—with the whip and the stick—in intentional cases requires one hundred camels, of which forty are pregnant she-camels with young in their bellies. Indeed, every blood claim and inherited privilege from the Age of Ignorance is under these two feet of mine, except for the custodianship of the House and the watering of the pilgrims, for I shall confirm them for their people as they were."],[5681,"When Abdullah b. Umar went to his bed, he would say: O God, You created my soul and You take it in death; to You belong its life and its death. O God, if You take it, forgive it, and if You keep it alive, protect it. O God, I ask You for well-being. A man of his children said to him: Father, did Umar say this? He said: Rather, one better than Umar used to say it. He said: We thought he meant the Prophet ﷺ."],[5682,"No prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from stolen property."],[5683,"Change gray hair and do not imitate the Jews."],[5684,"I said to Ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we enter upon the ruler when he issues a judgment that we consider unjust, and we say: May God grant you success, and we look at a man among us and praise him?! He said: As for us, the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, we used to consider this hypocrisy, and I do not know what you consider it."],[5685,"The Prophet ﷺ stood at the well of Badr and said: Have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? Then he said: They are listening to what I say. This was mentioned to Aisha, and she said: He erred—meaning Ibn Umar—he only said: Now they know that what I used to tell them is the truth. Then she recited this verse: Indeed, you cannot make the dead hear, until she finished the verse."],[5686,"Indeed, the dead is punished by the weeping of his family over him. I mentioned that to Aisha, and she said: He erred—meaning Ibn Umar—the Messenger of God ﷺ only passed by a grave and said: The occupant of this grave is being punished while his family weep over him. Then she recited this verse: And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another."],[5687,"A man called out to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Which part of the night is most answered for supplication? He said: The last part of the night."],[5688,"When the edge of the sun appears, delay the prayer until it is fully risen, and when the edge of the sun disappears, delay the prayer until it has set."],[5689,"Do not intentionally aim your prayers at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."],[5690,"I said: O Messenger of God, tell me a saying and be brief, that perhaps I may understand it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not become angry. I repeated twice, and each time the Prophet ﷺ returned to me: Do not become angry."],[5691,"Whoever drinks wine, no prayer is accepted from him for forty mornings. If he repents, God turns to him. If he returns, no prayer is accepted from him for forty mornings. If he repents, God turns to him. If he returns, no prayer is accepted from him for forty mornings. If he repents, God turns to him. If he returns a fourth time, no prayer is accepted from him for forty mornings, and if he repents, God will not turn to him, and He will give him to drink from the river of putrid pus. It was said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the river of putrid pus? He said: A river of the pus of the people of Hell."],[5692,"He used to crowd at the two corners, so I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have seen you crowd at the two corners with a crowding I have not seen any of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ do. He said: If I do so, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Wiping them is an expiation for sins. And I heard him say: Whoever circumambulates the House seven times and counts them, it is like freeing a slave. And I heard him say: He does not place a foot nor raise the other except that God removes a sin from him, writes a good deed for him, and raises him a degree."],[5693,"I said to Ibn Umar: Why do I see you only touching these two corners: the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner? Ibn Umar said: If I do so, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Touching them wipes away sins. And I heard him say: Whoever circumambulates seven circuits, counting them, and prays two rak'ahs, it is like freeing a slave. And I heard him say: A man does not raise a foot or place it except that ten good deeds are written for him, ten evil deeds are removed from him, and he is raised ten degrees."],[5694,"What is the matter with you that I see you touching these two corners and not touching others? Meaning: the Black Stone and the Yamani Corner. He said: If I do so, it is because I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Touching them erases sins, and no man lifts a foot or puts it down except that ten good deeds are written for him and ten evil deeds are erased from him. And I heard him say: Whoever counts seven circuits and prays two rak'ahs, it is like freeing a slave."],[5695,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to a man: Did you do such and such? He said: No, by the One besides whom there is no god, I did not do it. Gabriel said to him: He did do it, but God, Blessed and Exalted, has forgiven him for saying: There is no god but God."],[5696,"I asked Ibn Umar about the vessels. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited those vessels."],[5697,"I witnessed Bakr b. Abdullah al-Muzani when a man asked him about the talbiyah of the Prophet ﷺ. He narrated to us from Ibn Umar that when the Messenger of God ﷺ made the talbiyah, he said: Labbayk, O God, labbayk; labbayk, You have no partner, labbayk. Indeed, all praise and blessings are Yours, and all sovereignty; You have no partner."],[5698,"The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Makkah making the talbiyah for Hajj. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Make it an Umrah, except for those who have the sacrificial animal with them. They said: O Messenger of God, one of us would go to Mina while his private part is dripping semen? He said: Yes. Then the incense burners flared up in al-Batha, and Ali arrived from Yemen. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: With what did you enter ihram, for we have your family with us? He said: I entered ihram with what the Messenger of God entered ihram."],[5699,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha at al-Batha, then slept a short sleep, then entered Makkah."],[5700,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered ihram for both of them together. Bakr said: I met Ibn Umar and told him what Anas said. Ibn Umar said: He entered ihram only for Hajj. I went back to Anas and told him what Ibn Umar said. He said: You consider us only as children – or as if we were children."],[5701,"When God sends down punishment upon a people, the punishment strikes those in their midst, then they will be resurrected according to their intentions."],[5702,"Swearing an oath is either a violation or a regret."],[5703,"Whoever wears a garment of fame, God will clothe him on the Day of Resurrection with a garment of humiliation."],[5704,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married a woman from Banu Ghifar. When she entered upon him, he saw a white spot on her flank and sent her back, saying: You deceived me."],[5705,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed inside the Ka'bah."],[5706,"Indeed in my ummah there will be more than seventy callers, all of them calling to the Fire. If I wished, I would inform you of their fathers and tribes. He said: Then we passed by some pools. He said: We began to lap water from them with our mouths, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not lap water; rather wash your hands, then drink from them, for there is no vessel better than the hand."],[5707,"This clan of Quraysh will remain secure until they turn you away from your religion in recompense for our kinship. He said: Then a man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of God, am I in Paradise or in the Fire? He said: In Paradise. Then another stood up to him and said: Am I in Paradise or in the Fire? [He said: In the Fire.] Then he said: Be silent about me as long as I am silent about you. Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would inform you of your company from the people of the Fire until you would recognize them, at death. And if I were commanded to do so, I would do it."],[5708,"Shall I show you the place from which the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The Beast of the Earth will come forth? He struck with his staff the crack in al-Safa and said: Indeed it has feathers and down, and indeed a third of it will emerge at the speed of a swift horse for three days and three nights. And it will pass by them while they flee from it to the mosques, and it will say to them: Do you think the mosques will save you from me? Then it will brand them on their noses, and they will be driven in the markets, and it will say: O disbeliever! O believer!"],[5709,"None of you should eat with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[5710,"None of you should eat with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[5711,"A man asked Ibn Umar about mut'ah of women — while I was with him — and he became angry and said: We were not, in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, fornicators or adulterers. Then he said: By God, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Before the Day of Resurrection there will surely be the Messiah al-Dajjal and thirty liars or more than that."],[5712,"A man came to Abdullah b. Umar — while I was with him — and asked him about mut'ah of women, so he became angry and said: By God, we were not in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ fornicators or adulterers."],[5713,"No household endures hardship for three days except that God brings them provision."],[5714,"I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ not fasting on a Friday."],[5715,"A guest came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he said to Bilal: Bring us food. Bilal went and exchanged two sa' of dates for one sa' of better dates — their dates were of poor quality — and it pleased the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: Where is this from? He informed him that he had exchanged two sa' for one sa'. The Prophet ﷺ said: Return our dates to us."],[5716,"The sweat will reach from the people on the Day of Resurrection, so he said — meaning one of them: up to the lobe of his ear."],[5717,"Indeed the lowest of the people of Paradise in station is one who will look upon his tent, his servants, his bliss, and his couches for a distance of a thousand years, and the most honored of them before God is one who will look upon God morning and evening. Then he recited this verse: 'Faces on that Day will be radiant, looking at their Lord.'"],[5718,"Whoever among you loves that his supplication be answered and his distress be relieved, let him ease the burden of one in hardship."],[5719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ clothed me in a silk suit from the fine silk garments that Fayruz had gifted to him. I wore the lower garment, and it was too wide and too long for me, so I dragged it, and I wore the upper garment, wrapping it around my head. Then he said, “O Abdullah, raise the lower garment, for whatever touches the dust down to below the ankles is in the Fire.” Abdullah b. Muhammad said: I have not seen anyone more diligent in tucking up the lower garment than Abdullah b. Umar."],[5720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray before the Eid prayer or after it."],[5721,"Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, dates for dates, like for like, measure for measure. Whoever gives more or asks for more has engaged in usury."],[5722,"Allah accepts the repentance of a servant as long as he has not yet reached the death rattle."],[5723,"I asked Ibn Umar, “From where is it permissible for me to enter ihram for Umrah?” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ designated for the people of Madinah Dhul-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd Qarn.”"],[5724,"I heard a man ask Ibn Umar about selling fruit. He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fruit until its ripeness appears.”"],[5725,"I observed Ibn Umar for a month and heard him in the two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer reciting: “Say, O disbelievers” and “Say, He is Allah, the One.” He said, “I mentioned that to him, and he said, ‘I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a month, or twenty-five days, reciting in the two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer: “Say, O disbelievers” and “Say, He is Allah, the One.”’ And he said, ‘One of them is equal to a third of the Quran, and the other to a quarter of the Quran. “Say, He is Allah, the One” is equal to a third of the Quran, and “Say, O disbelievers” is equal to a quarter of the Quran.’”"],[5726,"I asked Ibn Umar in Mina about the prayer here. He said, “I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, with Umar two rak'ahs, and with Uthman at the beginning of his caliphate two rak'ahs. When we prayed with them, we prayed as they prayed, and when we prayed alone, we prayed [two rak'ahs as well].”"],[5727,"I wore a silk garment and came upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—while he was near the room of Hafsah—on a dark night. He heard the rustling of the garment and said, “Who is this?” I said, “Abdullah b. Umar.” He said, “Raise your garment, for the one who drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him.” He said, “That night my lower garment was up to the middle of my shins.”"],[5728,"Seventy prophets took shade under a lote tree; it is not to be cut down, stripped of leaves, or pruned."],[5729,"Abdullah b. Umar went out for Hajj until when he was between Makkah and Madinah, he came to a tree he recognized and sat beneath it. Then he said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under this tree when a young man came from this mountain pass until he stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, I have come to fight alongside you in the path of Allah, seeking thereby the countenance of Allah and the Hereafter.’ He said, ‘Are both of your parents alive?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then return and be dutiful to them.’” He said, “So he turned back, returning the way he came.”"],[5730,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I broke the fast on one day of Ramadan. He said: Without excuse or travel? He said: Yes. He said: What an evil thing you have done! He said: Indeed, so what do you command me? He said: Free a slave. He said: By the One who sent you with truth, I have never owned a slave. He said: Then fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot do that. He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. He said: By the One who sent you with truth, I cannot even satisfy my own family. He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ was brought a large basket containing dates, and he said: Give this in charity to sixty poor persons. He said: To whom shall I give it? He said: To the poorest person you know. He said: By the One who sent you with truth, there is no household between its two sides more needy than us. He said: Then give it in charity to your own dependents."],[5731,"Al-Kifl of the Children of Israel did not abstain from any sin he committed. A woman came to him, and he gave her sixty dinars on condition that he have intercourse with her. When he sat from her as a man sits, she trembled and wept. He said: What makes you weep? Did I compel you? She said: No, but this is a deed I have never done, and only need drove me to it. He said: You would do this and you have never done it? He said: Then he got down and said: Go, and the dinars are yours. Then he said: By Allah, al-Kifl will never disobey Allah again. He said: He died that night, and in the morning it was written on his door: Allah has forgiven al-Kifl."],[5732,"Whoever is a judge and judges unjustly is among the people of the Fire; whoever is a judge and judges ignorantly is among the people of the Fire; and whoever is a judge and judges justly is most likely to escape with nothing."],[5733,"While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer, a man among the people said: Allah is the Greatest, greatly; and much praise be to Allah; and glory be to Allah morning and evening. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: Which of you is the owner of those words? The people remained silent. A man among the people said: I said them, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended only good by them. The Messenger of Allah said: The gates of heaven were opened for them. Ibn Umar said: I have not abandoned them since I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying that."],[5734,"The lowest of the people of Paradise in station will look over his kingdom for two thousand years, seeing its farthest extent, looking at his wives and couches. And the best of them in station will look upon the face of Allah twice every day."],[5735,"Abd al-Aziz b. Marwan wrote to Ibn Umar: Raise to me your need. He said: Ibn Umar wrote back: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. I will not ask you for anything, nor will I reject any provision Allah has granted me from you."],[5736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: You and your wealth belong to your father."],[5737,"Would any of you be unable, when a man comes to him wanting to kill him, to be like the two sons of Adam: the killer will be in the Fire, and the killed will be in Paradise?"],[5738,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a jar of unripe-date infusion – and he was in the Mosque of al-Fadikh – and he drank it. For that reason it was named the Mosque of al-Fadikh."],[5739,"He used to halt at Arafah in the valley of Namirah."],[5740,"I asked Ibn Umar about the prayer at Mina. He said: Have you heard of Muhammad ﷺ? I said: Yes, and I believe in him. He said: He used to pray two rak'ahs at Mina."],[5741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade joining dates together until you seek permission from your companions."],[5742,"He kissed the Prophet ﷺ"],[5743,"Leave the beards and trim the moustaches"],[5744,"A man asked Ibn Umar about the blood of mosquitoes. He said: “Where are you from?” He said: “From the people of Iraq.” He said: “Look at this one! He asks me about the blood of mosquitoes while they have killed the son of the Messenger of Allah! I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘These two are my two fragrant flowers in this world.’”"],[5745,"A man said to Ibn Umar: “What do you think about the witr—is it a Sunnah?” He said: “What is a Sunnah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed witr, and the Muslims did.” He said: “Is it a Sunnah?” He said to him: “Do you not understand? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed witr, and the Muslims did.”"],[5746,"He was standing praying in the mosque while Ibn Umar was facing him, leaning his back against the qibla of the mosque. When Wasi' finished, he turned from his left toward Ibn Umar and sat with him. Ibn Umar said to him: “What prevents you from turning to your right?” He said: “Nothing, except that I saw you and turned to you.” He said: “You have done well. Some people say: If you are praying and finish, then turn to your right.” Ibn Umar said: “If you are praying and finish, then turn, if you wish, to your right, and if you wish, to your left.” Ibn Umar said: “Other people say: When one sits to relieve himself, let him not face the qibla or Bayt al-Maqdis. One day I climbed onto our house and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relieving himself—Abu Yala was uncertain—facing Bayt al-Maqdis.”"],[5747,"They both testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while he was on the pulpit: “Let a people stop neglecting the Friday prayers, or Allah will seal their hearts, and they will surely be among the heedless.”"],[5748,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in the first rak'ah of the Zuhr prayer, and his companions perceived that he had recited “Tanzeel” (i.e., Surat al-Sajdah)."],[5749,"Do not strike the slaves, for you do not know what you will achieve."],[5750,"He saw a servant of his named Yasar praying after dawn and forbade him. He said: “Only what remains of my portion of recitation.” Abdullah said to him: “Could you not have delayed it until it becomes daytime?” Then Abdullah said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while people were praying after the break of dawn and said: ‘There is no prayer after dawn except two rak'ahs.’”"],[5751,"Whoever hoards food for forty nights has disowned Allah and Allah has disowned him. And any people of a neighborhood in which a hungry person spends the morning, the protection of Allah is withdrawn from them."],[5752,"Abdullah b. al-Zubayr led us in prayer in the dark before dawn while Ibn Umar was beside me. When he said the salam, I said: “What is this prayer, O Abu Abd al-Rahman?” He said: “This was our prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with Abu Bakr and Umar. When Umar was killed, Uthman made it later when it became light.”"],[5753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed four rak'ahs before Asr."],[5754,"He would not sleep except with the tooth-stick (siwak) by his side. When he woke up, he would begin with the tooth-stick."],[5755,"Ibn Umar entered upon Abdullah b. Amir to visit him, and he said: What prevents you from supplicating for me? He said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: Allah does not accept prayer without purification."],[5756,"A man asked Ibn Umar: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [describe] the private conversation (najwa)? He said: He used to say: The servant draws near to his Lord, and He places His covering (kanaf) over him and makes him confess. He says: You did such-and-such and you did such-and-such. He says: Yes, O Lord. He says: Then He says: I concealed it for you in the world, and I forgive it for you today. He said: Then he is given the page of his good deeds, and he says: Take it, read my book! He said: As for the hypocrites, they will be called: These are the ones who lied against their Lord. Surely the curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers."],[5757,"Congregational prayer is superior to the prayer of a solitary person by twenty-seven degrees."],[5758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us that among Thaqif there would be a destroyer (mubir) and a liar (kadhdhab)."],[5759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ encouraged jihad one day, and they crowded around him until they overwhelmed him. In the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a palm branch from which its leaves had been stripped, but one leaf remained which he did not notice. He said: Move back from me—like this—for you have crowded me. The Prophet ﷺ struck the belly of a man and made him bleed. The man went out saying: This is the action of your Prophet, so how [will it be] with the people? Umar heard him and said: Come to the Prophet ﷺ. If he is the one who struck you, he will give you your right from himself; but if you have lied, I will drag you by your turban until you speak. The man said: Go in peace, for I do not want to go with you. He said: I am not leaving you. Umar took him until he brought him to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: This man claims that you struck him and made his belly bleed. What do you think? The Prophet ﷺ said: Is it true that I struck him? The man said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Did anyone see that? He said: There were people of the Muslims here. He said: O Allah, I testify by the testimony of a man who saw that—except."],[5760,"When you place your dead in the grave niche (lahd), say: In the name of Allah and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."],[5761,"I asked Ibn Abbas about the witr. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: One rak'ah from the last part of the night."],[5762,"One rak'ah from the last part of the night."],[5763,"When he lay down in his bed, he used to say: Praise be to Allah who has sufficed me, sheltered me, fed me, and given me drink; who has bestowed favor upon me and been generous; who has given me and granted abundantly. Praise be to Allah in every condition. Praise be to Allah, Lord of everything, King of everything, God of everything, and to You belongs everything. I seek refuge in You from the Fire."],[5764,"Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in a dream what a man sees. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: If a woman sees that and has a discharge, she should perform ghusl."],[5765,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: My servant does wrong and oppresses. Should I beat him? He said: Forgive him seventy times every day."],[5766,"The Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulated on his mount on the day of the conquest of Makkah, touching the corners with a staff that he had with him."],[5767,"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, its expiation is to abandon it."],[5768,"The most compassionate of my community toward my community is Abu Bakr; the strongest of them in Islam is Umar; the most truthful of them in modesty is Uthman b. Affan; the most judicious of them is Ali b. Abi Talib; the most knowledgeable of them in inheritance law is Zayd b. Thabit; the most learned of them in what is lawful and unlawful is Muadh b. Jabal; the best reciter of them is Ubayy b. Kab; and every community has a trustworthy keeper, and the trustworthy keeper of this community is Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah."],[5769,"He asked Abdullah b. Umar about the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: God is greatest, whenever he raised and whenever he lowered. Then he said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of God, to his right; peace be upon you and the mercy of God, to his left."],[5770,"We heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the planks of his pulpit: Let people stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or God will seal their hearts, and then they will be among the heedless."],[5771,"Amr b. Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Affan b. Muslim narrated to us, Aban b. Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, Yahya b. Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd Abu Sallam, from al-Hakam b. Mina, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of God ﷺ, something similar to the hadith of Ismail b. Ibrahim."],[5772,"I prayed beside Ibn Umar, and I began to fidget with the pebbles. He said: Do not fidget with the pebbles, for fidgeting with the pebbles is from Satan. Do as I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how did you see him do? He said: Like this. He placed his left hand on his left thigh and his right hand on his right thigh, and he pointed with the finger next to the thumb."],[5773,"He used to pray at night in pairs, and he would perform witr with one rak'a, and he would pray two rak'as before the dawn prayer."],[5774,"I asked Ibn Umar: The two rak'as before the dawn prayer, should I lengthen the recitation in them? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray at night in pairs, and he would perform witr with one rak'a. I said: I am not asking you about that. He said: You are indeed bulky! Will you not let me recount the hadith to you? The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray at night in pairs, and he would perform witr with one rak'a, then he would pray two rak'as before the dawn prayer as if the call to prayer were in his ears."],[5775,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: How is the night prayer? He said: In pairs. When you fear the coming of dawn, pray one rak'a and make the last of your prayer witr. Then he asked him at the end of the year, while I was in that place near the Messenger of God, and I do not know whether it was the same man or another, and he said to him the same thing."],[5776,"From Ibn Umar: He prayed them with one iqama and said: This is how the Messenger of God ﷺ did in this place."],[5777,"The Prophet ﷺ conducted a mutual imprecation between a woman and her husband and separated them."],[5778,"The Messenger of God ﷺ besieged the people of al-Ta’if, but he did not gain anything from them. He said, 'We are returning, God willing.' His companions said, 'Shall we return without having conquered?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them, 'Set out for battle in the morning.' They set out in the morning, and they were wounded. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them, 'We are returning tomorrow,' and that pleased them. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled."],[5779,"I was standing praying toward the House, and an old man was beside me. I prolonged the prayer, and I placed my hands on my waist. The old man struck my chest with his hand, a blow not sparing me. I said to myself, 'What did he find objectionable in me?' I hastened to finish, and there was a boy sitting behind him. I said, 'Who is this old man?' He said, 'This is Abdullah b. Umar.' I sat until he finished. I said, 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what did you find objectionable in me?' He said, 'It was you?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That is the placing of the hand on the waist in prayer; the Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid it.'"],[5780,"When God wants to create a soul, the angel of the wombs says, turning aside: 'O Lord, male or female?' Then God decrees His command. Then he says: 'O Lord, wretched or blessed?' Then God decrees His command. Then he writes between his eyes what he is to meet, even the misfortune that will befall him."],[5781,"I memorized from the Messenger of God ﷺ ten rak’ahs: two before the dawn prayer, two before the noon prayer, two after the noon prayer, two after the sunset prayer, and two after the night prayer."],[5782,"Ibn Umar used to perform ablution three times, three times, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[5783,"He was with Ibn Umar on the road to Makkah, and he led them in prayer. Then he went to his mount, and we went with him. He turned and saw people praying, so he said, 'What are these people doing?' I said, 'They are praying voluntary prayers.' He said, 'If I were to pray voluntary prayers, I would have completed my prayer. O son of my brother, I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not add in travel to more than two rak’ahs until God took him. Then I accompanied Abu Bakr, and he did not add to more than two rak’ahs. Then I accompanied Umar, and he did not add to more than two rak’ahs. Then I accompanied Uthman, and he did not add to more than two rak’ahs until God took him. And God said: You have indeed in the Messenger of God an excellent example.'"],[5784,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey, and he passed by a pool of water, and they lapped it up. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not lap it up, but wash your hands and drink, for there is no vessel cleaner than the hand.'"],[5785,"I said to Abdullah b. Umar, while he was at Mina, 'How many do you pray here?' He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed two rak’ahs, Abu Bakr two rak’ahs, Umar two rak’ahs, and Uthman prayed them two rak’ahs for six years, then they prayed them four. So when we prayed with them, we prayed four, and when we prayed separately, we prayed two rak’ahs.'"],[5786,"We were in an army that the Messenger of God ﷺ had sent, and the people fled in a rout, and we were defeated and we were a small group. We said, 'Shall we flee in the land and not come to the Messenger of God ﷺ, out of shame for what we did?' Then some of us said, 'If we came to Madinah, we could buy provisions from it and prepare ourselves.' When we entered Madinah, we said, 'If we presented ourselves to the Prophet ﷺ?' He said, 'We waited for him at the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of God ﷺ came out, we said, 'O Messenger of God, we are the deserters.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Rather, you are the ones who return to fight; I am the group of the Muslims.'"],[5787,"Ibn Umar slapped a slave of his, then freed him, and said, 'I have no reward from him except this'—and he took some earth—'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever strikes his slave unjustly, there is no expiation for him short of freeing him.'"],[5788,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a drunkard, and he inflicted the legal punishment on him. Then he said, 'What is your drink?' He said, 'Raisins and dates.' He said, 'You mix them? Each one has reached the other.'"],[5789,"We used to count—while the Messenger of God ﷺ was alive and his companions were numerous—Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, then we would remain silent."],[5790,"He used to enter the state of ihram when his mount stood up with him, and he would enter ihram at the end of the prayer, and he would say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[5791,"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the witr prayer on a camel."],[5792,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque."],[5793,"Islam is built on five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan."],[5794,"A freedwoman of Ibn Umar came to greet him in order to leave Madinah, and she said: I am going to the countryside, for times have become hard for us. Ibn Umar said: Sit down, O Lakāʿ, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever patiently endures its hardship and severity, I will be an intercessor – or a witness – for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5795,"A freedwoman of Ibn Umar came to him and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman. He said: What is the matter with you? She said: I intended to go out to the countryside, and she mentioned the prices. He said to her: Stay, O Lakāʿ, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No one patiently endures its hardship and severity except that I will be an intercessor – or a witness – for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5796,"He prayed the maghrib and ʿisha prayers at Jamʿ with a single iqama, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it."],[5797,"I prayed with Ibn Umar the maghrib and ʿisha prayers at al-Muzdalifa. He prayed maghrib as three rakʿahs and ʿisha as two rakʿahs with one iqama. When he finished, a man said to him: What is this prayer, O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman? He said: I prayed it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5798,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said while standing on the pulpit: Whoever of you comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."],[5799,"Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at the one who drags his lower garment out of pride."],[5800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade shighār."],[5801,"He forbade najsh."],[5802,"Whoever sells palm trees that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it."],[5803,"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes possession of it."],[5804,"He forbade selling fruits until their ripeness appears; he forbade both the seller and the buyer."],[5805,"Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Abdullah b. Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it."],[5806,"We were in the time of the Prophet ﷺ buying food, and he would send someone to us to order us to move it from the place where we bought it to another place before we sold it."],[5807,"None of you should sell against the sale of another."],[5808,"Whoever frees his share in a slave, and has wealth reaching the price of the slave, the slave is valued at a fair price, and he gives his partners their shares and the slave is freed on his behalf; otherwise, only what he freed is freed."],[5809,"The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn. Abdullah said: It has reached me that the Prophet ﷺ said: And the people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam."],[5810,"The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: Labbayka Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak. He said: Abdullah would add to it: Labbayka labbayka labbayk, wa sa'dayka, wa al-khayru fi yadayka, wa al-raghba'u ilayka wa al-'amal."],[5811,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What does a pilgrim in ihram wear? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He should not wear a shirt, a turban, trousers, or leather socks, except someone who cannot find sandals, then he may wear leather socks and cut them below the ankles. And he should not wear any clothing touched by saffron or wars."],[5812,"Indeed, the one who misses the Asr prayer, it is as if his family and wealth have been taken away."],[5813,"A town-dweller should not sell for a desert-dweller. And he said: Do not meet the caravans, and none of you should sell against the sale of another, and none of you should propose marriage against the proposal of his brother, until the first suitor leaves or gives him permission to propose."],[5814,"Whoever frees a share of his in a slave, and he has wealth sufficient to cover its price, a fair value is assessed for him, and otherwise there is freed of him what is freed."],[5815,"A man called out to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was on the pulpit, saying, “O Messenger of God, how is the night prayer?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Like this” — describing with his finger — “two by two, and when you fear the dawn, pray one rakʿah to make your prayer odd-numbered.”"],[5816,"A man said while the Messenger of God ﷺ was on the pulpit, “O Messenger of God, which of the beasts may the pilgrim in iḥrām kill?” He said, “The crow, the kite, and the rabid dog.”"],[5817,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ touching the Black Stone, and I have not passed by it since I saw him except that I touched it."],[5818,"A man said while the Messenger of God ﷺ was on the pulpit, “What does the pilgrim in iḥrām wear?” He said, “He does not wear the shirt, nor the turban, nor the trousers, nor the burnoose, nor the leather socks, except for one who does not find sandals, then what is below the two ankles, and nothing of clothing touched by wars or saffron.”"],[5819,"We used to refrain from seeking forgiveness for those who commit major sins, until we heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “God does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that to whom He wills.” He said: “I have reserved my supplication as intercession for the major sinners of my community.” He said: “So we refrained from much of what was in our hearts, then afterwards we spoke and hoped.”"],[5820,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb saw ʿUṭārid al-Tamīmī displaying in the market a striped silk garment, and he was a man who frequented kings and obtained from them. ʿUmar said, “O Messenger of God, I saw ʿUṭārid displaying in the market a striped silk garment; if only you would buy it and wear it for the Arab delegations when they come to you” — and I think he said, “and wear it on Friday.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears silk in this world.” Later, the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought striped silk garments, and he sent ʿUmar a garment, sent Usāma a garment, and gave ʿAlī a garment, saying, “Tear it into veils among your women.” ʿUmar came with his garment and said, “O Messenger of God, you sent me this, yet yesterday you said about ʿUṭārid’s garment what you said.” He said, “I did not send it to you to wear it, but I sent it to you to benefit from it.” As for Usāma, he went about in his garment, and the Messenger of God ﷺ looked at him with a look by which he knew that the Messenger of God ﷺ disapproved of what he had done. He said, “O Messenger of God, why do you look at me? You sent it to me.” He said, “I did not send it to you to wear it, but I sent it to you to tear it into veils among your women.”"],[5821,"The talbiyah of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: “Labbayka Allāhumma labbayk, labbayka lā sharīka laka labbayk, inna al-ḥamda wa-al-niʿmata laka wa-al-mulk, lā sharīka lak.”"],[5822,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[5823,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ praying two rakʿahs after Maghrib in his family’s quarters, and two rakʿahs after the ʿIshāʾ prayer in his family’s quarters."],[5824,"The woman in iḥrām does not wear a face veil."],[5825,"He forbade shighār."],[5826,"He forbade (the use of) dubba' (a gourd container) and muqayyar (a container smeared with pitch)."],[5827,"He forbade habal al-habala (the sale of the offspring of the offspring of a pregnant camel). He said: The people of the Jahiliyyah used to buy it; a man would buy a she-camel to be delivered when the she-camel gives birth, then when the one in her belly gives birth."],[5828,"The two parties to a sale have the option (to cancel) as long as they have not separated, except in the case of a sale with an option."],[5829,"Indeed Allah is not one-eyed. The Dajjal, the False Messiah, is one-eyed; his right eye is like a floating grape."],[5830,"Indeed the one who misses the 'Asr prayer, it is as if he has lost his family and his wealth."],[5831,"Indeed the one who drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a military detachment to Najd, among them was 'Abd Allah. They captured abundant spoils of war, and their shares were twelve camels each, and each person among them was given an extra portion (nafal)."],[5833,"Whoever bears arms against us is not one of us."],[5834,"It is not right for any Muslim who has something to bequeath to pass two nights except that his will is written with him."],[5835,"He used to forbid us, when we were three people, that two of them should converse privately excluding the third."],[5836,"Indeed when one of you dies, his seat is shown to him morning and evening. If he is from the people of Paradise, then (he sees his seat) from the people of Paradise; and if he is from the people of the Fire, then (he sees his seat) from the people of the Fire, until Allah resurrects him on the Day of Resurrection."],[5837,"Indeed all of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for your flocks. Indeed the ruler who is over the people is a shepherd over them and is responsible for them. A man is a shepherd over his household and is responsible for them. A man's wife is a shepherd over her husband's house and his children and is responsible for them. A man's slave is a shepherd over his master's property and is responsible for it. Indeed all of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for your flocks."],[5838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard Umar swearing by his father while he was in a travelling party riding with them, so he called out to them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'God forbids you to swear by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by God or remain silent.'"],[5839,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cut off the hand of a thief for a shield worth three dirhams."],[5840,"He used to give a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley as zakat al-fitr. Abdullah used to say: 'The people made its equivalent two mudds of wheat.'"],[5841,"The Messenger of God ﷺ made a ring of gold and used to place its stone towards the palm of his hand when he wore it on his right hand. The people then made rings of gold. The Messenger of God ﷺ sat on the pulpit, removed it, and said: 'I used to wear this ring and place its stone towards the palm of my hand.' He threw it away and said: 'By God, I will never wear it again.' The Messenger of God ﷺ discarded the ring, and the people discarded their rings."],[5842,"Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day. It was said to him: 'Abu Hurayra says: or a farm dog?' He said: 'Abu Hurayra is a man who owns farms.'"],[5843,"He burned the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir, and about them Hassan said: 'The burning of al-Buwayra spread, and it was of little consequence to the nobles of Banu Lu'ayy.'"],[5844,"Your appointed term is but in comparison to the appointed term of the nations that came before you like the time between the afternoon prayer and sunset. Your example and the example of the Jews and Christians is like that of a man who employed workers and said: 'Who will work for me until midday for one qirat?' The Jews worked until midday for one qirat. Then he said: 'Who will work for me from midday until the afternoon prayer for one qirat, one qirat?' The Christians worked. Then he said: 'Who will work from the afternoon prayer until sunset for two qirats, two qirats? Indeed, you are the ones who work from the afternoon prayer until sunset for two qirats, two qirats, so you will have the reward twice.' The Jews and Christians became angry and said: 'We have worked more but received less.' He said: 'Have I wronged you in anything of your due?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'That is My bounty which I give to whomever I will.'"],[5845,"The Messenger of God ﷺ held a horse race. He sent the horses that had been specially trained from al-Hafya, and their course was up to Thaniyyat al-Wada'. He also held a race between horses that had not been specially trained, and their course was from Thaniyyat al-Wada' to the mosque of Banu Zurayq. He said: And he informed me that Abdullah used to race with them."],[5846,"Umar b. al-Khattab dedicated a horse for the sake of God. The Messenger of God ﷺ mounted a man on that horse. Umar found him selling it, so Umar said to the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'The one you mounted on the horse, I found him selling it. Should I buy it, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'Do not buy it and do not take back your charity.'"],[5847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said: 'If it is solid, take it and what is around it; if it is melted – or liquid – do not eat it.'"],[5848,"You should use black seed, for in it is a cure for every disease except death."],[5849,"There will come people – or there will be people – who will lead you in prayer. If they complete it, then it is for them and for you; if they fall short, then it is against them and for you."],[5850,"May Allah destroy the Jews! They took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."],[5851,"Indeed, the likeness of the mujāhid in the path of Allah—and Allah knows best who truly strives in His path—is like the likeness of one who fasts, who is devoted, humble, bowing, and prostrating."],[5852,"If you say to your companion, 'Be quiet,' on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon, you have engaged in idle talk."],[5853,"Whoever becomes Muslim upon something, it belongs to him."],[5854,"An ant bit one of the prophets, so he ordered the ant village to be burned. Then Allah revealed to him: 'Because an ant bit you, you destroyed a community among the communities that glorifies Allah?'"],[5855,"Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Muthanna b. al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Amr b. Shu'ayb, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5856,"Allah will seize the earth on the Day of Resurrection and fold the heavens in His Right Hand, then He will say: 'I am the King. Where are the kings?'"],[5857,"An ant bit one of the prophets, so he ordered the ant village to be burned. Then Allah revealed to him: 'Because an ant bit you, you burned a community among the communities that glorifies Allah?!'"],[5858,"When you carry (a bier), walk quickly, for the leg is bound and the hand is shackled."],[5859,"Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it. And recite if you wish: 'and extended shade.'"],[5860,"Let none of you say: 'My soul has become vile.' Rather, let him say: 'My soul has become weary.'"],[5861,"When Allah wills good for a servant, He grants him understanding of the religion. And he said: I am only a distributor, and Allah is the One who gives."],[5862,"This community will act according to the Book of Allah for a time, then it will act according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah for a time, then it will act according to opinion. When they act according to opinion, they have gone astray and led others astray."],[5863,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque, except the Sacred Mosque."],[5864,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a funeral and said the takbeer, then placed his right hand upon his left hand."],[5865,"When you say to your companion, 'Listen,' while the imam is delivering the sermon, you have engaged in idle talk."],[5866,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam after two rak'ahs. Dhu al-Shimalayn b. 'Abd 'Amr b. Nadlah, a man from Khuza'ah and an ally of Banu Zuhrah, said to him: 'Has the prayer been shortened, or have you forgotten, O Messenger of Allah?' He replied: 'It has not been shortened, and I have not forgotten.' Dhu al-Shimalayn said: 'Some of that has occurred, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to those who had prayed with him and said: 'Is Dhu al-Yadayn telling the truth?' They said: 'Yes.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and completed the prayer, and he did not perform the two prostrations that are made for doubt in the prayer when the people prompted him."],[5867,"Some people recited with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a prayer in which he recited aloud. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he turned to them and said: 'Did anyone recite with me?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I say, what is the matter with me that I am contended with in the Quran?'"],[5868,"I traveled with the Prophet ﷺ, and with Abu Bakr and 'Umar. All of them prayed two rak'ahs from the time they left Madinah until they returned to it, while traveling and while staying in Makkah."],[5869,"When one of you wakes up from sleep, he should pour water over his hands three times before inserting them, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[5870,"Whoever enters a horse between two others hoping that it will be beaten, there is no good in it. And whoever enters a horse between two others not hoping that it will be beaten, there is no harm in it."],[5871,"O Abu Hurayra, be scrupulous and you will be a devoted worshiper. Avoid what is forbidden and you will be ascetic. Be good to your neighbor and you will be a Muslim. Love for people what you love for yourself and you will be a believer."],[5872,"Whoever is appointed to the judiciary, it is as if he has been slaughtered without a knife."],[5873,"When one of you is afflicted with judging between the Muslims, let him not judge while he is angry; let him treat them equally in looking, seating, and gesture, and let him not raise his voice over either of the two litigants."],[5874,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, mentioning Madinah: There will be conquests, and there will be people wandering with their clans, and Madinah is better for them, if only they knew."],[5875,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My wife has given birth to a black boy. He said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors? He said: Red. He said: Is there among them a grey one? He said: Among them there is a grey one. He said: How did that come to it? He said: Perhaps a vein stirred it. He said: And this one, perhaps a vein stirred him."],[5876,"Some men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: We are people who stay in the sand, and we become junub—and among us are menstruating women and women in postnatal bleeding—and we find no water for four months or five months. The Prophet ﷺ said: You must use the earth."],[5877,"When the heat becomes intense, cool down the prayer, for intense heat is from the blast of Jahannam. The Fire complained to its Lord and said: My Lord, one part of me has consumed another, so He permitted it to breathe twice: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. So it is the most intense heat you experience and the most intense cold you experience."],[5878,"Five are part of the fitra: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, trimming the moustache, clipping the nails, and plucking the armpit hair."],[5879,"When the Prophet ﷺ raised his head from the final rak'a in the Fajr prayer, he said: O God, save al-Walid b. al-Walid, Salama b. Hisham, 'Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'a, and the weak ones in Makkah. O God, tighten Your grip on Mudar and make it on them years like the years of Yusuf. Then he fell prostrate."],[5880,"When the imam recites: 'not of those who earned wrath nor of those who went astray,' and the imam says Amin, then say Amin, for the angels say Amin upon his supplication. Whoever's Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his previous sins are forgiven."],[5881,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque."],[5882,"A bedouin urinated in the mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that a bucket of water or a pail of water be poured over his urine, and said: You have been sent as facilitators, not as make-things-difficult people."],[5883,"The Hour will not come until the son of Maryam descends as a just judge and an equitable imam; he will kill the pig, break the cross, the jizya will be lifted, and wealth will overflow until no one accepts it."],[5884,"The Hour will not come until you fight a people whose sandals are hair."],[5885,"No fara' and no 'atira in Islam."],[5886,"Do not undertake a journey except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and the Aqsa Mosque."],[5887,"When Kisra is destroyed, there will be no Kisra, and when Qaysar is destroyed, there will be no Qaysar. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will certainly be spent in the cause of Allah."],[5888,"No Muslim loses three children and then enters the Fire, except for the fulfillment of the oath."],[5889,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment?' He said, 'Does every one of you have two garments?' Then Abu Hurayra said to the man who asked him, 'Do you know Abu Hurayra? He used to pray in a single garment while his clothes were placed on the peg.'"],[5890,"A resident may not sell on behalf of a bedouin."],[5891,"Umar passed by Hassan while he was reciting poetry in the mosque and glanced at him. Hassan said, 'I used to recite poetry in it when there was someone better than you in it.' Then he turned to Abu Hurayra and said, 'I ask you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Respond on my behalf; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit?' He said, 'O Allah, yes.'"],[5892,"A man from Banu Fizara came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'My wife has given birth to a black boy.' He said, 'Do you have camels?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What are their colors?' He said, 'Red.' He said, 'Is there any gray among them?' He said, 'Yes, there are gray ones among them.' He said, 'How did that come to them?' He said, 'Perhaps some vein pulled it.' He said, 'And this one, perhaps some vein pulled it.'"],[5893,"Do not practice najash, and none of you should sell over the sale of his brother, nor propose over his proposal, and a man should not bargain over the bargain of his brother, and a resident should not sell on behalf of a bedouin, and a woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty her plate and to be married; for her provision is from Allah."],[5894,"A questioner asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'May a man pray in a single garment?' The Messenger of Allah said, 'Does every one of you have two garments?'"],[5895,"A man would come to Abu Hurayra asking his ruling about praying in a single garment, and he would say, 'Do you know Abu Hurayra?' The man would say, 'He is you.' He would say, 'I pray in a single garment, and my garment is indeed placed on the peg.'"],[5896,"Hospitality is three days; whatever is beyond that is charity."],[5897,"The worst food is the food of a wedding feast; the rich are invited and the poor are left out. Whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ."],[5898,"ʿUyayna b. Ḥiṣn al-Fazārī came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and saw him kissing Ḥasan and Ḥusayn. He said, \"Do you kiss him, O Messenger of God? I have had ten children and have never kissed any of them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.\""],[5899,"Whoever catches one rakʿa of the ʿaṣr prayer before the sun sets, and one rakʿa of the ṣubḥ prayer before the sun rises, has caught it."],[5900,"While I was asleep, I saw in what is seen two bracelets of gold, and their affair distressed me. He said: While I was asleep, it was revealed to me: Blow on them. So I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as two liars who would emerge. One of them was al-ʿAnsī, the man of Ṣanʿāʾ, and the other was Musaylima."],[5901,"The dead person is punished by the weeping of the living."],[5902,"People whose hearts are like the hearts of birds will enter Paradise."],[5903,"Disputing about the Qurʾān is disbelief."],[5904,"A person's debt, when he dies, remains attached to him until it is paid on his behalf."],[5905,"When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand; for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."],[5906,"Whoever assists in killing a Muslim with even half a word will meet God on the day he meets Him with written on his forehead: 'Despairing of God's mercy.'"],[5907,"There is no ruler—or he said: prophet—but he has two inner circles: an inner circle that commands him to what is right and forbids him from what is wrong, and an inner circle that spares no effort to corrupt him. Whoever is protected from its evil is protected."],[5908,"After me there will be caliphs who act according to what they know and do what they are commanded. And after me there will be caliphs who act according to what they do not know and do what they are not commanded. Whoever denounces them is free, and whoever restrains his hand is safe, but whoever is pleased and follows—!"],[5909,"When a judge passes judgment and strives his utmost and is correct, he gets two rewards; and when he passes judgment and strives his utmost and errs, he gets one reward."],[5910,"Three things are incumbent upon a Muslim: visiting the sick, attending funerals, and saying \"May Allah have mercy on you\" to the one who sneezes when he praises Allah."],[5911,"When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him make it an odd number."],[5912,"When a slave steals, sell him, even for an uqiyyah. An uqiyyah is forty dirhams."],[5913,"Let one of you consider what he wishes for, for he does not know what will be recorded for him concerning his wish."],[5914,"Allah has cursed women who visit graves frequently."],[5915,"The imam is only appointed to be followed. So when he says the takbir, you say the takbir; when he bows, you bow; when he says, \"Allah hears those who praise Him,\" say, \"Our Lord, to You belongs praise.\" If he prays standing, pray standing; and if he prays sitting, pray sitting, all of you."],[5916,"The Jews split into seventy-one sects, the Christians split into seventy-one - or seventy-two - sects, and my community will split into seventy-three sects."],[5917,"Abu Hind cupped the Prophet ﷺ on the crown of his head. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O assembly of the Ansar, marry Abu Hind and marry your women to him.\" And he said, \"If there is good in anything with which you treat yourselves, it is cupping.\""],[5918,"Affliction does not cease to befall the believing man and the believing woman in their body, wealth, and children until they meet Allah without any sin upon them."],[5919,"The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."],[5920,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we find within ourselves things that we would hate to speak of, and we would rather have everything the sun rises on than to utter them.\" He said, \"Have you found that?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"That is pure faith.\""],[5921,"Do not prevent the maidservants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unperfumed."],[5922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed the smell of garlic in the mosque and said: Whoever eats from this plant should not approach our mosque."],[5923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning the fetus: a slave, male or female, as blood money. He said: The one against whom the ruling was made said: Should compensation be paid for one who did not eat, drink, cry out, or raise its voice? Such a one is to be disregarded. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: This man speaks with the words of a poet. For it there is a ghurra: a slave, male or female."],[5924,"Black seed is a cure for every disease except death. They said: And what is death? He said: Dying."],[5925,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in (Surah) Sad."],[5926,"I am only a human being, and perhaps some of you are more eloquent in argument than others. So whoever I cut off a piece of his brother's property for, I am only cutting off a piece of the Fire for him."],[5927,"Four rivers were made to gush forth from Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile of Egypt, Sayhan, and Jayhan."],[5928,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: Ameen, Ameen, Ameen. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when you ascended the pulpit you said: Ameen, Ameen, Ameen. He said: Gabriel came to me and said: Whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him. Say Ameen. So I said Ameen. And whoever reaches his parents—or one of them—and does not treat them kindly, then dies and enters the Fire, may Allah distance him. Say Ameen. So I said Ameen. And whoever I am mentioned in his presence and he does not invoke blessings upon you, then dies and enters the Fire, may Allah distance him. Say Ameen. So I said Ameen."],[5929,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: O Messenger of Allah, we find within ourselves something that we would not like to speak of, and indeed we have everything the sun rises upon. He said: Have you found that? They said: Yes. He said: That is pure faith."],[5930,"The best of you are those who are best to my family after me."],[5931,"The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday: on it Adam was created, on it he was admitted to Paradise, and on it he was expelled from it."],[5932,"The most virtuous of the believers in faith are those with the best character, and the best of you are those who are best to their women."],[5933,"Muhammad b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us with something similar."],[5934,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Fatima: Move to Umm Sharik, and do not miss us with yourself."],[5935,"Do not call the grapevine 'al-karm', for al-karm is the heart of the believer."],[5936,"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[5937,"God's anger was severe upon a people who cracked the egg on the head of their Prophet while he was calling them to God."],[5938,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard a man say: 'I am the son of noble elders.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, the noble son of the noble son of the noble son of the noble is Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim.'"],[5939,"Do not prevent the female servants of God from the mosques of God, and let them go out unperfumed."],[5940,"Among the rights of a Muslim over a Muslim: attending his funeral, returning the greeting, visiting the sick, blessing the sneezer when he praises God, and accepting an invitation."],[5941,"A woman entered the Fire because of a cat which she tied up, neither feeding it nor letting it eat from the vermin of the earth."],[5942,"When half the night—or a third of the night—has passed, He commands a caller who calls out: Is there any supplicant that he may be answered? Is there any asker that he may be given his request? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that he may be forgiven? Is there any repentant that his repentance may be accepted?"],[5943,"until dawn breaks."],[5944,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer and performed it in the dark. Then he prayed the next day and performed it in a little light. Then he said: Where is the one asking about the time of prayer? The time is between these two—yesterday and my prayer today."],[5945,"The least of the people of Paradise in rank is one who makes wishes upon Allah, and He says: 'You shall have that and the like of it with it,' except that when it is said to him: 'You shall have such-and-such,' he says: 'All of that is for me?' He said: 'And the like of it is with it.'"],[5946,"When Allah created Paradise and the Fire, He sent Jibril to Paradise and said: 'Go and look at it and at what I have prepared for its people therein.' He said: So he went and looked at it, then returned and said: 'By Your might, I feared that no one would enter it.' Then He sent him to the Fire and said: 'Go and look at it and at what I have prepared for its people therein.' He said: So he went, and behold, its parts were mounting one upon another. He said: 'By Your might, no one who hears of it will enter it.' He said: So He commanded concerning it, and it was surrounded with desires. Then He said: 'Return and look at it and at what I have prepared for its people.' He said: So he looked at it and said: 'By Your might, I feared that no one would be saved except that he would enter it.'"],[5947,"I am only a human being, and perhaps some of you is more eloquent in his argument than another. Whoever I have cut off for him something from his brother's property, then I am only cutting off for him a piece of the Fire."],[5948,"A woman entered the Fire on account of a cat which she tied up, and she did not feed it, nor give it water, nor let it loose to eat from the vermin of the earth."],[5949,"No one endures its hardships and its severity except that I will be an intercessor - or a witness - for him on the Day of Resurrection. And no one leaves it out of aversion to it, except that Allah will replace it with what is better than it. And al-Madinah is better for them, if only they knew."],[5950,"He forbade that nabidh be made in the muzaffat, the dubbaʾ, the hantamah, and the naqir. And he said: 'Every intoxicant is haram.'"],[5951,"The Hour will not come until thirty liars, deceivers emerge, all of them lying about Allah and about His Messenger."],[5952,"The heart of an old man is youthful in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth."],[5953,"Every deed of the son of Adam belongs to him: a good deed is multiplied tenfold up to seven hundred times, except fasting, for it is Mine, and I reward for it; he leaves food and desire, and he leaves drink for his desire for My sake. It is Mine, and I reward for it."],[5954,"Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves dependents, they come to me."],[5955,"He used to lead them in prayer and he would say the takbir whenever he placed his head and raised it. When he finished, he said: 'I am the one among you whose prayer most resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[5956,"I saw Abu Hurayra prostrate in 'When the sky is split asunder,' and when he finished, I said to him: 'You prostrated in a surah in which one does not prostrate?' He said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate in it.'"],[5957,"Satan intercepted me in this prayer place of mine, so I seized him and choked him until I felt the coldness of his tongue on the back of my hand. Were it not for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have been tied up this morning for you to see."],[5958,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every beast of prey with a canine tooth, the mujaththama (animals tied up and shot), and the domestic donkey."],[5959,"I am al-Rahman (the Merciful), and it is the rahim (womb). I derived its name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I will maintain him, and whoever severs it, I will sever him and cut him off."],[5960,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood at al-Hajun in the year of the conquest and said: \"By God, you are the best land of God, and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left. It was not made lawful for anyone before me; it was only made lawful for me for an hour of the day. Then it is sacred from this hour of mine: its trees shall not be cut, its fresh herbage shall not be gathered, and its lost property shall not be picked up except by one who will announce it.\" A man called Shah—whom people claimed was al-Abbas—said: \"O Messenger of God, except for idhkhir (a kind of sweet rush), for it is for our houses and our graves.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Except for idhkhir.\""],[5961,"Saying subhan Allah (glory be to God) is for men, and clapping is for women."],[5962,"When the Negus died, the Messenger of God ﷺ informed them that he had died, so they asked forgiveness for him."],[5963,"The Jews and the Christians do not dye (their grey hair), so differ from them."],[5964,"Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and confuses him until he does not know how many (rak'ahs) he has prayed. Whoever experiences any of that should prostrate twice while sitting."],[5965,"God has not listened to anything as He listens to a prophet chanting the Qur'an."],[5966,"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven. And whoever stands (in prayer) on the Night of Decree out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven."],[5967,"When one of you wakes up from sleep, he should not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[5968,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught (the prayer)."],[5969,"You should use the black seed, for in it is a cure for every disease except death. And death is demise."],[5970,"Verily Satan comes to one of you until he does not know how many (rak'ahs) he has prayed. So when that happens, let him prostrate twice while he is sitting."],[5971,"There will be trials like the winds of summer. The one sitting in them is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking. Whoever seeks them out, they will seek him out."],[5972,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught the prayer."],[5973,"Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught the entire prayer."],[5974,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced to them the death of the Negus on the day he died, and said: 'Ask forgiveness for your brother.'"],[5975,"He used to encourage the standing in prayer during Ramadan without making it obligatory."],[5976,"Do not practice najash (artificially inflating prices)."],[5977,"There is no newborn except that Satan touches him, and he cries out from Satan's touch, except Jesus son of Mary and his mother; for Allah says: 'I seek refuge for her and her offspring from the accursed Satan.'"],[5978,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the Night of Decree. He said: 'I was shown it, then I was made to forget it, and perhaps that is better for them. But seek it in the last ten nights of Ramadan.'"],[5979,"When one of you gets up from his sleep, let him pour water over his hands from his vessel, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[5980,"Among the most beloved of My servants to Me are those who are quickest to break the fast."],[5981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited before dawn, then he recited six rak'ahs, turning in every two rak'ahs to the right and to the left, so we thought that he did two rak'ahs for every seven, and he did not say the salam."],[5982,"The Dajjal will descend upon Khuz and Kirman with eighty thousand, wearing hair sandals and wearing tayalisah, as if their faces were layered shields."],[5983,"Change gray hair and do not resemble the Jews or the Christians."],[5984,"The Jews divided into seventy-one sects, and the Christians divided into seventy-one or seventy-two sects. He said: One of the two groups said: seventy-one, and the other said: seventy-two. And my nation will divide into seventy-three sects."],[5985,"A funeral passed by him and they praised it with good in the merits of good. He said: It became due. Then another passed by him, and they praised it with evil in the merits of evil. He said: It became due. Then he said: You are the witnesses of Allah on the earth."],[5986,"Ghifar, Aslam, Muzaynah, and whoever was from Juhaynah are better than the two allies: Ghatafan and Asad, and Hawazin and Tamim, and below them, for they are the people of horses and fur."],[5987,"Ibrahim circumcised himself at the age of eighty years, and he circumcised with an adze."],[5988,"The right of the neighbor is forty houses, like this, and like this, and like this, to the right and to the left, and in front and behind."],[5989,"Uyaynah b. Hisn entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw him kissing al-Hasan and al-Husayn. He said: Do you kiss them, O Messenger of Allah?! Uyaynah said: I have ten and I have never kissed any of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."],[5990,"A drinker was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Strike him. Among us were those who struck with their garment, and among us were those who struck with their sandal. Some of the people said: May Allah disgrace you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not say that; do not help the Shaytan against him."],[5991,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying while the muezzin was giving the iqamah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Two prayers together?"],[5992,"I drew out for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a shoulder from al-Abbas's pot, and he ate it and stood to pray without performing ablution."],[5993,"Whoever has intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill the animal with him."],[5994,"Whoever catches one rakʿa of the prayer has caught it."],[5995,"The heart of an old man remains young in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth."],[5996,"The lifespans of my ummah are between sixty and seventy, and few of them pass beyond that."],[5997,"Whoever intends evil against the people of Madinah, Allah will dissolve him as salt dissolves in water."],[5998,"I saw Abu Hurayra making this takbīr that you see, so I said to him: O Abu Hurayra, what is this takbīr? He said: It is indeed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5999,"When the muezzin calls, Satan turns his back, passing wind. When the call is finished, he returns. When the iqāma is given, he turns his back, and when it is finished, he returns, until he comes between a man and his own self, saying: Remember such and such, what he had not remembered, until the man does not know whether he prayed three or four. If one of you does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him prostrate twice while sitting."],[6000,"The one who hurries to Jumuʿa is like one who offers a camel; the next is like one who offers a sheep; and the next is like one who offers a bird."],[6001,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt in the night prayer – after saying: Allah hears the one who praises Him – for a month, saying in his qunūt: O Allah, save al-Walīd b. al-Walīd; O Allah, save Salama b. Hishām; O Allah, save ʿAyyāsh b. Abī Rabīʿa; O Allah, save the weak believers; O Allah, tighten Your grip on Muḍar; O Allah, make it years like the years of Yūsuf upon them."],[6002,"I saw Abu Hurayra prostrate in 'When the sky splits open', so I said: O Abu Hurayra, I see you prostrating in 'When the sky splits open'? He said: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate in it, I would not have prostrated."],[6003,"Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven. And whoever stands in prayer on Laylat al-Qadr out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven."],[6004,"Allah is jealous, and the believer is jealous. Allah's jealousy is that a servant should commit what He has forbidden him."],[6005,"Do not go ahead of Ramadan by fasting a day or two before it, unless a man who was already fasting a fast, then let him fast it."],[6006,"There is no prophet, nor governor, but he has two inner circles: an inner circle that commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and an inner circle that does not spare any effort to corrupt him. So whoever is protected from the evil of that one, then he is indeed protected, and he is from the one which overcomes him of the two."],[6007,"Indeed the Jews and the Christians do not dye [their hair], so differ from them."],[6008,"Wine is from these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."],[6009,"Indeed the Jews and the Christians do not dye [their hair], so differ from them."],[6010,"For everything there is sweepings, and the sweepings of the mosque are: 'No, by Allah,' and 'Yes, by Allah.'"],[6011,"Any wailing woman who dies before she repents, Allah will clothe her in a garment of tar and will stand her up before the people on the Day of Resurrection."],[6012,"Whoever swears an oath, then it is as he said: if he says, 'I am a Jew,' then he is a Jew; if he says, 'I am a Christian,' then he is a Christian; and if he says, 'I am a Magian,' then he is a Magian."],[6013,"The believer is guileless and noble, while the wicked is deceitful and vile."],[6014,"The believer is guileless and noble, while the wicked is deceitful and vile."],[6015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in the funeral prayer: 'O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our small and our great. O Allah, whoever You give life to, give him life upon Islam, and whoever You take from us, take him upon faith. O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward and do not lead us astray after him.'"],[6016,"When he prayed over the deceased, he would say: 'O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our small and our great, our male and our female. Whoever You keep alive from us, keep him alive upon Islam, and whoever You take, take him upon faith.'"],[6017,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'The Jews claim that coitus interruptus is the minor infanticide.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The Jews have lied, the Jews have lied. Had God willed to create it, he would not have been able to practice coitus interruptus.'"],[6018,"Affliction will not cease to befall the believing man and the believing woman—in their body, their wealth, and their children—until they meet God with no sin upon them."],[6019,"A previously married woman is not to be married until she gives her consent, and a virgin is not to be married until she is consulted. Her consent is her silence."],[6020,"Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. The likeness of the one who spends on them is like the one who extends his hand in charity."],[6021,"The truest word spoken by the Arabs is the saying of Labid: 'Indeed, everything besides God is false.'"],[6022,"The Quran was revealed in seven modes. Quarreling about the Quran is disbelief—he said it three times—so whatever of it you know, act upon it, and whatever of it you are ignorant of, refer it to its knower."],[6023,"He heard Hassan b. Thabit al-Ansari asking Abu Hurayra to bear witness: 'I adjure you by God, did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: \"O Hassan, respond on behalf of the Messenger of God. O God, support him with the Holy Spirit\"?' Abu Hurayra said: 'Yes.'"],[6024,"The poor among the Muslims will enter Paradise five hundred years before their wealthy."],[6025,"The orphan girl is to be consulted concerning herself; if she remains silent, that is her consent."],[6026,"The fasting person has two joys: a joy in this world when he breaks his fast, and a joy in the Hereafter."],[6027,"Change gray hair, and do not imitate the Jews."],[6028,"Whoever prays six rakʿahs after Maghrib, not speaking any evil between them, it will be counted for him as equal to the worship of twelve years."],[6029,"God has not sent any prophet, nor has there been after him any caliph—I think he said—without his having two close entourages: an entourage that commands him to what is right and forbids him from evil, and an entourage that spares no effort to ruin him. Whoever is protected from the evil has indeed been protected."],[6030,"The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."],[6031,"People will stand for the Lord of the Worlds for the length of half a day of a fifty-thousand-year period, and that day will become easy for the believer like the sun's descent toward setting until it sets."],[6032,"The believer's soul is suspended by his debt until it is paid on his behalf."],[6033,"Would any of you be incapable of taking a rope and gathering firewood, and eating from it and giving charity? That is better for him than asking people, whether they give him or refuse him."],[6034,"An ant bit a prophet among the prophets, so he ordered the ant colony to be burned, and it was burned. Then God revealed to him: 'Because an ant bit you, you destroyed a community among the communities that glorifies Me?'"],[6035,"When he wanted to prostrate, he said the takbir and then prostrated; and when he stood up from the sitting position, he said the takbir and then stood up."],[6036,"He forbade anticipating Ramadan by fasting a day or two before it."],[6037,"A community of the Children of Israel went missing, and it was not known what happened to it. I do not think it is anything but the mouse. Have you not seen that when camel's milk is brought near it, it does not drink, but when sheep's milk is brought near it, it drinks? Abu Hurayra said: I narrated this hadith to Ka'b, and he said: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He asked him repeatedly. Abu Hurayra said: 'Did the Torah descend upon me?'"],[6038,"What do you consider the childless one among you? They said: 'The one who has no child.' He said: 'No, rather it is the one who has no child who has preceded him in death.'"],[6039,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man supplicating with both his fingers together and forbade him, saying: 'With one of them, with the right one.'"],[6040,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade riba in exchange: the dirham for two dirhams. And Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman also forbade it."],[6041,"A prostitute saw a dog on a hot day circling a well, its tongue lolling from thirst, so she drew water for it with her leather sock, and she was forgiven."],[6042,"When one of you is invited, let him respond; if he is fasting, let him pray, and if he is not fasting, let him eat."],[6043,"Had ten of the Jews followed me and believed in me, every Jew would have submitted."],[6044,"Whoever eats out of forgetfulness or drinks out of forgetfulness, it is only provision that Allah has provided for him."],[6045,"Ibrahim did not lie except for three lies, all of them for the sake of Allah: his saying, 'Indeed, I am ill,' and his saying, 'Rather, the biggest of them did this.' And the Prophet ﷺ said: Ibrahim ﷺ went out traveling in the land of a tyrant among the tyrants, and with him was Sarah, and she was among the most beautiful of women. It reached that tyrant that in your land there is a man with a woman the like of whom no onlooker has seen more beautiful. So he sent for him, and he came to him, and he asked him about the woman, 'Who is the woman who is with you?' He said, 'My sister.' He said, 'Then send her to me.' So he sent a messenger with him to her. He came to her and said, 'This tyrant asked me about you, and I told him that you are my sister—and you are my sister in Islam—and he asked me to send you to him. So go to him, for Allah will protect you from him.' He said: So she went to him with his messenger. When he brought her before him, he lunged at her but was held back from her. He said to her, 'Call upon your God whom you worship to release me, and I will not return to what you dislike.' So she called upon Allah and He released him. He did that three times. Then he said to the one who brought her, 'Take her away from me, for you have not brought me a human; you have brought me a she-devil.' He gave her Hagar as a servant. She returned to Ibrahim, and he asked her to give Hagar to him, so she gave her to him."],[6046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Bilal, and he brought out to him heaps of dates. He said, 'What is this, O Bilal?' He said, 'Dates that I have stored up, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Were you not afraid that you would hear a bubbling for them in Jahannam? Spend, Bilal, and do not fear any decrease from the Owner of the Throne.'"],[6047,"He used to distribute sheep among his companions from the charity; a sheep would fall between two men, and one of them would say, 'Leave your share to me so that I may marry with it.'"],[6048,"When one of you is in his prayer and a need arises for him, then glorification is for men and clapping is for women."],[6049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to pray while placing his hand on his waist."],[6050,"A woman entered the Fire because of a cat that she tied up; she neither fed it nor gave it water, nor let it eat from the insects of the earth until it died in its tether."],[6051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while we were disputing about destiny. He became angry until his face turned red, as if pomegranate seeds had been burst upon his face. Then he turned to us and said, 'Were you commanded with this? Was I sent to you for this? Indeed, those before you perished only when they disputed about this matter. I adjure you not to dispute about it.'"],[6052,"What do you count as the childless among you? They said: The one who has no child. He said: Rather, it is the one who has no child who has preceded him."],[6053,"He prostrated in “When the sky splits open,” as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and one better than them, and he prostrated in “Read in the name of your Lord,” as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and one better than them."],[6054,"Do not swear by your fathers, nor by your mothers, nor by rivals, and do not swear by Allah unless you are truthful."],[6055,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled regarding the sheep with milk retained in its udder: when a man buys it and milks it, he has the choice to keep it or return it, along with a saa‘ of dates."],[6056,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled that injury caused by a beast is without liability, that damage from a mine is without liability, that damage from a well is without liability, and that a fifth is due on buried treasure."],[6057,"A man was forgiven for removing a branch from the road."],[6058,"Insulting a believer is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[6059,"A man called out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Can one of us pray in a single garment? He said: If Allah has granted you abundance, then be generous to yourselves: a man may gather his garments upon himself, pray in a waist-wrap and a cloak, in a waist-wrap and a shirt, in trousers and a short robe, in trousers and a cloak, in under-trousers and a short robe—and I think he said: in under-trousers and a cloak."],[6060,"Aslam, Ghifar, and part of Muzayna and Juhayna—or part of Juhayna—and Muzayna are better in the sight of Allah—I think he said: on the Day of Resurrection—than Asad, Ghatafan, Hawazin, and Tamim."],[6061,"On Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim stands praying, asking Allah for good, but He grants it to him. And he gestured with his hand, indicating its brevity and insignificance."],[6062,"People will keep asking about knowledge until they say: Allah created us, so who created Allah? He said: He was holding a man’s hand and said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. A man asked me about it, and this is the second—or two men, and this is the third."],[6063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade exchanging a dirham for two dirhams, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[6064,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'I was fasting and I ate and drank forgetfully.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'God fed you and gave you drink, then He enabled you to fast.'"],[6065,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted (reciting) the poetry of the pre-Islamic era, except the ode of Umayya b. Abi al-Salt about the people of Badr, and the ode of al-A'sha in mentioning Amir, and 'Alqama."],[6066,"The mouse is a Jew, and it does not drink the milk of camels."],[6067,"The mouse is a metamorphosed creature, and the sign of that is that it drinks the milk of sheep and does not drink the milk of camels."],[6068,"The best of the people of the east are 'Abd al-Qays."],[6069,"Name yourselves after me, but do not use my kunya."],[6070,"A prophet among the prophets was on a military expedition. He sat under a tree and an ant stung him. When he departed, he ordered that what was under the tree be burned. Then God revealed to him: 'Why not just one ant?'"],[6071,"Whoever buys a sheep that has been kept from being milked (musarra) has the option for three days. If he wishes, he may return it along with a sa' of dates, not wheat."],[6072,"Do not revile time (al-dahr), for God is time."],[6073,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by al-Baqi' and saw a woman crouching over a grave weeping. He said to her: 'O servant of God, fear God and be patient.' She said: 'O servant of God, I am bereaved and childless.' He said: 'O servant of God, fear God and be patient.' She said: 'O servant of God, if you had been afflicted you would excuse me.' He said: 'O servant of God, fear God and be patient.' She said: 'O servant of God, you have made me hear; go away from me.' The Messenger of God ﷺ went on. A man from his companions followed him and stood by the woman and said to her: 'What did the departing man say to you?' She said: 'He said such and such to me.' He said: 'Do you know him?' She said: 'No.' He said: 'That was the Messenger of God ﷺ.' She sprang up quickly, saying: 'I will be patient, I will be patient, O Messenger of God?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Patience is at the first shock, patience is at the first shock.'"],[6074,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with a sick son of hers and said: 'O Messenger of God, supplicate to God to cure this son of mine.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: 'Do you have any child who died before?' She said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'In the pre-Islamic era or in Islam?' She said: 'Rather in Islam.' He said: 'A strong shield, a strong shield, a strong shield.'"],[6075,"He has been shielded with a strong shield, whoever has had three children die in Islam."],[6076,"People are mines in good and evil; the best of them in the pre-Islamic era are the best of them in Islam if they gain understanding."],[6077,"Whoever forgets and eats or drinks, let him complete his fast, for Allah has fed him and given him drink."],[6078,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure a fifth is due."],[6079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade meeting caravans."],[6080,"The intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell—or from the blast of the gates of Hell—so cool down the prayer."],[6081,"The injury caused by a beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure a fifth is due."],[6082,"None of you should urinate in stagnant water and then bathe in it."],[6083,"He said to the delegation of Abd al-Qays: I forbid you from using the naqir, the hantam, the dubba, the muzaffat, and the mazada with its mouth cut off, but drink in your waterskin and tie its mouth."],[6084,"He forbade meeting caravans, and if a person meets one and buys, the owner of the goods has the option when he reaches the market."],[6085,"There are no two Muslims between whom three children die before reaching the age of sin, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy towards them. He said: It will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise,' and they will say: 'Until our parents come.' Then it will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise, you and your parents.'"],[6086,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?' He said: 'That you give charity while you are healthy and miserly, fearing poverty and hoping for life; and do not delay until it reaches the throat, and you say: \"For so-and-so this much, and for so-and-so this much,\" and it has already become for so-and-so.'"],[6087,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir in prayer, he remained silent for a short while before reciting the Quran. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, what do you say during your silence between the takbir and the recitation?' He said: 'I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced the east from the west; O Allah, purify me from my sins as a white garment is purified from dirt; O Allah, wash me from my sins with water, snow, and hail.'"],[6088,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Who is most deserving of my good companionship? He said: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your father."],[6089,"Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck that bellows, saying: O Messenger of God, and I say: I cannot avail you anything against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep on his neck that bleats, saying: O Messenger of God, and I say: I cannot avail you anything against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck that neighs, saying: O Messenger of God, and I say: I cannot avail you anything against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul on his neck that cries out, saying: O Messenger of God, and I say: I cannot avail you anything against God; I have conveyed to you. And let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with silent wealth on his neck, saying: O Messenger of God, and I say: I cannot avail you anything against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any one of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with scraps of cloth fluttering on his neck, saying: O Messenger of God, and I say: I cannot avail you anything against God; I have conveyed to you."],[6090,"The first group to enter Paradise will be in the image of the moon on the night when it is full, and those who follow them will be in the image of the most radiant shining star in the sky in brilliance. They will not urinate, defecate, or blow their noses. Their combs will be of gold, their sweat will be musk, their incense burners will be aloeswood, and their spouses will be the wide-eyed houris. Their character will be of one nature, in the image of their father Adam, sixty cubits tall in the sky."],[6091,"The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its west. When it has risen and the people see it, all who are on it will believe, but that is when a soul's faith will not benefit it if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."],[6092,"I and Abu Hurayra entered a house being built in Madinah for Sa'id – or for Marwan. He said: Abu Hurayra performed ablution and washed his hands until he reached his armpits, and washed his feet until he reached his knees. I said: What is this, O Abu Hurayra? He said: It is the limit of adornment. He said: And he saw a painter painting in the house, and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God Almighty said: And who is more unjust than one who goes to create as I create! Let them create a grain, and let them create an atom."],[6093,"Whoever asks people for their wealth in order to increase it is only asking for embers, so let him take little or much."],[6094,"Beware of continuous fasting – three times. They said: O Messenger of God, you fast continuously. He said: You are not like me in that; I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. Take on of deeds what you are able to."],[6095,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, here is Khadija coming to you with a vessel in which there is condiment, or food, or drink. When she comes to you, convey to her peace from her Lord, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of reeds, in which there is no clamor and no toil."],[6096,"The cat is a wild beast."],[6097,"A woman came with a child of hers and said: O Prophet of God, supplicate to God, supplicate to God, for I have buried three. He said: You buried three? She said: Yes. He said: You have shielded yourself with a strong barrier from the Fire."],[6098,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, tell me who is most deserving of my good companionship? He said: Yes, by your father, you will be told: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Then your father. He said: Tell me, O Messenger of God, about wealth I should give in charity. He said: Yes, by God, you will be told: Give charity while you are healthy and miserly, hoping for life and fearing poverty, and do not delay until when your soul reaches here, and here, you say: My wealth is for so-and-so, and my wealth is for so-and-so, while it is already theirs even if you dislike it."],[6099,"My nation will perish at the hands of this clan of Quraysh. They said: What do you command us? He said: If only the people would keep away from them."],[6100,"A man said: O Messenger of God, which of the people is most deserving of my good companionship? He said: Your mother, then your father, then the next nearest, and the next nearest."],[6101,"Indeed a man may have a station with God that he does not attain by [his] deeds, and God does not cease to test him with what he hates until He brings him to it."],[6102,"Two words are light on the tongue, beloved to the Merciful, heavy in the Balance: Glory be to God and by His praise; glory be to God, the Magnificent."],[6103,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ said the takbir for prayer, he would pause briefly before reciting. I said to him: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, what do you say in this pause of yours between the takbir and the recitation? He said: O God, put between me and my sins a distance as You have put between the east and the west. O God, purify me from my sins as the white garment is purified from dirt. O God, wash me from my sins with snow, water, and hail."],[6104,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us one day and mentioned unlawful withholding of spoils, and emphasized its seriousness. Then he said: O people, let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck that bellows, and he says: O Messenger of God, help me, and I say: I possess nothing for you against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a ewe on his neck that bleats, and he says: O Messenger of God, help me, and I say: I possess nothing for you against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck that neighs, and he says: O Messenger of God, help me, and I say: I possess nothing for you against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a soul on his neck that cries out, and he says: O Messenger of God, help me, and I say: I possess nothing for you against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with patches [of cloth] on his neck that flutter, and he says: O Messenger of God, help me, and I say: I possess nothing for you against God; I have conveyed to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with property on his neck, and he says: O Messenger of God, help me, and I say: I possess nothing for you against God; I have conveyed to you."],[6105,"That a woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a sick son of hers, so that he might supplicate for his healing. The Messenger of God ﷺ began to say: If he dies, may God reward you for him. She said: I have offered three [children] forward in Islam."],[6106,"Indeed the servant may have a lofty station with God that he does not attain by [his] deeds. God does not cease to test him with what he hates until He brings him to it."],[6107,"I entered with Abu Hurayra the house of Marwan, and there were images in it. Abu Hurayra said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God, Mighty and Majestic, said: And who is more unjust than one who creates a creation like My creation? Let them create a speck, or let them create a seed, or let them create a grain of barley."],[6108,"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya."],[6109,"O God, make the provision of the family of Muhammad in this world just enough."],[6110,"O Bilal, what act that you have done do you most hope will benefit you in Islam? Bilal said: I have not done any act in Islam that I more hope will benefit me than that whenever I have purified myself with a purification, by night or by day, I have prayed with that purification for my Lord whatever was ordained for me to pray. He said: Indeed I heard tonight the rustle of your sandals before me in Paradise."],[6111,"Gabriel sat with the Prophet ﷺ, and he looked at the sky, and behold, an angel was descending. Gabriel said to him: This angel has not descended since he was created before this hour. When he descended, he said: O Muhammad, your Lord has sent me to you: [will He make you] a king, or a servant messenger? Gabriel said to him: Be humble before your Lord, O Muhammad. He said: No, rather a servant messenger."],[6112,"Whoever wishes to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[6113,"Dates for dates, wheat for wheat, and salt for salt, like for like. Whoever gives more or asks for more has engaged in riba, except for those whose types differ."],[6114,"I will not cease loving Banu Tamim after three things: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'They are the strongest of my ummah against the Dajjal.' And 'A'ishah had a slave of the children of Isma'il, and captives of Khawlan arrived, so 'A'ishah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I buy from them?' He said: 'No.' When captives of Bal'anbar arrived, he said: 'Buy, for they are the children of Isma'il.' And the sadaqat of Banu Tamim came, and he said: 'These are the sadaqat of our people.'"],[6115,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pronounced the takbir in prayer, he would remain silent between the takbir and the recitation."],[6116,"'Among Allah's servants are servants whom the prophets and martyrs envy.' It was said: 'Who are they? Perhaps we may love them.' He said: 'They are a people who loved one another by the light of Allah without ties of kinship or lineages. Their faces are light upon pulpits of light; they do not fear when people fear, nor do they grieve when people grieve.' Then he recited: 'Verily, the friends of Allah have no fear, nor do they grieve' (Qur'an 10:62)."],[6117,"A prescribed punishment carried out on earth is better than rain for forty mornings."],[6118,"No contagion, no evil omen, no hama, and no safar. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, sometimes a patch of mange appears on the rump or tail of a camel and then spreads to all of it as mange?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who infected the first one? Allah created every creature and decreed its provision, its death, and its appointed term.'"],[6119,"'Uyayna b. Hisn al-Fazari entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw him kissing Hasan or Husayn. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have had ten children and I have never kissed any of them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.'"],[6120,"He heard Wahb addressing the people from the pulpit, saying: 'Preserve from me three things: beware of a followed desire, an evil companion, and a person's admiration of himself.'"],[6121,"'Everything has two ends and a middle. If one end is held, the other tilts; if the middle is held, the two ends are balanced.' And he said: 'Keep to the middle of things.'"],[6122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every beast of prey with fangs, the mujaththama, and the domestic donkey on the day of Khaybar."],[6123,"The Jews split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, the Christians split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, and my ummah will split into seventy-three sects."],[6124,"The Messenger of God ﷺ noticed a smell in the mosque and said, “Whoever has eaten from this foul tree must not enter our mosque.”"],[6125,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out while Aslam were shooting arrows, and he said, “Shoot, sons of Ishmael, for your ancestor was an archer. Shoot, and I am with Ibn al-Adraʿ.” The people then held back their bows and said, “Whoever you are with will win.” He said, “Shoot, and I am with all of you.”"],[6126,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said, “God knows best what they would have done.”"],[6127,"The Fire was shown to me, and I saw in it Ibn Qamaʿa b. Khindif dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to let loose the sāʾiba and alter the covenant of Abraham. The person I have seen who most resembles him is Aktham b. al-Jawn. Aktham said, “O Messenger of God, will his resemblance harm me?” He said, “No, for you are a Muslim and he is an unbeliever.”"],[6128,"Satan confronted me in my prayer, so I seized him by the throat and choked him, and I felt the coldness of his tongue on the back of my hand. Were it not for the supplication of my brother Solomon, he would have been tied up for you to look at.”"],[6129,"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[6130,"He forbade two sales in one sale, two ways of wearing clothes, a man sitting with his legs drawn up while nothing is between him and the sky, and one of you wrapping himself in the ṣammāʾ garment over one of his shoulders."],[6131,"When he intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives, and the lot fell to ʿĀʾisha in the expedition of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq."],[6132,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw an effeminate man who had dyed his feet with henna, and he said, “What is the matter with this one?” It was said, “O Messenger of God, he imitates women.” He said, “So he ordered him, and he was banished to al-Naqīʿ.” They said, “O Messenger of God, shall we kill him?” He said, “I have been forbidden to kill those who pray.”"],[6133,"Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Every weak, humble person in two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid, who, if he swore by God, God would fulfill his oath. Shall I not tell you about the people of the Fire? I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Every coarse, arrogant, haughty person.” I said to Abū Hurayra, “What is jaẓẓ?” He said, “Large-bodied.” I said, “What is jaʿẓ?” He said, “One who considers himself great.”"],[6134,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade nabīdh, pitch-glazed vessels, and gourds."],[6135,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for us, so we came and asked permission."],[6136,"If a man were to fast one day voluntarily and then be given the fill of the earth in gold, he would not receive his full reward for it before the Day of Reckoning."],[6137,"I witnessed Abu Hurayra give a boy the choice between his father and his mother. And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a boy the choice between his father and his mother."],[6138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand and said: Allah created the soil on Saturday, created the mountains in it on Sunday, created the trees on Monday, created the detestable on Tuesday, created light on Wednesday, spread the beasts on Thursday, and created Adam after the afternoon on Friday, the last of creation in the last hour of the hours of Friday."],[6139,"When one of you finishes the tashahhud, let him seek refuge in Allah from four things: from the punishment of Jahannam, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the false messiah, the Dajjal."],[6140,"Fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. If they do that, they have thereby made their blood and their wealth inviolable, except for its right, and their reckoning is with Allah."],[6141,"Indeed, the stray is to be returned."],[6142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the privy, so I brought him water and he performed istinja', wiped his hand with dust, then washed his hand."],[6143,"The angels do not pray for a wailing woman or a lamenting woman."],[6144,"There is no sadaqah due on a Muslim's slave nor on his horse."],[6145,"There is no sadaqah due on horses or slaves except the sadaqah of fitr."],[6146,"Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. But he turned away from him, until he said it four times. When it was the fifth time, he said: You committed adultery? He said: Yes. He said: And do you know what adultery is? He said: Yes, I came to her in a forbidden way, the way a man comes to his wife in a lawful way. He said: What do you seek by this statement? He said: I want you to purify me. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: Did you enter that part of you into that part of her, as the needle disappears into the kohl container and the stick into the thing? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he ordered him stoned, and he was stoned. Then the Prophet ﷺ heard two men, one of them saying to his companion: Did you not see this man? Allah had concealed his sin, but his own self did not leave him until he was stoned like the stoning of a dog. The Prophet ﷺ walked on a little, then passed by the carcass of a donkey and said: Where are so-and-so and so-and-so? Come down and eat from the carcass of this donkey. They said: May Allah forgive you, O Messenger of Allah, is this edible? He said: What you said about your brother earlier is more severe in eating than this. By the One in whose hand is my soul, he is now in the rivers of Paradise, plunging into them."],[6147,"Mercy is not removed except from a wretched person."],[6148,"A wind overtook the people on the road to Makkah while Umar was performing Hajj, and it became severe upon them. He said to those around him: \"What is the wind?\" But nothing came back to him. Then the news of what Umar asked about reached me, so I urged my riding camel until I caught up with him and said: \"O Commander of the Believers,\""],[6149,"Everything has a best part, and the best part of prayer is the first takbir."],[6150,"Regarding His saying: 'On the Day We will call every people with their imam,' he said: \"One of them will be called and given his book in his right hand, his body will be extended for him sixty cubits, his face will be whitened, and a crown of pearl will be placed on his head.\" He said: \"Then he will go to his companions, and they will see him from afar and say: 'O Allah, bring us this one and bless us in this one,' until he comes to them, and he will say: 'Rejoice, for each man among you will have the like of this.' As for the disbeliever, he will be given his book in his left hand, his face will be blackened, his body will be increased sixty cubits over the form of Adam, and he will be made to wear a crown of fire. His companions will see him and say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from the evil of this one. O Allah, do not bring this one to us.' Then he will come to them, and they will say: 'O Allah, keep him back,' and he will say: 'May Allah distance you, for each man among you will have the like of this.'\""],[6151,"Whoever dies ill dies a martyr, is protected from the two trial-givers of the grave, and is provided for morning and evening with sustenance from Paradise."],[6152,"Ibn Abi Rawwad and Muhammad b. Rabi'a al-Kilabi both narrated to me, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Musa b. Wardan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it:"],[6153,"Multiply the testimony that there is no god but Allah before a barrier is placed between you and it."],[6154,"Give gifts and you will love one another."],[6155,"O Banu Qusayy, O Banu Hashim, O Banu Abd Manaf, I am the warner, death is the raider, and the Hour is the appointed time."],[6156,"Fever and headache never cease to afflict the male slave and the female slave, even if they have sins like Mount Uhud, until they leave them with not even the weight of a mustard seed of sins upon them."],[6157,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a man stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how incapable—or he said: how weak—is so-and-so?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have backbitten your companion and eaten his flesh.\""],[6158,"A woman was punished because of a cat which she tied up and did not let it eat from the vermin of the earth until it died."],[6159,"Five phrases: whoever says them, Allah will confirm him as truthful: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner; there is no god but Allah, the King, the Truth, to Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise; there is no god but Allah and Allah is greater; there is no god but Allah and there is no power and no strength except with Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever utters these words in his illness, Allah will forbid him from the Fire.\""],[6160,"When the servant says: 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest,' Allah says: 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me alone.' When he says: 'There is no god but Allah; to Him belongs dominion, and to Him belongs praise,' He says: 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me; Mine is dominion and praise.' He said: When he says: 'There is no god but Allah, and there is no might nor power except with Allah,' He says: 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, and there is no might except through Me.' Abu Ishaq said: Then al-Agharr said something I did not understand. I said to Abu Ja'far: 'What did he say?' He said: 'Whoever is granted these at his death, the Fire will not touch him.'"],[6161,"Allah descends when the last third of the night remains to the lowest heaven every night and says: 'Who complains that I may give him? Who calls upon Me that I may answer him? Who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him?' For that reason they used to prefer the prayer at the end of the night over its beginning."],[6162,"The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of an individual by twenty-five degrees."],[6163,"No Muslim people sit remembering Allah except that the angels surround them, mercy covers them, and tranquility descends upon them."],[6164,"On Friday, at every gate of the mosque there are angels recording the arrivals, first then next. When the imam sits, they roll up the scrolls and come to listen to the remembrance. The likeness of one who comes early is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a ram, then like one who offers a chicken, then like one who offers an egg."],[6165,"No people sit remembering Allah except that the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."],[6166,"No people sit remembering Allah except that the angels surround them, tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."],[6167,"Perform ablution from what fire has cooked."],[6168,"I entered the market one day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He sat with the cloth-sellers and bought a pair of trousers for four dirhams. The market people had a weigher who weighed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Weigh and give more.' The weigher said: 'This is a word I have never heard from anyone.' Abu Hurayra said: I said to him: 'Enough for you of sin and rudeness in your religion that you do not recognize your Prophet!' He threw down the scale and jumped toward the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanting to kiss it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pulled his hand away from him and said: 'What is this? Only the non-Arabs do this with their kings. I am not a king; I am only a man from among you.' He weighed and gave more, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the trousers. Abu Hurayra said: I went to carry them for him, and he said: 'The owner of a thing is more entitled to carry his thing, unless he is weak and unable, in which case his Muslim brother helps him.' He said: I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you wear trousers?' He said: 'Yes, in travel and at home, by night and day, for I was commanded to cover and I found nothing more concealing than it.'"],[6169,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, affirms the servant in five words he says. When he says: 'There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner,' He says: 'My servant has spoken truth.' When he says: 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest,' He says: 'My servant has spoken truth.' When he says: 'There is no god but Allah, and praise belongs to Allah,' He says: 'My servant has spoken truth.' When he says: 'There is no god but Allah; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise,' He says: 'My servant has spoken truth.'"],[6170,"If he says them in his illness and then dies, he will not enter the Fire."],[6171,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."],[6172,"Muhammad said: Salman al-Agharr informed me, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of God ﷺ, the like of this:"],[6173,"I wanted to hire a donkey to Jerusalem, and I saw Abu Hurayra, and he said: Stay close to this mosque of yours, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque, and what is between my house and my pulpit is one of the gardens of Paradise."],[6174,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I am exhausted. So he sent to one of his wives, and she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing but water. Then he sent to another, and she said the like of that, until all of them said the like of that: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing but water. Then he said: Who will host this man tonight? A man from the Ansar stood up and said: I will, O Messenger of God. So he took him to his tent and said to his wife: Do you have anything? She said: No, except the food of my children. He said: Then distract them with something, and when our guest enters, light the lamp and show him that we are eating, and when he reaches for the food, go to the lamp and put it out. He said: So they sat down and the guest ate. When morning came, he went to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: God has marveled at what you two did tonight."],[6175,"Wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, hand to hand, equal weight for equal weight. Whoever adds or asks for addition has committed usury, except what differs in kind."],[6176,"Three things: when they come forth, no soul's faith will benefit it: the beast, the Dajjal, and the rising of the sun from its west."],[6177,"The earth will vomit the lumps of its liver, like columns of silver and gold. The thief will come and say: For this my hand was cut off. The murderer will come and say: For this I killed. The one who severed ties will come and say: For this I cut my kinship. And they will leave it and take nothing from it."],[6178,"Three things: when they come forth, no soul's faith will benefit it if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith: the rising of the sun from its west, the emergence of the Dajjal, and the emergence of the beast."],[6179,"Severe hardship befell me, and I met Umar b. al-Khattab and asked him to help me read a verse of the Book of God. He entered his house and opened it for me. I walked not far and fell on my face from hardship. Then I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ standing at my head, and he said: O Abu Hurayra. I said: At your service, O Messenger of God, at your service. He took my hand, lifted me up, and recognized what was wrong with me. He took me to his tent, ordered a bowl of milk for me, and I drank from it. Then he said: Drink again, O Abu Hurayra. So I drank again. Then he said: Drink again, O Abu Hurayra. So I drank again, until my stomach became full and like a cup. Then I saw Umar and told him what had happened to me, and I said to him: The one who had more right to that than you, O Umar, took care of it. By God, I asked you to read the verses, and I know them better than you. Umar said: By God, if I had brought you in, that would be dearer to me than having red camels."],[6180,"It was said: O Messenger of God, pray against the polytheists. He said: I was not sent as a curser; rather, I was sent as a mercy."],[6181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never gave his family their fill of wheat bread three days in a row until he departed from this world, ﷺ."],[6182,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ and we mentioned the Night of Decree. The Prophet ﷺ said: Which of you remembers our nights at al-Sahba' near Hunayn when the moon rose, looking like the half of a bowl?"],[6183,"A man from the Ansar took a knife while the Prophet ﷺ was in the house of an Ansari, and the Prophet ﷺ said: Beware of the milch animal."],[6184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abu Talib when death came to him: \"Say: There is no god but God; I will intercede for you on the Day of Resurrection.\" He said: \"O son of my brother, were it not that Quraysh would taunt me, I would have brought joy to your eye with it.\" Then it was revealed: You do not guide whom you love."],[6185,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when we heard a loud crash, and we were startled by it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"This is a stone that was thrown into Jahannam seventy autumns ago, and this is when it fell into it, so you heard it.\""],[6186,"\"Gather together, for I will recite to you a third of the Qur'an.\" So they gathered, and he recited to us: Say: He is God, the One, until he completed it. Then he entered. Some of us said: \"The Prophet ﷺ had said: 'I will recite to you a third of the Qur'an,' and he did not recite. This is nothing but news that came to him from heaven.\" He said: Then he came out to us and said: \"It is a third of the Qur'an.\""],[6187,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out one day and came upon Abu Bakr and Umar. He said: \"What brought you two out at this hour?\" They said: \"Hunger.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"And I, by the One who sent me with the truth, nothing brought me out except what brought you out. Get up.\" So they got up with him, and he came to the house of a man from the Ansar, but he was not there; only the woman was. When she saw the Messenger of God ﷺ and his two companions, she said: \"Welcome and greetings.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: \"Where is Abu so-and-so?\" She said: \"He has gone to fetch fresh water for us.\" While they were thus, the Ansari came carrying a waterskin. When he saw the Prophet of God ﷺ and his companions, he said: \"God is greatest,\" then said: \"Praise be to God. I find no people today more honored as guests.\" So he went and cut a bunch of dates for them, containing unripe and ripe dates, and placed it before them. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Why not pick them for us?\" The Ansari said: \"O Messenger of God, choose as you like.\" He took the knife and went. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Beware of the milking animal.\" So he slaughtered for them, and they ate from that bunch and from that sheep, and drank from the water. The Prophet of God said to them: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will surely be asked about this blessing on the Day of Resurrection. Hunger brought you out of your homes, and you did not return until you obtained this. This is part of the blessing.\""],[6188,"A guest once came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he sent to his wives: \"Do you have anything? A guest is with me tonight.\" They sent back to him: \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth, we have nothing but water.\" While he was thus, a man from the Ansar came. The Prophet of God said: \"Do you have anything to take our guest with you tonight?\" The Ansari said: \"Yes, O Prophet of God.\" So he went with the guest. When he reached his home, he said to his wife: \"Do you have anything?\" She said: \"Yes, a loaf of bread we have.\" He said: \"It seems you are fixing the lamp, so extinguish it, and place the bread.\" He began to put his hand with the guest, he and his wife, and they raised their hands to their mouths but did not eat anything. They left the guest and the bread, and he ate it. In the morning, the guest went on his way. The Ansari said: \"My time came for me to go to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he looked at me from afar and said: \"What did you do with your guest last night?\" I thought the guest had complained about me to the Messenger of God, so I said: \"O Messenger of God, I did such-and-such.\" He said: \"Gabriel ﷺ came to me and informed me that your Lord was amazed at what you did with your guest\"—or he said: \"He laughed.\""],[6189,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, this community will not perish until a man stands over a woman and spreads her on the road; then the best of them that day will be the one who says: \"If only you had hidden her behind this wall.\""],[6190,"Prompt your dying ones to say: There is no god but God."],[6191,"The Messenger of God ﷺ slept through the two rak'ahs of Fajr and prayed them after the sun had risen."],[6192,"A man married a woman from the Ansar. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Did you not look at her? For in the eyes of the Ansar there is something.\" He said: \"I did look.\""],[6193,"He forbade a man to bargain over the bargaining of his brother; he forbade najsh; he forbade going out to meet caravans; he forbade a woman to ask for the divorce of her sister; he forbade withholding water for fear of pasture being grazed; he forbade a settled person from selling on behalf of a bedouin. And whoever grants a milking animal, it goes out as charity and returns as charity, its morning drink and evening drink."],[6194,"Whoever walks with a funeral until it is finished has two qirats, and whoever returns before it is finished has one qirat. We said: \"What is a qirat, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"Like Mount Uhud.\""],[6195,"Remember Me in yourself, I will remember you in Myself; and remember Me in an assembly of people, I will remember you in an assembly—meaning better than them."],[6196,"Islam began as something strange, and it will return as something strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."],[6197,"A man said: O Messenger of God, I owe the Hajj of Islam and I have a debt. He said: Then pay off your debt."],[6198,"No servant seeks refuge from the Fire seven times in a day except that the Fire says: O Lord, Your servant so-and-so has sought refuge with You from me, so grant him refuge. And no servant asks God for Paradise seven times in a day except that Paradise says: O Lord, Your servant so-and-so has asked me, so admit him."],[6199,"I asked my Lord for permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, but He did not permit me. And I asked Him for permission to visit her grave, and He permitted me."],[6200,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I am afflicted by hardship. He sent to his wives but found nothing with them. He said: Is there not a man who will host this one tonight? A man stood up and went to his family. He said to his family: This is a guest of the Messenger of God ﷺ, do not hold back anything from him. She said: By God, I have nothing but the food of the children. He said: When the children want dinner, put them to sleep, and come and extinguish the lamp, and we will go hungry tonight. She did so. Then the man went early to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: God has indeed wondered - or: God has laughed - at so-and-so and so-and-so. Then God revealed: \"They give preference over themselves even though they are in need.\""],[6201,"There is no tree in Paradise except that its trunk is of gold."],[6202,"If a man invites his wife to his bed and she does not respond, and she spends the night disobedient, the angels curse her until morning."],[6203,"Three people God will not speak to nor look at on the Day of Resurrection, and they will have a painful punishment: a lying leader, an arrogant poor person, and an old adulterer."],[6204,"Whoever performs Hajj of the House and does not engage in obscenity or wickedness returns as on the day his mother gave birth to him."],[6205,"Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one who is strong and able-bodied."],[6206,"Whoever is protected from the evil of what is between his two jaws and between his two legs will enter Paradise."],[6207,"Whoever purifies himself in his house, then walks to one of the houses of God to fulfill an obligation from the obligations of God, his two steps are: one of them wipes away a sin and the other raises a degree."],[6208,"The adornment of Paradise will reach the extent of the wudu, and that is because Abu Hurayra performed wudu one day, and the wudu reached up to his armpit."],[6209,"The Hour will not come until Allah sends a red wind from the direction of Yemen, and Allah will take away every soul that believes in Allah and the Last Day. What will people find strange about the scarcity of those who die from it: the elder of Banu So-and-so died, the old woman of Banu So-and-so died!"],[6210,"Indeed this ummah is a community that is shown mercy; it will have no punishment except what it inflicts upon itself. He said: I said: How does it punish itself? He said: Was there not punishment on the day of al-Nahar? Was there not punishment on the day of al-Jamal? Was there not punishment on the day of Siffin?"],[6211,"The quickest of Arab tribes to perish is Quraysh, and it is almost certain that a passerby will pass by a sandal and say: This is the sandal of a Qurayshi."],[6212,"There is no harm in omitting the audible glorification or the audible recitation of prayer."],[6213,"Abu Jahl said: Does Muhammad rub his face in the dust among you? They said: Yes. He said: Then by the one we swear by, if I saw that I would surely trample on his neck. He said: So it was said to him: There he is praying. So he went to him, claiming he would trample on his neck. He said: But no sooner did he approach him than he was retreating on his heels and shielding himself with his hands. His companions came to him and said: What is wrong with you, O Abu al-Hakam? He said: Indeed between me and him there is a trench of fire and wings. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: By the one in whose hand is my soul, if he had come near me, the angels would have snatched him away limb by limb. He said: Then Allah revealed: Have you seen the one who forbids a servant when he prays?"],[6214,"We made a night stop with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and we did not wake up until the sun had harmed us. The Prophet ﷺ said: Let each man take hold of his mount's head, then move away from these camps. Then he called for water and performed wudu, then he prostrated twice, then the prayer was commenced."],[6215,"You will come forth with white marks on your faces and limbs from the wudu, the distinguishing sign of my ummah, which no one else has."],[6216,"He forbade the price of a dog and the dowry of a prostitute."],[6217,"Indeed the Children of Israel were governed by their prophets; whenever a prophet passed away, another prophet succeeded him. And indeed there will be no prophet among you. They said: Then what will happen, O Messenger of Allah? He said: There will be caliphs and they will be many. They said: How should we act? He said: Fulfill the allegiance to the first, then the first, and give them their due, for Allah will ask them about what they are responsible for."],[6218,"Three people Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, nor look at them, and they will have a painful punishment: a lying ruler, an arrogant poor person, and an adulterous old man."],[6219,"When a man invites his wife to his bed and she does not come, and he spends the night angry with her, the angels curse her until morning."],[6220,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never found fault with any food. If he desired it, he ate it, and if he disliked it, he left it."],[6221,"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me."],[6222,"God caused those before us to stray from Friday. For the Jews it was Saturday, and for the Christians Sunday. Then God brought us and guided us to Friday. He made Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, and likewise they will follow us on the Day of Resurrection. We are the last in this world, the first on the Day of Resurrection, the ones for whom judgment will be passed on the Day of Resurrection over all creatures. God will gather people on a single plain. When the Garden is brought near, the believers will say, 'Who will open the Garden for us?' They will come to Adam and say, 'O Adam, open the Garden for us.' He will say, 'Did anything expel you from the Garden except the sin of your father Adam? I am not the one for that. Go to your father Ibrahim, the intimate friend of his Lord.' They will come to him and say, 'O Ibrahim, open the Garden for us.' He will say, 'I am not the one for that. I was only an intimate friend from behind a veil. Go to my brother Musa, the one to whom God spoke directly.' They will come to Musa, and he will say, 'I am not the one for that. Go to the word of God and His spirit, Isa.' They will come to him, and he will say, 'I am not the one for that. Go to Muhammad ﷺ.' They will come to Muhammad, and he will ask permission and be granted permission. Then al-Amanah (the Trust) and al-Rahim (the womb) will be sent with him, and they will stand on the two sides of the Sirat, on his right and his left. The first of you will pass like lightning, how quickly will he pass? Then he will return in the blink of an eye. Then he will pass like the wind. Then he will pass like birds. Then like the running of men, their deeds carrying them along. Your Prophet ﷺ will be standing on the Sirat saying, 'Save, save,' until people's deeds fall short. Until a man comes who can only cross crawling. On the edges of the Sirat there are hooked hooks, suspended, commanded to seize whomever they are commanded to seize. So some are saved but scratched, and some are piled into the Fire. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayra, the depth of Jahannam is seventy autumns."],[6223,"Woe to the rulers, woe to the chiefs, woe to the trustees. Some people on the Day of Resurrection will wish that their forelocks were suspended from the Pleiades, dangling between heaven and earth, and that they had never taken on any responsibility."],[6224,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. It was said, 'O Messenger of God, what is the guest's due?' He said, 'Three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity.' Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. And treat women kindly, for woman was created from a rib. The most crooked part of the rib is its top. If you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it, it remains crooked. So treat women kindly."],[6225,"I complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about poor memory. He said, 'Spread open your cloak.' He said, 'So I spread it open.' He said, 'Gather it to yourself.' He said, 'And after that I never forgot anything.'"],[6226,"People have abandoned saying 'Amin.' When the Messenger of God ﷺ recited 'not of those who have incurred anger, nor of those who have gone astray,' he would say 'Amin' so that the first row could hear him."],[6227,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to begin the recitation with 'All praise is due to God, Lord of the Worlds.'"],[6228,"Whoever says 'There is no god but God' with certainty will enter the Garden."],[6229,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came bringing a young fat, excellent goat and a young emaciated, inferior sheep. He said, 'O Messenger of God, this is a young emaciated, inferior sheep, and this is a young fat, excellent goat, and it is the better of the two. Shall I sacrifice it?' He said, 'Sacrifice it, for to God belongs the good.'"],[6230,"Whoever recites Ya Sin in a night will wake up forgiven, and whoever recites Ha Mim, the one in which the Smoke is mentioned, on the night of Friday will wake up forgiven."],[6231,"Abu Hurayra met a man in Madinah and said to him, 'It seems you are not from this town.' He said, 'Indeed.' He said, 'Shall I tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, perhaps God will benefit you by it?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The first thing for which the son of Adam will be brought to account is his prayer. God says to His angels: Look at My servant's prayer. If they find it complete, it is recorded for him as complete. If they find that some of it is lacking, He says: Look and see if he has any voluntary prayers. Then his prayer is completed from his voluntary prayers, and the deeds are taken according to that measure.'"],[6232,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things that I will never abandon: witr before sleeping, fasting three days of each month, and the major ablution on Friday."],[6233,"When he sits between her four limbs and then exerts himself, the major ablution becomes obligatory for both of them, even if he does not ejaculate."],[6234,"I was at an estate of mine, and I saw a gathering. I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ is admonishing his companions.' So I inserted my head among the people, and there was the Prophet ﷺ saying: 'A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim'—three times—'he does not wrong him, nor does he forsake him. Godwariness is here,' and he gestured with his hand to his chest."],[6235,"Who will take from what God and His Messenger have prescribed a word or two, or three, or four, or five, and tie them in the corner of his garment and learn them? He said: So I spread out my garment while the Messenger of God ﷺ was speaking, then I gathered it up. I hope that I have not forgotten a single hadith of what the Messenger of God ﷺ said."],[6236,"God does not accept a prayer without purification, nor charity from stolen property."],[6237,"The deeds will be presented on the Day of Resurrection, and the prayer will come and say: 'O Lord, I am the prayer.' Then God, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'You are upon good.' Then charity will come and say: 'O Lord, I am charity.' He will say: 'You are upon good.' Then fasting will come, and the deeds will come in that manner, saying: 'O Lord.' Then, I think he said, Islam will come and say: 'O Lord, You are Peace and I am Islam.' God will say: 'You are upon good. Through you I take today and through you I give.'"],[6238,"Whoever recites Surah al-Dukhan on the night of Friday will wake up forgiven."],[6239,"A time will come upon people when they will consume usury. He said: It was asked, 'O Messenger of God, all of them?' He said: 'Whoever does not consume it among them will be reached by its dust.'"],[6240,"The rider should greet the walker, the walker should greet the sitter, and the few should greet the many."],[6241,"Indeed, a man may utter a word and not think that it reaches where it has reached; with it he will fall into the Fire for seventy autumns."],[6242,"My close friend enjoined upon me three things."],[6243,"Women who seek khulʿ and those who snatch themselves away are the female hypocrites."],[6244,"Indeed Allah loves ease in selling, ease in buying, and ease in settling debts."],[6245,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[6246,"He said: 'Who will take these words from me and act upon them, or teach them to one who will act upon them?' He said: I said: 'I, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Then he took my hand and counted five in it, and said: Avoid what is forbidden, and you will be the most devout of people. Be content with what Allah has allotted for you, and you will be the richest of people. Be good to your neighbor, and you will be a believer. Love for people what you love for yourself, and you will be a Muslim. And do not laugh excessively, for excessive laughter kills the heart.'"],[6247,"A time will come upon people when they will consume usury. They said: 'All people?' or 'All of the people?' He said: 'Whoever does not consume it, some of its dust will reach him.'"],[6248,"If one of you were to gather a bundle of firewood, carry it on his back, and sell it, that would be better for him than asking a man who might give him or refuse him."],[6249,"No one's deeds will admit him to Paradise. They said: 'Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with His mercy.'"],[6250,"Sulayman ﷺ swore an oath that he would go around that night to ninety women, each of whom would give birth to a boy who would fight in the path of Allah. The angel—or his companion—said: 'Say: If Allah wills.' But he forgot. So he went around them, and no woman brought forth anything except one of them, who brought forth half a boy. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If Sulayman had made an exception, he would not have broken his oath, and it would have been a means for him to attain his need.'"],[6251,"Adam and Musa argued. Musa said: 'O Adam, you are our father, and you brought us out of Paradise by your sin.' Adam said to him: 'O Musa, Allah chose you and wrote the Torah for you with His hand. Why do you blame me for a matter Allah decreed for me forty years before He created me?' So Adam confuted Musa."],[6252,"Whoever swears an oath and says: 'If Allah wills,' does not break it."],[6253,"People will be resurrected according to their intentions."],[6254,"You claim that Abu Hurayra narrates many hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah is the appointed time. I was a poor man serving the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the filling of my stomach. The Muhajirun were occupied with trading in the markets, and the Ansar were occupied with looking after their properties. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever spreads his garment will not forget anything he hears from me.' So I spread my garment until he finished his speech, then I gathered it to myself, and I have not forgotten anything I heard from him."],[6255,"If one of your neighbors asks permission to fix a piece of wood in your wall, do not prevent him."],[6256,"The worst of food is the food of a walimah, to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. And whoever does not attend the invitation has disobeyed God and His Messenger."],[6257,"The strong believer is better and more beloved to God than the weak believer, and in each there is good. Be keen on what benefits you, and seek help from God and do not be helpless. And if something befalls you, do not say: 'If only I had done such and such,' but say: 'God has decreed, and what He wills He does.' For 'if only' opens the work of Satan."],[6258,"The crescent was mentioned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'When you see it, fast; and when you see it, break the fast. And if it is obscured from you, then count thirty.'"],[6259,"Whoever is offered fragrant herb should not refuse it, for it is light to carry and pleasant in scent."],[6260,"When you hear the crowing of roosters, they have seen an angel, so ask and desire. And when you hear the braying of a donkey, it has seen a devil, so seek refuge in God from the evil of what it saw."],[6261,"When one of you performs ablution, let him put water into his nose and then blow it out."],[6262,"Excess water should not be withheld to prevent thereby the herbage."],[6263,"The old man remains young in love of two things: love of life and love of wealth."],[6264,"Wealth is not from abundance of goods, but wealth is wealth of the soul."],[6265,"O son of Adam, spend and I will spend on you. And he said: God's right hand is full, ever-flowing, nothing diminishes it, night and day."],[6266,"When one of you looks at someone who has been favored over him in wealth and body, let him look at one who is below him in wealth and body."],[6267,"None of you should pray in a single garment with nothing of it on his shoulder."],[6268,"No one is wounded in the path of God—and God knows best who is wounded in His path—but that he will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound flowing blood: the color is the color of blood, and the smell is the smell of musk."],[6269,"People are followers of Quraysh in this matter: their Muslims are followers of their Muslims, and their disbelievers are followers of their disbelievers."],[6270,"You will find among the worst of people the one with two faces, who comes to these with one face and to those with another face."],[6271,"When one of you begins the day fasting, he must not use obscene language or behave ignorantly. If someone insults him or fights him, let him say, 'I am fasting, I am fasting.'"],[6272,"Do not go out to meet the caravans for trade, and do not tie the udders of camels and sheep. Whoever buys them after that has the better of the two options: if he wishes, he may keep them, or if he wishes, he may return them with a saa' of dates, not wheat."],[6273,"Is there not a man who will lend a milch-camel to a household? It goes out in the morning with evening milk and returns in the evening with evening milk. Its reward is indeed great."],[6274,"We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that every nation ..."],[6275,"Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would have commanded them to delay the Isha prayer and commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer."],[6276,"The Hour will come while a man is milking his milch-camel: the vessel will not reach his mouth before it comes. And while two men are bargaining over a garment: they will not complete the bargain before it comes. And while a man is plastering his cistern: he will not finish before it comes."],[6277,"Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me."],[6278,"A woman must not fast a day other than Ramadan while her husband is present except with his permission."],[6279,"When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face."],[6280,"The food of two suffices three, and the food of three suffices four."],[6281,"I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. Its confirmation is in the Book of God: 'No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort for the eyes as a reward for what they used to do.'"],[6282,"God has ninety-nine names, one hundred less one. Whoever preserves them enters Paradise. He is Odd and loves the odd."],[6283,"Satan ties three knots on the back of the head of any one of you when he sleeps. For each knot he strikes: 'You have a long night ahead, so sleep.' If he wakes up and remembers God, one knot is untied. If he performs ablution, a second knot is untied. If he prays, the knots are all untied. Otherwise, he wakes up foul in spirit and lazy."],[6284,"Seek refuge in God from the punishment of the grave. Seek refuge in God from the trial of the false Messiah. Seek refuge in God from the trial of life and death."],[6285,"When any one of you is invited to food while fasting, let him say: 'I am fasting.'"],[6286,"My mercy has preceded My wrath."],[6287,"If My servant intends a good deed, write it for him as a good deed. If he does it, write it as ten times its like. If he intends an evil deed, do not write it. If he does it, write it as one evil deed. If he leaves it, write it as a good deed."],[6288,"Delaying payment by a rich person is wrongdoing. If any one of you is referred to a wealthy person, let him follow."],[6289,"Whoever catches a prostration of the afternoon prayer or the morning prayer before the sun rises or before it sets has caught the prayer."],[6290,"Excess water is not to be withheld to prevent thereby access to pasture."],[6291,"The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it he was expelled from Paradise, and on it he was returned to it."],[6292,"I was aided by terror, and I was given concise speech, and while I was sleeping I was brought the keys to the treasures of the earth and they were placed in my hand."],[6293,"An excellent charity is a milch camel lent for its milk, or a sheep lent for its milk, which goes forth in the morning with one vessel and returns in the evening with another."],[6294,"While a woman was nursing her son, a rider passed by her as she was nursing him, and she said, 'O Allah, do not let my son die until he becomes like this rider.' The child said, 'O Allah, do not make me like him.' Then he returned to the breast. Then a woman was passed by who was being dragged and with whom the boys were playing, and she said, 'O Allah, do not make my son like her.' The child said, 'O Allah, make me like her.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for the rider, he was a disbeliever. As for the woman, they would say to her, \"You commit adultery,\" and she would say, \"Allah is sufficient for me.\" They would say to her, \"You steal,\" and she would say, \"Allah is sufficient for me.\"'"],[6295,"Paradise and the Fire disputed. The Fire said, 'I have been favored with the arrogant and the tyrants.' Paradise said, 'What is wrong with me that only the weak, the lowly, and the incapable among people enter me?' Allah said to Paradise, 'You are only My mercy; I show mercy through you to whomever I will.' And He said to the Fire, 'You are only My punishment; I punish through you whomever I will. And each of you will have its fill.'"],[6296,"The earth consumes every part of the son of Adam except the coccyx, from which he was created and from which he will be reassembled."],[6297,"You will certainly follow the ways of those nations who were before you, span by span, cubit by cubit, and fathom by fathom, until even if one of them entered a lizard's hole you would enter it. Abu Hurayra said: Recite, if you wish, the Qur'an: 'Like those before you; they were stronger than you in power' to the end of the verse. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, as Persia and Byzantium did?' He said, 'Who are the people except them?'"],[6298,"The Hour will not come until killing increases. They said, 'What is killing, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Killing.' Three times. They said, 'Every year we kill a thousand or two thousand of the polytheists?' He said, 'I do not mean that, but rather that you will kill one another.' They said, 'While we are alive and doing so?' He said, 'Allah will cause the hearts of the people of that time to die just as He causes their bodies to die.'"],[6299,"The likeness of the believer is like a stalk of grain; the winds buffet it until a wind blows upon it and knocks it down."],[6300,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have married off my daughter and I would like you to help me with something.' He said, 'I have nothing, but when tomorrow comes, bring me a wide-mouthed bottle and a branch of a tree.'"],[6301,"When you hear the braying of a donkey, the barking of a dog, or the crowing of a rooster at night, seek refuge in Allah from Satan, for they see what you do not see."],[6302,"There is no hāmah; there is no hāmah."],[6303,"Delay in payment by a rich man is wrongdoing, and if one of you is referred for payment to a wealthy man, let him accept the transfer."],[6304,"The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer."],[6305,"The thief does not steal while he is a believer, and he does not drink wine while he is a believer, and he does not commit adultery while he is a believer."],[6306,"And he does not seize a plunder that the Muslims raise their eyes toward while he is a believer."],[6307,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of Fajr before sunrise has caught Fajr, or two rak'ahs of 'Asr before sunset has caught 'Asr."],[6308,"One of you remains in prayer as long as the prayer detains him, and nothing prevents him from returning to his family except waiting for the prayer."],[6309,"A prophet among the prophets encamped under a tree, and an ant bit him. He ordered his baggage to be taken out from under it, then he ordered it to be burned. It was revealed to him: 'Why not a single ant?'"],[6310,"Leave me with what I have left you. Those before you were destroyed only because of their excessive questioning and their disagreement with their prophets. What I forbid you, avoid it, and what I command you, do as much of it as you can."],[6311,"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah; his parents make him a Jew or a Christian, just as camels are born from a sound beast. Do you sense any defective one? They said: 'What do you think of one who dies?' He said: 'Allah knows best what they used to do.'"],[6312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: 'Ride it.' The man said: 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said: 'Ride it.' The man said: 'It is a sacrificial camel.' He said: 'Woe to you, ride it.'"],[6313,"The injury caused by an animal is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[6314,"If one of you asks his brother to place a piece of wood on his wall, let him do it."],[6315,"The Ansar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, divide the wealth between us and our brothers among the Muhajirun.' He said: 'You will not be denied the provision, and you will share the fruits.' They said: 'We hear and we obey.'"],[6316,"When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."],[6317,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is not a believing man or woman on the face of the earth but I am closer to him. Whichever of you leaves behind a debt or destitute dependants, let him be called to me, for I am his guardian. And whichever of you leaves behind wealth, it goes to his male relatives, whoever they are."],[6318,"O Allah, I make a covenant with You that You will never break. I am only a human being. Whichever believer I strike, revile, harm, or curse, make it a mercy for him, a purification, and a means of nearness by which You bring him close on the Day of Resurrection."],[6319,"Perform the prayer when it is cooler, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."],[6320,"None of you should say 'al-karm' (for grapes), for al-karm is the Muslim man."],[6321,"The space of a whip of one of you in Paradise is better than what is between the heaven and the earth."],[6322,"None of you should sell over the sale of his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother until he marries or gives up."],[6323,"Were it not for the emigration, I would be a man of the Ansar. If the people were to travel through a valley or a mountain pass, and the Ansar traveled through a valley or a mountain pass, I would travel through the valley of the Ansar or the mountain pass of the Ansar."],[6324,"The treasure of one of you will come on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed poisonous snake from which its owner will flee, and it will pursue him and say, 'I am your treasure,' until he puts his finger into its mouth."],[6325,"When the servant of one of you brings him his food, having spared him its heat and its labor, let him say: 'Sit and eat,' or let him take some food for him—and he gestured with his hand, meaning: like this and like this—let him place it in his palm and say: 'Eat these.'"],[6326,"Do not go out to meet the caravans for trade, do not bid against each other to raise the price, none of you should sell over the sale of another, and do not leave the camels and sheep unmilked. Whoever buys them after that has the choice of the two options after milking them: if he is pleased with them, he keeps them, and if he is displeased, he returns them along with a sa' of dates."],[6327,"The Hour will not come until one of you has much wealth and it overflows, until the owner of wealth is concerned about who will accept it from him, and until he displays it and the one to whom he displays it says: 'I have no need of it.'"],[6328,"The Hour will not come until knowledge is taken away, ignorance becomes widespread, tribulations appear, time passes quickly, and killing increases. They said: What is killing, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It is killing, killing."],[6329,"Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at the one who drags his lower garment—or his cloak—out of pride."],[6330,"The imam is only a shield; fighting is done behind him and protection is sought through him. If he commands fear of Allah and is just, he has a reward for that; if he commands otherwise, it is upon him."],[6331,"The imam is appointed only to be followed, so do not differ from him. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' say, 'Our Lord, to You be praise'; when he prostrates, prostrate; and if he prays sitting, pray sitting, all of you."],[6332,"O Banu Abd Manaf, ransom yourselves from Allah. O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, ransom yourselves from Allah. O Umm al-Zubayr, paternal aunt of Muhammad, O Fatimah bt. Muhammad, I cannot avail you anything against Allah. Ransom yourselves from Allah. Ask me of my wealth whatever you wish."],[6333,"When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."],[6334,"Ghifar: may Allah forgive her. Aslam: may Allah grant her peace."],[6335,"Angels take turns among you: angels of the night and angels of the day. They meet at the afternoon prayer and the dawn prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He asks them, though He knows best: 'How did you leave My servants?' They say: 'We came to them while they were praying and left them while they were praying.'"],[6336,"Whoever leads the people in prayer should lighten it, for among them are the sick, the weak, and those with needs. When one of you prays alone, he may lengthen as he wishes."],[6337,"Whoever catches a prostration of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets, or of the dawn prayer before the sun rises, has caught the prayer."],[6338,"Satan ties three knots on the back of the head of one of you when he sleeps. At each knot he strikes and says, 'You have a long night, so sleep.' If he wakes and remembers his Lord, one knot is loosened. If he performs ablution, another knot is loosened. If he prays, the remaining knot is loosened. In the morning he is energetic and good in spirit. If he does not do that, he wakes up foul in spirit and lazy."],[6339,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look on the Day of Resurrection at a man who drags his lower garment out of pride. He said: While a man was walking arrogantly in his two cloaks, pleased with himself, Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he will be sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."],[6340,"Do you see my qiblah here? By Allah, neither your humility nor your bowing is hidden from me, and indeed I see you from behind my back."],[6341,"Do not say 'the vine' (al-karm), for indeed al-karm is the Muslim man."],[6342,"The poor person is not this one who goes around among the people, whom a morsel or a date or two dates turns away. They said, 'Then who is the poor person, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'The one who does not find enough to make him self-sufficient, and whose condition is not noticed so that charity may be given to him, and who does not stand and beg from people.'"],[6343,"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I was on the point of ordering that firewood be gathered, then ordering the prayer and the call to prayer be made, then ordering a man to lead the people in prayer, and then going off to some men and burning their houses down upon them. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if one of you knew that he would find a fat bone or two fine sheep's trotters, he would attend the evening prayer."],[6344,"When a servant loves to meet Me, I love to meet him; and when he dislikes to meet Me, I dislike to meet him."],[6345,"The head of disbelief is towards the east, and pride and arrogance are among the owners of horses and camels—the loud, boorish people of the tents—while tranquility is among the owners of sheep."],[6346,"The imam is only a shield; fighting is done behind him. If he fears Allah and acts justly, he will have a reward for that; but if he commands otherwise, then it will be against him. And the imam is only to be followed."],[6347,"Angels take turns among you: angels at night and angels by day, and they meet together at the afternoon prayer and the dawn prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He asks them—though He knows best—saying, 'How did you leave My servants?' They say, 'We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying.'"],[6348,"Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would command them to use the tooth-stick."],[6349,"Allah's right hand is full, and spending does not diminish it, pouring out abundantly night and day. Have you considered what He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth? Indeed, it has not diminished what is in His right hand. His throne was upon the water, and in His other hand is the balance; He lowers and raises."],[6350,"Delay in payment by a rich man is wrongdoing, and if one of you is referred for payment to a wealthy man, let him accept the transfer."],[6351,"Do not go out to meet caravans for trade, and let none of you sell against the sale of another, and do not bid against each other to raise prices, and let no town-dweller sell on behalf of a desert-dweller, and do not leave camels or sheep unmilked. Whoever buys them after that has the choice of the two options after milking them: if he is pleased with them, he keeps them; if he is displeased, he returns them along with a saa of dates."],[6352,"The strong believer is better, more excellent, and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, and in each there is good. Be keen on what benefits you and do not be helpless. If something overcomes you, then say: “Allah has decreed, and what He wills He does.” Beware of “if,” for “if” opens the work of Satan."],[6353,"Sulayman ﷺ said: “I will surely go around tonight to a hundred women, each of whom will give birth to a boy who will fight in the path of Allah.” The angel said to him: “Say: ‘If Allah wills.’” But he forgot, so he went around to them, and none of them conceived except one woman who came with half a boy. The Prophet ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, had he said ‘If Allah wills,’ every woman among them would have come with a boy who fights in the path of Allah, and it would have been a means for him to attain his need.”"],[6354,"I do not like that a Muslim spend the night in a state of janabah; I fear that if he dies, the angels would not attend his funeral."],[6355,"Our place tomorrow, if Allah wills, is at al-Khayf, the mosque of Banu Kinanah, where they swore together on disbelief."],[6356,"Whoever sees his brother should greet him with salam. If a tree, a wall, or a rock comes between them and then he meets him, he should greet him with salam."],[6357,"And with the same chain, Mu'awiyah b. Salih narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Wahhab b. Bukht, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[6358,"Whoever narrates a hadith and someone sneezes in his presence, it is true."],[6359,"A man should not pray in a single garment with nothing of it on his shoulder."],[6360,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon an old man walking between his two sons, leaning on them. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What is the matter with this old man?” His two sons said: “O Messenger of Allah, he had made a vow.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Ride, O old man, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is in no need of you or your vow.”"],[6361,"A vow does not bring near to the son of Adam anything Allah has not decreed, but the vow coincides with destiny, and by it is extracted from the miser what the miser did not want to give out."],[6362,"Jibril ﷺ commanded me to give sincere counsel."],[6363,"Whoever goes out as a pilgrim and dies, Allah will write for him the reward of a pilgrim until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever goes out as a performer of 'umrah and dies, Allah will write for him the reward of a performer of 'umrah until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever goes out as a warrior in the path of Allah and dies, Allah will write for him the reward of a warrior until the Day of Resurrection."],[6364,"When you enter upon your Muslim brother, eat from his food and do not ask him, and drink from his drink and do not ask him."],[6365,"Whoever glorifies Allah thirty-three times, magnifies Him thirty-three times, praises Him thirty-three times, and says: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful—after the prayer, his sins will be forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea."],[6366,"Would you harm one another in seeing the sun when there is no cloud beneath it? Would you harm one another in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon? They said: No. He said: Thus you will see Him. Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and He will say: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. So those who used to worship the sun will follow the sun, those who used to worship the moon will follow the moon, and those who used to worship false deities will follow the false deities, until this Ummah remains, including its intercessors. The bridge will be set up across the midst of Hell. Then I will be called, and I will be the first to speak. On that day none will speak except the messengers, and the supplication of the messengers on that day will be: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. On the bridge there will be hooks like the thorns of the sa'dan plant. Have you seen the sa'dan? They said: Yes. He said: They are like the thorns of the sa'dan, except that no one knows the extent of their size except Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. They will snatch people according to their deeds. Among them is the believer who will be saved by his deed, and among them is the one who will be recompensed—or a word resembling it that Ibrahim did not memorize—until when Allah finishes the judgment between the servants, He commands the angels to bring out of the Fire whoever did not associate anything with Allah, among those whom Allah wishes to show mercy. They will bring them out and recognize them by the marks of prostration. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden the Fire to consume the marks of prostration. The water of life will be poured upon them—or he said: from the water of life—and they will grow as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood. A man will remain, facing the Fire, saying: O Lord, turn my face away; its wind has scorched me and its smoke has burned me. He will say: Did you see that if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else? He will say: No, by Your might. He will give Allah whatever covenants and pledges He wishes. He will continue supplicating until He turns his face away from the Fire. When he turns his face toward Paradise, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent. Then he will say: O Lord, bring me forward to the gate of Paradise. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: Woe to you—or: Woe to you—O son of Adam, how treacherous you are! Did you not give Me your covenants and pledges that you would not ask Me for anything other than what I gave you? He will continue supplicating until He says: Perhaps if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else. He will give his Lord whatever covenants and pledges He wishes that he will not ask Him for anything else. So He will bring him forward to the gate of Paradise. When he stands at the gate of Paradise, Paradise will open up for him, and he will see what is in it of joy and delight. He will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent. Then he will say: O Lord, admit me to Paradise. He will say: O son of Adam, how treacherous you are! Did you not give Me your covenants and pledges that you would not ask Me for anything other than what I gave you? He will say: O Lord, I do not want to be the most wretched of Your creation. He will continue supplicating and asking Him until it is said to him: Enter Paradise. Then it will be said to him: Wish. He will wish, until Allah reminds him of such and such, until when his wishes are exhausted, He will say: This is for you and the like of it with it. 521 - (6361) - Ata b. Yazid said: Abu Sa'id was with Abu Hurayra, listening to his hadith without rejecting anything from it, until when he said: This is for you and the like of it with it, Abu Sa'id said: This is for you and ten times the like of it. Abu Hurayra said: I did not memorize from his statement except: This is for you and the like of it with it. Abu Sa'id said: I bear witness that I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: It is for you and ten times the like of it. Abu Hurayra said: That is the last man to enter Paradise."],[6367,"Would you harm one another in seeing the sun when there is no cloud beneath it? Would you harm one another in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon? They said: No. He said: Thus you will see Him. Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and He will say: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. So those who used to worship the sun will follow the sun, those who used to worship the moon will follow the moon, and those who used to worship false deities will follow the false deities, until this Ummah remains, including its intercessors. The bridge will be set up across the midst of Hell. Then I will be called, and I will be the first to speak. On that day none will speak except the messengers, and the supplication of the messengers on that day will be: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. On the bridge there will be hooks like the thorns of the sa'dan plant. Have you seen the sa'dan? They said: Yes. He said: They are like the thorns of the sa'dan, except that no one knows the extent of their size except Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. They will snatch people according to their deeds. Among them is the believer who will be saved by his deed, and among them is the one who will be recompensed—or a word resembling it that Ibrahim did not memorize—until when Allah finishes the judgment between the servants, He commands the angels to bring out of the Fire whoever did not associate anything with Allah, among those whom Allah wishes to show mercy. They will bring them out and recognize them by the marks of prostration. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden the Fire to consume the marks of prostration. The water of life will be poured upon them—or he said: from the water of life—and they will grow as a seed grows in the silt carried by a flood. A man will remain, facing the Fire, saying: O Lord, turn my face away; its wind has scorched me and its smoke has burned me. He will say: Did you see that if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else? He will say: No, by Your might. He will give Allah whatever covenants and pledges He wishes. He will continue supplicating until He turns his face away from the Fire. When he turns his face toward Paradise, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent. Then he will say: O Lord, bring me forward to the gate of Paradise. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: Woe to you—or: Woe to you—O son of Adam, how treacherous you are! Did you not give Me your covenants and pledges that you would not ask Me for anything other than what I gave you? He will continue supplicating until He says: Perhaps if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else. He will give his Lord whatever covenants and pledges He wishes that he will not ask Him for anything else. So He will bring him forward to the gate of Paradise. When he stands at the gate of Paradise, Paradise will open up for him, and he will see what is in it of joy and delight. He will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent. Then he will say: O Lord, admit me to Paradise. He will say: O son of Adam, how treacherous you are! Did you not give Me your covenants and pledges that you would not ask Me for anything other than what I gave you? He will say: O Lord, I do not want to be the most wretched of Your creation. He will continue supplicating and asking Him until it is said to him: Enter Paradise. Then it will be said to him: Wish. He will wish, until Allah reminds him of such and such, until when his wishes are exhausted, He will say: This is for you and the like of it with it. 521 - (6361) - Ata b. Yazid said: Abu Sa'id was with Abu Hurayra, listening to his hadith without rejecting anything from it, until when he said: This is for you and the like of it with it, Abu Sa'id said: This is for you and ten times the like of it. Abu Hurayra said: I did not memorize from his statement except: This is for you and the like of it with it. Abu Sa'id said: I bear witness that I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: It is for you and ten times the like of it. Abu Hurayra said: That is the last man to enter Paradise."],[6368,"Whoever glorifies Allah after every prescribed prayer thirty-three times, praises Him thirty-three times, and magnifies Him thirty-three times—that is ninety-nine—and says to complete one hundred: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful, his sins will be forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea."],[6369,"On the bridge there are thorns of the sa'dan. Have you seen the sa'dan?"],[6370,"The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal when he steals while he is a believer, nor does the drinker drink wine when he drinks it while he is a believer."],[6371,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."],[6372,"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."],[6373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for blessing in the pre-dawn meal and in tharid."],[6374,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I am ruined. He said: What is that? He said: I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan. He said: Free a slave. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Sacrifice a camel. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Sit down. A man gave him something, and he said: Give this as charity, for it will suffice for you. He said: No one is more in need of it, O Messenger of Allah, than my family. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought nineteen sa's, or twenty, or twenty-one, and he gave them to him, saying: This is for you and your family."],[6375,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined upon me three things: the witr prayer before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and the two rak'ahs of the forenoon."],[6376,"When one of you performs ablution, let him rinse his mouth and snuff water into his nose, and the ears are part of the head."],[6377,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the stud fee."],[6378,"God has one hundred mercies; He sent down one of them among humans, jinn, beasts, and vermin. By it they show affection to one another, by it they show mercy to one another, by it the beast shows affection to its young. He held back ninety-nine mercies for Himself, with which He will show mercy to His servants on the Day of Resurrection."],[6379,"Whoever learns knowledge by which he seeks the face of God but does not learn it except to obtain by it some worldly gain will not find the fragrance of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection."],[6380,"I was commanded to a town that eats towns: Yathrib, and it is al-Madinah. It expels people as the bellows expels the dross of iron."],[6381,"A dinar for a dinar, no superiority between them."],[6382,"A dinar for a dinar, and a dirham for a dirham, no superiority between them."],[6383,"When God created Adam, He wiped his back, and every soul that would exist until the Day of Resurrection fell from his back. He presented them to Adam, and he saw in the face of every man among them a glint of light. He saw a man among them whose glint pleased him, so he said: Who is this, O Lord? He said: This is one of your descendants; his name is Dawud. He said: And how long is his lifespan, O Lord? He said: Sixty years. He said: Add to him from my lifespan forty years. He said: Then it will be written, sealed, and not altered. He said: When Adam's lifespan reached the forty that he had given to Dawud, the angel of death came to him, and Adam said: There remain of my lifespan forty years. He said: Did you not give them to your son Dawud? He said: So he denied, and his descendants denied; and Adam erred, and his descendants erred; and he forgot, and his descendants forgot. And he saw among them the strong, the weak, the rich, the poor, and the afflicted. He said: O Lord, would you not make them equal? He said: I wanted to be thanked."],[6384,"The poor person is not the one who is turned away by a date or two dates, and a morsel or two morsels; rather the poor person is the one who refrains from asking. Recite, if you wish: 'They do not ask people importunately.'"],[6385,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[6386,"When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the prescribed one."],[6387,"We prostrated with the Messenger of God ﷺ in 'When the sky is split asunder' and 'Recite in the name of your Lord who created.'"],[6388,"He used to prostrate in 'Recite in the name of your Lord' and 'When the sky is split asunder.'"],[6389,"There is no man who preserves knowledge, then is asked about it and conceals it, but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."],[6390,"There will be in the last time people from my community who will narrate to you what neither you nor your fathers have heard, so beware of them and avoid them."],[6391,"A woman passed by whose perfume was wafting strongly, so he said, 'O slave woman of the Compeller, do you intend the mosque?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And for it have you perfumed yourself?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then go back, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No woman goes out to the mosque with her perfume wafting strongly, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept prayer from her until she returns and performs a full bath.'"],[6392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession in the sale of 'araya for less than five wasqs, or in five wasqs."],[6393,"An army will raid this House and they will be swallowed up by the earth at al-Bayda'."],[6394,"The example of one who hears wisdom but narrates the worst of what he hears is like a man who came to a shepherd and said, 'O shepherd, give me a sheep from your flock to slaughter.' He said, 'Go and take hold of the ear of the best of them.' So he went and took hold of the ear of the sheepdog."],[6395,"Allah has pardoned my community for what their souls whisper to them, as long as they do not speak it or act upon it."],[6396,"Allah has pardoned my community for what their souls whisper to them, as long as they do not act upon it or speak it."],[6397,"The Prophet ﷺ went out until he came to the house of Fatimah, and I went out with him. He said, 'Is the little one there?' He said: He waited, and I thought she was putting on him a necklace of beads — or washing him. He said: Then al-Hasan came running, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced him and said, 'O Allah, I love him, so love him, and love the one who loves him.'"],[6398,"The best prayer after the obligatory prayer is the night prayer."],[6399,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined.' He said, 'Woe to you, what is that?' He said, 'I had intercourse with my wife while I was fasting.' He said, 'Free a slave.' He said, 'I cannot find one.' He said, 'Fast two consecutive months.' He said, 'I am not able.' He said, 'Feed sixty poor people.' He said, 'I cannot find.' He said: So a large basket of dates was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Take it and give it in charity.' He said, 'Is there anyone needier than my own household, O Messenger of Allah? By Allah, there is no household between the two lava tracts of al-Madinah more in need of it than mine.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his teeth showed, then said, 'Take it and feed your family, and seek forgiveness from your Lord.'"],[6400,"Every newborn is born upon the natural disposition, and his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian."],[6401,"He was asked: Which prayer is best after the prescribed prayer? And which fast is best after Ramadan? He said: He replied: The best prayer after the prescribed prayer is prayer in the middle of the night, and the best fast after Ramadan is the month of Allah, al-Muharram."],[6402,"Whoever would like Allah to answer him during distress and hardship, let him supplicate often in times of ease."],[6403,"Whoever would like Allah to answer him during distress and hardship, let him supplicate often in times of ease."],[6404,"Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye; and pressed dates are from Paradise, and in them is a cure for poison."],[6405,"He spoke after what he said to Abd al-Qays about vessels, saying: Drink what seems good to you; every person is accountable for his own soul."],[6406,"Truffles are a remnant of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."],[6407,"Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person, nor for one who is strong and able-bodied."],[6408,"Slow down! By Allah, slow down! Were it not for humble youth, bowing old men, suckling infants, and grazing livestock, punishment would have been poured upon you abundantly."],[6409,"There will come upon people a time when a man will be given the choice between incapacity and wickedness. Whoever lives to see that, let him choose incapacity over wickedness."],[6410,"Whoever does not believe in predestination, its good and its evil, I am free of him."],[6411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a funeral with women weeping. Umar b. al-Khattab forbade them, but the Prophet ﷺ said: Leave them, O Ibn al-Khattab, for the soul is stricken, the eye sheds tears, and the covenant is recent."],[6412,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution washing each part three times."],[6413,"The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ disputed about truffles. Some of them said: I consider them the tree that was uprooted from above the ground, having no stability. Others held back. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: Truffles are only from manna, and their water is a healing for the eye. And pressed dates are from Paradise, and they are a healing from poison."],[6414,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to pray witr before I sleep."],[6415,"No prayer for one without ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of God over it."],[6416,"You are the ones with white blazes and white marks on the Day of Resurrection from the traces of ablution. Whoever of you can extend his blaze should do so."],[6417,"When the imam says: 'not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray,' and those behind him say: Amen, and the Amen of the people of heaven and the people of earth meet, God forgives the servant his previous sins. He said: The example of one who does not say Amen is like a man who went on an expedition with a people and they cast lots, and their arrows came out but his arrow did not. He said: Why did my arrow not come out? He said: Because you did not say Amen."],[6418,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is a bad companion, and I seek refuge in You from treachery, for it is a bad inner garment, or: a bad mark."],[6419,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrate in 'When the sky is split open.'"],[6420,"Increase prayers upon me, for your prayers upon me are purification for you. And ask God to grant me the wasila. It was said: O Messenger of God, what is the wasila? He said: The highest degree in Paradise, which none attains except one man among people, and I hope that I am he."],[6421,"Whoever licks honey three licks each month will not be struck by a great affliction."],[6422,"If you say to your companion: 'Listen,' on Friday while the imam is preaching, you have engaged in idle talk."],[6423,"A group of my community will not cease fighting at the gates of Damascus and its surroundings, and at the gates of Jerusalem and its surroundings. The desertion of those who desert them will not harm them, manifest upon the truth until the Hour arises."],[6424,"Let not a believing man hate a believing woman. If he dislikes one trait in her, he is pleased with another."],[6425,"A believer should not hate a believing woman. If he dislikes one trait in her, he is pleased with another."],[6426,"How will you be, O people, when your women become insolent and your young men become wicked? They said: O Messenger of God, will this really happen? He said: Yes, and worse than that. How will you be when you abandon enjoining good and forbidding evil? They said: O Messenger of God, will this really happen? He said: Yes, and worse than that. How will you be when you see evil as good and good as evil?"],[6427,"A mine will appear in the land of Banu Sulaym, called Pharaoh or Pharan—and that, in the tongue of Abu al-Jahm, is near to the same—to which the worst of people will go out. Or: to which the worst of people will be gathered."],[6428,"My father used to pray behind Abu Hurayra in Madinah. He said: His prayer was similar to the prayer of Qays—he completed the bowing and prostration. It was said to Abu Hurayra: Was this how the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ was? He said: Yes, and more concise."],[6429,"Abu Hurayra entered the mosque, and people gathered around him. A young man stood before him and said: I ask you by God, did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever I am the mawla of, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him'? He said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever I am the mawla of, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.'"],[6430,"There was a tree that obstructed the road. A man cut it down and removed it from the road, and he was forgiven."],[6431,"The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, the two feet commit adultery, and the private part confirms that or denies it."],[6432,"Zachariah was a carpenter."],[6433,"If a slave obeys his master and obeys his Lord, he has two rewards."],[6434,"Whoever enters Paradise will enjoy bliss and will not be miserable. His clothes will not wear out and his youth will not fade. In Paradise there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined."],[6435,"A man used to pick up litter from the mosque, and he died. The Prophet ﷺ missed him and said: What happened to so-and-so? They said: He died. He said: Why did you not inform me of him? It was as if they considered his affair insignificant. So he said to his companions: Go and show me his grave. He went and prayed over him, then said: These graves are filled with darkness for their occupants, and God illuminates them for them by my prayer."],[6436,"The servant remains in prayer as long as he is waiting for the prayer. The angels say: O God, forgive him; O God, have mercy on him—until he leaves or breaks wind."],[6437,"Pharaoh drove four stakes into his wife's hands and feet. When they dispersed from her, the angels shaded her. She said: My Lord, build for me a house with You in Paradise, and save me from Pharaoh and his deeds, and save me from the wrongdoing people. Then her house in Paradise was revealed to her."],[6438,"Allah wrote a book before He created creation: My mercy has preceded My wrath."],[6439,"I asked al-Hasan about fasting on Friday. He said: It is prohibited except in consecutive days. He said: Abu Rafi' narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited fasting on Friday except with days before it or after it."],[6440,"I prayed the late night prayer behind Abu Hurayrah, and we prostrated in 'When the sky is split asunder.' When he finished his prayer, I said: Do you prostrate in 'When the sky is split asunder'? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer and prostrated in it, so I will continue to prostrate in it."],[6441,"When one of you is in his prayer, let him not spit toward the qiblah or to his right, but under his left foot. If he cannot, then let him spit into the edge of his garment, then fold one part over the other. Abu Hurayrah said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ folding his garment one part over another."],[6442,"They dig every day until they almost see the rays of the sun, then they say: We will return to it tomorrow. They return and it is as strong as it was. When their time is complete and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wants to send them upon the people, they say: We will return to it, if Allah wills, tomorrow. They return to it as they left it and dig it, or as he said. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The people will flee from them into their fortresses, or as he said. Al-Mu'tamir said: My father said: From Qatadah: They shoot arrows into the sky and they return to them with blood on them, so they say: We have prevailed over the earth and subdued the people of the sky, or as he said. He said: Then Allah sends upon them worms in their necks, and they kill them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Even their beasts grow fat and proud from eating their flesh, or as he said."],[6443,"The believer has two wives, and he can see the marrow of their shins through their clothes."],[6444,"Two men disputed over a sale, and there was no evidence between them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to cast lots over the oath, whether they liked it or not."],[6445,"People are followers of Quraysh: their disbelievers are followers of their disbelievers, and their Muslims are followers of their Muslims."],[6446,"When one of you gets up from his sleep, let him pour water over his right hand three times before he puts it in the vessel, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."],[6447,"While I was sleeping, I saw in my hands two bracelets of gold. Their affair concerned me, so I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as two liars who would emerge after me. It was revealed to me to blow on them, so I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as two liars who would emerge after me. One of them was al-Ansi, the man of San'a', and the other was Musaylimah."],[6448,"The deceased is punished by the weeping of the living."],[6449,"The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and the wine-drinker does not drink wine while he is a believer."],[6450,"The testimony of a Bedouin against a settled town-dweller is not accepted."],[6451,"Indeed, Allah has one hundred mercies: one of them between humankind, the jinn, the wild beasts, and the vermin. Through it they show affection to one another, and through it they show mercy to one another, and through it the wild beast is affectionate to its young. He has delayed ninety-nine mercies by which He will show mercy to His servants on the Day of Resurrection."],[6452,"Part of the excellence of the prayer is the length of the qunūt (supplication while standing)."],[6453,"The pre-dawn meal (saḥūr) is a blessing, tharīd (bread soaked in broth) is a blessing, and the congregation is a blessing."],[6454,"ʿUmar entered the mosque while the Abyssinians were playing, so he rebuked them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave them, for they are the Banū Arfida.”"],[6455,"Two ravenous, hungry wolves among sheep that have scattered, one of them at the head of the flock and the other at its tail, do not hasten the ruin of a man in his religion who loves the honour of this world and its wealth."],[6456,"Would any of you perhaps take to sheep, then stand at the top of a mountain: a mile or two from al-Madīnah? Then the Friday prayer comes and he does not attend the Friday prayer, then the Friday prayer comes and he does not attend the Friday prayer, so his heart is sealed, and he becomes one of the heedless."],[6457,"The nobility of the believer is his piety, his manly virtue is his intellect, his lineage is his religion. Cowardice and daring are innate dispositions that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, places wherever He wills. The coward flees from his own father and mother, while the daring one fights for what he does not care whether it returns him to his family."],[6458,"Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so let not Allah pursue you for His protection. Verily, whoever kills a muʿāhad (one who has a treaty) who has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger has violated the protection of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance can be found from a distance of seventy autumns."],[6459,"Whoever announces a funeral and then turns away from it to his family has a qīrāṭ. If he follows it, he has a qīrāṭ. If he prays over it, he has a qīrāṭ. If he sits until its affair is concluded, he has a qīrāṭ. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The qīrāṭ with Allah is like Mount Uḥud, or greater than Mount Uḥud.”"],[6460,"Every prayer in which the Mother of the Qurʾān (Sūrat al-Fātiḥah) is not recited is defective, defective, defective — not complete."],[6461,"He witnessed a funeral, and Marwan b. al-Hakam prayed over it. Abu Hurayra went until we sat in the graveyard. Then Abu Sa'id came and said to Marwan, \"Show me your hand.\" He gave him his hand, and he said, \"Stand.\" So he stood. Then Marwan said, \"Why did you make me stand?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he saw a funeral, would stand until it passed by. And he said, 'Death is a terror.'\" Marwan said, \"Is he truthful, Abu Hurayra?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What prevented you from telling me?\" He said, \"You were the imam, so you sat, and I sat.\""],[6462,"Yawning is from Satan. So when one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can."],[6463,"When a person dies, his deeds come to an end except from three: continuous charity, knowledge that is benefited from, or a righteous child who supplicates for him."],[6464,"Charity does not diminish wealth, and Allah does not increase a servant through pardon except in honor, and no one humbles himself for Allah except that Allah raises him."],[6465,"The Messiah will come from the direction of the east, his intention being Madinah, until he descends behind Uhud. Then the angels will turn his face toward Syria, and there he will perish."],[6466,"A false oath sells goods but wipes out the profit."],[6467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in a dream as if the Banu al-Hakam were leaping on his minbar and descending. He woke up as if in anger and said, \"What is with me? I saw the Banu al-Hakam leaping on my minbar like the leaping of monkeys.\" He said, \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen laughing heartily after that, until he died ﷺ.\""],[6468,"Cursed is the one who has intercourse with women in their anuses."],[6469,"When he prays and then remains seated in the place where he prayed, the angels do not cease to bless him: 'O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him,' as long as he does not invalidate his ablution or get up."],[6470,"I saw Ja'far b. Abi Talib as an angel flying with the angels with two wings in Paradise."],[6471,"The world is the believer's prison and the disbeliever's paradise."],[6472,"I asked My servant for a loan, but he did not lend to Me. And My servant reviled Me while he did not know; he says, 'Woe to time! Woe to time!' And I am time."],[6473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who delays and the woman who lies about menstruation. As for the one who delays, she is the one who, when her husband desires her, says: “Later, now.” As for the one who lies about menstruation, she is the one who, when her husband desires her, says: “I am menstruating,” but she is not menstruating."],[6474,"The sun has not risen nor set on a day better than Friday. There is no creature but is startled on Friday except these two heavy ones: the jinn and humans. At every gate of the mosque are two angels writing down whoever comes first, then the next, like a man who brings a camel, like a man who brings a cow, like a man who brings a sheep, like a man who brings a chicken or a bird. When the imam comes out, the angels sit and listen to the reminder, and the scrolls are rolled up."],[6475,"Seek—or he said: seek—trustworthiness among Quraysh, for the trustworthy one of Quraysh has merit over the trustworthy one of others, and the strong one of Quraysh has merit over the strong one of others."],[6476,"Whoever finds his exact property with a man who has become bankrupt, he has more right to it than the other creditors."],[6477,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the noblest of people? He said: The most God-fearing of them. They said: It is not about this that we ask you."],[6478,"Whoever comes to this mosque of mine, coming only for good to learn it or to teach it, he is in the position of a warrior in the path of Allah. Whoever comes for other than that is in the position of a man who looks at the goods of another."],[6479,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out an expedition, and they thought highly of the spoils and returned quickly. A man said..."],[6480,"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images. He said: We said: Let us go to Aisha. We informed her of what Abu Talha said. She said: I do not know, but I will tell you what I saw him do. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on one of his expeditions, and I used to await his return. I took a covering we had and hung it over the alcove. When he came back, I stood and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. Praise be to Allah who has honored you, supported you, and dignified you. She said: He raised his head and looked at the covering and did not respond to me. I recognized dislike in his face. He went until he tore down the covering. Then he said: O Aisha, Allah has not commanded us, in what He has provided us, to clothe stones and bricks. She said: I took it and made it into a cushion and stuffed it with palm fiber, and he did not find fault with me for that."],[6481,"If people knew what is in the first row, it would be by drawing lots."],[6482,"I prayed the night prayer with Abu Hurayra, and he recited: “When the sky is split open.” I said to him, and he said: Abu al-Qasim ﷺ prostrated with it, and I was with him. Al-Taymi said: Or he said: I prostrated with it with Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, so I will not cease prostrating with it until I meet Abu al-Qasim ﷺ."],[6483,"Abu Hurayra visited his people, and they brought him thin bread of the first thin bread. When he saw it, he wept. It was said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu Hurayra? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw this with his own eyes at all."],[6484,"Months would pass by the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without a lamp being lit in the house of any of them, nor a fire kindled in it. If they found oil, they anointed themselves with it; if they found fat, they ate it."],[6485,"I was walking with Abu Hurayrah to the mosque, and a perfumed woman passed by him, her scent wafting. He said to her: Where are you going, O slave woman of the Compeller? She said: To the mosque. He said: And for it you have perfumed yourself? She said: Yes. He said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Any woman who perfumes herself for this mosque, intending to go out to it, her prayer will not be accepted until she washes from it as she washes from major ritual impurity."],[6486,"A false oath sells the goods but wipes out the profit."],[6487,"When two people exchange insults, whatever they say is upon the one who initiated it, as long as the one wronged does not transgress."],[6488,"Ubayy b. Ka'b recited to him Umm al-Qur'an, and he said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, God has not sent down in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Criterion anything like it. Indeed it is the Seven Oft-Repeated and the Mighty Qur'an which I have been given."],[6489,"Beware of the two cursers. They said: What are the two cursers, O Messenger of God? He said: The one who relieves himself in the path of the people or in their shade."],[6490,"While a man was walking on a road in a fine garment of his, he was impressed by himself and his fine garment, and the earth swallowed him, and he will keep sinking in the earth until the Day of Resurrection."],[6491,"While a man was walking on a road, he saw a thorny branch and said: By God, I will remove this so that it does not harm anyone of the Muslims. So he removed it, and God forgave him."],[6492,"The five prayers and the Friday prayer to the next Friday prayer are an expiation for what is between them, as long as major sins are not committed."],[6493,"No one of my community endures the hardship and severity of Madinah but that I will be an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection. Or: a witness."],[6494,"Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot take my form."],[6495,"Whoever calls to guidance will have a reward like the rewards of those who follow him, without diminishing their rewards in anything. And whoever calls to misguidance will bear a sin like the sins of those who follow him, without diminishing their sins in anything."],[6496,"One whose neighbor does not feel safe from his harms will not enter Paradise."],[6497,"I was favored above the prophets with six things: I was given the comprehensive words; I was aided with awe; the spoils of war were made lawful for me; the earth was made for me a means of purification and a place of prayer; I was sent to all creation; and with me the prophets were sealed."],[6498,"Mansur b. Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, with his chain of transmission, similarly:"],[6499,"\"Do you know what backbiting is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Mentioning your brother with what he dislikes.\" It was said, \"What if my brother actually has what I say?\" He said, \"If he has what you say, you have backbitten him; and if he does not have it, you have slandered him.\""],[6500,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"My father died and left wealth, but he did not make a will. Will it expiate for him if I give charity on his behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[6501,"Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah will send ten blessings upon him."],[6502,"When one of you supplicates, let him not say, 'O Allah, forgive me if You will.' Rather, let him be resolute and let his desire be great, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not burdened by anything He gives."],[6503,"When the call to prayer is given, do not come to it while running; come to it with tranquility. Whatever you catch, pray; and whatever you miss, complete. For when one of you heads to the prayer, he is in prayer."],[6504,"The sun does not rise or set on a day better than Friday. There is no creature except that it is terrified of Friday, except these two heavy ones: jinn and humans. At every gate of the mosque there are two angels writing the first, then the first. It is like a man who brings a camel, and like a man who brings a cow, and like a man who brings a sheep, and like a man who brings a bird, and like a man who brings an egg. When the imam sits, the scrolls are rolled up."],[6505,"\"Do you know who the bankrupt one is?\" They said, \"The bankrupt one among us is he who has no dirhams or goods.\" He said, \"The bankrupt one of my community is he who comes on the Day of Resurrection with prayer, fasting, and zakat, but he has insulted this one, slandered this one, consumed the wealth of this one, shed the blood of this one, and struck this one. This one will be given from his good deeds, and this one from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before what is owed is settled, their sins will be taken and cast upon him, then he will be cast into the Fire.\""],[6506,"\"When My servant intends a good deed and does not do it, I record it for him as one good deed. If he does it, I record it for him as ten good deeds up to seven hundred times. When My servant intends an evil deed and does not do it, I do not record it against him. If he does it, I record it against him as one evil deed.\""],[6507,"The eyes commit zina, the tongue commits zina, and the feet commit zina; the private part confirms that or denies it."],[6508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the graveyard and said: \"Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people. We, if Allah wills, will join you. I wish we could see our brothers.\" They said, \"Are we not your brothers, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You are my companions. Our brothers are those who have not yet come.\" They said, \"How will you recognize those of your community who have not yet come, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"What do you think: if a man had horses with white blazes and white feet among pure black horses, would he not recognize his own horses?\" They said, \"Of course, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"They will come with white blazes and white marks from the ablution, and I will precede them to the cistern. Indeed, some will be driven away from my cistern as a stray camel is driven away. I will call to them, 'Come here!' but it will be said, 'They changed after you.' Then I will say, 'Away, away!'\""],[6509,"Shall I not point you to that by which Allah erases sins and raises degrees? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Performing ablution thoroughly despite difficulties, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after a prayer. That is the ribat."],[6510,"The Muslim has six rights over another Muslim. He said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When you meet him, greet him with salam; when he invites you, accept his invitation; when he asks you for counsel, give him sincere counsel; when he sneezes and praises Allah, Mighty and Majestic, say yarhamuk Allah (may Allah have mercy on you); when he falls ill, visit him; and when he dies, follow his funeral."],[6511,"A disbeliever and his killer will never be brought together in the Fire, ever."],[6512,"Let none of you say 'my slave' or 'my slave-girl'. All of you are the slaves of Allah and all your women are the slave-women of Allah. But let him say: my boy, my girl, my servant, my maidservant."],[6513,"If the believer knew what punishment is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, no one would covet His Paradise. And if the disbeliever knew what mercy is with Allah, no one would despair of His Paradise."],[6514,"There is no contagion, no hama, no naw', and no Safar."],[6515,"Allah created one hundred mercies. He placed one among His creation and kept back ninety-nine with Himself."],[6516,"Faith is Yemeni, disbelief is toward the east, tranquility is among the owners of sheep, and pride and ostentation are among the boastful owners of horses and camels."],[6517,"The Hour will not come until thirty dajjals appear, each claiming to be the Messenger of Allah; until knowledge is taken away, trials appear, and killing increases. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is killing? He said: Slaughter."],[6518,"There is no disease but that in the black seed there is a cure for it, except death."],[6519,"Rights will certainly be returned to their owners on the Day of Resurrection, even the hornless sheep will be allowed to retaliate against the horned sheep."],[6520,"A Muslim must not outbid his brother, nor propose marriage over his brother's proposal."],[6521,"Hasten to perform good deeds before trials that come like patches of a dark night, when a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, or a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning, selling his religion for a worldly gain."],[6522,"Hasten to perform good deeds before six things: the rising of the sun from its west, or the Dajjal, or the smoke, or the beast, or the death of one of you, or a general calamity."],[6523,"The Hour will not come until the sun rises from its west. When it rises from its west, all people will believe together, but on that day no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith."],[6524,"When two people insult each other, the sin of what they say is on the one who started it, as long as the one wronged does not transgress."],[6525,"The bell is the flute of Satan."],[6526,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a heap of food. He put his hand into it, and his fingers felt moisture. He said, “What is this, O owner of the food?” He said, “It was affected by the sky, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Why did you not put it on top of the food so that people could see it? Whoever deceives us is not of us.”"],[6527,"A man said, “Set the price, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Indeed, God raises and lowers. I hope to meet God while no one has a complaint against me.” Another man said to him, “Set the price.” He said, “I will call upon God, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[6528,"Whoever prays a prayer and does not recite the Opening of the Book (Umm al-Qur’an) in it, it is deficient, it is deficient, it is deficient, not complete."],[6529,"When the Banu Abi al-‘As reach thirty, the religion of God will become corrupted, the wealth of God will be traded among them, and the servants of God will be their slaves."],[6530,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was building the mosque. When the people carried one stone, ‘Ammar would carry two; when they carried one brick, he carried two. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Woe to Ibn Sumayya; the transgressing party will kill him.”"],[6531,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred House."],[6532,"This world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."],[6533,"Whoever sends blessings upon me once, ten good deeds are written for him thereby."],[6534,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about backbiting, so he said: \"That you say about your brother what he dislikes. If you are truthful, then you have backbitten him, and if you are lying, then you have slandered him.\""],[6535,"None of you should say 'my slave' and 'my slave girl,' for all of you are slaves of God and all your women are slave girls of God. Rather, let him say 'my young man,' 'my boy,' and 'my girl.'"],[6536,"Whoever has seen me has seen me, for Satan cannot take my form."],[6537,"The Mother of the Qur'an is among the seven oft-repeated ones that I was given, as if he meant the Prophet."],[6538,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about backbiting. He said: \"Your mentioning your brother with what he dislikes.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, what if what I say is true of my brother?\" He said: \"If it is in him, then you have backbitten him, and if it is not in him as you say, then you have slandered him.\""],[6539,"The sign of a hypocrite is three, even if he fasts, prays, and claims to be a Muslim: when he speaks he lies, when he is trusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks it."],[6540,"My servant committed a sin, and said: 'O Lord, forgive me my sin.' Then the Blessed and Exalted said: 'My servant committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and punishes for sin.' Then he returned and committed a sin, and said: 'O Lord, forgive me my sin.' Then the Blessed and Exalted said: 'My servant committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and punishes for sin. Do what you will, for I have forgiven you.'"],[6541,"Three are all a right upon God to aid: the warrior in the path of God, the mukatab who intends to pay, and the one who marries intending chastity."],[6542,"O God, I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor in the permanent abode, for the neighbor of the desert moves away."],[6543,"Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ was: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, from a supplication that is not heard, from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a soul that is not satisfied.'"],[6544,"A man asked him: 'How many handfuls of water should I pour over my head while I am in a state of major ritual impurity?' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pour three handfuls over his head.' The man said: 'My hair is long.' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ had more hair than you and it was better.'"],[6545,"May Allah have mercy on a servant against whom his brother has a grievance involving honor or property and who seeks to be absolved of it before it is taken from him, when there is no dinar or dirham there. If he has good deeds, some of his good deeds will be taken; if he has no good deeds, they will place upon him some of their sins."],[6546,"When one of you prostrates, he should begin with his knees before his hands, and he should not kneel like a camel kneels."],[6547,"If a slave woman of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes clear, let him flog her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her. Then if she commits adultery again, let him flog her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her. Then if she commits adultery, let him flog her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her. Then if she commits adultery, let him sell her even for a rope."],[6548,"None of you is waiting for anything except wealth that makes one tyrannical, poverty that makes one forget, an illness that corrupts the mind, a death that comes suddenly, or the Dajjal—and the Dajjal is the worst absent thing awaited—or the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter."],[6549,"The arena of deaths is between sixty and seventy."],[6550,"The least of my community are those who reach seventy years of age."],[6551,"When he exerted himself in supplication, he would say: O Ever-Living, O Sustainer."],[6552,"When a matter distressed him, he would look to the sky and say: Glory be to Allah, the Magnificent."],[6553,"When Thumama accepted Islam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to perform the ritual bath and pray two rak'ahs."],[6554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode to the meeting place of the flood channels and said: Shall I tell you of the Dajjal's station from Madinah? He then said: This is his station, meaning Madinah. He will not be able to enter it; at every one of its entrances there is an angel with unsheathed weapon, and the Dajjal will not enter it."],[6555,"Whoever performs the ritual bath on Friday, wears the best of his clothes, goes early in the morning, and hastens until he arrives, then listens and remains silent, will be forgiven what is between him and the next Friday."],[6556,"You will never be able to encompass all people with your wealth, but what will encompass them from you is a cheerful face."],[6557,"How many a fasting person has no share from his fasting except hunger and thirst, and how many a standing person has no share from his standing except sleeplessness."],[6558,"I am the most self-sufficient of partners with regard to association; whoever performs a deed in which he associates another besides Me, I am free of him."],[6559,"I was sent from the best generations of the children of Adam, generation after generation, until I was sent from the generation in which I was."],[6560,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other, except the Sacred Mosque."],[6561,"Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr b. Muhammad b. Amr b. Hazm, from al-Agharr, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of that."],[6562,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ, and his health and vigor pleased him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When did you feel Umm Mildam?\" The bedouin said: \"What is Umm Mildam?\" He said: \"Fever.\" He said: \"What is fever?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"A heat that occurs between the skin and the bone.\" The bedouin said: \"I have no experience with that.\" He said to him: \"Then when did you feel headache?\" He said: \"What is headache?\" He said to him: \"A throbbing that occurs in the temples and the head.\" He said: \"I have no experience with that.\" He said: When the bedouin turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of the Fire, let him look at this one.\""],[6563,"Verily, this Quran has a period of keenness, and people have a period of slackness regarding it. So whoever's slackness is toward moderation, then how good it is; and whoever's slackness is toward turning away, then those are the ruined ones."],[6564,"Abu Basra Humayl b. Basra met Abu Hurayra while he was coming from al-Tur, and said: \"If I had met you before you went to it, you would not have gone to it. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The livers of mounts are struck (i.e., journeys are undertaken) to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque.'\""],[6565,"The Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched an expedition, and they made great booty and returned quickly. A man said: \"O Messenger of God, we have never seen an expedition return quicker, nor with greater booty, than this expedition.\" He said: \"Shall I not tell you of one who returns quicker than it and gains greater booty? A man who performs ablution in his house and perfects his ablution, then goes to the mosque and prays the dawn prayer in it, then follows it with the mid-morning prayer. He has indeed returned quicker and gained greater booty.\""],[6566,"Decline the Quran grammatically and seek out its unusual expressions."],[6567,"We were with Abu Hurayra when al-Hasan b. Ali came and greeted us. We returned the greeting, but Abu Hurayra did not know, so he went on. We said: \"O Abu Hurayra, this is al-Hasan b. Ali; he greeted us.\" He said: He followed him and caught up with him, and said: \"And peace be upon you, O my master.\" He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Verily, he is a master.\""],[6568,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: \"Which people are the most noble?\" He said: \"The most noble of them in the sight of God, Mighty and Majestic, are the most God-fearing of them.\" They said: \"We are not asking you about this, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Then the most noble of people is Yusuf, son of the Prophet of God, son of the Prophet of God, son of the Friend of God.\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then the best of them in the time of ignorance are the best of them in Islam, when they gain understanding.\""],[6569,"There is no sadaqa due on a man for his horse or his slave."],[6570,"Makhul narrated to me, from ʿIrak b. Malik, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[6571,"When one of you intends to greet with salam, let him say: al-salamu ʿalaykum, for Allah is al-Salam (the Source of Peace). Do not begin with anything before Allah."],[6572,"When one of you comes to a gathering, let him greet with salam; and if he rises, let him greet with salam. The first is not more deserving than the last."],[6573,"Sahl narrated to us; al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAjlan, from Saʿid, from Abu Hurayra, something similar, but he did not mention his father."],[6574,"Whoever keeps a horse in the path of Allah out of faith and belief in Allah's promise, its satiety, its drinking, its urine, and its dung will be good deeds in his balance on the Day of Resurrection."],[6575,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a funeral and they praised it with good, and the Prophet ﷺ said: It has become due. Then another funeral was brought past him and they praised it with evil, and the Prophet ﷺ said: It has become due. Then he said: You are Allah's witnesses on earth."],[6576,"There is no guardian of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand bound to his neck until justice releases him or oppression destroys him."],[6577,"There are three whose opponent I am, and whoever I oppose, I will defeat him: a man who gave a pledge in My name then betrayed; a man who sold a free person and consumed the price; and a man who hired a laborer, took full work from him, but did not give him his wage."],[6578,"The imam has been appointed only to be followed. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he raises, raise; when he sits, sit; and when he stands, stand. The imam is a protection and guarantor for the prayer of the people. If he prays it at its proper time and upholds its requirements—I think he said—he will have his reward and the like of their rewards, without diminishing anything from their rewards. But if he does not pray it at its proper time and does not uphold its requirements, he will bear its burden and their burdens, and nothing will be upon them."],[6579,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would seek a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."],[6580,"Allah is al-Salam (the Source of Peace), so do not begin with anything before Him. When it is said: al-salamu ʿalaykum, then say: al-salamu ʿalaykum."],[6581,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has creatures whom He disperses throughout the night as He wills. So tie up your waterskins, close your doors, and cover your vessels, for He does not open a door, nor uncover a covering, nor untie a waterskin tie."],[6582,"Uqbah b. Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Sa'id b. Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah."],[6583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque. Then a man entered and prayed as he had prayed, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned his greeting and said: 'Go back and pray, for you have not prayed,' until he did that three times. The man said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I do not know any other than this, so teach me.' He said: 'When you stand for prayer, say 'Allah is greater,' then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur'an, then bow until you are at ease bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at ease prostrating, then rise until you are standing straight, then do that in all of your prayer.'"],[6584,"Women are married for four things: for their wealth, for their lineage, for their beauty, and for their religion. So win the one with religion, may your hands be dusty."],[6585,"A man from the desert people gifted me a she-camel from his camels, and I compensated him for it with six young she-camels. He spent the day displeased. By Allah, after this day I will not accept a gift except from a Qurayshi, a Thaqafi, a Dawsi, or an Ansari."],[6586,"Allah created Adam from dust, then made him clay, then left him until he became black mud shaped. He created him and formed him, then left him until he became dry clay like pottery. He said: Iblis would pass by him and say: 'You have been created for a tremendous matter.' Then Allah blew into him His spirit. The first thing in which the spirit flowed was his sight and his nostrils, and he sneezed. Allah taught him to praise his Lord. The Lord said: 'Your Lord has mercy on you.' Then Allah said: 'O Adam, go to those people, greet them, and see what they say.' He came and greeted them, and they said: 'And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah.' He returned to his Lord, and He said—though He was most knowing of what they said to him—: 'What did they say to you?' He said: 'O Lord, when I greeted them, they said: And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah.' He said: 'O Adam, this is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants.' He said: 'O Lord, and what are my descendants?' He said: 'Choose My hand, O Adam.' He said: 'I choose the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are right.' Allah spread His palm, and behold, all that would be from his descendants was in the palm of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic. Among them were men with light upon their mouths. There was a man whose light amazed Adam. He said: 'O Lord, who is this?' He said: 'Your son Dawud.' He said: 'O Lord, how much lifespan have you given him?' He said: 'I have given him sixty years.' He said: 'O Lord, complete for him from my lifespan so that his lifespan becomes one hundred years.' Allah did so and made it witnessed. When Adam's lifespan was ending, Allah sent the angel of death to him. Adam said: 'Do I not have forty years remaining from my lifespan?' The angel said: 'Did you not give them to your son Dawud?' Adam denied that, so his descendants deny, and he forgot, so his descendants forget."],[6587,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there any hour of the night or day in which you command me not to pray?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When you have prayed the morning prayer, refrain from praying until the sun has risen, for it rises between the two horns of a devil. Then prayer is witnessed, attended, and accepted until midday. When midday comes, refrain from praying until the sun declines.' He said: 'At that time Hell is stoked, and the intense heat is from the blaze of Hell. When the sun has declined, prayer is attended, witnessed, and accepted until you pray 'Asr. When you have prayed 'Asr, refrain from praying until the sun sets. Then prayer is witnessed, attended, and accepted until you pray the morning prayer.'"],[6588,"The one who eats and is grateful is like the one who fasts and is patient."],[6589,"O people, richness is not from an abundance of worldly goods, but richness is richness of the soul. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives His servant in full what He has decreed for him of provision, so be moderate in seeking. Take what is lawful and leave what is forbidden."],[6590,"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, 'Isa b. Maryam will certainly descend as a just leader and a fair judge. He will break the cross, kill the pig, reconcile between people, remove enmity, and wealth will be offered to him but he will not accept it. Then if he stands at my grave and says: 'O Muhammad,' I will surely answer him."],[6591,"O assembly of women, I have not seen any among those deficient in intellect and religion who more captivate the hearts of intelligent men than you. I have seen that you are the majority of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, so draw near to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, with whatever you can. Among the women was the wife of 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud. She went to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud and told him what she had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she took some jewelry of hers. Ibn Mas'ud said: 'Where are you going with this jewelry?' She said: 'I seek to draw near to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His Messenger ﷺ with it, so that Allah may not make me one of the people of the Fire.' He said: 'Come here, woe to you, give it in charity to me and my children, for we are more deserving of it.' She said: 'No, by Allah, until I take it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' She went to seek permission to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they said: 'This is Zaynab seeking permission, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Which Zaynab is she?' They said: 'The wife of 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud.' He said: 'Give her permission.' She entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I heard a statement from you, and I returned to Ibn Mas'ud and told him. I took some jewelry to draw near to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and to you with it, hoping that Allah will not make me one of the people of the Fire. Ibn Mas'ud said to me: Give it in charity to me and my children, for we are more deserving of it. I said: Until I ask permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Give it in charity to his children and to him, for they are more deserving of it.' Then she said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what about what I heard from you when you stood before us: I have not seen any among those deficient in intellect and religion who more captivate the hearts of intelligent men than you? O Messenger of Allah, what is the deficiency in our religion and our intellect?' He said: 'As for what I mentioned about the deficiency in your religion, it is the menstruation that afflicts you. One of you remains as long as Allah wills without praying or fasting, and that is the deficiency in your religion. As for what I mentioned about the deficiency in your intellect, it is that the testimony of a woman is half of a testimony.'"],[6592,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the angels and the prophets will intercede, until it is said to one of them: 'Whoever has in his heart the weight of a dinar.' Then it will be said: 'Half a dinar.' Then it will be said: 'A carat.' Then it will be said: 'Half a carat.' Then it will be said: 'A barley grain.' Then it will be said: 'A mustard seed.' When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, the Compeller (al-Jabbar) will say: 'The creatures interceded for the creatures, and the mercy of the Creator remains.' He said: Then He will take a handful from Hell and cast it into the River of Life. He said: Then they will grow as vegetation grows. Have you not seen the seed in the torrent's deposit? Whatever of it is exposed to the sun is green, and whatever of it is in the shade is white. They said: 'O Messenger of God, it is as if you were looking at the seed when it sprouts.' He said: Then they will enter Paradise. He said: Then it will be said: 'These are the freed ones of the Merciful (al-Rahman).'"],[6593,"Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah."],[6594,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to trim the mustaches and let the beards grow."],[6595,"Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah."],[6596,"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. His reward is three days; whatever is after that is charity. It is not lawful for him to stay with him until he turns him out."],[6597,"God does not love wasting wealth, nor excessive asking, nor gossip (qil wa qal)."],[6598,"Two men sat with the Messenger of God ﷺ, one of them nobler than the other. The noble one sneezed but did not praise God, so he did not respond to him. The other sneezed and praised God, so he responded to him."],[6599,"Every child of Adam is born upon the natural disposition (fitra), then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."],[6600,"Do what is right, keep close, and rejoice, and seek help in the early morning, the late afternoon, and a portion of the night; and upon you is moderation, and you will reach. And know that none of you is saved by his deeds.' We said: 'Not even you, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'Not even me, unless God, Mighty and Majestic, envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."],[6601,"Five are from the natural disposition (fitra): circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpit hair, trimming the mustache, and clipping the nails."],[6602,"Whoever has a debt, let him pay it to him, or let him seek release from it before he pays it on a day when there is no gold or silver. They said: 'Then with what will he pay it, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'It will be taken from his good deeds; if they suffice, then fine, otherwise some of the other's evil deeds will be cast upon him.'"],[6603,"There are three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: an old man who commits adultery, a lying ruler, and a poor man who is arrogant."],[6604,"When he prayed over a funeral, he would say: O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your servant; he used to testify that there is no god but You, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, and You know him best. If he was a doer of good, increase his good; and if he was a doer of evil, forgive him. Do not deprive us of his reward, and do not cause us to be tempted after him."],[6605,"Wealth is not from an abundance of goods; rather, wealth is the wealth of the soul."],[6606,"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, Allah is happier with the repentance of His servant than one of you is with his stray camel when he finds it in the desert."],[6607,"When My servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; and when he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him running."],[6608,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, whoever fights in the cause of Allah, will he enter Paradise? He said: Yes. He paused for a while as if he had heard something, then asked: Where is the questioner from earlier? The man stood up. The Prophet ﷺ said: What did you say? The man replied: I said: What do you think of one who strives in the cause of Allah and is killed—will he enter Paradise? You said: Yes. The Prophet ﷺ then said: Indeed, Gabriel informed me of that, unless he has a debt."],[6609,"Do not sit in the middle of roads or in courtyards. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot avoid that. He said: If you must, then give them their right. They asked: O Prophet of Allah, what is their right? He said: Returning the greeting, lowering the gaze, saying yarhamuk Allah to the one who sneezes, and guiding the way."],[6610,"Whoever is overcome by vomiting does not have to make up the fast, but whoever makes himself vomit must make it up."],[6611,"We saw Abu Hurayrah performing ablution on the roof of the mosque, so I said: O Abu Hurayrah, from what are you performing ablution? He said: I ate a piece of dried curd. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Perform ablution from that which fire has changed."],[6612,"This wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it—Yahya said: he mentioned something I do not know what it is—will be blessed in it. But many a person wallowing in the wealth of Allah and His Messenger according to his own desires will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[6613,"I was taken up to the lowest heaven, and I did not pass by any heaven except that I found in it my name: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq behind me."],[6614,"If the slave woman of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes clear, he should flog her and not blame her. Then if she commits adultery again, he should flog her the prescribed punishment and not blame her—Sufyan said: meaning he should not reproach her—then if she commits adultery again, he should flog her the prescribed punishment and not blame her. Then if she commits adultery again, he should sell her, even for a rope of hair."],[6615,"Treasure trove: the gold that grows from the earth."],[6616,"When one of you buys a servant, let him take hold of her forelock and say: O Allah, I ask You for the good in her and the good of what You have created her upon. And when he buys a camel, let him take hold of the top of its hump and say the like of that."],[6617,"If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would long for a third; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."],[6618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a leaning wall, so he hastened and said: I dislike the death of suddenness."],[6619,"Whoever is appointed judge among the people has been slaughtered without a knife."],[6620,"There is no commander of ten except he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bound in chains; justice will release him or injustice will destroy him."],[6621,"Abu Hurayrah prayed with us, and he said takbir every time he raised and prostrated. When he finished, he said: This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray with us."],[6622,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar. He said: Spend it on yourself. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your wife. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your child. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Spend it on your servant. He said: I have another dinar. He said: You know best."],[6623,"I had intended to command the use of the tooth-stick with ablution, and to delay the prayer until half the night, or: until a third of the night."],[6624,"Ward off the prescribed punishments as much as you can."],[6625,"I have been permitted to speak of an angel whose feet have pierced the seventh earth, and the Throne is upon his shoulder, and he says: Glory be to You, where were You and where will You be."],[6626,"Whoever is pleased that his lifespan be extended and his provision be expanded, let him maintain his ties of kinship."],[6627,"I entered the house of Marwan with Abu Hurayra, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “That one—and who is more unjust than one who creates a creation?”"],[6628,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was in the mosque and prayed. Then he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” He repeated that three times. Then he said: “O Messenger of God, I do not know how to do anything better than this, so teach me.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “When you intend to pray, say the takbir, then recite whatever is easy for you from the Quran, then bow until you are at ease in bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at ease in prostration, then rise until you are sitting upright, then do that throughout your entire prayer.”"],[6629,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque when a man entered and prayed. The Messenger of God ﷺ began watching him. He prayed, then came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him. The Messenger of God ﷺ returned the greeting and then said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” He went back and prayed, then came to the Messenger of God and greeted him. The Messenger of God returned the greeting and then said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” He did that two or three times. Then he said to him on the second or third occasion: “O Messenger of God, I have exerted myself, so teach me and show me.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “When you intend to pray, perform ablution and do it well, then face the qibla and say the takbir, then recite, then bow until you are at ease in bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at ease in prostration, then rise until you are at ease sitting, then prostrate until you are at ease in prostration, then rise until you are at ease sitting. If you complete your prayer in this manner, you have completed it, and whatever you detract from any of that, you only detract from your prayer.”"],[6630,"Ammar b. Yasir prayed two rak'as and made them very brief. Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith said to him: \"O Abu al-Yaqzan, I see you have made them very brief.\" He said: \"I hastened through them to ward off whispering, and I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'A man prays a prayer and perhaps he receives from it only a tenth, or a ninth, or an eighth, or a seventh, or a sixth'—until he completed the enumeration.\""],[6631,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition to Tabuk and stopped at Thaniyyat al-Wada'. The Messenger of God ﷺ saw lamps and women weeping. He said: \"What is this?\" It was said: \"They have been enjoyed in temporary marriage, and they are weeping.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Marriage, divorce, waiting period, and inheritance have forbidden—or he said: destroyed—mut'a.\""],[6632,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade sitting in courtyards and on elevated paths. The Muslims said to him: \"We cannot avoid that.\" He said: \"If you must, then give them their right.\" They said: \"What is their right?\" He said: \"Returning the greeting, responding to the sneezer when he praises God, Mighty and Majestic, lowering the gaze, and guiding the way.\""],[6633,"God loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. When one of you yawns, he should not say 'ah, ah,' for Satan laughs at him and toys with him."],[6634,"Two men sat with the Messenger of God ﷺ, one of them nobler than the other. The noble one sneezed but did not praise God, so he did not respond to him. The other sneezed and praised God, so he responded to him."],[6635,"There is no leader of ten but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in chains, until justice releases him or injustice destroys him."],[6636,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained about a neighbor of his. The Prophet ﷺ said three times: \"Be patient.\" Then he said to him on the fourth or third time: \"Put your belongings out on the road.\" He did so, and people began passing by him and saying: \"What is the matter with you?\" He said: \"His neighbor has harmed him.\" They began saying: \"May God curse him.\" Then his neighbor came and said: \"Take back your belongings, and I will never harm you again.\""],[6637,"How will you be when you do not collect a dinar or a dirham?\" They said: \"Do you think that will happen?\" He said: \"Yes, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayra, according to the words of the truthful one who was believed.\" They said: \"And why will that happen?\" He said: \"The protection of God and the protection of His Messenger will be violated, so God will harden the hearts of the protected people, and they will withhold what is in their hands.\""],[6638,"I said: \"Have you heard from your close friend a hadith that you can narrate?\" He said: \"Yes, I heard him say: 'There is no contagion, no evil omen, and the best of omens is the good omen. The evil eye is real. The cross will soon be broken, the pig will be killed, and the jizya will be abolished.'\""],[6639,"Gently, by Allah, gently! For were it not for elderly men who bow in prayer, youths who humble themselves, infants who suckle, and grazing livestock, the punishment would have been poured upon you in torrents."],[6640,"The first thing to be raised from this ummah is modesty and trustworthiness, and the last of it to remain is the prayer. It seems to me that he said: There may be people who pray but have no share of good."],[6641,"When this verse was revealed: “Then, on that Day, you shall surely be asked about the bliss” [Q 102:8], they said: O Messenger of Allah, which bliss will we be asked about? Our swords are on our shoulders."],[6642,"Abdullah b. Salima narrated to us: Ash’ath b. Barraz narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abdullah b. Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to this."],[6643,"No Muslim performs ablution and does it well, then walks to one of the houses of Allah and prays an obligatory prayer therein, except that a good deed is written for him for every step, an evil deed is erased from him with another, and with another he is raised a degree."],[6644,"No servant falls ill with an illness except that Allah commands his guardian angels: Whatever evil deed he does, do not record it, and whatever good deed he does, record it as ten good deeds, and record for him from righteous deeds as he used to do while healthy, even if he does not do them."],[6645,"A pledged animal may be ridden and fed, and the milk of a milch animal may be drunk, and the one who drinks it bears the expense and feed."],[6646,"Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits until it is buried has two qirats; the qirat is like Mount Uhud."],[6647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt, and a maternal aunt in addition to her sister’s daughter, and the younger is not to be married over the older, nor the older over the younger."],[6648,"Adam was met by Musa, who said to him: Are you Adam who brought people out of Paradise?"],[6649,"I am the first to raise his head after the final blast, and there is Musa clinging to the Throne, so I do not know whether it was so or after the blast."],[6650,"The believer in his grave is in a garden, and his grave is widened for him by seventy cubits and illuminated for him like the moon on the night of the full moon. Do you see in what was revealed this verse: “Then for him there is a straitened life, and We shall raise him blind on the Day of Resurrection” [Q 20:124]? He said: Do you know what the straitened life is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The punishment of the disbeliever in his grave. By the One in whose hand is my soul, ninety-nine dragons are set upon them. Do you know what a dragon is? He said: Ninety-nine serpents, each serpent with seven heads, which blow upon his body, sting him, and scratch him until the Day of Resurrection."],[6651,"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near: knowledge will decrease and killing will increase. He said: I said: What does 'killing will increase' mean, O Messenger of God? He said: Killing, killing."],[6652,"A man was killed in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ as a martyr. He said: Then a female mourner wept over him and said: Alas, a martyr! He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: Stop! What makes you know that he is a martyr? Perhaps he used to speak about what did not concern him, or was stingy with what would not diminish him."],[6653,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out for Makkah to conquer it. He said to Abu Hurayra: O Abu Hurayra, call out to the Ansar. So he said: O company of the Ansar, answer the Messenger of God. They came as if they had an appointment. He said: Take this road, and let no one appear before you except that you put him to sleep, meaning: you kill him. The Messenger of God ﷺ marched and God granted him victory. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulated the House and prayed two rak'as, then left through the gate adjacent to al-Safa, climbed al-Safa, and addressed the people while the Ansar were below him. The Ansar said to one another: As for the man, compassion for his people and desire for his town have taken hold of him. Then God Almighty sent down revelation to him about what the Ansar had said. He said: O company of the Ansar, do you say: As for the man, compassion for his people and desire for his town have overtaken him? Then who am I? No, by God, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. Indeed, the living is your living, and the dying is your dying. They said: O Messenger of God, we only said that out of fear that you would leave us. He said: You are truthful before God and before His Messenger. By God, there was not one of them but that his chest was wet with tears from his eyes."],[6654,"The lower garment of the believer reaches to mid-calf, and the least of that is to above the anklebones. Whatever is below the anklebones is in the Fire."],[6655,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed dates, and I received five dates and one dry inferior date. He said: I found the dry inferior date to be the hardest of them on my molar."],[6656,"Abu Hurayra was on a journey. When they stopped and the eating mat was laid out, they sent for him while he was praying. He said: I am fasting. When they were about to finish, he came and began to eat. The people looked at their messenger, so he said: What are you looking at? By God, indeed."],[6657,"I am the first for whom the gate of Paradise will be opened, except that a woman will come hastening ahead of me. I will say to her: What is with you? And who are you? She will say: I am a woman who stayed caring for my orphans."],[6658,"Mercy is not removed except from a wretched person."],[6659,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed among us seven dates. We were seven, and he gave us one date each."],[6660,"When God, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam, He wiped his back, and from his back fell every soul He would create until the Day of Resurrection. He placed between the eyes of each person among them a glint of light. Then He presented them to Adam, who said: O Lord, who are these? He said: These are your descendants. He saw a man among them, and the glint between his eyes pleased him. He said: O Lord, who is this? He said: A man from your descendants in the last of the nations, called Dawud. He said: O Lord, how much lifetime have You set for him? He said: Sixty years. He said: Increase him forty years from my lifetime. He said: Then it would be written, sealed, and not changed. When Adam's lifetime ﷺ came to an end, the Angel of Death came to him. He said: Is there not remaining of my lifetime forty years? He said: Did you not give them to your son Dawud? So he denied, and his descendants denied; he forgot, and his descendants forgot; he erred, and his descendants erred."],[6661,"Whoever does not ask God, God is angry with him."],[6662,"The lifespan of my Ummah is between sixty and seventy years."],[6663,"An Umrah to the next Umrah is an expiation for what is between them, and an accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise."],[6664,"The closest a servant is to his Lord is when he is prostrating, so increase supplication."],[6665,"Whoever prays over a funeral receives a qirat, and whoever follows it until it is finished receives two qirats, the smaller of them or one of them is like Uhud."],[6666,"An accepted Hajj has no reward other than Paradise, and an Umrah to the next Umrah or the two Umrahs expiate what is between them."],[6667,"Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who traced it back to the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[6668,"He used to seek refuge from the hardship of affliction, the attainment of misery, an evil decree, and the gloating of enemies."],[6669,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sneezed, he lowered his voice with it and covered his face."],[6670,"Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Messenger of Allah, spreading our hands is difficult for us in prayer, so he ordered them to seek support with their knees."],[6671,"The Hour will not come until a man from my household goes out against them and strikes them until they return to the truth. He said: I said: How long will he be? He said: Five and two. He said: I said: What is five and two? He said: I do not know."],[6672,"Abu Hurayra was on a journey, and when they stopped, the eating mat was placed, and they sat at it."],[6673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: I saw him walking alongside the Prophet ﷺ while a sandal was on its neck."],[6674,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit while he was mentioning the hour that is in Friday, and I saw him closing his fingers and making them few."],[6675,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relating about Musa ﷺ on the pulpit. He said: It occurred in his mind: Does Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sleep? So Allah sent an angel to him and kept him awake for three nights. Then He gave him two glass bottles, a bottle in each hand, and commanded him to guard them. He said: He began to doze and his hands almost met, then he would wake up and hold one over the other until he slept a sleep, and his hands struck together, and the two bottles broke. He said: Allah struck for him a parable that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, if He slept, the heaven and the earth would not hold together."],[6676,"If there were in this mosque a hundred or more, and in it a man from the Fire, and he breathed and his breath struck, the mosque and those in it would burn."],[6677,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while his hand was in my hand, and he came upon a man of shabby appearance. He said: Abu so-and-so? What has brought you to what I see? He said: Sickness and harm, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Shall I not teach you words by which Allah may remove from you sickness and harm? He said: No, it does not please me to have them even if I had witnessed Badr and Uhud with you. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed, then said: And can the people of Badr and the people of Uhud attain what the contented poor person attains? He said: Abu Hurayra said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me. He said: Say, O Abu Hurayra: I have relied on the Living who does not die. Praise be to Allah who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness. And magnify Him with all magnificence. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me when my condition had become good, and said: What is the matter? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not ceased saying the words you taught me."],[6678,"A man said to him: Are you the one who forbids fasting on Friday? He said: No, by the Lord of this building, or this sacred precinct, I did not forbid it. Muhammad ﷺ forbade it."],[6679,"The women of Quraysh are the best women who ever rode camels: the most tender to a child in his infancy and the most careful of a husband in what he possesses. Abu Hurayra said: We say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew that the daughter of Imran did not ride camels."],[6680,"By Allah, for one of you to take a rope and gather firewood, carry it on his back, and eat and give charity is better for him than to come to a man whom Allah has enriched from His bounty and ask him, whether he gives or refuses."],[6681,"Muhammad b. Qudama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar to it."],[6682,"Leave me with what I have left you, and do not ask me about anything. For those before you were destroyed only by their many questions and their disagreements with their prophets. So what I forbid you, avoid it, and what I command you, do as much of it as you can."],[6683,"None of you should breathe into the vessel when he has drunk from it, but if he wants to drink from it, let him move it away, then breathe."],[6684,"The purification of your vessel when a dog has lapped in it is to wash it seven times."],[6685,"When one of you yawns, let him put his hand over his mouth, lest it enter."],[6686,"The Hour will not come until time contracts: a year becomes like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, and a day like the burning of a palm-leaf."],[6687,"Do not make my grave an idol. May God curse a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."],[6688,"Give the hired worker his wage before his sweat dries."],[6689,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled by an oath together with a witness."],[6690,"The gates of Paradise are opened every Monday and Thursday. Suhayl said in his hadith: Then God forgives every servant who does not associate anything with God, except the two who bear mutual rancor. God, Mighty and Majestic, says to His angels: Leave them until they reconcile."],[6691,"When God loves a servant, He says: O Gabriel, I love so-and-so, so love him. Gabriel then says to the inhabitants of heaven: Your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him. Then the inhabitants of heaven love him. And acceptance is placed for him on earth. When He hates someone, it is likewise."],[6692,"When one of you intends to travel, let him greet his brothers, for they increase him in good by their supplication along with his supplication."],[6693,"The one who does the deed of the people of Lut: stone the top and the bottom; stone them both together."],[6694,"The Prophet ﷺ missed a man from his companions. Then he met him and said: Why did I not see you? He said: I did not sleep last night; a scorpion stung me. He said: Had you said when evening came: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created, it would not have harmed you. Ubayd Allah said: I only know that he said in the hadith, raising it: Whoever says it in the evening and in the morning, it will not harm him."],[6695,"They said: O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Do you have difficulty seeing the moon on a full-moon night with no cloud before it? They said: No. He said: Do you have difficulty seeing the sun at midday with no cloud before it? They said: No. He said: By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, you will see Him just as you see them."],[6696,"Two kinds of my community I have not yet seen: women who are clothed yet naked, swaying and causing to sway, with on their heads something like the leaning humps of Bactrian camels. They will not enter Paradise nor find its fragrance, and men who hold whips like the tails of cows, striking the people with them."],[6697,"None of you opens a door of begging for himself except that God opens upon him a door of poverty."],[6698,"Whoever is content with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet has tasted the flavor of faith."],[6699,"When the servant prostrates, seven parts prostrate with him: his face, his two palms, his two knees, and his two feet."],[6700,"Your uncle Abu Talib used to protect you and do for you. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me he would have been in the lowest depth."],[6701,"Abu Talib used to protect you and defend you; have you benefited him with anything? He said: I found him in the depths of the Fire, and I brought him out to the shallow part."],[6702,"O Messenger of Allah, teach me something I may ask of my Lord. He said: Ask your Lord for well-being. Then he waited as long as Allah willed, then said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something I may ask of my Lord. He said: Ask your Lord for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."],[6703,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Husayn b. Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Yazid, from Abd Allah b. al-Harith, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[6704,"The religion will prevail until it crosses the seas, and the seas will be crossed in the path of Allah. Then after you will come peoples who recite the Quran, saying: We have recited the Quran; who among us recites better? Who among us has more understanding? Or who among us has more knowledge? Then he turned to his companions and said: Is there any good in those? They said: No. He said: Those are from you, from this nation, and those are the fuel of the Fire."],[6705,"I was leading Ibn Abbas in the alley of Abu Lahab, and he said: O Kurayb, have we reached such-and-such a place? He said: You are at it now. He said: Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib narrated to me, saying: While I was with the Prophet ﷺ in this spot, a man came swaggering between his two cloaks, looking at his sides, pleased with himself, when Allah caused the earth to swallow him in this place, and he is sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."],[6706,"There is no retaliation for a head wound reaching the brain, nor for a wound piercing the body cavity."],[6707,"He forbade branding on the face. Al-Abbas said: I will only brand on the two haunches."],[6708,"There is no retaliation for a wound piercing the body cavity, nor for a wound that dislodges a bone, nor for a head wound reaching the brain; in them is only the blood money."],[6709,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a tree. The wind blew, and the decayed leaves in it fell, while the green leaves remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What is the likeness of this tree? The people said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Its likeness is the likeness of the believer: when he shivers from fear of Allah, his sins fall from him and his good deeds remain."],[6710,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while his wives were with him, and they veiled themselves from me except Maymunah. A snuff was pounded for him and he was given it orally. He said: 'No one in the house shall remain without being given it orally except al-Abbas, for my right hand did not reach him.' Then he said: 'Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' Aishah said to Hafsah: 'Tell him that when Abu Bakr stands in that place he weeps.' She told him, and he said: 'Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' Abu Bakr led the prayer. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ felt some relief and came out. When Abu Bakr saw him he stepped back, but he gestured to him with his hand, meaning 'stay where you are.' He came and sat beside him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ recited from where Abu Bakr had ended."],[6711,"A man from Banu Kinanah suffered a head wound reaching the brain membrane, and Umar b. al-Khattab wanted to exact retaliation from the one who struck him. Al-Abbas said to him: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"No retaliation for a wound reaching the brain membrane, nor for a penetrating wound to the body cavity, nor for a wound that dislodges a bone.\" So he made him pay blood money."],[6712,"I heard Abu Hurayrah say to Ibn Abbas: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The believer's dream is one of forty parts of prophethood.\" Ibn Abbas said: 'Of sixty.' Abu Hurayrah said: 'You hear me say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said,\" and you say: \"Of sixty\"?'"],[6714,"I witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When the Muslims were routed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was on a mule that Farwah b. Nufathah al-Judhami had given him, the Messenger of God ﷺ spurred it toward the faces of the disbelievers while I held its bridle fearing it might bolt. Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib held the stirrup of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Call out to the companions of the acacia tree.' I called at the top of my voice: 'O companions of the acacia tree!' And callers among the Ansar called: 'O company of the Ansar!' Then the call was restricted to Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and they were the most steadfast in facing death. They said: 'Labbayk, labbayk!' By God, I did not compare their turning toward the Messenger of God ﷺ except to cows turning toward their calves. He said: They advanced and fought fiercely. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that, he took a handful of pebbles and threw them at the faces of the people, saying: 'May the faces be ugly!' He said: By God, I kept seeing their edge blunted and their affair in retreat until God routed them."],[6715,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ from Madinah, and he turned toward it and said: 'God has purified this peninsula of polytheism, but I fear that the stars may mislead them.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, how could the stars mislead them?' He said: 'Rain falls, and they say: \"We were given rain by such-and-such a star.\""],[6716,"They used to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ without using the tooth-stick. He said: 'You enter upon me with yellow teeth and do not use the tooth-stick? Use the tooth-stick. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory upon them just as I made ablution obligatory upon them.' Aishah said: 'The Prophet ﷺ kept mentioning the tooth-stick until we feared that Quran would be revealed about it.'"],[6717,"I heard al-Abbas say to al-Zubayr: 'O Abu Abd Allah, here the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded you to plant the banner.'"],[6718,"Regarding His saying: 'And above them eight will bear the Throne of your Lord that Day' (Quran 69:17), he said: 'Eight angels in the form of mountain goats.'"],[6719,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ in al-Batha. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do you know what this is?' He said: We said: 'The clouds.' He said: 'And the rain-clouds.' We said: 'And the rain-clouds.' He said: 'And the high clouds.' He said: We fell silent. He said: 'Do you know how much is between heaven and earth?' We said: 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Between them is a distance of five hundred years' journey, and between each heaven and the next is a distance of five hundred years' journey, and the thickness of each heaven is a distance of five hundred years' journey. The seventh heaven, between its bottom and its top, is like what is between heaven and earth. Then above that are eight mountain goats, between their knees and their hooves is like what is between heaven and earth. Then above that is the Throne, and nothing of the deeds of the children of Adam is hidden from Him.'"],[6720,"God has purified this town of polytheism, if the stars do not mislead them."],[6721,"O Messenger of God, did you benefit Abu Talib? For he used to protect you and become angry for you. He said: 'He is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me he would be in the lowest depth.'"],[6722,"The Messenger of God ﷺ departed from Arafah with Usamah b. Zayd riding behind him, and he departed from Muzdalifah with al-Fadl b. Abbas riding behind him. Al-Fadl said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah.'"],[6723,"A man said, 'O Messenger of God, my father reached Islam as a very old man. If I bind him tightly on the saddle, I fear he may die, and if I do not bind him, he will not stay on. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said, 'Do you think that if your father had a debt and you paid it, would that suffice him?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'So perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"],[6724,"Al-Ghumaysa' or al-Rumaysa' came complaining about her husband to the Messenger of God ﷺ. She said, 'He cannot reach her.' He said, 'She has lied, O Messenger of God; I do it, but she wants to return to her first husband.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'She is not lawful for him until she tastes his sweetness.'"],[6725,"The Prophet ﷺ broke the fast at Arafat."],[6726,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded in two white Sahuli garments."],[6727,"I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ from Jam', and his mount did not raise its leg as it set out in the early morning until he reached Jam'."],[6728,"He was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ from Arafat. When the Messenger of God ﷺ reached the left pass that is before Muzdalifah, he made the camel kneel. He said, 'Then he came and I poured water for his ablution, and he performed ablution.' I said, 'The prayer, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'The prayer is ahead of you.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ rode until he reached Muzdalifah and prayed. Then al-Fadl rode behind the Messenger of God ﷺ on the morning of Jam'."],[6729,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he reached the Jamrah."],[6730,"He was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said in the evening of Arafah and the morning of Jam': 'O people, when you move on, upon you be calmness,' while he was restraining his she-camel, until when he entered Muhassir— which is part of Mina— he said, 'Upon you be the small pebbles with which the Jamrah is thrown.' And the Messenger of God ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah."],[6731,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded the weak ones of Banu Hashim to depart from Jam' at night."],[6732,"The Prophet ﷺ visited al-Abbas in a desert land of ours. There was a dog and a donkey of ours grazing. The Prophet ﷺ prayed the afternoon prayer while they were in front of him, and they were not scared away nor moved back."],[6733,"I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I did not stop hearing him reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah. When he threw, he stopped."],[6734,"The Prophet ﷺ did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah. He threw it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble."],[6735,"The Prophet ﷺ drank on the Day of Arafah."],[6736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Arafah and from Muzdalifah with tranquility upon him until he reached Mina. When he descended into Muhassir, he said: O people, upon you is to throw small pebbles."],[6737,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and there was a bedouin with him who had a beautiful daughter. He began presenting her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hoping that he would marry her. He said: I began looking at her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began taking hold of my head and turning it away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[6738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Arafat with Usamah riding behind him. The she-camel swerved with him while he was standing, and he struck it before departing, raising his hands not beyond his head. When he departed, he proceeded at his own pace until he came to Muzdalifah. Then he departed from Muzdalifah with al-Fadl riding behind him. Al-Fadl said: The Prophet ﷺ did not stop the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[6739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in the Kabah, but did not bow or prostrate."],[6740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the weak among Banu Hashim to hasten from Muzdalifah at night."],[6741,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ and he threw seven pebbles at Jamrat al-Aqabah, saying takbir with each pebble."],[6742,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drink on the Day of Arafah."],[6743,"A woman from Khatham came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father has been overtaken by Allah's obligation of Hajj, but he is a very old man who cannot stay firm on his mount. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father."],[6744,"The prayer is two by two, and you testify facing the qiblah in every two rak'ahs, and you humble yourself, show submissiveness, and be calm. Then you raise your hands, saying: You raise them to your Lord, facing their palms toward your face, and you say: O Lord, O Lord. Whoever does not do that, it is deficient."],[6745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed nine years in Madinah without performing Hajj. Then he announced to the people that they should set out. When he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, he prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr, and she sent word to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Take a bath, wrap yourself with a cloth, and enter ihram. He said: So she did. When the chest of the Messenger of Allah's mount was settled on the back of al-Bayda, he entered ihram and we entered ihram with him. We knew nothing but Hajj, and for that we set out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, and the Quran was being revealed to him, and he knew its interpretation. He only did what he was commanded. Jabir said: I looked before me, behind me, to my right, and to my left as far as my sight could extend, and the people were on foot and mounted. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the talbiyah, saying: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak. When we reached Makkah, he began by touching the corner, then he hastened for three circuits and walked for four. When he finished his tawaf, he went to the Maqam and said: Allah said: And take the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. He prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam of Ibrahim. Jafar b. Muhammad said: My father said: He used to recite in them the Surah of Tawhid: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, the One.' He said: And that was not mentioned from Jabir. Jabir said: Then he went to the corner and touched it, then he went to al-Safa and said: We begin with what Allah began with: Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. He ascended al-Safa until the House became visible to him, and he said takbir three times and said: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise, He gives life and causes death, in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things—three times, and he supplicated during that. Then he descended from al-Safa and walked until when his feet were placed in the bottom of the valley, he hastened until when his feet ascended from the bottom of the valley, he walked to al-Marwah and ascended al-Marwah until the House became visible to him, and he said the like of what he said on al-Safa. He performed seven circuits, then said: Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram, and whoever has a sacrificial animal should remain in ihram. If I did not have a sacrificial animal with me, I would have exited ihram. And if I were to face in my affair what I have left behind, I would have entered ihram for Umrah. He said: Ali came from Yemen, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: With what did you enter ihram, O Ali? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger enters ihram. He said: For I have a sacrificial animal, so do not exit ihram. Ali said: I entered upon Fatimah, and she had applied kohl and put on dyed clothes. I said: Who commanded you to do this? She said: My father commanded me. He said: Ali used to say in Iraq: I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, angry with Fatimah, seeking confirmation of what she said. He said: She has spoken the truth; I commanded her. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered one hundred camels from that, sixty-three with his own hand, and Ali slaughtered the rest. Then he took a piece from each camel, and they cooked them all together, and they both ate from the meat and drank from the broth. Suraqah b. Malik b. Jushum said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year of ours or forever? He said: Rather, forever. The Umrah has entered into the Hajj, and he interlaced his fingers."],[6746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a bone with meat in her house. Bilal came to him and called him to prayer, so he stood up to pray. I took hold of his garment and said: O father, should you not perform wudu? He said: From what should I perform wudu, O my little daughter? I said: From what the fire has touched. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Is not the purest of your food that which the fire has touched?"],[6747,"Every son of a mother has kin to whom he belongs, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and I am their kin."],[6748,"Jesus son of Mary remained among the Children of Israel for forty years."],[6749,"Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he confided something to her, and she wept. Then he confided something to her, and she laughed. So I asked her about it, and she said..."],[6750,"Ibn Isma'il b. Abi Samina narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Zakariyya narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, something similar. [Hidden text, linked 23067511: \"Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he confided something to her, and she wept. Then he confided something to her, and she laughed. So I asked her about it, and she said...\"]"],[6751,"Fatimah approached walking, and her gait resembled the gait of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Welcome to my daughter. Then he seated her on his right or on his left, and he secretly told her something, so she wept. Then he secretly told her something, so she laughed. I said: I have never seen sorrow closer to joy than today! What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ secretly tell you? She said: I would not divulge the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he passed away, I asked her, and she said: He said: Gabriel used to come to me and review the Qur'an with me once a year, but this year he came to me and reviewed it with me twice. I do not think my term has come except that it is near. What an excellent predecessor I am for you, and you are the first of my household to join me. So I wept for that. Then he said: Are you not pleased to be the mistress of the women of the believers, or the women of this community? She said: So I laughed."],[6752,"We buried with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and when he finished, he departed and stood in the middle of the road. Then there was a woman approaching whom we did not think he recognized. When she drew near, it was Fatimah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: O Fatimah, what brought you out of your house? She said: I came, O Messenger of Allah, to the family of this house to show mercy to their deceased, or to console them—I do not remember which of the two she said. Rabi'ah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Perhaps you reached the graves with them? She said: I seek refuge with Allah, and I have heard you mention concerning it what you mention. He said: If you had reached the graves, you would not have seen Paradise until your grandfather, the father of your mother, or the father of your father, sees it."],[6754,"Let no one blame except himself if he spends the night with the smell of grease on his hand."],[6755,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at 'Ali and said: This one is in Paradise. Among his followers there will be people who learn Islam and then abandon it. They have a nickname by which they are called: the Rafidah. Whoever meets them, let him kill them, for they are polytheists."],[6756,"He entered the privy and found a morsel—or he said: a piece of bread—in the path of excrement and urine. He took it, removed the filth from it, and washed it thoroughly. Then he handed it to his servant and said: O boy, remind me of it when I perform ablution. When he performed ablution, he said to the boy: O boy, hand me the morsel—or he said: the piece of bread. The boy said: O my master, I ate it. He said: Then go, for you are free for the sake of Allah. The boy said to him: O my master, for what reason did you set me free? He said: Because I heard Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah, mention from her father, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Whoever takes a morsel or a piece of bread from the path of excrement and urine, removes the filth from it, washes it thoroughly, then eats it—it will not settle in his stomach until he is forgiven. So I would not employ a man from the people of Paradise."],[6757,"We came to Jabir b. 'Abd Allah, and he was among Banu Salimah. We asked him about the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah."],[6758,"Fatimah came to Abu Bakr and said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, did you inherit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or his family? He said: Rather his family. She said: Then what about the share of the Messenger of Allah? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When Allah gives a prophet a provision and then takes him, He makes it for the one who stands after him. So I thought to return it to the Muslims. She said: You and the Messenger of Allah know best."],[6759,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ gathered together to Fatimah and said to her: Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and say to him: Your wives beseech you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah. So she went to him and mentioned that to him. He said: Would you not love the one whom I love? She said: Yes. He said: For I love this one."],[6760,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, he would say: In the name of Allah, and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your mercy. And when he left, he would say: In the name of Allah, and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your bounty."],[6761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called his daughter Fatimah and whispered to her, and she wept. Then he whispered to her, and she laughed. 'A'ishah said: I said to Fatimah, 'What is this that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whispered to you, so you wept, then he whispered to you, so you laughed?' She said: 'He whispered to me and told me of his death, so I wept. Then he whispered to me and told me that I would be the first of his family to follow him, so I laughed.'"],[6762,"Fatimah asked the Prophet ﷺ for a servant. He said: 'Shall I not direct you to something better than that? Glorify Allah, magnify Him, and praise Allah one hundred times when you go to your bed.'"],[6763,"When 'Ali was killed, al-Hasan b. 'Ali stood up as a speaker. He praised and extolled Allah, then said: 'Now then, by Allah, you have killed tonight a man on a night in which the Qur'an was sent down, in which 'Isa son of Maryam was raised up, and in which Yusha' b. Nun, the servant of Musa ﷺ , was killed.'"],[6764,"'And in it the Children of Israel were forgiven.' And he said: 'By Allah, no one before him surpassed him, and no one after him will reach him. The Prophet ﷺ would send him on a military expedition with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left. By Allah, he left neither gold nor silver except seven hundred or eight hundred dirhams, which he had set aside to buy a servant.'"],[6765,"What do you memorize from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: 'I heard him supplicating with this supplication: O Allah, guide us among those You have guided, grant us well-being among those You have granted well-being, take us under Your care among those You have taken under Your care, bless us in what You have given, and protect us from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed, You decree and none decrees against You. And none whom You befriend is humiliated. Blessed and exalted are You.'"],[6766,"I entered upon al-Hasan b. 'Ali, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: War is deception.'"],[6767,"Pray in your houses and do not make them graves. Do not make my grave a place of festivity. Send blessings upon me and greet me, for your blessings and greetings reach me wherever you are."],[6768,"I found a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it out of my mouth with its saliva and threw it among the dates. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you take it?' He said: 'Because charity is not lawful for the family of Muhammad.'"],[6769,"The gift of the fasting person is oil and the incense burner."],[6770,"I was between al-Husayn and al-Hasan while they and Marwan were insulting each other. Al-Hasan began to restrain al-Husayn. Marwan said: 'A cursed household.' Al-Hasan became angry and said: 'Did you say a cursed household? By Allah, Allah cursed you on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ while you were in your father's loins.'"],[6771,"My grandfather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, taught me words to say in the qunut of the witr: O Allah, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take me under Your care among those You have taken under Your care, guide me among those You have guided, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed, You decree and none decrees against You. And none whom You befriend is humiliated. Glory be to You, blessed and exalted are You."],[6772,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn passed by Marwan, and he said something vile to them. Al-Hasan—or al-Husayn—said: 'By God, and again by God, God cursed you while you were still in the loins of al-Hakam upon the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ.' He said: Marwan fell silent."],[6773,"I was in Kufa when al-Hasan b. Ali stood up to give a sermon and said: 'O people, last night I saw something wondrous in my sleep. I saw the Lord, exalted is He, above His Throne. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came and stood beside one of the supports of the Throne. Then Abu Bakr came and placed his hand on the shoulder of the Messenger of God. Then Umar came and placed his hand on the shoulder of Abu Bakr. Then Uthman came and was a short distance away, and said: \"Lord, ask Your servants why they killed me.\" He said: Then two spouts of blood poured down from the sky to the earth. He said: It was said to Ali: \"Do you not see what al-Hasan is relating?\" He said: \"He relates what he saw.\""],[6774,"I will not fight after a dream I saw. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ placing his hand on the Throne, and I saw Abu Bakr placing his hand on the Prophet ﷺ, and I saw Umar placing his hand on Abu Bakr, and I saw Uthman placing his hand on Umar, and I saw blood below them. I said: \"What are these bloods?\" It was said: \"The blood of Uthman, for which God is seeking retribution.\""],[6775,"From al-Hasan b. Ali that he said to Abu al-A'war: 'Woe to you! Did not the Messenger of God ﷺ curse Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Amr b. Sufyan?'"],[6776,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the house of Fatimah."],[6777,"Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan performed the Hajj, and Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj performed it with him; he was among the people most abusive to Ali. He said: They passed through Madinah while al-Hasan b. Ali and a group of his companions were sitting. It was said to him: \"This is Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj, the one who abuses Ali.\" He said: \"Bring the man to me.\" He said: A messenger came to him and said: \"Answer him.\" He said: \"Who?\" He said: \"Al-Hasan b. Ali is calling you.\" So he came to him and greeted him. Al-Hasan said to him: \"Are you Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: He repeated that to him. He said: \"So you are the one who abuses Ali?\" He said: It was as if he felt ashamed. Al-Hasan said to him: \"By God, if you come to him at the Pool—and I do not think you will reach it—you will find him with his garment tucked up to his shin, driving away from it the banners of the hypocrites as a man drives away strange camels. This is the saying of the truthful one who was believed, and whoever fabricates has failed.\""],[6778,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Muhammad, God loves three of your companions, so love them: Ali b. Abi Talib, Abu Dharr, and al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad.' He said: Then Gabriel came to him and said: 'O Muhammad, Paradise yearns for three of your companions.' Anas b. Malik was with him, and he hoped that it would be for some of the Ansar. He said: He wanted to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about them but was in awe of him. So he went out and met Abu Bakr and said: 'O Abu Bakr, I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ a short while ago when Gabriel came to him and said: \"Paradise yearns for three of your companions.\" I hoped that it would be for some of the Ansar, but I was in awe of him to ask him. Would you go in to the Prophet of God ﷺ and ask him?' He said: 'I fear to ask him, lest I not be among them and my people gloat over me.' Then Umar b. al-Khattab met me and said to him something like what Abu Bakr had said. He said: Then he met Ali, and Ali said to him: 'Yes, if I am among them, I praise God; and if I am not among them, I still praise God.' So he went in to the Prophet of God ﷺ and said: 'Anas is...'"],[6779,"I said to Ubayd Allah b. Abi Yazid: 'Did you see al-Husayn b. Ali?' He said: 'His hair and beard were black except for a few hairs here in the front of his beard. I do not know whether he dyed it and left that place out of resemblance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, or whether only that part had not turned white.' He said: 'And I saw al-Hasan when the prayer had been commenced; he prostrated between the imam and some of the people. It was said to him: \"Sit down.\" He said: \"The prayer has already commenced.\""],[6780,"Do not keep staring at lepers, and when you speak to them, let there be between you and them the distance of a spear's length."],[6781,"Whoever is killed defending his right is a martyr."],[6782,"The miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me."],[6783,"There is no Muslim man or woman who is struck by a calamity—even if its time has long passed—and then renews for it an istirja', except that God renews for him at that moment and gives him the reward of what He promised for it on the day he was struck by it."],[6784,"Hawtharah narrated to us: Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us with his chain something similar."],[6785,"Indeed, in Friday there is an hour in which no one is cupped except that he dies."],[6786,"Whoever has a child born to him and calls the adhan in his right ear and the iqamah in his left ear, Umm al-Sibyan will not harm him."],[6787,"The safeguard of my community from drowning when they embark is that they say: 'In the name of Allah is its course and its mooring. Indeed, my Lord is Forgiving and Merciful.' And they did not appraise Allah with true appraisal - the verse."],[6788,"He used to perform ablution and washed the place of his prostration with water until it flowed over the place of prostration."],[6789,"The one who is cheated is neither praiseworthy nor rewarded."],[6790,"The beggar has a right, even if he comes on a horse."],[6791,"Whoever witnesses a matter and dislikes it is like one who was absent from it, and whoever is absent from a matter and approves of it is like one who witnessed it."],[6792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me words to say in the qunut of witr: 'My Lord, guide me among those You have guided, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and take me as a friend among those You have taken as friends, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for indeed You decree and none decrees over You, and indeed You do not humiliate those You befriend. Blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted.'"],[6828,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, he would say: In the name of Allah, and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your mercy. And when he left, he would say: In the name of Allah, and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your bounty."],[6860,"“After me there will be trials, in which the one sleeping is better than the one awake, and the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking. Whoever comes upon it, let him take his sword, then walk to a rock and strike it until it breaks, then lie down for it until it clears as it clears.”"],[6888,"Indeed, the one who misses the Asr prayer, it is as if his family and wealth have been taken away."],[6892,"Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he confided something to her, and she wept. Then he confided something to her, and she laughed. So I asked her about it, and she said..."],[6911,"'A'ishah and Umm Salamah were asked, \"Which deed was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" They both said, \"That which its doer persists in, even if it is little.\""],[6930,"When one of you is afflicted with judging between the Muslims, let him not judge while he is angry; let him treat them equally in looking, seating, and gesture, and let him not raise his voice over either of the two litigants."],[6949,"\"O Messenger of God, is the slaughter only from the throat or the upper chest?\" He said: \"If you had stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed for you.\" 2 - (1504) - Hawtharah added: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed for you.\""],[7031,"I have not forgotten the Day of the Trench when he was passing milk to them, and his hair had become dusty—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—and he was saying: 'Indeed, the best good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun.' Then Ammar came, and he [the Prophet] said: 'Woe to you, or woe upon you'—Khalid was uncertain—'O Ibn Sumayya, the transgressing group will kill you.'"],[7038,"The injury caused by an animal is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[7039,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn over a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband."],[7041,"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn over a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband."],[7042,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who makes lawful [a woman for her former husband] and the one for whom it is made lawful."],[7095,"The one among them most resembling the Prophet ﷺ was al-Hasan b. 'Ali."],[7144,"Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."],[7188,"While they were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a shooting star was cast and it lit up. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: \"What would you say in the pre-Islamic era when something like this was cast?\" They said: \"God and His Messenger know best. We used to say: 'Tonight a great man was born, and tonight a great man died.'\" He said: \"It is not cast for anyone's death or life. But when our Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He, decrees a matter, the bearers of the Throne glorify Him, then the inhabitants of the heaven that follows them glorify Him, until the glorification reaches the inhabitants of the lowest heaven. Then they say to those who follow the bearers of the Throne: 'What did your Lord say?' They inform them, and the inhabitants of the heavens ask one another until the news reaches the inhabitants of the lowest heaven. Then the jinn snatch the hearing and cast it to their allies, and they are pelted. So what they bring as it is is true, but they distort it and add to it.\""],[7200,"The one among them most resembling the Prophet ﷺ was al-Hasan b. 'Ali."],[7228,"Indeed, praise belongs to Allah; we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can lead astray, and whomever He leads astray, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but He, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he recites verses from the Book of Allah: 'Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims'; 'Fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs; indeed Allah is ever watchful over you'; 'Fear Allah and speak a right word, He will amend your deeds and forgive your sins; and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has achieved a great success.'"],[7238,"Seventy prophets passed by the rock of al-Rawḥāʾ, barefoot, wearing cloaks, heading to the Ancient House of God; among them was Moses, the prophet of God, may God bless him."],[7255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: You and your wealth belong to your father."],[7271,"The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."],[7307,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us hate death. He said: That is not the hatred of death; but when the bringer of good tidings comes to him from Allah with what he is heading towards, he loves to meet Allah and Allah loves to meet him. And the disbeliever — or: the wicked — when he is attended by death, there comes to him what he will encounter, so he hates to meet Allah and Allah hates to meet him."],[7342,"The injury caused by an animal is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure one-fifth is due."],[7445,"Ghifar: may Allah forgive her. Aslam: may Allah grant her peace."],[7476,"I am your predecessor at the pond."],[7511,"Islam is built on five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan."],[7516,"Islam is built on five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan."],[7522,"Saying subhan Allah (glory be to God) is for men, and clapping is for women."],[7554,"Saying subhan Allah (glory be to God) is for men, and clapping is for women."]]);
